</node>
<node id="NPH">
  <data key="d0">NPH</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">NPH (Neutral Protamine Hagedorn) is a protaminated human insulin formulation that appears as a cloudy suspension and must be gently mixed before administration. It provides an intermediate‑duration, or “Lenta,” glucose‑lowering effect, making it suitable as a basal insulin. As the protaminated component of many human insulin premixes, NPH is commonly referenced in clinical research as the standard comparator insulin. It has been used as the basal insulin control in studies evaluating diabetic retinopathy, patient satisfaction, and antibody responses, and it is frequently listed among treatment groups in various clinical trials.&lt;SEP&gt;NPH is an intermediate‑acting insulin formulation listed as a possible basal insulin.&lt;SEP&gt;NPH (Neutral Protamine Hagedorn) is an intermediate‑acting insulin used as a comparator in clinical studies of Levemir® FlexPen®.&lt;SEP&gt;NPH (Neutral Protamine Hagedorn) is an intermediate‑acting insulin used as a comparator in the studies.&lt;SEP&gt;NPH is an intermediate‑acting insulin formulation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-54575ceb6b15fc8abcc2afcec7b36792&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a8768fa32f88d682aa4ddf677297047e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aa127476a5c98492d7b7e0fcd1212886&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-89eaf7a8bcccf1ef8657b22ee03b5dd9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d194d06ef99b3f8aa6b6542b7e93e762&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a72472938feb27131681a1591081e8c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b916f29e047f8579110cf5da3fd73847&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bf25fca295be60e28b7c7d3103f722fc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db832f06717859b8ba6cf7fd70aa22d8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9f85d0ab4cfadc905544cb9e30752dab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-68b98187c6ab15468f1c0d8f5e7f9f6a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b65a4249ac93aec086cb333ed1507ea7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dfa23fc15cc4d520a32488843dbd710b</data>
