<node id="Hiperglicemia">
  <data key="d0">Hiperglicemia</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Hiperglicemia is a medical condition defined by an abnormally high concentration of glucose in the bloodstream. It is generally diagnosed when blood‑glucose measurements exceed the normal range, often cited as values greater than 10 mmol/L (180 mg/dL), and can be identified through clinical glucose meters, capillary glucose testing, or continuous glucose monitoring (CGM) systems.

The condition commonly arises in individuals with poorly controlled diabetes mellitus. Key pathophysiological contributors include insufficient endogenous insulin production, inadequate insulin dosing, and lifestyle or physiological factors that disrupt glucose homeostasis. In the context of insulin therapy, hiperglicemia may be precipitated by improper administration techniques such as injecting into compromised tissue (e.g., lipodystrophy or localized cutaneous amyloid deposits), reusing needles, or selecting suboptimal injection sites. Specific reports have linked repeated injections of products like APIDRA SOLOSTAR into amyloid‑affected areas with acute hyperglycemic episodes. Additionally, hiperglicemia can follow episodes of hypoglycemia, reflecting the fluctuating nature of glucose regulation in diabetic patients.

Clinically, hiperglicemia presents with classic hyperglycemic symptoms: excessive thirst (polydipsia), increased urination (polyuria), nausea, and, in severe or prolonged cases, a risk of diabetic ketoacidosis (DKA). Elevated glucose also impairs cognitive functions, reducing concentration, slowing reaction time, and affecting vision, which raises safety concerns for activities requiring sustained attention, such as driving. In pregnant individuals, sustained hyperglycemia markedly increases the risk of fetal malformations and intra‑uterine death, making tight glycemic control essential during prenatal care.

Management focuses on optimal insulin therapy and technical aspects of insulin delivery. Rapid‑acting insulin analogues (e.g., Humalog) are employed to correct acute elevations, while long‑acting basal insulins (e.g., Lantus) and structured basal regimens aim to maintain stable glucose levels over time. Effective strategies include careful dose adjustments, selection of healthy injection sites, strict avoidance of needle reuse, and regular monitoring of blood glucose and ketone levels. In intensive‑care settings, glucose levels above 10 mmol/L are often targeted for treatment with short‑acting formulations such as Novolin® R. By addressing both pharmacologic and procedural factors, healthcare providers can reduce the frequency of hyperglycemic episodes, mitigate acute complications like DKA, and lower the risk of long‑term sequelae associated with chronic hiperglicemia.&lt;SEP&gt;A medical condition of dangerously high blood glucose.&lt;SEP&gt;High blood glucose episodes, which are reduced when using a CGM during pregnancy.&lt;SEP&gt;Hiperglicemia denotes high blood glucose levels that may present with typical symptoms.&lt;SEP&gt;Hiperglicemia is elevated blood glucose, noted as a diagnostic sign in adolescents with DM2.&lt;SEP&gt;Hiperglicemia is elevated blood glucose considered in secondary diabetes assessment.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1be43b1b23852278983f60d0f150b0f9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d4cfc50689ef0b918230df31cb99e5e5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7982460136aa21cc2de3969af556c4d2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fe370bbb9ac4bc4d475b9ef58ec9fee9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c3daabbd42055dc30154f5f97c85fb7d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a976e1642df27c488174759a35ca23f2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-572e715aada476f4dac69a032e16cc09&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c032d0271c85fd24982516368a62b1a9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-072d97721eef045503ec1dce0363b58e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4d0ac8ad5968d54922b924fdb16b61d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-61cacf80ada6db26d2b975df763c137a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-17844a4a12e6c05ba2d7b5f54b0f9bd7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2db4ee43ed7cc39546184320e1328d06&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5b40c2fbad301807d9646f27d94635cb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a247846b9ec5d44d0bcbe6c5f15599f8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aca0b919135813e1d5b772face36989d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9cd336474a2e9457985162b1ddb4b603&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-56fb3d61e8c32af5d6b8be06cc54f904&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b060d4f68031bd35dfafc19eadf1e9fe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-04b345bc26ec7f5d7c9db8c6004a50a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0e7689ca0fc736d9eae94256f73fed52&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-45ee3dcb366c1301c9fb1d2ce9f323c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4615ca664e7ff898d8c5929cbc79e7d8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d6101c469482b48e341b4095a54907fd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0851222a21a012cffce7a16710847208&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e4e1124e7acf6619a1a7c60febd5211c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ba6b31518be6fff1db8b68a28e82f200&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-93f7f04b0529d6f0ace11829cc4fa3b4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fb0cd81f0439cbb74e3c0ff54236c45d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cbe87fd92ad66dcb02b25b669d829f6c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-91a09040fc4581d7aad2216dba9fba79&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-276b766b8d515b1e7f388b5b7381bfbc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-97acd5016384ec4abfe4d43c6a9cad08&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5341c88e6470a893413f9aaec70dbdae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e5570f88766511a4a62cbe9a2dff0bdb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5dce7a759a9de18a4d1bcc77a071fbe2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1136d6aac4c2e881387a4db1a0f4a3a3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-078f5907e86c2158587c79b26b0cd683&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2e6267110f4ae5f4df4c49c0653a09b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fee32f1fb0c848b0799071a86119b142</data>
