<node id="Thermal Bag">
  <data key="d0">Thermal Bag</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Thermal Bag is a small insulated bag recommended for transporting insulin, used with a recyclable ice pack but without direct contact between the insulin container and ice.&lt;SEP&gt;Thermal Bag is a transport bag for insulin that must avoid direct contact with ice or frozen elements.&lt;SEP&gt;A rigid‑walled container, often with gel packs, used to keep insulin vials between 2 °C and 8 °C during transport.&lt;SEP&gt;A thermal bag is an insulated carrier used to transport insulin at controlled temperatures.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-022aabbd0c94aa681dcd00c49d072b46&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-03a1de93a53fbcb513268c123e2c5a16&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2df359ca3783191b2159f8d3f6ea6c52&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8336dc27990f6189c99863d64435c6c6</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/Documento sem título.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/insulinas em seringa.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Armazenamento e Transporte/Armazenamento e transporte.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1786302100</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Ice Pack">
  <data key="d0">Ice Pack</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Ice Pack is a recyclable ice element placed inside the thermal bag to keep insulin cool during transport.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-022aabbd0c94aa681dcd00c49d072b46</data>
