<node id="Needle">
  <data key="d0">Needle</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Needle (insulin‑pen needle) – The needle used with disposable insulin pens such as the NovoRapid® FlexPen®, KwikPen (including the BASAGLAR version), SoloStar/Caneta SoloStar and similar devices is a thin‑walled, sharp, hollow steel shaft that is sterile, detachable, and intended for single‑use only. It is typically available in lengths ranging from 4 mm to 8 mm, with the most common options being 4 mm, 5 mm, 6 mm and 8 mm; longer versions exist for specific clinical needs. Shorter needles (4–5 mm) are inserted at a shallow angle, whereas longer needles (6–8 mm) require a steeper angle to ensure the tip reaches the subcutaneous tissue. The needle is protected by a cap or protective seal during preparation, and after each injection it must be removed and discarded in accordance with sharps‑waste protocols to prevent injury, contamination and dosing errors. Proper technique calls for a single, gentle motion, avoidance of blood vessels, and a dwell time of at least ten seconds after full insertion to allow optimal insulin absorption. Although its primary purpose is sub‑cutaneous insulin delivery, the same needle can be employed for intradermal, intramuscular, or even intravenous injections when clinical circumstances demand. Specific models such as the BASAGLAR KwikPen may experience needle obstruction, underscoring the need to inspect the needle before each use.

Needle (syringe needle for insulin) – In some contexts the term “needle” refers to the metal needle attached to a conventional syringe for insulin administration. These needles are similarly sharp, hollow, and made of steel, but unlike the dedicated pen needles they are sometimes described as being reusable for multiple injections, provided they are properly cleaned and inspected. The reuse practice is not universally endorsed because of infection‑control concerns, and many guidelines still recommend single‑use disposable syringes for insulin to maintain sterility and dosing accuracy.

Needle (infusion‑set needle) – A third usage of the term describes the small, sharp instrument incorporated into insulin infusion sets such as the Sure‑T system. This needle is inserted subcutaneously to anchor the infusion set and deliver rapid‑acting insulin continuously. Because the metal tip remains in the body for an extended period, it must be removed before certain imaging procedures (e.g., MRI or CT) to avoid artifact or safety issues. The infusion‑set needle is also designed for single‑use and is discarded together with the set after the prescribed wear time.&lt;SEP&gt;Needle is the sharp component of the infusion set that penetrates the skin to deliver insulin.&lt;SEP&gt;Needle (agulha) is used with catheters for pump sets and may need replacement when the pump malfunctions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-022aabbd0c94aa681dcd00c49d072b46&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-26c5ab6d7b3b32c5f6aca2b58489782a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d9f7234865211afc5d8343294b276d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-191286ebd759321d40620f77c84ef5a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b91b40e47c97be1b62c0f3d271cd4efd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ebdb9452013f0e340884677832714553&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-35a8ffab5eb63600b93fb2c67160b5ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-03a1de93a53fbcb513268c123e2c5a16&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8abf9336f83edf5c92071da1032dc483&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-708e3c514f667dc9979cfa8df875e473&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a8768fa32f88d682aa4ddf677297047e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cc6a26a5d2c41087b58a0f7f71ad21cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d8310c065da1c624d58d9a0a8e9ff7d4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7ed0b3e64751c1a28d72e087f711cc20&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-74b3171b97fd80965359afadc0af9312&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b5b4c60b3de8c56d9ab869d868345fb7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-64b999805e924800faef3b856e45d8bf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9725072a361e9b1b97c5daa35e061e58&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f0c10866496bbb0b388b1e5ed69901c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bbae57922175913b7c36c594b4673fa2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0b9c41c968bcc1d46185583661e8f989&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7638273060df996ad502ec2fadfc9c82&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d7223c781e745e72311fccfcdd58583&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b79dcaf41f7f07eed90788ce9e50dddd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ffe095bda1b787c5b5ae2d61a2f74c98&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e9835d6684db67541402527b3182b6c5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-79f891b1d7c0c6ca0eab9dbcc76c902d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f0710d91bd443ae1af3fd98049f4ad42&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dd25c8bd4672601d6ee40e4b7e28a69c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ddb8954aaa1e1230598596ce6f5df249&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5c24a2af0d0291fc4f4730256c420e93&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c68e2c07786710dd5250c6610f52b14d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-55f8c8b2b40633cf37993b620002b889&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cf3629e41b33d8907b96157ddd2be394&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fdabdf4730f349f4b46e7242c65d440d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b6025fa711665988fad0f789b9eb901a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6fba8ea0c6bdb8427804ba05f9fe49f9</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/Documento sem título.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Cópia de Técnicas de aplicação de insulina.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Documento sem título.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Insulinas CANETAS.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/insulinas em seringa.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/NOVORAPID _ BulasMed.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Basaglar.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Toujeo.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_apidra.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_fiasp.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/Documento sem título.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf</data>
