<node id="Plastic Bottle">
  <data key="d0">Plastic Bottle</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Plastic Bottle is a rigid container, such as a bleach or fabric softener bottle, used to collect used needles before taking them to a health unit for safe disposal.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-022aabbd0c94aa681dcd00c49d072b46</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/Documento sem título.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1786297932</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Health Unit">
  <data key="d0">Health Unit</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Health Unit is a medical facility where collected needles in a plastic bottle should be delivered for correct and safe disposal.&lt;SEP&gt;A health unit is a nearby health service that receives discarded sharps for proper handling.&lt;SEP&gt;The nearest health unit (Unidade de Saúde) receives discarded medical sharps for proper disposal.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-022aabbd0c94aa681dcd00c49d072b46&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ebdb9452013f0e340884677832714553&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a8768fa32f88d682aa4ddf677297047e</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/Documento sem título.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Insulinas CANETAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786300725</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Rapid Insulin">
  <data key="d0">Rapid Insulin</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Rapid Insulin is a fast‑acting insulin type that is transparent and typically administered before meals to control post‑meal blood sugar.&lt;SEP&gt;Rapid insulin is a fast‑acting insulin type that begins working in 10 to 20 minutes and peaks in 1 to 2 hours.&lt;SEP&gt;Rapid Insulin is a category encompassing fast‑acting insulin products such as Humulin R and Novolin R.&lt;SEP&gt;A fast-acting insulin formulation used for glucose regulation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-022aabbd0c94aa681dcd00c49d072b46&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2a0a3f492aa5ef7771b2246547cb5f02&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a8768fa32f88d682aa4ddf677297047e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-91a09040fc4581d7aad2216dba9fba79</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/Documento sem título.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Insulinas CANETAS.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/cgm.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786335246</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Slow Insulin">
  <data key="d0">Slow Insulin</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Slow Insulin is a long‑acting insulin (including NPH) that may appear transparent or milky and is usually taken once or twice daily to maintain glucose balance between meals and overnight.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-022aabbd0c94aa681dcd00c49d072b46</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/Documento sem título.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1786297932</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="NPH Insulin">
  <data key="d0">NPH Insulin</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">NPH Insulin, short for neutral protamine Hagedorn insulin, is a traditional intermediate‑acting formulation of human insulin. After subcutaneous injection it typically begins to lower blood glucose within 1–2 hours, reaches its maximal effect between 4 and 12 hours, and can sustain activity for 18–24 hours, providing basal insulin coverage. The product is supplied as a milky‑white suspension that often requires gentle rolling of the vial or cartridge before use to ensure uniformity.

In clinical practice NPH Insulin is used as a basal therapy, frequently administered twice daily (morning and night) in both adult and pediatric diabetes regimens. It is commonly combined with rapid‑acting analogues such as insulin lispro (Humalog®) in basal‑bolus or mixed‑insulin protocols, and it serves as a reference comparator in dose‑adjustment guides and mixed‑insulin studies.

Research literature routinely cites NPH Insulin as a benchmark basal insulin. It appears as the comparator arm in studies of newer long‑acting analogues (e.g., insulin glargine), in retinopathy progression trials, euglycemic clamp investigations, and pharmacokinetic profile assessments. It is also employed as a reference insulin in antibody cross‑reactivity experiments, safety and efficacy analyses of alternative formulations, and evaluations of potency variability and hypoglycemia risk across manufacturers.

While the overwhelming majority of descriptions identify NPH Insulin as an intermediate‑acting human insulin, one source characterizes it as a short‑acting analogue. This characterization conflicts with the established pharmacologic profile and is likely an error; the consensus across clinical and research contexts confirms NPH Insulin’s intermediate‑acting nature.&lt;SEP&gt;NPH Insulin is an intermediate‑acting insulin used as basal therapy.&lt;SEP&gt;NPH Insulin is an intermediate‑acting basal insulin listed in the Brazilian insulin formulation table.&lt;SEP&gt;NPH insulin is an intermediate‑acting insulin used as a reference point for variability and nocturnal hypoglycaemia.&lt;SEP&gt;NPH Insulin is an intermediate-acting basal insulin used as a comparator in several trials with insulin glargine and insulin detemir.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-022aabbd0c94aa681dcd00c49d072b46&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-622f3feb1f15564393e91cefc71256ec&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cc6a26a5d2c41087b58a0f7f71ad21cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c3daabbd42055dc30154f5f97c85fb7d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6e42637e4286cbc19cce4502b22634bd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fe094dd3d94334373a8497a7cb841e0f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3a279eef99c9c70338c74ffc7b4e260e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-133169995b3ab942fd96f1fdfe7269ad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3e50c145614f04be2319a31b74b80411&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fb0fb965e5ddd796999856ca376d4b9d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7084240a735ca2fe3b6d426e3b8c5756&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-afc28422755c2c44f931bab7b6a2b477&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-863286c185f2a62e5b28d7e4577a1088&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c95471c4c993fa3a499f99443ee7c922&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-891989adf06518cd34c94853444495e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f36263c657ad99a80e578ac49a333d5b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ddb8954aaa1e1230598596ce6f5df249&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e5f5165b3185feb3c6ec93a3c0ef8d02&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3237e202569462c758ec3d878c9faeae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fd6fa98b7767319460b4a421a719c5c2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e7e6ca9bf63e843b814736c0409c70fb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0f272d1c9c38e2a6b6d02b5aa66809e1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-494fef0b8efc2c44b3b49ebf9d74b7f2</data>
