<node id="Catheter">
  <data key="d0">Catheter</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Catheter is a thin tube connected to the insulin pump that penetrates the skin to deliver insulin and needs replacement every 2–3 days.&lt;SEP&gt;Catheter is a thin, flexible, transparent tube connecting the reservoir to the cannula.&lt;SEP&gt;A catheter is a tube component of infusion pumps that can experience insulin precipitation when Novolin® R is used.&lt;SEP&gt;Catheter is a medical tube that can be used for continuous subcutaneous insulin infusion.&lt;SEP&gt;Catheter is a component of the insulin pump whose partial or total obstruction is the most common malfunction.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-022aabbd0c94aa681dcd00c49d072b46&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7ed0b3e64751c1a28d72e087f711cc20&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dd396c45bc09fb646d156b4e69d328e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-acaa1440ae268669e1894588bb9e37c2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6fba8ea0c6bdb8427804ba05f9fe49f9</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/Documento sem título.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786330166</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Glucose">
  <data key="d0">Glucose</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Glucose is a simple carbohydrate that functions as the primary blood‑sugar molecule in humans, serving as the main fuel that cells throughout the body use to obtain energy. It circulates not only in the bloodstream but also in interstitial fluid, allowing rapid transport between metabolic compartments. The concentration of glucose in blood is expressed in milligrams per deciliter (mg/dL) and is tightly regulated by the hormones insulin and glucagon; insulin promotes uptake of glucose into cells, while glucagon stimulates release of glucose from storage when levels fall.

Because blood‑glucose levels reflect an individual’s glycemic status, measuring glucose is a fundamental clinical tool. Routine blood tests, continuous glucose sensors, and GS‑type sensor readings provide quantitative data that guide insulin therapy, inform dosing decisions, and assess metabolic control in both routine care and research studies. Elevated glucose concentrations can occur when insulin is insufficient, during illness, or in the context of diabetes, whereas low concentrations indicate hypoglycemia.

Therapeutically, glucose is administered to correct hypoglycemic states. Oral glucose is used for mild or moderate low‑blood‑sugar episodes, while intravenous glucose infusion delivers rapid restoration of plasma glucose in severe or life‑threatening situations. These interventions underscore glucose’s dual role as both a vital metabolic substrate and a therapeutic agent for managing blood‑sugar abnormalities.&lt;SEP&gt;Glucose is a sugar administered intravenously or orally in the experiments.&lt;SEP&gt;Glucose is the blood sugar whose absorption after meals creates the postprandial glucose excursions addressed by insulin therapies.&lt;SEP&gt;The blood sugar molecule whose levels are monitored by the sensors.&lt;SEP&gt;Glucose is the sugar measured in blood or interstitial fluid to assess glycemic control.&lt;SEP&gt;Glucose passes through the semipermeable membrane in the Dextrostix test, producing a color that estimates glycemia.&lt;SEP&gt;A simple sugar used to reverse insulin-induced hypoglycemia.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-022aabbd0c94aa681dcd00c49d072b46&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b91b40e47c97be1b62c0f3d271cd4efd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-431b48980656b0322f263c358250b593&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4f079198593c1702b56062aa87e7801a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db832f06717859b8ba6cf7fd70aa22d8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d5bb996e52cb71f15bc8c30d1b1d321&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d01ed6a801b11c1b53f4668059c1f9cb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-786395f3716fb61a79fd183c63e1a9d6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a1245bd9ff75c998b49dab861cc4cebf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2dada456819c45230012103650ccc14a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dd31a315488bb0669257b83dd88b9809&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b7715667f5fca178f0988984e932ecfb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4b9f6a4a440ccb40e47c326ca6dd9346&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e91ce385a4956221ce891caa7456655a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-65c6beab51324e055f4a39b388e2eefe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2dc33cf2a90bf53c26226e44bc285c22&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-36de8c99d97d234e12244c240c45f156&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c2474d83c9e01bbd20c6e68744a2dad5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b3d901ee668c4fdbd518454aa3ebea3a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9f4d152d83c514f926b18413e065c2fa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f2b8be67edef23560656776b89947c10&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-edbbe2e207a7e0a28611a2a16fa2845f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-780f90d656277126a05ed136a084fd77&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d9b29e7a7839d7ff2b29e72fb4912618&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6b867cec4c5eed3b10e431cbd4078dee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bec9e867c8de5a0beabd70ea9209c1a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8e89a2540c525a104b0a1a5513347a8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ad5d126f417014eb5c7a07a85db48d1d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3c9d162accf67a3761df6b1c9113e193&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-545c19428427ece2c838e352e759e388&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5c804699375feba4c866cc3a1bc00211&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7f716359c14483f9be36a73861d75008&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c8df31d65b128b9d70b82bb8af257332</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/Documento sem título.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/Bula Humalog.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/NOVORAPID _ BulasMed.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_1778357531609.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_fiasp.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/The Discovery and Development.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/cengiz-beck-2026-use-of-inhaled-insulin-with-automated-insulin-delivery-systems.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/Documento sem título.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/glicemias capilares.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Metas glicêmicas/metas cuidado do diabetes.pdf</data>
