<node id="Diretriz da Sociedade Brasileira de Diabetes">
  <data key="d0">Diretriz da Sociedade Brasileira de Diabetes</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Diretriz da Sociedade Brasileira de Diabetes is a comprehensive clinical guideline issued by the Sociedade Brasileira de Diabetes (Brazilian Diabetes Society). The document serves as the official reference for health professionals in Brazil on both the diagnosis and management of diabetes mellitus, providing standardized criteria for screening, case definition, and classification of the disease.

In the diagnostic section, the guideline delineates the contemporary diagnostic criteria for diabetes mellitus, including recommended glucose thresholds, laboratory testing protocols, and algorithms for early detection. It also outlines screening strategies for high‑risk populations, advises on the use of glycated hemoglobin (HbA1c) versus fasting plasma glucose, and provides guidance on interpreting borderline results to ensure timely and accurate identification of new cases.

The management portion of the Diretriz da Sociedade Brasileira de Diabetes gives detailed recommendations on insulin therapy, emphasizing proper injection techniques and device selection. It specifies appropriate needle lengths for subcutaneous administration, stresses the importance of rotating injection sites to prevent lipohypertrophy, and describes best practices for insulin preparation, storage, and handling of injection devices. The guideline furthermore advocates intensive patient education on injection technique, encouraging clinicians to train patients thoroughly to improve adherence, minimize injection‑related complications, and optimize glycemic control.&lt;SEP&gt;Diretriz da Sociedade Brasileira de Diabetes is the official guideline issued by the Sociedade Brasileira de Diabetes containing the diabetes classification.&lt;SEP&gt;Diretriz da Sociedade Brasileira de Diabetes is a guideline document outlining recommendations for diabetes classification.&lt;SEP&gt;Diretriz da Sociedade Brasileira de Diabetes is a guideline document published by the Sociedade Brasileira de Diabetes.&lt;SEP&gt;Diretriz da Sociedade Brasileira de Diabetes is the guideline document that classifies diabetes types and recommends genetic testing.</data>
