<node id="Prega Subcutânea">
  <data key="d0">Prega Subcutânea</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Prega Subcutânea is the subcutaneous skin‑fold technique performed before inserting the needle for insulina injection.&lt;SEP&gt;Prega Subcutânea is the method of creating a skin fold to ensure subcutaneous insulin injection.&lt;SEP&gt;Gentle pinch of the skin performed before inserting the needle to ensure proper subcutaneous delivery.&lt;SEP&gt;The light pinch of skin performed with thumb and index finger to lift subcutaneous tissue before insulin injection.&lt;SEP&gt;A subcutaneous skin fold technique used to create a skin pocket before insulin injection.&lt;SEP&gt;The technique of pinching a fold of skin to create a subcutaneous space for needle insertion.</data>
