<node id="Randomized Controlled Trial">
  <data key="d0">Randomized Controlled Trial</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Randomized Controlled Trial (RCT) is an experimental study design in which participants are assigned to intervention or control groups by chance, allowing researchers to evaluate the efficacy or effectiveness of a given treatment while minimizing bias.  By employing random allocation, the design creates comparable groups and supports causal inference about the impact of the intervention under investigation.

In the field of diabetes research, RCTs have been used to assess a wide range of interventions.  One example is a trial that examined the effect of proper insulin injection‑technique training on glycemic control.  Other RCTs have compared pharmacologic agents, such as the APIDRA insulin analogue versus other insulin comparators in both type 1 and type 2 diabetes populations.  A double‑blind, dose‑response RCT specifically compared Levemir® with insulin NPH in pregnant women with type 1 diabetes, illustrating how the design can accommodate specialized populations and blinded dosing regimens.

Beyond drug evaluations, RCTs serve as the gold‑standard framework for testing digital health solutions for diabetes.  Although many diabetes‑related mobile applications lack rigorous RCT evidence, the design remains the preferred method for establishing the effectiveness of such digital interventions.  Overall, the randomized controlled trial is the principal methodological approach for objectively measuring the outcomes of clinical and behavioral interventions across diverse diabetes contexts.&lt;SEP&gt;Randomized controlled trial is a study design that compares interventions under controlled conditions.&lt;SEP&gt;Randomized Controlled Trial is a research method referenced as being conducted with CGM in adults with type 1 diabetes.&lt;SEP&gt;Randomized controlled trials are experimental studies cited for comparing GDM screening methods and treatment approaches.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e480a6a15b0d8e7069746e3f3f788f80&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3f0b85829c02f82470489f3f5e487996&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6a7ca48868f79f7be782198d67ffefd0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-42ddf181cf4422a3b24643a2252d99b0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b4d7abd3e1e5418ee5a931e28a18e8ad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b4b76ae88b212b3a0a4d05c250e05e0c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-41b7df11ccfb12f819e6f60481970587&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5227749196a4c9226dba64a500d84b3a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-345ad64f464691cc28341ccd246032db&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aff91698679a52cd7b07563b7b2627a3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-36ddeaa53bc38bee375d7ac6d71485d4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-59dd4faf2a2706d073fdb93e1a29da81</data>
