</node>
<node id="Injecting Sites">
  <data key="d0">Injecting Sites</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Anatomical locations on the body chosen for insulin administration.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e480a6a15b0d8e7069746e3f3f788f80</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Cópia de Técnicas de aplicação de insulina.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786298835</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Subcutaneous Injection">
  <data key="d0">Subcutaneous Injection</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Subcutaneous injection is a medical route of drug administration in which a medication is deposited into the layer of fatty tissue located directly beneath the skin. Because the subcutaneous layer has relatively low blood flow, the drug is absorbed more slowly than with intramuscular injection, producing a steady and predictable pharmacokinetic profile that is useful for therapies requiring gradual systemic uptake and prolonged or controlled action. This slower, prolonged effect also makes the route suitable for many biologic and peptide therapeutics.

The subcutaneous route is the standard method for delivering a wide range of diabetes‑related and other biologic agents. All major insulin formulations are routinely given subcutaneously, including rapid‑acting insulins such as Humalog Mix 25 KwikPen and Fiasp, basal insulins such as Levemir®, long‑acting analogues like insulin glargine (Lantus®) and insulin degludec (Tresiba®), as well as the concentrated insulin Toujeo 300 U/mL. Other commonly cited products are the pegfilgrastim biologic BASAGLAR (Pegfilgrastim) with its prefilled KwikPen, the recombinant leptin analogue metreleptin, and various human insulin preparations such as Novolin® R and Humulin R. These agents are specifically indicated for subcutaneous injection to achieve the gradual absorption and extended duration needed for their therapeutic goals.

Typical anatomical sites for a subcutaneous injection are areas with sufficient subcutaneous fat: the abdomen, the thigh, the upper arm (particularly the deltoid region), and the gluteal region. Selection of the injection site is guided by patient preference, clinical guidelines, and rotation schedules designed to minimize local tissue irritation, lipodystrophy, cutaneous amyloidosis, and other skin complications that can arise from repeated injections. Proper technique—including the use of an appropriate needle length for the chosen device and ensuring the needle penetrates only to the fatty layer—helps place the medication correctly and achieve the intended therapeutic effect.

In practice, subcutaneous injection requires compatible syringes or prefilled devices and needles that match the formulation’s viscosity and volume. Healthcare providers advise patients on site rotation, needle disposal, and monitoring for local adverse reactions. When performed correctly, subcutaneous injection provides a reliable, convenient, and relatively safe method for delivering a broad spectrum of medications that benefit from slow, sustained systemic exposure.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e480a6a15b0d8e7069746e3f3f788f80&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-26c5ab6d7b3b32c5f6aca2b58489782a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d9f7234865211afc5d8343294b276d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8abf9336f83edf5c92071da1032dc483&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a8768fa32f88d682aa4ddf677297047e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5de4e99a192602fe98c8b7e8e270a49c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-67563459bb64c390a40207da52944afd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-048d8fafb712e12cec45f2d3ec2c1e3b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e590341aac73dca916e560c2df9e60e0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bbae57922175913b7c36c594b4673fa2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cc9821850f5a0f8be1e4dd3fd0df6fcf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f14ce019f10c2a88765380143498ba5b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3db0edd23b6b502ccbbf62bfd601ce68&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3a279eef99c9c70338c74ffc7b4e260e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d96761d60c65f05f1530bc19b144cf1b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bf25fca295be60e28b7c7d3103f722fc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4ce520f0fe7dc4a6c79f92a25dfaff19&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1ee5400065df79b02b6c04efc0f4854d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-465ad8b77c1c2a2a179062da20337ff5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2f4f01a72f35d6db3ff333e64f8400ce&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bc2aa5d85d666eabc9dbaa5d2ecfe874&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cedd8e88a8d35eade68ce02222b9e276&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0955cb70a6ce135722726162a9811e78&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-df616353e032c899b02bfa4368bc2667&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-779af610d7298ce98490962cd90b4e76&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-577779892c0d463cd6bb1966b8a8ce2d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8ac99e7359716e2cecc2ec93159218b6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c96221c60c19f02ac6efa6a987b1e15b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ad5d126f417014eb5c7a07a85db48d1d</data>
