</node>
<node id="Rotação dos Locais de Aplicação de Insulina">
  <data key="d0">Rotação dos Locais de Aplicação de Insulina</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Rotação dos Locais de Aplicação de Insulina is the practice of alternating insulin injection sites to reduce glycemic variability and lipodistrofia.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0b4dfd5f7bda9f876ccb805f6f77f34e</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Cópia de Técnicas de aplicação de insulina.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786298836</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Variabilidade Glicêmica">
  <data key="d0">Variabilidade Glicêmica</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Variabilidade Glicêmica denotes fluctuations in blood glucose levels associated with inconsistent insulin absorption.&lt;SEP&gt;Variabilidade Glicêmica measures the percentage variation of Glicemia throughout the day.&lt;SEP&gt;Glycemic variability, a measure of fluctuations in blood glucose levels.&lt;SEP&gt;Variabilidade glicêmica refers to fluctuations in glucose levels throughout the day.&lt;SEP&gt;Variabilidade glicêmica indicates how much blood glucose rises and falls throughout the day.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0b4dfd5f7bda9f876ccb805f6f77f34e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bcba435392a61e072dfaad9195e42ed7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c2d6e4597425d2a83c3efcd9ca07f65c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-82e0d8e22a06c73855abed11561ce467&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-12999315830b302d973dd1908eab1e12</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Cópia de Técnicas de aplicação de insulina.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Documento sem título.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1786368415</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Lipodistrofia">
  <data key="d0">Lipodistrofia</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Lipodistrofia is a localized alteration of the skin and sub‑cutaneous tissue that occurs when insulin injections are repeatedly administered in the same area, most frequently in individuals with type 1 diabetes. The condition encompasses two opposite phenotypes: lipohypertrophy, an excessive accumulation of fat, and lipoatrophy, a loss of sub‑cutaneous fat. Clinically, affected sites may develop hard nodules, thickened skin, or palpable lumps, reflecting the tissue’s response to chronic mechanical trauma and repeated exposure to insulin‑containing formulations.  

Because the altered tissue can impair the normal absorption of insulin, lipodistrofia often leads to unpredictable glycemic control and may increase the risk of hyperglycemia. Delayed or erratic local insulin uptake can compromise the effectiveness of therapy, potentially necessitating adjustments in dose or injection technique.  

Lipodistrofia is documented as an injection‑site adverse effect for several insulin products, including APIDRA SOLOSTAR, FIASP®, Levemir®, and Novolin® R Penfill®. Although some sources classify it as an uncommon skin/sub‑cutaneous disorder, epidemiological studies indicate that a majority of insulin‑using patients experience some degree of tissue alteration, underscoring its status as a frequent complication of insulin therapy.  

Prevention and management focus on diligent rotation of injection sites and avoidance of areas that already display signs of lipohypertrophy or lipoatrophy. Regular inspection of injection regions and patient education on proper site‑rotation techniques are essential strategies to reduce the incidence of lipodistrofia and to maintain reliable insulin absorption.&lt;SEP&gt;Lipodystrophy is a skin condition risk associated with repeated subcutaneous injection sites.&lt;SEP&gt;Lipodistrofia is a change in skin tissue where insulin is frequently injected, characterized by localized alterations.&lt;SEP&gt;A condition occurring in 42% to 64% of patients at the catheter site rotation associated with insulin pump therapy.&lt;SEP&gt;A dermatological complication (lipoatrophy or lipo‑hypertrófia) linked to unpredictable insulin absorption in SICI users.&lt;SEP&gt;Lipodistrofia encompasses inherited or acquired disorders characterized by loss of adipose tissue.&lt;SEP&gt;Lipodistrofia refers to abnormal loss or distribution of body fat, identified by low skin‑fold values or densitometry ratios.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0b4dfd5f7bda9f876ccb805f6f77f34e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e490a7e963a20e2221a8097b50073543&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-da4ea6b1580793801f801a34c92f1905&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-11cce86325de9748e794648198242578&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-da44554b006e6bd1b841f4246a054669&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-072d97721eef045503ec1dce0363b58e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-61cacf80ada6db26d2b975df763c137a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8ef35bd45e4ba8d20f4e9181011ccfcd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a247846b9ec5d44d0bcbe6c5f15599f8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aca0b919135813e1d5b772face36989d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9cd336474a2e9457985162b1ddb4b603&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e212a20942ed5387efe96e92bdb4ba98&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-15a498084b9a0c4cfcd9aa9553e12a14&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b060d4f68031bd35dfafc19eadf1e9fe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e3418c4ee80182ca29214dd54b0d9647&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-04b345bc26ec7f5d7c9db8c6004a50a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0e7689ca0fc736d9eae94256f73fed52&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3a70857656e32cc73aaa270a75eb33af&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-45ee3dcb366c1301c9fb1d2ce9f323c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-922791f49d1bf928fe4f02ddd336927b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a49c8461f43dc12d7df9c921efeb0465&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9bcc4202330d45ebfca8f79c3d4998b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8a68ba1e8cc1defda76cde0eff9592e6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d01ed6a801b11c1b53f4668059c1f9cb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3396320470ee682ec5cc4f70ab001ef4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d6101c469482b48e341b4095a54907fd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7f2714936869e55e840f5294caefeaee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0b4034f7cf7e37425b7c76f5e0f9fd11&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0689fd73d2061ee466b9b90e03bda141&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-786395f3716fb61a79fd183c63e1a9d6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a7ca732691e1cbcafd65e378b8d80144&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-929e31613caadc967412041c8c2155b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-55f8c8b2b40633cf37993b620002b889&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-336a2f2c9b510e23c35be95e2ff7a72a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c2d6e4597425d2a83c3efcd9ca07f65c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ed325288512881a80fa42dba504c4bff&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fee32f1fb0c848b0799071a86119b142</data>
