<node id="Dispositivo com Caneta">
  <data key="d0">Dispositivo com Caneta</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Dispositivo com caneta is an insulin pen device evaluated for patient adherence, clinical benefits, and quality‑of‑life improvements compared with syringes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8d870035815524d8e4f6b0d6b05e5c2a</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Cópia de Técnicas de aplicação de insulina.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786298838</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Seringa com Agulha Fixa">
  <data key="d0">Seringa com Agulha Fixa</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Seringa com agulha fixa is a syringe type recommended for insulin injection due to better dose precision, less dead space, and ability to mix insulins.&lt;SEP&gt;Syringe with fixed needle that registers even, odd and fractional doses, has no dead space, can hold two insulin types, and is common in clinical practice.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8d870035815524d8e4f6b0d6b05e5c2a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8041b0c4fb8dc726149807b6b3e61287</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Cópia de Técnicas de aplicação de insulina.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Armazenamento e Transporte/transporte e conservação Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-20201.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786302746</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Seringa Graduada em Unidades Internacionais">
  <data key="d0">Seringa Graduada em Unidades Internacionais</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Seringa graduada em unidades internacionais is a syringe graduated in international units, recommended to avoid dose errors.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8d870035815524d8e4f6b0d6b05e5c2a</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Cópia de Técnicas de aplicação de insulina.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786298838</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Seringa Graduada em mL">
  <data key="d0">Seringa Graduada em mL</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Seringa graduada em mL is a syringe graduated in milliliters, which the guideline advises not to use because of high risk of dosing errors.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8d870035815524d8e4f6b0d6b05e5c2a</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Cópia de Técnicas de aplicação de insulina.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786298838</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Instrument SF-36">
  <data key="d0">Instrument SF-36</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Instrument SF‑36 is a health‑related quality‑of‑life questionnaire used to assess improvements associated with insulin pen use.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8d870035815524d8e4f6b0d6b05e5c2a</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Cópia de Técnicas de aplicação de insulina.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786298838</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Insulina de Ação Intermediária">
  <data key="d0">Insulina de Ação Intermediária</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Insulina de ação intermediária is a type of insulin that can be combined in the same syringe with rapid‑acting insulin for immediate or later use.&lt;SEP&gt;Intermediate‑acting insulin used in basal‑bolus regimens together with Fiasp®.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8d870035815524d8e4f6b0d6b05e5c2a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-add4469fba80232b7c0742f24c0914c9</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Cópia de Técnicas de aplicação de insulina.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_fiasp.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786316112</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Insulina de Ação Rápida">
  <data key="d0">Insulina de Ação Rápida</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Insulina de ação rápida is a fast‑acting insulin that may be mixed with intermediate‑acting insulin in a single syringe.&lt;SEP&gt;Rapid‑acting insulin analogs, category that includes Fiasp®.&lt;SEP&gt;Insulina de Ação Rápida refers to rapid‑acting insulin preparations that may be co‑administered with Levemir® requiring dose or schedule adjustments.&lt;SEP&gt;Insulina de Ação Rápida describes insulin formulations, like Novolin® R, that act quickly to lower blood glucose.&lt;SEP&gt;Insulina de Ação Rápida refers to rapid‑acting insulin analogues such as lispro, aspart and glulisina used in basal‑bolus therapy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8d870035815524d8e4f6b0d6b05e5c2a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-add4469fba80232b7c0742f24c0914c9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8a68ba1e8cc1defda76cde0eff9592e6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0689fd73d2061ee466b9b90e03bda141&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-95c81e7ab8160456d9a63a9e0868205b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Cópia de Técnicas de aplicação de insulina.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_fiasp.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/Insulinoterapia – Diretriz da Sociedade Brasileira de Diabetes – Ed. 2024.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786331405</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Insulina Bifásica">
  <data key="d0">Insulina Bifásica</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Insulina bifásica is a biphasic insulin formulation that requires proper homogenization to maintain concentration stability.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8d870035815524d8e4f6b0d6b05e5c2a</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Cópia de Técnicas de aplicação de insulina.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786298838</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Movimento Suave">
  <data key="d0">Movimento Suave</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Movimento suave refers to the recommended 20 gentle mixing strokes performed with the palms or pendulum to homogenize insulin suspensions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8d870035815524d8e4f6b0d6b05e5c2a</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Cópia de Técnicas de aplicação de insulina.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786298838</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Homogeneização de Insulina">
  <data key="d0">Homogeneização de Insulina</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Homogeneização de insulina is the process of gently mixing insulin suspensions to reduce concentration variability.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8d870035815524d8e4f6b0d6b05e5c2a</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Cópia de Técnicas de aplicação de insulina.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786298838</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Estudo Experimental">
  <data key="d0">Estudo Experimental</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">Estudo experimental is a study that evaluated the efficacy of mixing insulin NPH from five manufacturers with fewer than the recommended mixing movements.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8d870035815524d8e4f6b0d6b05e5c2a</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Cópia de Técnicas de aplicação de insulina.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786298838</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Estudo de Clamp Euglicêmico">
  <data key="d0">Estudo de Clamp Euglicêmico</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">Estudo de clamp euglicêmico is a clamp study with eleven type‑1 diabetes patients comparing pharmacokinetics and pharmacodynamics of resuspended versus non‑resuspended insulin NPH.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8d870035815524d8e4f6b0d6b05e5c2a</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Cópia de Técnicas de aplicação de insulina.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786298839</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Seringa com Agulha Removível">
  <data key="d0">Seringa com Agulha Removível</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Seringa com agulha removível is a syringe type that the guideline advises to avoid because fixed‑needle syringes provide better dose precision.&lt;SEP&gt;Syringe with removable needle, graduated, capable of holding up to 100 insulin units.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8d870035815524d8e4f6b0d6b05e5c2a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8041b0c4fb8dc726149807b6b3e61287</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Cópia de Técnicas de aplicação de insulina.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Armazenamento e Transporte/transporte e conservação Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-20201.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786302746</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Agulha de 6 mm">
  <data key="d0">Agulha de 6 mm</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Agulha de 6 mm is a 6‑millimetre needle whose use in children triples the risk of intramuscular injection compared with a 4‑mm needle.&lt;SEP&gt;Agulha de 6 mm is a short needle option available for fixed‑needle syringes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8d870035815524d8e4f6b0d6b05e5c2a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b64741e11a7d852f462b1269fabfbe43</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Cópia de Técnicas de aplicação de insulina.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786298839</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Insulina U100">
  <data key="d0">Insulina U100</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Insulina U100 refers to insulin concentration of 100 units per milliliter, for which syringes are graduated in appropriate units.&lt;SEP&gt;Insulin formulation containing 100 units per millilitre, intended for use with insulin pens.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8d870035815524d8e4f6b0d6b05e5c2a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aafda750d4900a464b1ac0c9bad5ba05</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Cópia de Técnicas de aplicação de insulina.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786301828</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Diabetes Tipo 1">
  <data key="d0">Diabetes Tipo 1</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Diabetes Tipo 1 is an autoimmune, chronic form of diabetes mellitus characterized by immune‑mediated destruction of the pancreatic β‑cells, which eliminates endogenous insulin production and creates a persistent insulin deficiency. The loss of β‑cell function leads to both hyperglycaemia and a risk of hypoglycaemia, making precise glucose management essential. Although it can affect individuals of any age, the condition is especially prevalent among children and adolescents.

Because the body can no longer synthesize insulin, patients with Diabetes Tipo 1 require lifelong exogenous insulin replacement. Standard management involves continuous insulin therapy, most commonly delivered through multiple daily injections or an insulin pump. Rapid‑acting formulations such as Novolin® R are frequently used for mealtime coverage, while long‑acting analogues (e.g., insulin glargine) may be employed for basal needs. Effective care also demands careful monitoring of carbohydrate intake and frequent adjustment of insulin doses to maintain an appropriate insulin‑carbohydrate balance, even when food consumption is limited. Guidance on safe exercise is important, as physical activity can markedly influence glucose levels in fully insulinized individuals.

Diabetes Tipo 1 is a frequent focus of clinical research, particularly in adult cohorts. Studies have employed clamp techniques, compared insulin glargine with human insulin, and included the disease in trials such as APIDRA to evaluate the efficacy, safety, and pharmacodynamics of various insulin formulations. Outcome data from these investigations underscore the disease’s relevance in therapeutic development and comparative effectiveness research.

Epidemiologically, individuals with Diabetes Tipo 1 have been reported to exhibit a higher prevalence of lipo‑hipertrofia, a condition involving abnormal fat deposition. This association, together with the metabolic challenges of the disease, highlights the need for comprehensive, multidisciplinary management that addresses both glycaemic control and related metabolic complications.&lt;SEP&gt;Diabetes Tipo 1 is an autoimmune form of diabetes characterized by severe insulin deficiency.&lt;SEP&gt;Diabetes Tipo 1 is an autoimmune form of diabetes typically diagnosed in younger patients and confirmed by positive autoantibodies.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8d870035815524d8e4f6b0d6b05e5c2a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a976e1642df27c488174759a35ca23f2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-46c9571a4df1570d4a097dc949f512cd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-02780a8bc1d372cc47e0ccf2eaab1a99&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-87576da8269707f5f8d929b71470e023&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-61cacf80ada6db26d2b975df763c137a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a247846b9ec5d44d0bcbe6c5f15599f8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f46c503a378e6c69618036a038672417&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b65ee62ad12239ddc729c50a1aef854c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2479751a6475c09415f0d79759db091d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-29710f08f3e10bba4a464e8b4da1917c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fb620bf44b37187faceacd0405c4a819&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50719bcc88f4515ec825b9d5a7aba107&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-45ee3dcb366c1301c9fb1d2ce9f323c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b65a4249ac93aec086cb333ed1507ea7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0689fd73d2061ee466b9b90e03bda141&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-55f8c8b2b40633cf37993b620002b889&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f645bd7019e94151caaff47d6cbfcaf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5dce7a759a9de18a4d1bcc77a071fbe2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea6df8d05eb3fdd356a1eaef16a26dd5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-72da6fb8b6a9ed059d146b43a3174f90&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ed325288512881a80fa42dba504c4bff</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Cópia de Técnicas de aplicação de insulina.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/LANTUS _ BulasMed.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Basaglar.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_1778357531609.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_apidra.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/Documento sem título.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/Orientacoes_Hipoglicemia_SBD_transcricao.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Documento sem título.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Diagnóstico de diabetes mellitus.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786373021</data>
