<node id="4 mm Needle">
  <data key="d0">4 mm Needle</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">4 mm needles are among the short lengths recommended for insulin injection, especially for children and adolescents.&lt;SEP&gt;A short insulin injection needle of length 4 mm described as safe, well‑tolerated, and suitable for adults, children, and adolescents, especially when used with a subcutaneous fold.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-26c5ab6d7b3b32c5f6aca2b58489782a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ae9010ed1abd5a5160b82713c862d22f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Cópia de Técnicas de aplicação de insulina.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1786299839</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="5 mm Needle">
  <data key="d0">5 mm Needle</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">5 mm needles are among the short lengths recommended for insulin injection, especially for children and adolescents.&lt;SEP&gt;A short insulin injection needle of length 5 mm mentioned as part of the range of short needles effective for adults.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-26c5ab6d7b3b32c5f6aca2b58489782a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ae9010ed1abd5a5160b82713c862d22f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Cópia de Técnicas de aplicação de insulina.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1786299839</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="6 mm Needle">
  <data key="d0">6 mm Needle</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">6 mm needles are indicated for adults and children, with angle adjustments depending on subcutaneous tissue availability.&lt;SEP&gt;6 mm Needle is a short insulin needle length considered safest and least painful, recommended for use with fixed‑needle syringes.&lt;SEP&gt;A short insulin injection needle of length 6 mm mentioned as part of the range of short needles effective for adults and required for children.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-26c5ab6d7b3b32c5f6aca2b58489782a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e4654b5e9fa02cf051c2d5ebc846c5d6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ae9010ed1abd5a5160b82713c862d22f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Cópia de Técnicas de aplicação de insulina.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1786299834</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="8 mm Needle">
  <data key="d0">8 mm Needle</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">8 mm needles are indicated for adults, with angle adjustments to avoid intramuscular injection in patients with low subcutaneous tissue.&lt;SEP&gt;A longer insulin injection needle of length 8 mm noted as an option for adults with very low subcutaneous fat when a slightly larger needle is easier to handle.&lt;SEP&gt;An 8 mm Needle is a disposable injection needle length compatible with the NovoRapid FlexPen® device.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-26c5ab6d7b3b32c5f6aca2b58489782a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ae9010ed1abd5a5160b82713c862d22f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-048d8fafb712e12cec45f2d3ec2c1e3b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Cópia de Técnicas de aplicação de insulina.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/NOVORAPID _ BulasMed.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786305904</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Needle &gt;12 mm">
  <data key="d0">Needle &gt;12 mm</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Needles longer than 12 mm are prohibited for insulin injection because of high risk of intramuscular delivery.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-26c5ab6d7b3b32c5f6aca2b58489782a</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Cópia de Técnicas de aplicação de insulina.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786298844</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Intramuscular Injection">
  <data key="d0">Intramuscular Injection</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Intramuscular Injection is a method of delivering medication directly into muscle tissue, typically performed with a needle of appropriate length inserted at a specific angle to reach the muscular layer. This route allows drugs to be absorbed into the bloodstream more quickly than subcutaneous administration because of the rich vascular supply of muscle.

When the medication in question is insulin, intramuscular injection is generally regarded as an undesirable and risky route. Delivering insulin into muscle tissue produces rapid absorption, which can precipitate severe hypoglycemia, especially if the dose is not carefully adjusted. For this reason, clinical guidelines advise that insulin should not be given intramuscularly; the practice is considered a mistake to be avoided, and specific insulin products such as Levemir® list the intramuscular route as prohibited.

Despite the prevailing consensus, some sources note that intramuscular injection may be employed in emergency situations or under explicit medical supervision when other routes are unavailable. In particular, a limited number of references describe intramuscular administration as an alternative route for Humulin R, though they also acknowledge the associated risks and the preference for subcutaneous delivery. Consequently, while intramuscular injection can technically be used to deliver insulin, it is recommended only in exceptional circumstances and with careful clinical oversight.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-26c5ab6d7b3b32c5f6aca2b58489782a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d9f7234865211afc5d8343294b276d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8abf9336f83edf5c92071da1032dc483&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-74b3171b97fd80965359afadc0af9312&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b5b4c60b3de8c56d9ab869d868345fb7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cedd8e88a8d35eade68ce02222b9e276&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0955cb70a6ce135722726162a9811e78&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-577779892c0d463cd6bb1966b8a8ce2d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8ac99e7359716e2cecc2ec93159218b6</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Cópia de Técnicas de aplicação de insulina.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Documento sem título.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786319756</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Pen">
  <data key="d0">Pen</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Pens are insulin delivery devices preferred for very low dose adjustments, especially in children.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-26c5ab6d7b3b32c5f6aca2b58489782a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0b9c41c968bcc1d46185583661e8f989</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Cópia de Técnicas de aplicação de insulina.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786298844</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="0.5U Pen">
  <data key="d0">0.5U Pen</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Pens with 0.5 U graduation allow fine dose adjustments for patients requiring very low insulin amounts.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-26c5ab6d7b3b32c5f6aca2b58489782a</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Cópia de Técnicas de aplicação de insulina.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786298844</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Syringe">
  <data key="d0">Syringe</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Syringe is a medical device employed to draw, hold, and inject insulin into the body. It consists of a barrel that contains a measured dose of insulin and a needle, which may be fixed to the barrel or removable, that delivers the medication subcutaneously. The device is commonly used with a fine‑gauge needle to promote patient comfort and accurate dosing.

Insulin syringes are available in disposable forms with typical capacities of 30 units or 50 units. The barrel is graduated in increments of 0.5 U or 1 U, allowing precise selection of the required dose; markings correspond to these increments. In Brazil, the syringe is the most common device for insulin administration and is graduated in units (U100) that match the standard insulin concentration. Although the intended graduation is in units, some syringes are incorrectly marked in milliliters, which can lead to dosing errors. Various needle configurations exist, ranging from fixed‑needle designs to removable needles, and the device may be supplied with different gauge sizes to suit individual preferences.

Proper injection technique with a syringe includes inserting the needle at the appropriate angle—generally 90 degrees for most subcutaneous sites—pressing the plunger only after the needle is fully inserted, and observing a brief dwell time after dose delivery to ensure complete absorption. Reuse of syringes or needles is discouraged because it can compromise sterility and dosing accuracy.

Syringes are frequently listed as part of travel supplies for individuals who need to carry insulin while away from home, ensuring that they have a reliable means of administration.

A specific safety precaution concerns the use of syringes with the SoloStar (Caneta SoloStar) pen: syringes must not be used to withdraw or transfer Toujeo 300 U/mL insulin from this pen, as the high‑concentration formulation requires dedicated delivery devices.&lt;SEP&gt;A syringe is a device used to inject Novolin® R and must be disposed of in appropriate collection containers.&lt;SEP&gt;A syringe is a device required to draw and administer Novolin® R from its vial.&lt;SEP&gt;Disposable syringes compatible with subcutaneous administration are required for delivering insulin; the quantity needed depends on the prescribed dose, and syringes must not be shared between people.&lt;SEP&gt;Syringe is a device used to inject insulin subcutaneously.&lt;SEP&gt;A device used to manually administer a correction dose of insulin.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-26c5ab6d7b3b32c5f6aca2b58489782a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-191286ebd759321d40620f77c84ef5a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ebdb9452013f0e340884677832714553&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e4654b5e9fa02cf051c2d5ebc846c5d6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ae9010ed1abd5a5160b82713c862d22f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-03a1de93a53fbcb513268c123e2c5a16&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2a0a3f492aa5ef7771b2246547cb5f02&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-622f3feb1f15564393e91cefc71256ec&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8abf9336f83edf5c92071da1032dc483&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d8310c065da1c624d58d9a0a8e9ff7d4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1b1b73e9b7285819a4ba5caa6fdfa785&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b5b4c60b3de8c56d9ab869d868345fb7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4d795dc393eb02c6418957ee1678504f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-45d489de28e8fda3c3be3bb09ab29eb2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3397508bdfddde019cb1dfdcfb352435&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d7223c781e745e72311fccfcdd58583&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1ee5400065df79b02b6c04efc0f4854d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-73559dc5d86ea52a348d603482e056e9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-df616353e032c899b02bfa4368bc2667&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8ac99e7359716e2cecc2ec93159218b6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e91ce385a4956221ce891caa7456655a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-65c6beab51324e055f4a39b388e2eefe</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Cópia de Técnicas de aplicação de insulina.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Documento sem título.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Armazenamento e Transporte/transporte e conservação Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-20201.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Basaglar.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Toujeo.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
