</node>
<node id="Lipodystrophy">
  <data key="d0">Lipodystrophy</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Lipodystrophy (injection‑site form) is a localized alteration of subcutaneous tissue that commonly develops as an adverse skin reaction to repeated insulin injections when proper site rotation and technique are not observed. The condition encompasses a spectrum that includes **lipohypertrophy**, characterized by localized thickening, hard nodules or palpable masses of fat, and **lipoatrophy**, in which loss of subcutaneous tissue creates visible depressions. Both manifestations can impair insulin delivery by delaying absorption and altering pharmacokinetics, leading to hyperglycemia and suboptimal glycemic control. Lipodystrophy has been reported with many insulin products, ranging from rapid‑acting analogues such as Humalog, NovoRapid, Fiasp®, Apidra Solostar, and BASAGLAR KWIKPEN to long‑acting formulations like Lantus, Levemir®, and human regular insulin (Novolin® R). Reported incidence of lipohypertrophy varies widely, with estimates from about 1 % to 10 % of patients using certain analogues. Risk factors include reuse of syringes or disposable needles, concentrating a single insulin formulation in one area, and failure to rotate injection sites. Prevention and management focus on systematic site rotation, using a fresh needle for each injection, and avoiding repeated administration of the same insulin product in one location, thereby preserving normal subcutaneous architecture, ensuring more consistent insulin absorption, and improving overall diabetes control.

Lipodystrophy (systemic form) denotes a group of rare disorders characterized by abnormal distribution of body fat that may involve **peripheral loss (lipoatrophy)**, **central or visceral accumulation (lipohypertrophy)**, or a combination of both. These disorders can be congenital or acquired and are distinct from the injection‑site phenomenon. Systemic lipodystrophy is associated with genetic mutations affecting adipocyte development and metabolism, as well as with certain medications—most notably antiretroviral drugs used in HIV treatment—and with HIV infection itself. Clinical manifestations include marked peripheral fat wasting, prominent dorsocervical fat pads, metabolic complications such as insulin resistance, dyslipidemia, and hepatic steatosis. Because the condition reflects a generalized abnormality of adipose tissue rather than a localized reaction, its management involves addressing the underlying cause, metabolic complications, and, in some cases, using leptin replacement or other targeted therapies.&lt;SEP&gt;Lipodystrophy is a rare side effect associated with rapid‑acting insulin analogues in SICI users.&lt;SEP&gt;Lipodystrophy refers to changes in fat tissue at injection sites that can affect insulin absorption.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-26c5ab6d7b3b32c5f6aca2b58489782a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-35a8ffab5eb63600b93fb2c67160b5ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-525086e26636af026c417773a8f11a92&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e150bb4043de862453b3e96cf6cb663e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e89f1dbae629e925f06732cebf41df16&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4d26ce64e79b8c4a147140be2f9c63dd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d59c9bf7f429a82cbfd7083e36ff8f9a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-048d8fafb712e12cec45f2d3ec2c1e3b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f9e5c50e8a808c537075377966ae2ccd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6d0f18c80f8de2dee960a03599d12052&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4f079198593c1702b56062aa87e7801a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-22df77f7bf817d736d90608e62a11d84&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3db0edd23b6b502ccbbf62bfd601ce68&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d96761d60c65f05f1530bc19b144cf1b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3e50c145614f04be2319a31b74b80411&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6ca13e396b094f0c2f482892f220f538&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4ce520f0fe7dc4a6c79f92a25dfaff19&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fd94288932ad6675a1de2b46b3fd9128&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a2416b3e5e8ebc96cdb451a794fc78e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e8934881ec5ab7cfeb836126b3f0e8b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1ee5400065df79b02b6c04efc0f4854d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-51761473ea6fe17b9e098a6bf98636b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c95471c4c993fa3a499f99443ee7c922&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2dc2313c92b2af4132faaa4d41449eef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bc2aa5d85d666eabc9dbaa5d2ecfe874&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-14772c7de5db762c492a75a1c744dae6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7fdc648ec086061141581e27adde6fc4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-831f4bbfc884fc8e9679630a819083e9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0ace26fdb0244e3d0f714a007c9bbb51&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c68e2c07786710dd5250c6610f52b14d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9a6f9e10c0d4af5fff0338eb861f9c86&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dd396c45bc09fb646d156b4e69d328e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0955cb70a6ce135722726162a9811e78&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-73559dc5d86ea52a348d603482e056e9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-acaa1440ae268669e1894588bb9e37c2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-df616353e032c899b02bfa4368bc2667&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2cd48799a027437b9fe2e1a48b61cb3d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a1245bd9ff75c998b49dab861cc4cebf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-779af610d7298ce98490962cd90b4e76&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1e622f0079074cd1916470223d22aa66&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-577779892c0d463cd