</node>
<node id="Glicosímetro">
  <data key="d0">Glicosímetro</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Glicosímetro is a handheld instrument designed primarily to measure blood glucose levels in capillary blood. The device works with disposable biosensor test strips that contain an enzymatic or electrochemical system; when a strip is inserted, the meter detects the electrical signal generated by the reaction with glucose and automatically activates, often after verifying a security code embedded in the strip. The measured glucose concentration is then displayed as a numeric value, and many models also provide simple “LO” (low) or “HI” (high) indicators to alert the user to hypoglycemic or hyperglycemic readings. In clinical and self‑monitoring contexts, the glicosímetro is used to assess glycemia and to track glycemic variability over time, supporting diabetes management and treatment adjustments.

In addition to glucose, some versions of the glicosímetro are equipped to quantify the ketone body β‑hydroxybutyrate (β‑OHB) in blood, allowing simultaneous monitoring of both glucose and ketone levels. This capability is useful for detecting ketoacidosis or for athletes and individuals following low‑carbohydrate diets. Regardless of the specific analyte, the core functionality of the glicosímetro remains the rapid, point‑of‑care measurement of a biochemical substance in a small capillary blood sample, with results presented instantly on the device’s display.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d4cfc50689ef0b918230df31cb99e5e5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bcba435392a61e072dfaad9195e42ed7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e5570f88766511a4a62cbe9a2dff0bdb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b2ef71fb1a347df36dbb8ea8f4856bcb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8fe1b07f3c84733fcbfca023fbfd70e6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-82e0d8e22a06c73855abed11561ce467&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5dce7a759a9de18a4d1bcc77a071fbe2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1136d6aac4c2e881387a4db1a0f4a3a3</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/Orientacoes_Glicemia_SBD.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Documento sem título.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1786368559</data>
