<node id="Lanceta">
  <data key="d0">Lanceta</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Lanceta is a small needle used to prick the fingertip to obtain a blood drop for glucose testing.&lt;SEP&gt;Small sharp device used for skin puncture, often disposed with needles.&lt;SEP&gt;Lanceta is a disposable lancet used for glucose testing that must be discarded in a proper collector.&lt;SEP&gt;A single‑use needle inserted into the lancetador to perform the finger puncture.</data>
