<node id="Bomba De Insulina">
  <data key="d0">Bomba De Insulina</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Bomba De Insulina is a medical device designed for continuous subcutaneous insulin infusion to manage diabetes. It delivers rapid‑action insulin from a reservoir through an infusion set, providing a basal insulin rate that runs continuously throughout the day and allowing the user to program additional bolus or correction doses for meals and high blood‑glucose events. The pump can administer very small amounts of rapid‑acting insulin every few minutes, effectively replacing the multiple daily injections traditionally required for insulin therapy.

The device is powered by a standard AA battery housed under a removable battery cover and includes a clip for secure attachment to clothing. Its home screen displays status icons and data such as current basal rate, battery level, and alarm notifications, enabling the user to monitor proper functioning at a glance. Bomba De Insulina incorporates an Autoapagado (auto‑shutoff) function that can stop insulin delivery, and it also supports manual suspension, disconnection, and automatic suspension with subsequent re‑addition of insulin when needed.

In addition to basal and bolus delivery, the pump allows precise adjustments of basal rates and supports therapy guidelines that emphasize individualized insulin dosing. Alarms and alerts are built into the system to warn of occlusions, low reservoir volume, or other issues, ensuring safety and reliability during use. The device is referenced throughout therapy manuals and guidelines as a generic insulin‑pump platform for delivering insulin based on programmed parameters.

Overall, Bomba De Insulina functions as a comprehensive insulin‑pump therapy device, offering continuous, programmable insulin delivery, rapid‑acting insulin administration, battery‑operated portability, and robust monitoring features to support effective diabetes management.&lt;SEP&gt;Bomba De Insulina is an insulin pump artifact that delivers insulin continuously according to programmed basal patterns.&lt;SEP&gt;Bomba De Insulina is the insulin pump whose operation, settings, and functions are discussed throughout the guide.&lt;SEP&gt;Bomba De Insulina is the common name for continuous insulin infusion devices derived from the original SICI.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d4cfc50689ef0b918230df31cb99e5e5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cf725cb54eea97f946e1f27eae125a0b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d41e93e7754b06eedcc2e2a44afcb32&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-63f6eb3be969569b166fc1e5f7e7567f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-310d06ee583c6aa24af77816642d0ba7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a717b5a81dbba0bd3cf2aae23dc0e309&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1fa7ad1de214645f0e643708dc1efab8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-34da912924aa29d035c8cd1c3f4f6ae3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6c123ae434326de3ccfe03d252e5d267&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1255cfcf42afb2c6045de0d45b11e99d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-646b0d64191b72fd929f7fb514a8cb8c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d0a4d039b786601ed8a06d8adad50938&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7d6466bdd61e024e50acc3fed9a5f9f8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fb3bd140c8e2ac53cf1b45386cb861ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f3d0dd38cbfd29061a0c9916efb7c5d8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-da325dc5071cd02bfe55ffc2f9b79aa5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-505b4450257d1a728c397959b044ee97&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4ed0e4c13d1643a77d1d74092a8cda5a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50d9a787da93a3bf7ea1e315273b560c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4eaa74c3ef8165f52ddf18e17a240a9d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7cbaec668e54aa5cf462a7bd08d7813c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2fb90cfe4a3993c8a19c8fd291cc4d67&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-de8328f990d0902170699f76dac78b01&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d7305e2b34a4a57db2afea4935fe2fc2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e796e8f4bb4721a269775c3d2ef0c06a</data>
