  <data key="d5">1786300284</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Endovenous Injection">
  <data key="d0">Endovenous Injection</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Endovenous injection administers insulin directly into a vein, used only in emergency settings under medical supervision.&lt;SEP&gt;Endovenous Injection is the administration of insulin directly into a vein, used in emergencies.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1d9f7234865211afc5d8343294b276d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8abf9336f83edf5c92071da1032dc483</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Documento sem título.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1786300285</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Abdomen">
  <data key="d0">Abdomen</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">Abdomen is the central region of the torso and is one of the most frequently used sites for subcutaneous insulin administration. Health professionals recommend the abdomen because insulin injected there is absorbed more rapidly than at most other subcutaneous locations, providing a slightly faster onset of action that can be advantageous for precise glycemic control. The site is listed as a permissible injection location for a range of insulin products, including insulin glargine (e.g., Toujeo 300 U/mL), the biosimilar BASAGLAR and its KWIKPEN delivery system, as well as standard insulin pens.

For practical and safety reasons, the abdominal area is commonly divided into four quadrants, allowing patients to rotate injection sites within each quadrant. Systematic rotation helps reduce the risk of lipohypertrophy, maintains tissue health, and ensures consistent insulin absorption. Clinical guidance emphasizes this practice for both insulin pens and syringes.

In addition to insulin delivery, the abdomen serves as a typical placement region for continuous glucose monitoring (CGM) sensors, which are affixed to the skin to track interstitial glucose levels continuously. The site’s relatively flat surface and good blood flow make it suitable for both injection and sensor attachment.

Pregnant individuals using insulin are advised to observe special restrictions when injecting into the abdomen; healthcare providers may modify injection techniques or recommend alternative sites to accommodate physiological changes during pregnancy and to ensure maternal‑fetal safety.&lt;SEP&gt;Abdomen is a body region where subcutaneous APIDRA injection shows slightly faster absorption.&lt;SEP&gt;Abdomen is a body region commonly used for subcutaneous injection of APIDRA.&lt;SEP&gt;Abdomen is an injection site where APIDRA showed slightly faster absorption compared with other sites.&lt;SEP&gt;Abdomen is a body region where Levemir® may be injected subcutaneously.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1d9f7234865211afc5d8343294b276d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-191286ebd759321d40620f77c84ef5a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b91b40e47c97be1b62c0f3d271cd4efd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c0ec5707b6df65f1a6822e01b9bb3fb9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-35a8ffab5eb63600b93fb2c67160b5ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8abf9336f83edf5c92071da1032dc483&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-708e3c514f667dc9979cfa8df875e473&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4902fb11e4844af5cf6fd61f18b6e4ce&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0b9c41c968bcc1d46185583661e8f989&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f14ce019f10c2a88765380143498ba5b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3db0edd23b6b502ccbbf62bfd601ce68&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d96761d60c65f05f1530bc19b144cf1b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-133169995b3ab942fd96f1fdfe7269ad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7638273060df996ad502ec2fadfc9c82&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1ee5400065df79b02b6c04efc0f4854d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-465ad8b77c1c2a2a179062da20337ff5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7621ac447c9044986ade86ce5f9be201&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50719bcc88f4515ec825b9d5a7aba107&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cedd8e88a8d35eade68ce02222b9e276</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Documento sem título.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Basaglar.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Toujeo.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_apidra.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786317613</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Arms">
  <data key="d0">Arms</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">Arms refer to the upper limbs where insulin absorption is slower than the abdomen but faster than thighs and buttocks.&lt;SEP&gt;Arms are a peripheral injection site where insulin absorption is slower than the abdomen.&lt;SEP&gt;Recommended injection site on the posterior upper arm, three finger widths below the armpit fold and above the elbow.&lt;SEP&gt;Arms are listed as a recommended injection site for the insulin pen.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1d9f7234865211afc5d8343294b276d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8abf9336f83edf5c92071da1032dc483&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cc6a26a5d2c41087b58a0f7f71ad21cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7638273060df996ad502ec2fadfc9c82</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Documento sem título.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/insulinas em seringa.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Toujeo.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786313608</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Thighs">
  <data key="d0">Thighs</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">Thighs are a subcutaneous injection site with moderate insulin absorption speed.&lt;SEP&gt;Thighs are a peripheral injection site with moderate insulin absorption speed.&lt;SEP&gt;Thighs are a region of the body recommended as an injection site for subcutaneous insulin.&lt;SEP&gt;Thighs are listed as a recommended injection site for the insulin pen.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1d9f7234865211afc5d8343294b276d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8abf9336f83edf5c92071da1032dc483&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0b9c41c968bcc1d46185583661e8f989&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7638273060df996ad502ec2fadfc9c82</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Documento sem título.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Basaglar.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Toujeo.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786313609</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Buttocks">
  <data key="d0">Buttocks</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">Buttocks (gluteal region) are a subcutaneous injection site with the slowest insulin absorption among common sites.&lt;SEP&gt;Buttocks are a peripheral injection site with the slowest insulin absorption among typical sites.&lt;SEP&gt;Recommended injection site on the upper outer lateral region of the buttocks.&lt;SEP&gt;Buttocks is a region of the body recommended as an injection site for subcutaneous insulin.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1d9f7234865211afc5d8343294b276d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8abf9336f83edf5c92071da1032dc483&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cc6a26a5d2c41087b58a0f7f71ad21cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0b9c41c968bcc1d46185583661e8f989</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Documento sem título.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/insulinas em seringa.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Basaglar.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786310013</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Exercise">
  <data key="d0">Exercise</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Exercise is a form of physical activity that raises the body’s demand for glucose as an energy source and influences overall glucose metabolism. By increasing muscular work, exercise creates a heightened need for circulating glucose, which can modify how the body processes and utilizes carbohydrates.

When a person engages in exercise, the rate at which injected insulin is absorbed can increase, particularly for rapid‑acting formulations such as Humalog and for basal products like insulin glargine (BASAGLAR) delivered via a KwikPen. This accelerated absorption is most pronounced when the activity involves the area around the injection site, leading to a faster onset of insulin action.

Because of the faster insulin effect and the greater glucose utilization during activity, exercise often reduces overall insulin requirements. If insulin doses are not adjusted, the combination of heightened insulin activity and increased glucose uptake can raise the risk of hypoglycemia. Consequently, clinical guidance commonly advises individuals who exercise to avoid lowering their basal insulin index (or basal rate) without careful monitoring, and to consider dose adjustments to maintain safe blood‑glucose levels.&lt;SEP&gt;Exercise is a physical activity that may trigger the use of a Temp Target to reduce insulin delivery.&lt;SEP&gt;Exercise refers to physical activity that can affect glucose levels after Afrezza inhalation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1d9f7234865211afc5d8343294b276d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8abf9336f83edf5c92071da1032dc483&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c3daabbd42055dc30154f5f97c85fb7d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3db0edd23b6b502ccbbf62bfd601ce68&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d96761d60c65f05f1530bc19b144cf1b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8ac99e7359716e2cecc2ec93159218b6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4b9f6a4a440ccb40e47c326ca6dd9346&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-70519ee85d46567e23db476b219f16a9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-780f90d656277126a05ed136a084fd77&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8741750a7bf86eb5d1fadf82a9c7720e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-70c5a1107fcc9b632361d9c52064f45d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Documento sem título.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/Bula Humalog.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Basaglar.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/edelman-et-al-2026-dosing-afrezza-it-s-not-that-complicated.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786333269</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Heat">
  <data key="d0">Heat</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">External warmth that speeds up insulin absorption.&lt;SEP&gt;Heat (including hot baths or warm compresses) accelerates insulin absorption.&lt;SEP&gt;Heat is an environmental factor from which Humalog should be protected during storage.&lt;SEP&gt;Heat is elevated temperature that can reduce the efficacy of Novolin® R, requiring protection from excess.&lt;SEP&gt;Heat is a natural factor that Humulin R must be protected from during storage.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1d9f7234865211afc5d8343294b276d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8abf9336f83edf5c92071da1032dc483&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e89f1dbae629e925f06732cebf41df16&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-df616353e032c899b02bfa4368bc2667&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-577779892c0d463cd6bb1966b8a8ce2d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Documento sem título.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/Bula Humalog.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786319732</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Fever">
  <data key="d0">Fever</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Elevated body temperature that can increase insulin uptake.&lt;SEP&gt;Medical symptom indicating elevated body temperature, listed as an indication for blood ketone testing.&lt;SEP&gt;Fever is an elevated body temperature that can increase insulin absorption speed.&lt;SEP&gt;Fever is an adverse event reported in ≥5% of patients with type 1 diabetes using Humalog.&lt;SEP&gt;Fever is cited as a possible trigger for elevated blood glucose.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1d9f7234865211afc5d8343294b276d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cd6b0367ed2176146798e5cf697d0aeb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4902fb11e4844af5cf6fd61f18b6e4ce&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4d26ce64e79b8c4a147140be2f9c63dd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2943becc796c8ce3f0aaedf0978c3213</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/Bula Humalog.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/TRESIBA _ BulasMed.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786306298</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Warm Compress">
  <data key="d0">Warm Compress</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Applying a warm compress to the injection site can hasten insulin absorption.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1d9f7234865211afc5d8343294b276d1</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1786299812</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cold Compress">
  <data key="d0">Cold Compress</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Applying a cold compress to the injection site can slow insulin absorption, increasing blood glucose levels.&lt;SEP&gt;Cold compress is the application of cold (e.g., cold pack, cold bath) that can slow insulin action and raise blood glucose.&lt;SEP&gt;Cold Compress is the application of a cool pack to the injection site, reducing insulin absorption speed.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1d9f7234865211afc5d8343294b276d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-84c3145631d64a0c7b9ea21dfb9c8275&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4902fb11e4844af5cf6fd61f18b6e4ce</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Documento sem título.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786301835</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Dehydration">
  <data key="d0">Dehydration</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Lack of adequate fluids that can decelerate insulin action and raise blood glucose.&lt;SEP&gt;Dehydration is a state of insufficient body water that can slow insulin action and increase blood sugar.&lt;SEP&gt;Dehydration is a state of reduced body fluid volume that slows insulin absorption.&lt;SEP&gt;Dehydration is a condition that increases the likelihood of hospitalization for people with diabetes.&lt;SEP&gt;Dehydration is identified as a condition that increases the likelihood of hospitalization for individuals with diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1d9f7234865211afc5d8343294b276d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-84c3145631d64a0c7b9ea21dfb9c8275&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4902fb11e4844af5cf6fd61f18b6e4ce&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-345ad64f464691cc28341ccd246032db&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b2cd796639bdb0e10eeda7ef3d9ebbce</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Documento sem título.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Metas glicêmicas/metas cuidado do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786372097</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Insulin Suspension">
  <data key="d0">Insulin Suspension</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Certain insulin formulations contain particles that must be mixed gently before injection.&lt;SEP&gt;Insulin Suspension is a mixed insulin formulation that requires proper homogenization to avoid concentration errors.&lt;SEP&gt;Insulin suspension is the liquid mixture containing insulin crystals that must be homogenized to ensure accurate dosing.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1d9f7234865211afc5d8343294b276d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4902fb11e4844af5cf6fd61f18b6e4ce&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4d795dc393eb02c6418957ee1678504f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Armazenamento e Transporte/transporte e conservação Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-20201.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786302748</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Mixing Technique">
  <data key="d0">Mixing Technique</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The recommended mixing technique involves rolling the insulin vial about 20 times gently to avoid bubbles.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1d9f7234865211afc5d8343294b276d1</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1786299813</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Temperature Range 2°C to 8°C">
  <data key="d0">Temperature Range 2°C to 8°C</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Temperature Range 2°C to 8°C is the recommended storage temperature for insulin in a refrigerator.&lt;SEP&gt;The ideal storage temperature for insulin is between 2 °C and 8 °C.&lt;SEP&gt;Temperature Range 2°C to 8°C specifies the refrigerated temperature interval required for Apidra Solostar stability.&lt;SEP&gt;Temperature Range 2°C to 8°C is the recommended refrigeration temperature for storing the SoloStar before first use.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1d9f7234865211afc5d8343294b276d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-03a1de93a53fbcb513268c123e2c5a16&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2dc2313c92b2af4132faaa4d41449eef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e9835d6684db67541402527b3182b6c5</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_apidra.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786315492</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Freezing">
  <data key="d0">Freezing</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Freezing damages insulin; frozen insulin must be discarded.&lt;SEP&gt;Freezing is the process of turning a liquid into ice, which renders insulin unusable.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1d9f7234865211afc5d8343294b276d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8336dc27990f6189c99863d64435c6c6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4ce520f0fe7dc4a6c79f92a25dfaff19</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Armazenamento e Transporte/Armazenamento e transporte.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1786302100</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="i-Port Device">
  <data key="d0">i-Port Device</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The i-Port is a device that allows multiple insulin administrations without repeated needle insertion.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1d9f7234865211afc5d8343294b276d1</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1786299813</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hand Luggage">
  <data key="d0">Hand Luggage</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Hand luggage is the recommended way to transport insulin during travel to avoid exposure to extreme temperatures.&lt;SEP&gt;Hand Luggage is a carry‑on bag where insulin should be placed during travel, never in checked baggage.&lt;SEP&gt;Hand luggage refers to carry‑on baggage where insulin should be placed during travel.&lt;SEP&gt;Hand Luggage refers to the carry‑on baggage in which insulin must be transported during travel.&lt;SEP&gt;Hand luggage is carry-on baggage where insulin should be placed during travel.&lt;SEP&gt;Hand luggage is the portion of travel baggage in which insulin must be carried to maintain its integrity during displacement.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1d9f7234865211afc5d8343294b276d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-525086e26636af026c417773a8f11a92&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-03a1de93a53fbcb513268c123e2c5a16&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1b1b73e9b7285819a4ba5caa6fdfa785&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8336dc27990f6189c99863d64435c6c6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4d795dc393eb02c6418957ee1678504f</data>
