<node id="Rapid‑acting Insulin">
  <data key="d0">Rapid‑acting Insulin</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Rapid‑acting insulin is a type of insulin that begins to work quickly after injection, often used in mixed regimens.&lt;SEP&gt;Rapid‑acting insulin is a class of insulin that begins to work within minutes after injection and has a short duration of action.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-191286ebd759321d40620f77c84ef5a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bf25fca295be60e28b7c7d3103f722fc</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_1778357531609.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786310682</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Intermediate‑acting Insulin">
  <data key="d0">Intermediate‑acting Insulin</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Intermediate‑acting insulin is a type of insulin with a longer onset, used in combination with rapid‑acting insulin.&lt;SEP&gt;Intermediate‑acting insulin is a class of insulin with a slower onset and longer duration than rapid‑acting insulin, exemplified by NPH.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-191286ebd759321d40620f77c84ef5a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bf25fca295be60e28b7c7d3103f722fc</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_1778357531609.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786310682</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Health Care Team">
  <data key="d0">Health Care Team</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">The health care team comprises medical professionals who help patients design and adjust insulin rotation plans.&lt;SEP&gt;The group of clinicians who prescribe and support diabetes technology for patients.&lt;SEP&gt;Group of professionals that assists people with diabetes in device selection, education, and training.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-191286ebd759321d40620f77c84ef5a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e4c5ae163a494feafedb71ed2205c02f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6fe769b03fc66d4a691f3b7f741b92cb</data>
