<node id="Needle Reuse">
  <data key="d0">Needle Reuse</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Reusing needles multiple times is a behavior that increases the risk of lipo‑hipertrofia.&lt;SEP&gt;Needle reuse is the practice of using the same insulin needle for multiple injections, often unnoticed due to reduced pain sensitivity.&lt;SEP&gt;Needle reuse refers to the practice of using the same insulin needle multiple times.&lt;SEP&gt;Needle reuse is the practice of using the same insulin injection needle multiple times, which raises safety concerns.&lt;SEP&gt;Needle reuse denotes the practice of using the same injection needle for multiple administrations, increasing risk of obstruction and infection.&lt;SEP&gt;Needle Reuse is the practice of using the same syringe needle for multiple insulin injections, increasing risk of lipohypertrophy.&lt;SEP&gt;Needle Reuse is the practice of using the same injection needle multiple times and is identified as a predisposing factor for lipohypertrofia.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b91b40e47c97be1b62c0f3d271cd4efd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-525086e26636af026c417773a8f11a92&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-74b3171b97fd80965359afadc0af9312&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3397508bdfddde019cb1dfdcfb352435&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1ee5400065df79b02b6c04efc0f4854d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-55f8c8b2b40633cf37993b620002b889&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c0cec9d1eb70ae81e8c1cb85f0b49621</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Toujeo.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/Documento sem título.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/O que você precisa saber sobre Lipohipertrofia - Sociedade Brasileira de Diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786322287</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Reduced Pain Sensitivity">
  <data key="d0">Reduced Pain Sensitivity</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Reduced pain sensitivity describes diminished sensation in lipo‑hypertrophic skin areas, making injections feel less painful.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b91b40e47c97be1b62c0f3d271cd4efd</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1786299818</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Insulin Injection into Nodule">
  <data key="d0">Insulin Injection into Nodule</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Insulin injection into nodule is the practice of delivering insulin directly into a lipohypertrophic nodule, which impairs insulin effectiveness.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b91b40e47c97be1b62c0f3d271cd4efd</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1786299818</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Health Professional">
  <data key="d0">Health Professional</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Health Professional is a qualified medical practitioner who plays a central role in the management of insulin therapy for individuals with diabetes. The professional is responsible for adjusting insulin doses, teaching patients how to monitor blood‑glucose levels, and reviewing skin condition to ensure safe and effective injection sites. They instruct patients in proper injection techniques, including the use of removable‑needle syringes, and monitor adherence to prescribed regimens. In addition to education and dose management, health professionals are authorized to perform clinical procedures involving insulin, such as administering intravenous infusions (e.g., Novolin® R) and delivering subcutaneous insulin, provided they possess the necessary qualifications and legal authority.

The health professional is also consulted before the insertion of an insulin‑pump reservoir and supplies the individual’s personal settings for the device’s Bolus Wizard feature. They advise a comprehensive plan that incorporates continuous glucose sensor measurements and corrective bolus dosing when the pump is disconnected and later reconnected. Guidance on insulin‑pump usage and overall management is routinely provided, and the professional must be notified if any insulin appears abnormal or compromised.

Beyond direct patient interaction, health professionals analyze retrospective sensor‑monitoring continuous glucose (retro‑SMCG) data to refine and adjust diabetes treatment strategies. Their role encompasses delivering medical instructions, offering expert guidance, and ensuring that all aspects of insulin therapy—whether manual injections or pump‑based delivery—are safely and effectively coordinated.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b91b40e47c97be1b62c0f3d271cd4efd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e4654b5e9fa02cf051c2d5ebc846c5d6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2a0a3f492aa5ef7771b2246547cb5f02&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3d0de4d525c273cda4939a501eaecc6d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-74b3171b97fd80965359afadc0af9312&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c68e2c07786710dd5250c6610f52b14d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-73559dc5d86ea52a348d603482e056e9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-df616353e032c899b02bfa4368bc2667&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7ce776458e256df9d6070a419cab7449&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1f3c75e751c36c2f270820a403b40ac0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-381370d223aabc9b355b55a05c98e07b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3d24fce6aa8866fb4a11514ae0e4d675&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-785aac5c827baebbe0c372f8c4550f23&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e94cedc7134adbb256c931b851235c53&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7ac99b8588a8c480f44a5519509f7713</data>
