<node id="Pancreatic Beta Cells">
  <data key="d0">Pancreatic Beta Cells</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Pancreatic beta cells are the insulin‑producing cells of the pancreas.&lt;SEP&gt;Pancreatic beta cells are the cells in the pancreas that produce insulin.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b91b40e47c97be1b62c0f3d271cd4efd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-22078404beeceb5adc3e688d239c585e</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/Documento sem título.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1786336921</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Type 2 Diabetes">
  <data key="d0">Type 2 Diabetes</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Type 2 Diabetes is the most common, chronic metabolic disorder of the diabetes mellitus spectrum, accounting for roughly 90–95 % of all diabetes cases. It is defined by marked peripheral insulin resistance together with a progressive, relative deficiency of endogenous insulin production caused by β‑cell dysfunction; the disease is non‑autoimmune and distinct from monogenic forms of diabetes. Although it typically presents in adulthood, its incidence is rising among youth, people of reproductive age, and during pregnancy, and it frequently follows gestational diabetes mellitus or prediabetes. Major risk factors include advancing age, obesity, metabolic syndrome, and other lifestyle‑related variables, and the condition often remains undiagnosed for years despite persistently elevated blood glucose levels.

Diagnosis relies on standard glycemic criteria—hemoglobin A1C, fasting plasma glucose, or a 2‑hour oral glucose tolerance test—and routine screening is recommended for adults and high‑risk groups. Clinically, Type 2 Diabetes is characterized by hyperglycemia, which drives both microvascular complications (retinopathy, nephropathy, neuropathy) and macrovascular disease (coronary artery disease, stroke, peripheral arterial disease). It is also used as a reference population in comparative‑effectiveness research, digital‑health investigations, and trials of novel glucose‑lowering agents, and it serves as a comparator group for outcomes in cystic fibrosis‑related diabetes (CFRD) and other specific diabetes subtypes (e.g., flatbush diabetes).

Management follows a stepped, individualized paradigm. First‑line therapy emphasizes lifestyle modification—dietary changes, regular physical activity, and weight control—combined with metformin as the preferred oral agent. When glycemic targets are not achieved, additional oral drugs, GLP‑1 receptor agonists, SGLT2 inhibitors, or non‑insulin injectables may be added. Insulin therapy is introduced progressively, beginning with basal insulin and advancing to prandial or mixed regimens; long‑acting analogues, high‑concentration basal formulations, inhaled insulin, and insulin pump or continuous subcutaneous insulin infusion systems are employed for insulin‑deficient patients. Continuous glucose monitoring (CGM) and flash glucose monitoring support precise glycemic control and time‑in‑range goals, while nutritional strategies such as bedtime snacks can mitigate hypoglycemia risk.

Across landmark randomized trials—including UKPDS, ACCORD, ADVANCE, VADT, and OpT2mise—Type 2 Diabetes has been the central disease entity for evaluating therapeutic strategies, cardiovascular outcomes, and disease progression. Its prominence in clinical guidelines, risk‑prediction models, and the A1C‑to‑average‑glucose relationship underscores its pivotal role in everyday practice and in the development of future pharmacologic, device‑based, and digital‑health innovations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b91b40e47c97be1b62c0f3d271cd4efd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cd6b0367ed2176146798e5cf697d0aeb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-525086e26636af026c417773a8f11a92&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6d0f18c80f8de2dee960a03599d12052&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bbae57922175913b7c36c594b4673fa2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-42b9c5d97c54f39fb69bb1169e1de4d2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-77dc1a2378f763ffabe8fa379881d1cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e5f5165b3185feb3c6ec93a3c0ef8d02&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-01fb767ae3a103c9d6c4775570df90c9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b4d7abd3e1e5418ee5a931e28a18e8ad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cd40a6d69921cf300ed8eda043698d1a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-005de970178a46619506bcc15fe94fa9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c0cec9d1eb70ae81e8c1cb85f0b49621&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5bd45744c4c50bb97abce1352018de47&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a23aee717dff7fe908d8a006fd48a5c7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-126f927723331d6ce149cf77ed397bbf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-16a76447c936e157673f084ffb74520d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-941c5035ce1f85963f1f564bf2bf73fb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-61a59544bbd02c2c82b13c7808f72c73&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0ba3c49b467b6d37cd2aab29bf4a3119&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0932e9c21a330869629b3fa70d2e1f5e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-06425d1f80d868bd58871b6a6e740102&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-161a201d846100f42e643139469a1e6c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d30bfc1840eec64224c3568470e6c539&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a0e51dec97ab970bbc2f21878a8735ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4655f823785fa91e72cba96e00dba34c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5419de5a030f812ab408ef47f361bebd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cbb54288f56e407604ea361f58e58233&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9cd925790899146eeb8a373879b5feac&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9e0c6a8245e883948688f77c2440ca4b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5ed3ce00d7a52cdffe7b550ffe0dd568&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-40c2c862887db201b07c741a1862dcc1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c93787ffd2c022283fc0663decb1a184&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-00d07129873894814fe6540ce243ef9f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-511f6be03d2ea98970bd4c1b29b3e5c8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b4b76ae88b212b3a0a4d05c250e05e0c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-76eaa3af026fbb91a96f70d3502e809d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-41b7df11ccfb12f819e6f60481970587&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0fe1eff7b58582dec4c8ae7578e20e66&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a414fa1274ab6f8e05af931a0c52be4b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d3a9b76fabae2f788