  <data key="d5">1786372129</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Infarct">
  <data key="d0">Infarct</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">An infarct is tissue death, such as a heart attack, linked to vascular complications of diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b91b40e47c97be1b62c0f3d271cd4efd</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1786299819</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Stroke">
  <data key="d0">Stroke</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A stroke is a cerebral vascular accident associated with diabetes‑related vascular damage.&lt;SEP&gt;Stroke (non‑fatal cerebrovascular accident) is a primary outcome component examined in the Origin study.&lt;SEP&gt;Stroke, also known as cerebrovascular accident, was observed to have doubled risk in individuals with fasting glucose (GJ) ≥126 mg/dL.&lt;SEP&gt;Stroke is a cerebrovascular event causing neurological impairment.&lt;SEP&gt;A cerebrovascular event caused by interruption of blood flow to the brain.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b91b40e47c97be1b62c0f3d271cd4efd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c41538e94f00eba70740ff188bcb6a94&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6a92f811a7d2d835dc4b730c9bbf08cf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e668c40e3bc21d982ed03a052f0f9339&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f99d05e1089d59496d56d86ff40197cc</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Basaglar.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Diagnóstico de diabetes mellitus.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Metas glicêmicas/metas cuidado do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786372137</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Disglycemia">
  <data key="d0">Disglycemia</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Disglycemia describes wide, frequent swings in blood‑glucose levels that are neither consistently high nor low.&lt;SEP&gt;Disglycemia is a condition where blood sugar is not balanced, fluctuating widely between high and low levels.&lt;SEP&gt;Disglycemia denotes uncontrolled blood glucose fluctuations, including acute hyperglycemia and chronic hyperglycemia, leading to metabolic abnormalities.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b91b40e47c97be1b62c0f3d271cd4efd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-22078404beeceb5adc3e688d239c585e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2d8f17f3f250a37a1effaaa88cc8b382</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/Documento sem título.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/glicemias capilares.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786338524</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Internal Inflammation">
  <data key="d0">Internal Inflammation</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Internal inflammation is the body's inflammatory response triggered by erratic glucose concentrations.&lt;SEP&gt;Internal inflammation is one of the harmful effects caused by the oscillations of blood sugar in disglycemia.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b91b40e47c97be1b62c0f3d271cd4efd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-22078404beeceb5adc3e688d239c585e</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/Documento sem título.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1786336922</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Vascular Damage">
  <data key="d0">Vascular Damage</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Vascular damage is harm to blood vessels caused by chronic glycemic fluctuations.&lt;SEP&gt;Vascular damage refers to damage to blood vessels caused by disglycemia.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b91b40e47c97be1b62c0f3d271cd4efd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-22078404beeceb5adc3e688d239c585e</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/Documento sem título.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1786336922</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Metabolic Memory">
  <data key="d0">Metabolic Memory</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Metabolic memory is the lingering cellular imprint of past high‑glucose exposure, affecting future metabolic response.&lt;SEP&gt;Metabolic memory is the phenomenon where the body retains the harmful effects of high sugar even after control improves.&lt;SEP&gt;Metabolic memory (legacy effect) describes lasting benefits from a finite period of intensive glycemic control.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b91b40e47c97be1b62c0f3d271cd4efd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-22078404beeceb5adc3e688d239c585e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aff91698679a52cd7b07563b7b2627a3</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/Documento sem título.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Metas glicêmicas/metas cuidado do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786372168</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Treatment Goal">
  <data key="d0">Treatment Goal</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The treatment goal in diabetes is to prevent complications by maintaining blood glucose within safe limits.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b91b40e47c97be1b62c0f3d271cd4efd</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1786299820</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Complications">
  <data key="d0">Complications</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Complications are serious health problems that can develop from poorly controlled diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b91b40e47c97be1b62c0f3d271cd4efd</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1786299820</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Glycemic Monitoring">
  <data key="d0">Glycemic Monitoring</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Glycemic monitoring is the ongoing measurement of blood‑glucose levels to guide diabetes management.&lt;SEP&gt;Glycemic monitoring is the routine measurement of blood glucose levels to guide insulin therapy and prevent hyperglycemia or hypoglycemia.&lt;SEP&gt;Glycemic monitoring is a rigorous blood‑glucose checking practice recommended to avoid hypoglycemia, especially nocturnal episodes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b91b40e47c97be1b62c0f3d271cd4efd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6ca13e396b094f0c2f482892f220f538&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-14772c7de5db762c492a75a1c744dae6</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Basaglar.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_fiasp.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786316094</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Fasting Glucose">
  <data key="d0">Fasting Glucose</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Fasting Glucose is the concentration of glucose in blood that is measured after an overnight fast and before any food intake.   It is a low‑cost laboratory test that provides a single, quantitative value reflecting the body’s basal glucose metabolism.  

In clinical practice, fasting glucose serves several complementary purposes.  It is a primary screening tool for identifying individuals at risk of diabetes mellitus, with commonly cited abnormal thresholds of ≥ 110 mg/dL (early abnormal glucose metabolism) and the higher range of 110–125 mg/dL used to denote impaired fasting glucose.  The same measurement is employed to monitor glycaemic control in people already diagnosed with diabetes, offering a target metric for treatment adjustment.  

Fasting glucose also has specific research and transplant‑medicine applications.  In metabolic evaluations of type 1 diabetes (DM1) Phase 1, the test is taken when two or more diabetes‑related autoantibodies are positive to help characterize disease onset.  Additionally, it is used to screen for post‑transplant diabetes mellitus (PTDM), identifying patients at high risk for this complication.  

Overall, fasting glucose is a widely accepted, inexpensive blood‑sugar test performed after an overnight fast, valued for both population‑level diabetes screening and individual disease monitoring across various clinical contexts.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b91b40e47c97be1b62c0f3d271cd4efd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-457b20f4d8d08ee6b3ed08a225c773de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-22078404beeceb5adc3e688d239c585e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2cf24d486949a568d61c1de206cd3e14&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-090b8f9281aa75054311d8f275a2c8f8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e4e7eef761aec994cc4558b2db5e1e08&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-83d72fbc44fe0c28f27702c0d4f2c140&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ae844f5b99d595c38f74e375112238e6</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/Documento sem título.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Diagnóstico de diabetes mellitus.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377286</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Postprandial Glucose">
  <data key="d0">Postprandial Glucose</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Postprandial glucose is the blood‑sugar level measured after meals.&lt;SEP&gt;Postprandial glucose is the blood sugar level measured after meals.&lt;SEP&gt;Blood glucose levels measured after meals, reported as lower in the APIDRA group than in the human regular insulin group.&lt;SEP&gt;Postprandial glucose is the blood glucose concentration after a meal, used to assess prandial insulin efficacy.&lt;SEP&gt;Postprandial glucose is a target measurement taken after meals to monitor diabetes control.&lt;SEP&gt;Postprandial glucose refers to blood glucose levels measured after a meal.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b91b40e47c97be1b62c0f3d271cd4efd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-457b20f4d8d08ee6b3ed08a225c773de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-891989adf06518cd34c94853444495e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f9416e8076c17175db0dbb12c3393566&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-22078404beeceb5adc3e688d239c585e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aff91698679a52cd7b07563b7b2627a3</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_apidra.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/Insulinoterapia – Diretriz da Sociedade Brasileira de Diabetes – Ed. 2024.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/Documento sem título.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Metas glicêmicas/metas cuidado do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786372169</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Discovery of Insulin">
  <data key="d0">Discovery of Insulin</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">The discovery of insulin in 1921 marked the first successful isolation of the hormone for therapeutic use.&lt;SEP&gt;Discovery of insulin in 1921 marked the first testing of the hormone in dogs and later in humans.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b91b40e47c97be1b62c0f3d271cd4efd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-457b20f4d8d08ee6b3ed08a225c773de</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1786299820</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Use of New Needle Each Application">
  <data key="d0">Use of New Needle Each Application</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Use of new needle each application is the practice of replacing the insulin needle for every injection to avoid tissue damage.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b91b40e47c97be1b62c0f3d271cd4efd</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1786299820</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Skin Inspection">
  <data key="d0">Skin Inspection</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Looking and feeling the skin before each insulin injection to identify altered or nodular areas.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b91b40e47c97be1b62c0f3d271cd4efd</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1786299820</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Altered Skin Area">
  <data key="d0">Altered Skin Area</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Skin regions that appear changed, hard, or contain nodules, making them unsuitable for insulin injection.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b91b40e47c97be1b62c0f3d271cd4efd</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1786299820</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Large Glycemic Variability">
  <data key="d0">Large Glycemic Variability</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Significant fluctuations in blood glucose levels throughout the day, often resulting from irregular insulin absorption.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b91b40e47c97be1b62c0f3d271cd4efd</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1786299821</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Tissue Recovery Time">
  <data key="d0">Tissue Recovery Time</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The variable period needed for skin tissue to heal after stopping injections in a lipohypertrophic site.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b91b40e47c97be1b62c0f3d271cd4efd</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1786299821</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Dose Reduction When Switching Sites">
  <data key="d0">Dose Reduction When Switching Sites</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Decreasing the insulin dose when moving from an affected injection area to a healthy one to avoid post‑switch hyperglycemia.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b91b40e47c97be1b62c0f3d271cd4efd</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1786299821</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Frequent Glycemic Monitoring During Site Switch">
  <data key="d0">Frequent Glycemic Monitoring During Site Switch</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Measuring blood glucose more often during the transition from a compromised to a healthy injection site.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b91b40e47c97be1b62c0f3d271cd4efd</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1786299821</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Postprandial Hyperglycemia Increase">
  <data key="d0">Postprandial Hyperglycemia Increase</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">An elevation of blood glucose after meals by up to 26% or more when insulin is injected into a lipohypertrophic nodule.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b91b40e47c97be1b62c0f3d271cd4efd</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1786299821</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Extreme Hyperglycemia (&gt;300 mg/dL)">
  <data key="d0">Extreme Hyperglycemia (&gt;300 mg/dL)</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Very high blood glucose levels exceeding 300 mg/dL observed after insulin injection into a nodule.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b91b40e47c97be1b62c0f3d271cd4efd</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1786299821</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Proper Insulin Function">
  <data key="d0">Proper Insulin Function</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The condition where insulin effectively lowers blood glucose, requiring correct injection technique and site selection.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b91b40e47c97be1b62c0f3d271cd4efd</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1786299821</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Avoid Repeated Injection at Same Point">
  <data key="d0">Avoid Repeated Injection at Same Point</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Advice to not inject repeatedly into the identical spot on abdomen, arm, or leg to prevent tissue changes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b91b40e47c97be1b62c0f3d271cd4efd</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1786299821</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Skin Palpation">
  <data key="d0">Skin Palpation</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Feeling the skin to detect nodules or hardness even when visual signs are absent.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b91b40e47c97be1b62c0f3d271cd4efd</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1786299821</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Lipohypertrophic Nodule">
  <data key="d0">Lipohypertrophic Nodule</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">A palpable, hardened lump in the skin resulting from repeated insulin injections, characteristic of lipohypertrophy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b91b40e47c97be1b62c0f3d271cd4efd</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1786299821</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Creams">
  <data key="d0">Creams</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Topical ointments or creams that should not be used without medical guidance in the context of insulin injection sites.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b91b40e47c97be1b62c0f3d271cd4efd</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1786299821</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Avoid Injection in Altered Skin Area">
  <data key="d0">Avoid Injection in Altered Skin Area</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Refraining from injecting insulin into skin that appears altered, hard, or nodular.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b91b40e47c97be1b62c0f3d271cd4efd</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1786299822</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hemoglobina Glicada (HbA1c)">
  <data key="d0">Hemoglobina Glicada (HbA1c)</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Hemoglobina Glicada (HbA1c) is a blood test that indicates average glucose levels over several months.&lt;SEP&gt;Hemoglobina glicada (HbA1c) is a blood test that shows the average glucose level over the past three months; a common target is below 7%.&lt;SEP&gt;Hemoglobina Glicada (HbA1c) measures average blood glucose over several months and is used for diabetes diagnosis.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bcba435392a61e072dfaad9195e42ed7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-12999315830b302d973dd1908eab1e12&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5e551f4b7f03919afc1d663b3b2a2efa</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Documento sem título.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Diagnóstico de diabetes mellitus.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786372034</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Carboidrato de Ação Rápida">
  <data key="d0">Carboidrato de Ação Rápida</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Carboidrato de Ação Rápida refers to fast‑acting carbohydrates used to raise Glicemia quickly during Hipoglicemia.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bcba435392a61e072dfaad9195e42ed7</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1786299822</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Suco de Laranja">
  <data key="d0">Suco de Laranja</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Suco de Laranja is a beverage recommended as a source of Carboidrato de Ação Rápida.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bcba435392a61e072dfaad9195e42ed7</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1786299822</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Refrigerante Comum">
  <data key="d0">Refrigerante Comum</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Refrigerante Comum (non‑diet soda) is suggested as a Carboidrato de Ação Rápida for treating Hipoglicemia.&lt;SEP&gt;Refrigerante comum is a regular soda serving as a rapid carbohydrate source for hypoglycemia.&lt;SEP&gt;Refrigerante comum (non‑diet) is a beverage used as a source of rapid carbohydrate.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bcba435392a61e072dfaad9195e42ed7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ee7ecd9171c82c15f635a8a9b605621c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-82e0d8e22a06c73855abed11561ce467</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/Orientacoes_Hipoglicemia_SBD_transcricao.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Documento sem título.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1786368416</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Açúcar Dissolvido em Água">
  <data key="d0">Açúcar Dissolvido em Água</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Açúcar Dissolvido em Água is a mixture suggested as a Carboidrato de Ação Rápida.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bcba435392a61e072dfaad9195e42ed7</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1786299822</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Balas de Glicose">
  <data key="d0">Balas de Glicose</data>
