  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Idosos refers to older adults, with subcategories (healthy, with disease, frail) that have tailored HbA1c goals.&lt;SEP&gt;Idosos denotes patients older than 65 years who may use Tresiba with more frequent blood‑sugar monitoring.&lt;SEP&gt;Idosos denotes patients aged 60 years or older, for whom conservative insulin dosing is advised to avoid hypoglycemia.&lt;SEP&gt;Elderly who may exhibit specific hypoglycemia symptoms.&lt;SEP&gt;Idosos are elderly individuals who, due to comorbidities and polypharmacy, have increased exposure to severe hypoglycemia.&lt;SEP&gt;Idosos (people aged 65 or older) have adapted diabetes treatment goals based on health status.</data>
