<node id="AMGC">
  <data key="d0">AMGC</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">AMGC (Automonitorização da Glicemia Capilar) is a capillary blood glucose self‑monitoring method that uses a finger prick and a glucose meter.&lt;SEP&gt;AMGC (Automonitorização da Glicemia Capilar) is the method of measuring blood glucose by finger prick with a glucometer.&lt;SEP&gt;AMGC is a method where a small finger prick is used with a device for capillary glucose self‑monitoring.&lt;SEP&gt;Auto-Monitorização da Glicemia Contínua, a continuous glucose monitoring technique recommended for patients using insulin.&lt;SEP&gt;AMGC (Automonitorização da Glicemia Capilar) is a method for continuous capillary glucose self‑monitoring throughout the day.&lt;SEP&gt;AMGC (Capillary Glucose Self‑Monitoring) is a method that measures capillary glucose using a disposable biosensor strip and a glucometer.</data>
