<node id="Glucose Meter">
  <data key="d0">Glucose Meter</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Glucose Meter is a handheld medical device designed to measure the concentration of glucose in a person’s blood. It obtains a sample typically by a finger‑prick or other capillary blood draw, which is applied to a disposable test strip that the meter reads to generate a numerical blood‑glucose value. The device displays this value to the user and can store the results in its internal memory for later review.

The primary purpose of a glucose meter is to enable individuals, especially those with diabetes, to monitor their blood‑glucose levels multiple times per day as part of self‑management and treatment planning. In addition to providing an immediate reading, many meters supply data that can be used for calibration of the test strips or for uploading to health‑record systems. The simplicity of the finger‑stick method and the portability of the meter make it a routine tool for daily glucose monitoring.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-457b20f4d8d08ee6b3ed08a225c773de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cd6b0367ed2176146798e5cf697d0aeb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f5f31f609ed760b9e36f235d0109b470&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c9bc5d11c9f848439320623cad3d3a38&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-545c19428427ece2c838e352e759e388&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-679002669c87907578534904694e17dc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2d8f17f3f250a37a1effaaa88cc8b382&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-208cda7ee40e8d266fadd1eadff49e03</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/blood glucose monitoring.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/Documento sem título.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/Orientacoes_Glicemia_SBD.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/glicemias capilares.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/hipoglicemia.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786372329</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Glucose Sensor">
  <data key="d0">Glucose Sensor</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Glucose Sensor (device) is a small, subcutaneous component of continuous glucose monitoring (CGM) systems that is inserted just beneath the skin to sample interstitial fluid. The sensor measures glucose concentrations in this fluid, typically converting the chemical signal into an electrical one, and updates the recorded value at regular intervals—most commonly every five minutes. Each measurement, referred to as sensor glucose (SG), is transmitted wirelessly to a display unit, an integrated insulin pump, or a separate transmitter such as the Guardian™ 2 Link used with the MiniMed™ 640G system. The transmitted data appear on a screen as numeric values, graphs, and trend arrows, and they can be employed to calculate metrics like Time‑In‑Range. By providing a continuous stream of glucose information, the sensor enables users and clinicians to track glucose dynamics, adjust therapy, and improve overall glycemic control. It is a central artifact in sensor‑augmented pump therapy and automated insulin delivery, and manufacturers typically require the sensor to be worn for at least 70 % of its usable lifespan to collect sufficient CGM data.

Glucose Sensor (reading) also denotes the glucose value (often labeled GS) displayed on an insulin pump that is derived from a linked meter or from the subcutaneous sensor itself. In this usage, the term refers to the processed glucose reading presented to the user rather than the physical sensing element.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-457b20f4d8d08ee6b3ed08a225c773de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b6828aacfba0c2a6ae59c439a4e4b161&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-986fc7ecc813c4b7942964d7fd64d429&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c1700b8f7c792afbd394001e28bf632f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4fe81d733c2a429da0726794b55350b0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1dd9a1bb820381073ad2475541a3a575&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4b9f6a4a440ccb40e47c326ca6dd9346&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-70519ee85d46567e23db476b219f16a9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d2f8a0d67f7320d6157b61dbbf428a40&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-59137a5f20ce729bcde5c65e1e45aa29&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c2474d83c9e01bbd20c6e68744a2dad5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3ce8c9873da330aac077f7ccaf108ccd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b3d901ee668c4fdbd518454aa3ebea3a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-edbbe2e207a7e0a28611a2a16fa2845f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bec9e867c8de5a0beabd70ea9209c1a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b9eee903de4b7e25fc53f52e2e739637&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8cceea4f7036977c7ddcbe81f76f8aa1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b6025fa711665988fad0f789b9eb901a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-08c7f7bb0209cabd75e27f9c8556c214&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-94150b57cc35a773b7c36f33f237f8a1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-545c19428427ece2c838e352e759e388&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6d83801272f7a0ae0d797d60572fe578</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/Documento sem título.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/cgm.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/Documento sem título.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Metas glicêmicas/Metas no tratamento.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786370128</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
