</node>
<node id="Glucometer">
  <data key="d0">Glucometer</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">A glucometer is a handheld device that measures glucose concentration from a finger‑prick blood sample.&lt;SEP&gt;A device that receives a blood sample on a test strip, measures blood glucose, and displays the glycemia value on its screen.&lt;SEP&gt;Glucometer is a device used for frequent glucose measurement, which can be substituted in many cases.&lt;SEP&gt;A finger‑prick device that measures blood glucose directly.&lt;SEP&gt;A device used to measure glucose via finger pricks, referenced for comparison of prick frequency.&lt;SEP&gt;A glucometer is a medical device that quantifies plasma glucose concentrations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c0ec5707b6df65f1a6822e01b9bb3fb9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b6828aacfba0c2a6ae59c439a4e4b161&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-63f18f20af642d4a480c16e7a6780bb6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-08c7f7bb0209cabd75e27f9c8556c214&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5c804699375feba4c866cc3a1bc00211&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a5f7cad1fb0e1a0a02f63b5928b8acd2</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/Documento sem título.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/Documento sem título.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/glicemias capilares.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786338531</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Continuous Glucose Sensor">
  <data key="d0">Continuous Glucose Sensor</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">A tiny sensor attached to the skin that continuously measures glucose in interstitial fluid and transmits the data for display.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c0ec5707b6df65f1a6822e01b9bb3fb9</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1786299827</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Interstitial Fluid">
  <data key="d0">Interstitial Fluid</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Interstitial Fluid is the extracellular liquid that occupies the spaces between the body’s cells. It receives glucose that has diffused from the bloodstream, providing the immediate source of carbohydrate that cells can take up for metabolism. Because it lies directly adjacent to cells, insulin that has entered the circulation also passes through this compartment as it travels toward its target tissues.

The composition of Interstitial Fluid therefore reflects the dynamic exchange of nutrients and hormones between blood and cells. Glucose can accumulate in this fluid when insulin action is insufficient, leading to higher interstitial concentrations that mirror hyperglycaemic states. Conversely, the fluid serves as the medium through which glucose moves from the vascular system into cells for utilization.

Because glucose concentration in Interstitial Fluid closely follows that in blood, continuous glucose monitoring devices commonly measure glucose levels in this compartment. The sensors detect the glucose present in Interstitial Fluid to provide real‑time readings of blood‑derived glucose concentrations, enabling accurate tracking of glycaemic trends for clinical and personal health management.&lt;SEP&gt;The fluid space between cells where the glucose sensor measures sensor glucose.&lt;SEP&gt;Interstitial Fluid is the fluid that surrounds the cells in the body.&lt;SEP&gt;The fluid between cells where glucose concentration is measured by the sensor.&lt;SEP&gt;Interstitial Fluid is the tissue fluid where the glucose sensor measures glucose levels.&lt;SEP&gt;Interstitial Fluid is the fluid between cells where the glucose sensor measures glucose levels.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c0ec5707b6df65f1a6822e01b9bb3fb9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b6828aacfba0c2a6ae59c439a4e4b161&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b7715667f5fca178f0988984e932ecfb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-65c6beab51324e055f4a39b388e2eefe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9f4d152d83c514f926b18413e065c2fa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-780f90d656277126a05ed136a084fd77&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6b867cec4c5eed3b10e431cbd4078dee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f5f31f609ed760b9e36f235d0109b470&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8cceea4f7036977c7ddcbe81f76f8aa1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b6025fa711665988fad0f789b9eb901a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-08c7f7bb0209cabd75e27f9c8556c214&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-94150b57cc35a773b7c36f33f237f8a1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-545c19428427ece2c838e352e759e388</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/Documento sem título.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/cgm.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/Documento sem título.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1786336918</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Transmitter">
  <data key="d0">Transmitter</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Transmitter is a wireless component of continuous glucose monitoring (CGM) systems that receives the electrical signal from a glucose sensor and sends the resulting glucose data to an external receiver, such as a reader, smartphone, or insulin pump. It acts as the communication bridge between the sensor and the pump, enabling real‑time glucose information to be displayed to the user or used by the pump’s automated insulin delivery algorithms.

The transmitter operates by radio frequency transmission and is typically indicated by a green LED on devices such as the Guardian 4 sensor. It can be paired or unpaired with the pump, and many models include a rechargeable battery that can be placed on a charger when depleted. Users must monitor battery status because a depleted battery will stop data transmission. The device is designed to be small and lightweight, but its detachable parts can pose a choking hazard if swallowed, especially by children.

Safety guidelines specify that the transmitter should not be exposed to intense magnetic fields, such as those generated by MRI equipment, as these could interfere with its operation or damage the unit. Routine exposure to ordinary magnetic fields (e.g., those from household appliances) is generally permissible, but caution is advised in environments with strong magnetic forces.

In the MiniMed system, the transmitter is paired with the Guardian 4 sensor and sends glucose readings directly to the insulin pump, allowing the pump to adjust insulin delivery based on current glucose levels. This integration makes the transmitter a critical element of the overall CGM and insulin delivery ecosystem.&lt;SEP&gt;Transmitter is the component of the Eversense system that wirelessly sends glucose readings from the implanted sensor to the smartphone application.&lt;SEP&gt;Transmitter is a component that sends the electrical signal from the glucose sensor to a reader or cellphone.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c0ec5707b6df65f1a6822e01b9bb3fb9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cf3629e41b33d8907b96157ddd2be394&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-381370d223aabc9b355b55a05c98e07b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-138cbaf5a43762d4c5b77a07ab51cbd4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-95ba6f1fa7d1791230f690255a8ba2df&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cdb000b83632c89167783ad4e6f1fb64&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4a75df3ab63706f501e8d3134e74a64b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db8e2f5011e0e0fe7dc11273e2f345b9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-28515a0aca492eeee478cd9947226498&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f3d819d6498d4482286628946e37a6b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3d0824c9d8a9ff5f2da52b7b5ea69c86&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a764dcbdd73fd1c50fa72a7cd60b6e19&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3895d65c9a22c257a4717f300d4086b0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8a0307c83d7b514ca00334e4c8ca2357&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dd545bc80ceae270c16406af736789b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b23dfd3ae95fca711f8f10fc98ab467c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c030749e7f9a2ae77cb8993d7250cffe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db5749bec4af1c3ea068b257c4376aaf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-93594146e1ebe099cfc47906e940939f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-545c19428427ece2c838e352e759e388</data>
