<node id="Gestational Diabetes">
  <data key="d0">Gestational Diabetes</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Gestational Diabetes is a form of glucose intolerance or diabetes that is first recognized during pregnancy. It is characterized by elevated blood‑glucose levels that develop as a result of hormonal changes and increased insulin resistance associated with gestation. Because the condition emerges only in the context of pregnancy, it is distinguished from pre‑existing type 1 or type 2 diabetes and requires specific clinical attention.

Management of Gestational Diabetes centers on careful monitoring of blood glucose through scheduled testing and, when necessary, pharmacologic therapy. Insulin is considered the treatment of choice; both rapid‑acting and, in some cases, long‑acting insulin formulations are used safely and effectively to achieve glycaemic control without harming the fetus. When insulin therapy is not required, dietary modification and exercise are first‑line strategies, but the condition always mandates a structured glucose‑monitoring schedule to guide treatment decisions and reduce the risk of maternal and neonatal complications.&lt;SEP&gt;Diabetes diagnosed during pregnancy, listed as part of maternal history risk factor for type 2 diabetes screening.&lt;SEP&gt;Gestational Diabetes is a form of diabetes diagnosed during pregnancy, referenced as a risk factor in the Diabetes Risk Test.&lt;SEP&gt;Diabetes diagnosed during pregnancy, examined for ethnic disparities.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cd6b0367ed2176146798e5cf697d0aeb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2a0a3f492aa5ef7771b2246547cb5f02&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6b14c2f0985ae4a417c8fc99e339bd9e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6d0f18c80f8de2dee960a03599d12052&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0fa819f7e1e42eb688d4894dc3ca7e64&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c7e6ef38db0b62d161b13473af47d738&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0932e9c21a330869629b3fa70d2e1f5e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-06425d1f80d868bd58871b6a6e740102&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-343246c2eef6e8430b581340d6cd4762&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2c37e26e62468b725533260347fb4e31&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8f1215318cea8c61dc12042476611f9f</data>
