  <data key="d2">National Institute for Health and Care Excellence (UK), which provides glycemic target recommendations for pregnant women with diabetes.&lt;SEP&gt;NICE is the abbreviation for the National Institute for Health and Care Excellence referenced in the manual.&lt;SEP&gt;National Institute for Health and Care Excellence, author of the updated guidance on diabetes in children and young people.&lt;SEP&gt;NICE (National Institute for Clinical Excellence) issues diabetes guidelines, including an HbA1c target of ≤6.5%.&lt;SEP&gt;NICE is referenced as an organization providing recommendations for SICI use in pregnant patients with DM1.&lt;SEP&gt;Instituto Nacional de Excelência Clínica e de Saúde, cited as providing guidelines for DM1 and DM2.&lt;SEP&gt;National Institute for Health and Care Excellence (UK), which recommends specific fasting and post‑meal glucose limits.</data>
