<node id="Disposable Pen">
  <data key="d0">Disposable Pen</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">A disposable pen is a type of insulin pen that comes pre‑filled with insulin and is discarded after the insulin is exhausted.&lt;SEP&gt;Disposable Pen is a single-use insulin pen intended for a limited number of injections.&lt;SEP&gt;Disposable pen is a device used to deliver insulin, equipped with a needle, injection button, and refill cartridge, designed for subcutaneous injection therapy.&lt;SEP&gt;The disposable pen is the applicator component of the BASAGLAR® KWIKPEN® system, designed for single‑use subcutaneous delivery and able to dispense up to 80 insulin units.&lt;SEP&gt;Disposable Pen refers to the single‑use or five‑use injectable pen packaging supplied with APIDRA.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ebdb9452013f0e340884677832714553&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7ed0b3e64751c1a28d72e087f711cc20&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1b1b73e9b7285819a4ba5caa6fdfa785&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4a89ae12c86f6f30741a3c6330e6c11b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fb620bf44b37187faceacd0405c4a819</data>
