  <data key="d5">1786300727</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="0.5 Unit Dose">
  <data key="d0">0.5 Unit Dose</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A 0.5 unit dose refers to a low‑volume insulin setting offered by some pens for precise dosing, especially in children.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ebdb9452013f0e340884677832714553</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1786299831</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="30 Unit Syringe">
  <data key="d0">30 Unit Syringe</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">A 30‑unit syringe is a small‑capacity syringe marked for 0.5‑unit increments, suitable for precise dosing.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ebdb9452013f0e340884677832714553</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1786299831</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="50 Unit Syringe">
  <data key="d0">50 Unit Syringe</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">A 50‑unit syringe is a larger‑capacity syringe marked for 0.5‑unit increments, also suitable for precise dosing.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ebdb9452013f0e340884677832714553</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1786299831</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Lancet">
  <data key="d0">Lancet</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Lancet (medical instrument) is a small, sharp needle designed to puncture the skin for finger‑prick blood sampling, most commonly used in glucose testing. The device is typically disposed of together with other sharps in a rigid plastic container that allows combined disposal of the lancet and any attached needle, thereby minimizing the risk of accidental injury and infection.  

Lancet (journal) is a leading, peer‑reviewed international medical journal renowned for publishing high‑impact clinical research across a wide range of medical specialties. It serves as a primary outlet for landmark trials that shape global medical practice, including the Rosenstock inhaled‑insulin study for type 2 diabetes, the OpT2mise randomized trial comparing insulin‑pump therapy with multiple daily injections, and a multicentre trial of automated insulin‑dosing guidance. The journal has also published the HypoDE study, a meta‑analysis on diabetes and vascular disease, investigations of intensive glucose control and cardiovascular outcomes, and research on novel glucose‑sensing technologies. Its reputation rests on a rigorous peer‑review process and its role in disseminating influential studies that inform clinical guidelines worldwide.&lt;SEP&gt;Lancet is a leading medical journal that published the global incidence study of type 1 diabetes.&lt;SEP&gt;A leading medical journal that published an article on glucose‑6‑phosphate dehydrogenase deficiency.&lt;SEP&gt;Lancet is a prestigious medical journal publishing high‑impact clinical research, including diabetes trials.&lt;SEP&gt;A leading medical journal.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ebdb9452013f0e340884677832714553&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a0e51dec97ab970bbc2f21878a8735ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-91a114d8b89cacee37b56501f349ce85&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5ed3ce00d7a52cdffe7b550ffe0dd568&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f35eed8b49aa0b698012777f6ec96ce5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-41b7df11ccfb12f819e6f60481970587&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a414fa1274ab6f8e05af931a0c52be4b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e0d0e5c511e72e62db88a57fa6ea198e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-545c19428427ece2c838e352e759e388&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6db2125b1b94840ea29100039a6fef20&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8393954b021d0ad02018d1a449e0cc93&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-034c9e1f42f0eec15fed18c25580b0eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e668c40e3bc21d982ed03a052f0f9339&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-54ce8d1437c0ec0329819123568df11e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c8df31d65b128b9d70b82bb8af257332&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c1ee3f56f3180d8544dbba6a542c9d68&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c83accc14a3b482690949ff04716a0aa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9ab98b1c07f7bbaa3ad28fb83167f489&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c14456299df06b01b603504def87f381</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/edelman-et-al-2026-dosing-afrezza-it-s-not-that-complicated.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/blood glucose monitoring.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/Documento sem título.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Metas glicêmicas/Metas no tratamento.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Diagnóstico de diabetes mellitus.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Metas glicêmicas/metas cuidado do diabetes.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377259</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Injection Procedure">
  <data key="d0">Injection Procedure</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The injection procedure encompasses the series of steps (hand washing, cleaning, skin fold, needle insertion, etc.) for administering insulin.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ebdb9452013f0e340884677832714553</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1786299831</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Exact Dosing">
  <data key="d0">Exact Dosing</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Exact dosing refers to the ability of insulin pens to deliver precise insulin amounts, including whole, half, and fractional units.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ebdb9452013f0e340884677832714553</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1786299832</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Correct Dose">
  <data key="d0">Correct Dose</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The correct dose is the insulin amount prescribed and measured during the injection process.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ebdb9452013f0e340884677832714553</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1786299832</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Prescription">
  <data key="d0">Prescription</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A prescription is the medical order that specifies the insulin dose to be administered.&lt;SEP&gt;Prescription is the written directive for medication orders, including insulin dosage, abbreviations, and symbols.&lt;SEP&gt;A medical prescription is required for the sale of Tresiba.&lt;SEP&gt;Prescription is the legal requirement under which BASAGLAR KwikPen is sold.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ebdb9452013f0e340884677832714553&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b5b4c60b3de8c56d9ab869d868345fb7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2943becc796c8ce3f0aaedf0978c3213&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f0c10866496bbb0b388b1e5ed69901c</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/TRESIBA _ BulasMed.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Basaglar.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786310007</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Insulin Flow">
  <data key="d0">Insulin Flow</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Insulin flow is the verification of insulin movement (e.g., 2 UI) when a new needle is attached to the pen.&lt;SEP&gt;Insulin Flow is the observable stream of insulin at the needle tip indicating successful delivery.&lt;SEP&gt;Insulin flow refers to the proper movement of insulin through the needle, verified by a drop at the needle tip.&lt;SEP&gt;The pathway through which insulin is delivered from pump to body.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ebdb9452013f0e340884677832714553&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f0710d91bd443ae1af3fd98049f4ad42&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dd25c8bd4672601d6ee40e4b7e28a69c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db8e2f5011e0e0fe7dc11273e2f345b9</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_fiasp.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329587</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Continuous Glucose Monitoring (CGM)">
  <data key="d0">Continuous Glucose Monitoring (CGM)</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Continuous Glucose Monitoring (CGM) is a technology and method that provides ongoing, real‑time measurement of glucose levels by means of a subcutaneous sensor. The sensor continuously samples interstitial fluid, converts the glucose concentration into a sensor glucose (SG) value, and transmits these readings wirelessly to a receiver, smartphone, or an insulin pump’s display.  

The transmitted data are presented on a Home Screen or similar interface, where users can view current glucose values together with trend information, trend arrows, and historical charts. CGM systems also generate alerts for high or low glucose excursions, enabling timely therapeutic decisions. When integrated with an insulin pump, the real‑time sensor glucose readings can be used by advanced control algorithms such as SmartGuard to modulate insulin delivery automatically.  

Overall, CGM offers a continuous, wearable solution for monitoring sensor glucose, delivering detailed glucose trends and alerts that support better diabetes management.&lt;SEP&gt;Continuous Glucose Monitoring (CGM) provides ongoing glucose readings to inform insulin dosing decisions.&lt;SEP&gt;Continuous Glucose Monitoring (CGM) is a sensor‑based technology that provides real‑time glucose readings, supporting the algorithms of Automated Insulin Delivery systems.&lt;SEP&gt;A sensor system that provides real‑time glucose readings, used to guide insulin delivery in multiple studies.&lt;SEP&gt;Continuous Glucose Monitoring (CGM) is a method that measures interstitial glucose every five minutes using a sensor.&lt;SEP&gt;Continuous Glucose Monitoring (CGM) is a method of measuring glucose levels in people with diabetes using sensors that track interstitial glucose.&lt;SEP&gt;Continuous Glucose Monitoring is a method/device that provides frequent glucose readings for assessing TIR and hypoglycemia.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b6828aacfba0c2a6ae59c439a4e4b161&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8cceea4f7036977c7ddcbe81f76f8aa1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4a75df3ab63706f501e8d3134e74a64b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7ceebe6fbf743053d7b55523365689e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a111edb31d6739acf013ce812b952366&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fd751b869edcd6c88d9e467cfb2cb0fd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d3b794ead59ea83de139af0358a0e7b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ede0f32eb8f8ea1eaab76cc0bc7648fd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7e3c3741659a85988124e5ddaf69c849&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e76c949a607724dd052d9fc4c7127a18&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3c9d162accf67a3761df6b1c9113e193&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-94150b57cc35a773b7c36f33f237f8a1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0fe1eff7b58582dec4c8ae7578e20e66&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6d83801272f7a0ae0d797d60572fe578</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/cengiz-beck-2026-use-of-inhaled-insulin-with-automated-insulin-delivery-systems.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/cgm.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/blood glucose monitoring.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Metas glicêmicas/Metas no tratamento.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786370023</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Finger Prick Blood Test">
  <data key="d0">Finger Prick Blood Test</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Finger prick blood test is a capillary glucose measurement performed by puncturing the fingertip, providing a direct blood glucose value.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b6828aacfba0c2a6ae59c439a4e4b161</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1786299832</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Medtronic MiniMed">
  <data key="d0">Medtronic MiniMed</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Medtronic MiniMed is a brand of insulin pump that can integrate with continuous glucose monitoring sensors.&lt;SEP&gt;Medtronic MiniMed is a medical device company located in Northridge, CA, USA, producing insulin pumps.&lt;SEP&gt;A CGM sensor integrated with Medtronic insulin pumps.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b6828aacfba0c2a6ae59c439a4e4b161&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f2dcbcd5e78200b20900f8955c826b2e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-08c7f7bb0209cabd75e27f9c8556c214</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/Documento sem título.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1786333895</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="FreeStyle Libre">
  <data key="d0">FreeStyle Libre</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">FreeStyle Libre is a CGM device that operates without calibration and provides up to 14 days of continuous glucose data.&lt;SEP&gt;A CGM sensor that works without calibration for up to 14 days, widely used in Brazil.&lt;SEP&gt;FreeStyle Libre is a standalone continuous glucose monitoring device that does not require calibration for its 14‑day sensor life.&lt;SEP&gt;FreeStyle Libre is the Brazilian‑available version of the flash glucose monitoring system that lacks alarm features for high or low glucose.&lt;SEP&gt;FreeStyle Libre is a continuous glucose monitoring device available in Brazil that lacks alarm features for high or low glucose levels.&lt;SEP&gt;FreeStyle Libre is a continuous glucose monitoring device.&lt;SEP&gt;FreeStyle Libre is an SFMG sensor produced by Abbott that is factory‑calibrated.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b6828aacfba0c2a6ae59c439a4e4b161&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-08c7f7bb0209cabd75e27f9c8556c214&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-94150b57cc35a773b7c36f33f237f8a1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-40fdfdc209a5e3bb46f199c55baac15b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-93594146e1ebe099cfc47906e940939f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-05cc642337c2a615c9b40de9336aec18&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7ac99b8588a8c480f44a5519509f7713</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/Documento sem título.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/cgm.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/monitoramento contínuo de glicose.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/blood glucose monitoring.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/glicemias capilares.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786338536</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Dexcom">
  <data key="d0">Dexcom</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Dexcom is a manufacturer of continuous glucose monitoring devices.&lt;SEP&gt;Dexcom is a company that provided grant funding and study supplies to R.W.B.&lt;SEP&gt;Dexcom is a company that provides consulting fees to author C.G.P.&lt;SEP&gt;A company that manufactures CGM sensors, including the Dexcom G6.&lt;SEP&gt;Dexcom is a company producing standalone continuous glucose monitoring devices.&lt;SEP&gt;Dexcom is the company that develops the Dexcom G6 continuous glucose monitoring system.&lt;SEP&gt;Dexcom is a commercial classic SMCG device listed among currently available sensors.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b6828aacfba0c2a6ae59c439a4e4b161&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2767372b4b5395439f542016058306a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5419de5a030f812ab408ef47f361bebd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-08c7f7bb0209cabd75e27f9c8556c214&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-94150b57cc35a773b7c36f33f237f8a1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-40fdfdc209a5e3bb46f199c55baac15b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7ac99b8588a8c480f44a5519509f7713</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/cengiz-beck-2026-use-of-inhaled-insulin-with-automated-insulin-delivery-systems.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/edelman-et-al-2026-dosing-afrezza-it-s-not-that-complicated.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/Documento sem título.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/cgm.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/monitoramento contínuo de glicose.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/glicemias capilares.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786338536</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Dexcom G6">
  <data key="d0">Dexcom G6</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Dexcom G6 is a CGM system approved for making direct insulin‑dosing decisions without finger‑prick confirmation.&lt;SEP&gt;A CGM sensor approved in the United States for direct insulin dosing decisions.&lt;SEP&gt;Dexcom G6 is a continuous glucose monitoring system approved in 2018 by the FDA, operating without capillary calibration, featuring a small transmitter and a sensor usable for up to ten days, and transmitting glucose data every five minutes.&lt;SEP&gt;Dexcom G6 is a specific rtCGM device that has been designated as an integrated CGM (iCGM) device and received FDA approval for use with AID systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Dexcom G6 is a continuous glucose monitoring device.&lt;SEP&gt;Dexcom G6 is a continuous glucose monitoring device evaluated for accuracy in hospitalized patients.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b6828aacfba0c2a6ae59c439a4e4b161&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-08c7f7bb0209cabd75e27f9c8556c214&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-40fdfdc209a5e3bb46f199c55baac15b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-05cc642337c2a615c9b40de9336aec18&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5958ff9ae6e3f3fb00f413f28bcde97c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0fe1eff7b58582dec4c8ae7578e20e66</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/Documento sem título.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/monitoramento contínuo de glicose.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/blood glucose monitoring.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786335935</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="REPLACE-BG Study">
  <data key="d0">REPLACE-BG Study</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">The REPLACE-BG Study is a clinical trial that evaluated the safety and efficacy of using Dexcom G6 data for insulin dosing in adults with Type 1 Diabetes.&lt;SEP&gt;A clinical study demonstrating safety of Dexcom G6 for adults with well‑controlled Type 1 Diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b6828aacfba0c2a6ae59c439a4e4b161&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-08c7f7bb0209cabd75e27f9c8556c214</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/Documento sem título.docx</data>
