</node>
<node id="Lag Time">
  <data key="d0">Lag Time</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Lag time refers to the approximate 10‑minute delay between glucose values measured by the sensor in interstitial fluid and values obtained from a finger‑prick blood test.&lt;SEP&gt;The ~10‑minute delay between sensor glucose readings and finger‑stick blood glucose values.&lt;SEP&gt;Lag Time is the average 10‑minute delay between capillary glucose measurements and interstitial glucose readings.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b6828aacfba0c2a6ae59c439a4e4b161&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-08c7f7bb0209cabd75e27f9c8556c214&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-94150b57cc35a773b7c36f33f237f8a1</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/Documento sem título.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/cgm.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786335244</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Glucose Reading">
  <data key="d0">Glucose Reading</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">A glucose reading is a numeric value, usually expressed in mg/dL, representing the concentration of glucose in blood or interstitial fluid.&lt;SEP&gt;The measured value of blood glucose entered into the insulin pump.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b6828aacfba0c2a6ae59c439a4e4b161&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e91ce385a4956221ce891caa7456655a</data>
