<node id="Insulin NPH">
  <data key="d0">Insulin NPH</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Insulin NPH (Neutral Protamine Hagedorn) is a conventional intermediate‑acting human insulin that serves as a basal component in diabetes therapy. It is administered by subcutaneous injection, typically once daily or in divided doses (often once or twice daily), providing a prolonged glucose‑lowering effect that forms the background insulin of a treatment regimen. In clinical practice the product can be mixed in the same syringe with a rapid‑acting insulin (e.g., NovoRapid®); when this is done the vial should be gently agitated before aspiration to keep the protamine‑bound insulin properly suspended.

The preparation is widely used across both pediatric and adult study populations and is frequently selected as the comparator basal insulin in clinical trials. It has historically been the standard basal insulin against which newer basal formulations—most notably insulin glargine (e.g., BASAGLAR, Levemir®)—are evaluated for safety, efficacy, dose‑titration intensity, glycemic control, and weight‑gain outcomes. Insulin NPH has therefore appeared as the reference insulin in randomized controlled trials, including studies involving pregnant women, where it is compared with Levemir® to assess maternal and fetal glycemic management.

Because of its established pharmacokinetic profile and long‑standing use, Insulin NPH continues to function as a benchmark basal insulin in research protocols, providing a consistent point of comparison for newer basal analogues and for investigations of dosing strategies in diverse patient groups.&lt;SEP&gt;Insulin NPH is an intermediate‑acting insulin compared with rapid‑acting analogues.&lt;SEP&gt;Insulin NPH is a type of insulin mentioned as being used, though its use is discussed in the text.&lt;SEP&gt;Insulin NPH is an intermediate‑acting human insulin used as a comparator for basal insulinization.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e4654b5e9fa02cf051c2d5ebc846c5d6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d8310c065da1c624d58d9a0a8e9ff7d4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b4f2935f492529f0d551140b53a84fe3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9725072a361e9b1b97c5daa35e061e58&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ecd2466ef4258dade38fbadd495188e5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-29e9c7394777a2e452b57285541f75f2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bbae57922175913b7c36c594b4673fa2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f14ce019f10c2a88765380143498ba5b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-91f290894e2d3b4216cac1721f22bb67&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-93623071acdcd0ba060c8826ab5a2a81&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b18f8ab53481bf1b63fda1bb71fe80ec&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50a4f77ab697e068f8cf31533065722b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-767d025776f0f59c05788e25616f412c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-42ddf181cf4422a3b24643a2252d99b0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9bcc4202330d45ebfca8f79c3d4998b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3059be019782459a72891cea5e0434ea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b4d7abd3e1e5418ee5a931e28a18e8ad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-56fc1d5df1b34d9120c3cf8a760c40f9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6fba8ea0c6bdb8427804ba05f9fe49f9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-277e136948d5572acf031988fd092dce&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-65cd86aee374fd1ea91bb4fd5ebee2a7</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/NOVORAPID _ BulasMed.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Basaglar.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Toujeo.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_apidra.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/Insulinoterapia – Diretriz da Sociedade Brasileira de Diabetes – Ed. 2024.pdf</data>
