  <data key="d2">Dead Space refers to residual insulin that remains trapped in a syringe, leading to medication waste and dosing errors.&lt;SEP&gt;Dead space is the residual insulin volume that remains in a syringe, potentially causing waste and dosing errors.&lt;SEP&gt;Residual volume remaining in a syringe after injection; fixed‑needle syringes are described as having no dead space.</data>
