<node id="Lipo‑hipertrofia (LH)">
  <data key="d0">Lipo‑hipertrofia (LH)</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Lipo‑hipertrofia is the most common form of lipodystrophy, producing hard nodules from fat accumulation at injection sites.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-525086e26636af026c417773a8f11a92</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1786299837</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Lipoatrofia">
  <data key="d0">Lipoatrofia</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Lipoatrofia is a relatively uncommon form of lipodystrophy (also referred to as lipodistrofia) that manifests as a localized loss or thinning of subcutaneous fatty tissue. It is specifically characterized by the reduction of subcutaneous fat at sites where injections are repeatedly administered, most frequently insulin injections. The condition can produce visible depressions or indentations in the skin where the fat layer has diminished.

Clinically, lipoatrofia presents as a focal atrophy of the subcutaneous layer, resulting in a noticeable thinning of the tissue beneath the epidermis. The loss of fat is typically confined to the injection site rather than being generalized across the body, and it may be identified as a distinct type of tissue loss in patient examinations.

Lipoatrofia has been reported as an adverse reaction in patients receiving insulin therapy, including those treated with insulin glargine, although it is considered uncommon. In some pharmacovigilance documentation the event is listed separately from the standard adverse‑event tables, whereas other sources cite it explicitly as an adverse reaction observed in insulin‑treated individuals. The overall consensus is that repeated injections at the same location increase the risk of developing this localized subcutaneous fat loss.&lt;SEP&gt;Lipoatrofia is a form of lipodystrophy involving loss of subcutaneous fat at injection sites.&lt;SEP&gt;Lipoatrofia is a subtype of lipodistrofia characterized by loss of subcutaneous fat.&lt;SEP&gt;Lipoatrophy is skin depression that can result from lipodystrophy.&lt;SEP&gt;Lipoatrofia is a rarer type of lipodystrophy, characterized by loss of fat at injection sites forming depressions in the skin.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-525086e26636af026c417773a8f11a92&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-da4ea6b1580793801f801a34c92f1905&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-74b3171b97fd80965359afadc0af9312&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c032d0271c85fd24982516368a62b1a9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-11cce86325de9748e794648198242578&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-22df77f7bf817d736d90608e62a11d84&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-da44554b006e6bd1b841f4246a054669&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d194d06ef99b3f8aa6b6542b7e93e762&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-072d97721eef045503ec1dce0363b58e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3e50c145614f04be2319a31b74b80411&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-922791f49d1bf928fe4f02ddd336927b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a7ca732691e1cbcafd65e378b8d80144&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-929e31613caadc967412041c8c2155b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-55f8c8b2b40633cf37993b620002b889</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/TRESIBA _ BulasMed.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Basaglar.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/Documento sem título.docx</data>
