<node id="Children">
  <data key="d0">Children</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Children are defined as minor, pediatric patients and constitute a distinct patient group in clinical, safety, and pharmacological contexts. In general usage the term refers to individuals who have not reached the age of majority and therefore require special protection when handling medications, medical devices, and other product components. Because children are a vulnerable population, all medicines—especially injectable therapies—must be stored out of their reach to prevent accidental ingestion, needle sticks, or misuse. This includes keeping open sharps containers, insulin pens (e.g., BASAGLAR KWIKPEN, BASAGLAR, SoloStar) and associated needles away from children, as well as any other insulin products such as Humalog, Humulin R, and long‑acting insulin degludec (Tresiba®).

When insulin therapy is prescribed for children, specific administration techniques are recommended. In pediatric patients the injection angle should be 45 degrees, and dosing must be closely coordinated with food intake and physical activity to maintain stable glucose levels. Children are particularly susceptible to severe hypoglycemia if insulin is delivered intramuscularly, making careful site selection and accurate dose calculation essential. Age‑related prescribing limits apply to several insulin products: Tresiba® may be used in children older than one year, but there is no established safety data for infants younger than twelve months; Apidra (insulin glulisine) has only been studied in children aged four years or older; and Humulin R guidance mentions usage for patients under three years of age or older, depending on the specific indication.

In clinical research, the term “children” has been used to denote narrower age brackets. For example, a pharmacokinetic study of Novolin® R enrolled patients aged 6 to 12 years, and the same age range (6‑12 years) is referenced in a diabetes study cohort. These study‑specific definitions do not alter the broader clinical meaning but illustrate that investigators may limit the group to a sub‑population of minors relevant to the trial objectives.

Beyond medication safety, children are also a user group for whom small parts of medical transmitters or devices present a choking hazard. Product labeling therefore advises that any detachable components that could be placed in the mouth be kept away from young users.

Overall, “children” encompasses all minor patients, with particular attention to age‑specific dosing, storage, and device‑safety requirements. Clinicians and caregivers must evaluate the developmental stage of each child, adhere to age‑appropriate prescribing information, and ensure that all medication, sharps, and small parts are securely stored out of reach to protect this vulnerable population.&lt;SEP&gt;Patients including infants and small children, for whom insulin Aspart ultrarapid can be used from one year of age and continuous insulin infusion is recommended as primary therapy.&lt;SEP&gt;A population group in which hypoglycemia occurs more frequently due to insulin overdose, missed meals, or intense activity.&lt;SEP&gt;Individuals under the age of adolescence, a population group discussed in relation to type 2 diabetes prevalence and screening.&lt;SEP&gt;Children are a pediatric population referenced for diabetes screening.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-525086e26636af026c417773a8f11a92&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a8768fa32f88d682aa4ddf677297047e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cc6a26a5d2c41087b58a0f7f71ad21cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4902fb11e4844af5cf6fd61f18b6e4ce&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e89f1dbae629e925f06732cebf41df16&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4704ea4d5c15ebc8c043a077f05fd7a3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e9ae5f9ffa7eff9bb36cf1a9764df3e7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0a20360c489112f7848983049bae7125&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0b9c41c968bcc1d46185583661e8f989&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3db0edd23b6b502ccbbf62bfd601ce68&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d96761d60c65f05f1530bc19b144cf1b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4ce520f0fe7dc4a6c79f92a25dfaff19&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d65840dd2cbd5c9984dfc4334378df5e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ffe095bda1b787c5b5ae2d61a2f74c98&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e9835d6684db67541402527b3182b6c5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5c24a2af0d0291fc4f4730256c420e93&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dd396c45bc09fb646d156b4e69d328e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0955cb70a6ce135722726162a9811e78&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea9b3836b3275f451c3acfb189f42a6f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-577779892c0d463cd6bb1966b8a8ce2d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-de69fd058597c808e8be5bd334395b84&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-379a204614747df98c1296e2f76c264f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db5749bec4af1c3ea068b257c4376aaf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ca8620e735c40bfe850134ccea9a7154&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dd2bfbe7cac15c6f6dc444a35691ae83&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-343246c2eef6e8430b581340d6cd4762&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0631ff2b95dd459677eaaebe9283a776</data>
