<node id="Hemoglobin A1c">
  <data key="d0">Hemoglobin A1c</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Hemoglobin A1c is a laboratory measurement of glycated hemoglobin that serves as a clinical biomarker for long‑term glycemic control. By quantifying the proportion of hemoglobin molecules with glucose attached, the test reflects average blood glucose concentrations over the preceding two to three months, providing a retrospective view of glucose exposure across several weeks. Because it captures sustained glucose levels rather than momentary fluctuations, Hemoglobin A1c is widely used to evaluate chronic blood‑sugar control in individuals with diabetes.  

In clinical practice, Hemoglobin A1c is a routine screening and monitoring tool for diabetes management, often reported in Ambulatory Glucose Profile reports and other standard care pathways. The abbreviated term “HbA1c” is commonly used in medical records and patient education to denote this glycated hemoglobin assay.  

Hemoglobin A1c also functions as a primary efficacy endpoint in diabetes research. It appears frequently in clinical trial outcomes, such as studies of insulin formulations (e.g., Apidra SoloStar) and other glucose‑lowering therapies, and is cited across numerous observational and interventional studies that examine long‑term blood‑glucose trends.  

Overall, Hemoglobin A1c provides a reliable, retrospective indicator of average blood glucose over several weeks to months, making it essential for both individual patient management and the evaluation of therapeutic interventions in diabetes research.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-986fc7ecc813c4b7942964d7fd64d429&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-45d489de28e8fda3c3be3bb09ab29eb2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db832f06717859b8ba6cf7fd70aa22d8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7084240a735ca2fe3b6d426e3b8c5756&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-162882e6afffb0db8ae5e9153e5f1e82&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-08c7f7bb0209cabd75e27f9c8556c214&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-93594146e1ebe099cfc47906e940939f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1dec009976a44828d0e619e7fa5b1c5d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-22078404beeceb5adc3e688d239c585e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2d8f17f3f250a37a1effaaa88cc8b382&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-29ea6999715cd3886bd7d4abc2a653b0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b2cd796639bdb0e10eeda7ef3d9ebbce&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-44888abd4ca8a1953f751ed6c41922e6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c14456299df06b01b603504def87f381&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a22fadf52eaea018160e4dd41d1d39b8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-84032013252fd71963ed381e09a3116d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Basaglar.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_1778357531609.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_apidra.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/Documento sem título.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/monitoramento contínuo de glicose.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/ref.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/Documento sem título.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/glicemias capilares.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Metas glicêmicas/Metas no tratamento.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Metas glicêmicas/metas cuidado do diabetes.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377234</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Capillary Glucose Test">
  <data key="d0">Capillary Glucose Test</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The capillary glucose test, performed by a finger prick, measures the blood glucose concentration at a specific moment.&lt;SEP&gt;Capillary Glucose Test is a method for measuring blood glucose from a finger prick sample.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-986fc7ecc813c4b7942964d7fd64d429&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2d8f17f3f250a37a1effaaa88cc8b382</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/glicemias capilares.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786338528</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Time In Range">
  <data key="d0">Time In Range</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Time In Range is a metric indicating the percentage of time that blood glucose stays within the target range of 70–180 mg/dL.&lt;SEP&gt;Time In Range (TIR) denotes the percentage of time glucose values stay within a target range.&lt;SEP&gt;Time In Range (TIR) measures the percentage of time glucose values stay within a target range, an outcome improved by AID use.&lt;SEP&gt;Time in Range (TIR) is the proportion of time glucose values stay within a predefined target range.&lt;SEP&gt;Metric indicating the percentage of time glucose stays within the target range of 70–180 mg/dL.&lt;SEP&gt;Time In Range (TIR) is a metric representing the percentage of time glucose values stay within the target range.&lt;SEP&gt;Time In Range represents the percentage of time glucose values fall within specified target ranges, with detailed percentages for very high, high, target, low, and very low zones.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-986fc7ecc813c4b7942964d7fd64d429&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9cd925790899146eeb8a373879b5feac&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-511f6be03d2ea98970bd4c1b29b3e5c8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d35e6caf612b4c4984ade9315ebc7431&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c5c8fa42a8437c5708b04fb4ad1272cf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b275f50028ef32e322bf8643e0342810&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a19f43c10a7a756e1597ff1a7f53296e</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/blood glucose monitoring.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Metas glicêmicas/Metas no tratamento.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Metas glicêmicas/metas cuidado do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786372155</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Individualized Goals">
  <data key="d0">Individualized Goals</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Individualized goals are personalized blood glucose targets tailored to a person's age, health status, diabetes type, and lifestyle.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-986fc7ecc813c4b7942964d7fd64d429</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1786299838</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Children And Adolescents With Type 1 Diabetes">
  <data key="d0">Children And Adolescents With Type 1 Diabetes</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">This group includes children and teenagers who have type 1 diabetes and follow specific glycemic targets.&lt;SEP&gt;Young patients diagnosed with type 1 diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-986fc7ecc813c4b7942964d7fd64d429&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c5c8fa42a8437c5708b04fb4ad1272cf</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Metas glicêmicas/Metas no tratamento.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786370041</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Adults With Type 1 Or Type 2 Diabetes">
  <data key="d0">Adults With Type 1 Or Type 2 Diabetes</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">This group comprises adult individuals diagnosed with type 1 or type 2 diabetes, for whom standard glycemic targets are recommended.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-986fc7ecc813c4b7942964d7fd64d429</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1786299838</data>
