  <data key="d5">1786303804</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="45° Angle">
  <data key="d0">45° Angle</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The recommended needle insertion angle for abdominal insulin injections during the first two trimesters of pregnancy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ae9010ed1abd5a5160b82713c862d22f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1786299840</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Third Trimester">
  <data key="d0">Third Trimester</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The final stage of pregnancy during which abdominal insulin injection is not recommended.&lt;SEP&gt;Third Trimester is the final three‑month period of pregnancy during which insulin needs generally increase.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ae9010ed1abd5a5160b82713c862d22f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c95471c4c993fa3a499f99443ee7c922</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_apidra.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786315459</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Used Needle">
  <data key="d0">Used Needle</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">A needle that has already been used for insulin injection and must be disposed of in a rigid collector.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ae9010ed1abd5a5160b82713c862d22f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0b9c41c968bcc1d46185583661e8f989</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1786299840</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Repeated Insulin Injection">
  <data key="d0">Repeated Insulin Injection</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The practice of administering insulin multiple times in the same skin area, which increases risk of lipohypertrophy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ae9010ed1abd5a5160b82713c862d22f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1786299840</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Person with Tremors">
  <data key="d0">Person with Tremors</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">An individual who experiences tremors or motor limitations and may need assistance or a larger needle for insulin injection.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ae9010ed1abd5a5160b82713c862d22f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1786299841</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Needle Bending Risk">
  <data key="d0">Needle Bending Risk</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The possibility that a needle may become bent during use, potentially affecting injection comfort and efficacy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ae9010ed1abd5a5160b82713c862d22f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1786299841</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Infection Risk">
  <data key="d0">Infection Risk</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The increased chance of infection when needles or syringes are reused or not disposed of properly.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ae9010ed1abd5a5160b82713c862d22f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1786299841</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Healthcare Professional">
  <data key="d0">Healthcare Professional</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Healthcare Professional refers to a qualified medical practitioner—such as a doctor, nurse, diabetes educator, or other certified clinician—who provides comprehensive guidance, education, and oversight for individuals using insulin therapy and associated diabetes technologies. In this role the professional instructs patients and caregivers on proper insulin injection techniques, including skin examination, site cleaning with alcohol or antiseptic, and rotation of injection sites to avoid common administration errors. They also prescribe insulin, offer treatment recommendations, and respond to acute events such as severe hypoglycemia or ketoacidosis.

For users of advanced devices, the Healthcare Professional delivers specialized training on the MiniMed 780G system and other insulin pumps, covering safe use, emergency‑kit composition, and device‑specific instructions. They determine and personalize pump parameters—including basal patterns, maximum basal and bolus rates, active insulin time, and sensor alert settings—based on the individual’s glycemic history and therapeutic goals. The professional is consulted to adjust these settings, interpret alerts, and program the recommended values accurately into the pump. Guidance also extends to appropriate wait times after manual injections before reactivating SmartGuard features.

The Healthcare Professional advises on medication interactions that may affect continuous glucose monitoring (CGM) or pump performance, such as hydroxyurea, acetaminophen, or other interfering drugs, and recommends when a temporary glucose target should be set. If pump therapy is discontinued, the practitioner helps determine alternate insulin delivery methods and provides instructions for transitioning back to injections. Throughout care, the Healthcare Professional supports glucose monitoring, educates on device maintenance, and serves as the primary point of contact for any health‑related questions, ensuring safe, effective, and individualized insulin management.&lt;SEP&gt;Medical provider who determines insulin dose, teaches glucose monitoring, and advises proper storage.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-03a1de93a53fbcb513268c123e2c5a16&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b5b4c60b3de8c56d9ab869d868345fb7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e9ae5f9ffa7eff9bb36cf1a9764df3e7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-55f8c8b2b40633cf37993b620002b889&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cdb000b83632c89167783ad4e6f1fb64&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-05241912c4f8f5e79ae75071a1c7c604&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4a4a75301f61fc3c86ad768de09d0c3f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8cceea4f7036977c7ddcbe81f76f8aa1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-474703bb16e6e26e009e9d433c3d3647&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d68acc5f59d78c14cf4d2e4d34edf5e4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-caf5071e54a797f595d8cac8e4653918&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-379a204614747df98c1296e2f76c264f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-df77f2ea988e5724effb4c71cc79a65a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b03b7fdf0dd9c96dc459929ccccdccff&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fe844728a502927fee80d42268408b1a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a0267d2986a48c4c31790b6f183277dc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-28515a0aca492eeee478cd9947226498&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bcdc240f555b6c71532ea6d04e0c5798&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6b53b69acbef0e172ea7719cc15bf3ad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ae3b43add031516d14e51c6d2a985bd7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3d0824c9d8a9ff5f2da52b7b5ea69c86&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-27b3ea1063acf8e0a407a89daea0dc32&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9ec9cae555a06ac660e6c16d90116c8b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a01dc8dc15b92e2b0b570753b0f57632&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-14031c05fdb4152e391234af47d0cfe4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d3b794ead59ea83de139af0358a0e7b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a764dcbdd73fd1c50fa72a7cd60b6e19&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7827239a998e7ac7379613d9e5f81ae0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7b2af59ac9cf813cb07dac53f30250d0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1dd74224daea51112742135154e46244&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-36ace822cd4873b8fd2adcfef0a7f9fd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f677e56841fc57bffd8bf5b6cc4a7797&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b907eb92deb747df3fb3b37fb9974142&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-20af4762343b8357c2c72473211f2918&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dd545bc80ceae270c16406af736789b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e8e9d04ca4b641b5d8d5ef85044f4566&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dcea1ff62aae96936f552880e96faa69&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f94cd06ab0d1bcc7a9349bc40ea3eb22&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-59d8fcf807f0beb090b2f3d68cc7c168&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c7e6ef38db0b62d161b13473af47d738</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/TRESIBA _ BulasMed.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/Documento sem título.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/Documento sem título.docx</data>
