</node>
<node id="Hospital">
  <data key="d0">Hospital</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">Hospital is a healthcare organization and medical facility that provides inpatient care and implements comprehensive protocols for the safe administration of insulin. Within the hospital setting, electronic prescriptions, continuous staff training, and double‑check procedures are standard practice to ensure accurate dosing, whether insulin is given routinely, emergently by intramuscular or intravenous injection, or administered under direct supervision.

The institution also enforces diabetes device policies, managing the use of insulin pumps, continuous glucose monitors, and related equipment for admitted patients. Hospitals admit individuals with diabetes who present with severe hyperglycemia, infection, dehydration, or other acute complications, offering a controlled environment for monitoring and treatment.

In addition to therapeutic services, hospitals maintain dedicated collection points and appropriate containers for the disposal of used needles, syringes, and cartridges. These disposal bins are strategically placed throughout the facility to promote safe handling of sharps and to comply with infection‑control standards.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-03a1de93a53fbcb513268c123e2c5a16&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3d0de4d525c273cda4939a501eaecc6d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8abf9336f83edf5c92071da1032dc483&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9725072a361e9b1b97c5daa35e061e58&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-df616353e032c899b02bfa4368bc2667&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2cd48799a027437b9fe2e1a48b61cb3d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6fe769b03fc66d4a691f3b7f741b92cb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-345ad64f464691cc28341ccd246032db</data>
