<node id="Alcohol">
  <data key="d0">Alcohol</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Alcohol refers to ethanol‑containing substances that play two distinct roles in the context of insulin therapy.  Medical‑grade alcohol, typically a 70 % solution of isopropyl or ethyl alcohol, is used as a topical disinfectant; a small amount is applied to a cotton swab and wiped on the skin immediately before an insulin injection or before placing an infusion set, and the site is allowed to air‑dry completely to reduce infection risk.  In addition, alcoholic beverages—any consumable drink that contains ethanol—directly influence glucose metabolism in people who use insulin.

When consumed, alcohol can either intensify or diminish insulin’s glucose‑lowering (hypoglycaemic) effect, producing unpredictable fluctuations in blood‑glucose levels.  It inhibits hepatic glucose output, leading to a gradual decline in circulating glucose and thereby increasing the risk of hypoglycaemia, especially after excessive intake.  Consequently, alcohol consumption may raise the likelihood of hypoglycaemia, lower the amount of insulin required to achieve glycaemic targets, or, conversely, blunt insulin action and cause hyperglycaemia.

Alcohol also affects sensor glucose measurements.  In some continuous glucose monitoring (CGM) systems, recent alcohol intake has been reported to produce higher sensor glucose readings, reflecting its impact on interstitial glucose dynamics and the sensor’s calibration algorithms.

Because of these bidirectional and dose‑dependent effects, individuals on insulin—whether using rapid‑acting formulations such as Humalog or long‑acting analogues such as Tresiba®—are advised to monitor blood glucose closely when alcohol is consumed, consider possible adjustments to insulin dosing, and adhere strictly to proper injection‑site preparation using alcohol as a disinfectant.  Careful surveillance helps mitigate the heightened risk of hypoglycaemia and ensures more accurate glucose monitoring.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-03a1de93a53fbcb513268c123e2c5a16&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-84c3145631d64a0c7b9ea21dfb9c8275&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4d26ce64e79b8c4a147140be2f9c63dd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-048d8fafb712e12cec45f2d3ec2c1e3b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4704ea4d5c15ebc8c043a077f05fd7a3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e9ae5f9ffa7eff9bb36cf1a9764df3e7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0b9c41c968bcc1d46185583661e8f989&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3db0edd23b6b502ccbbf62bfd601ce68&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d96761d60c65f05f1530bc19b144cf1b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4ce520f0fe7dc4a6c79f92a25dfaff19&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fd94288932ad6675a1de2b46b3fd9128&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-465ad8b77c1c2a2a179062da20337ff5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f09811b149a29105854a0b1e84951e5d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6c32255a7f064c18ff0b079798cfeaf5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cedd8e88a8d35eade68ce02222b9e276&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3237e202569462c758ec3d878c9faeae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-df616353e032c899b02bfa4368bc2667&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1e622f0079074cd1916470223d22aa66&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1f5ccf80661c0e52c3a3465ab87c6343&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-59137a5f20ce729bcde5c65e1e45aa29&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6ab7cedc48ea8fdd199a2c12c99416a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3ce8c9873da330aac077f7ccaf108ccd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-05cc642337c2a615c9b40de9336aec18</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Documento sem título.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/Bula Humalog.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/NOVORAPID _ BulasMed.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/TRESIBA _ BulasMed.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Basaglar.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_1778357531609.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_apidra.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_fiasp.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/blood glucose monitoring.pdf</data>
