<node id="Pancreas">
  <data key="d0">Pancreas</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Pancreas is a dual‑purpose organ in the human body that belongs to the digestive system but is primarily renowned for its crucial role in glucose homeostasis. It continuously monitors blood‑glucose concentrations and, in response, synthesizes and releases the hormone insulin, adjusting the rate of secretion to match the body’s current metabolic needs. This insulin release occurs in two patterns: a low‑level basal secretion that maintains glucose balance between meals, and rapid bolus bursts that manage the rise in glucose after food intake.  

In addition to insulin, the pancreas also produces the counter‑regulatory hormone glucagon, which raises blood glucose when levels fall, thereby providing a complementary mechanism for precise regulation of circulating sugar. The organ’s endocrine function is so central to diabetes management that medical devices such as the MiniMed 780G insulin pump are designed to emulate its natural insulin‑secreting behavior.  

Thus, the pancreas integrates digestive functions with endocrine activity, detecting glucose levels and orchestrating the secretion of insulin and glucagon to keep blood‑sugar concentrations within a narrow, healthy range.&lt;SEP&gt;Pancreas is the organ whose ducts were ligated, leading to degeneration used in early insulin research.&lt;SEP&gt;Pancreas is the organ from which extracts were prepared for experimental treatment.&lt;SEP&gt;The pancreas is a glandular organ that synthesizes and secretes insulin.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2a0a3f492aa5ef7771b2246547cb5f02&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b7715667f5fca178f0988984e932ecfb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-65c6beab51324e055f4a39b388e2eefe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9f4d152d83c514f926b18413e065c2fa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-780f90d656277126a05ed136a084fd77&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6b867cec4c5eed3b10e431cbd4078dee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b03b7fdf0dd9c96dc459929ccccdccff&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c7e6ef38db0b62d161b13473af47d738&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eff48c1408719e81f1f423f76dfd19e5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ad5d126f417014eb5c7a07a85db48d1d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0932e9c21a330869629b3fa70d2e1f5e</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/Documento sem título.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/The Discovery and Development.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/Understanding insulin - International Diabetes Federation.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786332445</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Diabetes Type 1">
  <data key="d0">Diabetes Type 1</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Diabetes Type 1 is a chronic autoimmune disease in which the immune system selectively destroys the pancreatic β‑cells, resulting in an absolute and lifelong deficiency of endogenous insulin. Because the body cannot produce insulin, individuals with Diabetes Type 1 must receive exogenous insulin every day, typically dosed at 0.5–1.0 UI per kilogram of body weight. Insulin can be delivered through multiple daily injections or continuous subcutaneous insulin infusion (insulin pump), and the dosage is often adjusted for each patient.

The condition most frequently presents in children and adolescents, although it can be diagnosed at any age. Without sufficient insulin, patients are prone to persistent hyperglycaemia and, in severe cases, diabetic ketoacidosis. At the same time, the need to match insulin delivery with food intake and physical activity creates a heightened risk of hypoglycaemia if dosing, nutrition, or activity are not carefully balanced. Management therefore centres on individualized insulin therapy combined with regular self‑monitoring of glucose concentrations.

Diabetes Type 1 is also a defined patient population in a wide range of pharmacological and clinical research. It is commonly used as the comparator group in studies evaluating new insulin formulations, delivery devices (e.g., Levemir®, Novolin® R FlexPen®), and adjunctive therapies aimed at improving glycaemic control and reducing hypoglycaemic episodes. The disease serves as the target cohort in pharmacodynamic investigations such as the APIDRA studies and in trials including specific sub‑populations, for example pregnant women with Diabetes Type 1. Across these contexts, the disease is referenced for its characteristic insulin deficiency, the necessity of daily insulin administration, and the associated risks of both hyper‑ and hypoglycaemia.&lt;SEP&gt;Autoimmune condition in which the body does not produce any insulin, requiring daily insulin administration.&lt;SEP&gt;Diabetes type 1 (DM1) is a form of diabetes where the body stops producing insulin because the immune system attacks the pancreatic cells that make insulin.&lt;SEP&gt;Diabetes Type 1 is a chronic condition characterized by insufficient insulin production.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2a0a3f492aa5ef7771b2246547cb5f02&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6e42637e4286cbc19cce4502b22634bd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ecd2466ef4258dade38fbadd495188e5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6b14c2f0985ae4a417c8fc99e339bd9e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f14ce019f10c2a88765380143498ba5b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3a279eef99c9c70338c74ffc7b4e260e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6ca13e396b094f0c2f482892f220f538&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bf25fca295be60e28b7c7d3103f722fc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3397508bdfddde019cb1dfdcfb352435&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7621ac447c9044986ade86ce5f9be201&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8ef15154a94043650617b3b24d8146a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-68b98187c6ab15468f1c0d8f5e7f9f6a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f36263c657ad99a80e578ac49a333d5b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-42ddf181cf4422a3b24643a2252d99b0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9a6f9e10c0d4af5fff0338eb861f9c86&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dd396c45bc09fb646d156b4e69d328e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0955cb70a6ce135722726162a9811e78&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-acaa1440ae268669e1894588bb9e37c2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-df616353e032c899b02bfa4368bc2667&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2cd48799a027437b9fe2e1a48b61cb3d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c7e6ef38db0b62d161b13473af47d738&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-22078404beeceb5adc3e688d239c585e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7ac99b8588a8c480f44a5519509f7713</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/NOVORAPID _ BulasMed.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Basaglar.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_1778357531609.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Toujeo.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_apidra.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/Documento sem título.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/Documento sem título.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/glicemias capilares.pdf</data>
