</node>
<node id="Ultra-rapid Insulin">
  <data key="d0">Ultra-rapid Insulin</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Ultra‑rapid insulin is an even faster insulin type that begins working in 2 to 5 minutes and peaks within 30 minutes to 1 hour.&lt;SEP&gt;An even faster insulin formulation used for glucose regulation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2a0a3f492aa5ef7771b2246547cb5f02&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-91a09040fc4581d7aad2216dba9fba79</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/cgm.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786335246</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Intermediate Insulin">
  <data key="d0">Intermediate Insulin</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Intermediate insulin (NPH) is an insulin type that starts acting in 1 to 3 hours, peaks between 4 and 10 hours, and lasts 10 to 18 hours.&lt;SEP&gt;Intermediate Insulin is a category covering medium‑duration insulin products like NPH.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2a0a3f492aa5ef7771b2246547cb5f02&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a8768fa32f88d682aa4ddf677297047e</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Insulinas CANETAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786300725</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Long-acting Insulin">
  <data key="d0">Long-acting Insulin</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Long‑acting insulin is a basal insulin that begins working in 1 to 2 hours, has no pronounced peak, and lasts 20 to 24 hours.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2a0a3f492aa5ef7771b2246547cb5f02</data>
