<node id="Detemir">
  <data key="d0">Detemir</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Detemir is the generic name of a long‑acting insulin analog that is marketed under the brand name Levemir® and is used as the basal insulin component of that formulation. It is classified as a basal insulin formulation and is listed as an example of a long‑acting insulin in various reference tables.

Detemir is produced through recombinant DNA technology, which allows the insulin analog to be synthesized in a controlled, bioengineered process. This manufacturing method yields a molecule that has been structurally modified to prolong its duration of action compared with native human insulin.

Clinically, Detemir is employed for basal insulin therapy, providing a steady background level of insulin to manage blood glucose in individuals with diabetes. Although described as a long‑acting agent, it is also referred to as an intermediate‑acting insulin analog in some pharmacological tables, with reported activity windows that include approximately 13 hours, a 6‑8 hour range, and an extended 18‑22 hour period, reflecting its prolonged and relatively flat pharmacokinetic profile.

Detemir appears in national drug listings such as the Brazilian insulin formulation table, where it is identified among other basal insulin options. It is also cited as an illustrative entry in educational or regulatory tables that categorize long‑acting insulin products.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2a0a3f492aa5ef7771b2246547cb5f02&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aa127476a5c98492d7b7e0fcd1212886&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-42ddf181cf4422a3b24643a2252d99b0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c7e6ef38db0b62d161b13473af47d738&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fd6fa98b7767319460b4a421a719c5c2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-65cd86aee374fd1ea91bb4fd5ebee2a7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-494fef0b8efc2c44b3b49ebf9d74b7f2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9d86d36b30e6f5b8ff44caade2d2400d</data>
