<node id="Weight">
  <data key="d0">Weight</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Weight is a personal factor that influences the appropriate insulin dose.&lt;SEP&gt;Weight refers to a person's body mass, a factor that can influence insulin dosing.&lt;SEP&gt;Body mass of the patient, a factor influencing the required insulin dose.&lt;SEP&gt;Weight is a measured body mass parameter recorded in diabetes studies.&lt;SEP&gt;Weight is a body measurement mentioned as a factor where loss or failure to gain prompts screening for CFRD.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2a0a3f492aa5ef7771b2246547cb5f02&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c7e6ef38db0b62d161b13473af47d738&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e94cedc7134adbb256c931b851235c53&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-511f6be03d2ea98970bd4c1b29b3e5c8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9cdf6af658e42c2f4f7dca5e4dbdd3db</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/Documento sem título.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/blood glucose monitoring.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377353</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Carbohydrate Intake">
  <data key="d0">Carbohydrate Intake</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Carbohydrate intake is the amount of carbs in a person's diet that affects insulin dosing.&lt;SEP&gt;Carbohydrate Intake refers to the amount of carbohydrates in a meal, used to calculate bolus insulin doses.&lt;SEP&gt;Carbohydrate Intake is the consumption of carbs recommended to treat low glucose episodes.&lt;SEP&gt;Additional consumption of carbohydrates that can help prevent hypoglycemia during physical activity.&lt;SEP&gt;Carbohydrate Intake is the consumption of carbs that a bolus is intended to cover.&lt;SEP&gt;Carbohydrate Intake is the consumption of carbohydrates, mentioned as a factor to balance with insulin use and physical activity.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2a0a3f492aa5ef7771b2246547cb5f02&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-65c6beab51324e055f4a39b388e2eefe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6ab7cedc48ea8fdd199a2c12c99416a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-36de8c99d97d234e12244c240c45f156&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b907eb92deb747df3fb3b37fb9974142&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-345ad64f464691cc28341ccd246032db</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Metas glicêmicas/metas cuidado do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786372100</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Physical Activity">
  <data key="d0">Physical Activity</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Physical Activity refers to any bodily movement, exercise, or sustained exertion that influences glucose metabolism and therefore plays a central role in diabetes management. By increasing energy expenditure, physical activity can alter basal insulin needs and modify the effectiveness of rapid‑acting insulins such as Humalog, which in turn impacts overall insulin dose requirements. The level and intensity of the activity determine how much insulin adjustment is necessary, and the activity can be tailored according to real‑time glucose monitoring results.

Because exercise—especially when intense or prolonged—raises the risk of hypoglycemia, individuals who use insulin must often modify their bolus doses, synchronize insulin administration with the timing and intensity of the activity, and sometimes ingest additional carbohydrates to maintain stable blood‑glucose levels during and after the workout. In hybrid closed‑loop systems, physical activity is explicitly noted as a condition that requires insulin delivery adjustments to prevent both low and high glucose episodes.

Digital diabetes‑management programs frequently incorporate exercise encouragement, offering structured physical‑activity interventions aimed at preventing the onset of diabetes and supporting ongoing glycemic control. These programs guide users on how to align their activity patterns with insulin therapy, reinforcing the principle that physical activity is both a therapeutic tool and a variable that must be managed within the broader context of diabetes care.&lt;SEP&gt;Physical activity refers to exercise and movement that affect glucose levels and are managed using CGM data.&lt;SEP&gt;Physical Activity is the engagement in bodily movement, noted alongside insulin use and carbohydrate intake for diabetes management.&lt;SEP&gt;Exercise or movement, cited as a means to improve insulin resistance and reduce Type 2 Diabetes risk.&lt;SEP&gt;Physical Activity refers to being physically active, which reduces points in the Diabetes Risk Test.&lt;SEP&gt;Physical activity is a lifestyle practice that, together with nutrition, aids weight loss and lowers diabetes risk.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2a0a3f492aa5ef7771b2246547cb5f02&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c3daabbd42055dc30154f5f97c85fb7d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ffb10c00517fa772be2ca9a42f497edf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4704ea4d5c15ebc8c043a077f05fd7a3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-45d489de28e8fda3c3be3bb09ab29eb2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5913d17c337be62cd526d46fbdcd9a6e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6ab7cedc48ea8fdd199a2c12c99416a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d03a310916c005d1dfa70800a753d1c5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c7e6ef38db0b62d161b13473af47d738&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4b355007bba178588f3928b6c8620a78&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9cd925790899146eeb8a373879b5feac&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-40c2c862887db201b07c741a1862dcc1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c9bc5d11c9f848439320623cad3d3a38&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5227749196a4c9226dba64a500d84b3a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e428438c632682ef93541430ec497ed5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-345ad64f464691cc28341ccd246032db&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a19f43c10a7a756e1597ff1a7f53296e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2c37e26e62468b725533260347fb4e31&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-55e58732610596ce9a8f3145d34f75a7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9eb02ab1ab7d834858bf60a8b402e6ea</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/Bula Humalog.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/LANTUS _ BulasMed.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/TRESIBA _ BulasMed.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Basaglar.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/Documento sem título.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/blood glucose monitoring.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Diagnóstico de diabetes mellitus.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Metas glicêmicas/metas cuidado do diabetes.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377191</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
