<node id="Adults">
  <data key="d0">Adults</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Adults refers to the adult patient population, defined as individuals aged 18 years or older, that is used as a reference or comparison group in various insulin‑related clinical contexts. In pharmacokinetic studies of rapid‑acting insulin analogues such as Fiasp® and long‑acting formulations like Levemir®, the adult group serves as the benchmark population against which drug exposure, absorption, and overall pharmacokinetic outcomes are evaluated. Dosage recommendations for Levemir® are specifically provided for this adult cohort, and the same population is employed to assess the relative performance of other insulin products.

In clinical practice, adults are also considered when determining the appropriate injection technique for insulin delivery. For patients with low subcutaneous fat, guidance advises the use of the subcutaneous fold to ensure proper depot formation, whereas individuals with higher subcutaneous fat may not require this maneuver. Additionally, the adult population is identified as the eligible group for therapies such as insulin Tecnósfera, reinforcing its role as the primary target demographic for many insulin regimens.&lt;SEP&gt;Individuals in the adult age group who may use diabetes management technologies.&lt;SEP&gt;Adults refer to mature individuals, a population in which CFRD occurs in 40–50%.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-708e3c514f667dc9979cfa8df875e473&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cc6a26a5d2c41087b58a0f7f71ad21cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-14772c7de5db762c492a75a1c744dae6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8ef15154a94043650617b3b24d8146a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f36263c657ad99a80e578ac49a333d5b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-56fc1d5df1b34d9120c3cf8a760c40f9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dd396c45bc09fb646d156b4e69d328e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ca8620e735c40bfe850134ccea9a7154&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c93787ffd2c022283fc0663decb1a184&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9cdf6af658e42c2f4f7dca5e4dbdd3db</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Documento sem título.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/insulinas em seringa.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_fiasp.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/Insulinoterapia – Diretriz da Sociedade Brasileira de Diabetes – Ed. 2024.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/blood glucose monitoring.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377348</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Injection Site Rotation">
  <data key="d0">Injection Site Rotation</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Injection Site Rotation is the practice of regularly changing the location of insulin or other subcutaneous injections. Individuals alternate among specific areas of skin and underlying subcutaneous tissue—most commonly the abdomen, thigh, buttock, or upper arm—to avoid repeatedly using the same spot.

The primary purpose of this systematic rotation is to prevent or reduce local injection‑site reactions and tissue complications. By varying the injection site, the development of lipohypertrophy, lipodystrophy, and other skin changes is minimized, and the risk of tissue damage is lowered. Inadequate rotation is recognized as a contributing factor to the formation of lipohypertrophy.

A consistent rotation pattern also supports better glycemic control. When injections are concentrated in damaged or scarred tissue, insulin absorption can become erratic, leading to variability in blood glucose levels. By spreading injections across healthy tissue, absorption becomes more predictable, enhancing the effectiveness of insulin therapy.

Healthcare guidelines and diabetes education programs therefore recommend that patients adopt a defined rotation schedule as an essential component of safe and effective insulin administration. This practice is considered a standard self‑care strategy for anyone receiving regular subcutaneous injections.&lt;SEP&gt;The practice of changing injection locations to avoid repeated trauma and prevent lipohypertrophy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-708e3c514f667dc9979cfa8df875e473&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a8768fa32f88d682aa4ddf677297047e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-74b3171b97fd80965359afadc0af9312&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d59c9bf7f429a82cbfd7083e36ff8f9a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f9e5c50e8a808c537075377966ae2ccd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6d0f18c80f8de2dee960a03599d12052&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c95471c4c993fa3a499f99443ee7c922&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-14772c7de5db762c492a75a1c744dae6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9a6f9e10c0d4af5fff0338eb861f9c86&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dd396c45bc09fb646d156b4e69d328e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea9b3836b3275f451c3acfb189f42a6f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-acaa1440ae268669e1894588bb9e37c2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-779af610d7298ce98490962cd90b4e76&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-55f8c8b2b40633cf37993b620002b889&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c0cec9d1eb70ae81e8c1cb85f0b49621&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c7e6ef38db0b62d161b13473af47d738</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Documento sem título.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Insulinas CANETAS.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/LANTUS _ BulasMed.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/NOVORAPID _ BulasMed.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_apidra.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_fiasp.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/Documento sem título.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/O que você precisa saber sobre Lipohipertrofia - Sociedade Brasileira de Diabetes.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/Documento sem título.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1786330481</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="American Diabetes Association (ADA)">
  <data key="d0">American Diabetes Association (ADA)</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">American Diabetes Association (ADA) is a United States‑based professional organization that develops and publishes standards of care, clinical guidelines, and classification systems for diabetes. It issues recommendations on insulin injection practices, including site rotation, and provides guidance on the use of insulin pumps and other diabetes management technologies. The ADA’s guidelines also define criteria for classifying hypoglycemia and establish the terminology “pre‑diabetes” to describe individuals with intermediate hyperglycemia.  

In 2015, the ADA revised its preprandial glycemic target in response to evidence from the ADAG (A1C‑Derived Average Glucose) study, reflecting its commitment to evidence‑based updates of therapeutic goals. Beyond clinical guidance, the association is dedicated to diabetes research, education, and advocacy, serving as a widely cited reference for diabetes classification, care standards, and public health initiatives.&lt;SEP&gt;The professional organization that provides the ADA Diabetes Risk Test and related guidelines.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-708e3c514f667dc9979cfa8df875e473&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-da4ea6b1580793801f801a34c92f1905&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dfa23fc15cc4d520a32488843dbd710b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-277e136948d5572acf031988fd092dce&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b2ef71fb1a347df36dbb8ea8f4856bcb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dd2bfbe7cac15c6f6dc444a35691ae83&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5e551f4b7f03919afc1d663b3b2a2efa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cc39a0c02d5f1bd08d5cb71bacc69a24&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-54ce8d1437c0ec0329819123568df11e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ca8741dfdb9ff0f12f049953db6cb9c0</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Documento sem título.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/Orientacoes_Glicemia_SBD.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/Orientacoes_Hipoglicemia_SBD_transcricao.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Diagnóstico de diabetes mellitus.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Metas glicêmicas/metas cuidado do diabetes.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377332</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Fourteen Days">
  <data key="d0">Fourteen Days</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Fourteen days is the recommended waiting period before re‑injecting insulin in the exact same spot to allow the skin to heal.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-708e3c514f667dc9979cfa8df875e473</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Documento sem título.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1786300288</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="One Centimeter">
  <data key="d0">One Centimeter</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">One centimeter is the minimal distance advised between two insulin injection points to avoid overlap.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-708e3c514f667dc9979cfa8df875e473</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Documento sem título.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1786300289</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Ninety Degrees Angle">
  <data key="d0">Ninety Degrees Angle</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Ninety degrees angle is the vertical (90°) insertion angle recommended for short needles (4 mm or 5 mm) during insulin injection.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-708e3c514f667dc9979cfa8df875e473</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Documento sem título.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1786300289</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Forty Five Degrees Angle">
  <data key="d0">Forty Five Degrees Angle</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Forty‑five degrees angle is the oblique (45°) insertion angle recommended for longer needles (6 mm or 8 mm) and for children when using such needles.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-708e3c514f667dc9979cfa8df875e473</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Documento sem título.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1786300289</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Needle 6 Mm">
  <data key="d0">Needle 6 Mm</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-622f3feb1f15564393e91cefc71256ec</data>
  <data key="d2">A 45° angle is recommended when using a 6 mm needle for safer injection.</data>
  <data key="d1">UNKNOWN</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Documento sem título.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1786300307</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Needle 8 Mm">
  <data key="d0">Needle 8 Mm</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-622f3feb1f15564393e91cefc71256ec</data>
  <data key="d2">An 8 mm needle may be inserted at either 45° or 90° based on patient preference.</data>
  <data key="d1">UNKNOWN</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Documento sem título.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1786300309</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Agulha Da Caneta">
  <data key="d0">Agulha Da Caneta</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e490a7e963a20e2221a8097b50073543&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7982460136aa21cc2de3969af556c4d2</data>
  <data key="d2">A bent needle can cause pain during insulin administration.&lt;SEP&gt;Agulha Da Caneta is the needle attached to an insulin pen that was left in the pen after use.</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Documento sem título.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf</data>
