<node id="Humulin R">
  <data key="d0">Humulin R</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Humulin R is a brand of human insulin produced by recombinant DNA technology and marketed as a rapid‑acting (regular, short‑acting) insulin preparation. It is listed under the “Rápida” category in pharmaceutical references and appears in drug bulários with a standard 12 IU dose cited in clinical observations.

The medication is supplied as a sterile aqueous solution that may be administered subcutaneously, intramuscularly, or intravenously. It is intended for use in the management of diabetes mellitus, providing a relatively short duration of action after injection. Humulin R can be mixed with Humulin N, another human insulin formulation, to achieve tailored dosing regimens.

Proper use requires that the solution be clear, non‑viscous, and free of discoloration or particulate matter; any deviation from these visual criteria contraindicates administration. Reported adverse reactions include typical insulin‑related effects such as hypoglycemia, especially when doses exceed therapeutic needs, as well as injection‑site reactions and systemic hypersensitivity responses</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a8768fa32f88d682aa4ddf677297047e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aa127476a5c98492d7b7e0fcd1212886&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a1245bd9ff75c998b49dab861cc4cebf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d29256dbc41e0c81e974f018d373c72d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6419fb3ef4249d6c7e8d8a45d82efe80&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1e622f0079074cd1916470223d22aa66&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0fa819f7e1e42eb688d4894dc3ca7e64&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-577779892c0d463cd6bb1966b8a8ce2d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8ac99e7359716e2cecc2ec93159218b6</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Insulinas CANETAS.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/Lista_Insulinas_Bulas (1).pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786319694</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Novolin R">
  <data key="d0">Novolin R</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Novolin R is a rapid‑acting insulin brand listed under the “Rápida” category.&lt;SEP&gt;Novolin R is a regular (short‑acting) insulin product listed without a specific bulletin entry.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a8768fa32f88d682aa4ddf677297047e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aa127476a5c98492d7b7e0fcd1212886</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Insulinas CANETAS.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/Lista_Insulinas_Bulas (1).pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786304727</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Lantus">
  <data key="d0">Lantus</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Lantus is the brand name for insulin glargine, an ultra‑long‑acting (often described as “ultralenta”) recombinant human insulin used for the management of diabetes mellitus. Marketed by Sanofi‑Aventis Farmacêutica Ltda, Lantus is supplied in both vial and refill‑pen (cartridge) presentations that are administered by subcutaneous injection. The medication is indicated for a broad range of patients, including adults, pregnant women, and children older than two years, and its dosage may be adjusted according to individual metabolic control and therapeutic response. Information leaflets for Lantus are available through resources such as BulasMed, and healthcare professionals can seek further guidance from specialists associated with CatalogoMed.&lt;SEP&gt;Lantus is a long‑acting (basal) insulin product listed with a bula link.&lt;SEP&gt;Lantus is a brand of insulin glargine previously used before conversion to BASAGLAR, with dose conversion typically 1 unit to 1 unit.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a8768fa32f88d682aa4ddf677297047e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-29a33072a90b4191a8b6c5136c417e4c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d59c9bf7f429a82cbfd7083e36ff8f9a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4da80e99fd3e43cb7d3b260aca23fe56&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f563c4251564fd1ab552464562a1876c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-67563459bb64c390a40207da52944afd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a976e1642df27c488174759a35ca23f2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-572e715aada476f4dac69a032e16cc09&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ffb10c00517fa772be2ca9a42f497edf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aa127476a5c98492d7b7e0fcd1212886&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bbae57922175913b7c36c594b4673fa2</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Insulinas CANETAS.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/LANTUS _ BulasMed.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/Lista_Insulinas_Bulas (1).pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Basaglar.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786310008</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Levemir">
  <data key="d0">Levemir</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Levemir® is an ultra‑long‑acting (Ultralenta) insulin brand.&lt;SEP&gt;Levemir is a long‑acting (basal) insulin product listed with a bulário link.&lt;SEP&gt;Levemir® is an insulin detemir medication used as part of a basal‑bolus insulin regimen, administered once or twice daily with dose individualized per patient.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a8768fa32f88d682aa4ddf677297047e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aa127476a5c98492d7b7e0fcd1212886&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0ace26fdb0244e3d0f714a007c9bbb51</data>
