<node id="Insulina Glargina">
  <data key="d0">Insulina Glargina</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Insulina Glargina is a recombinant long‑acting insulin analogue that is marketed as the active ingredient of Lantus® and the BASAGLAR® KwikPen, both supplied at a concentration of 100 UI per milliliter (approximately 3.64 mg per mL). The molecule is a synthetic analogue of human insulin in which the asparagine at position A21 is replaced by glycine and two arginine residues are added to the C‑terminus of the B‑chain; these modifications give it the empirical formula C₂₆₇H₄₀₄N₇₂O₇₈S₆ and a molecular weight of about 6 063 Da. The structural changes create a depot from which insulin is released slowly, providing a basal glucose‑lowering effect that permits once‑daily subcutaneous dosing, typically administered at bedtime.

Pharmacologically, Insulina Glargina is equipotent to human insulin but must not be mixed with other insulins in the same syringe. It is indicated for the treatment of diabetes mellitus, serving as basal insulin therapy in both type 1 and type 2 diabetes. Clinical use spans a broad range of patient populations, including pregnant women, children, the elderly, and individuals with renal or hepatic impairment who may require dose adjustments. Because of its prolonged action, recovery from hypoglycaemic episodes can be delayed relative to shorter‑acting insulins.

Insulina Glargina has been employed as a comparator or reference basal insulin in numerous clinical investigations. It has been used as an alternative to NPH insulin in trials, served as the basal insulin arm in type 1 diabetes studies, and been directly compared with other long‑acting products such as Levemir® (insulin detemir) in glycaemic‑control research. The analogue has also been evaluated in pre‑clinical toxicology studies that examined a variety of safety endpoints in animal models.

Overall, Insulina Glargina provides a well‑characterized, once‑daily basal insulin option with a predictable pharmacokinetic profile, standardized potency, and applicability across diverse clinical scenarios, while requiring careful monitoring for potential delayed hypoglycaemia and adherence to mixing restrictions.&lt;SEP&gt;A long‑acting insulin analogue.&lt;SEP&gt;Long‑acting glargine insulin, referenced as a comparator to ultra‑rapid analogues.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2df359ca3783191b2159f8d3f6ea6c52&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-29a33072a90b4191a8b6c5136c417e4c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9e62226007200589cb2143f0fb75b302&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4a89ae12c86f6f30741a3c6330e6c11b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-02780a8bc1d372cc47e0ccf2eaab1a99&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a72472938feb27131681a1591081e8c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3a279eef99c9c70338c74ffc7b4e260e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4d0ac8ad5968d54922b924fdb16b61d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-61cacf80ada6db26d2b975df763c137a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-17844a4a12e6c05ba2d7b5f54b0f9bd7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2db4ee43ed7cc39546184320e1328d06&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5b40c2fbad301807d9646f27d94635cb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9cd336474a2e9457985162b1ddb4b603&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d99841fd6d1e1fbf23f184e202bc760e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2479751a6475c09415f0d79759db091d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3f0b85829c02f82470489f3f5e487996&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fb620bf44b37187faceacd0405c4a819&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aecb3968c37f57b78a756e4b661ad089&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b65a4249ac93aec086cb333ed1507ea7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-60530d1861f7c2d1efecc069c0913d37&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-51c7617f1e335789b870332231de4058</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/insulinas em seringa.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/LANTUS _ BulasMed.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Basaglar.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Toujeo.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_apidra.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf</data>
