  <data key="d5">1786318532</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Thigh">
  <data key="d0">Thigh</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">Thigh – the thigh (or coxa) is a body region commonly recommended for sub‑cutaneous injections, particularly on the front or outer‑lateral aspect. The preferred site is located approximately three finger‑widths below the groin or just above the knee, providing a convenient and accessible area for self‑administration.

As an injection site, the thigh offers moderate absorption speed for insulin and is approved for several insulin formulations. It has been studied as a site for insulin glargine (including its duration of action) and is an authorized location for administering BASAGLAR and the BASAGLAR KWIKPEN. The thigh also serves as an alternative sub‑cutaneous site for Toujeo 300 U/mL and is routinely used for injecting APIDRA, making it a versatile option for various basal insulin therapies.&lt;SEP&gt;Thigh is a body region where Levemir® may be injected subcutaneously.&lt;SEP&gt;Thigh is an injection site for subcutaneous delivery of Novolin® R FlexPen®.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cc6a26a5d2c41087b58a0f7f71ad21cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4902fb11e4844af5cf6fd61f18b6e4ce&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f14ce019f10c2a88765380143498ba5b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3db0edd23b6b502ccbbf62bfd601ce68&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d96761d60c65f05f1530bc19b144cf1b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-133169995b3ab942fd96f1fdfe7269ad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1ee5400065df79b02b6c04efc0f4854d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-465ad8b77c1c2a2a179062da20337ff5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cedd8e88a8d35eade68ce02222b9e276&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2cd48799a027437b9fe2e1a48b61cb3d</data>
