<node id="Symbol &quot;+&quot;">
  <data key="d0">Symbol "+"</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Symbol "+" is used to separate doses in prescriptions but can be misinterpreted as the number four.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b5b4c60b3de8c56d9ab869d868345fb7</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786301842</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Abbreviation &quot;UI&quot;">
  <data key="d0">Abbreviation "UI"</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Abbreviation "UI" denotes units of insulin similar to "U" and its misuse can cause dosing errors.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b5b4c60b3de8c56d9ab869d868345fb7</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786301843</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hospital Discharge">
  <data key="d0">Hospital Discharge</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">Hospital Discharge refers to the patient’s release from the hospital, for which education and preparation are emphasized.&lt;SEP&gt;Hospital Discharge is the event when a patient leaves the hospital after transplantation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b5b4c60b3de8c56d9ab869d868345fb7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e4e7eef761aec994cc4558b2db5e1e08</data>
