<node id="Diabetes Mellitus Tipo 2">
  <data key="d0">Diabetes Mellitus Tipo 2</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Diabetes Mellitus Tipo 2 is a chronic, non‑insulin‑dependent metabolic disorder that primarily affects adult patients and is characterized by impaired regulation of blood glucose levels. As a major target of contemporary diabetes management, the condition is commonly treated with long‑acting basal insulin analogues; for example, the basal insulin product BASAGLAR® (including its KWIKPEN delivery system) lists adult type‑2 diabetes as an approved indication. Other insulin formulations such as Toujeo may be used in combination with additional antihyperglycemic agents, and rapid‑acting insulin analogues such as Fiasp® have specific dosing recommendations that allow daily adjustment based on automated glucose monitoring (AMG) readings.

Adults with Diabetes Mellitus Tipo 2 have been the central disease cohort in several clinical investigations. The ORIGIN Study enrolled eligible participants with type‑2 diabetes to evaluate long‑term clinical outcomes, while a separate 26‑week randomized, open‑label trial compared the basal‑bolus regimen APIDRA with regular insulin in this population. The same disease group was also the focus of a 26‑week basal‑bolus study that examined overall treatment effects in chronic type‑2 diabetes patients. 

Research specific to Diabetes Mellitus Tipo 2 has examined the incidence of nocturnal and severe hypoglycemia, underscoring the importance of vigilant monitoring and risk management when basal insulin or other glucose‑lowering therapies are employed. Collectively, these studies and therapeutic guidelines reflect the pivotal role of Diabetes Mellitus Tipo 2 in both clinical practice and ongoing investigations aimed at optimizing metabolic control in adult patients.&lt;SEP&gt;Diabetes mellitus type 2 is a chronic metabolic disease for which Levemir® may be prescribed alone or in combination with other agents.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-96f91060a07d79071735f666e2b8aee2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-afc9722167670b0bfeef0b43f4b0df79&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9e62226007200589cb2143f0fb75b302&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c078e8c2861146fb455f1dc3d4af2456&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a72472938feb27131681a1591081e8c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b916f29e047f8579110cf5da3fd73847&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7a592aedb257bad9532268b4056ec15c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4d0ac8ad5968d54922b924fdb16b61d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-97208e231aa338c60205244ac12e0492&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-56fb3d61e8c32af5d6b8be06cc54f904&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3f0b85829c02f82470489f3f5e487996&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aecb3968c37f57b78a756e4b661ad089&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-add4469fba80232b7c0742f24c0914c9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2073bddd90c7dd8e156b67821f0f3247&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-09d60e0b850d87c77dd67ca2d709912c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-00cf434060561bb7d46b6ce50f095c91</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Armazenamento e Transporte/Cuidados com a Insulinoterapia conservar.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Basaglar.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Toujeo.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_apidra.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_fiasp.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786317447</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Insulinoterapia">
  <data key="d0">Insulinoterapia</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Insulinoterapia is the method of managing diabetes using insulin administration.&lt;SEP&gt;Insulinoterapia is the medical method of treating diabetes by administering insulin, as described in Brazilian diabetes guidelines.&lt;SEP&gt;Insulinoterapia is the initiation of insulin therapy, typically lasting 5 to 7 days, after which most patients develop antibodies against exogenous insulin.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-96f91060a07d79071735f666e2b8aee2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b50a9fb21c77773aec36a9b8e9f5e1d5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-858cd6ea7fba353827f5ab95be1157ae</data>
