<node id="Diabetes Mellitus Tipo 1">
  <data key="d0">Diabetes Mellitus Tipo 1</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Diabetes Mellitus Tipo 1 is a chronic, autoimmune form of diabetes characterized by the body’s inability to produce sufficient insulin, which predisposes patients to persistent hyperglycemia and an increased risk of diabetic ketoacidosis. Because endogenous insulin production is markedly reduced or absent, the disease is insulin‑dependent; management therefore requires exogenous insulin therapy, typically a basal insulin component supplemented with rapid‑acting insulin at each meal.

The condition affects individuals across the lifespan. Pediatric cases are usually diagnosed from about two years of age onward, while adult‑onset presentations also occur. Both children and adults are included in clinical research programs that evaluate insulin regimens and treatment satisfaction. Notably, a 30‑week pediatric study and a 12‑week adult randomized trial have enrolled participants with Diabetes Mellitus Tipo 1, many of whom were described as having inadequately controlled disease at baseline.

Therapeutically, Diabetes Mellitus Tipo 1 is an explicit indication for several modern insulin products. The BASAGLAR® product line, including the BASAGLAR KWIKPEN delivery system, is approved for use in this insulin‑dependent population. In addition, Toujeo (insulin glargine) is recommended to be combined with a rapid‑acting insulin at each meal, and specific dosing guidelines have been published for Fiasp® (a fast‑acting insulin formulation) to address the rapid glucose excursions typical of the disease.

Across the pediatric and adult FIASP® studies, as well as the BASAGLAR® trials, participants with Diabetes Mellitus Tipo 1 were evaluated for therapeutic outcomes, safety, and satisfaction with their insulin delivery methods. The collective evidence underscores that Diabetes Mellitus Tipo 1 requires lifelong insulin replacement, careful monitoring of blood glucose, and individualized dosing strategies to achieve optimal glycemic control and to mitigate the complications associated with chronic hyperglycemia.&lt;SEP&gt;Type 1 diabetes, the chronic condition targeted by insulin pump (SICI) and MDI therapies.&lt;SEP&gt;An autoimmune form of diabetes affecting the adult and pediatric populations discussed in the clinical evidence.&lt;SEP&gt;Diabetes Mellitus Tipo 1 is a form of diabetes discussed in the dissertation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0d399f9e64e21e86fd4e2a48869d80e2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-afc9722167670b0bfeef0b43f4b0df79&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9e62226007200589cb2143f0fb75b302&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c078e8c2861146fb455f1dc3d4af2456&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a72472938feb27131681a1591081e8c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b916f29e047f8579110cf5da3fd73847&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7a592aedb257bad9532268b4056ec15c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4d0ac8ad5968d54922b924fdb16b61d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-56fb3d61e8c32af5d6b8be06cc54f904&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3f0b85829c02f82470489f3f5e487996&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aecb3968c37f57b78a756e4b661ad089&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-add4469fba80232b7c0742f24c0914c9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3a70857656e32cc73aaa270a75eb33af&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fb0cd81f0439cbb74e3c0ff54236c45d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cbe87fd92ad66dcb02b25b669d829f6c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-51c7617f1e335789b870332231de4058&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ca8620e735c40bfe850134ccea9a7154&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1e99a265d5e53a3da6b755599d395791</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Armazenamento e Transporte/Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-20201.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Basaglar.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Toujeo.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_apidra.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_fiasp.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/Insulinoterapia – Diretriz da Sociedade Brasileira de Diabetes – Ed. 2024.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/Orientacoes_Hipoglicemia_SBD_transcricao.docx</data>
