<node id="Homogenization (20 Gentle Movements)">
  <data key="d0">Homogenization (20 Gentle Movements)</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Homogenization (20 Gentle Movements) is the recommended process of performing about twenty gentle rolling motions between the palms to evenly disperse insulin crystals.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4d795dc393eb02c6418957ee1678504f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Armazenamento e Transporte/transporte e conservação Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-20201.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786302748</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Temperature 2 °C to 8 °C">
  <data key="d0">Temperature 2 °C to 8 °C</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Temperature 2 °C to 8 °C is the recommended refrigeration range for maintaining insulin stability.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4d795dc393eb02c6418957ee1678504f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Armazenamento e Transporte/transporte e conservação Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-20201.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786302748</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Temperature Up To 30 °C">
  <data key="d0">Temperature Up To 30 °C</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Temperature up to 30 °C is the allowable ambient temperature for insulin in use when stored outside the refrigerator.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4d795dc393eb02c6418957ee1678504f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Armazenamento e Transporte/transporte e conservação Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-20201.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786302748</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Validity Period (Sealed Insulin)">
  <data key="d0">Validity Period (Sealed Insulin)</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Validity period (sealed insulin) indicates a shelf‑life of 2 to 3 years from the manufacturing date when insulin remains unopened.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4d795dc393eb02c6418957ee1678504f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Armazenamento e Transporte/transporte e conservação Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-20201.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786302748</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Validity Period (Insulin In Use)">
  <data key="d0">Validity Period (Insulin In Use)</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Validity period (insulin in use) specifies that opened insulin remains usable for 4 to 8 weeks after first use, depending on device type.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4d795dc393eb02c6418957ee1678504f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Armazenamento e Transporte/transporte e conservação Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-20201.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786302749</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Plastic Or Metal Container With Lid">
  <data key="d0">Plastic Or Metal Container With Lid</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Plastic or metal container with lid is the recommended secondary packaging for refrigerated insulin, protecting it from damage.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4d795dc393eb02c6418957ee1678504f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Armazenamento e Transporte/transporte e conservação Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-20201.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786302749</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Thermal Packaging">
  <data key="d0">Thermal Packaging</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Thermal packaging, such as an insulated bag or styrofoam, is used for transporting insulin while preventing direct contact with ice.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4d795dc393eb02c6418957ee1678504f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Armazenamento e Transporte/transporte e conservação Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-20201.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786302749</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Syringe With Removable Needle">
  <data key="d0">Syringe With Removable Needle</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Syringe with removable needle is an alternative syringe type that includes a detachable needle.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4d795dc393eb02c6418957ee1678504f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Armazenamento e Transporte/transporte e conservação Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-20201.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786302749</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Manufacturers">
  <data key="d0">Manufacturers</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Manufacturers are companies that produce insulin and related devices and provide storage and handling recommendations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4d795dc393eb02c6418957ee1678504f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Armazenamento e Transporte/transporte e conservação Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-20201.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786302749</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Insulin Pen (Disposable)">
  <data key="d0">Insulin Pen (Disposable)</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Insulin pen (disposable) is a single‑use device for delivering insulin, mentioned as an in‑use form that can be refrigerated.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4d795dc393eb02c6418957ee1678504f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Armazenamento e Transporte/transporte e conservação Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-20201.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786302749</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Insulin Pen (Rechargeable)">
  <data key="d0">Insulin Pen (Rechargeable)</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Insulin pen (rechargeable) is a refillable insulin delivery device, for which manufacturers advise against refrigeration.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4d795dc393eb02c6418957ee1678504f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Armazenamento e Transporte/transporte e conservação Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-20201.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786302749</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Safe Preparation">
  <data key="d0">Safe Preparation</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Safe preparation denotes the recommended practices and equipment that minimize errors during insulin dosing.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4d795dc393eb02c6418957ee1678504f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Armazenamento e Transporte/transporte e conservação Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-20201.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786302750</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="U100 Scale">
  <data key="d0">U100 Scale</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">U100 Scale is the graduation marking on syringes representing units that correspond to the concentration of insulin (100 units per milliliter).</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4d795dc393eb02c6418957ee1678504f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Armazenamento e Transporte/transporte e conservação Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-20201.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786302750</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
