<node id="Subcutaneous Administration">
  <data key="d0">Subcutaneous Administration</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Subcutaneous administration is a route of drug delivery in which a medication is injected into the layer of tissue directly beneath the skin, known as the subcutaneous (SC) tissue. The drug deposited in this layer is absorbed gradually into the systemic circulation, providing a relatively slow and sustained onset of action compared with intramuscular or intravenous routes.

In clinical practice the subcutaneous route is the preferred method for a broad spectrum of injectable diabetes therapies. Rapid‑acting insulins such as Humalog, Humalog Mix 25 Kwikpen, Humalog Mix 50 Kwikpen, NovoRapid®, and the rapid‑acting analogue Apidra (insulin glulisine) are routinely given subcutaneously, often within 15 minutes before a meal. Intermediate‑acting insulin NPH, regular human insulin, and long‑acting analogues including Lantus® (insulin glargine), BASAGLAR KWIKPEN, and Levemir® (insulin detemir) are also administered by this route, serving as basal insulin to maintain a steady background level. Subcutaneous injection is likewise employed for glucagon formulations used to treat severe hypoglycemia and for insulin suspensions delivered with disposable pens.

Typical injection sites for subcutaneous delivery include the abdomen, upper arms, thighs, and buttocks. The choice of site may be guided by patient comfort, rotation practices, and the pharmacokinetic profile of the specific insulin product. In research settings, subcutaneous administration is the designated route for pharmacokinetic, teratology, and glucose‑infusion studies involving both Apidra and Levemir, allowing evaluation of absorption, distribution, and therapeutic effect under controlled conditions.&lt;SEP&gt;Subcutaneous Administration is the route of delivering insulin under the skin, producing peak plasma concentration 1.5‑2.5 hours after injection.&lt;SEP&gt;Subcutaneous Administration is an injection method delivering Novolin® R FlexPen® into the fatty tissue under the skin.&lt;SEP&gt;Subcutaneous administration is an injection route influencing insulin absorption and onset of action.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-431b48980656b0322f263c358250b593&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ecd2466ef4258dade38fbadd495188e5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4f079198593c1702b56062aa87e7801a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fe094dd3d94334373a8497a7cb841e0f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4a89ae12c86f6f30741a3c6330e6c11b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-133169995b3ab942fd96f1fdfe7269ad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db832f06717859b8ba6cf7fd70aa22d8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7084240a735ca2fe3b6d426e3b8c5756&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fd94288932ad6675a1de2b46b3fd9128&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fb620bf44b37187faceacd0405c4a819&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7621ac447c9044986ade86ce5f9be201&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ee2684edaea64aa597fd29c3bbda611d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2dc2313c92b2af4132faaa4d41449eef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50719bcc88f4515ec825b9d5a7aba107&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8ef15154a94043650617b3b24d8146a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f36263c657ad99a80e578ac49a333d5b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea9b3836b3275f451c3acfb189f42a6f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2cd48799a027437b9fe2e1a48b61cb3d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1e622f0079074cd1916470223d22aa66</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/Bula Humalog.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/NOVORAPID _ BulasMed.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Basaglar.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_1778357531609.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_apidra.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786319707</data>
