<node id="Coma">
  <data key="d0">Coma</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Coma is a severe state of unconsciousness that may follow extreme hypoglycemia.&lt;SEP&gt;Coma is a loss of consciousness that can result from untreated hypoglycemia or hyperglycemia.&lt;SEP&gt;Coma is a deep state of unconsciousness that may result from severe hypoglycemia.&lt;SEP&gt;Coma is a severe manifestation of hypoglycemia mentioned as a condition treated with glucagon or intravenous glucose.&lt;SEP&gt;Coma is a state of deep unconsciousness that can result from severe hypoglycemia.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-431b48980656b0322f263c358250b593&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a247846b9ec5d44d0bcbe6c5f15599f8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d7223c781e745e72311fccfcdd58583&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6419fb3ef4249d6c7e8d8a45d82efe80&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0e484a5a1df875be2e1525c8c64e2007</data>
