<node id="Carbohydrates">
  <data key="d0">Carbohydrates</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Carbohydrates are dietary nutrients classified as macronutrients that, when digested, raise blood glucose levels. Because their absorption directly increases glucose in the bloodstream, they are a primary factor in determining the amount of insulin required; the quantity of carbohydrates consumed is measured in rations or carbohydrate counts to calculate appropriate bolus doses.  

In diabetes management, carbohydrates play several specific roles. They are recommended for continuous intake during episodes of hypoglycemia to raise low blood glucose, and they are often included in post‑injection meals to help maintain glucose balance. Insulin dosing can be adjusted according to glucose trends, with carbohydrate consumption guiding the timing and size of bolus insulin to match the anticipated rise in blood glucose.  

Overall, carbohydrates are essential nutrients whose digestion triggers a rise in blood glucose, thereby influencing both the need for insulin and the strategies used to achieve stable glucose control.&lt;SEP&gt;Carbohydrates are nutrients constituting the mixed diet required before glucose testing.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-431b48980656b0322f263c358250b593&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-73559dc5d86ea52a348d603482e056e9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2dada456819c45230012103650ccc14a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-70519ee85d46567e23db476b219f16a9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-07b23fc13c50867e0aa61204fb79bc2b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d03a310916c005d1dfa70800a753d1c5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3ce8c9873da330aac077f7ccaf108ccd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3d24fce6aa8866fb4a11514ae0e4d675&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-138cbaf5a43762d4c5b77a07ab51cbd4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6601fea85bfbb9f20040c70b7e21695d</data>
