</node>
<node id="Systemic Allergic Reaction">
  <data key="d0">Systemic Allergic Reaction</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Systemic allergic reaction to insulin can cause rash, dyspnea, wheezing, blood pressure drop, rapid pulse, sweating, and risk of death.&lt;SEP&gt;Systemic allergic reaction includes widespread cutaneous signs, angioedema, bronchospasm, hypotension, and shock.&lt;SEP&gt;Systemic allergic reaction includes rash, dyspnea, wheezing, blood pressure drop, rapid pulse, or sweating after insulin exposure.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e89f1dbae629e925f06732cebf41df16&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e8934881ec5ab7cfeb836126b3f0e8b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-51761473ea6fe17b9e098a6bf98636b3</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/Bula Humalog.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Toujeo.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_apidra.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786315441</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Doctor">
  <data key="d0">Doctor</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Doctor is a medical professional responsible for managing a patient’s insulin therapy and overall diabetes care. The doctor determines the appropriate insulin dosage, taking into account the individual’s glycemic targets, comorbid conditions, and any episodes of hypoglycemia, and then communicates the prescribed dose and injection schedule to the patient.

In addition to dosage calculation, the doctor provides comprehensive guidance on glucose monitoring and advises on how to adjust insulin in response to factors such as illness, exercise, travel, pregnancy, and changes in medication regimens. The physician must be informed of, and counsel the patient about, potential adverse reactions to specific insulin products such as Humalog, as well as possible drug‑drug interactions that could affect glycaemic control.

A key component of the doctor’s role is patient education on injection technique. This includes demonstrating the correct method for inserting the needle, selecting the appropriate injection site, and ensuring the patient understands how to administer the prescribed dose safely and effectively. The doctor also offers instructions on the use of any related devices or equipment.

Overall, the doctor serves as the primary source of advice, supervision, and ongoing support for individuals using insulin, ensuring that treatment is individualized, safe, and responsive to the patient’s lifestyle and health circumstances.&lt;SEP&gt;Doctor is the medical professional who advises the patient on glucose monitoring frequency and insulin pump settings.&lt;SEP&gt;Doctor is a medical professional who advises patients on glucose monitoring and treatment.&lt;SEP&gt;Doctor is a medical doctor who should be consulted regularly regarding insulin dose adjustments.&lt;SEP&gt;Doctor is the medical professional referenced as “seu médico” who can adjust treatment and discuss sensor usage.&lt;SEP&gt;A medical professional who downloads and analyzes glucose data recorded by the retro sensor.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e89f1dbae629e925f06732cebf41df16&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c3daabbd42055dc30154f5f97c85fb7d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ffb10c00517fa772be2ca9a42f497edf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4704ea4d5c15ebc8c043a077f05fd7a3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e9835d6684db67541402527b3182b6c5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dd25c8bd4672601d6ee40e4b7e28a69c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dd396c45bc09fb646d156b4e69d328e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8ac99e7359716e2cecc2ec93159218b6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4b9f6a4a440ccb40e47c326ca6dd9346&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d2f8a0d67f7320d6157b61dbbf428a40&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e94cedc7134adbb256c931b851235c53&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-63f18f20af642d4a480c16e7a6780bb6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5c804699375feba4c866cc3a1bc00211</data>
