  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Ambient Temperature">
  <data key="d0">Ambient Temperature</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Ambient temperature (below 30 °C) is the condition for storing Humalog pens and refills during use.&lt;SEP&gt;Ambient temperature refers to storage conditions below 30 °C for Levemir® Penfill®.&lt;SEP&gt;Ambient Temperature refers to room‑temperature conditions (15 °C to 30 °C) allowed for storing opened Novolin® R.&lt;SEP&gt;Ambient temperature refers to typical room conditions under which Novolin® R in infusion bags remains stable for 24 hours.&lt;SEP&gt;The recommended storage temperature for batteries, specified as room temperature.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e89f1dbae629e925f06732cebf41df16&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cedd8e88a8d35eade68ce02222b9e276&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-73559dc5d86ea52a348d603482e056e9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-df616353e032c899b02bfa4368bc2667&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-527777f044e20410ca47d2c5b35306ca</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/Bula Humalog.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786325539</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Light">
  <data key="d0">Light</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Light is an environmental factor from which Humalog should be protected during storage.&lt;SEP&gt;Light is electromagnetic radiation that can degrade insulin stability if exposure is not prevented.&lt;SEP&gt;Light is electromagnetic radiation that can degrade Novolin® R if the medication is not protected.&lt;SEP&gt;Light is a natural element from which Humulin R should be protected during storage.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e89f1dbae629e925f06732cebf41df16&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-048d8fafb712e12cec45f2d3ec2c1e3b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-df616353e032c899b02bfa4368bc2667&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-577779892c0d463cd6bb1966b8a8ce2d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/Bula Humalog.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/NOVORAPID _ BulasMed.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786319732</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="28 Days">
  <data key="d0">28 Days</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">28 days is the maximum period a Humalog refill can be kept at ambient temperature after opening before disposal.&lt;SEP&gt;28 Days specifies the maximum period SoloStar can be stored at ambient temperature after removal from refrigeration.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e89f1dbae629e925f06732cebf41df16&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ffe095bda1b787c5b5ae2d61a2f74c98</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/Bula Humalog.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_apidra.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786315487</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Lilly">
