<node id="Expiration Date">
  <data key="d0">Expiration Date</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Expiration Date is the specific calendar day printed on the packaging, label, or cartridge of an insulin product that denotes the final day the medication may be used safely and retain its expected potency. For each insulin brand and delivery system, the Expiration Date appears in a slightly different context but serves the same regulatory and safety purpose.  

In Humalog and Humalog Mix 50 KwikPen, the Expiration Date is printed on the pen label and signals when the insulin should no longer be administered. The same practice applies to Humulin R, whose packaging carries an Expiration Date indicating the cutoff for use.  

Tresiba® packaging also displays an Expiration Date, marking the last day the drug may be used without risking reduced efficacy or safety concerns. For BASAGLAR KWIKPEN, the Expiration Date similarly identifies the point at which the pen becomes invalid for use.  

SoloStar pens and cartridges include an Expiration Date on the label, informing users that after this date the pen must not be used. Across all these products, the Expiration Date functions as a clear, manufacturer‑provided guideline to ensure patients administer insulin that is still within its approved potency and sterility window.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e89f1dbae629e925f06732cebf41df16&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e9ae5f9ffa7eff9bb36cf1a9764df3e7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0b9c41c968bcc1d46185583661e8f989&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d96761d60c65f05f1530bc19b144cf1b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fd94288932ad6675a1de2b46b3fd9128&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ffe095bda1b787c5b5ae2d61a2f74c98&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e9835d6684db67541402527b3182b6c5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0fa819f7e1e42eb688d4894dc3ca7e64&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-577779892c0d463cd6bb1966b8a8ce2d</data>
