<node id="Cardiac Insufficiency">
  <data key="d0">Cardiac Insufficiency</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Cardiac insufficiency is heart‑failure risk that may rise when TZD is used with insulin, especially in patients with pre‑existing heart disease.&lt;SEP&gt;Cardiac insufficiency refers to reduced heart function, considered when selecting Humalog dosage for patients.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c3daabbd42055dc30154f5f97c85fb7d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4d26ce64e79b8c4a147140be2f9c63dd</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/Bula Humalog.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786303804</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Disease">
  <data key="d0">Disease</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Any disease, particularly those causing nausea or vomiting, can alter insulin needs.&lt;SEP&gt;Disease refers to any illness or infection that can raise glucose levels, ketone bodies, and insulin requirements.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c3daabbd42055dc30154f5f97c85fb7d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2dc33cf2a90bf53c26226e44bc285c22</data>
