<node id="Animal Insulin">
  <data key="d0">Animal Insulin</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Animal insulin is a non‑human source of insulin discussed in the context of species differences.&lt;SEP&gt;Animal Insulin is insulin derived from animal sources, previously used before human insulin formulations.&lt;SEP&gt;Animal insulin is insulin derived from animal sources, whose mixing with Humulin R has not been studied.&lt;SEP&gt;Animal insulin refers to insulin preparations derived from bovine, porcine, or mixed animal sources.&lt;SEP&gt;Animal insulin is insulin extracted from the pancreas of beef or pork, used historically to treat diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c3daabbd42055dc30154f5f97c85fb7d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a2416b3e5e8ebc96cdb451a794fc78e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a1245bd9ff75c998b49dab861cc4cebf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0fa819f7e1e42eb688d4894dc3ca7e64&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0932e9c21a330869629b3fa70d2e1f5e</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/Bula Humalog.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_1778357531609.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/Understanding insulin - International Diabetes Federation.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786332448</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Human Insulin">
  <data key="d0">Human Insulin</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Human insulin is the endogenous peptide hormone produced by the β‑cells of the human pancreas that regulates blood‑glucose concentrations. It can be isolated from human donors or manufactured recombinantly, and the resulting product is chemically identical to the hormone naturally secreted by the body. Because it represents the reference molecule for insulin activity, human insulin is routinely used as the comparator in pharmacodynamic, binding‑affinity, pharmacokinetic and safety assessments of insulin analogues such as insulin aspart, insulin glargine, insulin lispro, insulin detemir (Levemir®) and other modified insulins. In these studies human insulin serves as the benchmark for evaluating elimination half‑life, therapeutic efficacy, metabolic potency, immunogenicity (antibody formation) and injection‑site reaction frequency.

In clinical research, regular human insulin and conventional premixed formulations (e.g., 50/50 and 70/30 mixtures) are employed as control treatments to establish dosing equivalence and to provide a baseline against which newer insulin products are compared. The molecule is also the active pharmaceutical ingredient in branded preparations such as Novolin® R, where it is administered as a rapid‑acting therapeutic agent for the correction of hyperglycaemia, although the term “rapid‑acting analogue” more accurately describes synthetic derivatives that have been engineered for faster absorption.

Overall, human insulin functions as the natural standard for all comparative and reference purposes in insulin research, development, and clinical use, enabling consistent evaluation of efficacy, safety, immunogenic potential and other critical performance characteristics across the spectrum of insulin‑based therapies.&lt;SEP&gt;Human insulin is a recombinant protein used for glucose regulation in diabetic patients.&lt;SEP&gt;Human insulin is a sterile, clear, colorless aqueous solution that acts as a short‑acting glucose‑lowering agent and is synthesized by a genetically modified Escherichia coli strain.&lt;SEP&gt;Human Insulin is a recombinant insulin identical in structure to pancreatic insulin, used therapeutically.&lt;SEP&gt;Human insulin is a type of insulin produced from recombinant DNA, referenced as a comparator to Humulin R in interaction studies.&lt;SEP&gt;Human insulin is insulin that was first produced synthetically in a laboratory in the early 1980s.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c3daabbd42055dc30154f5f97c85fb7d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f895f97a023b65cced82334a7f1d1e0b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6d0f18c80f8de2dee960a03599d12052&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c41538e94f00eba70740ff188bcb6a94&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d194d06ef99b3f8aa6b6542b7e93e762&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-133169995b3ab942fd96f1fdfe7269ad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6ca13e396b094f0c2f482892f220f538&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bf25fca295be60e28b7c7d3103f722fc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7084240a735ca2fe3b6d426e3b8c5756&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a2416b3e5e8ebc96cdb451a794fc78e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-afc28422755c2c44f931bab7b6a2b477&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-14772c7de5db762c492a75a1c744dae6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8ef15154a94043650617b3b24d8146a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f36263c657ad99a80e578ac49a333d5b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0ace26fdb0244e3d0f714a007c9bbb51&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-acaa1440ae268669e1894588bb9e37c2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cd40a6d69921cf300ed8eda043698d1a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a1245bd9ff75c998b49dab861cc4cebf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1e622f0079074cd1916470223d22aa66&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0fa819f7e1e42eb688d4894dc3ca7e64&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-577779892c0d463cd6bb1966b8a8ce2d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0932e9c21a330869629b3fa70d2e1f5e</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/Bula Humalog.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/NOVORAPID _ BulasMed.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Basaglar.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_1778357531609.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Toujeo.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_fiasp.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/Understanding insulin - International Diabetes Federation.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786332448</data>
