  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Elderly Patients">
  <data key="d0">Elderly Patients</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Elderly patients are older individuals, generally defined as those aged 60 years or older, with many sources specifying an age of 65 years or older as the threshold for this population. This group is considered a special population in diabetes management because physiological changes associated with aging—such as hepatic, renal, and cardiac impairment—can alter insulin pharmacokinetics and increase the risk of adverse events.

Because of these age‑related changes, conservative insulin dosing is recommended for elderly patients to minimize the likelihood of hypoglycemia, which may be difficult for them to recognize. Initial, incremental, and maintenance doses of basal insulins such as Lantus and Toujeo (insulin glargine 300 U/mL) should be started low and titrated cautiously. For Toujeo, careful glucose monitoring and dose adjustments are advised, and the progressive decline in renal function that often accompanies aging may further reduce insulin requirements. Similarly, rapid‑acting insulin analogs such as Humalog may require dose reductions in this population due to the higher prevalence of hepatic, renal, or cardiac impairment that can prolong insulin action.

In the context of newer agents, hypoglycemia caused by APIDRA SOLOSTAR (insulin glulisine) can also be difficult for elderly patients to detect, reinforcing the need for vigilant monitoring and individualized dose adjustments across all insulin types used in this age group.&lt;SEP&gt;Elderly Patients refers to study participants aged ≥65 years (and ≥75 years) analyzed as a subgroup in the clinical trials.&lt;SEP&gt;Elderly patients refer to older individuals with diabetes mellitus type 1 examined for drug response.&lt;SEP&gt;Elderly patients refer to older individuals with Type 1 Diabetes included as a subgroup in the trial.&lt;SEP&gt;Elderly patients are a special population that requires intensified glucose monitoring and individualized Levemir® dosing.&lt;SEP&gt;Elderly patients using any insulin, including Levemir®, require intensified blood glucose monitoring and individualized dose adjustment.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4d26ce64e79b8c4a147140be2f9c63dd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d59c9bf7f429a82cbfd7083e36ff8f9a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bbae57922175913b7c36c594b4673fa2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4319d08c10ed2b48857a6d42eadd9db0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-93623071acdcd0ba060c8826ab5a2a81&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d6b9a8472aefa6e90793233284c15a3f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1ee5400065df79b02b6c04efc0f4854d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d65840dd2cbd5c9984dfc4334378df5e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f09811b149a29105854a0b1e84951e5d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2f4f01a72f35d6db3ff333e64f8400ce&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9f85d0ab4cfadc905544cb9e30752dab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1bb9ea85b9ad8cd6940ae41a3ab5d1fd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0ace26fdb0244e3d0f714a007c9bbb51&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-56fc1d5df1b34d9120c3cf8a760c40f9</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/Bula Humalog.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/LANTUS _ BulasMed.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Basaglar.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_1778357531609.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Toujeo.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_apidra.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_fiasp.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786317639</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Renal Insufficiency">
  <data key="d0">Renal Insufficiency</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Renal Insufficiency refers to a condition of reduced kidney function, commonly classified by measured creatinine clearance levels, and encompasses a spectrum from mild impairment to kidney failure. Because the kidneys are a major route for insulin degradation, diminished renal function generally slows insulin clearance, leading to higher circulating insulin concentrations and an increased risk of hypoglycaemia. Consequently, patients with renal insufficiency often require lower total insulin doses and more intensive glycaemic monitoring, with dose adjustments individualized to the degree of impairment and the specific insulin formulation used.

For most insulin products, the altered pharmacokinetics associated with renal insufficiency have been observed, although detailed data are lacking for certain long‑acting analogues such as insulin glargine (Humalog) and insulin glargine (Lantus). Clinical experience with regular human insulin suggests that reduced kidney function can elevate insulin levels, supporting the broader principle that insulin dosing should be reduced in this population to avoid hypoglycaemia.

Regarding insulin glulisine marketed as APIDRA (Apidra Solostar), study findings are mixed. Some investigations reported that APIDRA’s pharmacokinetic profile is largely maintained in patients with renal insufficiency, while other sources note that formal pharmacokinetic studies in this subgroup have not been conducted. Nevertheless, clinical guidance commonly advises that the APIDRA dose may need to be lowered in patients with reduced creatinine clearance, reflecting the general effect of renal impairment on insulin metabolism rather than a proven change in the drug’s intrinsic kinetics.

Similar considerations apply to rapid‑acting formulations such as Fiasp® (faster‑acting insulin aspart); patients with renal insufficiency require intensified glycaemic monitoring and personalized dose adjustments. Overall, clinicians should assess the severity of kidney dysfunction, monitor blood glucose closely, and be prepared to reduce insulin requirements across all insulin types—including APIDRA, Fiasp, Humalog, and Lantus—while recognizing that precise pharmacokinetic effects may vary among individual agents.&lt;SEP&gt;Kidney impairment examined for its impact on Levemir® pharmacokinetics, showing no relevant difference.&lt;SEP&gt;Renal Insufficiency is a medical condition mentioned as having no clinically relevant impact on Levemir® pharmacokinetics.&lt;SEP&gt;Renal insufficiency is a condition of impaired kidney function that may require reduced insulin dosing.&lt;SEP&gt;Renal insufficiency is a medical condition that may require reduction of insulin dose for patients using Humulin R.&lt;SEP&gt;Renal insufficiency impacts HbA1c measurement reliability.&lt;SEP&gt;A condition of impaired kidney function, risk increased sevenfold by low birth weight.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4d26ce64e79b8c4a147140be2f9c63dd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bbae57922175913b7c36c594b4673fa2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f14ce019f10c2a88765380143498ba5b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-133169995b3ab942fd96f1fdfe7269ad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3e50c145614f04be2319a31b74b80411&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6ca13e396b094f0c2f482892f220f538&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4319d08c10ed2b48857a6d42eadd9db0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7d9c944d51a42525c017d9109f46684c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1ee5400065df79b02b6c04efc0f4854d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4d0e34bef478ed432c8de7ef68dc9025&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d65840dd2cbd5c9984dfc4334378df5e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ee2684edaea64aa597fd29c3bbda611d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2dc2313c92b2af4132faaa4d41449eef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50719bcc88f4515ec825b9d5a7aba107&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f09811b149a29105854a0b1e84951e5d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-14772c7de5db762c492a75a1c744dae6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-88b97cde53943160602b20f634ba5c1f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8ef15154a94043650617b3b24d8146a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f36263c657ad99a80e578ac49a333d5b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0fa819f7e1e42eb688d4894dc3ca7e64&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-577779892c0d463cd6bb1966b8a8ce2d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7f716359c14483f9be36a73861d75008&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-343246c2eef6e8430b581340d6cd4762</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/Bula Humalog.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Basaglar.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_1778357531609.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Toujeo.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_apidra.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_fiasp.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/glicemias capilares.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Diagnóstico de diabetes mellitus.pdf</data>
