<node id="Hepatic Insufficiency">
  <data key="d0">Hepatic Insufficiency</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Hepatic insufficiency is a medical condition characterized by impaired or reduced liver function, often described as liver failure or liver‑function impairment. The diminished capacity of the liver affects numerous metabolic processes, including the synthesis and clearance of hormones such as insulin.

Because the liver plays a central role in gluconeogenesis and in the metabolism of circulating insulin, hepatic insufficiency typically leads to lower endogenous glucose production and slower insulin degradation. Consequently, patients with this condition often require reduced exogenous insulin doses, regardless of the insulin formulation being used. The decrease in insulin requirements is attributed primarily to the combined effects of reduced gluconeogenesis and altered insulin metabolism.

Pharmacokinetic studies specifically evaluating insulin glargine products—Humalog (insulin lispro) and Apidra (insulin glargine) Solostar—have not been conducted in populations with hepatic insufficiency, so the precise impact on absorption, distribution, metabolism, and elimination of these analogues remains undefined. In contrast, limited data on insulin humana indicate that hepatic insufficiency may be associated with higher circulating insulin levels, suggesting altered clearance in this setting.

Clinicians should therefore consider the potential for decreased insulin needs when prescribing rapid‑acting (e.g., Humalog) or long‑acting (e.g., Apidra Solostar) insulin to patients with hepatic insufficiency. Dose adjustments should be guided by careful glucose monitoring, with awareness that standard dosing recommendations may overestimate the required insulin amount in this population.&lt;SEP&gt;Hepatic Insufficiency denotes impaired liver function affecting drug absorption.&lt;SEP&gt;Liver impairment examined for its impact on Levemir® pharmacokinetics, showing no relevant difference.&lt;SEP&gt;Hepatic Insufficiency is a medical condition mentioned as having no clinically relevant impact on Levemir® pharmacokinetics.&lt;SEP&gt;Hepatic insufficiency is a condition of impaired liver function that necessitates careful glucose monitoring and insulin dose adjustment.&lt;SEP&gt;Hepatic insufficiency is a medical condition that necessitates careful glucose monitoring and possible insulin dose adjustment for Humulin R users.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4d26ce64e79b8c4a147140be2f9c63dd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f14ce019f10c2a88765380143498ba5b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3e50c145614f04be2319a31b74b80411&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6ca13e396b094f0c2f482892f220f538&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4319d08c10ed2b48857a6d42eadd9db0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1ee5400065df79b02b6c04efc0f4854d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4d0e34bef478ed432c8de7ef68dc9025&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d65840dd2cbd5c9984dfc4334378df5e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ee2684edaea64aa597fd29c3bbda611d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2dc2313c92b2af4132faaa4d41449eef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50719bcc88f4515ec825b9d5a7aba107&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f09811b149a29105854a0b1e84951e5d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-88b97cde53943160602b20f634ba5c1f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8ef15154a94043650617b3b24d8146a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f36263c657ad99a80e578ac49a333d5b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0fa819f7e1e42eb688d4894dc3ca7e64&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-577779892c0d463cd6bb1966b8a8ce2d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/Bula Humalog.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Basaglar.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_1778357531609.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Toujeo.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_apidra.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_fiasp.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786319722</data>
