<node id="Nicotine">
  <data key="d0">Nicotine</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Nicotine is a natural alkaloid and central nervous system stimulant most commonly associated with tobacco products; it is known to influence drug‑metabolizing enzymes and therefore can affect the pharmacokinetics and pharmacodynamics of concomitantly administered medicines.  

Research on nicotine’s drug‑interaction profile is heterogeneous. An interaction between nicotine and the rapid‑acting insulin analogue Humalog has been examined, although the specific outcomes of that investigation are not detailed in the provided descriptions. In contrast, nicotine’s potential interactions with several other agents have not been studied or investigated. These agents include the insulin‑glucose‑lowering product BASAGLAR (both the standard formulation and the KWIKPEN device), the GLP‑1 receptor agonist APIDRA (including its SOLOSTAR formulation), and the human insulin preparation Humulin R. Consequently, for these medications, the effect of nicotine on their pharmacokinetics and pharmacodynamics remains unknown.&lt;SEP&gt;Nicotine is the tobacco‑derived alkaloid whose plasma levels were measured after aerosol inhalation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4d26ce64e79b8c4a147140be2f9c63dd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3db0edd23b6b502ccbbf62bfd601ce68&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d96761d60c65f05f1530bc19b144cf1b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4ce520f0fe7dc4a6c79f92a25dfaff19&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-465ad8b77c1c2a2a179062da20337ff5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f09811b149a29105854a0b1e84951e5d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0fa819f7e1e42eb688d4894dc3ca7e64&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-577779892c0d463cd6bb1966b8a8ce2d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6b95d32a33501b281cbbf40dd69ba1e5</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/Bula Humalog.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Basaglar.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_1778357531609.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_apidra.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/Inhaling medicines_ delivering drugs to the body through the lungs _ Nature Reviews Drug Discovery.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786330906</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Laboratory Tests">
  <data key="d0">Laboratory Tests</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Laboratory tests are diagnostic procedures that may have potential interactions with Humalog.&lt;SEP&gt;Laboratory tests are diagnostic procedures for which interaction with BASAGLAR remains uninvestigated.&lt;SEP&gt;Laboratory Tests are medical examinations whose interaction with BASAGLAR KWIKPEN was not investigated.&lt;SEP&gt;Laboratory tests are medical examinations performed on biological samples to assess health status.&lt;SEP&gt;Laboratory tests are clinical examinations that may interact with Humulin R, though no studies exist.&lt;SEP&gt;Laboratory tests are clinical examinations that have not been studied for interaction with Humulin R.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4d26ce64e79b8c4a147140be2f9c63dd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3db0edd23b6b502ccbbf62bfd601ce68&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d96761d60c65f05f1530bc19b144cf1b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4ce520f0fe7dc4a6c79f92a25dfaff19&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0fa819f7e1e42eb688d4894dc3ca7e64&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-577779892c0d463cd6bb1966b8a8ce2d</data>
