</node>
<node id="Injeção subcutânea">
  <data key="d0">Injeção subcutânea</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Injeção subcutânea is the recommended route for administering Lantus, involving injection into the subcutaneous tissue.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-29a33072a90b4191a8b6c5136c417e4c</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/LANTUS _ BulasMed.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786304201</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Coxa">
  <data key="d0">Coxa</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">Coxa is the anatomical term for the thigh region, specifically the upper part of the leg near the hip, and it is commonly employed as a sub‑cutaneous injection site for several insulin preparations. Health professionals consider the coxa a suitable and often recommended location for delivering insulin analogues such as Lantus (insulin glargine), Tresiba (insulin degludec), APIDRA (insulin glulisine), APIDRA SOLOSTAR, and the short‑acting formulation Novolin® R.

For Lantus, Tresiba, and APIDRA, the coxa is listed among the preferred sites because it provides reliable absorption while allowing patients to rotate injection areas to reduce lipohypertrophy. In the case of APIDRA, the thigh (coxa) yields a bioavailability of approximately 68 % and demonstrates a slightly slower absorption rate compared with other sites, a characteristic that is similarly reported for insulin glulisine when injected into this region. APIDRA SOLOSTAR follows the same recommendation, using the coxa as a safe sub‑cutaneous location.

Novolin® R may be administered in the coxa as an alternative to more traditional sites such as the abdomen or upper arm, offering comparable efficacy while giving patients flexibility in site selection. Across all mentioned insulins, the coxa’s muscular and sub‑cutaneous tissue composition supports consistent pharmacokinetic profiles, making it a practical choice for both routine and individualized insulin therapy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-29a33072a90b4191a8b6c5136c417e4c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-11cce86325de9748e794648198242578&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b65ee62ad12239ddc729c50a1aef854c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4d0e34bef478ed432c8de7ef68dc9025&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-15a498084b9a0c4cfcd9aa9553e12a14&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7621ac447c9044986ade86ce5f9be201&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b060d4f68031bd35dfafc19eadf1e9fe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0689fd73d2061ee466b9b90e03bda141</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/LANTUS _ BulasMed.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/TRESIBA _ BulasMed.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_apidra.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786318573</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Deltoide">
  <data key="d0">Deltoide</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Deltoide is the shoulder muscle area acceptable for subcutaneous injection of Lantus.&lt;SEP&gt;Deltoide refers to the deltoid muscle region used for subcutaneous APIDRA injection.&lt;SEP&gt;Deltoide is a body region where APIDRA can be injected, showing a biodisponibilidade of about 71 %.&lt;SEP&gt;The deltoid muscle, a recommended site for subcutaneous injection of APIDRA.&lt;SEP&gt;Deltoide is a recommended subcutaneous injection site for APIDRA SOLOSTAR.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-29a33072a90b4191a8b6c5136c417e4c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4d0e34bef478ed432c8de7ef68dc9025&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-15a498084b9a0c4cfcd9aa9553e12a14&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7621ac447c9044986ade86ce5f9be201&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b060d4f68031bd35dfafc19eadf1e9fe</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/LANTUS _ BulasMed.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_apidra.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786315414</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Temperatura de 2–8°C">
  <data key="d0">Temperatura de 2–8°C</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Temperatura de 2–8°C is the recommended refrigerated storage range for Lantus to maintain stability.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-29a33072a90b4191a8b6c5136c417e4c</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/LANTUS _ BulasMed.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786304201</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Antidiabetic Oral Medications">
  <data key="d0">Antidiabetic Oral Medications</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Antidiabetic oral medications are non‑insulin drugs mentioned as alternatives that may require dose adjustment when used with Lantus.&lt;SEP&gt;Antidiabetic Oral Medications are pills taken to lower blood glucose that can be combined with Tresiba® therapy.&lt;SEP&gt;Antidiabetic oral medications are tablets taken by people with diabetes that can increase the glucose‑lowering effect of insulin.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d59c9bf7f429a82cbfd7083e36ff8f9a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e9ae5f9ffa7eff9bb36cf1a9764df3e7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d96761d60c65f05f1530bc19b144cf1b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/LANTUS _ BulasMed.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/TRESIBA _ BulasMed.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Basaglar.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786310038</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Diabetic Patients">
  <data key="d0">Diabetic Patients</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Diabetic patients are individuals with diabetes who require glucose monitoring and may be treated with Lantus or other insulin therapies.&lt;SEP&gt;Diabetic Patients are individuals with diabetes who may require insulin therapy and are advised about APIDRA use.&lt;SEP&gt;Diabetic Patients are individuals receiving insulin therapy, including APIDRA SOLOSTAR, and requiring glucose monitoring and dose adjustments.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d59c9bf7f429a82cbfd7083e36ff8f9a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-518838d3c8e8110567b1891b704bfef9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c95471c4c993fa3a499f99443ee7c922&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e3418c4ee80182ca29214dd54b0d9647</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/LANTUS _ BulasMed.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_apidra.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786315447</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Children Above 2 Years">
  <data key="d0">Children Above 2 Years</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Children above two years are pediatric diabetic patients for whom Lantus dosing must be individualized by a physician based on metabolic needs and frequent glucose monitoring.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d59c9bf7f429a82cbfd7083e36ff8f9a</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/LANTUS _ BulasMed.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786304201</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Adult Patients">
  <data key="d0">Adult Patients</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Adult patients are diabetic individuals for whom Lantus dosing follows similar individualized principles as in pediatric patients.&lt;SEP&gt;Adult patients represent the adult population whose pharmacodynamic response to insulin aspart was used as a reference.&lt;SEP&gt;Adult Patients are the adult population (including healthy adults and adults with Type 1 Diabetes) used as reference groups in APIDRA studies.&lt;SEP&gt;Adult patients refer to study participants aged 18 years or older enrolled in the clinical trials evaluating Apidra SoloStar.&lt;SEP&gt;Adults with Type 2 diabetes who participated in the Phase III adult clinical trial.&lt;SEP&gt;Adult patients refer to study participants aged 18 years and older.&lt;SEP&gt;Adult Patients are individuals aged 18 years or older with diabetes for whom TIR targets are defined.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d59c9bf7f429a82cbfd7083e36ff8f9a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6b14c2f0985ae4a417c8fc99e339bd9e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-162882e6afffb0db8ae5e9153e5f1e82&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4d0e34bef478ed432c8de7ef68dc9025&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-891989adf06518cd34c94853444495e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c8c7e36686d077dcb6239405f60ea031&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-94150b57cc35a773b7c36f33f237f8a1</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/LANTUS _ BulasMed.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/NOVORAPID _ BulasMed.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_apidra.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_fiasp.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/cgm.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786335245</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Patients Under 2 Years">
  <data key="d0">Patients Under 2 Years</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Patients under two years are a population for which no clinical safety data are available for Lantus use.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d59c9bf7f429a82cbfd7083e36ff8f9a</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/LANTUS _ BulasMed.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786304202</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Neurological Disorders">
  <data key="d0">Neurological Disorders</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Neurological disorders are adverse neurological effects that may follow severe or recurrent hypoglycemic episodes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d59c9bf7f429a82cbfd7083e36ff8f9a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-da44554b006e6bd1b841f4246a054669</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/LANTUS _ BulasMed.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786304202</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Vision">
  <data key="d0">Vision</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Vision refers to visual function that can be temporarily impaired or lost during severe hypoglycemia, especially in patients with proliferative retinopathy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d59c9bf7f429a82cbfd7083e36ff8f9a</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/LANTUS _ BulasMed.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786304202</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Diabetic Retinopathy">
  <data key="d0">Diabetic Retinopathy</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Diabetic retinopathy is a progressive ocular disease characterized by damage to the retinal cells that results from chronic exposure to high blood‑glucose levels and poor glycemic control.  

The condition may experience a transient exacerbation when blood‑sugar levels are rapidly lowered, such as during intensive insulin therapy, sudden improvement of glycemia, or the abrupt intensification of regimens that include agents like Levemir® or Novolin® R. This short‑term worsening reflects a temporary response of the retinal vasculature to rapid metabolic shifts rather than an indication of permanent damage.  

Despite this temporary flare‑up, sustained and well‑maintained glycemic control over the long term reduces the likelihood of disease progression and lowers the overall risk of vision‑threatening complications associated with diabetic retinopathy.&lt;SEP&gt;An eye condition that can worsen during rapid glucose control improvements associated with MiniMed 780G use.&lt;SEP&gt;Diabetic Retinopathy is a microvascular complication of diabetes affecting the retina.&lt;SEP&gt;Diabetic retinopathy is an eye disease whose presence was associated with higher HbA1c levels in the cited studies.&lt;SEP&gt;Diabetic Retinopathy is a microvascular eye complication of diabetes causing vision loss.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d59c9bf7f429a82cbfd7083e36ff8f9a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f9e5c50e8a808c537075377966ae2ccd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3e50c145614f04be2319a31b74b80411&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e8934881ec5ab7cfeb836126b3f0e8b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d10a1f849386df540104c79e33a7b242&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0ace26fdb0244e3d0f714a007c9bbb51&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c68e2c07786710dd5250c6610f52b14d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-73559dc5d86ea52a348d603482e056e9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-474703bb16e6e26e009e9d433c3d3647&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6a92f811a7d2d835dc4b730c9bbf08cf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-44aa59c0e5cc620a11b8fb017d1aefcf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5e551f4b7f03919afc1d663b3b2a2efa</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/LANTUS _ BulasMed.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/NOVORAPID _ BulasMed.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Basaglar.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Toujeo.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_fiasp.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Diagnóstico de diabetes mellitus.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786371922</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Proliferative Retinopathy">
  <data key="d0">Proliferative Retinopathy</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Proliferative retinopathy is an advanced stage of diabetic retinopathy that can be aggravated by severe hypoglycemic episodes if not treated with photocoagulation.&lt;SEP&gt;Proliferative retinopathy is an advanced diabetic eye disease that can cause transient blindness after hypoglycemia.&lt;SEP&gt;Proliferative retinopathy is an advanced stage of diabetic retinopathy characterized by abnormal blood vessel growth.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d59c9bf7f429a82cbfd7083e36ff8f9a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6ca13e396b094f0c2f482892f220f538&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e8934881ec5ab7cfeb836126b3f0e8b2</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/LANTUS _ BulasMed.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Basaglar.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Toujeo.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786313629</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Lipo‑Hypertrophy">
  <data key="d0">Lipo‑Hypertrophy</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Lipo‑hypertrophy is an increase in fatty tissue at the insulin injection site observed in a small percentage of patients.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d59c9bf7f429a82cbfd7083e36ff8f9a</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/LANTUS _ BulasMed.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786304202</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Lipoatrophy">
  <data key="d0">Lipoatrophy</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Lipoatrophy is a decrease of fatty tissue at the insulin injection site, reported as uncommon.&lt;SEP&gt;Lipoatrophy is a loss of subcutaneous fat reported as an adverse reaction in insulin‑treated patients.&lt;SEP&gt;Lipoatrophy is a localized loss of subcutaneous fat at injection sites.&lt;SEP&gt;Lipoatrophy is a depression of the skin occurring rarely after subcutaneous insulin administration.&lt;SEP&gt;Lipoatrophy is a less frequent skin issue linked to insulin pump therapy.&lt;SEP&gt;Lipoatrophy is a loss of fat tissue linked to NRTI use and insulin resistance.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d59c9bf7f429a82cbfd7083e36ff8f9a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d194d06ef99b3f8aa6b6542b7e93e762&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e8934881ec5ab7cfeb836126b3f0e8b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-779af610d7298ce98490962cd90b4e76&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b3b81193a603a098b1ff9f6f0f665fec&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-55e58732610596ce9a8f3145d34f75a7</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/LANTUS _ BulasMed.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Basaglar.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Toujeo.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/blood glucose monitoring.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377373</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Injection Site Reactions">
  <data key="d0">Injection Site Reactions</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Injection Site Reactions are local adverse events that can occur at the site of insulin administration.  They typically manifest as pain, redness, itching or pruritus, urticaria, swelling, bruising or ecchymosis, edema, and inflammation.  These reactions represent the most common types of local responses observed after subcutaneous insulin injection, regardless of the specific product used.  

The frequency and prominence of Injection Site Reactions may vary among different insulin formulations.  They are reported as uncommon adverse events with the rapid‑acting analogue NovoRapid, where local inflammation has been noted.  Similar local reactions are listed for the ultra‑fast acting Fiasp® product, without indication of a particular incidence rate.  In contrast, the long‑acting analogue Levemir® has been associated with a higher occurrence of these reactions—such as pain, redness, urticaria, inflammation, ecchymosis, edema, and pruritus—when compared with traditional human insulin preparations.  

Overall, Injection Site Reactions encompass a spectrum of mild to moderate skin and sub‑skin changes that arise shortly after insulin injection and are generally self‑limiting, though they may influence patient comfort and adherence to therapy.&lt;SEP&gt;Injection site reactions include redness, swelling, or itching where insulin is injected.&lt;SEP&gt;Injection site reactions are adverse responses associated with subcutaneous insulin injections.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d59c9bf7f429a82cbfd7083e36ff8f9a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6d0f18c80f8de2dee960a03599d12052&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4f079198593c1702b56062aa87e7801a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7fdc648ec086061141581e27adde6fc4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0ace26fdb0244e3d0f714a007c9bbb51&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9a6f9e10c0d4af5fff0338eb861f9c86&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dd396c45bc09fb646d156b4e69d328e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea9b3836b3275f451c3acfb189f42a6f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-06425d1f80d868bd58871b6a6e740102&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8644d98286c4a296063176435b45d589</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/LANTUS _ BulasMed.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/NOVORAPID _ BulasMed.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_fiasp.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/Understanding insulin - International Diabetes Federation.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/edelman-et-al-2026-dosing-afrezza-it-s-not-that-complicated.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786333267</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Allergic Reactions">
  <data key="d0">Allergic Reactions</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Allergic reactions are immediate-type hypersensitivity responses to insulin or its excipients, potentially causing generalized skin eruptions, angioedema, bronchospasm, hypotension, or shock.&lt;SEP&gt;Allergic reactions are adverse events reported for both BASAGLAR and Lantus® groups.&lt;SEP&gt;Allergic reactions are adverse events evaluated in clinical studies comparing BASAGLAR and Lantus.&lt;SEP&gt;Allergic reactions encompass cutaneous manifestations such as eczema, rash, urticaria, and dermatitis reported with Fiasp®.&lt;SEP&gt;Allergic reactions to insulin are rare but can cause rash, breathing difficulty, or swelling.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d59c9bf7f429a82cbfd7083e36ff8f9a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-22df77f7bf817d736d90608e62a11d84&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5c580ebfc111aa29796af1a6f15941c7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7fdc648ec086061141581e27adde6fc4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-06425d1f80d868bd58871b6a6e740102</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/LANTUS _ BulasMed.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Basaglar.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_fiasp.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/Understanding insulin - International Diabetes Federation.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786332451</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Antibodies">
  <data key="d0">Antibodies</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Antibodies are immune proteins that can be formed in response to insulin therapy.&lt;SEP&gt;Antibodies are immune proteins that may develop after insulin administration and can necessitate insulin dose adjustments.&lt;SEP&gt;Antibodies are immune proteins that can cross‑react with insulin glargine and human insulin, sometimes affecting dosing.&lt;SEP&gt;Antibodies are immune proteins that can develop after insulin administration and may cross‑react with human insulin and insulin glargine.&lt;SEP&gt;Antibodies are immune proteins that can develop against Levemir® but were reported not to affect glycemic control.&lt;SEP&gt;Antibodies are immune proteins that were detected in patients using Levemir® but reported not to affect glycemic control.&lt;SEP&gt;Antibodies are biomarkers referenced in the context of assessing whether they predict success with insulin pump therapy, which they do not.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d59c9bf7f429a82cbfd7083e36ff8f9a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4da80e99fd3e43cb7d3b260aca23fe56&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d194d06ef99b3f8aa6b6542b7e93e762&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3e50c145614f04be2319a31b74b80411&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50a4f77ab697e068f8cf31533065722b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-68b98187c6ab15468f1c0d8f5e7f9f6a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b3b81193a603a098b1ff9f6f0f665fec</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/LANTUS _ BulasMed.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Basaglar.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/blood glucose monitoring.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786335867</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Dose Adjustment">
  <data key="d0">Dose Adjustment</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Dose Adjustment is the clinical process of modifying the amount, timing, or administration schedule of insulin in order to achieve and maintain optimal glycemic control for an individual patient. The adjustment may involve changing the dosage of specific insulin products such as Lantus, Humalog Mix 50 KwikPen, Levemir®, Humulin R, or any other formulation, and can also include altering the number of daily injections or switching to a different insulin type or regimen.

The decision to adjust a dose is driven by a range of patient‑specific factors. Continuous or periodic glucose monitoring results, overall metabolic control indicators, and individual glycemic readings are primary triggers. Clinicians also respond to changes in insulin potency, manufacturer, or co‑medication, as well as to physiological or lifestyle changes such as illness, variations in activity level, diet, organ insufficiency, or drug interactions. Episodes of extreme hyper‑ or hypoglycemia, adverse effects, the presence of anti‑insulin antibodies, and recent modifications in the broader therapeutic regimen further inform the need for adjustment.

Individual characteristics are evaluated to tailor each modification. Age, weight, renal and hepatic function, dietary habits, physical activity, and concurrent medications all influence the appropriate insulin dose. Lifestyle factors, including daily routine and exercise patterns, are considered alongside clinical parameters to ensure the adjustment is personalized. The overarching goal of any dose adjustment is to lower blood glucose effectively while minimizing the risk of hypoglycemia and other insulin‑related complications, thereby providing a balanced and safe therapeutic outcome for each patient.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d59c9bf7f429a82cbfd7083e36ff8f9a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6d0f18c80f8de2dee960a03599d12052&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d194d06ef99b3f8aa6b6542b7e93e762&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3e50c145614f04be2319a31b74b80411&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6ca13e396b094f0c2f482892f220f538&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a2416b3e5e8ebc96cdb451a794fc78e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-93623071acdcd0ba060c8826ab5a2a81&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d7223c781e745e72311fccfcdd58583&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c95471c4c993fa3a499f99443ee7c922&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0ace26fdb0244e3d0f714a007c9bbb51&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8a68ba1e8cc1defda76cde0eff9592e6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0955cb70a6ce135722726162a9811e78&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a1245bd9ff75c998b49dab861cc4cebf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0fa819f7e1e42eb688d4894dc3ca7e64&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-577779892c0d463cd6bb1966b8a8ce2d</data>
