<node id="Insulin Glargina">
  <data key="d0">Insulin Glargina</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Insulin glargine is a long‑acting insulin analogue produced by recombinant DNA technology and administered by subcutaneous injection to regulate blood glucose levels in patients with diabetes. It provides a prolonged glucose‑lowering effect with a relatively flat time‑action profile and no pronounced peak, allowing for sustained glycemic control over 24 hours. The molecule is the active insulin analogue found in commercial preparations such as Lantus® and BASAGLAR, the latter being supplied in a KwikPen at a concentration of 100 IU/mL.

Because of its extended duration of action, insulin glargine’s effect can delay the recovery from hypoglycemia once it occurs, a characteristic that clinicians consider when titrating doses. Pharmacokinetic and pharmacodynamic properties—including absorption, metabolism, and activity—are described in the product labeling and reflect its stable, slow release from the subcutaneous depot.

Clinical observations have noted that insulin glargine may offer an improved therapeutic response in patients who have developed antibodies to human insulin, and its safety profile includes the typical adverse reactions associated with insulin therapy. Overall, insulin glargine serves as a cornerstone basal insulin for maintaining consistent blood glucose control in both type 1 and type 2 diabetes management.&lt;SEP&gt;Insulin Glargina is a long‑acting insulin that is the active ingredient in TOUJEO 300 U/mL.&lt;SEP&gt;Insulin Glargina is a basal insulin administered once daily at bedtime in the described studies.&lt;SEP&gt;Insulin glargina is a long‑acting basal insulin used as part of combination therapy in the adult Type 1 diabetes arms of the studies.&lt;SEP&gt;Insulin Glargina is a long‑acting basal insulin combined with Fiasp® or NovoRapid® in the study.&lt;SEP&gt;Insulin glargina is a long‑acting insulin analogue listed as a possible basal insulin.&lt;SEP&gt;Insulin glargina is a long‑acting insulin analogue mentioned as a comparator for glycemic control.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-67563459bb64c390a40207da52944afd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-572e715aada476f4dac69a032e16cc09&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ffb10c00517fa772be2ca9a42f497edf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-da44554b006e6bd1b841f4246a054669&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-46c9571a4df1570d4a097dc949f512cd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cc9821850f5a0f8be1e4dd3fd0df6fcf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f14ce019f10c2a88765380143498ba5b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-45d489de28e8fda3c3be3bb09ab29eb2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-133169995b3ab942fd96f1fdfe7269ad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d7223c781e745e72311fccfcdd58583&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-29710f08f3e10bba4a464e8b4da1917c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b18f8ab53481bf1b63fda1bb71fe80ec&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9f85d0ab4cfadc905544cb9e30752dab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2073bddd90c7dd8e156b67821f0f3247&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-68b98187c6ab15468f1c0d8f5e7f9f6a</data>
