<node id="Oral Antidiabetic Medication">
  <data key="d0">Oral Antidiabetic Medication</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Oral antidiabetic medications are drug classes taken by mouth to help control blood glucose in diabetic patients.&lt;SEP&gt;Oral antidiabetic medication denotes non‑insulin drugs taken by mouth to control blood glucose in diabetes.&lt;SEP&gt;Oral Antidiabetic Medication is a class of non‑insulin drugs that may require dose adjustment when used with insulin therapy.&lt;SEP&gt;Medications taken by mouth to control early diabetes in lipodystrophy patients.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-67563459bb64c390a40207da52944afd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bbae57922175913b7c36c594b4673fa2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c95471c4c993fa3a499f99443ee7c922&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-005de970178a46619506bcc15fe94fa9</data>
