</node>
<node id="Crianças">
  <data key="d0">Crianças</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Crianças refers to pediatric patients, specifically children who are considered for insulin therapy with insulin glargine (Lantus). In the approved labeling, Lantus may be used in children aged two years or older, while safety and efficacy have not been studied in children younger than two years.

Because the medication is delivered via injection devices, children classified as Crianças must be kept away from pens, needles, the injection system, and any associated collectors to prevent accidental exposure or injury. Likewise, the medication itself should be stored out of reach of these children for safety reasons.

When Crianças receive insulin via infusion, they may develop scar formation and other infusion‑site reactions at the injection site. Additionally, they can exhibit specific symptoms of hypoglycemia, which necessitates careful monitoring.

To address these risks, children identified as Crianças are often included in training programs that teach hypoglycemia awareness and safe handling of insulin delivery equipment, ensuring both the children’s safety and effective disease management.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a976e1642df27c488174759a35ca23f2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5b40c2fbad301807d9646f27d94635cb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1aba4eb027a027fb1ad6e0105b97cfa3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a557234bf75633a4af048115a6f0c449&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0689fd73d2061ee466b9b90e03bda141&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a48e1013c4a32aca64a00d073b2ee797&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-336a2f2c9b510e23c35be95e2ff7a72a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cbede05ec60d9c79d637d9a0eb0efe48&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0e484a5a1df875be2e1525c8c64e2007</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/LANTUS _ BulasMed.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Basaglar.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_1778357531609.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_fiasp.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Descarte/descarte.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/Orientacoes_Hipoglicemia_SBD_transcricao.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1786338256</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Mulheres Grávidas">
  <data key="d0">Mulheres Grávidas</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Mulheres Grávidas are pregnant women with diabetes who must monitor glucose closely and may use Lantus under medical guidance.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a976e1642df27c488174759a35ca23f2</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/LANTUS _ BulasMed.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786304210</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Insuficiência Renal">
  <data key="d0">Insuficiência Renal</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Insuficiência Renal, also referred to as renal insufficiency or renal failure, is a medical condition characterized by a reduction in kidney function. The diminished capacity of the kidneys impairs the normal metabolism and clearance of insulin, which can consequently lower the insulin requirements of patients with diabetes.  

Because the altered insulin handling may lead to a higher circulating insulin exposure, clinicians often need to adjust insulin dosing when treating diabetic individuals who have Insuficiência Renal. This adjustment can apply to various insulin formulations, including rapid‑acting agents such as Fiasp® and long‑acting analogues such as APIDRA SOLOSTAR. The need for dose modification is typically accompanied by more intensive glucose monitoring to avoid hypoglycemia and to maintain glycemic targets.  

In Portuguese, the condition is described as “comprometimento da função renal que pode alterar as necessidades de insulina,” emphasizing that kidney impairment can change how much insulin a patient requires. Overall, Insuficiência Renal denotes a state of reduced renal function that necessitates careful evaluation of insulin therapy, possible dose reductions, and heightened surveillance of blood glucose levels.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a976e1642df27c488174759a35ca23f2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-da44554b006e6bd1b841f4246a054669&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-46c9571a4df1570d4a097dc949f512cd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-61cacf80ada6db26d2b975df763c137a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5b40c2fbad301807d9646f27d94635cb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-518838d3c8e8110567b1891b704bfef9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e4ba52cc293c5c002b470566321026d6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-09d60e0b850d87c77dd67ca2d709912c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cbe87fd92ad66dcb02b25b669d829f6c</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/LANTUS _ BulasMed.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Basaglar.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_apidra.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_fiasp.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786319744</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Insuficiência Hepática">
  <data key="d0">Insuficiência Hepática</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Insuficiência Hepática refers to severe liver dysfunction or hepatic failure that markedly impairs the liver’s metabolic activities. Because the damaged liver produces less glucose through gluconeogenesis and has a diminished capacity to metabolize insulin, patients with this condition typically experience lower insulin requirements. The reduction in endogenous glucose production and the slower clearance of insulin from the circulation mean that standard insulin doses can lead to hypoglycemia if not adjusted.

Consequently, individuals with Insuficiência Hepática need intensified glucose monitoring and careful titration of insulin therapy. Clinicians are advised to regularly assess blood glucose levels and consider dose reductions for both basal and rapid‑acting insulins, including formulations such as Fiasp®. Adjustments should be individualized, taking into account the degree of hepatic impairment and the patient’s overall glycemic control, to maintain safe and effective diabetes management while accounting for the altered pharmacokinetics associated with hepatic insufficiency.&lt;SEP&gt;Comprometimento da função hepática que pode mudar a dose de insulina.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a976e1642df27c488174759a35ca23f2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-da44554b006e6bd1b841f4246a054669&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-46c9571a4df1570d4a097dc949f512cd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-61cacf80ada6db26d2b975df763c137a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-17844a4a12e6c05ba2d7b5f54b0f9bd7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5b40c2fbad301807d9646f27d94635cb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-518838d3c8e8110567b1891b704bfef9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e4ba52cc293c5c002b470566321026d6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-09d60e0b850d87c77dd67ca2d709912c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cbe87fd92ad66dcb02b25b669d829f6c</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/LANTUS _ BulasMed.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Basaglar.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_apidra.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_fiasp.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786319737</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Viagem">
  <data key="d0">Viagem</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Viagem denotes travel, during which patients should consult a médico about insulin availability, storage, and dose adjustments.&lt;SEP&gt;Travel refers to journeys that may involve time‑zone differences affecting insulin scheduling.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a976e1642df27c488174759a35ca23f2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-929e31613caadc967412041c8c2155b3</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/LANTUS _ BulasMed.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786319689</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Driving">
  <data key="d0">Driving</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Driving, the activity of operating a motor vehicle, requires full concentration, quick reaction, and sustained attention to ensure safety on the road.  

The safety and performance of driving can be compromised in individuals with diabetes. Episodes of hypoglycemia (low blood‑glucose levels) are repeatedly identified as a condition that may impair a driver’s ability to concentrate, react promptly, and maintain control of the vehicle. Extreme blood‑glucose fluctuations, including hyperglycemia (high blood‑glucose levels), similarly pose safety risks, potentially reducing alertness and decision‑making capacity. In addition, vision impairment associated with diabetic eye disease can further diminish a driver’s ability to perceive hazards and navigate effectively.  

Overall, driving is defined as the operation of a motor vehicle, and in the context of diabetes it is an activity that may become unsafe when blood‑glucose levels are poorly controlled or when visual complications are present.&lt;SEP&gt;Driving is the activity of operating a motor vehicle, which may be impaired by hypoglycemia.&lt;SEP&gt;Driving is an activity that may be hazardous for patients experiencing hypoglycemia while using Humulin R.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a976e1642df27c488174759a35ca23f2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6d0f18c80f8de2dee960a03599d12052&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4704ea4d5c15ebc8c043a077f05fd7a3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fd94288932ad6675a1de2b46b3fd9128&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cedd8e88a8d35eade68ce02222b9e276&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3237e202569462c758ec3d878c9faeae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4615ca664e7ff898d8c5929cbc79e7d8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ba6b31518be6fff1db8b68a28e82f200&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0fa819f7e1e42eb688d4894dc3ca7e64&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-577779892c0d463cd6bb1966b8a8ce2d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/LANTUS _ BulasMed.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/NOVORAPID _ BulasMed.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/TRESIBA _ BulasMed.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_1778357531609.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786319727</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Interacting Substances">
  <data key="d0">Interacting Substances</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Interacting Substances are various medications (e.g., oral antidiabetics, corticosteroids, beta‑blockers) that can alter insulin’s glucose‑lowering effect and require dose monitoring.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a976e1642df27c488174759a35ca23f2</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/LANTUS _ BulasMed.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786304210</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Carboidrato">
  <data key="d0">Carboidrato</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Carboidrato refers to dietary carbohydrates that must be maintained in intake for patients with Diabetes Tipo 1.&lt;SEP&gt;Carboidrato is a source of glucose that patients should carry (at least 20 g) for immediate treatment of hypoglycemia.&lt;SEP&gt;Carboidrato is a fast‑acting carbohydrate recommended for immediate correction of hypoglycemia.&lt;SEP&gt;Nutrient offered to treat hypoglycemia.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a976e1642df27c488174759a35ca23f2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-46c9571a4df1570d4a097dc949f512cd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9cd336474a2e9457985162b1ddb4b603&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5341c88e6470a893413f9aaec70dbdae</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/LANTUS _ BulasMed.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Basaglar.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Toujeo.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/HIPO_HIPER.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786337243</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Seringas">
  <data key="d0">Seringas</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Seringas are syringes used for administering insulin.&lt;SEP&gt;Seringas are devices used to inject insulin.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a976e1642df27c488174759a35ca23f2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-46c9571a4df1570d4a097dc949f512cd</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/LANTUS _ BulasMed.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Basaglar.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786310006</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Armazenagem da Insulina">
  <data key="d0">Armazenagem da Insulina</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Armazenagem da Insulina is the proper storage of insulin, especially important during travel.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a976e1642df27c488174759a35ca23f2</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/LANTUS _ BulasMed.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786304211</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Zonas Climáticas">
  <data key="d0">Zonas Climáticas</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Zonas Climáticas are different climate zones that may alter insulin’s effects and require dosage adjustments.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a976e1642df27c488174759a35ca23f2</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/LANTUS _ BulasMed.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786304211</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Visão Prejudicada">
  <data key="d0">Visão Prejudicada</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Visão Prejudicada is impaired vision that can affect concentration and driving safety in diabetic patients.&lt;SEP&gt;Visão Prejudicada describes impaired eyesight, listed as a factor that may affect driving ability.&lt;SEP&gt;Impaired vision is a condition that can diminish concentration and reaction, affecting tasks like driving.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a976e1642df27c488174759a35ca23f2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-17844a4a12e6c05ba2d7b5f54b0f9bd7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5b40c2fbad301807d9646f27d94635cb</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/LANTUS _ BulasMed.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Basaglar.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786310045</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Amamentação">
  <data key="d0">Amamentação</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Amamentação is breastfeeding, during which insulin dose and diet may need adjustment.&lt;SEP&gt;Amamentação (lactation) refers to breastfeeding, during which insulin exposure through milk is considered.&lt;SEP&gt;Amamentação denotes lactation, a condition where dose adjustments of insulin may be needed and excretion of insulin into human milk is uncertain.&lt;SEP&gt;Amamentação is breastfeeding, mentioned alongside pregnancy regarding the lack of clinical studies for Humalog Mix 25 KwikPen.&lt;SEP&gt;Período de lactação que pode demandar ajustes na dose de insulina.&lt;SEP&gt;Amamentação is the act of breastfeeding, which should be encouraged and supported.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a976e1642df27c488174759a35ca23f2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-17844a4a12e6c05ba2d7b5f54b0f9bd7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-518838d3c8e8110567b1891b704bfef9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a247846b9ec5d44d0bcbe6c5f15599f8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cbe87fd92ad66dcb02b25b669d829f6c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f645bd7019e94151caaff47d6cbfcaf</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/LANTUS _ BulasMed.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Basaglar.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_1778357531609.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/Orientacoes_Hipoglicemia_SBD_transcricao.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1786338267</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Primeiro Trimestre">
  <data key="d0">Primeiro Trimestre</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Primeiro Trimestre refers to the first three months of pregnancy, during which insulin needs may decrease.&lt;SEP&gt;Primeiro período da gestação em que as necessidades de insulina tendem a diminuir.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a976e1642df27c488174759a35ca23f2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cbe87fd92ad66dcb02b25b669d829f6c</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/LANTUS _ BulasMed.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786319735</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Segundo Trimestre">
  <data key="d0">Segundo Trimestre</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Segundo Trimestre refers to the second three months of pregnancy, during which insulin needs generally increase.&lt;SEP&gt;Segundo período da gestação em que as necessidades de insulina aumentam.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a976e1642df27c488174759a35ca23f2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cbe87fd92ad66dcb02b25b669d829f6c</data>
