  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Glicerol">
  <data key="d0">Glicerol</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Glicerol, also known as glycerol, is a polyhydric alcohol (polyol) that is commonly employed as an excipient in pharmaceutical formulations, particularly in injectable insulin products. As an excipient, it functions to stabilize the active ingredient, adjust tonicity, and improve the overall physicochemical properties of the preparation.

In the context of insulin therapeutics, glicerol is listed as an excipient in several commercially available formulations. It is included in the Lantus® insulin glargine injection, as well as in the BASAGLAR® insulin glargine formulation and its KWIKPEN delivery device. The compound also appears in the Novolin® R regular insulin product, including the FlexPen® version designed for pen‑based injection, and it is present in the Humulin® R regular insulin solution. Across these products, glicerol serves the same role of supporting the stability and usability of the injectable insulin formulation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-572e715aada476f4dac69a032e16cc09&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9e62226007200589cb2143f0fb75b302&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4d0ac8ad5968d54922b924fdb16b61d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d01ed6a801b11c1b53f4668059c1f9cb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e4e1124e7acf6619a1a7c60febd5211c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2378c57a337d1ce7103c7086ebba76ac&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-93f7f04b0529d6f0ace11829cc4fa3b4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-10dad476eb9d365159c539ced3aeec4b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-438cbb95853cdda42f2c87bcefa714dd</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/LANTUS _ BulasMed.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Basaglar.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786319709</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Ácido Clorídrico">
  <data key="d0">Ácido Clorídrico</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Ácido Clorídrico, the Spanish term for hydrochloric acid, is employed as an excipient in several injectable insulin products. In the formulation of Lantus, it is listed among the auxiliary substances that support the stability and delivery of the drug. The same acid is included in the BASAGLAR® and BASAGLAR KWIKPEN insulin solutions, where it serves specifically to adjust the pH of the preparation.

The excipient also appears in the Novolin® R product line, both in the standard vial formulation and in the Novolin® R FlexPen® prefilled pen, where it is identified as a hydrochloric acid component. Additionally, Humulin® R incorporates Ácido Clorídrico for pH regulation within its injectable formulation. Across all these insulin preparations, the primary function of Ácido Clorídrico is to fine‑tune the acidity of the solution, ensuring optimal stability and compatibility with the active insulin molecule.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-572e715aada476f4dac69a032e16cc09&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9e62226007200589cb2143f0fb75b302&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4d0ac8ad5968d54922b924fdb16b61d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d01ed6a801b11c1b53f4668059c1f9cb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e4e1124e7acf6619a1a7c60febd5211c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2378c57a337d1ce7103c7086ebba76ac&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-93f7f04b0529d6f0ace11829cc4fa3b4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-10dad476eb9d365159c539ced3aeec4b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/LANTUS _ BulasMed.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Basaglar.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786319714</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hidróxido de Sódio">
  <data key="d0">Hidróxido de Sódio</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Hidróxido de sódio is an excipient used in Lantus formulations.&lt;SEP&gt;Hidróxido de Sódio (aqueous solution) is used to adjust the pH of the BASAGLAR KWIKPEN insulin solution.&lt;SEP&gt;Hidróxido de Sódio is a sodium hydroxide listed as an excipient in Novolin® R.&lt;SEP&gt;Hidróxido de Sódio is an excipient used in the insulin formulation.&lt;SEP&gt;Hidróxido de sódio is an excipient used in the formulation of Novolin® R FlexPen® for injectable use.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-572e715aada476f4dac69a032e16cc09&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4d0ac8ad5968d54922b924fdb16b61d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d01ed6a801b11c1b53f4668059c1f9cb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2378c57a337d1ce7103c7086ebba76ac&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-93f7f04b0529d6f0ace11829cc4fa3b4</data>
