<node id="Carbohydrate">
  <data key="d0">Carbohydrate</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Carbohydrate is a nutrient that can be ingested immediately to correct hypoglycemia, such as orange juice or sugar.&lt;SEP&gt;Carbohydrate refers to a source of glucose that patients should ingest immediately to correct hypoglycemia.&lt;SEP&gt;Carbohydrate refers to oral sugars used to treat mild hypoglycemia.&lt;SEP&gt;Carbohydrate‑containing foods provide glucose; any form containing glucose can raise blood glucose during hypoglycemia treatment.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ffb10c00517fa772be2ca9a42f497edf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-45d489de28e8fda3c3be3bb09ab29eb2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d7223c781e745e72311fccfcdd58583&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cc39a0c02d5f1bd08d5cb71bacc69a24</data>
