  <data key="d5">1786372160</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Blood Glucose Monitoring">
  <data key="d0">Blood Glucose Monitoring</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Blood Glucose Monitoring is the systematic measurement of blood‑sugar (glycaemia) levels, typically performed with finger‑stick devices, test strips, or handheld meters. It is a self‑monitoring method that requires individuals with diabetes to check their glucose concentrations intermittently, often multiple times per day, and forms a core component of contemporary diabetes technology.  

As a recommended clinical practice, blood glucose monitoring guides the initiation, titration, and adjustment of insulin therapy, helping patients and health‑care providers achieve rigorous glycaemic control. The method is considered essential in several specific situations: when changing insulin injection sites, throughout pregnancy to manage maternal and fetal glucose levels, and continuously during any insulin infusion, including intravenous administration of products such as Novolin® R and its FlexPen® formulation. In these contexts, monitoring ensures that administered insulin produces the desired therapeutic effect while minimizing the risk of hypo‑ or hyperglycaemia.  

Blood glucose monitoring remains the traditional point‑of‑care approach approved for use in hospitals and is frequently employed as a reference or comparator in clinical investigations, such as the REPLACE‑BG trial that evaluated flash glucose‑sensing technology as a potential replacement for conventional finger‑stick testing. While newer continuous and flash sensing systems are emerging, traditional intermittent testing continues to be a fundamental tool for diabetes management and research.&lt;SEP&gt;Blood glucose monitoring is the method of regularly measuring glucose levels in patients with diabetes.&lt;SEP&gt;Blood Glucose Monitoring (BGM) is a method for measuring glucose levels intermittently in people with diabetes.&lt;SEP&gt;Blood Glucose Monitoring is a method of measuring glucose levels using finger‑stick tests.&lt;SEP&gt;Blood Glucose Monitoring (BGM) is the practice of measuring glucose concentrations before and after meals.&lt;SEP&gt;Blood Glucose Monitoring is the practice of frequently checking blood glucose levels, required when hyperglycemia occurs.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ffb10c00517fa772be2ca9a42f497edf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6d0f18c80f8de2dee960a03599d12052&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-42b9c5d97c54f39fb69bb1169e1de4d2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d65840dd2cbd5c9984dfc4334378df5e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bc2aa5d85d666eabc9dbaa5d2ecfe874&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d10a1f849386df540104c79e33a7b242&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0955cb70a6ce135722726162a9811e78&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-73559dc5d86ea52a348d603482e056e9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2cd48799a027437b9fe2e1a48b61cb3d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dbd74c7f87bf62557b2b4c750ec596b7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-40c2c862887db201b07c741a1862dcc1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e4c5ae163a494feafedb71ed2205c02f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c9bc5d11c9f848439320623cad3d3a38&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6fe769b03fc66d4a691f3b7f741b92cb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b4b76ae88b212b3a0a4d05c250e05e0c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d3a9b76fabae2f788f96d06b7d98c924&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-679002669c87907578534904694e17dc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-345ad64f464691cc28341ccd246032db&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b9fe6f17fdb504b9177e8ebc48505716&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a19f43c10a7a756e1597ff1a7f53296e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aff91698679a52cd7b07563b7b2627a3</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/LANTUS _ BulasMed.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/NOVORAPID _ BulasMed.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Toujeo.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_apidra.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_fiasp.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/blood glucose monitoring.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/Orientacoes_Glicemia_SBD.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Metas glicêmicas/metas cuidado do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786372099</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Retinopathy Proliferative">
  <data key="d0">Retinopathy Proliferative</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Retinopathy proliferative is a retinal lesion risk associated with severe hypoglycemia, potentially leading to transient blindness.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ffb10c00517fa772be2ca9a42f497edf</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/LANTUS _ BulasMed.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786304214</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Autonomic Neuropathy">
  <data key="d0">Autonomic Neuropathy</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Autonomic neuropathy is a nerve disease that increases the risk of severe hypoglycemia and may mask warning symptoms.&lt;SEP&gt;Autonomic neuropathy is nerve damage affecting automatic bodily functions, which may blunt hypoglycemia warning signs.&lt;SEP&gt;Autonomic neuropathy is nervous system damage in diabetic patients that increases susceptibility to hypoglycemia unawareness.&lt;SEP&gt;Autonomic Neuropathy is a disorder of the autonomic nerves, mentioned as an indication for SICI.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ffb10c00517fa772be2ca9a42f497edf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-45d489de28e8fda3c3be3bb09ab29eb2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6ca13e396b094f0c2f482892f220f538&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a7387e81b8141435df1372f5d8b27662</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/LANTUS _ BulasMed.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Basaglar.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786330138</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Interações Medicamentosas">
  <data key="d0">Interações Medicamentosas</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Interações Medicamentosas is a labeled section that provides comprehensive information on drug‑drug interactions relevant to insulin therapy. It enumerates how concomitant medications can modify the glucose‑lowering effect of insulin, including insulin glargine, by either enhancing or diminishing its efficacy. The section highlights that such interactions may alter insulin requirements, potentially necessitating dose adjustments when patients are also using other hypoglycemic agents.

The descriptions emphasize that certain drug combinations—such as thiazolidinediones (TZDs) taken together with insulin—can increase the risk of adverse effects, including severe hypoglycemia. In general, Interações Medicamentosas identifies interactions that may increase the likelihood of hypoglycemia symptoms, as well as those that could reduce insulin effectiveness, thereby influencing overall glycemic control. By detailing these potential interactions, the section serves as a reference for clinicians to assess and manage the safety and therapeutic outcomes of insulin‑based regimens.&lt;SEP&gt;Interações medicamentosas is a section of the Bula describing potential drug interactions with the Fiasp medication.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ffb10c00517fa772be2ca9a42f497edf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-46c9571a4df1570d4a097dc949f512cd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-61cacf80ada6db26d2b975df763c137a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-518838d3c8e8110567b1891b704bfef9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a86b24480e35d6df7395a60371a5f2fc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9cd336474a2e9457985162b1ddb4b603&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3397508bdfddde019cb1dfdcfb352435&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d99841fd6d1e1fbf23f184e202bc760e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53644541333e5ca7f2785d80235d27e9</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/LANTUS _ BulasMed.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Basaglar.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_1778357531609.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Toujeo.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_fiasp.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786316124</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Travel Precautions">
  <data key="d0">Travel Precautions</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Travel precautions advise patients to consult their doctor before traveling to manage insulin and glucose monitoring.&lt;SEP&gt;Travel precautions include checking insulin availability, proper storage, and dose adjustments during trips.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ffb10c00517fa772be2ca9a42f497edf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-45d489de28e8fda3c3be3bb09ab29eb2</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/LANTUS _ BulasMed.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Basaglar.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786310043</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Stress">
  <data key="d0">Stress</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Stress denotes factors that can increase the body's sensitivity to insulin, affecting dosage needs.&lt;SEP&gt;Stress refers to physiological stressors whose removal can increase insulin sensitivity.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ffb10c00517fa772be2ca9a42f497edf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9cd336474a2e9457985162b1ddb4b603</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/LANTUS _ BulasMed.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Toujeo.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786313543</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Alcohol Consumption">
  <data key="d0">Alcohol Consumption</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Alcohol Consumption is the intake of alcoholic beverages that can modify insulin needs and raise hypoglycemia risk.&lt;SEP&gt;Alcohol consumption is mentioned as a factor that can raise blood glucose levels.&lt;SEP&gt;Alcohol consumption is listed as a factor that can predispose patients to hypoglycemia.&lt;SEP&gt;Alcohol consumption is listed as a condition that can increase the risk of hypoglycemia in insulin‑treated patients.&lt;SEP&gt;The intake of alcoholic beverages that can precipitate hypoglycemic episodes.&lt;SEP&gt;Alcohol Consumption is the intake of alcoholic beverages, identified as a trigger for hypoglycemia.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ffb10c00517fa772be2ca9a42f497edf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2943becc796c8ce3f0aaedf0978c3213&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-45d489de28e8fda3c3be3bb09ab29eb2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3397508bdfddde019cb1dfdcfb352435&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dd2bfbe7cac15c6f6dc444a35691ae83&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-345ad64f464691cc28341ccd246032db</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/LANTUS _ BulasMed.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/TRESIBA _ BulasMed.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Basaglar.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Toujeo.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/Orientacoes_Hipoglicemia_SBD_transcricao.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Metas glicêmicas/metas cuidado do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786372097</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Endocrine Disorders">
  <data key="d0">Endocrine Disorders</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Endocrine Disorders are hormonal imbalances that can affect insulin action and increase hypoglycemia risk.&lt;SEP&gt;Non‑compensated endocrine disorders are noted as risk factors for hypoglycemia.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ffb10c00517fa772be2ca9a42f497edf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-45d489de28e8fda3c3be3bb09ab29eb2</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/LANTUS _ BulasMed.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Basaglar.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786310042</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Psychiatric Diseases">
  <data key="d0">Psychiatric Diseases</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Psychiatric Diseases are mental health conditions that can mask hypoglycemia symptoms, making detection harder.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ffb10c00517fa772be2ca9a42f497edf</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/LANTUS _ BulasMed.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786304215</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Metabolic Monitoring">
  <data key="d0">Metabolic Monitoring</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Metabolic Monitoring is intensified observation of metabolic parameters required when intercurrent diseases are present.&lt;SEP&gt;Metabolic monitoring denotes the increased observation of glucose levels required when intercurrent illnesses occur.&lt;SEP&gt;Metabolic monitoring involves regularly checking blood glucose to adjust insulin dosage safely.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ffb10c00517fa772be2ca9a42f497edf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3397508bdfddde019cb1dfdcfb352435&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1ee5400065df79b02b6c04efc0f4854d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/LANTUS _ BulasMed.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Toujeo.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786313560</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Insulin Sensitivity">
  <data key="d0">Insulin Sensitivity</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Insulin Sensitivity refers to the degree to which the body’s cells respond to the actions of insulin in regulating glucose metabolism. Higher insulin sensitivity means that cells more readily take up glucose in response to insulin, thereby reducing the amount of exogenous insulin required to achieve glycemic control. Conversely, lower sensitivity—often termed insulin resistance—demands larger insulin doses to obtain the same metabolic effect.

Clinically, insulin sensitivity is a patient‑specific factor that influences therapeutic decisions, including the calculation of insulin dosages, dose rounding, and adjustments of inhaled insulin products such as Afrezza. Patients with greater sensitivity may require lower dose increments, while those with reduced sensitivity may need higher or more frequent dosing to maintain target glucose levels.

Insulin sensitivity is not static; it can be modified by both pharmacologic agents and physiological conditions. Medications such as metformin and thiazolidinediones (TZDs) are known to improve sensitivity, enhancing the body’s response to insulin. Conversely, acute illness, infection, stress, and other disease‑related factors can diminish sensitivity, necessitating temporary changes in insulin therapy.

Overall, insulin sensitivity serves as a key determinant in individualized diabetes management, guiding clinicians in optimizing insulin regimens to match each patient’s metabolic responsiveness.&lt;SEP&gt;The efficiency of insulin in promoting glucose uptake, examined in the RISC study for its relationship with cardiovascular risk.&lt;SEP&gt;Insulin Sensitivity refers to how responsive cells are to insulin, noted as reduced in offspring of mothers with Gestational Diabetes Mellitus.&lt;SEP&gt;The responsiveness of tissues to insulin, mentioned as reduced in offspring of mothers with GDM.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ffb10c00517fa772be2ca9a42f497edf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-da44554b006e6bd1b841f4246a054669&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7eabee57ef0af575162ce8d36f3589a5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eb7105c2156cb3f814ebb240d4a8a1fb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4655f823785fa91e72cba96e00dba34c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5419de5a030f812ab408ef47f361bebd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-70c5a1107fcc9b632361d9c52064f45d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6fe769b03fc66d4a691f3b7f741b92cb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ec7e786a85b1b6e6cc75bcfc9189fd27&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-59dd4faf2a2706d073fdb93e1a29da81&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-49c21dd27a63d44c5d80b53aa7e1f48d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/LANTUS _ BulasMed.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Basaglar.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/edelman-et-al-2026-dosing-afrezza-it-s-not-that-complicated.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/blood glucose monitoring.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Diagnóstico de diabetes mellitus.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
