<node id="Insulin Aspart">
  <data key="d0">Insulin Aspart</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Insulin Aspart is a rapid‑acting insulin analogue produced by recombinant DNA technology that serves as the active pharmaceutical ingredient in several commercially available prandial insulin products, most prominently NovoRapid® (Novorapid) and Fiasp®. Designed for mealtime glucose control in individuals with diabetes, Insulin Aspart exhibits a fast onset of action that closely mimics the physiological response of endogenous insulin to a meal. Pharmacologically, it shows low plasma protein binding and receptor‑binding and dissociation characteristics comparable to native human insulin, enabling rapid reduction of post‑prandial blood glucose levels.

In clinical practice, Insulin Aspart is administered as the bolus component of a basal‑bolus insulin regimen. It is co‑administered with long‑acting basal insulin analogues such as insulin detemir (Levemir®) to provide comprehensive glycaemic management for both type 1 and type 2 diabetes. The analogue is also formulated for use in continuous subcutaneous insulin infusion (CSII) pumps, where it functions as the rapid‑acting insulin delivered by the device.

Insulin Aspart has been featured extensively in comparative clinical studies. It has been used as a reference or comparator insulin in trials evaluating fast‑acting insulin aspart formulations, inhaled insulin products, and Technosphere (inhaled) insulin. Additional investigations have examined its performance as a comparator in studies of hypoglycaemia rates when delivered via pen versus vial, as well as in broader assessments of rapid‑acting insulins such as Apidra®.

Overall, Insulin Aspart functions as the core rapid‑acting insulin in both Fiasp® and NovoRapid® formulations, offering a convenient, recombinant‑produced option for prandial insulin therapy while maintaining a pharmacodynamic profile that aligns closely with that of native human insulin and supporting a wide range of therapeutic and research applications.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b4f2935f492529f0d551140b53a84fe3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6e42637e4286cbc19cce4502b22634bd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f9e5c50e8a808c537075377966ae2ccd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6b14c2f0985ae4a417c8fc99e339bd9e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-29710f08f3e10bba4a464e8b4da1917c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2f4f01a72f35d6db3ff333e64f8400ce&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1bb9ea85b9ad8cd6940ae41a3ab5d1fd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-14772c7de5db762c492a75a1c744dae6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-88b97cde53943160602b20f634ba5c1f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6a7ca48868f79f7be782198d67ffefd0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d5bb996e52cb71f15bc8c30d1b1d321&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c8c7e36686d077dcb6239405f60ea031&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-68b98187c6ab15468f1c0d8f5e7f9f6a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ddb8954aaa1e1230598596ce6f5df249&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e5f5165b3185feb3c6ec93a3c0ef8d02&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-767d025776f0f59c05788e25616f412c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-42ddf181cf4422a3b24643a2252d99b0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9bcc4202330d45ebfca8f79c3d4998b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b4d7abd3e1e5418ee5a931e28a18e8ad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-277e136948d5572acf031988fd092dce&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-65cd86aee374fd1ea91bb4fd5ebee2a7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e7e6ca9bf63e843b814736c0409c70fb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f9416e8076c17175db0dbb12c3393566&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d30bfc1840eec64224c3568470e6c539&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a0e51dec97ab970bbc2f21878a8735ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5ed3ce00d7a52cdffe7b550ffe0dd568</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/NOVORAPID _ BulasMed.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_apidra.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_fiasp.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/Insulinoterapia – Diretriz da Sociedade Brasileira de Diabetes – Ed. 2024.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/cengiz-beck-2026-use-of-inhaled-insulin-with-automated-insulin-delivery-systems.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/edelman-et-al-2026-dosing-afrezza-it-s-not-that-complicated.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/blood glucose monitoring.pdf</data>
