<node id="Study NN1250‑3561">
  <data key="d0">Study NN1250‑3561</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Study NN1250‑3561 is a 26‑week multinational, multicentre, randomised, open parallel trial comparing the efficacy and safety of insulin degludec versus insulin detemir in children and adolescents with diabetes type 1, using a basal‑bolus regimen with insulin aspart as bolus.&lt;SEP&gt;Study NN1250‑3561 is a randomized controlled trial assessing Levemir®’s efficacy and safety in children with type 1 diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6e42637e4286cbc19cce4502b22634bd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-68b98187c6ab15468f1c0d8f5e7f9f6a</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/NOVORAPID _ BulasMed.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786317592</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Study NN5401‑3816">
  <data key="d0">Study NN5401‑3816</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">Study NN5401‑3816 is a safety and efficacy trial comparing once‑daily insulin degludec plus insulin aspart with twice‑daily insulin detemir plus insulin aspart in children and adolescents with diabetes type 1.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6e42637e4286cbc19cce4502b22634bd</data>
