<node id="Basal‑Bolus Regimen">
  <data key="d0">Basal‑Bolus Regimen</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Basal‑Bolus Regimen is an insulin therapy approach that integrates a long‑acting basal insulin with rapid‑acting prandial (bolus) insulin to achieve comprehensive glucose control. The basal component—commonly a slow‑acting insulin such as insulin detemir (Levemir®) or NPH insulin—provides a steady background level of insulin throughout the day and night. The bolus component consists of a rapid‑acting insulin, often insulin aspart, which is administered at mealtimes to cover the carbohydrate load and to correct post‑prandial glucose excursions.

The regimen is designed to mimic the physiological pattern of insulin secretion, matching basal insulin delivery to the body’s continuous metabolic needs while aligning bolus doses with meals and activity levels. It is employed across diverse patient groups, including children, pregnant women with Type 1 diabetes, and study participants in clinical trials evaluating insulin delivery strategies. By coordinating basal and bolus doses, the regimen seeks to maintain target blood glucose ranges, reduce the risk of hyperglycemia after meals, and minimize overall glycemic variability.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6e42637e4286cbc19cce4502b22634bd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9725072a361e9b1b97c5daa35e061e58&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0a20360c489112f7848983049bae7125&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2073bddd90c7dd8e156b67821f0f3247&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-767d025776f0f59c05788e25616f412c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0ace26fdb0244e3d0f714a007c9bbb51&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-42ddf181cf4422a3b24643a2252d99b0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c7e6ef38db0b62d161b13473af47d738</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/NOVORAPID _ BulasMed.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/TRESIBA _ BulasMed.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_fiasp.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/Documento sem título.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1786330486</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
