</node>
<node id="Cartridge">
  <data key="d0">Cartridge</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The cartridge is the internal component of NovoRapid® FlexPen® that does not contact medication and may be placed in recyclable waste after use.&lt;SEP&gt;Cartridge (carpule) is the replaceable container inside SoloStar that holds up to 300 units of insulin.&lt;SEP&gt;Cartridge is the internal container within the SoloStar that holds up to 300 units of insulin.&lt;SEP&gt;A cartridge is a sealed container holding a fixed volume of insulin detemir solution for use with the pen.&lt;SEP&gt;The cartridge is part of Novolin® R packaging that can be discarded in recyclable waste.&lt;SEP&gt;The cartridge contains Novolin® R insulin and does not contact the medication directly.&lt;SEP&gt;Cartridge is the internal component of the Novolin® R FlexPen® pen that holds the insulin solution and can be discarded after the pen is empty.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9725072a361e9b1b97c5daa35e061e58&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ffe095bda1b787c5b5ae2d61a2f74c98&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e9835d6684db67541402527b3182b6c5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ddb8954aaa1e1230598596ce6f5df249&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0955cb70a6ce135722726162a9811e78&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-df616353e032c899b02bfa4368bc2667&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2cd48799a027437b9fe2e1a48b61cb3d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/NOVORAPID _ BulasMed.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_apidra.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786318496</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Regular Human Insulin">
  <data key="d0">Regular Human Insulin</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Regular Human Insulin is the native, short‑acting insulin formulation that serves as the standard reference product in diabetes therapy and research. It is the traditional rapid‑onset insulin used for subcutaneous administration to control post‑prandial glucose, and it forms the short‑acting component of premixed human insulin preparations such as the 50/50 and 70/30 ratios. Because of its well‑characterized pharmacokinetic and pharmacodynamic profile, Regular Human Insulin is routinely employed as a comparator in clinical studies evaluating newer rapid‑acting insulin analogues, including insulin lispro, NovoRapid®, and the newer basal‑bolus agents APIDRA and APIDRA SOLOSTAR. In these investigations it provides a benchmark for potency, safety, and adverse‑event assessments.

In pediatric practice, Regular Human Insulin can be substituted for NovoRapid® in children older than one year, offering a familiar and widely available option for managing type 1 diabetes in this age group. Its role as the reference insulin underpins both regulatory evaluation and routine clinical decision‑making, ensuring consistent dosing comparisons across a broad range of insulin products and therapeutic regimens.&lt;SEP&gt;Regular human insulin is a short‑acting insulin analogue used as a reference in comparative studies.&lt;SEP&gt;Regular Human Insulin is a subcutaneous insulin formulation used as a comparator in pharmacokinetic studies.&lt;SEP&gt;Regular Human Insulin is a form of insulin to which some patients may be hypersensitive, contraindicating Afrezza.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9725072a361e9b1b97c5daa35e061e58&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6b14c2f0985ae4a417c8fc99e339bd9e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bf25fca295be60e28b7c7d3103f722fc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db832f06717859b8ba6cf7fd70aa22d8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8ef35bd45e4ba8d20f4e9181011ccfcd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c95471c4c993fa3a499f99443ee7c922&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-465ad8b77c1c2a2a179062da20337ff5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b4d7abd3e1e5418ee5a931e28a18e8ad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f9416e8076c17175db0dbb12c3393566&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-161a201d846100f42e643139469a1e6c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4e6371d8083fb20b137912cdaeec1b8b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/NOVORAPID _ BulasMed.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_1778357531609.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_apidra.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/Insulinoterapia – Diretriz da Sociedade Brasileira de Diabetes – Ed. 2024.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/cengiz-beck-2026-use-of-inhaled-insulin-with-automated-insulin-delivery-systems.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/edelman-et-al-2026-dosing-afrezza-it-s-not-that-complicated.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786333247</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Intermediate‑Action Insulin">
  <data key="d0">Intermediate‑Action Insulin</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Intermediate‑action insulin is a type of insulin used in basal‑bolus regimens together with NovoRapid® and typically administered once daily.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9725072a361e9b1b97c5daa35e061e58</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/NOVORAPID _ BulasMed.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786305900</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Long‑Acting Insulin">
  <data key="d0">Long‑Acting Insulin</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Long‑acting insulin is a basal insulin used together with NovoRapid® to provide prolonged glucose control.&lt;SEP&gt;Long‑acting insulin is a prolonged‑action insulin formulation needed alongside APIDRA SOLOSTAR to maintain adequate glucose control.&lt;SEP&gt;Long‑acting insulin is a class of insulin with prolonged duration, mentioned in the context of transferring to Levemir®.&lt;SEP&gt;Long‑Acting Insulin is an extended‑duration insulin used for basal coverage when delivered by injection.&lt;SEP&gt;Long‑acting insulin is a form of insulin that may be stored in the emergency kit.&lt;SEP&gt;Basal insulin (e.g., Glargina, Detemir) with no pronounced peak, lasting 20–24 hours.&lt;SEP&gt;Long‑acting insulin is an insulin category with onset several hours after injection and duration up to 24 hours or longer.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9725072a361e9b1b97c5daa35e061e58&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c95471c4c993fa3a499f99443ee7c922&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0ace26fdb0244e3d0f714a007c9bbb51&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-65c6beab51324e055f4a39b388e2eefe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-36ace822cd4873b8fd2adcfef0a7f9fd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c7e6ef38db0b62d161b13473af47d738&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0932e9c21a330869629b3fa70d2e1f5e</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/NOVORAPID _ BulasMed.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_apidra.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/Documento sem título.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/Understanding insulin - International Diabetes Federation.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786332449</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Adverse Reactions">
  <data key="d0">Adverse Reactions</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Adverse reactions observed with NovoRapid® include hypoglycemia, injection‑site pain, redness, itching, edema, bruising, and urticaria.&lt;SEP&gt;Adverse reactions are unintended harmful effects associated with Toujeo administration, referenced in the product label.&lt;SEP&gt;The heading “Reações adversas” introduces a section describing side effects.&lt;SEP&gt;Adverse reactions are dose‑dependent side effects observed in patients using Levemir®.&lt;SEP&gt;Adverse reactions are the unwanted effects associated with Novolin® R, categorized by frequency and system organ class.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9725072a361e9b1b97c5daa35e061e58&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1ee5400065df79b02b6c04efc0f4854d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fed8264ddac9525305e06a64be3eeb60&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-56fc1d5df1b34d9120c3cf8a760c40f9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-73559dc5d86ea52a348d603482e056e9</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/NOVORAPID _ BulasMed.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Toujeo.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_apidra.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786318527</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Dosage Guidance">
  <data key="d0">Dosage Guidance</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Dosage guidance for NovoRapid® recommends 0.5‑1.0 U/kg/day, representing 50‑70% of total daily insulin in basal‑bolus therapy and administration before meals.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9725072a361e9b1b97c5daa35e061e58</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/NOVORAPID _ BulasMed.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786305900</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Special Population">
  <data key="d0">Special Population</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Special populations such as elderly patients or those with renal or hepatic dysfunction require intensified glucose monitoring and individualized dose adjustments when using NovoRapid®.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9725072a361e9b1b97c5daa35e061e58</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/NOVORAPID _ BulasMed.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786305900</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Recyclable Waste">
  <data key="d0">Recyclable Waste</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Recyclable waste refers to material that can be processed for recycling, such as the cartridge of NovoRapid® FlexPen® after use.&lt;SEP&gt;Recyclable Waste is waste material that can be processed for recycling, used for discarding cartridges and leaflets.&lt;SEP&gt;Recyclable Waste refers to waste material such as cartons and plastics that can be placed in recycling bins, as mentioned for discarding the cartridge and the leaflet.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9725072a361e9b1b97c5daa35e061e58&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0955cb70a6ce135722726162a9811e78&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2cd48799a027437b9fe2e1a48b61cb3d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/NOVORAPID _ BulasMed.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786318500</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Lactação">
  <data key="d0">Lactação</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Lactação (breastfeeding) is the physiological condition of nursing infants, mentioned regarding medication safety.&lt;SEP&gt;Breastfeeding condition mentioned in the pregnancy and lactation section.&lt;SEP&gt;Lactação (lactation) is mentioned regarding unknown excretion of insulin detemir in breast milk and possible dose adjustments.&lt;SEP&gt;Lactação is the period of breastfeeding, during which insulin therapy is considered safe for the infant.&lt;SEP&gt;Lactação denotes breastfeeding, during which insulin treatment presents no risk to the infant.&lt;SEP&gt;Lactação (breastfeeding) allows continued insulin treatment without risk to the infant, though dose adjustments may be needed.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-048d8fafb712e12cec45f2d3ec2c1e3b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-45ee3dcb366c1301c9fb1d2ce9f323c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9bcc4202330d45ebfca8f79c3d4998b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4615ca664e7ff898d8c5929cbc79e7d8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d6101c469482b48e341b4095a54907fd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0851222a21a012cffce7a16710847208</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/NOVORAPID _ BulasMed.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786318512</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Gravidez">
  <data key="d0">Gravidez</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Gravidez, the Portuguese term for pregnancy, is the physiological condition of carrying a developing fetus. In the context of insulin therapy, gravidez is regarded as a medical condition in which insulin may be prescribed, but its use must be guided by a health‑care professional. The insulin dosage required during gravidez can vary considerably, necessitating careful adjustment and continuous monitoring to maintain appropriate glycaemic control.  

Regulatory information places insulin use in gravidez in risk category B, indicating that no definitive evidence of fetal risk has been found and that insulin is generally not restricted when prescribed under medical supervision. Specific insulin products have differing levels of study: no clinical trials have been conducted with Humalog Mix 25 KwikPen in pregnant patients, whereas Levemir® has been mentioned as an insulin that may be employed during gravidez when overseen by a qualified clinician. Overall, the guidance emphasizes that insulin therapy during gravidez should be individualized, closely supervised, and adjusted according to the evolving metabolic needs of the pregnancy.&lt;SEP&gt;Estado fisiológico que requer controle rigoroso da insulina em pacientes diabéticos.&lt;SEP&gt;Gravidez (pregnancy) is a physiological state that can cause inaccurate HbA1c results.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-048d8fafb712e12cec45f2d3ec2c1e3b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5b40c2fbad301807d9646f27d94635cb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a247846b9ec5d44d0bcbe6c5f15599f8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-45ee3dcb366c1301c9fb1d2ce9f323c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9bcc4202330d45ebfca8f79c3d4998b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4615ca664e7ff898d8c5929cbc79e7d8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d6101c469482b48e341b4095a54907fd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0851222a21a012cffce7a16710847208&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cbe87fd92ad66dcb02b25b669d829f6c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a79d0e4d0f656bd87d2d0c4657378db4</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/NOVORAPID _ BulasMed.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Basaglar.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_1778357531609.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/Documento sem título.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1786336914</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Beta Blockers">
  <data key="d0">Beta Blockers</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Beta Blockers are a class of drugs that can mask symptoms of hypoglycemia in patients using insulin.&lt;SEP&gt;Beta blockers are a class of cardiovascular drugs that may mask hypoglycemia symptoms.&lt;SEP&gt;Beta Blockers are a class of drugs that can both potentiate and weaken the hypoglycemic effect of insulin.&lt;SEP&gt;Beta‑adrenergic antagonists that can lower insulin requirements and may mask hypoglycemia.&lt;SEP&gt;Beta Blockers are a class of medications that can reduce insulin needs and mask hypoglycemia symptoms.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-048d8fafb712e12cec45f2d3ec2c1e3b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d65840dd2cbd5c9984dfc4334378df5e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-465ad8b77c1c2a2a179062da20337ff5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cedd8e88a8d35eade68ce02222b9e276&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3237e202569462c758ec3d878c9faeae</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/NOVORAPID _ BulasMed.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_apidra.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786317606</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="MAO Inhibitors">
  <data key="d0">MAO Inhibitors</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">MAO Inhibitors (monoamine oxidase inhibitors) are medications that may reduce a patient’s insulin requirements.&lt;SEP&gt;Monoamine oxidase inhibitors are antidepressants that can increase insulin‑induced hypoglycemia.&lt;SEP&gt;MAO inhibitors are drugs that intensify the insulin‑induced reduction of blood glucose.&lt;SEP&gt;Monoamine oxidase inhibitors that can lower insulin requirements.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-048d8fafb712e12cec45f2d3ec2c1e3b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d65840dd2cbd5c9984dfc4334378df5e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f09811b149a29105854a0b1e84951e5d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3237e202569462c758ec3d878c9faeae</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/NOVORAPID _ BulasMed.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_apidra.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786317643</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Anabolic Steroids">
  <data key="d0">Anabolic Steroids</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Anabolic Steroids are synthetic derivatives of testosterone that may reduce insulin requirements.&lt;SEP&gt;Anabolic steroids such as testosterone are listed as agents that may decrease blood‑glucose levels.&lt;SEP&gt;Anabolic steroids are substances that can lower the need for insulin.&lt;SEP&gt;Synthetic testosterone derivatives that can lower insulin requirements.&lt;SEP&gt;Anabolic steroids are compounds that can reduce the insulin requirements of Levemir®.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-048d8fafb712e12cec45f2d3ec2c1e3b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4704ea4d5c15ebc8c043a077f05fd7a3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6c32255a7f064c18ff0b079798cfeaf5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cedd8e88a8d35eade68ce02222b9e276&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3237e202569462c758ec3d878c9faeae</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/NOVORAPID _ BulasMed.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/TRESIBA _ BulasMed.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_fiasp.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786317607</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Sulfonamides">
  <data key="d0">Sulfonamides</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Sulfonamides are a group of antibiotics that can lower the needed insulin dosage.&lt;SEP&gt;Sulfonamides are antibiotics listed as drugs that can lower blood‑glucose levels.&lt;SEP&gt;Sulfonamides are drugs that can diminish insulin needs.&lt;SEP&gt;Antibiotic agents that can lower insulin requirements.&lt;SEP&gt;Sulfonamides are compounds that can reduce the insulin requirements of Levemir®.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-048d8fafb712e12cec45f2d3ec2c1e3b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4704ea4d5c15ebc8c043a077f05fd7a3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6c32255a7f064c18ff0b079798cfeaf5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cedd8e88a8d35eade68ce02222b9e276&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3237e202569462c758ec3d878c9faeae</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/NOVORAPID _ BulasMed.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/TRESIBA _ BulasMed.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_fiasp.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786317607</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Thiazides">
  <data key="d0">Thiazides</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Thiazides are a class of diuretic drugs that can raise insulin needs.&lt;SEP&gt;Thiazides are diuretics that can increase blood‑glucose or cause fluid retention.&lt;SEP&gt;Thiazides are diuretics that can raise insulin requirements.&lt;SEP&gt;Thiazide diuretics that can increase insulin requirements.&lt;SEP&gt;Thiazides are diuretics that can increase the insulin requirements of Levemir®.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-048d8fafb712e12cec45f2d3ec2c1e3b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4704ea4d5c15ebc8c043a077f05fd7a3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6c32255a7f064c18ff0b079798cfeaf5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cedd8e88a8d35eade68ce02222b9e276&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3237e202569462c758ec3d878c9faeae</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/NOVORAPID _ BulasMed.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/TRESIBA _ BulasMed.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_fiasp.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786317607</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Glucocorticoids">
  <data key="d0">Glucocorticoids</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Glucocorticoids are steroid hormones that may increase the amount of insulin required.&lt;SEP&gt;Glucocorticoids such as cortisone are anti‑inflammatory agents that can raise blood‑glucose.&lt;SEP&gt;Glucocorticoids are steroid hormones that can elevate insulin need.&lt;SEP&gt;Corticosteroid hormones that can increase insulin requirements.&lt;SEP&gt;Glucocorticoids are steroid hormones that can increase the insulin requirements of Levemir®.&lt;SEP&gt;Glucocorticoids are a class of steroid hormones whose inhaled pharmacodynamics and pharmacokinetics were reviewed.&lt;SEP&gt;Glucocorticoids are a class of medications known to increase the risk of diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-048d8fafb712e12cec45f2d3ec2c1e3b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4704ea4d5c15ebc8c043a077f05fd7a3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6c32255a7f064c18ff0b079798cfeaf5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cedd8e88a8d35eade68ce02222b9e276&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3237e202569462c758ec3d878c9faeae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6b95d32a33501b281cbbf40dd69ba1e5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-55e58732610596ce9a8f3145d34f75a7</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/NOVORAPID _ BulasMed.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/TRESIBA _ BulasMed.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_fiasp.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/Inhaling medicines_ delivering drugs to the body through the lungs _ Nature Reviews Drug Discovery.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377371</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Thyroid Hormones">
  <data key="d0">Thyroid Hormones</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Thyroid Hormones are a class of endogenous endocrine substances produced by the thyroid gland that play a central role in regulating basal metabolic rate, thermogenesis, and overall energy metabolism. In clinical practice they are also formulated as hormonal medications used to treat various thyroid disorders, and they are listed among standard drug categories for endocrine therapy.  

In addition to their metabolic actions, thyroid hormones influence carbohydrate homeostasis by attenuating the glucose‑lowering effect of insulin. They can raise blood‑glucose levels, diminish insulin‑mediated glucose reduction, and consequently increase the amount of exogenous insulin required to achieve glycaemic control. This effect is observed both physiologically and when thyroid hormones are administered therapeutically, underscoring their capacity to reduce the hypoglycaemic impact of insulin and augment insulin requirements.&lt;SEP&gt;Hormones regulating metabolism that can increase insulin requirements.&lt;SEP&gt;Thyroid hormones are hormones that can increase the insulin requirements of Levemir®.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-048d8fafb712e12cec45f2d3ec2c1e3b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4704ea4d5c15ebc8c043a077f05fd7a3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3db0edd23b6b502ccbbf62bfd601ce68&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d96761d60c65f05f1530bc19b144cf1b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d65840dd2cbd5c9984dfc4334378df5e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-465ad8b77c1c2a2a179062da20337ff5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f09811b149a29105854a0b1e84951e5d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6c32255a7f064c18ff0b079798cfeaf5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cedd8e88a8d35eade68ce02222b9e276&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3237e202569462c758ec3d878c9faeae</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/NOVORAPID _ BulasMed.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/TRESIBA _ BulasMed.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Basaglar.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_apidra.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_fiasp.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786317608</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Sympathomimetics">
  <data key="d0">Sympathomimetics</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Sympathomimetics are drugs that mimic sympathetic nervous system activity and may raise insulin needs.&lt;SEP&gt;Sympathomimetics like epinephrine, salbutamol, or terbutaline are bronchodilators that may increase blood‑glucose.&lt;SEP&gt;Sympathomimetic agents stimulate the sympathetic nervous system and can reduce insulin’s hypoglycemic effect.&lt;SEP&gt;Sympathomimetics are drugs that reduce the insulin‑induced reduction of blood glucose.&lt;SEP&gt;Sympathomimetics are agents that can increase insulin demand.&lt;SEP&gt;Agents that stimulate sympathetic activity and can increase insulin requirements.&lt;SEP&gt;Sympathomimetics are agents that can increase the insulin requirements of Levemir®.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-048d8fafb712e12cec45f2d3ec2c1e3b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4704ea4d5c15ebc8c043a077f05fd7a3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d65840dd2cbd5c9984dfc4334378df5e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f09811b149a29105854a0b1e84951e5d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6c32255a7f064c18ff0b079798cfeaf5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cedd8e88a8d35eade68ce02222b9e276&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3237e202569462c758ec3d878c9faeae</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/NOVORAPID _ BulasMed.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/TRESIBA _ BulasMed.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_apidra.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_fiasp.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786317609</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Growth Hormone">
  <data key="d0">Growth Hormone</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Growth Hormone is a peptide hormone that can increase the demand for insulin.&lt;SEP&gt;Growth hormone therapy is cited as a cause of increased blood‑glucose.&lt;SEP&gt;Growth hormone is a hormone that can raise insulin requirements.&lt;SEP&gt;An anabolic peptide that can increase insulin requirements.&lt;SEP&gt;Growth hormone is a hormone that can increase the insulin requirements of Levemir®.&lt;SEP&gt;Growth Hormone is a counter‑regulatory hormone that may increase during insulin deficiency.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-048d8fafb712e12cec45f2d3ec2c1e3b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4704ea4d5c15ebc8c043a077f05fd7a3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6c32255a7f064c18ff0b079798cfeaf5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cedd8e88a8d35eade68ce02222b9e276&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3237e202569462c758ec3d878c9faeae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fd6fa98b7767319460b4a421a719c5c2</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/NOVORAPID _ BulasMed.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/TRESIBA _ BulasMed.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_fiasp.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/Insulinoterapia – Diretriz da Sociedade Brasileira de Diabetes – Ed. 2024.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786331391</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Danazol">
  <data key="d0">Danazol</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Danazol is a synthetic steroid and androgenic drug that is primarily prescribed for the treatment of endometriosis.  Across multiple pharmacological reports, Danazol has been consistently noted to interfere with the action of insulin and insulin‑based therapies.  The compound can raise blood‑glucose levels, thereby increasing the amount of insulin required to achieve glycaemic control.  It diminishes the hypoglycaemic effect of various insulin formulations, including insulin glargine (Lantus) and insulin glulisine (Apidra Solostar), by reducing insulin‑induced glucose uptake and the overall glucose‑lowering response.  Consequently, patients receiving Danazol may experience a reduced efficacy of insulin therapy and may need adjustments to their insulin dosing to maintain target blood‑sugar levels.&lt;SEP&gt;Danazol is a medication that can increase the need for insulin.&lt;SEP&gt;A synthetic androgenic steroid that can increase insulin requirements.&lt;SEP&gt;Danazol is a medication that can increase the insulin requirements of Levemir®.&lt;SEP&gt;Danazol is a synthetic steroid medication that can raise insulin requirements.&lt;SEP&gt;Danazol is a synthetic steroid that can increase a patient’s insulin needs.&lt;SEP&gt;Danazol is a medication that can increase insulin requirements.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-048d8fafb712e12cec45f2d3ec2c1e3b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4704ea4d5c15ebc8c043a077f05fd7a3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3db0edd23b6b502ccbbf62bfd601ce68&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d96761d60c65f05f1530bc19b144cf1b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d99841fd6d1e1fbf23f184e202bc760e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e4ba52cc293c5c002b470566321026d6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d65840dd2cbd5c9984dfc4334378df5e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f09811b149a29105854a0b1e84951e5d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6c32255a7f064c18ff0b079798cfeaf5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cedd8e88a8d35eade68ce02222b9e276&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3237e202569462c758ec3d878c9faeae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4615ca664e7ff898d8c5929cbc79e7d8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d6101c469482b48e341b4095a54907fd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ba6b31518be6fff1db8b68a28e82f200</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/NOVORAPID _ BulasMed.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/TRESIBA _ BulasMed.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Basaglar.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Toujeo.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_apidra.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_fiasp.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786318520</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Octreotida">
  <data key="d0">Octreotida</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Octreotida is a medication that can either increase or decrease insulin needs in patients.&lt;SEP&gt;Octreotida is a medication that can both reduce and increase insulin requirements.&lt;SEP&gt;Octreotida is a peptide drug that may both decrease and increase insulin needs depending on context.&lt;SEP&gt;Octreotida is a medication that can both increase and decrease insulin needs.&lt;SEP&gt;Octreotida is a medication that can both reduce and increase a patient’s insulin requirements.&lt;SEP&gt;Octreotida is a peptide drug that may both reduce and increase insulin needs.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-048d8fafb712e12cec45f2d3ec2c1e3b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4615ca664e7ff898d8c5929cbc79e7d8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d6101c469482b48e341b4095a54907fd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-df616353e032c899b02bfa4368bc2667&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0851222a21a012cffce7a16710847208&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ba6b31518be6fff1db8b68a28e82f200</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/NOVORAPID _ BulasMed.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786318513</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Lanreotida">
  <data key="d0">Lanreotida</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Lanreotida is a medication capable of modulating insulin requirements upward or downward.&lt;SEP&gt;Lanreotida is a medication that can both reduce and increase insulin requirements.&lt;SEP&gt;Lanreotida is a long‑acting somatostatin analogue that can both lower and raise insulin requirements.&lt;SEP&gt;Lanreotida is a medication that can similarly raise or lower insulin requirements.&lt;SEP&gt;Lanreotida is a medication that can both reduce and increase a patient’s insulin requirements.&lt;SEP&gt;Lanreotida is a peptide analog that may both reduce and increase insulin requirements.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-048d8fafb712e12cec45f2d3ec2c1e3b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4615ca664e7ff898d8c5929cbc79e7d8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d6101c469482b48e341b4095a54907fd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-df616353e032c899b02bfa4368bc2667&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0851222a21a012cffce7a16710847208&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ba6b31518be6fff1db8b68a28e82f200</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/NOVORAPID _ BulasMed.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786318513</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Refrigerador">
  <data key="d0">Refrigerador</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Refrigerador is a cooling appliance used to store NovoRapid® at 2 °C to 8 °C before opening.&lt;SEP&gt;A refrigerator is recommended for storing unopened Levemir® FlexPen® at controlled cold temperatures.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-048d8fafb712e12cec45f2d3ec2c1e3b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a49c8461f43dc12d7df9c921efeb0465</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/NOVORAPID _ BulasMed.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786317647</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="NovoRapid FlexPen®">
  <data key="d0">NovoRapid FlexPen®</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">NovoRapid FlexPen® is a pre‑filled pen device that delivers NovoRapid® insulin in doses from 1 to 60 units.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-048d8fafb712e12cec45f2d3ec2c1e3b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/NOVORAPID _ BulasMed.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786305903</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="NovoFine®">
  <data key="d0">NovoFine®</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">NovoFine® is a registered trademark and brand owned by Novo Nordisk A/S that comprises disposable insulin‑delivery needles. These needles are designed for use with a range of Novo Nordisk injection devices, including the NovoRapid FlexPen® and the FlexTouch® insulin delivery system, as well as Levemir® FlexPen® and Levemir® Penfill® insulin pens. The product line also states compatibility with other Novo Nordisk injection systems, providing a versatile option for patients using the company’s various insulin therapies. The needles are available in lengths up to 8 mm, offering a compact and convenient solution for subcutaneous insulin administration.&lt;SEP&gt;NovoFine® are disposable insulin needles up to 8 mm in length intended for use with Novolin® R Penfill®.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-048d8fafb712e12cec45f2d3ec2c1e3b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-09d60e0b850d87c77dd67ca2d709912c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d5bb996e52cb71f15bc8c30d1b1d321&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-00cf434060561bb7d46b6ce50f095c91&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fdee4bcd64faa476dd057e21e2525e53&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cedd8e88a8d35eade68ce02222b9e276&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-922791f49d1bf928fe4f02ddd336927b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-831f4bbfc884fc8e9679630a819083e9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0b4034f7cf7e37425b7c76f5e0f9fd11</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/NOVORAPID _ BulasMed.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_fiasp.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786318536</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Bula">
  <data key="d0">Bula</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Bula is the official medication leaflet, also known as a package insert or product‑labeling document, that accompanies a range of insulin products and delivery devices. For each medication—such as NovoRapid®, Tresiba®, BASAGLAR KwikPen, Caneta SoloStar, and Fiasp (including the Fiasp FlexTouch)—the Bula supplies the full set of usage instructions, storage guidelines, dosage recommendations, indications, contraindications, safety warnings, and any required legal statements. It serves as the primary source of prescribing information for health‑care professionals and as a user guide for patients.

The Bula also functions as a regulatory artifact: its contents are recorded in a historical change log whenever updates are made, ensuring traceability of revisions. In Brazil, the Bula for a medication becomes legally binding once approved by the National Health Surveillance Agency (Anvisa), as exemplified by a Bula approved on 03 July 2023. Thus, the Bula integrates clinical guidance with compliance requirements, providing a standardized, authoritative reference for each insulin product it covers.&lt;SEP&gt;The bula (package insert) provides usage instructions for Novolin® R and can be discarded in recyclable waste.&lt;SEP&gt;The Bula is the professional package insert accompanying Novolin® R, containing detailed usage instructions.&lt;SEP&gt;Bula is the instruction leaflet that accompanies Novolin® R and provides detailed usage guidelines.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-048d8fafb712e12cec45f2d3ec2c1e3b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0a20360c489112f7848983049bae7125&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-22df77f7bf817d736d90608e62a11d84&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cc9821850f5a0f8be1e4dd3fd0df6fcf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9f2feff6017b7b438ef10a0741399f08&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ca91c7c60e1068f10c786e7ff7f21339&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fdeef3e06ffaa7cc0442c3d94917f0c4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bc2aa5d85d666eabc9dbaa5d2ecfe874&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-add4469fba80232b7c0742f24c0914c9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53644541333e5ca7f2785d80235d27e9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-73559dc5d86ea52a348d603482e056e9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-df616353e032c899b02bfa4368bc2667&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0689fd73d2061ee466b9b90e03bda141</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/NOVORAPID _ BulasMed.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/TRESIBA _ BulasMed.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Basaglar.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Toujeo.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_apidra.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_fiasp.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786318525</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Excessive Heat">
  <data key="d0">Excessive Heat</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Excessive Heat refers to high temperature conditions that can impair the efficacy of insulin formulations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-048d8fafb712e12cec45f2d3ec2c1e3b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/NOVORAPID _ BulasMed.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786305903</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Dose Range 1‑60 Units">
  <data key="d0">Dose Range 1‑60 Units</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Dose Range 1‑60 Units denotes the interval of insulin units (from one to sixty) that the NovoRapid FlexPen® can deliver.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-048d8fafb712e12cec45f2d3ec2c1e3b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/NOVORAPID _ BulasMed.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786305904</data>
