</node>
<node id="Protective Transport Packaging">
  <data key="d0">Protective Transport Packaging</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Protective Transport Packaging is a specially designed container that provides thermal protection, blocks direct light, and dampens vibration during shipment of insulin products.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-048d8fafb712e12cec45f2d3ec2c1e3b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/NOVORAPID _ BulasMed.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786305904</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cutaneous Amyloidosis">
  <data key="d0">Cutaneous Amyloidosis</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Cutaneous Amyloidosis is a dermatological disorder characterized by the localized deposition of amyloid protein within the skin, most frequently observed at sites where insulin or insulin analogues (such as APIDRA insulin glulisine and Fiasp® fast‑acting insulin aspart) are repeatedly injected. The condition is reported as an adverse skin reaction in post‑marketing safety data for these products and is considered a local adverse effect of insulin therapy, especially when injections are administered repeatedly in the same location without proper site rotation.

The pathogenesis is thought to involve chronic hyperglycemia combined with repeated mechanical trauma from the needle, leading to localized amyloid formation in the dermis and subcutaneous tissue. Clinically, cutaneous amyloidosis appears as palpable or visible lesions—often nodular, papular, or plaque‑like—at the injection site, and it may impair insulin absorption, potentially delaying the intended glucose‑lowering effect. The frequency of this reaction is not well established, and it is described in the literature as an “unknown frequency” skin tissue reaction observed after commercialization of insulin products.

Risk mitigation centers on educating patients and healthcare providers about the importance of regular injection‑site rotation, thorough inspection of injection areas, and prompt reporting of any skin changes. By rotating sites and monitoring the skin, the likelihood of developing cutaneous amyloidosis can be reduced, helping to maintain optimal insulin pharmacokinetics and skin health.&lt;SEP&gt;Cutaneous amyloidosis is a localized skin condition that should be avoided when selecting injection sites for Humulin R.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-048d8fafb712e12cec45f2d3ec2c1e3b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f9e5c50e8a808c537075377966ae2ccd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6d0f18c80f8de2dee960a03599d12052&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a2416b3e5e8ebc96cdb451a794fc78e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-51761473ea6fe17b9e098a6bf98636b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bc2aa5d85d666eabc9dbaa5d2ecfe874&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-14772c7de5db762c492a75a1c744dae6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7fdc648ec086061141581e27adde6fc4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c68e2c07786710dd5250c6610f52b14d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9a6f9e10c0d4af5fff0338eb861f9c86&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dd396c45bc09fb646d156b4e69d328e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0955cb70a6ce135722726162a9811e78&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-acaa1440ae268669e1894588bb9e37c2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-df616353e032c899b02bfa4368bc2667&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2cd48799a027437b9fe2e1a48b61cb3d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-577779892c0d463cd6bb1966b8a8ce2d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/NOVORAPID _ BulasMed.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_1778357531609.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_apidra.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_fiasp.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786319733</data>
