<node id="Acute Painful Neuropathy">
  <data key="d0">Acute Painful Neuropathy</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Acute painful neuropathy is a reversible nerve disorder that may appear with rapid improvement of glycemic control.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f9e5c50e8a808c537075377966ae2ccd</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/NOVORAPID _ BulasMed.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786305905</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Anaphylactic Reaction">
  <data key="d0">Anaphylactic Reaction</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Anaphylactic reaction is a severe, potentially life‑threatening hypersensitivity response classified as very rare.&lt;SEP&gt;Anaphylactic reaction is a severe, potentially fatal systemic allergic response to insulin.&lt;SEP&gt;Anaphylactic reactions are classified as very rare adverse events related to Levemir®.&lt;SEP&gt;Anaphylactic reaction is a very rare severe hypersensitivity response associated with Novolin® R.&lt;SEP&gt;Anaphylactic reaction is a very rare severe allergic response linked to insulin compounds.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f9e5c50e8a808c537075377966ae2ccd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-51761473ea6fe17b9e098a6bf98636b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0ace26fdb0244e3d0f714a007c9bbb51&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c68e2c07786710dd5250c6610f52b14d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-73559dc5d86ea52a348d603482e056e9</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/NOVORAPID _ BulasMed.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_apidra.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786318454</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="MedDRA">
  <data key="d0">MedDRA</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">MedDRA, the Medical Dictionary for Regulatory Activities, is a standardized classification system employed to organize and report adverse‑reaction information. It provides a hierarchical framework that categorizes adverse events by organ system and, where applicable, by frequency of occurrence. The dictionary is used across regulatory documentation, clinical tables, and product‑specific literature—including the labeling for medicines such as Levemir® and Novolin® R—to ensure consistent recording and communication of safety data. By applying MedDRA, regulators, sponsors, and health‑care professionals can uniformly capture, analyze, and exchange adverse‑reaction information, facilitating clearer assessment of drug safety across different regions and therapeutic areas.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f9e5c50e8a808c537075377966ae2ccd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d194d06ef99b3f8aa6b6542b7e93e762&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5c580ebfc111aa29796af1a6f15941c7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-831f4bbfc884fc8e9679630a819083e9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0ace26fdb0244e3d0f714a007c9bbb51&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8a68ba1e8cc1defda76cde0eff9592e6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3396320470ee682ec5cc4f70ab001ef4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-73559dc5d86ea52a348d603482e056e9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0b4034f7cf7e37425b7c76f5e0f9fd11</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/NOVORAPID _ BulasMed.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Basaglar.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786318521</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Immune System Disorders">
  <data key="d0">Immune System Disorders</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Immune system disorders category groups uncommon adverse events such as urticaria, skin eruptions, and erythema.&lt;SEP&gt;Immune system disorders is the category under which allergic reactions are listed in the adverse event tables.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f9e5c50e8a808c537075377966ae2ccd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5c580ebfc111aa29796af1a6f15941c7</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/NOVORAPID _ BulasMed.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Basaglar.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786310010</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Metabolism and Nutrition Disorders">
  <data key="d0">Metabolism and Nutrition Disorders</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Metabolism and nutrition disorders category lists very common adverse events such as hypoglycemia.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f9e5c50e8a808c537075377966ae2ccd</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/NOVORAPID _ BulasMed.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786305906</data>
