</node>
<node id="Anvisa">
  <data key="d0">Anvisa</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Anvisa (Agência Nacional de Vigilância Sanitária), officially the Brazilian National Health Surveillance Agency, is Brazil’s principal health regulatory authority. It is tasked with ensuring the safety, efficacy, and quality of medicines, medical devices, food products, and other health‑related goods, as well as supervising adverse‑event reporting and pharmacovigilance activities across the country.

A core element of Anvisa’s pharmacovigilance system is the publicly accessible Sistema VigiMed platform. VigiMed collects and disseminates reports of suspected adverse drug reactions, allowing health professionals, patients, and manufacturers to submit safety data that the agency analyzes to protect public health and to inform regulatory actions.

In its regulatory capacity, Anvisa evaluates and authorizes pharmaceutical products for the Brazilian market. Recent approvals include the insulin formulation TOUJEO 300 U/mL, the medication label for APIDRA issued on 3 July 2023, and the APIDRA SOLOSTAR product approved in July 2023. The agency also approved the Levemir® FlexPen® leaflet (and the corresponding Levemir® leaflet/Bula) on 9 December 2021, and it authorized the Novolin® R product, the Novolin® R Penfill® brochure, the professional label for Novolin® products, and the Novolin® R FlexPen® leaflet, all on 17 April 2026.

Through these combined functions—regulatory approval, label verification, and the operation of the VigiMed reporting system—Anvisa serves as the central institution safeguarding public health in Brazil.&lt;SEP&gt;Anvisa is Brazil’s National Health Surveillance Agency responsible for regulating health products and providing the adverse‑event reporting portal.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f9e5c50e8a808c537075377966ae2ccd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-22df77f7bf817d736d90608e62a11d84&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-072d97721eef045503ec1dce0363b58e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8ef35bd45e4ba8d20f4e9181011ccfcd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aca0b919135813e1d5b772face36989d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d7223c781e745e72311fccfcdd58583&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ca91c7c60e1068f10c786e7ff7f21339&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-51761473ea6fe17b9e098a6bf98636b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b79dcaf41f7f07eed90788ce9e50dddd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-04b345bc26ec7f5d7c9db8c6004a50a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0e7689ca0fc736d9eae94256f73fed52&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fdee4bcd64faa476dd057e21e2525e53&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-922791f49d1bf928fe4f02ddd336927b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-831f4bbfc884fc8e9679630a819083e9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d01ed6a801b11c1b53f4668059c1f9cb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7f2714936869e55e840f5294caefeaee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-786395f3716fb61a79fd183c63e1a9d6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a7ca732691e1cbcafd65e378b8d80144&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8ac99e7359716e2cecc2ec93159218b6</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/NOVORAPID _ BulasMed.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Basaglar.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_1778357531609.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Toujeo.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_apidra.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786319740</data>
