<node id="Insulin Human Regular">
  <data key="d0">Insulin Human Regular</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Insulin Human Regular is a formulation of regular human insulin used as a comparator in clinical studies of type 1 diabetes.&lt;SEP&gt;Insulin Human Regular is regular human insulin used as an active comparator, administered subcutaneously 30 minutes before meals.&lt;SEP&gt;Regular human insulin administered before meals in the pediatric type 1 diabetes study.&lt;SEP&gt;Short‑acting regular insulin used in the treatment arms reported in Table 4.&lt;SEP&gt;Insulin human regular is a short‑acting insulin administered before meals in the pediatric type 1 diabetes study.&lt;SEP&gt;Insulin human regular is a short‑acting insulin used as a comparator to APIDRA in the adult Type 2 diabetes trial.&lt;SEP&gt;Insulin Human Regular is the standard human insulin referenced for potency comparison with Apidra Solostar.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ecd2466ef4258dade38fbadd495188e5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fe094dd3d94334373a8497a7cb841e0f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c078e8c2861146fb455f1dc3d4af2456&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3ce5998d1ff6a67e2e549405b16f744f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-91f290894e2d3b4216cac1721f22bb67&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b18f8ab53481bf1b63fda1bb71fe80ec&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2dc2313c92b2af4132faaa4d41449eef</data>
