</node>
<node id="Operating Machines">
  <data key="d0">Operating Machines</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Operating Machines refers to using machinery, an activity that can be compromised by low blood glucose.&lt;SEP&gt;Operating machines refers to the use of equipment or machinery, a task that can be unsafe during hypoglycemia.&lt;SEP&gt;Operating machines refers to using equipment such as industrial or household machinery, which can be impaired by hypo‑ or hyperglycemia.&lt;SEP&gt;Operating machines denotes the use of equipment or machinery, which can be hazardous if hypoglycemia occurs.&lt;SEP&gt;Operating machines denotes the use of equipment or machinery, which may be hazardous when hypoglycemic.&lt;SEP&gt;Operating Machines refers to the use of equipment or machinery, which may be unsafe during hypoglycemia.&lt;SEP&gt;Operating machines refers to the use of equipment whose safe performance may be compromised by hypoglycemia in Humulin R patients.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6d0f18c80f8de2dee960a03599d12052&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fd94288932ad6675a1de2b46b3fd9128&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f09811b149a29105854a0b1e84951e5d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cedd8e88a8d35eade68ce02222b9e276&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3237e202569462c758ec3d878c9faeae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0fa819f7e1e42eb688d4894dc3ca7e64&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-577779892c0d463cd6bb1966b8a8ce2d</data>
