<node id="Insulin Degludeca">
  <data key="d0">Insulin Degludeca</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Insulin Degludeca is a basal insulin combined with NovoRapid® in bolus‑basal therapy studies.&lt;SEP&gt;Insulin degludeca is the active, ultra‑long‑acting insulin ingredient of Tresiba®, produced by recombinant DNA technology.&lt;SEP&gt;Insulin degludeca is the active ingredient of Tresiba, providing a linear and stable glucose‑lowering effect for more than 24 hours.&lt;SEP&gt;Insulin degludeca is a basal‑bolus insulin formulation for which there is no clinical experience in children and adolescents up to 18 years with type 2 diabetes.&lt;SEP&gt;Insulin degludeca is a basal insulin analogue combined with rapid‑acting insulins in the pediatric study.&lt;SEP&gt;Insulin Degludeca is a long‑acting insulin used in combination with Fiasp® in pediatric patient data.&lt;SEP&gt;Insulin Degludeca is a basal insulin compared with Levemir® in a hypoglycemia study.</data>
