  <data key="d2">Breastfeeding is noted as a situation that may require insulin dose modification.&lt;SEP&gt;Breastfeeding is the lactation period during which Fiasp® use imposes no restrictions and does not endanger the infant.&lt;SEP&gt;Breastfeeding is the act of feeding an infant with human milk, noted as compatible with the use of Fiasp®.&lt;SEP&gt;Breastfeeding is the period of lactation during which medication use requires dose adjustments and medical supervision.</data>
