  <data key="d5">1786306296</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Maximum Single Dose 80 Units">
  <data key="d0">Maximum Single Dose 80 Units</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Maximum Single Dose 80 Units describes the highest amount of Tresiba® that can be administered in one injection.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e590341aac73dca916e560c2df9e60e0</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/TRESIBA _ BulasMed.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786306296</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Dose Increment 1 Unit">
  <data key="d0">Dose Increment 1 Unit</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Dose Increment 1 Unit defines the smallest adjustable dosing step for Tresiba® injections.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e590341aac73dca916e560c2df9e60e0</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/TRESIBA _ BulasMed.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786306296</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Price 211.67 Brazilian Real">
  <data key="d0">Price 211.67 Brazilian Real</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Price 211.67 Brazilian Real is the listed cost of Tresiba® in São Paulo, SP.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e590341aac73dca916e560c2df9e60e0</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/TRESIBA _ BulasMed.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786306297</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="High Blood Sugar">
  <data key="d0">High Blood Sugar</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">High Blood Sugar denotes a very elevated level of glucose in the blood, associated with symptoms like skin redness, dry mouth, and fruity‑smelling breath.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2943becc796c8ce3f0aaedf0978c3213</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/TRESIBA _ BulasMed.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786306297</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cetoacidosis">
  <data key="d0">Cetoacidosis</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Cetoacidosis is a severe condition marked by acid accumulation in the blood due to fat metabolism when blood sugar is very high.&lt;SEP&gt;Cetoacidosis is a severe metabolic condition that can result from prolonged hyperglycemia.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2943becc796c8ce3f0aaedf0978c3213&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-817893fc39ccf7551d476cefaf7f32ca</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/TRESIBA _ BulasMed.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786324187</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Diabetic Coma">
  <data key="d0">Diabetic Coma</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Diabetic Coma is a life‑threatening state that can result from untreated cetoacidosis.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2943becc796c8ce3f0aaedf0978c3213</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/TRESIBA _ BulasMed.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786306297</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Novo Nordisk Farmacêutica Do Brasil Ltda.">
  <data key="d0">Novo Nordisk Farmacêutica Do Brasil Ltda.</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Novo Nordisk Farmacêutica Do Brasil Ltda. is the Brazilian importer of Tresiba.&lt;SEP&gt;Novo Nordisk Farmacêutica do Brasil Ltda. is the pharmaceutical company listed on the label of Novolin® R.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2943becc796c8ce3f0aaedf0978c3213&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-93f7f04b0529d6f0ace11829cc4fa3b4</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/TRESIBA _ BulasMed.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786318549</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Araucária/PR">
  <data key="d0">Araucária/PR</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">Araucária/PR is the Brazilian city where the importer’s address is located.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2943becc796c8ce3f0aaedf0978c3213</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/TRESIBA _ BulasMed.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786306298</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="0800 144488">
  <data key="d0">0800 144488</data>
  <data key="d1">other</data>
  <data key="d2">0800 144488 is a customer‑service line for inquiries about Tresiba.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2943becc796c8ce3f0aaedf0978c3213</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/TRESIBA _ BulasMed.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786306298</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Reduced Physical Activity">
  <data key="d0">Reduced Physical Activity</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Reduced physical activity (exercising less) is noted as a behavior that can increase blood sugar.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2943becc796c8ce3f0aaedf0978c3213</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/TRESIBA _ BulasMed.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786306298</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Increased Food Intake">
  <data key="d0">Increased Food Intake</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Eating more than usual is identified as a cause of higher blood glucose.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2943becc796c8ce3f0aaedf0978c3213</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/TRESIBA _ BulasMed.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786306298</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Skin Redness">
  <data key="d0">Skin Redness</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Skin redness is a symptom that may appear gradually with very high blood sugar.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2943becc796c8ce3f0aaedf0978c3213</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/TRESIBA _ BulasMed.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786306298</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Dry Skin">
  <data key="d0">Dry Skin</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Dry skin is listed as a warning sign of extremely high blood glucose.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2943becc796c8ce3f0aaedf0978c3213</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/TRESIBA _ BulasMed.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786306299</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Sleepiness">
  <data key="d0">Sleepiness</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Sleepiness is described as a possible early indication of high blood sugar.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2943becc796c8ce3f0aaedf0978c3213</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/TRESIBA _ BulasMed.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786306299</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Fatigue">
  <data key="d0">Fatigue</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Fatigue is mentioned as a gradual symptom of very high blood glucose.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2943becc796c8ce3f0aaedf0978c3213</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/TRESIBA _ BulasMed.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786306299</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Dry Mouth">
  <data key="d0">Dry Mouth</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Dry mouth is included among the alert signs of elevated blood sugar.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2943becc796c8ce3f0aaedf0978c3213</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/TRESIBA _ BulasMed.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786306299</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Fruity Breath">
  <data key="d0">Fruity Breath</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Fruity‑smelling breath (ketone breath) is a symptom associated with severe hyperglycemia.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2943becc796c8ce3f0aaedf0978c3213</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/TRESIBA _ BulasMed.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786306299</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Frequent Urination">
  <data key="d0">Frequent Urination</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Increased frequency of urination is noted as a sign of very high blood sugar.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2943becc796c8ce3f0aaedf0978c3213</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/TRESIBA _ BulasMed.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786306299</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Thirst">
  <data key="d0">Thirst</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Excessive thirst is a common symptom of elevated blood glucose levels.&lt;SEP&gt;Thirst is the sensation of needing water, mentioned in relation to water metabolism.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2943becc796c8ce3f0aaedf0978c3213&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-172719b5694ed1fb8003b6874395d641</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/TRESIBA _ BulasMed.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/The Discovery and Development.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786332073</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Loss of Appetite">
  <data key="d0">Loss of Appetite</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Loss of appetite is reported as a possible manifestation of severe hyperglycemia.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2943becc796c8ce3f0aaedf0978c3213</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/TRESIBA _ BulasMed.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786306300</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Blood Sugar Test">
  <data key="d0">Blood Sugar Test</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A blood sugar test is a diagnostic method to measure glucose concentration in the blood.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2943becc796c8ce3f0aaedf0978c3213</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/TRESIBA _ BulasMed.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786306300</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Reação Alérgica Grave">
  <data key="d0">Reação Alérgica Grave</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Reação Alérgica Grave is a potentially life‑threatening allergic reaction that may be triggered by Tresiba.&lt;SEP&gt;Reação Alérgica Grave is a life‑threatening allergic response that can include spreading skin reactions, vomiting, breathing difficulty, rapid heartbeat, and dizziness.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c032d0271c85fd24982516368a62b1a9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-11cce86325de9748e794648198242578</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/TRESIBA _ BulasMed.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786306301</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Urticária">
  <data key="d0">Urticária</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Urticária is a skin reaction characterized by hives that may occur as an allergic side effect of Tresiba®.&lt;SEP&gt;Urticária is a hives skin reaction recorded as an allergic adverse event for Fiasp®.&lt;SEP&gt;Urticária is a hive‑like skin reaction that can occur at the Levemir® injection site.&lt;SEP&gt;Urticária is an hives‑type allergic skin reaction observed after insulin injections.&lt;SEP&gt;Urticária is hives, listed as an uncommon immune‑system disorder.&lt;SEP&gt;Urticária is a skin reaction classified as an uncommon immune‑system disorder linked to Novolin® R Penfill®.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c032d0271c85fd24982516368a62b1a9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7fdc648ec086061141581e27adde6fc4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8a68ba1e8cc1defda76cde0eff9592e6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3396320470ee682ec5cc4f70ab001ef4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d6101c469482b48e341b4095a54907fd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0b4034f7cf7e37425b7c76f5e0f9fd11</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/TRESIBA _ BulasMed.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_fiasp.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786318504</data>
