<node id="Insulina Basal">
  <data key="d0">Insulina Basal</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Insulina Basal is the term used for long‑acting, background insulin that provides continuous “basal” glucose control in people with diabetes.  It mimics the pancreas’s normal low‑level secretion, supplying a steady supply of insulin between meals and overnight to prevent hyperglycaemia when rapid‑acting insulin is not being administered.  In clinical practice Insulina Basal is regarded as the background insulin dose that must be balanced with prandial (meal‑time) rapid‑acting insulin to achieve stable day‑and‑night glucose levels.

Insulina Basal can be delivered in two principal ways.  Most injection regimens use a once‑daily subcutaneous dose of a long‑acting formulation; common pharmaceutical products in this class include Tresiba® (insulin degludec), insulin glargine (often called “insulina glargina”), and Levemir® (insulin detemir).  All of these analogues are designed to produce a prolonged, flat insulin effect.  Alternatively, the same basal insulin can be administered continuously by the basal channel of an insulin pump, where it is infused in very small, steady amounts to maintain baseline glucose homeostasis.

Regardless of the delivery method, the essential function of Insulina Basal is to provide the background insulin needed continuously to maintain baseline glucose levels, thereby supporting overall energy metabolism and reducing the risk of both hyperglycaemia and ketosis.  Its role is therefore central to the overall insulin regimen, serving as the steady foundational layer upon which rapid‑acting, mealtime insulin doses are added.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c032d0271c85fd24982516368a62b1a9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-56fb3d61e8c32af5d6b8be06cc54f904&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2479751a6475c09415f0d79759db091d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-00cf434060561bb7d46b6ce50f095c91&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a49c8461f43dc12d7df9c921efeb0465&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1312783ffe5039c618a48f7f29ec51ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d41e93e7754b06eedcc2e2a44afcb32&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9688a6d3c7f751ad34af5a1cde24fa2a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-63f6eb3be969569b166fc1e5f7e7567f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b4cf85d0e1e129080fae6f9bea5bd77f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-34da912924aa29d035c8cd1c3f4f6ae3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b56965a1473183cf6e1086bfecabe348&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c1a77062463b62317e84265a3b2b6d4a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dc1b97c88d050500f2b90b8837bd34bd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2e303ffa37ca96974ad7399e052659bb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-60530d1861f7c2d1efecc069c0913d37&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dfa23fc15cc4d520a32488843dbd710b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/TRESIBA _ BulasMed.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Toujeo.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_apidra.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786330167</data>
