<node id="Cetoacidose">
  <data key="d0">Cetoacidose</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Cetoacidose is a medical emergency of severe hyperglycemia with ketone accumulation that can result from stopping Tresiba abruptly.&lt;SEP&gt;Ketoacidosis, a metabolic complication mentioned alongside hyperglycemia in SICI failures.&lt;SEP&gt;Cetoacidose is ketoacidosis that may be present at diagnosis of DM2.&lt;SEP&gt;Cetoacidose is a metabolic complication of diabetes characterized by high ketone levels.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-11cce86325de9748e794648198242578&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-336a2f2c9b510e23c35be95e2ff7a72a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2e6267110f4ae5f4df4c49c0653a09b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fee32f1fb0c848b0799071a86119b142</data>
