<node id="Visual Impairment">
  <data key="d0">Visual Impairment</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Visual Impairment describes reduced eyesight conditions that require additional label‑checking precautions when using Tresiba.&lt;SEP&gt;Condition of total or partial loss of vision referenced as a contraindication for using the BASAGLAR KwikPen.&lt;SEP&gt;Visual impairment describes patients who lack sufficient sight to read the insulin pen dose counter and thus need assistance.&lt;SEP&gt;Visual impairment denotes patients with poor vision who need assistance to use an insulin pen.&lt;SEP&gt;Visual impairment describes limited or absent vision, for which patients are advised to obtain assistance when administering insulin.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0a20360c489112f7848983049bae7125&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cc9821850f5a0f8be1e4dd3fd0df6fcf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3397508bdfddde019cb1dfdcfb352435&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-93623071acdcd0ba060c8826ab5a2a81&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d10a1f849386df540104c79e33a7b242</data>
