<node id="Origin">
  <data key="d0">Origin</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">Origin is a clinical trial that compared Lantus® with Standard Treatment over an average of 6.2 years, evaluating cardiovascular events, all‑cause mortality, cancer, and diabetes incidence.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c41538e94f00eba70740ff188bcb6a94</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Basaglar.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786309950</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Standard Treatment">
  <data key="d0">Standard Treatment</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Standard Treatment refers to the usual glucose‑lowering therapy used as the control arm in the Origin study.&lt;SEP&gt;Standard Treatment refers to the comparator regimen used in Study ORIGIN against which TOUJEO 300 U/mL was evaluated.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c41538e94f00eba70740ff188bcb6a94&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-76df79998cbb923bc6c94e375c220eac</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Basaglar.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Toujeo.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786313658</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="All‑Cause Mortality">
  <data key="d0">All‑Cause Mortality</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">All‑Cause Mortality is an outcome measuring death from any cause, reported as a secondary endpoint in the Origin trial.&lt;SEP&gt;Overall death rate found to be similar between the insulin glargine and standard therapy groups.&lt;SEP&gt;All‑cause mortality is death from any cause, reported as increased in the ACCORD intensive arm and reduced in other analyses.&lt;SEP&gt;All‑cause mortality is death from any cause, used as an outcome measure in studies.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c41538e94f00eba70740ff188bcb6a94&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-863286c185f2a62e5b28d7e4577a1088&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4f9624abde6cf128707fcc0466a4c9a7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f99d05e1089d59496d56d86ff40197cc</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Basaglar.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Toujeo.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Metas glicêmicas/Metas no tratamento.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Metas glicêmicas/metas cuidado do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786372144</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Composite Microvascular Outcome">
  <data key="d0">Composite Microvascular Outcome</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Composite Microvascular Outcome is a secondary endpoint that includes laser photocoagulation, vitrectomy, diabetic‑retinopathy blindness, progressive albuminuria, serum creatinine doubling, or need for renal transplant.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c41538e94f00eba70740ff188bcb6a94</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Basaglar.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786309950</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Type 2 Diabetes Development">
  <data key="d0">Type 2 Diabetes Development</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Type 2 Diabetes Development denotes participants who progressed to diabetes during the study, assessed as a secondary outcome.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c41538e94f00eba70740ff188bcb6a94</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Basaglar.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786309950</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Primary Outcomes">
  <data key="d0">Primary Outcomes</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Primary Outcomes are the main efficacy endpoints of the Origin trial, comprising cardiovascular death, non‑fatal myocardial infarction, non‑fatal stroke, heart‑failure hospitalization, or revascularization.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c41538e94f00eba70740ff188bcb6a94</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Basaglar.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786309950</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Secondary Outcomes">
  <data key="d0">Secondary Outcomes</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Secondary Outcomes are additional efficacy endpoints in the Origin trial, including all‑cause mortality, composite microvascular outcome, and type 2 diabetes development.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c41538e94f00eba70740ff188bcb6a94</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Basaglar.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786309950</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Oral Glucose Tolerance Test">
  <data key="d0">Oral Glucose Tolerance Test</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Oral Glucose Tolerance Test (OGTT) is a diagnostic procedure that evaluates glucose metabolism by measuring blood or plasma glucose concentrations after a standardized oral glucose load. The test typically involves the ingestion of a 75‑gram glucose solution, although variations such as a mixed‑diet challenge are also described, and glucose levels are measured at baseline and at specified intervals, most commonly two hours after ingestion. The resulting post‑challenge glucose values are used to assess the body’s ability to handle a glucose load.

The OGTT is employed to diagnose and classify diabetes mellitus, prediabetes, and gestational diabetes mellitus (GDM). In the context of diabetes screening, the two‑hour plasma glucose measurement after the 75‑g load forms part of the criteria for prediabetes and aligns with International Association of the Diabetes and Pregnancy Study Groups (IADPSG) thresholds for GDM. Omission of the OGTT in high‑risk adult populations has been shown to lead to underdiagnosis of (pre)diabetes, highlighting its importance in comprehensive metabolic assessment.

In research settings, the OGTT may be administered at the conclusion of a study to determine the incidence of diabetes among participants, providing a standardized endpoint for epidemiologic investigations. Overall, the test serves as a cornerstone for evaluating glucose tolerance, guiding clinical decision‑making, and informing public health strategies related to diabetes detection and prevention.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c41538e94f00eba70740ff188bcb6a94&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8393954b021d0ad02018d1a449e0cc93&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ec7e786a85b1b6e6cc75bcfc9189fd27&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aff91698679a52cd7b07563b7b2627a3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-44888abd4ca8a1953f751ed6c41922e6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-525031caa389d084bc170433212cdca8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-72a2488e8176f7676c76504e76dd6c04&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-59dd4faf2a2706d073fdb93e1a29da81&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6601fea85bfbb9f20040c70b7e21695d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2a430bf53157529ccb22e67171fb28e5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3a15ed0aa8749d4f76e8d725e8752873&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c14456299df06b01b603504def87f381&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1a111d4b40ec241cf54126f594a80308&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a22fadf52eaea018160e4dd41d1d39b8</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Basaglar.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Diagnóstico de diabetes mellitus.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Metas glicêmicas/metas cuidado do diabetes.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377243</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Escherichia coli K12">
  <data key="d0">Escherichia coli K12</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Escherichia coli K12 is a non‑pathogenic laboratory bacterial strain employed as the production organism for recombinant DNA technology.&lt;SEP&gt;Escherichia coli K12 is the bacterial strain used to produce recombinant insulin glargine.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c41538e94f00eba70740ff188bcb6a94&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-42b9c5d97c54f39fb69bb1169e1de4d2</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Basaglar.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Toujeo.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786313572</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cancer">
  <data key="d0">Cancer</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Cancer refers to any malignant neoplasm; the trial reported no significant difference in overall cancer incidence between treatment groups.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c41538e94f00eba70740ff188bcb6a94</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Basaglar.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786309951</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cardiovascular Events">
  <data key="d0">Cardiovascular Events</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Cardiovascular Events include cardiovascular death, myocardial infarction, stroke, heart‑failure hospitalization, or revascularization, evaluated as primary outcomes in the Origin trial.&lt;SEP&gt;Cardiovascular Events are heart‑related clinical outcomes such as heart attacks or strokes.&lt;SEP&gt;Cardiovascular outcomes evaluated in meta‑analysis.&lt;SEP&gt;Cardiovascular events are major health outcomes (e.g., heart disease, stroke) examined as endpoints in the diabetes trials.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c41538e94f00eba70740ff188bcb6a94&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a5f7cad1fb0e1a0a02f63b5928b8acd2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d0cc9dbb0b2eb4685ac17cfe445b7ce7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-38ab5af7e42588297df4330ffb2c046b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Basaglar.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/glicemias capilares.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Metas glicêmicas/Metas no tratamento.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Metas glicêmicas/metas cuidado do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786372160</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Myocardial Infarction">
  <data key="d0">Myocardial Infarction</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Myocardial Infarction (MI) is a non‑fatal cardiovascular event evaluated as part of the primary outcomes in the Origin trial.&lt;SEP&gt;Myocardial infarction is a cardiac event that can trigger diabetic ketoacidosis in type 2 diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c41538e94f00eba70740ff188bcb6a94&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1a111d4b40ec241cf54126f594a80308</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Basaglar.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377426</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Lantus®">
  <data key="d0">Lantus®</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Lantus® is the brand name of insulin glargine, a long‑acting recombinant human insulin analog that serves as a basal insulin. It is supplied as a 100 U/mL formulation and is administered once daily, most commonly at bedtime, although flexible dosing times have also been examined. Lantus® is indicated for the treatment of both type 1 and type 2 diabetes and may be used in combination with oral antidiabetic agents.

In clinical development, Lantus® has been employed as the reference or active comparator in a variety of studies. It is the standard insulin glargine product used in biosimilarity trials with BASAGLAR® (including BASAGLAR KwikPen), where it has been shown to be equipotent when given at equal unit doses on a 1:1 conversion basis. The drug has also served as the comparator in pharmacokinetic and pharmacodynamic investigations, as well as in Phase III trials that evaluated its glycemic efficacy against human NPH insulin. These trials reported comparable glucose‑lowering effects and a lower incidence of nighttime hypoglycemia for Lantus®.

Safety data from the studies consistently note hypoglycemia as a frequent adverse reaction associated with Lantus®. Adverse‑reaction information has been collected alongside the comparator data in the same clinical programs. Overall, Lantus® is recognized as a well‑characterized, long‑acting basal insulin that provides reliable glycemic control and serves as the benchmark insulin glargine product in numerous comparative and biosimilarity studies.&lt;SEP&gt;Lantus® is a brand name for insulin glargine injected once daily, compared with Toujeo 300 Units/mL in clinical studies.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c41538e94f00eba70740ff188bcb6a94&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-89eaf7a8bcccf1ef8657b22ee03b5dd9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-afc9722167670b0bfeef0b43f4b0df79&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9e62226007200589cb2143f0fb75b302&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-22df77f7bf817d736d90608e62a11d84&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-da44554b006e6bd1b841f4246a054669&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c078e8c2861146fb455f1dc3d4af2456&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d194d06ef99b3f8aa6b6542b7e93e762&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-072d97721eef045503ec1dce0363b58e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5c580ebfc111aa29796af1a6f15941c7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-02780a8bc1d372cc47e0ccf2eaab1a99&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a72472938feb27131681a1591081e8c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b916f29e047f8579110cf5da3fd73847&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f14ce019f10c2a88765380143498ba5b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d87cbe9886e7203b6e7b26c85d60cb9d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d648fb4d9a20040dd617a7ca164c9f10&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-87576da8269707f5f8d929b71470e023&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7a592aedb257bad9532268b4056ec15c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3a279eef99c9c70338c74ffc7b4e260e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-09cd61106182a6d47854a32a39b66057&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4d0ac8ad5968d54922b924fdb16b61d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3ce5998d1ff6a67e2e549405b16f744f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2db4ee43ed7cc39546184320e1328d06&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-133169995b3ab942fd96f1fdfe7269ad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-91f290894e2d3b4216cac1721f22bb67&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3e50c145614f04be2319a31b74b80411&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-42b9c5d97c54f39fb69bb1169e1de4d2</data>
