  <data key="d2">Hazard Ratio is the statistical measure expressing relative risk between treatment groups for each clinical outcome.&lt;SEP&gt;Hazard Ratio is a statistical measure reported for primary and secondary outcomes in the ORIGIN trial.&lt;SEP&gt;Hazard Ratio is a statistical measure reported for primary and secondary endpoints in the Origin trial.&lt;SEP&gt;Hazard ratio (HR) is a statistical measure used to express risk reductions, e.g., HR 0.86 for microvascular events.</data>
