<node id="Impaired Fasting Glucose (IFG)">
  <data key="d0">Impaired Fasting Glucose (IFG)</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Impaired Fasting Glucose (IFG) identifies participants with pre‑diabetes at baseline, referenced in the study.&lt;SEP&gt;A pre‑diabetic condition characterized by elevated fasting glucose.&lt;SEP&gt;Impaired Fasting Glucose (IFG) is a condition of elevated fasting plasma glucose used in diabetes staging and prediabetes assessment.&lt;SEP&gt;Fasting plasma glucose 100–125 mg/dL (WHO defines lower limit 110 mg/dL) used as a prediabetes marker.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c41538e94f00eba70740ff188bcb6a94&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ca8741dfdb9ff0f12f049953db6cb9c0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3cc61bc2e95346d553972b4371912e7f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ba38023866c2db7437e618a60033f21f</data>
