  <data key="d5">1786377328</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Impaired Glucose Tolerance (IGT)">
  <data key="d0">Impaired Glucose Tolerance (IGT)</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Impaired Glucose Tolerance (IGT) denotes baseline pre‑diabetic status used to stratify participants.&lt;SEP&gt;A pre‑diabetic state where glucose tolerance is reduced, targeted for primary prevention of type 2 diabetes.&lt;SEP&gt;Impaired Glucose Tolerance (IGT) is a condition of abnormal glucose regulation used in diabetes staging and prediabetes assessment.&lt;SEP&gt;2‑hour plasma glucose 140–199 mg/dL during a 75‑g OGTT, used as a prediabetes marker.&lt;SEP&gt;Impaired Glucose Tolerance (IGT) is a milder abnormality of glucose metabolism that occurs earlier than CFRD.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c41538e94f00eba70740ff188bcb6a94&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ca8741dfdb9ff0f12f049953db6cb9c0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9cdf6af658e42c2f4f7dca5e4dbdd3db&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3cc61bc2e95346d553972b4371912e7f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ba38023866c2db7437e618a60033f21f</data>
