<node id="Retinopatia Diabética">
  <data key="d0">Retinopatia Diabética</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Retinopatia Diabética is a diabetes‑related eye disease, more commonly referred to as diabetic retinopathy, that affects the retinal vasculature and can lead to visual impairment. Its clinical course has been the subject of a dedicated five‑year, Lantus®‑controlled study in which the progression of the condition was systematically evaluated, measured, and examined across the study period.

Evidence from that and other investigations indicates that sustained, good glycemic control markedly lowers the long‑term risk of disease progression. However, a rapid improvement in blood‑glucose levels—such as that achieved with intensive insulin therapy—can provoke a transient worsening of retinal findings. This short‑term exacerbation is typically reversible, and the overall trajectory of the disease improves when tight glucose control is maintained over time.

One description characterises Retinopatia Diabética as a “very rare” diabetic eye disorder that may temporarily worsen with rapid glycemic improvement specifically from Novolin® R Penfill®. This rarity claim conflicts with the broader medical understanding that diabetic retinopathy is a common complication of diabetes, suggesting that the statement may reflect a limited or atypical observation rather than the condition’s overall prevalence. Nonetheless, it underscores the same pattern of temporary deterioration following swift glucose normalization.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-89eaf7a8bcccf1ef8657b22ee03b5dd9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-da44554b006e6bd1b841f4246a054669&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a72472938feb27131681a1591081e8c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b916f29e047f8579110cf5da3fd73847&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d648fb4d9a20040dd617a7ca164c9f10&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8a68ba1e8cc1defda76cde0eff9592e6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3396320470ee682ec5cc4f70ab001ef4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0b4034f7cf7e37425b7c76f5e0f9fd11</data>
