<node id="Hipoglicemia Noturna">
  <data key="d0">Hipoglicemia Noturna</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Hipoglicemia Noturna refers to nocturnal hypoglycemia, defined as episodes of abnormally low blood glucose that occur during the night. In the clinical studies it is recorded as an adverse safety event and is evaluated as an outcome measure when comparing insulin therapies, including the insulin comparison study and the safety assessment of Levemir® FlexPen®.  

The episodes are specifically identified as occurring between 00:00 hours and 05:59 hours, although they may arise periodically or remain undetected. Undetected nocturnal hypoglycemia can be suggested by abnormal glycated hemoglobin (HbA1c) levels. Evidence from the trials indicates that the frequency of Hipoglicemia Noturna decreases when rapid‑acting insulin analogues are used instead of other insulin formulations.&lt;SEP&gt;Hipoglicemia Noturna is nighttime hypoglycemia that can affect mood and well‑being and often goes unrecognized.&lt;SEP&gt;Hipoglicemia noturna is nighttime hypoglycemia that can affect memory consolidation during sleep.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-89eaf7a8bcccf1ef8657b22ee03b5dd9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d87cbe9886e7203b6e7b26c85d60cb9d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-87576da8269707f5f8d929b71470e023&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9cd336474a2e9457985162b1ddb4b603&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3553e80da33ab48fb157ac9ff75436eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-78f859befb6230d94e8af9144794e0d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b65a4249ac93aec086cb333ed1507ea7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-95c81e7ab8160456d9a63a9e0868205b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0e484a5a1df875be2e1525c8c64e2007&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f645bd7019e94151caaff47d6cbfcaf</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Basaglar.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Toujeo.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/Insulinoterapia – Diretriz da Sociedade Brasileira de Diabetes – Ed. 2024.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/Orientacoes_Hipoglicemia_SBD_transcricao.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1786338257</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Eli Lilly">
  <data key="d0">Eli Lilly</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Eli Lilly is a pharmaceutical company that is identified as the confidential owner of a specific document and its associated package‑insert information, as well as the source of listed label‑change notifications. In addition to this role as a document holder, Eli Lilly is a historic producer of insulin. The company offered assistance in developing methods to extract insulin and entered into a one‑year exclusive partnership with the University of Toronto beginning on May 30 1922 to scale up large‑scale insulin production. Under this collaboration, Eli Lilly secured U.S. patent rights on process improvements, supplied insulin free of charge in the initial phase, and operated a new large‑scale insulin manufacturing plant that opened on October 1 1922. By the summer of 1922 the plant employed more than one hundred workers, marking a significant expansion of the company’s insulin‑production capacity.&lt;SEP&gt;Eli Lilly is a pharmaceutical company that received consulting or funding relationships with E.C. and R.W.B.&lt;SEP&gt;Eli Lilly is a pharmaceutical company that provides consulting, speaker‑bureau, and research funding to multiple authors.&lt;SEP&gt;Eli Lilly is the pharmaceutical company that commercialized the first insulin product in 1923.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a8993f40975183bb8e3b3398f179a00d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-03d88897d0924973d84bfdd68b45230c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a86b24480e35d6df7395a60371a5f2fc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6174696e253339408f72a777ad6cd3ad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0ba3c49b467b6d37cd2aab29bf4a3119&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9043f44e67d9ed02b4864043d3cbb59a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-47acdaf58d4f121a3948976c07c3d03c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c53f6d8d7aad59b28e557f5971d0d828&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-17a38cd3b50722f2d9ae2a618121bb61&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2767372b4b5395439f542016058306a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5419de5a030f812ab408ef47f361bebd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2d8f17f3f250a37a1effaaa88cc8b382</data>
