<node id="BMI">
  <data key="d0">BMI</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Body mass index (IMC) is a measure of body composition, with a mean of 25.54 kg/m² among participants.&lt;SEP&gt;Body mass index; values under 25 kg/m² constitute one of the Five LADA criteria.&lt;SEP&gt;BMI (Body Mass Index) is an index of body mass used to assess obesity, a characteristic feature of Diabetes Tipo 2.&lt;SEP&gt;Body Mass Index (BMI) is a measurement used to assess body weight relative to height, referenced in diabetes classification.&lt;SEP&gt;Body Mass Index (BMI) is a measurement used as a risk factor for diabetes screening.&lt;SEP&gt;Body mass index (BMI) is a measure used to assess overweight and obesity risk.&lt;SEP&gt;BMI (Body Mass Index) is a measurement used as a risk factor for diabetes, with specific cut points for different populations.</data>
