</node>
<node id="Antibody Production">
  <data key="d0">Antibody Production</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Antibody production is the immunogenic response measured in clinical studies comparing BASAGLAR and Lantus®.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-22df77f7bf817d736d90608e62a11d84</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Basaglar.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786309971</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="BASAGLAR">
  <data key="d0">BASAGLAR</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">BASAGLAR is a basal insulin product that contains the long‑acting insulin analog insulin glargine, produced by recombinant DNA technology. It is supplied as an acidic injectable solution (approximately pH 4) that forms micro‑precipitates upon subcutaneous injection, creating a prolonged, peak‑free glucose‑lowering profile suitable for once‑daily administration. The medication is marketed under the brand name BASAGLAR and is identical to the international non‑proprietary name “insulin glargine.”  

Clinical development of BASAGLAR has included randomized controlled and phase 3 trials in which it was compared with the reference product Lantus® for glycemic efficacy, pharmacokinetics, safety, and adverse‑reaction profiles. These studies demonstrated comparable reductions in blood glucose levels in patients with type 2 diabetes, while also evaluating specific safety concerns such as allergic reactions, hypokalemia, delayed recovery from hypoglycemia, and potential drug interactions with thiazolidinediones (TZDs). Dosing‑error scenarios have been documented in the product literature, emphasizing the need for careful administration.  

BASAGLAR is intended for subcutaneous injection using dedicated pen devices, including the BASAGLAR KwikPen as well as other disposable or reusable pens. Each pen refill is labeled for use by a single patient and must not be shared. The formulation is contraindicated in individuals with known hypersensitivity to insulin glargine or any of its excipients.  

Overall, BASAGLAR provides a once‑daily basal insulin option for the management of diabetes, with a pharmacological profile that supports stable glucose control and a safety and usage framework that mirrors that of other insulin glargine products on the market.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-afc9722167670b0bfeef0b43f4b0df79&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-22df77f7bf817d736d90608e62a11d84&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fec70e5369024cec08c0820152befe39&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c078e8c2861146fb455f1dc3d4af2456&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-46c9571a4df1570d4a097dc949f512cd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bbae57922175913b7c36c594b4673fa2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5c580ebfc111aa29796af1a6f15941c7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0b9c41c968bcc1d46185583661e8f989&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f14ce019f10c2a88765380143498ba5b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3db0edd23b6b502ccbbf62bfd601ce68&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3a279eef99c9c70338c74ffc7b4e260e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-09cd61106182a6d47854a32a39b66057&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-61cacf80ada6db26d2b975df763c137a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-17844a4a12e6c05ba2d7b5f54b0f9bd7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3e50c145614f04be2319a31b74b80411</data>
