</node>
<node id="Anticorpos à Insulina Humana">
  <data key="d0">Anticorpos à Insulina Humana</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Anticorpos à insulina humana are antibodies against human insulin that can cause patients to require high insulin doses and to respond better to insulin glargina.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-da44554b006e6bd1b841f4246a054669</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Basaglar.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786309982</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Metabolic Control">
  <data key="d0">Metabolic Control</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Metabolic control refers to the overall regulation of glucose metabolism and is described as improving insulin sensitivity.&lt;SEP&gt;A health outcome assessed in relation to HbA1c testing and SMBG frequencies.&lt;SEP&gt;Metabolic control is the regulation of blood glucose levels achieved through continuous glucose monitoring and insulin management.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-da44554b006e6bd1b841f4246a054669&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1dec009976a44828d0e619e7fa5b1c5d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7ac99b8588a8c480f44a5519509f7713</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Basaglar.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/ref.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/glicemias capilares.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786338539</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Insulin Needs">
  <data key="d0">Insulin Needs</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Insulin needs represent the amount of insulin required by a patient, which may be reduced by better metabolic control.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-da44554b006e6bd1b841f4246a054669</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Basaglar.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786309983</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="População Pediátrica">
  <data key="d0">População Pediátrica</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">População pediátrica refers to patients aged 18 years or younger, for whom BASAGLAR KWIKPEN dosing must be individualized.&lt;SEP&gt;População Pediátrica includes children from 1 year of age who may use Fiasp® instead of regular human insulin for rapid‑acting needs.&lt;SEP&gt;População pediátrica refers to children aged 2–18 years with type‑1 diabetes who were enrolled in a confirmatory therapeutic study of FIASP®.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-da44554b006e6bd1b841f4246a054669&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3a70857656e32cc73aaa270a75eb33af&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-09d60e0b850d87c77dd67ca2d709912c</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Basaglar.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_fiasp.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786316117</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Nível Glicêmico Elevado">
  <data key="d0">Nível Glicêmico Elevado</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Nível glicêmico elevado is an excessively high blood‑glucose level that may occur after a missed BASAGLAR KWIKPEN dose.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-da44554b006e6bd1b841f4246a054669</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Basaglar.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786309985</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Distúrbios Visuais">
  <data key="d0">Distúrbios Visuais</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Distúrbios visuais are temporary visual impairments caused by acute changes in blood‑glucose levels.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-da44554b006e6bd1b841f4246a054669</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Basaglar.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786309985</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Rotação do Local de Injeção">
  <data key="d0">Rotação do Local de Injeção</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Rotação do local de injeção is a technique of alternating injection sites to minimise lipodistrofia.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-da44554b006e6bd1b841f4246a054669</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Basaglar.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786309986</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Reações Alérgicas à Insulina Glargina">
  <data key="d0">Reações Alérgicas à Insulina Glargina</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Reações alérgicas à insulina glargina are immune responses to the insulin analogue that may cause urticaria, angioedema, broncoespasmo, hypotensão ou choque.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-da44554b006e6bd1b841f4246a054669</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Basaglar.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786309986</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Insulin Humana">
  <data key="d0">Insulin Humana</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Insulin humana is human insulin used as a comparator in intravenous administration studies.&lt;SEP&gt;Insulin humana refers to human insulin, against which some patients develop antibodies.&lt;SEP&gt;Insulin Humana is the human insulin hormone used in the HUMULIN®R formulation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-da44554b006e6bd1b841f4246a054669&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f14ce019f10c2a88765380143498ba5b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-438cbb95853cdda42f2c87bcefa714dd</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Basaglar.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786319729</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Nível Glicêmico">
  <data key="d0">Nível Glicêmico</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Nível glicêmico denotes the blood‑glucose level measured in patients.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-da44554b006e6bd1b841f4246a054669</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Basaglar.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786309987</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hipoglicemia Severa">
  <data key="d0">Hipoglicemia Severa</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Hipoglicemia Severa refers to severe hypoglycemia, a safety outcome that was systematically recorded in the clinical studies. It denotes episodes of markedly low blood‑glucose levels that meet predefined clinical criteria for severity, often requiring assistance from another person or medical intervention. The event is quantified in the trials both as a rate per 100 participant‑years and as a proportion of participants experiencing at least one episode during the follow‑up period.

The descriptions emphasize that Hipoglicemia Severa can occur under a variety of circumstances, including during the night and in situations where the patient may be unaware of the hypoglycemic state. Such unrecognized or nocturnal episodes are of particular concern because they can lead to acute neurological disturbances, ranging from confusion and seizures to more prolonged cognitive impairment. Consequently, the occurrence of Hipoglicemia Severa is monitored as an important indicator of treatment safety across the different study arms.

In the reported data, severe low‑blood‑glucose events classified as Hipoglicemia Severa were observed in 3.7 % of participants over a six‑year follow‑up, illustrating a relatively low but clinically significant incidence. The consistent reporting of these episodes across the studies underscores their relevance for evaluating the risk profile of the interventions under investigation.&lt;SEP&gt;Hipoglicemia Severa denotes severe low blood glucose, defined by thresholds such as &lt; 54 mg/dL.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-da44554b006e6bd1b841f4246a054669&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a72472938feb27131681a1591081e8c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b916f29e047f8579110cf5da3fd73847&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d87cbe9886e7203b6e7b26c85d60cb9d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-87576da8269707f5f8d929b71470e023&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-61cacf80ada6db26d2b975df763c137a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1b30ff3c650cf7cb71a3cf6e99f2c581&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-78f859befb6230d94e8af9144794e0d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d35e6caf612b4c4984ade9315ebc7431</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Basaglar.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Toujeo.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Metas glicêmicas/Metas no tratamento.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786370040</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Neuroglicopenia">
  <data key="d0">Neuroglicopenia</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Neuroglicopenia is a neurological condition caused by low blood glucose, characterized by symptoms that precede counterregulatory signs.&lt;SEP&gt;Neuroglicopenia is a condition of insufficient glucose in the brain, preceded by adrenergic counter‑regulatory signs.&lt;SEP&gt;Neuroglicopenia describes neurological symptoms that arise from low blood glucose levels.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-da44554b006e6bd1b841f4246a054669&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3e50c145614f04be2319a31b74b80411&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e8934881ec5ab7cfeb836126b3f0e8b2</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Basaglar.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Toujeo.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786313634</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Contrarregulação Adrenérgica">
  <data key="d0">Contrarregulação Adrenérgica</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Contrarregulação adrenérgica refers to the adrenaline‑mediated counterregulatory response triggered during rapid declines in blood glucose.&lt;SEP&gt;Contrarregulação adrenérgica refers to the body's adrenergic response to falling blood‑glucose levels.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-da44554b006e6bd1b841f4246a054669&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3e50c145614f04be2319a31b74b80411</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Basaglar.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786309988</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Retinopatia Proliferativa">
  <data key="d0">Retinopatia Proliferativa</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Retinopatia proliferativa is an advanced stage of diabetic eye disease that may be worsened by severe hypoglycemia if not treated.&lt;SEP&gt;Retinopatia proliferativa is an advanced diabetic eye disease that can cause transient blindness if untreated.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-da44554b006e6bd1b841f4246a054669&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9cd336474a2e9457985162b1ddb4b603</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Basaglar.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Toujeo.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786313542</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Fotocoagulação">
  <data key="d0">Fotocoagulação</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Fotocoagulação is a laser treatment used for proliferative diabetic retinopathy.&lt;SEP&gt;Fotocoagulação is a laser treatment used to manage proliferative diabetic retinopathy.&lt;SEP&gt;Fotocoagulação is a laser treatment used to manage proliferative retinopathy in diabetic patients.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-da44554b006e6bd1b841f4246a054669&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3e50c145614f04be2319a31b74b80411&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9cd336474a2e9457985162b1ddb4b603</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Basaglar.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Toujeo.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786313542</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Reações no Local das Injeções">
  <data key="d0">Reações no Local das Injeções</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Reações no local das injeções are injection‑site reactions such as erythema, pain, itching, urticaria, swelling and inflammation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-da44554b006e6bd1b841f4246a054669</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Basaglar.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786309989</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Reações Alérgicas Imediatas">
  <data key="d0">Reações Alérgicas Imediatas</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Reações alérgicas imediatas are rare immediate hypersensitivity responses to insulin or its excipients, potentially causing anaphylaxis.</data>
