</node>
<node id="Amiloidose Cutânea Localizada">
  <data key="d0">Amiloidose Cutânea Localizada</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Amiloidose Cutânea Localizada is a form of localized cutaneous amyloidosis characterized by the deposition of amyloid protein within the skin at sites of repeated injections. The condition is most commonly reported in association with chronic insulin administration, where the trauma of frequent needle punctures leads to focal amyloid accumulation. It has also been observed as an adverse event following repeated injections of the glucagon‑like peptide‑1 receptor agonist APIDRA SOLOSTAR, and the presence of such lesions is considered a contraindication to further administration of this medication in the affected areas.

Clinically, the amyloid deposits appear as firm, sometimes nodular or papular lesions at the injection sites and may be accompanied by local skin changes. Although the primary manifestation is cutaneous, the lesions have been linked to metabolic consequences, including the potential development of hyperglycemia, likely secondary to impaired insulin absorption at the compromised sites. Management typically involves avoiding further injections in the involved region, rotating injection sites, and monitoring for systemic effects.&lt;SEP&gt;Localized cutaneous amyloidosis is a skin condition risk linked to repeated injection sites.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-072d97721eef045503ec1dce0363b58e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-61cacf80ada6db26d2b975df763c137a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8ef35bd45e4ba8d20f4e9181011ccfcd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a247846b9ec5d44d0bcbe6c5f15599f8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aca0b919135813e1d5b772face36989d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9cd336474a2e9457985162b1ddb4b603&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e212a20942ed5387efe96e92bdb4ba98&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-15a498084b9a0c4cfcd9aa9553e12a14&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b060d4f68031bd35dfafc19eadf1e9fe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e3418c4ee80182ca29214dd54b0d9647&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-04b345bc26ec7f5d7c9db8c6004a50a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0e7689ca0fc736d9eae94256f73fed52&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-929e31613caadc967412041c8c2155b3</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Basaglar.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_1778357531609.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Toujeo.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_apidra.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786319689</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Dose de Insulina">
  <data key="d0">Dose de Insulina</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Dose de insulina is the amount of insulin administered, mentioned as not correlated with antibody production.&lt;SEP&gt;Dose de Insulina refers to the amount of insulin administered, which may require adjustment based on pregnancy, lactation, age, or organ insufficiency.&lt;SEP&gt;Dose de Insulina denotes the amount of insulin administered, influencing pharmacokinetic variability.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-072d97721eef045503ec1dce0363b58e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-518838d3c8e8110567b1891b704bfef9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-93f7f04b0529d6f0ace11829cc4fa3b4</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Basaglar.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_1778357531609.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786318550</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hemoglobina Glicosilada">
  <data key="d0">Hemoglobina Glicosilada</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Measurement of glycated hemoglobin used to assess glycemic control; low values may indicate risk of periodic hypoglycemia.&lt;SEP&gt;Hemoglobina glicosilada is a laboratory measure of glycated hemoglobin used to detect episodes of periodic or unrecognized hypoglycemia.&lt;SEP&gt;Hemoglobina glicosilada is a laboratory measurement of average blood glucose; low or normal values may indicate periodic hypoglycemia.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-46c9571a4df1570d4a097dc949f512cd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-61cacf80ada6db26d2b975df763c137a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9cd336474a2e9457985162b1ddb4b603</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Basaglar.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Toujeo.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786313542</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="TZDs (Tiazolidinedionas)">
  <data key="d0">TZDs (Tiazolidinedionas)</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">TZDs are a class of medications that, when combined with insulin, increase the risk of edema and heart failure.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-46c9571a4df1570d4a097dc949f512cd</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Basaglar.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786310005</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Insuficiência Cardíaca">
  <data key="d0">Insuficiência Cardíaca</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Insuficiência cardíaca is heart failure that may be precipitated by the combination of TZDs and insulin.&lt;SEP&gt;Insuficiência Cardíaca is heart failure, a risk increased when TZD is used together with insulin.&lt;SEP&gt;Comprometimento da função cardíaca que pode ser desencadeado por TZD em pacientes com doença cardíaca subjacente.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-46c9571a4df1570d4a097dc949f512cd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a247846b9ec5d44d0bcbe6c5f15599f8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cbe87fd92ad66dcb02b25b669d829f6c</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Basaglar.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_1778357531609.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786319736</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hipocalemia">
  <data key="d0">Hipocalemia</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Hipocalemia is a drop in extracellular potassium caused by insulin shifting potassium intracellularly, potentially leading to respiratory paralysis, ventricular arrhythmia, or death.&lt;SEP&gt;Hipocalemia is a condition of low blood potassium that can cause respiratory paralysis, ventricular arrhythmia, and death.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-46c9571a4df1570d4a097dc949f512cd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5b40c2fbad301807d9646f27d94635cb</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Basaglar.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786310005</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Potássio">
  <data key="d0">Potássio</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Potássio is an electrolyte whose extracellular levels can decrease after insulin administration.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-46c9571a4df1570d4a097dc949f512cd</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Basaglar.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786310005</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Doenças Intercorrentes">
  <data key="d0">Doenças Intercorrentes</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Doenças intercorrentes such as vomiting or diarrhea can increase susceptibility to hypoglycemia.&lt;SEP&gt;Concurrent illnesses that affect insulin dosing.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-46c9571a4df1570d4a097dc949f512cd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-60530d1861f7c2d1efecc069c0913d37</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Basaglar.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786330162</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Necessidade de Insulina">
  <data key="d0">Necessidade de Insulina</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Necessidade de insulina denotes the amount of insulin required, which may be adjusted in renal or hepatic insufficiency.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-46c9571a4df1570d4a097dc949f512cd</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Basaglar.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786310006</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Sensibilidade à Insulina">
  <data key="d0">Sensibilidade à Insulina</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Sensibilidade à insulina describes how responsive a patient is to insulin, influencing hypoglycemia risk.&lt;SEP&gt;Insulin sensitivity is reduced by about 30 % in Afro‑American individuals compared with Caucasians, contributing to higher diabetes prevalence.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-46c9571a4df1570d4a097dc949f512cd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e7b4535dbb2554b84c7a2e024c4b82c4</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Basaglar.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Diagnóstico de diabetes mellitus.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786371976</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Rótulo Da Insulina">
  <data key="d0">Rótulo Da Insulina</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Rótulo Da Insulina is the label on insulin containers that must be verified before each injection to avoid medication errors.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-46c9571a4df1570d4a097dc949f512cd</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Basaglar.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786310006</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Insulina De Curta Ação">
  <data key="d0">Insulina De Curta Ação</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Insulina De Curta Ação refers to short‑acting insulin types that were mistakenly administered instead of BASAGLAR in reported medication errors.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-46c9571a4df1570d4a097dc949f512cd</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Basaglar.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786310006</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Anafilaxia">
  <data key="d0">Anafilaxia</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Anafilaxia is a severe, life‑threatening allergic reaction that can occur with insulin administration, including BASAGLAR.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-46c9571a4df1570d4a097dc949f512cd</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Basaglar.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786310006</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Teste De Urina Para Cetonas">
  <data key="d0">Teste De Urina Para Cetonas</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Teste De Urina Para Cetonas is a diagnostic method involving urine analysis for ketones to monitor metabolic status.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-46c9571a4df1570d4a097dc949f512cd</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Basaglar.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786310006</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Monitoramento Metabólico">
  <data key="d0">Monitoramento Metabólico</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Monitoramento Metabólico is the ongoing assessment of metabolic parameters, including ketone testing, in patients with intercurrent diseases.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-46c9571a4df1570d4a097dc949f512cd</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Basaglar.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786310007</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Ajuste De Dose">
  <data key="d0">Ajuste De Dose</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Ajuste De Dose denotes the modification of insulin dosage in response to factors like renal or hepatic insufficiency.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-46c9571a4df1570d4a097dc949f512cd</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Basaglar.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786310007</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Restrição Dietética">
  <data key="d0">Restrição Dietética</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Restrição Dietética refers to dietary limitations advised to patients to lower hypoglycemia risk.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-46c9571a4df1570d4a097dc949f512cd</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Basaglar.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786310007</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Erro De Medicação">
  <data key="d0">Erro De Medicação</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Erro De Medicação describes medication administration mistakes, such as giving short‑acting insulin instead of BASAGLAR.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-46c9571a4df1570d4a097dc949f512cd</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Basaglar.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786310007</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Eli Lilly and Company">
  <data key="d0">Eli Lilly and Company</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Eli Lilly and Company is the parent company owning the BASAGLAR KwikPen trademark.&lt;SEP&gt;Eli Lilly and Company holds the trademarks for HUMALOG® MIX KWIKPEN products.&lt;SEP&gt;Eli Lilly and Company is the pharmaceutical manufacturer listed as the producer of the product, located in Indianapolis, USA.&lt;SEP&gt;Eli Lilly and Company is the organization credited with the design of glucagón.&lt;SEP&gt;Pharmaceutical company that markets the Glucagon Emergency Kit.&lt;SEP&gt;Eli Lilly and Company is the company that holds the trademark for the glucagon design used in emergency kits.&lt;SEP&gt;Eli Lilly and Company employed George H. A. Clowes as research director and was interested in the pancreatic extract findings.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6f0c10866496bbb0b388b1e5ed69901c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b4916e2524690f1ce85df7c187f6d7a7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6419fb3ef4249d6c7e8d8a45d82efe80&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-644dc086af7b196cc5bc332524608d5f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4bbf34cee3d731d22b25c31db33dd183&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7ce776458e256df9d6070a419cab7449&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-247d0735bf59962683d382203243d395</data>
