</node>
<node id="Short‑Acting Insulin">
  <data key="d0">Short‑Acting Insulin</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Short‑acting insulin refers to rapid‑acting insulin formulations used for prandial glucose control.&lt;SEP&gt;Short‑acting insulin refers to rapid‑onset insulin formulations, mentioned as being mistakenly administered instead of Basaglar KwikPen.&lt;SEP&gt;Short‑acting insulin is a form of insulin that may be stored in the emergency kit.&lt;SEP&gt;Short‑acting insulin is an insulin category that begins to work within about 30 minutes after injection.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bbae57922175913b7c36c594b4673fa2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-45d489de28e8fda3c3be3bb09ab29eb2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-36ace822cd4873b8fd2adcfef0a7f9fd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0932e9c21a330869629b3fa70d2e1f5e</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Basaglar.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/Understanding insulin - International Diabetes Federation.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786332449</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Intravenous Short‑Acting Insulin">
  <data key="d0">Intravenous Short‑Acting Insulin</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Intravenous short‑acting insulin is a rapid insulin administered intravenously, preferred for acute diabetic ketoacidosis treatment.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bbae57922175913b7c36c594b4673fa2</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Basaglar.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786310008</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Intravenous Injection">
  <data key="d0">Intravenous Injection</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Intravenous Injection is a route of drug administration in which medication is delivered directly into a vein, allowing the substance to enter the bloodstream immediately. This method is commonly employed by health professionals when rapid systemic absorption is required, and it can be performed using standard syringes or infusion systems.  

In clinical research, intravenous injection has been used as the delivery method in comparative studies of long‑acting insulin formulations, such as investigations contrasting Lantus® with human insulin, to ensure precise dosing and swift pharmacokinetic measurement.  

Regulatory guidance and product labeling specify that intravenous injection is expressly prohibited for several insulin products. The route is not permitted for BASAGLAR, including the BASAGLAR KWIKPEN device, nor for Humalog Mix 25 Kwikpen, and it is also disallowed for Levemir®. These restrictions are intended to prevent off‑label use that could compromise safety or efficacy.  

Conversely, intravenous injection is an accepted administration route for Novolin® R when performed by qualified health professionals using infusion systems, reflecting the product’s labeling that allows this method under controlled clinical conditions.&lt;SEP&gt;Intravenous injection is another optional route for administering Humulin R.&lt;SEP&gt;Intravenous injection is another possible route for administering Humulin R.&lt;SEP&gt;Intravenous injection is a method of delivering the extract directly into the bloodstream, shown to reduce blood sugar rapidly.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bbae57922175913b7c36c594b4673fa2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3db0edd23b6b502ccbbf62bfd601ce68&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3a279eef99c9c70338c74ffc7b4e260e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d96761d60c65f05f1530bc19b144cf1b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4ce520f0fe7dc4a6c79f92a25dfaff19&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-465ad8b77c1c2a2a179062da20337ff5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cedd8e88a8d35eade68ce02222b9e276&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0955cb70a6ce135722726162a9811e78&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-df616353e032c899b02bfa4368bc2667&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-577779892c0d463cd6bb1966b8a8ce2d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8ac99e7359716e2cecc2ec93159218b6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ad5d126f417014eb5c7a07a85db48d1d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Basaglar.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_1778357531609.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_apidra.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/The Discovery and Development.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786332097</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="BASAGLAR Refill">
  <data key="d0">BASAGLAR Refill</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">A BASAGLAR refill is a single‑use cartridge of BASAGLAR intended for use by one patient only.&lt;SEP&gt;BASAGLAR Refill is a 3 mL glass cartridge containing sterile insulin glargine solution.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bbae57922175913b7c36c594b4673fa2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3db0edd23b6b502ccbbf62bfd601ce68</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Basaglar.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786310008</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Pediatric Patients">
  <data key="d0">Pediatric Patients</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Pediatric patients are individuals who are younger than 18 years of age, encompassing children and adolescents. In the context of the insulin‑related clinical programs described, the term is applied to study participants whose ages fall within various sub‑ranges depending on the product and protocol: some trials include children older than 1 year, others define the cohort as children and adolescents over 4 years old, while specific pharmacokinetic assessments of Toujeo (insulin glargine 300 U/mL) focus on participants aged 6 years up to, but not including, 18 years. Across these studies, pediatric patients receive individualized insulin dosing—either as a tailored dose of Toujeo 300 U/mL for those aged six years or older, or as customized regimens of other insulin formulations such as Apidra SoloStar. The populations referenced are therefore a subset of the broader pediatric age group who were enrolled in Phase III or other clinical trials, including children and adolescents with Type 1 diabetes who were evaluated for safety, efficacy, and pharmacokinetic outcomes.&lt;SEP&gt;Pediatric patients refer to children from one year of age for whom Levemir® may be used with individualized dosing to minimize hypoglycemia risk.&lt;SEP&gt;Pediatric patients (adolescents and children from 1 year old) may use Levemir® with individualized dose reduction to minimize hypoglycemia risk.&lt;SEP&gt;Children with diabetes who were studied for durability of insulin pump use.&lt;SEP&gt;Children who are subjects of medical studies.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bbae57922175913b7c36c594b4673fa2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4319d08c10ed2b48857a6d42eadd9db0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7d9c944d51a42525c017d9109f46684c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d6b9a8472aefa6e90793233284c15a3f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1ee5400065df79b02b6c04efc0f4854d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-162882e6afffb0db8ae5e9153e5f1e82&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-891989adf06518cd34c94853444495e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c8c7e36686d077dcb6239405f60ea031&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0ace26fdb0244e3d0f714a007c9bbb51&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-56fc1d5df1b34d9120c3cf8a760c40f9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-16a76447c936e157673f084ffb74520d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c83accc14a3b482690949ff04716a0aa</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Basaglar.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_1778357531609.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Toujeo.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_apidra.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_fiasp.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377254</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
