<node id="Insulina Humana">
  <data key="d0">Insulina Humana</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Insulina Humana is recombinant human insulin that is chemically identical to the insulin produced endogenously in the human pancreas. It is manufactured by recombinant DNA technology and is the active ingredient in several commercial short‑acting insulin products, including Novolin® R Penfill®, Novolin® R FlexPen®, and Humulin® R (100 U mL⁻¹). As a generic, short‑acting formulation, Insulina Humana is used in clinical practice to achieve rapid onset and predictable control of blood‑glucose levels in patients with diabetes, particularly when a reference standard is needed for comparing the efficacy of other insulin preparations.

In the pharmaceutical and research arenas, Insulina Humana serves as the benchmark molecule for unit equivalence (e.g., with Fiasp®) and for evaluating the pharmacokinetic, pharmacodynamic, and immunogenic properties of newer insulin analogues such as insulin glargine, insulin lispro, and other rapid‑acting formulations. Comparative studies consistently show that Insulina Humana produces fewer injection‑site reactions than insulin detemir (Levemir®) and elicits lower anti‑insulin antibody levels than animal‑derived insulins, reflecting its reduced immunogenicity after the transition from animal to recombinant insulin therapy.

Animal‑model investigations have reported potential carcinogenic, mutagenic, and fertility‑risk effects associated with Insulina Humana, although these findings are confined to pre‑clinical settings. Consequently, ongoing safety monitoring and risk assessment are emphasized when the molecule is employed therapeutically or experimentally. Overall, Insulina Humana functions both as a standard therapeutic agent for diabetes management and as a critical reference comparator in the development and evaluation of insulin analogues.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-02780a8bc1d372cc47e0ccf2eaab1a99&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3a279eef99c9c70338c74ffc7b4e260e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-61cacf80ada6db26d2b975df763c137a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2db4ee43ed7cc39546184320e1328d06&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4319d08c10ed2b48857a6d42eadd9db0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-518838d3c8e8110567b1891b704bfef9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a247846b9ec5d44d0bcbe6c5f15599f8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d99841fd6d1e1fbf23f184e202bc760e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-add4469fba80232b7c0742f24c0914c9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-45ee3dcb366c1301c9fb1d2ce9f323c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8a68ba1e8cc1defda76cde0eff9592e6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d01ed6a801b11c1b53f4668059c1f9cb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a7ca732691e1cbcafd65e378b8d80144&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d29256dbc41e0c81e974f018d373c72d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-10dad476eb9d365159c539ced3aeec4b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cbe87fd92ad66dcb02b25b669d829f6c</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Basaglar.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_1778357531609.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Toujeo.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_fiasp.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786319709</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
