  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Euglycemic Clamp Study">
  <data key="d0">Euglycemic Clamp Study</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">The euglycemic clamp study involved 91 healthy volunteers receiving a single 0.5 UI/Kg subcutaneous dose to assess pharmacokinetics.&lt;SEP&gt;Euglycemic Clamp Study is a clinical pharmacology method used to assess insulin pharmacodynamics.&lt;SEP&gt;The euglycemic clamp study is a controlled method used to determine the pharmacokinetic profile of BASAGLAR KWIKPEN.&lt;SEP&gt;Euglycemic clamp study is a clinical method used to assess insulin action and glucose infusion rates in healthy subjects or patients with type 1 diabetes.&lt;SEP&gt;The euglycemic clamp study measured the onset of pharmacologic action of Humulin R by detecting the first change in glucose infusion rate.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-02780a8bc1d372cc47e0ccf2eaab1a99&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f14ce019f10c2a88765380143498ba5b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-133169995b3ab942fd96f1fdfe7269ad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-afc28422755c2c44f931bab7b6a2b477&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a1245bd9ff75c998b49dab861cc4cebf</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Basaglar.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Toujeo.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786319694</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Glucose Metabolism">
  <data key="d0">Glucose Metabolism</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Glucose Metabolism encompasses the regulation of blood glucose levels, the primary activity of insulin.&lt;SEP&gt;Glucose metabolism is the biochemical pathway regulated by insulin, including peripheral glucose uptake and hepatic glucose production.&lt;SEP&gt;Glucose metabolism involves the body's processing of glucose.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-02780a8bc1d372cc47e0ccf2eaab1a99&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-afc28422755c2c44f931bab7b6a2b477&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-44aa59c0e5cc620a11b8fb017d1aefcf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-72a2488e8176f7676c76504e76dd6c04</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Basaglar.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Toujeo.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377304</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Skeletal Muscle Tissue">
  <data key="d0">Skeletal Muscle Tissue</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Skeletal muscle tissue is a type of muscle that absorbs glucose in response to insulin.&lt;SEP&gt;Skeletal Muscle Tissue is a major peripheral tissue where insulin stimulates glucose uptake.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-02780a8bc1d372cc47e0ccf2eaab1a99&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3a279eef99c9c70338c74ffc7b4e260e</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Basaglar.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786310017</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Adipose Tissue">
  <data key="d0">Adipose Tissue</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Adipose tissue is fatty tissue that takes up glucose under insulin stimulation and where lipolysis occurs.&lt;SEP&gt;Adipose Tissue is a peripheral tissue where insulin promotes glucose uptake and inhibits lipolysis.&lt;SEP&gt;Adipose tissue is a peripheral tissue that uptake glucose and where insulin inhibits lipolysis.&lt;SEP&gt;Adipose tissue is a body tissue that receives glucose via insulin‑mediated uptake.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-02780a8bc1d372cc47e0ccf2eaab1a99&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3a279eef99c9c70338c74ffc7b4e260e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-afc28422755c2c44f931bab7b6a2b477&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1bb9ea85b9ad8cd6940ae41a3ab5d1fd</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Basaglar.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Toujeo.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_fiasp.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786316080</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hepatic Glucose Production">
  <data key="d0">Hepatic Glucose Production</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Hepatic Glucose Production is the liver’s generation of glucose, which insulin inhibits.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-02780a8bc1d372cc47e0ccf2eaab1a99</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Basaglar.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786310017</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Lipolysis">
  <data key="d0">Lipolysis</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Lipolysis is the metabolic process of breaking down triglycerides in adipocytes, which insulin glargina inhibits.&lt;SEP&gt;Lipolysis is the breakdown of fats in adipocytes that insulin suppresses.&lt;SEP&gt;Lipolysis is the metabolic process of breaking down lipids, which insulin inhibits.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-02780a8bc1d372cc47e0ccf2eaab1a99&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3a279eef99c9c70338c74ffc7b4e260e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1bb9ea85b9ad8cd6940ae41a3ab5d1fd</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Basaglar.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_fiasp.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786316082</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Proteolysis">
  <data key="d0">Proteolysis</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Proteolysis is the degradation of proteins, a process inhibited by insulin and its analogues.&lt;SEP&gt;Proteolysis is the degradation of proteins that insulin inhibits.&lt;SEP&gt;Proteolysis is the breakdown of proteins, which insulin inhibits.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-02780a8bc1d372cc47e0ccf2eaab1a99&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3a279eef99c9c70338c74ffc7b4e260e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1bb9ea85b9ad8cd6940ae41a3ab5d1fd</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Basaglar.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_fiasp.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786316082</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Protein Synthesis">
  <data key="d0">Protein Synthesis</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Protein synthesis is the cellular process of building proteins, which insulin promotes.&lt;SEP&gt;Protein Synthesis is the creation of proteins that insulin enhances.&lt;SEP&gt;Protein synthesis is the cellular process of building proteins, which insulin stimulates.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-02780a8bc1d372cc47e0ccf2eaab1a99&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3a279eef99c9c70338c74ffc7b4e260e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1bb9ea85b9ad8cd6940ae41a3ab5d1fd</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Basaglar.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_fiasp.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786316082</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="pH 4">
  <data key="d0">pH 4</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">pH 4 denotes the acidic pH of the BASAGLAR injectable solution, where insulin glargina is fully soluble.&lt;SEP&gt;pH 4 denotes the acidic pH of the BASAGLAR Kwikpen solution that keeps Insulina Glargina soluble.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-02780a8bc1d372cc47e0ccf2eaab1a99&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3a279eef99c9c70338c74ffc7b4e260e</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Basaglar.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786310018</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Figure 1">
  <data key="d0">Figure 1</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Figure 1 illustrates the pharmacodynamic activity profile of insulin glargine (also described as Insulina Glargina) in patients with type 1 diabetes, showing how the long‑acting analogue influences glucose metabolism over time.  

Figure 1 depicts the activity profile of Toujeo 300 U/mL observed over up to 36 hours in a crossover euglycemic clamp study that enrolled 18 individuals with type 1 diabetes, highlighting the duration and magnitude of its glucose‑lowering effect.  

Figure 1 visualizes the six‑hour hypoglycemic effect of APIDRA when administered either before or after a meal, and compares this pattern with that of regular insulin, thereby illustrating the timing‑dependent impact on blood‑glucose levels.  

Figure 1 illustrates the activity profile of Levemir® in patients with type 1 diabetes, presenting its onset, peak, and duration of action within a typical dosing interval.  

Figure 1 illustrates the recommended time‑in‑range (TIR) target of 50 % for elderly or high‑risk patients, indicating the proportion of daily glucose readings that should fall within the therapeutic window for this population.  

Figure 1 displays the FINDRISC questionnaire, a standardized tool used to assess an individual’s risk of developing type 2 diabetes based on lifestyle, anthropometric, and clinical factors.  

Figure 1 is a decision flowchart that outlines the differential‑diagnosis process for various diabetes types, guiding clinicians through key clinical features and laboratory criteria to distinguish among type 1, type 2, gestational, and other specific forms of diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-02780a8bc1d372cc47e0ccf2eaab1a99&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3a279eef99c9c70338c74ffc7b4e260e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-afc28422755c2c44f931bab7b6a2b477&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7621ac447c9044986ade86ce5f9be201&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-01fb767ae3a103c9d6c4775570df90c9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6d83801272f7a0ae0d797d60572fe578&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-67792416bc5f0609842dd2a9940d8749&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2e6267110f4ae5f4df4c49c0653a09b2</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Basaglar.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Toujeo.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_apidra.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Metas glicêmicas/Metas no tratamento.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Diagnóstico de diabetes mellitus.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786373111</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Figure 2">
  <data key="d0">Figure 2</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Figure 2 shows the pharmacodynamic activity profile of insulin glargine in healthy volunteers.&lt;SEP&gt;Figure 2 shows the pharmacodynamic activity profile of BASAGLAR Kwikpen in healthy volunteers.&lt;SEP&gt;Figure 2 presents the pharmacokinetic profiles of Insulina Glulisina and Insulina Humana Regular after a subcutaneous dose in Type 1 diabetes patients.&lt;SEP&gt;Figure 2 depicts the pharmacokinetic profiles of insulin glulisina and insulin regular after a 0.15 UI/kg dose in patients with Type 1 diabetes.&lt;SEP&gt;Figure 2 illustrates post‑prandial glucose increment after 26 weeks of treatment with Fiasp® and NovoRapid®.&lt;SEP&gt;Figure 2 is a graph illustrating continuous glucose monitoring data from the Medtronic MiniMed 640G insulin pump.&lt;SEP&gt;Figure 2 illustrates two cases of differing glycemic fluctuations with the same HbA1c over a 15‑day period.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-02780a8bc1d372cc47e0ccf2eaab1a99&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3a279eef99c9c70338c74ffc7b4e260e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7621ac447c9044986ade86ce5f9be201&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50719bcc88f4515ec825b9d5a7aba107&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1bb9ea85b9ad8cd6940ae41a3ab5d1fd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-94150b57cc35a773b7c36f33f237f8a1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a5f7cad1fb0e1a0a02f63b5928b8acd2</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Basaglar.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_apidra.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_fiasp.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/cgm.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/glicemias capilares.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786338529</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
