</node>
<node id="Molecular Weight 6063">
  <data key="d0">Molecular Weight 6063</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Molecular weight 6063 (Daltons) is the mass of an Insulina Glargina molecule.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-02780a8bc1d372cc47e0ccf2eaab1a99</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Basaglar.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786310018</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Micro‑Precipitates">
  <data key="d0">Micro‑Precipitates</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Micro‑precipitates are microscopic particles formed after injection of BASAGLAR Kwikpen that enable continuous release of Insulina Glargina.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-02780a8bc1d372cc47e0ccf2eaab1a99</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Basaglar.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786310018</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="pH Neutral">
  <data key="d0">pH Neutral</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">pH neutral refers to a neutral pH condition where Insulina Glargina has low solubility.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-02780a8bc1d372cc47e0ccf2eaab1a99</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Basaglar.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786310019</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Rmax">
  <data key="d0">Rmax</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Rmax is the maximum rate of glucose infusion measured as a pharmacodynamic parameter.&lt;SEP&gt;Rmax is a pharmacodynamic response metric representing the maximal effect of insulin formulations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-02780a8bc1d372cc47e0ccf2eaab1a99&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-133169995b3ab942fd96f1fdfe7269ad</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Basaglar.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786310019</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Gtot">
  <data key="d0">Gtot</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Gtot is the total amount of glucose infused during a clamp study, used as a pharmacodynamic measure.&lt;SEP&gt;Gtot is a pharmacodynamic response metric representing the total glucose‑lowering effect of insulin formulations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-02780a8bc1d372cc47e0ccf2eaab1a99&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-133169995b3ab942fd96f1fdfe7269ad</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Basaglar.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786310019</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="12.0 Hours">
  <data key="d0">12.0 Hours</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">12.0 Hours is the average time to maximal effect after subcutaneous administration of BASAGLAR Kwikpen.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-02780a8bc1d372cc47e0ccf2eaab1a99</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Basaglar.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786310019</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="24 Hours">
  <data key="d0">24 Hours</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">24 Hours is the duration over which BASAGLAR Kwikpen maintains glucose reduction without a pronounced peak.&lt;SEP&gt;A duration of 24 hours denotes the period during which Novolin® R in polypropylene infusion bags stays stable at ambient temperature.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-02780a8bc1d372cc47e0ccf2eaab1a99&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-73559dc5d86ea52a348d603482e056e9</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Basaglar.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786318526</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="0.5 U/I·Kg">
  <data key="d0">0.5 U/I·Kg</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">0.5 U per kilogram is the insulin dose used in the Euglycemic Clamp Study with healthy volunteers.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-02780a8bc1d372cc47e0ccf2eaab1a99</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Basaglar.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786310019</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="0.3 UI/Kg">
  <data key="d0">0.3 UI/Kg</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">0.3 UI per kilogram is the insulin dose used in the Euglycemic Clamp Study with Diabetes Tipo 1 patients.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-02780a8bc1d372cc47e0ccf2eaab1a99</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Basaglar.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786310020</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="1.670 mg/Kg">
  <data key="d0">1.670 mg/Kg</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">1.670 mg per kilogram is the average glucose infusion rate area under the curve observed in the clamp study.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-02780a8bc1d372cc47e0ccf2eaab1a99</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Basaglar.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786310020</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="2.12 mg/Kg/min">
  <data key="d0">2.12 mg/Kg/min</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">2.12 mg per kilogram per minute is the maximum glucose infusion rate recorded in the clamp study.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-02780a8bc1d372cc47e0ccf2eaab1a99</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Basaglar.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786310020</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Prolonged Duration of Action">
  <data key="d0">Prolonged Duration of Action</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Prolonged Duration of Action describes the extended effect of Insulina Glargina without a pronounced peak.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-02780a8bc1d372cc47e0ccf2eaab1a99</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Basaglar.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786310020</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="ETDRS Scale">
  <data key="d0">ETDRS Scale</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The ETDRS Scale is a classification protocol derived from the Early Treatment Diabetic Retinopathy Study used to grade retinopathy stages.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a72472938feb27131681a1591081e8c1</data>
