<node id="Metabolite M2 (21A‑Gly‑des‑30B‑Thr‑insulin)">
  <data key="d0">Metabolite M2 (21A‑Gly‑des‑30B‑Thr‑insulin)</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Metabolite M2 is a second active metabolite derived from insulin glargine metabolism exhibiting similar in‑vitro activity to insulin.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f14ce019f10c2a88765380143498ba5b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Basaglar.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786310023</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Pharmacokinetic Profile">
  <data key="d0">Pharmacokinetic Profile</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Pharmacokinetic profile describes the absorption, distribution, metabolism and elimination characteristics of a drug over time.&lt;SEP&gt;Pharmacokinetic profile describes the absorption, distribution, and elimination characteristics of the insulin products over 24 hours.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f14ce019f10c2a88765380143498ba5b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-133169995b3ab942fd96f1fdfe7269ad</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Basaglar.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786310023</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Biodisponibilidade">
  <data key="d0">Biodisponibilidade</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Biodisponibilidade refers to the relative bioavailability of BASAGLAR compared with Lantus®, expressed as a ratio near 1.0.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f14ce019f10c2a88765380143498ba5b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Basaglar.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786310023</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="AUC(0‑24)">
  <data key="d0">AUC(0‑24)</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">AUC(0‑24) is the area under the serum insulin concentration‑time curve from 0 to 24 hours, used to compare BASAGLAR and Lantus®.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f14ce019f10c2a88765380143498ba5b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Basaglar.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786310023</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Deltoid">
  <data key="d0">Deltoid</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Deltoid is a subcutaneous injection site examined for insulin glargina pharmacodynamics.&lt;SEP&gt;Deltoid is an approved subcutaneous injection site for BASAGLAR.&lt;SEP&gt;Deltoid is an injection site where subcutaneous insulin was administered.&lt;SEP&gt;Deltoid is a recommended injection site for BASAGLAR KWIKPEN.&lt;SEP&gt;The deltoid muscle is another permissible subcutaneous injection site for Toujeo 300 U/mL.&lt;SEP&gt;Deltoid is a body region commonly used for subcutaneous injection of APIDRA.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f14ce019f10c2a88765380143498ba5b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3db0edd23b6b502ccbbf62bfd601ce68&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d96761d60c65f05f1530bc19b144cf1b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-133169995b3ab942fd96f1fdfe7269ad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1ee5400065df79b02b6c04efc0f4854d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-465ad8b77c1c2a2a179062da20337ff5</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Basaglar.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Toujeo.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_apidra.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786315477</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Age">
  <data key="d0">Age</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Age is a demographic and chronological characteristic that denotes the length of time an individual has lived and is commonly used in clinical and epidemiological contexts. In diabetes research, Age functions as a key variable in subgroup safety and efficacy assessments of insulin products such as Lantus® and insulin NPH, influencing dosing decisions and the interpretation of trial outcomes. Reported participant ages differ across studies: one clinical trial recorded an average age of 41.2 years, while another cited a mean of approximately 59 years, with the overall age range of enrolled patients spanning from 18 to 83 years. Age also encompasses life‑stage considerations, such as puberty, which can affect insulin requirements.

Beyond its role in trial design, Age is recognized as a major risk factor for developing Type 2 Diabetes. Advancing years increase susceptibility, prompting public‑health guidelines that recommend diabetes screening begin no later than age 35. The Diabetes Risk Test explicitly incorporates Age, assigning points based on chronological age to estimate an individual’s likelihood of developing the disease. In cystic fibrosis‑related diabetes (CFRD), prevalence rises by roughly 10 % for each additional decade of life, further illustrating the impact of Age on diabetes risk across different populations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f14ce019f10c2a88765380143498ba5b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7a592aedb257bad9532268b4056ec15c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3ce5998d1ff6a67e2e549405b16f744f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-88b97cde53943160602b20f634ba5c1f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c7e6ef38db0b62d161b13473af47d738&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2c37e26e62468b725533260347fb4e31&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9cdf6af658e42c2f4f7dca5e4dbdd3db&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-55e58732610596ce9a8f3145d34f75a7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c14456299df06b01b603504def87f381&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9eb02ab1ab7d834858bf60a8b402e6ea</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Basaglar.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_fiasp.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/Documento sem título.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377211</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Race">
  <data key="d0">Race</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Race is a demographic variable examined in clinical subgroup analyses for Lantus® versus insulin NPH.&lt;SEP&gt;Ethnic classification examined as a subgroup factor in efficacy and safety analyses.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f14ce019f10c2a88765380143498ba5b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-863286c185f2a62e5b28d7e4577a1088</data>
