<node id="Body Mass Index (BMI)">
  <data key="d0">Body Mass Index (BMI)</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Body Mass Index (BMI) is a numerical measure of body fat that is calculated from an individual’s weight and height, expressed in kilograms per square metre (kg/m²). It is widely used as an indicator of body adiposity and to define obesity subgroups in clinical analyses. Standard screening thresholds commonly cited are a BMI of 30 kg/m² to identify obesity, with additional cut‑offs of 25 kg/m² and 23 kg/m² employed in some screening recommendations.

In research settings, BMI serves several specific purposes. It is used to assess the impact of obesity on the efficacy of insulin therapies, such as evaluating how body size influences insulin effect. BMI also functions as a safety and efficacy subgroup factor; for example, participants with a BMI up to 49.6 kg/m² were examined in studies comparing Lantus® (insulin glargine) with insulin NPH. In clinical trials involving adult patients with Type 2 diabetes, the average baseline BMI reported was 34.55 kg/m², and changes in BMI are often recorded as trial outcomes.

Elevated BMI is recognized as a risk factor for post‑transplant diabetes mellitus (PTDM) and other metabolic complications. Consequently, BMI is routinely measured and reported in studies to stratify participants, monitor treatment effects, and guide clinical decision‑making regarding obesity‑related health risks.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f14ce019f10c2a88765380143498ba5b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-133169995b3ab942fd96f1fdfe7269ad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b18f8ab53481bf1b63fda1bb71fe80ec&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2f4f01a72f35d6db3ff333e64f8400ce&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-88b97cde53943160602b20f634ba5c1f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3c6dca13b685243e63fb6f24f7cb301d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ca8741dfdb9ff0f12f049953db6cb9c0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e4e7eef761aec994cc4558b2db5e1e08&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9cdf6af658e42c2f4f7dca5e4dbdd3db</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Basaglar.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_apidra.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_fiasp.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Diagnóstico de diabetes mellitus.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377365</data>
