<node id="Insulin Humana NPH">
  <data key="d0">Insulin Humana NPH</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Insulin Humana NPH is a human intermediate‑acting insulin used as a comparator in studies, administered once or twice daily, demonstrating similar reductions in glycated hemoglobin and fasting glucose but higher nighttime hypoglycemia rates.&lt;SEP&gt;Insulin Humana NPH is an intermediate‑acting human insulin used once or twice daily as basal therapy in the described studies.&lt;SEP&gt;Insulin humana NPH is a human intermediate‑acting insulin referenced in prior‑use data of volunteers.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d87cbe9886e7203b6e7b26c85d60cb9d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-87576da8269707f5f8d929b71470e023&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7a592aedb257bad9532268b4056ec15c</data>
