<node id="Insulin Humana Regular">
  <data key="d0">Insulin Humana Regular</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Insulin Humana Regular is short‑acting human insulin used before meals as needed within basal‑bolus regimens in the studies.&lt;SEP&gt;Insulin Humana Regular is a short‑acting human insulin administered before meals according to need in the basal‑bolus regimen.&lt;SEP&gt;Insulin Humana Regular is a short‑acting insulin given subcutaneously 30–45 minutes before meals, used as a comparator in the studies.&lt;SEP&gt;Insulin Humana Regular is a short‑acting human insulin formulation used as a comparator in pharmacokinetic studies.&lt;SEP&gt;Insulin humana regular is a short‑acting human insulin formulation that reduces blood glucose with a slower onset and longer duration compared to Apidra.&lt;SEP&gt;Regular human insulin is a short‑acting insulin formulation used as a comparator in studies of APIDRA.</data>
