<node id="Sympathomimetic Agents">
  <data key="d0">Sympathomimetic Agents</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Sympathomimetic agents (e.g., epinephrine, salbutamol, terbutaline) can reduce insulin effectiveness.&lt;SEP&gt;Sympathomimetic agents such as epinephrine, salbutamol and terbutaline can diminish the glucose‑lowering effect of insulin.&lt;SEP&gt;Sympathomimetic Agents are drugs that stimulate the sympathetic nervous system, exemplified by epinefrina, salbutamol, and terbutalina.</data>
