  <data key="d2">Clozapine is an atypical antipsychotic cited as diminishing insulin efficacy.&lt;SEP&gt;Clozapine is an atypical antipsychotic that can reduce insulin’s hypoglycemic action.&lt;SEP&gt;Clozapine is an atypical antipsychotic that can decrease insulin’s hypoglycemic effect.&lt;SEP&gt;Clozapine is an atypical antipsychotic that reduces the insulin‑induced reduction of blood glucose.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3db0edd23b6b502ccbbf62bfd601ce68&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d96761d60c65f05f1530bc19b144cf1b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d65840dd2cbd5c9984dfc4334378df5e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f09811b149a29105854a0b1e84951e5d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Basaglar.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_apidra.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786315472</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Clonidine">
  <data key="d0">Clonidine</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Clonidine is an antihypertensive agent that can both increase and decrease insulin effect and may mask hypoglycemia signs.&lt;SEP&gt;Clonidine is a centrally acting antihypertensive that may either increase or decrease insulin’s effect on blood glucose.&lt;SEP&gt;Clonidine is a medication that can both potentiate and weaken the hypoglycemic effect of insulin.&lt;SEP&gt;Clonidine is an α2‑agonist antihypertensive that may reduce insulin‑related hypoglycemia.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3db0edd23b6b502ccbbf62bfd601ce68&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d96761d60c65f05f1530bc19b144cf1b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d65840dd2cbd5c9984dfc4334378df5e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-465ad8b77c1c2a2a179062da20337ff5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f09811b149a29105854a0b1e84951e5d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Basaglar.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_apidra.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786315472</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Lithium Salts">
  <data key="d0">Lithium Salts</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Lithium salts are mood‑stabilizing agents that can modulate insulin’s glucose‑lowering effect.&lt;SEP&gt;Lithium salts are mood‑stabilizing agents that can both potentiate and reduce insulin’s hypoglycemic action.&lt;SEP&gt;Lithium salts are compounds that can both potentiate and weaken the hypoglycemic effect of insulin.&lt;SEP&gt;Lithium salts are chemical compounds that can both potentiate and weaken the hypoglycemic effect of insulin.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3db0edd23b6b502ccbbf62bfd601ce68&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d96761d60c65f05f1530bc19b144cf1b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-465ad8b77c1c2a2a179062da20337ff5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f09811b149a29105854a0b1e84951e5d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Basaglar.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_apidra.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786315473</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Pentamidine">
  <data key="d0">Pentamidine</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Pentamidine is an antimicrobial that can cause hypoglycemia, occasionally followed by hyperglycemia.&lt;SEP&gt;Pentamidine is a medication that may induce hypoglycemia followed by hyperglycemia.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3db0edd23b6b502ccbbf62bfd601ce68&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d96761d60c65f05f1530bc19b144cf1b</data>
