<node id="Metabolite M2 (21A-Gly-des-30B-Thr-insulin)">
  <data key="d0">Metabolite M2 (21A-Gly-des-30B-Thr-insulin)</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Metabolite M2 (21A‑Gly‑des‑30B‑Thr‑insulin) is another active degradation product of insulin glargine present in the bloodstream.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-133169995b3ab942fd96f1fdfe7269ad</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Basaglar.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786310047</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="AUC(0-24)">
  <data key="d0">AUC(0-24)</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">AUC(0‑24) is the area under the serum insulin concentration‑time curve measured from zero to 24 hours for comparative bioavailability analysis.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-133169995b3ab942fd96f1fdfe7269ad</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Basaglar.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786310047</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="0.5 UI/Kg Dose">
  <data key="d0">0.5 UI/Kg Dose</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">0.5 UI/Kg Dose is the single subcutaneous dose administered to healthy volunteers in the euglycemic clamp study.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-133169995b3ab942fd96f1fdfe7269ad</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Basaglar.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786310047</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="0.3 UI/Kg Dose">
  <data key="d0">0.3 UI/Kg Dose</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">0.3 UI/Kg Dose is the subcutaneous dose of insulin glargine given to type 1 diabetes patients for pharmacokinetic observation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-133169995b3ab942fd96f1fdfe7269ad</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Basaglar.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786310047</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Bioavailability">
  <data key="d0">Bioavailability</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Bioavailability denotes the proportion of administered insulin that reaches systemic circulation, reported as approximately 1 for BASAGLAR KWIKPEN relative to Lantus®.&lt;SEP&gt;Bioavailability is the proportion of an administered dose that reaches systemic circulation; APIDRA shows an absolute bioavailability of about 70% after subcutaneous injection.&lt;SEP&gt;Bioavailability measures the proportion of inhaled insulin reaching systemic circulation.&lt;SEP&gt;Bioavailability is the fraction or percentage of an administered drug that reaches the target tissue or blood.&lt;SEP&gt;Bioavailability is the proportion of an administered dose that reaches systemic circulation.&lt;SEP&gt;Bioavailability denotes the degree and rate at which a drug is absorbed, studied in the context of lipid nanoparticles.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-133169995b3ab942fd96f1fdfe7269ad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50719bcc88f4515ec825b9d5a7aba107&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-941c5035ce1f85963f1f564bf2bf73fb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-61a59544bbd02c2c82b13c7808f72c73&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cbb54288f56e407604ea361f58e58233&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-516458dac1dbd08de0719a17162e4979</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Basaglar.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_apidra.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/Inhaling medicines_ delivering drugs to the body through the lungs _ Nature Reviews Drug Discovery.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/edelman-et-al-2026-dosing-afrezza-it-s-not-that-complicated.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/insulina inalavel.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786333598</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Pharmacodynamic Response (Rmax, Gtot)">
  <data key="d0">Pharmacodynamic Response (Rmax, Gtot)</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Pharmacodynamic response, measured by Rmax and Gtot, reflects the glucose‑lowering effect of the insulin formulations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-133169995b3ab942fd96f1fdfe7269ad</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Basaglar.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786310048</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Smokers">
  <data key="d0">Smokers</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Smokers represent a special population for which the effect on insulin glargine pharmacokinetics was not studied.&lt;SEP&gt;Smokers are individuals for whom Afrezza use is not recommended.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-133169995b3ab942fd96f1fdfe7269ad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5419de5a030f812ab408ef47f361bebd</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Basaglar.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/edelman-et-al-2026-dosing-afrezza-it-s-not-that-complicated.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786333259</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Obesity (BMI up to 49.6 kg/m2)">
  <data key="d0">Obesity (BMI up to 49.6 kg/m2)</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Obesity (BMI up to 49.6 kg/m2) is a subgroup analyzed for safety and efficacy, showing no difference between Lantus® and NPH insulin.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-133169995b3ab942fd96f1fdfe7269ad</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Basaglar.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786310048</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="90% Confidence Interval">
  <data key="d0">90% Confidence Interval</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">90% Confidence Interval is the statistical range used to assess bioavailability equivalence between BASAGLAR KWIKPEN and Lantus®.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-133169995b3ab942fd96f1fdfe7269ad</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Basaglar.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786310048</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
