<node id="HUMALOG MIX 50 KWIKPEN">
  <data key="d0">HUMALOG MIX 50 KWIKPEN</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">HUMALOG MIX 50 KWIKPEN is a pharmaceutical formulation that combines insulin lispro with an insulin lispro protamine suspension.&lt;SEP&gt;HUMALOG MIX 50 KWIKPEN is a mixed insulin preparation containing rapid‑acting insulin lispro and a protamine‑crystallized lispro suspension, used for diabetes management.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4319d08c10ed2b48857a6d42eadd9db0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bf25fca295be60e28b7c7d3103f722fc</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_1778357531609.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786310678</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Insulina Lispro Protamina">
  <data key="d0">Insulina Lispro Protamina</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Insulina Lispro Protamina is a protamine‑based suspension combined with Insulina Lispro in the Humalog Mix 25 KwikPen formulation.&lt;SEP&gt;Insulina Lispro Protamina is a protamine‑crystallized suspension of insulin lispro that provides prolonged insulin action.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4319d08c10ed2b48857a6d42eadd9db0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-518838d3c8e8110567b1891b704bfef9</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_1778357531609.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786310678</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Fertility">
  <data key="d0">Fertility</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Fertility denotes the capacity to reproduce; it was not adversely affected by insulin lispro in animal studies.&lt;SEP&gt;Fertility refers to reproductive capability; animal studies showed no difference between Fiasp® and human insulin.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4319d08c10ed2b48857a6d42eadd9db0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d10a1f849386df540104c79e33a7b242</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_1778357531609.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_fiasp.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786316122</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Carcinogenesis">
  <data key="d0">Carcinogenesis</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Carcinogenesis is the potential tumor‑forming effect examined in long‑term animal studies of insulin lispro.&lt;SEP&gt;Carcinogenesis is the process of tumor formation; insulin lispro showed no proliferative or tumor‑inducing effects.&lt;SEP&gt;Carcinogenesis is the process of cancer development, which was not observed with human insulin in studies.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4319d08c10ed2b48857a6d42eadd9db0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a2416b3e5e8ebc96cdb451a794fc78e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0fa819f7e1e42eb688d4894dc3ca7e64</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_1778357531609.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786319728</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Mutagenicity">
  <data key="d0">Mutagenicity</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Mutagenicity refers to the potential of a substance to cause genetic mutations; insulin lispro was not mutagenic in tests.&lt;SEP&gt;Mutagenicity is the potential to cause genetic mutations, evaluated for APIDRA using several assays.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4319d08c10ed2b48857a6d42eadd9db0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4d0e34bef478ed432c8de7ef68dc9025</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_1778357531609.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_apidra.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786315417</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Category B">
  <data key="d0">Category B</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Category B is a pregnancy safety classification indicating limited clinical data but no demonstrated fetal risk.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4319d08c10ed2b48857a6d42eadd9db0</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_1778357531609.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786310680</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Underlying Cardiac Disease">
  <data key="d0">Underlying Cardiac Disease</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Underlying Cardiac Disease refers to pre‑existing heart conditions that may affect insulin therapy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4319d08c10ed2b48857a6d42eadd9db0</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_1778357531609.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786310680</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Chronic Toxicity Test">
  <data key="d0">Chronic Toxicity Test</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Chronic Toxicity Test is a long‑term safety study evaluating adverse effects of a substance over extended exposure.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4319d08c10ed2b48857a6d42eadd9db0</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_1778357531609.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786310680</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="In Vitro Test">
  <data key="d0">In Vitro Test</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">In Vitro Test is an experimental assay performed outside a living organism, often used to assess mutagenicity.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4319d08c10ed2b48857a6d42eadd9db0</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_1778357531609.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786310680</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="In Vivo Test">
  <data key="d0">In Vivo Test</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">In Vivo Test is an experimental study conducted in living organisms to evaluate safety and efficacy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4319d08c10ed2b48857a6d42eadd9db0</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_1778357531609.pdf</data>
