</node>
<node id="Volume of Distribution">
  <data key="d0">Volume of Distribution</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Volume of distribution is a pharmacokinetic parameter indicating the extent to which insulin distributes in the body after injection.&lt;SEP&gt;Volume of distribution is a pharmacokinetic parameter indicating the theoretical volume in which a drug would need to be uniformly distributed to produce the observed blood concentration.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bf25fca295be60e28b7c7d3103f722fc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fb0fb965e5ddd796999856ca376d4b9d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_1778357531609.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786310683</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
