</node>
<node id="Alergia Local">
  <data key="d0">Alergia Local</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Alergia Local denotes allergic reactions occurring at the injection site, such as redness, swelling, or itching.&lt;SEP&gt;Local allergy is an adverse reaction at the injection site characterized by redness, swelling, and itching.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-aca0b919135813e1d5b772face36989d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-929e31613caadc967412041c8c2155b3</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_1778357531609.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786319689</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Alergia Sistêmica">
  <data key="d0">Alergia Sistêmica</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Alergia Sistêmica denotes a generalized insulin allergy that can cause widespread rash, dyspnea, hypotension, and potentially death.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-aca0b919135813e1d5b772face36989d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_1778357531609.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786310753</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Glucose Oral">
  <data key="d0">Glucose Oral</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Glucose Oral is an oral glucose preparation used to treat mild hypoglycemia.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-aca0b919135813e1d5b772face36989d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_1778357531609.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786310753</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Prurido">
  <data key="d0">Prurido</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Prurido denotes itching at the injection site, listed among local skin reactions.&lt;SEP&gt;Prurido is itching at the injection site linked to Levemir® administration.&lt;SEP&gt;Prurido is an itching symptom mentioned as a possible injection‑site reaction.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-aca0b919135813e1d5b772face36989d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9bcc4202330d45ebfca8f79c3d4998b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8a68ba1e8cc1defda76cde0eff9592e6</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_1778357531609.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786317652</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Erupção Cutânea">
  <data key="d0">Erupção Cutânea</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Erupção Cutânea refers to skin rash occurring locally or systemically after insulin injection.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-aca0b919135813e1d5b772face36989d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_1778357531609.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786310753</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Apatia">
  <data key="d0">Apatia</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Apatia is a symptom of severe hypoglycemia described in the superdose section.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-aca0b919135813e1d5b772face36989d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_1778357531609.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786310753</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Confusão">
  <data key="d0">Confusão</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Confusão is a symptom of severe hypoglycemia described in the superdose section.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-aca0b919135813e1d5b772face36989d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_1778357531609.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786310754</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Palpitações">
  <data key="d0">Palpitações</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Palpitações denotes heart palpitations as a symptom of severe hypoglycemia.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-aca0b919135813e1d5b772face36989d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_1778357531609.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786310754</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Vômito">
  <data key="d0">Vômito</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Vômito is a symptom of severe hypoglycemia mentioned in the superdose description.&lt;SEP&gt;Vômito is an intercurrent illness that can predispose a patient to hypoglycemia.&lt;SEP&gt;Vômito is vomiting, a common symptom of severe ketoacidosis.&lt;SEP&gt;Expulsão do conteúdo gástrico, complicação da cetoacidose.&lt;SEP&gt;Vomiting, listed as a condition indicating the need for a ketone test.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-aca0b919135813e1d5b772face36989d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9cd336474a2e9457985162b1ddb4b603&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fb0cd81f0439cbb74e3c0ff54236c45d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cbe87fd92ad66dcb02b25b669d829f6c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5dce7a759a9de18a4d1bcc77a071fbe2</data>
