<node id="Basal Insulin">
  <data key="d0">Basal Insulin</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Basal insulin is a low‑dose, long‑acting form of insulin that provides continuous, background coverage of glucose metabolism over a 24‑hour period. By mimicking the low‑level secretion of a healthy pancreas, basal insulin supplies a steady supply of hormone that maintains fasting and inter‑meal glucose within target ranges when a person is at rest, during sleep, and throughout the day. In clinical practice it is administered subcutaneously, most commonly as insulin glargine, insulin detemir (e.g., Levemir®), or similar long‑acting analogues, and may be delivered once or twice daily. It can also be infused continuously by an insulin pump, where the basal dose is automatically resumed after any suspension and may be limited by safety features such as SmartGuard, which can sustain delivery up to a preset maximum for several hours.

Basal insulin constitutes the essential “backdrop” of many diabetes treatment regimens, typically representing about 30‑50 % of the total daily insulin dose. It may be used alone as the background component or combined with rapid‑acting or bolus insulins (e.g., insulin lispro, Fiasp®) that address post‑prandial glucose excursions. The steady, low‑level delivery of basal insulin therefore supports stable glucose levels for patients initiating insulin therapy as well as for those who have been on insulin for some time. In research studies, basal insulin formulations often serve as the comparator arm for newer rapid‑acting products and are evaluated in trials that incorporate continuous glucose monitoring (CGM) or flash glucose monitoring, particularly in type 2 diabetes cohorts.

Because basal insulin provides the constant background insulin needed to maintain baseline glucose control, it must be correctly set before adding other therapies such as inhaled insulin (Afrezza) or other adjunctive agents. Its role as the background insulin dose is recognized across diabetes management guidelines and is a core element of both type 1 and type 2 diabetes treatment strategies.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-97208e231aa338c60205244ac12e0492&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-77dc1a2378f763ffabe8fa379881d1cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c8c7e36686d077dcb6239405f60ea031&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7fdc648ec086061141581e27adde6fc4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5e7e47ca39ac4f4975da2b4b7e6d3c36&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-56fc1d5df1b34d9120c3cf8a760c40f9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c96221c60c19f02ac6efa6a987b1e15b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b7715667f5fca178f0988984e932ecfb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5913d17c337be62cd526d46fbdcd9a6e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6b867cec4c5eed3b10e431cbd4078dee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3d24fce6aa8866fb4a11514ae0e4d675&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-83bb94d08bdb958eff25f76c9a6ac18a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d68acc5f59d78c14cf4d2e4d34edf5e4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b03b7fdf0dd9c96dc459929ccccdccff&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a0267d2986a48c4c31790b6f183277dc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-92417ae942a11c591feb2ee9b5fadd7e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d4d222786e6ed163a90874659266c72a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1c5a5c97986d9b31b155b0c8f0cac1c5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8741750a7bf86eb5d1fadf82a9c7720e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c7e6ef38db0b62d161b13473af47d738&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ca8620e735c40bfe850134ccea9a7154&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0f272d1c9c38e2a6b6d02b5aa66809e1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0932e9c21a330869629b3fa70d2e1f5e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-06425d1f80d868bd58871b6a6e740102&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4655f823785fa91e72cba96e00dba34c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9cd925790899146eeb8a373879b5feac&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-40c2c862887db201b07c741a1862dcc1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-511f6be03d2ea98970bd4c1b29b3e5c8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-41b7df11ccfb12f819e6f60481970587&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0fe1eff7b58582dec4c8ae7578e20e66&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e0d0e5c511e72e62db88a57fa6ea198e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d3a9b76fabae2f788f96d06b7d98c924</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Toujeo.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_apidra.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_fiasp.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/Documento sem título.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/Insulinoterapia – Diretriz da Sociedade Brasileira de Diabetes – Ed. 2024.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/Understanding insulin - International Diabetes Federation.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/edelman-et-al-2026-dosing-afrezza-it-s-not-that-complicated.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/blood glucose monitoring.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786335900</data>
