<node id="Prandial Insulin">
  <data key="d0">Prandial Insulin</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Prandial insulin refers to rapid‑acting insulins (glulisina, lispro, aspart) administered with meals.&lt;SEP&gt;Prandial insulin refers to rapid‑acting insulin administered around meals to control post‑prandial glucose spikes.&lt;SEP&gt;Prandial insulin refers to insulin administered around meals to control postprandial glucose excursions.&lt;SEP&gt;Prandial insulin is insulin administered at mealtime to control post‑meal glucose spikes.&lt;SEP&gt;Prandial insulin refers to insulin taken around meals, noted as having timing issues compared to Afrezza.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7d9c944d51a42525c017d9109f46684c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fd6fa98b7767319460b4a421a719c5c2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f9416e8076c17175db0dbb12c3393566&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4e6371d8083fb20b137912cdaeec1b8b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-70c5a1107fcc9b632361d9c52064f45d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Toujeo.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/Insulinoterapia – Diretriz da Sociedade Brasileira de Diabetes – Ed. 2024.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/edelman-et-al-2026-dosing-afrezza-it-s-not-that-complicated.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786333244</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Glomerular Filtration Rate">
  <data key="d0">Glomerular Filtration Rate</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Glomerular Filtration Rate is a measure of kidney filtration used to categorize renal function (&lt;60 or ≥60 mL/min/1.73 m²).&lt;SEP&gt;Glomerular Filtration Rate is a measure of kidney function that may affect drug dosing in transplant patients.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7d9c944d51a42525c017d9109f46684c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e4e7eef761aec994cc4558b2db5e1e08</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Toujeo.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377339</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Obesity">
  <data key="d0">Obesity</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Obesity is a clinical condition characterized by an excess of body fat, typically identified and quantified using the body‑mass index (BMI). In medical research and drug development, obesity is frequently examined as a subgroup variable, such as in safety and efficacy analyses of insulin formulations, where participants are stratified by BMI to assess pharmacodynamic and pharmacokinetic differences. The condition is also noted for its impact on insulin demand; individuals with obesity often require higher insulin dosages, a factor that influences dosing recommendations for products like Novolin® R FlexPen®.  

In addition to its role in diabetes management, obesity is recognized as a risk factor that can modify the effects of other therapeutic agents, including HIV protease inhibitors, where excess body weight may alter drug distribution and efficacy. Clinicians also consider obesity a key screening criterion for type 2 diabetes in children and adolescents, reflecting its contribution to the development of insulin resistance and the broader metabolic syndrome. Consequently, obesity is commonly listed among the clinical characteristics associated with the presentation and progression of diabetes, underscoring its importance in both preventive screening and therapeutic decision‑making.&lt;SEP&gt;Increased body weight that, while not typical at Type 1 Diabetes onset, is becoming common and should not exclude testing for the disease.&lt;SEP&gt;Obesity denotes a higher level of excess body fat, associated with insulin resistance and increased risk of type 2 diabetes.&lt;SEP&gt;Excess body fat, identified as a risk factor and common condition among those with Type 2 Diabetes.&lt;SEP&gt;Obesity is a condition that, together with overweight, qualifies adults for diabetes screening.&lt;SEP&gt;Obesity is an ongoing epidemic contributing to increased type 2 diabetes among people of reproductive age.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7d9c944d51a42525c017d9109f46684c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-42b9c5d97c54f39fb69bb1169e1de4d2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2f4f01a72f35d6db3ff333e64f8400ce&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2cd48799a027437b9fe2e1a48b61cb3d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-336c6084eb6cb7c8ada29ed26c0cd20d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-343246c2eef6e8430b581340d6cd4762&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-429fba9c3900b6d0b0c3ccfb38323e54&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e4adabacd09697393ca15fc999724c51&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2752a78fbaafd94ca566ff099a4ba551&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-55e58732610596ce9a8f3145d34f75a7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-83d72fbc44fe0c28f27702c0d4f2c140&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1a111d4b40ec241cf54126f594a80308&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9eb02ab1ab7d834858bf60a8b402e6ea</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Toujeo.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_fiasp.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Diagnóstico de diabetes mellitus.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377347</data>
