</node>
<node id="Needle Obstruction">
  <data key="d0">Needle Obstruction</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Needle obstruction is the blockage that can occur when a reused needle becomes clogged, potentially leading to dosing errors.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3397508bdfddde019cb1dfdcfb352435</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Toujeo.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786313562</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Dosage Error">
  <data key="d0">Dosage Error</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Dosage error encompasses sub‑dosage or over‑dosage events that may result from improper needle handling or device misuse.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3397508bdfddde019cb1dfdcfb352435</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Toujeo.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786313563</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Dose Counter">
  <data key="d0">Dose Counter</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The dose counter is the visual display on the insulin pen that shows the number of units selected for injection.&lt;SEP&gt;The dose counter is a feature of the SoloStar pen that displays the number of units to be injected.&lt;SEP&gt;The dose counter displays the remaining insulin units on an insulin pen.&lt;SEP&gt;Dose Counter is the display on the application system that shows the number of insulin units selected and returns to zero after injection.&lt;SEP&gt;The dose counter displays the selected insulin dose numerically.</data>
