<node id="New England Journal of Medicine">
  <data key="d0">New England Journal of Medicine</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">New England Journal of Medicine (N Engl J Med) is a leading, peer‑reviewed medical journal that publishes original, high‑impact clinical research across a broad range of specialties. It is widely recognized for disseminating landmark studies that shape medical practice and policy.  

The journal has been cited for several pivotal diabetes investigations, including the ORIGIN Trial, multiple intensive‑treatment studies, and research on intranasal aerosolized insulin for type 1 diabetes. In addition, New England Journal of Medicine published the 2025 randomized trial evaluating automated insulin delivery systems, further underscoring its role as a primary source for cutting‑edge diabetes research.  

Overall, New England Journal of Medicine serves as a premier venue for influential clinical evidence, regularly referenced for its contributions to diabetes care and numerous other areas of medicine.&lt;SEP&gt;NEJM published the multicenter randomized trial of treatment for mild gestational diabetes and other key studies.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-42b9c5d97c54f39fb69bb1169e1de4d2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-61a59544bbd02c2c82b13c7808f72c73&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e7e6ca9bf63e843b814736c0409c70fb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d30bfc1840eec64224c3568470e6c539&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f35eed8b49aa0b698012777f6ec96ce5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6db2125b1b94840ea29100039a6fef20&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e668c40e3bc21d982ed03a052f0f9339&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-54ce8d1437c0ec0329819123568df11e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fedb8cdc485be3c8e38133ddb9ea67cf</data>
