  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Glucose infusion rate is the amount of glucose administered to maintain constant plasma glucose levels during clamp studies.&lt;SEP&gt;Glucose Infusion Rate is the amount of glucose infused per hour to maintain constant plasma glucose levels during the clamp study.&lt;SEP&gt;Glucose infusion rate is the rate at which glucose is infused during euglycemic studies to assess insulin action.</data>
