  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Skeletal Muscle">
  <data key="d0">Skeletal Muscle</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Skeletal muscle is a major peripheral tissue that uptake glucose in response to insulin signaling.&lt;SEP&gt;Skeletal muscle is a tissue where insulin‑mediated glucose uptake occurs.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-afc28422755c2c44f931bab7b6a2b477&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1bb9ea85b9ad8cd6940ae41a3ab5d1fd</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Toujeo.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_fiasp.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786316079</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Liver">
  <data key="d0">Liver</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Liver is a central organ in glucose metabolism, responsible for hepatic glucose production (gluconeogenesis) and the regulation of blood‑sugar levels. Insulin acts on the liver to inhibit gluconeogenesis, promote glucose uptake, and stimulate the conversion of glucose into glycogen for storage. Conversely, when insulin levels fall and glucagon rises, the liver breaks down its glycogen stores and releases glucose back into the bloodstream to meet the body’s energy demands.

The liver therefore serves as a dynamic reservoir of glucose. It stores excess glucose as glycogen after meals, under the influence of insulin, and releases that glucose during periods of fasting, between meals, or during sleep, ensuring a continuous supply of fuel for peripheral tissues. This dual role—storing glucose when it is abundant and producing or releasing it when it is scarce—makes the liver essential for maintaining normal glucose homeostasis.&lt;SEP&gt;Liver is an organ from which extracts were tested and found to have no effect on blood sugar.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-afc28422755c2c44f931bab7b6a2b477&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1bb9ea85b9ad8cd6940ae41a3ab5d1fd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2378c57a337d1ce7103c7086ebba76ac&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a1245bd9ff75c998b49dab861cc4cebf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b7715667f5fca178f0988984e932ecfb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-65c6beab51324e055f4a39b388e2eefe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9f4d152d83c514f926b18413e065c2fa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-780f90d656277126a05ed136a084fd77&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6b867cec4c5eed3b10e431cbd4078dee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-172719b5694ed1fb8003b6874395d641</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Toujeo.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_fiasp.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/The Discovery and Development.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786332072</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="SANOFI">
  <data key="d0">SANOFI</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">SANOFI is the pharmaceutical company referenced as the source of flexible dosing schedule data.&lt;SEP&gt;SANOFI is the pharmaceutical company that produces Toujeo insulin and the SoloStar pen.</data>
