  <data key="d0">Toujeo 300 U/Ml</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Toujeo 300 U/mL is an insulin formulation intended for administration with a SoloStar pen, delivering up to 450 units per pen.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7638273060df996ad502ec2fadfc9c82</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Toujeo.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786313600</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="External Needle Cap">
  <data key="d0">External Needle Cap</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The external cap is placed on the needle after use to protect the needle and allow safe removal.&lt;SEP&gt;External Needle Cap is the outer protective cap of the needle that is removed before injection.&lt;SEP&gt;External Needle Cap is the outer protective cap used to unscrew the needle from the SoloStar.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7638273060df996ad502ec2fadfc9c82&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e9835d6684db67541402527b3182b6c5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-79f891b1d7c0c6ca0eab9dbcc76c902d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Toujeo.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_apidra.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786315498</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Internal Needle Cap">
  <data key="d0">Internal Needle Cap</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The internal cap is the inner needle cap that should never be re‑attached after needle removal.&lt;SEP&gt;Internal Needle Cap is the inner protective cap of the needle that is removed and discarded after use.&lt;SEP&gt;Internal Needle Cap is the inner protective cap that should not be reattached to avoid accidental needle injury.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7638273060df996ad502ec2fadfc9c82&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e9835d6684db67541402527b3182b6c5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-79f891b1d7c0c6ca0eab9dbcc76c902d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Toujeo.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_apidra.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786315498</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Dosage Selector">
  <data key="d0">Dosage Selector</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The dosage selector is a dial that is turned until the pointer indicates the desired number of insulin units.&lt;SEP&gt;Dosage Selector is the rotary mechanism on the SoloStar that allows the user to choose the number of insulin units to inject.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7638273060df996ad502ec2fadfc9c82&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e9835d6684db67541402527b3182b6c5</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Toujeo.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_apidra.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786315497</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Dosage Window">
  <data key="d0">Dosage Window</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The dosage window displays the selected dose and returns to “0” after the injection is completed.&lt;SEP&gt;Dosage Window is the display on SoloStar showing the selected dose, resetting to zero after injection.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7638273060df996ad502ec2fadfc9c82&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ffe095bda1b787c5b5ae2d61a2f74c98</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Toujeo.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_apidra.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786315486</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Safety Test">
  <data key="d0">Safety Test</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The safety test is performed before injection to verify that the needle is attached and the dosage window reads “0”.&lt;SEP&gt;Safety Test is the pre‑injection check recommended for each use of the Caneta SoloStar pen.&lt;SEP&gt;Safety Test is a procedure performed by tapping the insulin reservoir and pressing the injection button to ensure insulin reaches the needle and to detect air bubbles.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7638273060df996ad502ec2fadfc9c82&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d7223c781e745e72311fccfcdd58583&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ffe095bda1b787c5b5ae2d61a2f74c98</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Toujeo.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_apidra.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786315486</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Dose Selection">
  <data key="d0">Dose Selection</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Dose selection is the step in which the user sets the desired insulin units using the selector and confirms the window reading.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7638273060df996ad502ec2fadfc9c82</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Toujeo.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786313605</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Injecting Dose">
  <data key="d0">Injecting Dose</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Injecting dose is the step where the user presses the injection button to deliver insulin, counts to five, and watches the window return to “0”.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7638273060df996ad502ec2fadfc9c82</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Toujeo.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786313606</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Needle Removal and Disposal">
  <data key="d0">Needle Removal and Disposal</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Needle removal and disposal is the step that involves replacing the external cap, twisting the pen to detach the needle, and discarding the needle in a puncture‑proof container.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7638273060df996ad502ec2fadfc9c82</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Toujeo.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786313606</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Toujeo 300 U/mL">
  <data key="d0">Toujeo 300 U/mL</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Toujeo 300 U/mL is a commercial formulation of insulin glargine that contains 300 units of the hormone per milliliter. It is supplied as a clear, color‑less solution in a disposable SoloStar pen, which is designed for subcutaneous injection. The high‑concentration, low‑solubility preparation at neutral pH creates a depot from which insulin is released slowly and steadily, providing a prolonged, basal glucose‑lowering effect.

As a long‑acting human insulin analogue, Toujeo 300 U/mL is indicated for the treatment of diabetes mellitus, particularly in adults with type 2 diabetes, and may be used in various patient groups requiring basal insulin support. The formulation is typically administered once daily, although it can be incorporated into multiple‑daily‑injection regimens as part of comprehensive diabetes management. Its pharmacokinetic profile offers a more constant and predictable insulin release compared with earlier glargine products, helping to reduce glycaemic variability and improve overall glycaemic control.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-97208e231aa338c60205244ac12e0492&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3397508bdfddde019cb1dfdcfb352435&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-afc28422755c2c44f931bab7b6a2b477&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7e7d46c64175d3f9ecf44672130dc3cd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-93623071acdcd0ba060c8826ab5a2a81&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e8934881ec5ab7cfeb836126b3f0e8b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-78f859befb6230d94e8af9144794e0d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-228b9514d97e62787d4a60078f932ceb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-78b302b74d715df9c3b9e9db38fa4c64&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-56fb3d61e8c32af5d6b8be06cc54f904&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d6b9a8472aefa6e90793233284c15a3f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1ee5400065df79b02b6c04efc0f4854d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Toujeo.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786313608</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
