<node id="Fasting Plasma Glucose (FPG)">
  <data key="d0">Fasting Plasma Glucose (FPG)</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Fasting glucose levels that decreased comparably with Toujeo 300 U/mL and insulin glargine 100 U/mL in the pediatric study.&lt;SEP&gt;Fasting Plasma Glucose is a blood glucose measurement taken after an overnight fast, used for diabetes screening.&lt;SEP&gt;A blood test measuring glucose after an overnight fast used to diagnose diabetes.&lt;SEP&gt;Fasting Plasma Glucose (FPG) is a blood glucose measurement used for diabetes diagnosis, with specific thresholds in Stage 3.&lt;SEP&gt;FPG is a plasma glucose measurement taken after fasting, mentioned as subject to preanalytic variability.&lt;SEP&gt;Blood glucose measurement after fasting, with diagnostic thresholds of 100–125 mg/dL for IFG.&lt;SEP&gt;Fasting plasma glucose (FPG) is a blood test suggested as suitable for pediatric diabetes diagnosis.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-863286c185f2a62e5b28d7e4577a1088&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a05276c5db43e3a1e9f987056012750f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6601fea85bfbb9f20040c70b7e21695d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ca8741dfdb9ff0f12f049953db6cb9c0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3cc61bc2e95346d553972b4371912e7f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ba38023866c2db7437e618a60033f21f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0631ff2b95dd459677eaaebe9283a776</data>
