<node id="Cardiovascular Disease">
  <data key="d0">Cardiovascular Disease</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Cardiovascular Disease (CVD) denotes a broad class of conditions that affect the heart and the blood vessels. It encompasses both established heart disorders and vascular diseases, and is frequently referenced in clinical studies and randomized trials as a key health outcome.

In the context of diabetes research, CVD is repeatedly identified as a major comorbid condition. Intensive diabetes treatment protocols, glycemic goal individualization, and therapy selection often consider the presence or risk of cardiovascular disease, recognizing that high HbA1c levels are associated with increased heart and vascular complications. Consequently, CVD influences decisions about diabetes management and serves as an important endpoint when evaluating the benefits of intensive versus standard glycemic control.

Overall, cardiovascular disease functions as a critical comorbidity in study populations, guiding both the design of clinical trials and the personalization of treatment strategies for patients with diabetes.&lt;SEP&gt;Cardiovascular Disease is a health risk associated with prediabetes and type 2 diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-76df79998cbb923bc6c94e375c220eac&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e7e6ca9bf63e843b814736c0409c70fb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-22078404beeceb5adc3e688d239c585e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fc59aba81df88fe020f6e1d93d9e403b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e668c40e3bc21d982ed03a052f0f9339&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-38ab5af7e42588297df4330ffb2c046b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-36ddeaa53bc38bee375d7ac6d71485d4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aff91698679a52cd7b07563b7b2627a3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2a430bf53157529ccb22e67171fb28e5</data>
