<node id="Excipients">
  <data key="d0">Excipients</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Excipients are the inactive ingredients incorporated into pharmaceutical dosage forms, serving functions such as adding bulk, enhancing stability, masking taste, improving injectability, reducing aggregation, increasing dispersibility, and prolonging dissolution. As non‑active components, they are deliberately selected to support the performance, safety, and patient acceptability of the drug product while not contributing therapeutic activity.

In insulin products, specific excipients are listed for each formulation. The long‑acting insulin glargine preparation Toujeo contains metacresol, glycerol, hydrochloric acid, sodium hydroxide, zinc chloride, and water. The rapid‑acting insulin glulisine marketed as APIDRA (including the Apidra SoloStar pen) includes metacresol, trometamol, sodium chloride, polysorbate 20, sodium hydroxide, concentrated hydrochloric acid, and water for injectable use. Similar excipient profiles are noted for APIDRA’s injectable solution, reflecting the same set of inactive substances. Other insulin brands such as Levemir®, Novolin® R, and the inhaled formulation Afrezza list excipients generically, emphasizing that they are present in the insulin formulation and may be responsible for hypersensitivity reactions.

Across these products, the inactive ingredients are recognized as potential triggers of hypersensitivity or allergic responses in some patients. While excipients are essential for the physical and chemical integrity of insulin preparations, clinicians and patients should be aware that reactions—ranging from mild irritation to more pronounced immune responses—can be attributed to these non‑active components.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-78b302b74d715df9c3b9e9db38fa4c64&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-162882e6afffb0db8ae5e9153e5f1e82&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-77dc1a2378f763ffabe8fa379881d1cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8ef15154a94043650617b3b24d8146a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dd396c45bc09fb646d156b4e69d328e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea9b3836b3275f451c3acfb189f42a6f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e337602a6f677dde49f4899bab5a07c9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4e6371d8083fb20b137912cdaeec1b8b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Toujeo.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_apidra.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/Inhaling medicines_ delivering drugs to the body through the lungs _ Nature Reviews Drug Discovery.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/edelman-et-al-2026-dosing-afrezza-it-s-not-that-complicated.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786333257</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Subcutaneous Use">
  <data key="d0">Subcutaneous Use</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Subcutaneous use denotes the route of administration for Toujeo 300 U/mL.&lt;SEP&gt;Subcutaneous use denotes the injection route for Apidra SoloStar, delivering insulin into the fatty tissue under the skin.&lt;SEP&gt;Subcutaneous use refers to delivering insulin into the tissue just beneath the skin.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-78b302b74d715df9c3b9e9db38fa4c64&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-162882e6afffb0db8ae5e9153e5f1e82&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9ec9cae555a06ac660e6c16d90116c8b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Toujeo.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_apidra.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329626</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Adult and Pediatric Use (≥6 Years)">
  <data key="d0">Adult and Pediatric Use (≥6 Years)</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Toujeo 300 U/mL is indicated for adults and children aged six years and older.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-78b302b74d715df9c3b9e9db38fa4c64</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Toujeo.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786313661</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Flexible Dosing Window">
  <data key="d0">Flexible Dosing Window</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Flexible dosing allows administration within three hours before or after the usual injection time without affecting glycemic control.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-78b302b74d715df9c3b9e9db38fa4c64</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Toujeo.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786313661</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Rapid‑acting Insulin Analogue">
  <data key="d0">Rapid‑acting Insulin Analogue</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The rapid‑acting insulin analogue is administered before each meal in the study regimen.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-78b302b74d715df9c3b9e9db38fa4c64</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Toujeo.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786313661</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="HbA1c Target (&lt;7%)">
  <data key="d0">HbA1c Target (&lt;7%)</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The target HbA1c value of below 7 % is used as a therapeutic goal in the trials.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-78b302b74d715df9c3b9e9db38fa4c64</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Toujeo.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786313661</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Body Weight Change (&lt;1 kg)">
  <data key="d0">Body Weight Change (&lt;1 kg)</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A mean body weight change of less than 1 kg was observed after six months of treatment with Toujeo 300 U/mL.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-78b302b74d715df9c3b9e9db38fa4c64</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Toujeo.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786313661</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Body Mass Index (IMC)">
  <data key="d0">Body Mass Index (IMC)</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Body mass index (IMC) is reported as a baseline characteristic influencing HbA1c response.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-78b302b74d715df9c3b9e9db38fa4c64</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Toujeo.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786313661</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Insulina Humana De Longa Duração">
  <data key="d0">Insulina Humana De Longa Duração</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Insulina humana de longa duração refers to the class of insulin to which Toujeo belongs.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-56fb3d61e8c32af5d6b8be06cc54f904</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Toujeo.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786313661</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Insulina De Rápida/Curta Ação">
  <data key="d0">Insulina De Rápida/Curta Ação</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Insulina de rápida/curta ação is a fast‑acting insulin that should be combined with Toujeo during meals for type‑1 diabetes patients.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-56fb3d61e8c32af5d6b8be06cc54f904</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Toujeo.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786313661</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Anti‑hiperglicêmicos">
  <data key="d0">Anti‑hiperglicêmicos</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Anti‑hiperglicêmicos are medications that lower blood glucose and may be co‑administered with Toujeo in type‑2 diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-56fb3d61e8c32af5d6b8be06cc54f904</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Toujeo.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786313662</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Embalagem Original">
  <data key="d0">Embalagem Original</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Embalagem original is the original packaging in which the medication and pen should be kept.&lt;SEP&gt;The original packaging is the container in which Levemir® FlexPen® should be kept to protect it from light and contamination.&lt;SEP&gt;Embalagem original is the original container that should be used to store Novolin® R to maintain its integrity.&lt;SEP&gt;Embalagem Original is the original packaging required for storage and transport of the medication.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-56fb3d61e8c32af5d6b8be06cc54f904&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a49c8461f43dc12d7df9c921efeb0465&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0689fd73d2061ee466b9b90e03bda141&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ba6b31518be6fff1db8b68a28e82f200</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Toujeo.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786318539</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Temperatura Até 30ºC">
  <data key="d0">Temperatura Até 30ºC</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Temperatura até 30ºC indicates the maximum ambient temperature allowed for storing the pen.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-56fb3d61e8c32af5d6b8be06cc54f904</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Toujeo.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786313662</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Luz E Calor">
  <data key="d0">Luz E Calor</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Luz e calor denote environmental factors from which the pen must be protected.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-56fb3d61e8c32af5d6b8be06cc54f904</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Toujeo.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786313662</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Dose Diária Inicial Recomendada de 0,2 U/Kg">
  <data key="d0">Dose Diária Inicial Recomendada de 0,2 U/Kg</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Dose diária inicial recomendada de 0,2 U/Kg is the starting daily dose for Toujeo in type‑2 diabetes patients.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-56fb3d61e8c32af5d6b8be06cc54f904</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Toujeo.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786313662</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Dose Única Habitual Diária">
  <data key="d0">Dose Única Habitual Diária</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Dose única habitual diária refers to the regular once‑daily dose that patients should not double if an injection is missed.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-56fb3d61e8c32af5d6b8be06cc54f904</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Toujeo.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786313662</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Anti‑Hiperglicêmicos">
  <data key="d0">Anti‑Hiperglicêmicos</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Anti‑hiperglicêmicos are medications that lower blood glucose and may be co‑administered with Toujeo in type‑2 diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-56fb3d61e8c32af5d6b8be06cc54f904</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Toujeo.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786313663</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Dose Diária Inicial Recomendada De 0,2 U/Kg">
  <data key="d0">Dose Diária Inicial Recomendada De 0,2 U/Kg</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Dose diária inicial recomendada de 0,2 U/Kg is the starting daily dose for Toujeo in type‑2 diabetes patients.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-56fb3d61e8c32af5d6b8be06cc54f904</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Toujeo.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786313663</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Número De Lote">
  <data key="d0">Número De Lote</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Número de lote is the batch identification number printed on the medication packaging.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-56fb3d61e8c32af5d6b8be06cc54f904</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Toujeo.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786313663</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Validade De 36 Meses">
  <data key="d0">Validade De 36 Meses</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Validade de 36 meses indicates the product’s shelf life of 36 months from the manufacturing date.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-56fb3d61e8c32af5d6b8be06cc54f904</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Toujeo.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786313663</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Período De Uso Após Abertura De 6 Semanas (42 Dias)">
  <data key="d0">Período De Uso Após Abertura De 6 Semanas (42 Dias)</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">After opening, the pen remains valid for 6 weeks (42 days) when protected from light and heat.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-56fb3d61e8c32af5d6b8be06cc54f904</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Toujeo.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786313663</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Insulina Intermediária">
  <data key="d0">Insulina Intermediária</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Insulina intermediária is an insulin with intermediate duration, referenced when switching to Toujeo.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-56fb3d61e8c32af5d6b8be06cc54f904</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Toujeo.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786313663</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Monitorização Metabólica Cuidadosa">
  <data key="d0">Monitorização Metabólica Cuidadosa</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Monitorização metabólica cuidadosa is careful metabolic monitoring recommended during therapy changes and the initial weeks.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-56fb3d61e8c32af5d6b8be06cc54f904</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Toujeo.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786313663</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Peso">
  <data key="d0">Peso</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Peso (weight) changes may necessitate adjustments in the insulin dose.&lt;SEP&gt;Patient’s weight, used as a variable in insulin dose calculations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-56fb3d61e8c32af5d6b8be06cc54f904&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-60530d1861f7c2d1efecc069c0913d37</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Toujeo.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786330161</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Estilo De Vida">
  <data key="d0">Estilo De Vida</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Estilo de vida alterations may require insulin dose modifications.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-56fb3d61e8c32af5d6b8be06cc54f904</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Toujeo.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786313664</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Advertências E Precauções">
  <data key="d0">Advertências E Precauções</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Advertências e precauções is the section containing warnings and precautions for the medication.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-56fb3d61e8c32af5d6b8be06cc54f904</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Toujeo.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786313664</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Posologia E Modo De Usar">
  <data key="d0">Posologia E Modo De Usar</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Posologia e modo de usar describes the dosage regimen and administration method for Toujeo.&lt;SEP&gt;Posologia E Modo De Usar is the section providing dosage and administration instructions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-56fb3d61e8c32af5d6b8be06cc54f904&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-759c20cc4c3fc0d3529aabc2fe7dbf99</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Toujeo.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786317645</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Flexibilidade No Horário Da Administração">
  <data key="d0">Flexibilidade No Horário Da Administração</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Flexibilidade no horário da administração allows dosing up to 3 hours before or after the usual injection time.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-56fb3d61e8c32af5d6b8be06cc54f904</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Toujeo.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786313664</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Euglycemic Clamp Study (36 Hours)">
  <data key="d0">Euglycemic Clamp Study (36 Hours)</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The Euglycemic Clamp Study lasting 36 hours is a research method used to maintain constant plasma glucose levels while assessing insulin activity.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d6b9a8472aefa6e90793233284c15a3f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Toujeo.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786313664</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Figure 1 – Activity Profile">
  <data key="d0">Figure 1 – Activity Profile</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Figure 1 illustrates the activity profile of patients with type 1 diabetes during the study.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d6b9a8472aefa6e90793233284c15a3f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Toujeo.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786313664</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Patients with Type 1 Diabetes">
  <data key="d0">Patients with Type 1 Diabetes</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Patients with type 1 diabetes are study participants evaluated for insulin pharmacokinetics and pharmacodynamics.&lt;SEP&gt;Patients with Type 1 Diabetes are individuals who require rapid‑acting insulin for mealtime glucose control and may use Afrezza.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d6b9a8472aefa6e90793233284c15a3f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4e6371d8083fb20b137912cdaeec1b8b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Toujeo.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/edelman-et-al-2026-dosing-afrezza-it-s-not-that-complicated.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786333246</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="AUC (Area Under the Curve)">
  <data key="d0">AUC (Area Under the Curve)</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">AUC is a pharmacokinetic metric representing exposure to insulin or its metabolites over time.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d6b9a8472aefa6e90793233284c15a3f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Toujeo.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786313664</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Therapeutic Equilibrium">
  <data key="d0">Therapeutic Equilibrium</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Therapeutic equilibrium is the steady‑state condition reached after several days of daily Toujeo administration.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d6b9a8472aefa6e90793233284c15a3f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Toujeo.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786313664</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Intra‑individual Variability">
  <data key="d0">Intra‑individual Variability</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Intra‑individual variability describes the coefficient of variation in insulin exposure within a single individual over 24 hours.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d6b9a8472aefa6e90793233284c15a3f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Toujeo.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786313664</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Insulin Effect">
  <data key="d0">Insulin Effect</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Insulin effect denotes the pharmacodynamic outcome of insulin administration.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d6b9a8472aefa6e90793233284c15a3f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Toujeo.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786313664</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Detectability">
  <data key="d0">Detectability</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Detectability indicates whether a substance can be measured in plasma.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d6b9a8472aefa6e90793233284c15a3f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Toujeo.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786313664</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Half‑Life of Metabolite M1">
  <data key="d0">Half‑Life of Metabolite M1</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Half‑Life of Metabolite M1 is the time required for its plasma concentration to decrease by half, reported as 18–19 hours.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d6b9a8472aefa6e90793233284c15a3f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Toujeo.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786313664</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Conservative Dosing">
  <data key="d0">Conservative Dosing</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Conservative dosing recommends lower initial and maintenance doses to reduce hypoglycemia risk.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d6b9a8472aefa6e90793233284c15a3f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Toujeo.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786313665</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Body Weight">
  <data key="d0">Body Weight</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Body weight is a physiological factor influencing drug clearance.&lt;SEP&gt;Body Weight (kg) is a baseline and study‑end measurement of participants’ mass recorded in the 18‑week trial.&lt;SEP&gt;Body weight changes measured as kilograms during the clinical trials.&lt;SEP&gt;Body Weight refers to the weight categories used in the Diabetes Risk Test, where higher weight adds points to the risk score.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d6b9a8472aefa6e90793233284c15a3f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9f85d0ab4cfadc905544cb9e30752dab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3059be019782459a72891cea5e0434ea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2c37e26e62468b725533260347fb4e31</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Toujeo.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_fiasp.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377191</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Clearance">
  <data key="d0">Clearance</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Clearance describes the rate at which a drug is eliminated from the body.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d6b9a8472aefa6e90793233284c15a3f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Toujeo.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786313665</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Anti‑Insulin Antibodies">
  <data key="d0">Anti‑Insulin Antibodies</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Anti‑Insulin Antibodies are antibodies formed against insulin that may appear after administration of TOUJEO.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1d7223c781e745e72311fccfcdd58583</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Toujeo.pdf</data>
