  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Underdose">
  <data key="d0">Underdose</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Underdose refers to an insufficient insulin dose that may lead to hyperglycemia.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1ee5400065df79b02b6c04efc0f4854d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Toujeo.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786313667</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Overdose">
  <data key="d0">Overdose</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Overdose denotes administration of insulin beyond the prescribed amount, risking hypoglycemia.&lt;SEP&gt;Overdose refers to administration of an insulin dose exceeding patient needs, potentially causing hypoglycemia.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1ee5400065df79b02b6c04efc0f4854d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dd396c45bc09fb646d156b4e69d328e3</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Toujeo.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786318492</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Mixture">
  <data key="d0">Mixture</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Mixture refers to the prohibited practice of combining Toujeo with other insulins in the same syringe or vial.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1ee5400065df79b02b6c04efc0f4854d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Toujeo.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786313668</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Dilution">
  <data key="d0">Dilution</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Dilution is the prohibited practice of adding fluids to Toujeo, which alters its action profile.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1ee5400065df79b02b6c04efc0f4854d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Toujeo.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786313668</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Contamination">
  <data key="d0">Contamination</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Contamination risk arises if the pen or needle is shared between individuals.&lt;SEP&gt;Contamination refers to the risk of bacterial entry when the needle is not properly removed and stored.&lt;SEP&gt;Contamination denotes the presence of unwanted substances or microbes that can affect the pen or insulin quality.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1ee5400065df79b02b6c04efc0f4854d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ffe095bda1b787c5b5ae2d61a2f74c98&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5c24a2af0d0291fc4f4730256c420e93</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Toujeo.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_apidra.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786318422</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Basal Insulins">
  <data key="d0">Basal Insulins</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Basal insulins are long‑acting insulin formulations used to maintain baseline glucose levels.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1ee5400065df79b02b6c04efc0f4854d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Toujeo.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786313668</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Insulin Pumps">
  <data key="d0">Insulin Pumps</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Insulin Pumps refer to devices for continuous subcutaneous insulin infusion, which should not be used with Toujeo 300 U/mL.&lt;SEP&gt;Portable devices that deliver insulin subcutaneously via programmable infusion.&lt;SEP&gt;Insulin pumps are medical devices that deliver continuous subcutaneous insulin infusion for diabetes management.&lt;SEP&gt;Insulin pumps are devices that provide continuous insulin infusion for diabetes management.&lt;SEP&gt;Insulin pumps are devices used in pump therapy that can experience complications such as infusion set failure, skin issues, and infections.&lt;SEP&gt;Insulin pumps are devices that provide continuous subcutaneous insulin infusion.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1ee5400065df79b02b6c04efc0f4854d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-16a76447c936e157673f084ffb74520d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b50a9fb21c77773aec36a9b8e9f5e1d5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b3b81193a603a098b1ff9f6f0f665fec&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4b355007bba178588f3928b6c8620a78&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-05cc642337c2a615c9b40de9336aec18</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Toujeo.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/Insulinoterapia – Diretriz da Sociedade Brasileira de Diabetes – Ed. 2024.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/blood glucose monitoring.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786335853</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Obstruction">
  <data key="d0">Obstruction</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Obstruction describes needle blockage that can lead to underdose or overdose of insulin.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1ee5400065df79b02b6c04efc0f4854d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Toujeo.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786313669</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Therapy Change">
  <data key="d0">Therapy Change</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Therapy change refers to the transition from Toujeo to other basal insulins, requiring medical supervision.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1ee5400065df79b02b6c04efc0f4854d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Toujeo.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786313669</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Pen Sharing">
  <data key="d0">Pen Sharing</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Pen sharing is the practice of multiple individuals using the same insulin pen, which raises contamination risk.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1ee5400065df79b02b6c04efc0f4854d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Toujeo.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786313669</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Therapeutic Concentration of Insulin Glargine">
  <data key="d0">Therapeutic Concentration of Insulin Glargine</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-afc28422755c2c44f931bab7b6a2b477</data>
  <data key="d2">Therapeutic concentrations of insulin glargine are far below those required to activate the IGF‑1 pathway and trigger mitogenic signaling.</data>
  <data key="d1">UNKNOWN</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Toujeo.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786313745</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="APIDRA SOLOSTAR">
  <data key="d0">APIDRA SOLOSTAR</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">APIDRA SOLOSTAR is an insulin medication used to treat diabetes, referenced throughout the text for dosing, safety, and interactions.&lt;SEP&gt;APIDRA SOLOSTAR is a formulation of APIDRA indicated as contraindicated for patients allergic to insulin glulisine.&lt;SEP&gt;APIDRA SOLOSTAR is a recombinant human insulin analog marketed in a pen, requiring specific storage, administration, and handling instructions.&lt;SEP&gt;APIDRA SOLOSTAR is a medication containing insulin glulisina intended for subcutaneous injection in diabetes treatment.&lt;SEP&gt;APIDRA SOLOSTAR is an insulin formulation administered subcutaneously and discussed for its safety, dosage effects, contraindications, and need for adjunct therapies.&lt;SEP&gt;APIDRA SOLOSTAR is an insulin glulisina medication used to control blood glucose in diabetic patients.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e4ba52cc293c5c002b470566321026d6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e212a20942ed5387efe96e92bdb4ba98&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c95471c4c993fa3a499f99443ee7c922&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b060d4f68031bd35dfafc19eadf1e9fe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-04b345bc26ec7f5d7c9db8c6004a50a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f09811b149a29105854a0b1e84951e5d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_apidra.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786315335</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Paciente Diabético">
  <data key="d0">Paciente Diabético</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Paciente Diabético refers to any individual diagnosed with diabetes who requires glucose monitoring and insulin therapy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e4ba52cc293c5c002b470566321026d6</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_apidra.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786315335</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Mulher Grávida">
  <data key="d0">Mulher Grávida</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Mulher Grávida denotes a pregnant woman, highlighted regarding limited clinical studies of APIDRA SOLOSTAR and insulin dosing changes across trimesters.&lt;SEP&gt;Mulher Grávida denotes a pregnant woman, for whom insulin treatment is allowed because insulin does not cross the placental barrier.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e4ba52cc293c5c002b470566321026d6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ba6b31518be6fff1db8b68a28e82f200</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_apidra.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786318548</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Mulher Lactante">
  <data key="d0">Mulher Lactante</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Mulher Lactante refers to a breastfeeding woman for whom it is uncertain whether APIDRA SOLOSTAR is excreted in breast milk and may need dose adjustment.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e4ba52cc293c5c002b470566321026d6</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_apidra.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786315335</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Criança≥4 Anos">
  <data key="d0">Criança≥4 Anos</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Criança≥4 Anos indicates a child aged four years or older who may be administered APIDRA SOLOSTAR, whereas younger children have not been studied.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e4ba52cc293c5c002b470566321026d6</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_apidra.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786315335</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Monitoramento da Glicose no Sangue">
  <data key="d0">Monitoramento da Glicose no Sangue</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Monitoramento da Glicose no Sangue is the recommended practice of checking blood glucose levels in all diabetic patients.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e4ba52cc293c5c002b470566321026d6</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_apidra.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786315335</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Controle Glicêmico">
  <data key="d0">Controle Glicêmico</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Controle Glicêmico refers to the management of blood glucose levels, essential during pregnancy and for avoiding hypoglycemia.&lt;SEP&gt;Controle glicêmico denotes the management of blood glucose levels in diabetic patients.&lt;SEP&gt;Overall management of blood glucose levels, referenced throughout the text.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e4ba52cc293c5c002b470566321026d6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e212a20942ed5387efe96e92bdb4ba98&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-91a09040fc4581d7aad2216dba9fba79</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_apidra.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/cgm.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786335249</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Inibidores da ECA">
  <data key="d0">Inibidores da ECA</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Inibidores da ECA are a class of drugs mentioned as intensifying the hypoglycemic effect of APIDRA SOLOSTAR.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e4ba52cc293c5c002b470566321026d6</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_apidra.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786315336</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Inibidores da MAO">
  <data key="d0">Inibidores da MAO</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Inibidores da MAO are a class of substances listed as intensifying the hypoglycemic effect of APIDRA SOLOSTAR.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e4ba52cc293c5c002b470566321026d6</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_apidra.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786315336</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Antibióticos sulfonamida">
  <data key="d0">Antibióticos sulfonamida</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Antibióticos sulfonamida are a group of substances listed as intensifying the hypoglycemic effect of APIDRA SOLOSTAR.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e4ba52cc293c5c002b470566321026d6</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_apidra.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786315337</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Estrogênios">
  <data key="d0">Estrogênios</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Estrogênios are substances listed as reducing the hypoglycemic effect of APIDRA SOLOSTAR.&lt;SEP&gt;Hormonal agents contraindicated for SOP in lipodystrophy due to heightened hypertriglyceridemia risk.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e4ba52cc293c5c002b470566321026d6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7eabee57ef0af575162ce8d36f3589a5</data>
