<node id="SoloStar">
  <data key="d0">SoloStar</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">SoloStar is an insulin pen used for subcutaneous injection, featuring a cartridge, dose selector, injection button, and removable needle.&lt;SEP&gt;SoloStar is a disposable insulin pen intended for subcutaneous injection, stored at room temperature up to 30 °C, protected from light, heat, dust, and not to be refrigerated; it must be discarded according to sanitary authority guidelines after use or expiration.&lt;SEP&gt;SoloStar is an insulin pen that delivers insulin doses and includes a dosage selector, needle attachment, and a reservoir of 300 insulin units.&lt;SEP&gt;SoloStar is an insulin pen designed to deliver insulin subcutaneously, featuring a dosage selector, plunger, cartridge, and detachable needle.&lt;SEP&gt;SoloStar is a pen intended for precise and safe writing, requiring careful handling to avoid damage.&lt;SEP&gt;SoloStar is the medication name associated with the biological product and appears in the label text.&lt;SEP&gt;A product or device referenced alongside the application system.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-162882e6afffb0db8ae5e9153e5f1e82&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2f2573669c38640b56efd6bd0668d1e2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fdeef3e06ffaa7cc0442c3d94917f0c4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ffe095bda1b787c5b5ae2d61a2f74c98&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e9835d6684db67541402527b3182b6c5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fed8264ddac9525305e06a64be3eeb60&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-79f891b1d7c0c6ca0eab9dbcc76c902d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_apidra.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786315341</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Apidra SoloStar">
  <data key="d0">Apidra SoloStar</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Apidra SoloStar is a 100 UI/mL insulin glulisine solution provided in a pre‑filled disposable pen, indicated for the treatment of diabetes mellitus in adults and children over 4 years.&lt;SEP&gt;Apidra SoloStar is a blue variant of the SoloStar insulin pen featuring a dark‑blue application button and a top ring.&lt;SEP&gt;Apidra SoloStar is a prefilled insulin pen containing insulin glulisina, used for subcutaneous administration.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-162882e6afffb0db8ae5e9153e5f1e82&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0e7689ca0fc736d9eae94256f73fed52&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-79f891b1d7c0c6ca0eab9dbcc76c902d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_apidra.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786315341</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Insulin Glulisine">
  <data key="d0">Insulin Glulisine</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Insulin glulisine is the generic name of the rapid‑acting insulin analog marketed as APIDRA.&lt;SEP&gt;Insulin glulisine is a rapid‑acting insulin evaluated against insulin lispro in children and adolescents with Type 1 diabetes.&lt;SEP&gt;Insulin glulisine is the specific glulisine form of insulin delivered by the APIDRA® SOLOSTAR® pen.&lt;SEP&gt;Insulin glulisine is a rapid‑acting insulin analogue, the active pharmaceutical ingredient in Apidra SoloStar, supplied at 100 UI per mL.&lt;SEP&gt;Insulin glulisine is the chemical name of the rapid‑acting insulin analog marketed as APIDRA.&lt;SEP&gt;Insulin Glulisine is an insulin mentioned as interfering with laboratory examinations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-162882e6afffb0db8ae5e9153e5f1e82&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b18f8ab53481bf1b63fda1bb71fe80ec&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d65840dd2cbd5c9984dfc4334378df5e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b79dcaf41f7f07eed90788ce9e50dddd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ee2684edaea64aa597fd29c3bbda611d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2dc2313c92b2af4132faaa4d41449eef</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_apidra.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786315341</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
