</node>
<node id="Glycated Hemoglobin">
  <data key="d0">Glycated Hemoglobin</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Glycated hemoglobin (GHb) is another term for hemoglobin A1c, used to assess glycemic control in the clinical study.&lt;SEP&gt;Glycated hemoglobin (HbA1c) is a form of hemoglobin measured to assess average blood glucose over preceding weeks.&lt;SEP&gt;Glycated hemoglobin refers to hemoglobin molecules bound to glucose, serving as a diagnostic marker for diabetes.&lt;SEP&gt;A measure of average blood glucose over time, studied for its association with diabetes and cardiovascular risk in nondiabetic adults.&lt;SEP&gt;A biomarker used to assess diabetes risk, kidney disease, and cardiovascular outcomes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-162882e6afffb0db8ae5e9153e5f1e82&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8393954b021d0ad02018d1a449e0cc93&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ec7e786a85b1b6e6cc75bcfc9189fd27&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea6df8d05eb3fdd356a1eaef16a26dd5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d5ec01ed3c32ac663f3dc6cfa6fa09a3</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_apidra.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Diagnóstico de diabetes mellitus.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377384</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Fase Basal">
  <data key="d0">Fase Basal</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Baseline measurement period before the 26‑week treatment phase.&lt;SEP&gt;Fase Basal refers to the baseline phase against which adjusted mean changes in the studies are compared.&lt;SEP&gt;Fase Basal refers to the baseline phase of insulin treatment used as a reference point for adjusted mean changes.&lt;SEP&gt;Fase Basal denotes the baseline phase of the studies against which changes in outcomes were measured.&lt;SEP&gt;Fase Basal is the baseline phase used as reference for adjusted mean changes in study outcomes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f46c503a378e6c69618036a038672417&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2479751a6475c09415f0d79759db091d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-29710f08f3e10bba4a464e8b4da1917c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3f0b85829c02f82470489f3f5e487996&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aecb3968c37f57b78a756e4b661ad089</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_apidra.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786315398</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Figura 1">
  <data key="d0">Figura 1</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Figura 1 illustrates the six‑hour hypoglycemic effect of Apidra and Insulina Humana Regular under different pre‑ and post‑meal timing conditions.&lt;SEP&gt;Figure 1 depicts the six‑hour hypoglycemic effect of Apidra administered before or after a standard meal compared with regular human insulin.&lt;SEP&gt;Figura 1 illustrates the CGM‑based goals for diabetes management in elderly patients.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f46c503a378e6c69618036a038672417&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b65ee62ad12239ddc729c50a1aef854c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9dee0a79e4583f41e757f9a20f56f397</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_apidra.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Metas glicêmicas/Metas no tratamento.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786370020</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Figura 2">
  <data key="d0">Figura 2</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Figura 2 presents the pharmacokinetic profiles of Insulina Glulisina and Insulina Humana Regular after a 0.15 UI/kg subcutaneous dose.&lt;SEP&gt;Figure 2 shows the pharmacokinetic profile of insulin glulisina and regular human insulin in patients with diabetes tipo 1 after a 0.15 UI/kg dose.&lt;SEP&gt;Figura 2 is a flowchart (algorithm) in the guideline illustrating the decision process for DM2 screening.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f46c503a378e6c69618036a038672417&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b65ee62ad12239ddc729c50a1aef854c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c92d117f7109ea1ce6995f23bc680ce3</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_apidra.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Diagnóstico de diabetes mellitus.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786372029</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
