<node id="APIDRA">
  <data key="d0">APIDRA</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">APIDRA is the commercial brand name for insulin glulisine, a recombinant rapid‑acting insulin analogue used for the management of diabetes mellitus. It is supplied in vial or refill presentations and is administered by subcutaneous injection, typically before or after meals, to provide post‑prandial glucose control in both type 1 and type 2 diabetes. In clinical studies, APIDRA has been evaluated as a monotherapy and in combination with other rapid‑acting insulins, and it is also employed in continuous subcutaneous insulin infusion (CSII) systems.

Pharmacologically, insulin glulisine (APIDRA) is characterized by a rapid onset of action and a short duration compared with regular human insulin, reflecting its fast absorption after subcutaneous delivery. Pharmacokinetic and pharmacodynamic investigations across diverse populations have confirmed these rapid‑acting properties, supporting its use up to 15 minutes before meals. The product may also be administered intravenously in specific clinical settings.

The label information and trial data describe APIDRA’s safety profile, highlighting the risk of severe hypoglycemia as a principal adverse effect. Pre‑clinical assessments have examined mutagenicity, teratogenicity, and other toxicological endpoints, and the drug is contraindicated in patients with known hypersensitivity to insulin glulisine or any of its excipients.

One source mistakenly refers to APIDRA as a brand of rapid‑acting insulin lispro; however, all other descriptions consistently identify APIDRA with insulin glulisine, and the prevailing regulatory and scientific literature supports this identification.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2479751a6475c09415f0d79759db091d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-29710f08f3e10bba4a464e8b4da1917c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4d0e34bef478ed432c8de7ef68dc9025&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3f0b85829c02f82470489f3f5e487996&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e212a20942ed5387efe96e92bdb4ba98&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b18f8ab53481bf1b63fda1bb71fe80ec&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-15a498084b9a0c4cfcd9aa9553e12a14&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-51761473ea6fe17b9e098a6bf98636b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d65840dd2cbd5c9984dfc4334378df5e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-465ad8b77c1c2a2a179062da20337ff5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7621ac447c9044986ade86ce5f9be201&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e3418c4ee80182ca29214dd54b0d9647&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ee2684edaea64aa597fd29c3bbda611d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50719bcc88f4515ec825b9d5a7aba107&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-77dc1a2378f763ffabe8fa379881d1cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-891989adf06518cd34c94853444495e3</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_apidra.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786315418</data>
