<node id="Infusão Subcutânea Contínua">
  <data key="d0">Infusão Subcutânea Contínua</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Continuous subcutaneous infusion is a delivery method for APIDRA using an insulin pump.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-15a498084b9a0c4cfcd9aa9553e12a14</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_apidra.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786315439</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Administração Subcutânea">
  <data key="d0">Administração Subcutânea</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Subcutaneous administration is the injection of APIDRA into the abdominal wall, thigh, or deltoid.&lt;SEP&gt;Administração Subcutânea is the subcutaneous injection technique used to deliver Novolin® R.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-15a498084b9a0c4cfcd9aa9553e12a14&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0689fd73d2061ee466b9b90e03bda141</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_apidra.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786318538</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Infusão Intravenosa">
  <data key="d0">Infusão Intravenosa</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Intravenous infusion is a delivery method for APIDRA using saline solution in a PVC bag.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-15a498084b9a0c4cfcd9aa9553e12a14</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_apidra.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786315440</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Mistura De Insulinas">
  <data key="d0">Mistura De Insulinas</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Mixing insulins refers to the practice of combining APIDRA with Insulin Human NPH in the same syringe.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-15a498084b9a0c4cfcd9aa9553e12a14</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_apidra.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786315440</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Sodium Chloride 0.9% Solution">
  <data key="d0">Sodium Chloride 0.9% Solution</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Sodium chloride 0.9% solution is the recommended diluent for intravenous administration of APIDRA.&lt;SEP&gt;Isotonic saline solution compatible as diluent for IV Fiasp infusions.&lt;SEP&gt;A 0.9% sodium chloride solution is an isotonic fluid that can serve as a diluent for intravenous Novolin® R infusions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-51761473ea6fe17b9e098a6bf98636b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bc2aa5d85d666eabc9dbaa5d2ecfe874&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-73559dc5d86ea52a348d603482e056e9</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_apidra.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_fiasp.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786318524</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Local Allergy">
  <data key="d0">Local Allergy</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Local allergy describes redness, swelling, and itching at the injection site of insulin.&lt;SEP&gt;Local allergy is a common injection‑site reaction to insulin, characterized by redness, swelling, and itching, usually resolving within days or weeks.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-51761473ea6fe17b9e098a6bf98636b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8ac99e7359716e2cecc2ec93159218b6</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_apidra.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786319740</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Glucagon Intramuscular/Subcutaneous">
  <data key="d0">Glucagon Intramuscular/Subcutaneous</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Glucagon administered intramuscularly or subcutaneously is used to treat severe hypoglycemia with coma or seizures.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-51761473ea6fe17b9e098a6bf98636b3</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_apidra.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786315442</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Registro 1.8326.0343">
  <data key="d0">Registro 1.8326.0343</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Registro 1.8326.0343 is the registration number assigned to APIDRA by the regulatory authority.&lt;SEP&gt;Registro 1.8326.0343 is the official registration number assigned to APIDRA SOLOSTAR by Brazilian health authorities.&lt;SEP&gt;Registro 1.8326.0343 is the registration number for Apidra SoloStar.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-51761473ea6fe17b9e098a6bf98636b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-04b345bc26ec7f5d7c9db8c6004a50a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0e7689ca0fc736d9eae94256f73fed52</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_apidra.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786315443</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Long-Acting Insulin">
  <data key="d0">Long-Acting Insulin</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Long-acting insulin refers to insulin products of prolonged action mentioned as being mistakenly administered instead of insulin glulisina.&lt;SEP&gt;Long‑acting insulin refers to insulin formulations with prolonged duration that may be transitioned to Levemir® with dose and timing adjustments.&lt;SEP&gt;Long-Acting Insulin is a basal insulin formulation that provides steady glucose regulation over many hours.&lt;SEP&gt;Insulin with prolonged effect used in injection therapy for basal needs.&lt;SEP&gt;Long‑acting insulin is advised as a basal replacement at the same dose when the insulin pump fails.&lt;SEP&gt;Long‑acting insulin provides basal insulin coverage over an extended period.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-51761473ea6fe17b9e098a6bf98636b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-56fc1d5df1b34d9120c3cf8a760c40f9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c1700b8f7c792afbd394001e28bf632f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5913d17c337be62cd526d46fbdcd9a6e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6fba8ea0c6bdb8427804ba05f9fe49f9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-06425d1f80d868bd58871b6a6e740102</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_apidra.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/Understanding insulin - International Diabetes Federation.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786332449</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="5. Advertências e Precauções">
  <data key="d0">5. Advertências e Precauções</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Section titled “5. Advertências e Precauções” containing warnings and precautions for APIDRA use.&lt;SEP&gt;Section 5 of the professional leaflet that provides warnings and precautions for Levemir® Penfill®.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-51761473ea6fe17b9e098a6bf98636b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-00cf434060561bb7d46b6ce50f095c91</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_apidra.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786317452</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Rabbits">
  <data key="d0">Rabbits</data>
  <data key="d1">creature</data>
  <data key="d2">Rabbits are laboratory animals used to assess the effects of APIDRA SOLOSTAR at low doses, with no observed adverse effects.&lt;SEP&gt;Laboratory rabbits used in the teratology study of APIDRA.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c95471c4c993fa3a499f99443ee7c922&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ee2684edaea64aa597fd29c3bbda611d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_apidra.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786315448</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Dose 1.5 UI/Kg Once Daily">
  <data key="d0">Dose 1.5 UI/Kg Once Daily</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">A high dose of 1.5 UI/kg administered once daily caused maternal hypoglycemia, fetal loss, skeletal defects, and female mortality in animal studies.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c95471c4c993fa3a499f99443ee7c922</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_apidra.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786315448</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Dose 0.5 UI/Kg Once Daily">
  <data key="d0">Dose 0.5 UI/Kg Once Daily</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">A dose of 0.5 UI/kg administered once daily led to a slight increase in post‑implantation loss and severe maternal hypoglycemia without skeletal defects.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c95471c4c993fa3a499f99443ee7c922</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_apidra.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786315448</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Dose 0.25 UI/Kg Once Daily">
  <data key="d0">Dose 0.25 UI/Kg Once Daily</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">A dose of 0.25 UI/kg administered once daily showed no observable effects in rabbits.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c95471c4c993fa3a499f99443ee7c922</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_apidra.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786315448</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Dose Up To 10 UI/Kg Once Daily">
  <data key="d0">Dose Up To 10 UI/Kg Once Daily</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Doses up to 10 UI/kg administered once daily showed no adverse effects on male or female fertility in rats.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c95471c4c993fa3a499f99443ee7c922</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_apidra.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786315449</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Fetal Development">
  <data key="d0">Fetal Development</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Fetal Development refers to the growth of the fetus, which was adversely affected (skeletal defects) at high APIDRA SOLOSTAR doses in animal studies.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c95471c4c993fa3a499f99443ee7c922</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_apidra.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786315450</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Sudden Injection Site Change">
  <data key="d0">Sudden Injection Site Change</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">A sudden switch of insulin injection location to a previously unaffected area.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c95471c4c993fa3a499f99443ee7c922</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_apidra.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786315452</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Repeated Injection at Same Site">
  <data key="d0">Repeated Injection at Same Site</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">Repeated administration of insulin in the same subcutaneous location.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c95471c4c993fa3a499f99443ee7c922</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_apidra.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786315453</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Insulin Dose Requirements">
  <data key="d0">Insulin Dose Requirements</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Insulin dose requirements refer to the amount of insulin needed, which varies throughout pregnancy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c95471c4c993fa3a499f99443ee7c922</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_apidra.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786315453</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="rDNA Insulin">
  <data key="d0">rDNA Insulin</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">rDNA Insulin is a recombinant DNA‑derived insulin formulation cited as a possible variation in insulin manufacturing.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c95471c4c993fa3a499f99443ee7c922</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_apidra.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786315455</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Animal‑Derived Insulin">
  <data key="d0">Animal‑Derived Insulin</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Animal‑Derived Insulin refers to insulin sourced from animal pancreas, listed among insulin species variations.&lt;SEP&gt;Insulin obtained from animal sources, mentioned as the previous insulin type compared with Novolin® R Penfill regarding hypoglycemia warning symptom intensity.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c95471c4c993fa3a499f99443ee7c922&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9a6f9e10c0d4af5fff0338eb861f9c86</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_apidra.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786318474</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Human‑Derived Insulin">
  <data key="d0">Human‑Derived Insulin</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Human‑Derived Insulin refers to insulin produced from human DNA or pancreas, listed among insulin species variations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c95471c4c993fa3a499f99443ee7c922</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_apidra.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786315456</data>
