<node id="Infusion Catheter">
  <data key="d0">Infusion Catheter</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The infusion catheter is the tubing component of a subcutaneous insulin pump; errors or malfunction can contribute to hyperglycemia and related metabolic complications.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d65840dd2cbd5c9984dfc4334378df5e</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_apidra.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786315464</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Ketosis">
  <data key="d0">Ketosis</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Ketosis is a metabolic state of elevated ketone bodies that can follow hyperglycemia in insulin‑pump failures.&lt;SEP&gt;Ketosis is a metabolic state of elevated ketone bodies that can develop secondary to severe hyperglycemia, especially in diabetic ketoacidosis.&lt;SEP&gt;Ketosis is a metabolic state that may result from prolonged insulin under‑delivery.&lt;SEP&gt;Ketosis is a metabolic condition that can result from infusion set problems in insulin pump therapy.&lt;SEP&gt;Ketosis is a metabolic state characterized by elevated ketone bodies, mentioned as requiring ketone monitoring.&lt;SEP&gt;Ketosis is a metabolic state mentioned as a symptom associated with hyperglycemia in diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d65840dd2cbd5c9984dfc4334378df5e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-14772c7de5db762c492a75a1c744dae6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d3b794ead59ea83de139af0358a0e7b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b3b81193a603a098b1ff9f6f0f665fec&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-345ad64f464691cc28341ccd246032db&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b2cd796639bdb0e10eeda7ef3d9ebbce</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_apidra.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_fiasp.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/blood glucose monitoring.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Metas glicêmicas/metas cuidado do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786372100</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Driving Vehicles">
  <data key="d0">Driving Vehicles</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Driving vehicles is an activity that may be impaired by hypoglycemia or hyperglycemia, posing safety risks.&lt;SEP&gt;Driving vehicles refers to operating a car or similar machine, an activity that can be impaired by hypoglycemia or hyperglycemia.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d65840dd2cbd5c9984dfc4334378df5e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f09811b149a29105854a0b1e84951e5d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_apidra.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786315465</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Oral Hypoglycemic Agents">
  <data key="d0">Oral Hypoglycemic Agents</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Oral hypoglycemic agents are medications that lower blood glucose and can intensify the hypoglycemic effect of insulin.&lt;SEP&gt;Oral hypoglycemic agents are drugs that intensify the insulin‑induced reduction of blood glucose.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d65840dd2cbd5c9984dfc4334378df5e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f09811b149a29105854a0b1e84951e5d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_apidra.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786315466</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Dipyridamole">
  <data key="d0">Dipyridamole</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Dipyridamole is an antiplatelet agent that can intensify the hypoglycemic effect of insulin.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d65840dd2cbd5c9984dfc4334378df5e</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_apidra.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786315467</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Propoxyphene">
  <data key="d0">Propoxyphene</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Propoxyphene is an opioid analgesic that can increase insulin‑related hypoglycemia.&lt;SEP&gt;Propoxyphene is a drug that intensifies the insulin‑induced reduction of blood glucose.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d65840dd2cbd5c9984dfc4334378df5e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f09811b149a29105854a0b1e84951e5d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_apidra.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786315468</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Pregnancy Risk Category C">
  <data key="d0">Pregnancy Risk Category C</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Pregnancy risk category C indicates that animal studies have shown adverse effects, but no well‑controlled human studies exist for APIDRA.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d65840dd2cbd5c9984dfc4334378df5e</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_apidra.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786315473</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Fenotiazina">
  <data key="d0">Fenotiazina</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Fenotiazina is a chemical base from which certain drug derivatives are derived.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-465ad8b77c1c2a2a179062da20337ff5</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_apidra.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786315473</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Sympatholytic Drugs">
  <data key="d0">Sympatholytic Drugs</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Sympatholytic Drugs are medications such as beta blockers, clonidine, guanetidina and reserpina that can reduce adrenergic counter‑regulation signals.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-465ad8b77c1c2a2a179062da20337ff5</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_apidra.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786315474</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Adrenergic Counter‑Regulation Signals">
  <data key="d0">Adrenergic Counter‑Regulation Signals</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Adrenergic Counter‑Regulation Signals are physiological signals that oppose insulin‑induced hypoglycemia.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-465ad8b77c1c2a2a179062da20337ff5</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_apidra.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786315474</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="APIDRA Vial‑Ampoule">
  <data key="d0">APIDRA Vial‑Ampoule</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">APIDRA Vial‑Ampoule is a sealed container of APIDRA intended for subcutaneous or intravenous use.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-465ad8b77c1c2a2a179062da20337ff5</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_apidra.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786315474</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="APIDRA Refill">
  <data key="d0">APIDRA Refill</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">APIDRA Refill is a packaging format containing one or five 3 mL insulin glulisina refills for use with a compatible pen.&lt;SEP&gt;APIDRA Refill is a replaceable cartridge of APIDRA designed for use with compatible insulin pens or infusion devices.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-465ad8b77c1c2a2a179062da20337ff5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-77dc1a2378f763ffabe8fa379881d1cc</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_apidra.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786315475</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Refrigeration 2‑8 °C">
  <data key="d0">Refrigeration 2‑8 °C</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Refrigeration 2‑8 °C is the storage condition required for unopened APIDRA to maintain stability.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-465ad8b77c1c2a2a179062da20337ff5</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_apidra.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786315475</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="28‑Day Usage Period">
  <data key="d0">28‑Day Usage Period</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">28‑Day Usage Period is the maximum time APIDRA may be used after opening, provided storage conditions are met.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-465ad8b77c1c2a2a179062da20337ff5</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_apidra.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786315475</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Compatible Insulin Pen">
  <data key="d0">Compatible Insulin Pen</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Compatible Insulin Pen is a device into which an APIDRA Refill can be inserted for insulin delivery.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-465ad8b77c1c2a2a179062da20337ff5</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_apidra.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786315475</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Infusion Equipment">
  <data key="d0">Infusion Equipment</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Infusion Equipment includes reservoirs, tubes and catheters used to deliver APIDRA via continuous subcutaneous infusion pumps.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-465ad8b77c1c2a2a179062da20337ff5</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_apidra.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786315475</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Infusion Pump">
  <data key="d0">Infusion Pump</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Infusion Pump is a device that provides continuous subcutaneous infusion of medication such as APIDRA.&lt;SEP&gt;An infusion pump is the equipment used in CSII whose defects can trigger rapid hyperglycemia and ketosis.&lt;SEP&gt;Infusion Pump is a device for continuous subcutaneous delivery of insulin.&lt;SEP&gt;A continuous subcutaneous infusion pump is a device that can deliver Humulin R continuously.&lt;SEP&gt;The infusion pump delivers insulin from a reservoir through an infusion set.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-465ad8b77c1c2a2a179062da20337ff5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-14772c7de5db762c492a75a1c744dae6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dd396c45bc09fb646d156b4e69d328e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-577779892c0d463cd6bb1966b8a8ce2d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4a4a75301f61fc3c86ad768de09d0c3f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_apidra.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_fiasp.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329500</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Intravenous Infusion Bag">
  <data key="d0">Intravenous Infusion Bag</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Intravenous Infusion Bag is a container prepared with APIDRA for intravenous administration, stable at room temperature for 48 hours.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-465ad8b77c1c2a2a179062da20337ff5</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_apidra.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786315476</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Recombinant Human Insulin Analog">
  <data key="d0">Recombinant Human Insulin Analog</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Recombinant Human Insulin Analog describes APIDRA as a bioengineered insulin analogue equivalent in potency to regular human insulin.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-465ad8b77c1c2a2a179062da20337ff5</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_apidra.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786315476</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Longer‑Acting Insulin">
  <data key="d0">Longer‑Acting Insulin</data>
