<node id="Adult Type 1 Diabetes Study">
  <data key="d0">Adult Type 1 Diabetes Study</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">A 26‑week, randomized, open‑label clinical trial enrolling 672 adult patients with Type 1 diabetes to compare APIDRA with insulin lispro and insulin glargine.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-77dc1a2378f763ffabe8fa379881d1cc</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_apidra.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786315496</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Pediatric Type 1 Diabetes Study">
  <data key="d0">Pediatric Type 1 Diabetes Study</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">A 26‑week, phase III, open‑label clinical trial enrolling 572 children and adolescents with Type 1 diabetes to compare APIDRA with insulin lispro and basal insulins.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-77dc1a2378f763ffabe8fa379881d1cc</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_apidra.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786315496</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="A1C (Hemoglobin A1c)">
  <data key="d0">A1C (Hemoglobin A1c)</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Hemoglobin A1c (GHb) is the primary efficacy endpoint used to assess glycemic control in the APIDRA studies.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-77dc1a2378f763ffabe8fa379881d1cc</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_apidra.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786315496</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="APIDRA Frasco‑Ampola">
  <data key="d0">APIDRA Frasco‑Ampola</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">APIDRA Frasco‑Ampola is a packaging format containing one or five 10 mL vials for subcutaneous or intravenous administration.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-77dc1a2378f763ffabe8fa379881d1cc</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_apidra.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786315496</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hydrochloric Acid (Concentrated)">
  <data key="d0">Hydrochloric Acid (Concentrated)</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Concentrated hydrochloric acid (ácido clorídrico concentrado) is an excipient present in APIDRA.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-77dc1a2378f763ffabe8fa379881d1cc</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_apidra.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786315496</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Water for Injectable">
  <data key="d0">Water for Injectable</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Water for injectable is an excipient used as a solvent in APIDRA.&lt;SEP&gt;Water for injectable is the aqueous carrier component of Levemir® FlexPen® solution.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-77dc1a2378f763ffabe8fa379881d1cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b65a4249ac93aec086cb333ed1507ea7</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_apidra.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786317652</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Compatible Pen">
  <data key="d0">Compatible Pen</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">A compatible pen is a device designed to deliver APIDRA refills subcutaneously.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-77dc1a2378f763ffabe8fa379881d1cc</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_apidra.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786315496</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="26‑Week Study Duration">
  <data key="d0">26‑Week Study Duration</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A 26‑week period is the length of both adult and pediatric Type 1 diabetes clinical trials.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-77dc1a2378f763ffabe8fa379881d1cc</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_apidra.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786315496</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Plunger">
  <data key="d0">Plunger</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Plunger is the moving component inside the SoloStar that advances with each injection and reaches the cartridge end when all insulin is used.&lt;SEP&gt;The plunger is used to push air bubbles from the reservoir into the tubing and can be twisted counter‑clockwise to loosen and remove it.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e9835d6684db67541402527b3182b6c5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fe844728a502927fee80d42268408b1a</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_apidra.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329589</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Sanitary Authorities">
  <data key="d0">Sanitary Authorities</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Sanitary Authorities are regulatory bodies that set standards for safe disposal of medical sharps such as used needles.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e9835d6684db67541402527b3182b6c5</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_apidra.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786315496</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Dose Selection Step">
  <data key="d0">Dose Selection Step</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">Dose Selection Step is the procedural event where the user sets the desired insulin units on the SoloStar dosage selector.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e9835d6684db67541402527b3182b6c5</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_apidra.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786315497</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Injection Step">
  <data key="d0">Injection Step</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">Injection Step is the procedural event where the needle is inserted, the dose is administered by pressing the injection button, and the device is held until completion.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e9835d6684db67541402527b3182b6c5</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_apidra.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786315497</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Needle Removal and Disposal Step">
  <data key="d0">Needle Removal and Disposal Step</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">Needle Removal and Disposal Step is the procedural event that involves detaching the used needle from the SoloStar and discarding it safely.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e9835d6684db67541402527b3182b6c5</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_apidra.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786315497</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Conservation Instructions">
  <data key="d0">Conservation Instructions</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Conservation Instructions are the set of guidelines for storing and maintaining the SoloStar, including temperature ranges and handling precautions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e9835d6684db67541402527b3182b6c5</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_apidra.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786315497</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Temperature Range Up to 30°C">
  <data key="d0">Temperature Range Up to 30°C</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Temperature Range Up to 30°C is the permissible ambient temperature for storing the SoloStar after removal from refrigeration for up to 28 days.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e9835d6684db67541402527b3182b6c5</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_apidra.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786315497</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Dose Indicator Window">
  <data key="d0">Dose Indicator Window</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Dose Indicator Window is the display component on the SoloStar that shows the selected insulin dose and returns to “0” after injection.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e9835d6684db67541402527b3182b6c5</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_apidra.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786315497</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Multiple Injections">
  <data key="d0">Multiple Injections</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Multiple Injections denotes the situation where a dose exceeds 80 units and requires more than one injection.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e9835d6684db67541402527b3182b6c5</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_apidra.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786315497</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Storage Period 28 Days">
  <data key="d0">Storage Period 28 Days</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Storage Period 28 Days is the maximum duration the SoloStar can be used after removal from refrigeration before it must be discarded.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e9835d6684db67541402527b3182b6c5</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_apidra.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786315497</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cleaning Procedure">
  <data key="d0">Cleaning Procedure</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Cleaning Procedure describes the method of wiping the exterior of the SoloStar with a damp cloth to maintain hygiene.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e9835d6684db67541402527b3182b6c5</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_apidra.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786315497</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Question On Medication Harm">
