<node id="Clinical Study (18‑Week Basal‑Bolus vs Basal)">
  <data key="d0">Clinical Study (18‑Week Basal‑Bolus vs Basal)</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">An 18‑week randomized clinical study comparing basal‑bolus therapy with basal insulin in patients with type 2 diabetes mellitus.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9f85d0ab4cfadc905544cb9e30752dab</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_fiasp.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786316049</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Metformin">
  <data key="d0">Metformin</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Metformin is an oral antihyperglycemic medication that belongs to the biguanide class and is widely employed as a first‑line therapy for diabetes mellitus, especially type 2 diabetes. It is recommended early in treatment algorithms to improve glycaemic control, reduce severe insulin resistance, and serve as a reference or background therapy in clinical research.  

In many clinical trials Metformin is administered in combination with other glucose‑lowering agents. It has been paired with basal insulin analogues such as insulin detemir (Levemir®), with rapid‑acting insulin formulations like Fiasp®, and with glucagon‑like peptide‑1 (GLP‑1) receptor agonists such as liraglutide. These combination regimens are used to assess additive effects on glucose reduction, safety, and tolerability in participants already enrolled in the studies.  

Beyond its primary indication, Metformin is considered safe for use in specific populations, including renal transplant recipients, and is frequently cited as a reference therapy in comparative studies. However, it should be avoided in individuals with mitochondrial diabetes because of an elevated risk of lactic acidosis.  

Metformin is also recommended for people with prediabetes, particularly women who have experienced gestational diabetes mellitus, as a preventive measure to reduce the likelihood of progression to overt diabetes. Clinical evaluations have specifically examined its efficacy in preventing diabetes in this postpartum population.  

Overall, Metformin remains a cornerstone oral antidiabetic drug for treating type 2 diabetes, serving both as monotherapy and as part of combination regimens, while its safety profile supports use in diverse patient groups, albeit with contraindications in mitochondrial diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9f85d0ab4cfadc905544cb9e30752dab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c8c7e36686d077dcb6239405f60ea031&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50a4f77ab697e068f8cf31533065722b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e5f5165b3185feb3c6ec93a3c0ef8d02&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-01fb767ae3a103c9d6c4775570df90c9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b4d7abd3e1e5418ee5a931e28a18e8ad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-005de970178a46619506bcc15fe94fa9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3c6dca13b685243e63fb6f24f7cb301d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-38ab5af7e42588297df4330ffb2c046b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-54ce8d1437c0ec0329819123568df11e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e007fc346ea9f699fecdba467cc5eac8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c83accc14a3b482690949ff04716a0aa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-525031caa389d084bc170433212cdca8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e4e7eef761aec994cc4558b2db5e1e08&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-83d72fbc44fe0c28f27702c0d4f2c140</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_fiasp.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Diagnóstico de diabetes mellitus.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Metas glicêmicas/metas cuidado do diabetes.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377273</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Insulin Basal">
  <data key="d0">Insulin Basal</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Insulin basal denotes the long‑acting insulin regimen administered to participants.&lt;SEP&gt;Basal insulin is a small, continuous amount of insulin released by the pancreas throughout the day to enable glucose uptake by cells between meals and during sleep.&lt;SEP&gt;Insulin Basal is the continuous low‑dose insulin delivery intended to maintain baseline glucose levels throughout the day.&lt;SEP&gt;Insulin Basal is a basal insulin supply that must be maintained even when a patient cannot eat, especially during illness.&lt;SEP&gt;Insulin Basal is the background insulin continuously delivered, representing 30‑70% of the Daily Total Dose.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9f85d0ab4cfadc905544cb9e30752dab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-65c6beab51324e055f4a39b388e2eefe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2dc33cf2a90bf53c26226e44bc285c22&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9f4d152d83c514f926b18413e065c2fa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7e3c3741659a85988124e5ddaf69c849</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_fiasp.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786330151</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Plasma Glucose (GP)">
  <data key="d0">Plasma Glucose (GP)</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Plasma glucose (GP) is the concentration of glucose in blood, used to define severe hypoglycemia.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9f85d0ab4cfadc905544cb9e30752dab</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_fiasp.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786316051</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Automonitoramento Glicêmico (AMG)">
  <data key="d0">Automonitoramento Glicêmico (AMG)</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Automonitoramento glicêmico (AMG) is a self‑monitoring of blood glucose performed two hours after meals.&lt;SEP&gt;Automonitoramento Glicêmico (AMG) is self‑monitoring of blood glucose used to guide Fiasp® dose adjustments before meals and at bedtime.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9f85d0ab4cfadc905544cb9e30752dab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-09d60e0b850d87c77dd67ca2d709912c</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_fiasp.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786316052</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
