<node id="Fiasp®">
  <data key="d0">Fiasp®</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Fiasp® is a fast‑acting insulin aspart formulation marketed for both subcutaneous and intravenous administration in the treatment of diabetes mellitus. It is presented as a clear, aqueous injectable solution that incorporates nicotinamide, an excipient that accelerates absorption and creates a distinct time‑action profile with a rapid onset and early hypoglycaemic effect, making it suitable for mealtime dosing. The product is indicated for use in adults and children with type 1 or type 2 diabetes and may be adjusted according to self‑monitored glucose levels.

Clinical evaluation of Fiasp® has encompassed a range of studies, including pre‑prandial and post‑prandial dosing regimens, pharmacokinetic assessments in type 1 diabetes, and a 26‑week pediatric trial. Both adult and pediatric populations have been examined in rapid‑acting insulin trials, and post‑marketing research continues to assess its safety, injection‑site reactions, and overall efficacy. The formulation’s rapid absorption has been shown to improve glycaemic control when used at mealtime.

Fiasp® is approved for use during pregnancy and breastfeeding, with specific storage requirements to maintain its stability. Its rapid‑acting nature, combined with the nicotinamide‑enhanced absorption, positions it as a convenient option for patients requiring prompt insulin action to manage post‑prandial glucose excursions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2f4f01a72f35d6db3ff333e64f8400ce&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9f85d0ab4cfadc905544cb9e30752dab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1bb9ea85b9ad8cd6940ae41a3ab5d1fd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-14772c7de5db762c492a75a1c744dae6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9ff211ed5ca723fa2074871af58a4eb8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-77c1608c27e3114f3a14f175efe260a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-add4469fba80232b7c0742f24c0914c9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2073bddd90c7dd8e156b67821f0f3247&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-88b97cde53943160602b20f634ba5c1f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d10a1f849386df540104c79e33a7b242&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6c32255a7f064c18ff0b079798cfeaf5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6a7ca48868f79f7be782198d67ffefd0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-09d60e0b850d87c77dd67ca2d709912c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d5bb996e52cb71f15bc8c30d1b1d321&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c8c7e36686d077dcb6239405f60ea031&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7fdc648ec086061141581e27adde6fc4</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_fiasp.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786316067</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Tubing">
  <data key="d0">Tubing</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Tubing is the flexible conduit that links an insulin reservoir (or pump) to the infusion set, conveying insulin—or other prescribed medication—from the storage compartment to the patient’s insertion site. The tube runs from the reservoir through the infusion set and terminates at the cannula or insertion point, allowing the medication to be delivered directly into the subcutaneous tissue. Its pliable material enables it to be comfortably positioned under clothing while maintaining a sealed pathway for fluid flow.

Before use, the tubing is filled with insulin (or the intended medication) and any air bubbles are removed to ensure accurate dosing. Once primed, the tube continuously transports the drug from the reservoir through the infusion set to the cannula, completing the closed‑loop delivery system that administers therapeutic doses to the body.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bc2aa5d85d666eabc9dbaa5d2ecfe874&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d8e2c8beb0e0581ef5724dc5c631252e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4a4a75301f61fc3c86ad768de09d0c3f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-83bb94d08bdb958eff25f76c9a6ac18a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-df77f2ea988e5724effb4c71cc79a65a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fe844728a502927fee80d42268408b1a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-28515a0aca492eeee478cd9947226498&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b6025fa711665988fad0f789b9eb901a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9bfe428f5a1381000cf6932b37aa2239&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a01dc8dc15b92e2b0b570753b0f57632&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b23dfd3ae95fca711f8f10fc98ab467c</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_fiasp.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329442</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
