<node id="Continuous Subcutaneous Insulin Infusion">
  <data key="d0">Continuous Subcutaneous Insulin Infusion</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Continuous Subcutaneous Insulin Infusion (CSII) is a medical technique that delivers insulin continuously beneath the skin using an infusion pump. The method involves a subcutaneous catheter that remains in place for the duration of therapy, allowing a steady, programmable flow of insulin to be administered without the need for multiple daily injections. CSII is commonly employed as the core component of insulin‑pump therapy and is referenced in clinical studies evaluating its efficacy and safety.

The infusion system is pump‑based and is designed to provide a basal rate of insulin delivery that can be adjusted to match the patient’s metabolic needs, with the option to administer bolus doses for meals or corrections. In practice, CSII is used primarily in adults with type 1 diabetes, offering improved glycemic control and greater flexibility compared with conventional injection regimens.

Certain insulin formulations are contraindicated with CSII. Specifically, Novolin® R and Novolin® R Penfill should not be used in the pump because they can precipitate within the catheter, leading to blockage or inconsistent dosing. These contraindications are highlighted in product guidelines to prevent complications associated with insulin precipitation during continuous subcutaneous infusion.&lt;SEP&gt;A method of insulin delivery using a pump or similar device, classified under diabetes technology.&lt;SEP&gt;Continuous subcutaneous insulin infusion is insulin delivery via an insulin pump.&lt;SEP&gt;A method of insulin delivery using an insulin pump to provide continuous subcutaneous insulin.&lt;SEP&gt;Continuous subcutaneous insulin infusion (CSII) is a method of delivering insulin via an implanted pump.&lt;SEP&gt;Continuous subcutaneous insulin infusion is an insulin delivery method studied for type 1 diabetes management.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1bb9ea85b9ad8cd6940ae41a3ab5d1fd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9a6f9e10c0d4af5fff0338eb861f9c86&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dd396c45bc09fb646d156b4e69d328e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea9b3836b3275f451c3acfb189f42a6f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a23aee717dff7fe908d8a006fd48a5c7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-126f927723331d6ce149cf77ed397bbf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f9416e8076c17175db0dbb12c3393566&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-494fef0b8efc2c44b3b49ebf9d74b7f2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e4c5ae163a494feafedb71ed2205c02f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-00f6c2252dc945e977b3a2b2f495ffe0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c93787ffd2c022283fc0663decb1a184&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-00d07129873894814fe6540ce243ef9f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c4af6b5c6f1fd844ec61928d1cce6ef9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-703ccc96df3edd610232f0cca4bf7afa</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_fiasp.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/Insulinoterapia – Diretriz da Sociedade Brasileira de Diabetes – Ed. 2024.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/blood glucose monitoring.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786335919</data>
