<node id="Cuidadores">
  <data key="d0">Cuidadores</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Cuidadores are caregivers who must handle used needles carefully to reduce injury and cross‑infection risk.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a557234bf75633a4af048115a6f0c449</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_fiasp.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786316089</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Penfill®">
  <data key="d0">Penfill®</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Penfill® is a branded, disposable cartridge that contains 3 mL of insulin aspart marketed under the name Fiasp®. The cartridge is intended as a refill accessory for insulin‑pen platforms such as the FlexTouch® pen and other Fiasp®‑compatible devices. It integrates with the pen’s dosing mechanism, allowing a single‑use filling of the pre‑filled insulin volume before the cartridge is discarded. Professional labeling and prescribing information for Fiasp® consistently refer to Penfill® as the cartridge‑type component that supplies the insulin formulation for injection, not as a standalone insulin product.  

In a separate context, the name Penfill® is also used to denote the delivery device—or presentation form—associated with Levemir® (insulin glargine). Several prescribing documents describe Penfill® as the Levemir® pen device, implying that it serves as the pen or cartridge system through which Levemir® is administered. This usage treats Penfill® as the primary pen‑type accessory for delivering Levemir® rather than as a distinct insulin formulation.  

Additional references describe Penfill® more generally as a pre‑filled insulin pen device capable of delivering other rapid‑acting insulins, for example Novolin® R. In these instances Penfill® is characterized as a cartridge system that can be loaded into compatible pen mechanisms, providing a ready‑to‑use insulin dose without the need for manual vial‑to‑pen transfer.  

Packaging‑level documentation sometimes lists Penfill® as a cartridge system that includes five individual carpules for insulin delivery. This formulation suggests a modular kit in which each carpule holds a measured volume of insulin, allowing multiple refill cycles from a single Penfill® package.  

Finally, some sources identify Penfill® as a brand or commercial entity that manufactures and markets insulin carpules. In this sense Penfill® functions as a company name rather than a specific medical device, overseeing the production, labeling, and distribution of the cartridge kits used across the various insulin products mentioned above.  

Because the term Penfill® appears in distinct product families—Fiasp® cartridge, Levemir® pen device, generic insulin pen kits, and as a corporate brand—the descriptions represent multiple, related but separate applications of the same trademark rather than a single, uniform entity.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2f4f01a72f35d6db3ff333e64f8400ce&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9f85d0ab4cfadc905544cb9e30752dab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1bb9ea85b9ad8cd6940ae41a3ab5d1fd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a557234bf75633a4af048115a6f0c449&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-14772c7de5db762c492a75a1c744dae6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9ff211ed5ca723fa2074871af58a4eb8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-77c1608c27e3114f3a14f175efe260a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-add4469fba80232b7c0742f24c0914c9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dd25c8bd4672601d6ee40e4b7e28a69c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3a70857656e32cc73aaa270a75eb33af&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2073bddd90c7dd8e156b67821f0f3247&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-88b97cde53943160602b20f634ba5c1f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d10a1f849386df540104c79e33a7b242&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6a7ca48868f79f7be782198d67ffefd0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-09d60e0b850d87c77dd67ca2d709912c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d5bb996e52cb71f15bc8c30d1b1d321&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c8c7e36686d077dcb6239405f60ea031&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7fdc648ec086061141581e27adde6fc4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fdee4bcd64faa476dd057e21e2525e53&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-831f4bbfc884fc8e9679630a819083e9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9bcc4202330d45ebfca8f79c3d4998b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-813e7e990dba10e8d4147252f6547423&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fce17a01f9697252910d19a41ca6c900&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cd40a6d69921cf300ed8eda043698d1a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3f957e1a9566d1d41252f7637b06da4f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_fiasp.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786318492</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Missed Meal">
  <data key="d0">Missed Meal</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Missed Meal is the omission of a scheduled food intake that can precipitate hypoglycemia in insulin‑treated patients.&lt;SEP&gt;Missed Meal is the omission of a scheduled food intake, identified as a trigger for hypoglycemia.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-14772c7de5db762c492a75a1c744dae6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea9b3836b3275f451c3acfb189f42a6f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_fiasp.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786318511</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Unplanned Physical Exercise">
  <data key="d0">Unplanned Physical Exercise</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Unplanned Physical Exercise refers to unexpected strenuous activity that can increase insulin‑induced glucose uptake and lead to hypoglycemia.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-14772c7de5db762c492a75a1c744dae6</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_fiasp.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786316100</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Inadequate Insulin Dose">
  <data key="d0">Inadequate Insulin Dose</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Inadequate Insulin Dose denotes an insulin amount that is insufficient to meet physiological needs, potentially causing hyperglycemia.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-14772c7de5db762c492a75a1c744dae6</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_fiasp.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786316100</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Discontinuation of Insulin">
  <data key="d0">Discontinuation of Insulin</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Discontinuation of Insulin is the abrupt cessation of insulin therapy, which can result in hyperglycemia and diabetic ketoacidosis.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-14772c7de5db762c492a75a1c744dae6</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_fiasp.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786316101</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Change of Injection Site">
  <data key="d0">Change of Injection Site</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Change of Injection Site is the practice of moving insulin injections to a different skin area, which may trigger hypoglycemia if the new site has different absorption characteristics.&lt;SEP&gt;Change of Injection Site refers to moving insulin administration to a different area to avoid lipodystrophy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-14772c7de5db762c492a75a1c744dae6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8ac99e7359716e2cecc2ec93159218b6</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_fiasp.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786319741</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Travel Across Time Zones">
  <data key="d0">Travel Across Time Zones</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Travel Across Time Zones refers to moving between regions with different clock times, requiring medical guidance for insulin timing and meal scheduling.&lt;SEP&gt;Travel Across Time Zones refers to patients needing to adjust Levemir® dosing and meals when crossing time zones.&lt;SEP&gt;Travel across different time zones may require adjustments in insulin administration and meal schedules.&lt;SEP&gt;Travel to locations with more than two hours of time‑zone difference requires adjustment of the insulin dose.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-14772c7de5db762c492a75a1c744dae6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8ef15154a94043650617b3b24d8146a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9a6f9e10c0d4af5fff0338eb861f9c86&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8ac99e7359716e2cecc2ec93159218b6</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_fiasp.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786319740</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Medical Guidance">
  <data key="d0">Medical Guidance</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Medical Guidance is professional advice provided to patients to adjust insulin therapy and meal schedules when traveling across time zones.&lt;SEP&gt;Medical guidance refers to the direction provided by a physician allowing intramuscular administration of Novolin® R.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-14772c7de5db762c492a75a1c744dae6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-73559dc5d86ea52a348d603482e056e9</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_fiasp.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786318526</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Delayed Gastric Emptying">
  <data key="d0">Delayed Gastric Emptying</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Delayed Gastric Emptying is a condition where stomach contents empty slowly, affecting the optimal timing of rapid‑acting insulin administration.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-14772c7de5db762c492a75a1c744dae6</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_fiasp.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786316102</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Meal Initiation">
  <data key="d0">Meal Initiation</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Meal Initiation is the start of a meal, the time point at which rapid‑acting insulin such as Fiasp® should be administered (within 20 minutes).</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-14772c7de5db762c492a75a1c744dae6</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_fiasp.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786316103</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Insulina basal diária">
  <data key="d0">Insulina basal diária</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Insulina basal diária refers to the daily basal insulin regimen used as background therapy in diabetes management.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9ff211ed5ca723fa2074871af58a4eb8</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_fiasp.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786316104</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Diabetes mellitus tipo 2">
  <data key="d0">Diabetes mellitus tipo 2</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Diabetes mellitus tipo 2 is a chronic metabolic disease targeted in the effectiveness assessment of Fiasp®.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9ff211ed5ca723fa2074871af58a4eb8</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_fiasp.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786316105</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Diabetes mellitus tipo 1">
  <data key="d0">Diabetes mellitus tipo 1</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Diabetes mellitus tipo 1 is a chronic metabolic disease of patients enrolled in a 26‑week basal‑bolus clinical study.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9ff211ed5ca723fa2074871af58a4eb8</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_fiasp.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786316105</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Insulina detemir">
  <data key="d0">Insulina detemir</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Insulina detemir is a long‑acting insulin used in combination with either Fiasp® or NovoRapid® in the study regimens.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9ff211ed5ca723fa2074871af58a4eb8</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_fiasp.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786316105</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Frasco Bula do Profissional (CCDS v.10_v.3)">
  <data key="d0">Frasco Bula do Profissional (CCDS v.10_v.3)</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Frasco Bula do Profissional (CCDS v.10_v.3) is the professional prescribing information sheet cited for Fiasp®.&lt;SEP&gt;Frasco Bula do Profissional (CCDS v.10_v.3) is a professional prescribing information document for the insulin products.&lt;SEP&gt;Frasco Bula do Profissional (CCDS v.10_v.3) is a professional labeling document referenced for Fiasp®.&lt;SEP&gt;The professional label (bula) providing detailed product information for Fiasp® and its devices.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9ff211ed5ca723fa2074871af58a4eb8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-77c1608c27e3114f3a14f175efe260a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d5bb996e52cb71f15bc8c30d1b1d321&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7fdc648ec086061141581e27adde6fc4</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_fiasp.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786316106</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Fiasp® FlexTouch®">
  <data key="d0">Fiasp® FlexTouch®</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Fiasp® FlexTouch® is a branded, pen‑type prefilled delivery system that combines the fast‑acting insulin product Fiasp® with the FlexTouch® prefilled pen injector. The device is marketed as a rapid‑acting insulin pen, enabling subcutaneous administration of the Fiasp® formulation in a convenient, ready‑to‑use format. It is referenced in clinical study documentation, professional labeling, and medical instructions for injection as the specific pen‑based delivery system for Fiasp® insulin.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a557234bf75633a4af048115a6f0c449&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-14772c7de5db762c492a75a1c744dae6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9ff211ed5ca723fa2074871af58a4eb8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-77c1608c27e3114f3a14f175efe260a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-add4469fba80232b7c0742f24c0914c9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dd25c8bd4672601d6ee40e4b7e28a69c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3a70857656e32cc73aaa270a75eb33af&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2073bddd90c7dd8e156b67821f0f3247&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6c32255a7f064c18ff0b079798cfeaf5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6a7ca48868f79f7be782198d67ffefd0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-09d60e0b850d87c77dd67ca2d709912c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7fdc648ec086061141581e27adde6fc4</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_fiasp.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786316106</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Estudo clínico de 26 semanas">
  <data key="d0">Estudo clínico de 26 semanas</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">Estudo clínico de 26 semanas is a basal‑bolus clinical trial assessing Fiasp®, NovoRapid®, and insulin detemir in diabetes patients.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9ff211ed5ca723fa2074871af58a4eb8</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_fiasp.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786316106</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="GPC">
  <data key="d0">GPC</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">GPC appears in the context of reporting the observed rate of severe hypoglycemia per patient‑year.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9ff211ed5ca723fa2074871af58a4eb8</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_fiasp.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786316106</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Taxa observada de hipoglicemia grave">
  <data key="d0">Taxa observada de hipoglicemia grave</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Taxa observada de hipoglicemia grave is the observed percentage of patients experiencing severe hypoglycemia during the study.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9ff211ed5ca723fa2074871af58a4eb8</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_fiasp.pdf</data>
