  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_fiasp.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786316116</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Damaged Needle">
  <data key="d0">Damaged Needle</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Damaged Needle describes a needle that is physically impaired, potentially obstructing insulin delivery.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-dd25c8bd4672601d6ee40e4b7e28a69c</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_fiasp.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786316116</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Injection">
  <data key="d0">Injection</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">Injection is the procedure of delivering insulin into the skin using the needle and application system.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-dd25c8bd4672601d6ee40e4b7e28a69c</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_fiasp.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786316116</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="FIASP®">
  <data key="d0">FIASP®</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">FIASP® is a medication examined in various regimens, combined with insulin degludeca, and associated with hypoglycemia rates and injection‑site adverse events.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3a70857656e32cc73aaa270a75eb33af</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_fiasp.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786316116</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Insulina Degludeca">
  <data key="d0">Insulina Degludeca</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Insulina degludeca is a long‑acting insulin analogue used in combination with FIASP® or NovoRapid® in the reported studies.&lt;SEP&gt;An ultra‑long‑acting insulin analogue.&lt;SEP&gt;Insulina Degludeca is an ultra‑long‑acting insulin analogue evaluated in the BEGIN Flex T1 trial with flexible dosing schedules.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3a70857656e32cc73aaa270a75eb33af&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-60530d1861f7c2d1efecc069c0913d37&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-95c81e7ab8160456d9a63a9e0868205b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_fiasp.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/Insulinoterapia – Diretriz da Sociedade Brasileira de Diabetes – Ed. 2024.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786331404</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hipoglicemia Geral">
  <data key="d0">Hipoglicemia Geral</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Hipoglicemia geral denotes the overall occurrence of hypoglycemia, reported as 96.2% for FIASP® + insulina degludeca, 96.9% for FIASP® + insulina degludeca post‑prandial, and 96.5% for NovoRapid® + insulina degludeca.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3a70857656e32cc73aaa270a75eb33af</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_fiasp.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786316116</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="ISPAD">
  <data key="d0">ISPAD</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">ISPAD (International Society for Pediatric and Adolescent Diabetes) provides the classification used to define hipoglicemia grave.&lt;SEP&gt;International Society for Pediatric and Adolescent Diabetes, author of the 2018 clinical practice consensus guidelines.&lt;SEP&gt;ISPAD (International Society for Pediatric and Adolescent Diabetes) issues diabetes guidelines, including an HbA1c target of ≤7%.&lt;SEP&gt;ISPAD is the International Society for Pediatric and Adolescent Diabetes, providing consensus recommendations on ketone monitoring.&lt;SEP&gt;ISPAD (International Society for Pediatric and Adolescent Diabetes) is an organization that authored clinical practice consensus guidelines for monogenic diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3a70857656e32cc73aaa270a75eb33af&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5bd45744c4c50bb97abce1352018de47&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7823719c01e7c914b4a58a1bb0d707bd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-276b766b8d515b1e7f388b5b7381bfbc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5c23c0554362bde8c591c91d4a0185a0</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_fiasp.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/cgm.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786372985</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Amiloidose Cutânea">
  <data key="d0">Amiloidose Cutânea</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Amiloidose Cutânea is a form of cutaneous amyloidosis characterized by the deposition of amyloid protein in the skin, most commonly observed at sites where insulin is repeatedly injected. The condition appears in post‑marketing safety data for insulin products such as Levemir® and Novolin® R Penfill®, and it is listed as an adverse skin reaction of unknown frequency associated with insulin therapy in general. The amyloid deposits can form a palpable or visible skin lesion and may interfere with local insulin absorption, potentially delaying the drug’s pharmacologic effect.

The reaction is thought to result from chronic exposure of the same injection area to insulin, leading to protein accumulation in the dermis. Because the exact incidence of Amiloidose Cutânea has not been established, it is considered a rare but recognized adverse event in the context of long‑term insulin use.

Clinical guidance emphasizes that the risk of Amiloidose Cutânea can be reduced by rotating injection sites regularly, thereby minimizing repeated trauma and protein deposition in any single area of skin. Proper rotation of injection sites is therefore recommended as a practical preventive measure for patients receiving insulin therapy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3a70857656e32cc73aaa270a75eb33af&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-45ee3dcb366c1301c9fb1d2ce9f323c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a49c8461f43dc12d7df9c921efeb0465&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9bcc4202330d45ebfca8f79c3d4998b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8a68ba1e8cc1defda76cde0eff9592e6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d01ed6a801b11c1b53f4668059c1f9cb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3396320470ee682ec5cc4f70ab001ef4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d6101c469482b48e341b4095a54907fd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0b4034f7cf7e37425b7c76f5e0f9fd11&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0689fd73d2061ee466b9b90e03bda141&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-786395f3716fb61a79fd183c63e1a9d6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a7ca732691e1cbcafd65e378b8d80144</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_fiasp.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786318452</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
