<node id="Acute Painful Peripheral Neuropathy">
  <data key="d0">Acute Painful Peripheral Neuropathy</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Acute painful peripheral neuropathy is a nerve condition that may appear transiently after rapid glycemic control improvement.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d10a1f849386df540104c79e33a7b242</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_fiasp.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786316122</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Renal Disease">
  <data key="d0">Renal Disease</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Renal disease is a kidney condition mentioned as a comorbid disease that may require insulin dose modifications.&lt;SEP&gt;Kidney disease listed as a comorbidity that can influence glycemia.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d10a1f849386df540104c79e33a7b242&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dd2bfbe7cac15c6f6dc444a35691ae83</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_fiasp.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/Orientacoes_Hipoglicemia_SBD_transcricao.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1786338252</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hepatic Disease">
  <data key="d0">Hepatic Disease</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Hepatic disease is a liver condition noted as a comorbid disease that may require insulin dose modifications.&lt;SEP&gt;Liver disease listed as a comorbidity that can influence glycemia.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d10a1f849386df540104c79e33a7b242&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dd2bfbe7cac15c6f6dc444a35691ae83</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_fiasp.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/Orientacoes_Hipoglicemia_SBD_transcricao.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1786338253</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Adrenal Gland Disease">
  <data key="d0">Adrenal Gland Disease</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Adrenal gland disease is a disorder of the adrenal glands referenced as a comorbid condition that may necessitate insulin dose adjustments.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d10a1f849386df540104c79e33a7b242</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_fiasp.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786316122</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Pituitary Disease">
  <data key="d0">Pituitary Disease</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Pituitary disease is a disorder of the pituitary gland listed among conditions that may require modification of insulin dosing.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d10a1f849386df540104c79e33a7b242</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_fiasp.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786316122</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Thyroid Disease">
  <data key="d0">Thyroid Disease</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Thyroid disease is a disorder of the thyroid gland mentioned as a comorbidity that may affect insulin dose requirements.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d10a1f849386df540104c79e33a7b242</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_fiasp.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786316123</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Antidiabetic Medication Dose Adjustment">
  <data key="d0">Antidiabetic Medication Dose Adjustment</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Adjustment of antidiabetic medication dose is a therapeutic change considered after injection‑site reactions or antibody formation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d10a1f849386df540104c79e33a7b242</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_fiasp.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786316123</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Insulin Dose Adjustment">
  <data key="d0">Insulin Dose Adjustment</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Insulin dose adjustment is the modification of insulin amount in response to factors such as antibodies, pregnancy, or comorbid disease.&lt;SEP&gt;Changes made to insulin dosing based on data review and clinical judgement.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d10a1f849386df540104c79e33a7b242&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c93787ffd2c022283fc0663decb1a184</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_fiasp.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/blood glucose monitoring.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786335929</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Contraindicações">
  <data key="d0">Contraindicações</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Contraindicações is a section of the Bula listing conditions under which the Fiasp medication should not be used.&lt;SEP&gt;Contraindicações is the section detailing situations where the medication should not be used.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-53644541333e5ca7f2785d80235d27e9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-759c20cc4c3fc0d3529aabc2fe7dbf99</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_fiasp.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786317645</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cuidados de Armazenamento do Medicamento">
  <data key="d0">Cuidados de Armazenamento do Medicamento</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Cuidados de armazenamento do medicamento is a section of the Bula giving guidance on how to store the Fiasp medication.&lt;SEP&gt;Cuidados de Armazenamento do Medicamento are the storage‑care guidelines listed in the notifications.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-53644541333e5ca7f2785d80235d27e9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-813e7e990dba10e8d4147252f6547423</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_fiasp.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786318469</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Identificação do Medicamento">
  <data key="d0">Identificação do Medicamento</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Identificação do medicamento is a section of the Bula that provides the name, form, and composition details of the Fiasp medication.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-53644541333e5ca7f2785d80235d27e9</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_fiasp.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786316124</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Oral Antidiabetic Medications">
  <data key="d0">Oral Antidiabetic Medications</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Oral antidiabetic medications are a class of drugs that can reduce the need for insulin.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6c32255a7f064c18ff0b079798cfeaf5</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_fiasp.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786316124</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Beta-Blockers">
  <data key="d0">Beta-Blockers</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Beta‑blockers are medications that can reduce insulin need and may mask hypoglycemia symptoms.&lt;SEP&gt;Beta‑blockers are medications that may blunt the clinical signs of hypoglycemia.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6c32255a7f064c18ff0b079798cfeaf5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1e622f0079074cd1916470223d22aa66</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_fiasp.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786319708</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Octreotide/Lanreotide">
  <data key="d0">Octreotide/Lanreotide</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Octreotide/Lanreotide are peptide analogs that may either increase or decrease insulin needs.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6c32255a7f064c18ff0b079798cfeaf5</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_fiasp.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786316126</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Fiasp® Penfill®">
  <data key="d0">Fiasp® Penfill®</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Fiasp® Penfill® is a cartridge‑based delivery format of the Fiasp® insulin medication.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6c32255a7f064c18ff0b079798cfeaf5</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_fiasp.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786316126</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Fiasp® Frasco">
  <data key="d0">Fiasp® Frasco</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Fiasp® Frasco is the bottle presentation of the Fiasp® insulin solution.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6c32255a7f064c18ff0b079798cfeaf5</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_fiasp.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786316126</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Infusion Pumps">
  <data key="d0">Infusion Pumps</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Infusion pumps are devices used to administer insulin via continuous subcutaneous infusion.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6c32255a7f064c18ff0b079798cfeaf5</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_fiasp.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786316126</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Transport Packaging">
  <data key="d0">Transport Packaging</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Transport packaging provides thermal and light protection for medication during shipment.&lt;SEP&gt;Transport Packaging is a container that provides thermal stability, blocks direct light, and minimizes vibration during medication transport.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6c32255a7f064c18ff0b079798cfeaf5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-df616353e032c899b02bfa4368bc2667</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_fiasp.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786318530</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Risk Category A">
  <data key="d0">Risk Category A</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Risk Category A denotes that the medication can be used during pregnancy under medical supervision.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6c32255a7f064c18ff0b079798cfeaf5</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_fiasp.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786316127</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Medical Prescription">
  <data key="d0">Medical Prescription</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Medical prescription refers to the requirement that the medication be prescribed by a physician for use in pregnancy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6c32255a7f064c18ff0b079798cfeaf5</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_fiasp.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786316127</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Dentist Prescription">
  <data key="d0">Dentist Prescription</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Dentist prescription indicates that a dental professional may also prescribe the medication during pregnancy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6c32255a7f064c18ff0b079798cfeaf5</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_fiasp.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786316127</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Human Milk Donation">
  <data key="d0">Human Milk Donation</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Human milk donation is the practice of donating breast milk, which is compatible with the use of the medication during lactation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6c32255a7f064c18ff0b079798cfeaf5</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_fiasp.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786316127</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Light Protection">
  <data key="d0">Light Protection</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Light protection is a storage requirement to shield the medication from direct illumination.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6c32255a7f064c18ff0b079798cfeaf5</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_fiasp.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786316127</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Refrigerated Storage (2‑8 °C)">
  <data key="d0">Refrigerated Storage (2‑8 °C)</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Refrigerated storage specifies keeping the medication between 2 °C and 8 °C before it is opened.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6c32255a7f064c18ff0b079798cfeaf5</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_fiasp.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786316128</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Ambient Temperature Storage (15‑30 °C)">
  <data key="d0">Ambient Temperature Storage (15‑30 °C)</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Ambient temperature storage allows the medication to be kept between 15 °C and 30 °C after opening.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6c32255a7f064c18ff0b079798cfeaf5</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_fiasp.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786316128</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Shelf Life 30 Months">
  <data key="d0">Shelf Life 30 Months</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Shelf life 30 months is the period from manufacture during which the medication remains valid if unopened.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6c32255a7f064c18ff0b079798cfeaf5</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_fiasp.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786316128</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Opened Vial Shelf Life 4 Weeks">
  <data key="d0">Opened Vial Shelf Life 4 Weeks</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Opened vial shelf life 4 weeks defines the timeframe the medication can be used after the container is opened or placed in a pump reservoir.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6c32255a7f064c18ff0b079798cfeaf5</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_fiasp.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786316128</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Temperature Threshold 37°C">
  <data key="d0">Temperature Threshold 37°C</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Temperature threshold 37 °C indicates the maximum temperature beyond which the medication must be discarded.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6c32255a7f064c18ff0b079798cfeaf5</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_fiasp.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786316128</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Children Safety">
  <data key="d0">Children Safety</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Children safety emphasizes keeping medication out of reach of children to prevent accidental exposure.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6c32255a7f064c18ff0b079798cfeaf5</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_fiasp.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786316128</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Infusion Set Site Rotation">
  <data key="d0">Infusion Set Site Rotation</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Infusion set site rotation is the practice of changing the infusion set and insertion site according to product instructions.</data>
