<node id="Levemir®">
  <data key="d0">Levemir®</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Levemir® is the commercial brand name for insulin detemir, a soluble long‑acting basal insulin analog used to treat diabetes mellitus. The molecule is a modified human insulin that achieves its prolonged action through self‑association and reversible binding to albumin in the bloodstream, resulting in a relatively stable and less variable glucose‑lowering profile compared with older basal insulins. Levemir® is supplied as a sterile injectable solution, most commonly at a concentration of 100 U/mL, and is described in detail in professional leaflets and medication labeling that include sections on dosage, storage, handling, and safety precautions.

Clinically, Levemir® is indicated for basal insulin therapy in both type 1 and type 2 diabetes. It may be administered as monotherapy or in combination with rapid‑acting (bolus) insulin, oral antidiabetic agents, or glucagon‑like peptide‑1 (GLP‑1) receptor agonists to achieve comprehensive glycaemic control in adults. The product has been evaluated in numerous clinical studies, including trials that specifically examined its efficacy, safety, and dosing adjustments in pregnant women with pre‑existing type 1 diabetes, as well as investigations comparing maternal and infant outcomes during pregnancy. Although a single description mistakenly referred to Levemir® as insulin glargine, the overwhelming consensus in the source material confirms that Levemir® is insulin detemir, not insulin glargine.

Adverse reactions associated with Levemir® are generally dose‑dependent and stem from its pharmacological insulin effect. Commonly reported events include hypoglycaemia, injection‑site reactions (such as erythema, lipodystrophy, or induration), and other insulin‑related side effects. The professional leaflet notes that the frequency and severity of these reactions can vary with the administered dose and patient‑specific factors. Overall, Levemir® is characterized as a basal insulin product that provides prolonged glucose control with a predictable pharmacodynamic profile, making it a widely used option in diabetes management across diverse patient populations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-50a4f77ab697e068f8cf31533065722b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-00cf434060561bb7d46b6ce50f095c91&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8ef15154a94043650617b3b24d8146a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5e7e47ca39ac4f4975da2b4b7e6d3c36&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-68b98187c6ab15468f1c0d8f5e7f9f6a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f36263c657ad99a80e578ac49a333d5b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-45ee3dcb366c1301c9fb1d2ce9f323c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fdee4bcd64faa476dd057e21e2525e53&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cedd8e88a8d35eade68ce02222b9e276&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-922791f49d1bf928fe4f02ddd336927b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e5f5165b3185feb3c6ec93a3c0ef8d02&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-767d025776f0f59c05788e25616f412c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-831f4bbfc884fc8e9679630a819083e9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-01fb767ae3a103c9d6c4775570df90c9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3237e202569462c758ec3d878c9faeae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-759c20cc4c3fc0d3529aabc2fe7dbf99&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-42ddf181cf4422a3b24643a2252d99b0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9bcc4202330d45ebfca8f79c3d4998b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8a68ba1e8cc1defda76cde0eff9592e6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3059be019782459a72891cea5e0434ea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b4d7abd3e1e5418ee5a931e28a18e8ad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-56fc1d5df1b34d9120c3cf8a760c40f9</data>
