<node id="Glicose">
  <data key="d0">Glicose</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Glicose (glucose) is administered orally or intravenously to treat mild hypoglycemia or when glucagon fails.&lt;SEP&gt;Glucose, the sugar whose plasma concentration is regulated by insulin.&lt;SEP&gt;Glicose is a glucose solution administered orally or intravenously to treat mild to moderate hypoglycemia.&lt;SEP&gt;Glicose is a carbohydrate administered orally or intravenously to treat mild to moderate hypoglycemia.&lt;SEP&gt;Glicose is the sugar measured in blood and interstitial fluid for diabetes monitoring.&lt;SEP&gt;Glicose is the blood sugar measured in mg/dL, with specific thresholds defining hypoglycemia levels.</data>
