  <data key="d5">1786317621</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Levemir FlexPen">
  <data key="d0">Levemir FlexPen</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Levemir FlexPen is a reusable insulin injection device referenced in the professional guide for administering insulin.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ddb8954aaa1e1230598596ce6f5df249</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786317621</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Levemir Penfill">
  <data key="d0">Levemir Penfill</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Levemir Penfill is a disposable insulin delivery system containing insulin detemir solution in multiple cartridges.&lt;SEP&gt;Levemir® Penfill® is a delivery device described in the professional prescribing information for Levemir®.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ddb8954aaa1e1230598596ce6f5df249&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0ace26fdb0244e3d0f714a007c9bbb51</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786317622</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Button Injector">
  <data key="d0">Button Injector</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The button injector is the push‑button on the pen that, when fully depressed, releases the insulin dose.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ddb8954aaa1e1230598596ce6f5df249</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786317622</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="DNA Recombinant Technology">
  <data key="d0">DNA Recombinant Technology</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">DNA recombinant technology is the biotechnological process used to produce insulin detemir in yeast cells.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ddb8954aaa1e1230598596ce6f5df249</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786317623</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Novo Nordisk Farm. do Brasil Ltda.">
  <data key="d0">Novo Nordisk Farm. do Brasil Ltda.</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Novo Nordisk Farm. do Brasil Ltda. is the pharmaceutical company that manufactures Levemir FlexPen and Penfill.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ddb8954aaa1e1230598596ce6f5df249</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786317624</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Insulin Detemir Solution (100 U/mL)">
  <data key="d0">Insulin Detemir Solution (100 U/mL)</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The insulin detemir solution is a sterile liquid containing 100 units of insulin per milliliter, supplied for injection.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ddb8954aaa1e1230598596ce6f5df249</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786317624</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Basal‑Bolus Therapy">
  <data key="d0">Basal‑Bolus Therapy</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Basal‑bolus therapy is an insulin regimen that pairs a long‑acting basal insulin with rapid‑acting bolus insulin to control blood glucose.&lt;SEP&gt;Basal‑bolus therapy is an insulin regimen combining long‑acting and rapid‑acting insulin, mentioned in detemir studies.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ddb8954aaa1e1230598596ce6f5df249&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e7e6ca9bf63e843b814736c0409c70fb</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/Insulinoterapia – Diretriz da Sociedade Brasileira de Diabetes – Ed. 2024.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786331410</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Needle Disposal">
  <data key="d0">Needle Disposal</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Needle Disposal is the safe process of discarding used needles to prevent injury, contamination, and cross‑infection.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ddb8954aaa1e1230598596ce6f5df249</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786317625</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Sharing Prohibition">
  <data key="d0">Sharing Prohibition</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Sharing Prohibition is the rule that needles and insulin pens must not be shared between individuals to avoid cross‑infection.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ddb8954aaa1e1230598596ce6f5df249</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786317625</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Dose‑Dependent Glucose Reduction">
  <data key="d0">Dose‑Dependent Glucose Reduction</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Dose‑Dependent Glucose Reduction describes how the glucose‑lowering effect of insulin detemir increases proportionally with the administered dose.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ddb8954aaa1e1230598596ce6f5df249</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786317625</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Incomplete Dose">
  <data key="d0">Incomplete Dose</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Incomplete Dose is a situation where the insulin dose is not fully administered because the dose selector stops before reaching zero.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ddb8954aaa1e1230598596ce6f5df249</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786317625</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Study NN 2211‑1842">
  <data key="d0">Study NN 2211‑1842</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Study NN 2211‑1842 is a 26‑week, randomised, open‑label, multinational trial comparing insulin detemir combined with liraglutide and metformin versus liraglutide and metformin alone in type 2 diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e5f5165b3185feb3c6ec93a3c0ef8d02</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786317625</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Study NN 304‑1687">
  <data key="d0">Study NN 304‑1687</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Study NN 304‑1687 is a randomised, parallel‑group, open‑label multinational trial comparing levemir (insulin detemir) with human NPH insulin, both combined with insulin aspart, in pregnant women with type 1 diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e5f5165b3185feb3c6ec93a3c0ef8d02</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786317626</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Study NN 1250‑3561">
  <data key="d0">Study NN 1250‑3561</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Study NN 1250‑3561 is a randomised, multicentre, two‑arm parallel group, treat‑to‑target trial comparing insulin degludec (IDeg) and insulin detemir (IDet) as basal insulin with insulin aspart bolus in subjects aged 1 to &lt;18 years with type 1 diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e5f5165b3185feb3c6ec93a3c0ef8d02</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786317626</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Study NN2211‑3917">
  <data key="d0">Study NN2211‑3917</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Study NN2211‑3917 is a 26‑week, double‑blind, placebo‑controlled, randomised, multinational parallel‑group trial assessing liraglutide versus placebo added to basal insulin analogues with or without metformin in type 2 diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e5f5165b3185feb3c6ec93a3c0ef8d02</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786317626</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Diabetic Medicine">
  <data key="d0">Diabetic Medicine</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Diabetic Medicine is a peer‑reviewed journal cited for studies comparing insulin detemir with NPH insulin.&lt;SEP&gt;Diabetic Medicine is a peer‑reviewed medical journal that published a study on insulin detemir versus NPH insulin.&lt;SEP&gt;Diabetic Medicine (Diabet Med) is a journal reporting comparative studies of insulin detemir and glargine.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e5f5165b3185feb3c6ec93a3c0ef8d02&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-42ddf181cf4422a3b24643a2252d99b0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e7e6ca9bf63e843b814736c0409c70fb</data>
