</node>
<node id="AUCGIR">
  <data key="d0">AUCGIR</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">AUCGIR (0‑24 h) is a pharmacodynamic metric reported for insulin detemir, NPH insulin, and insulin glargine.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e5f5165b3185feb3c6ec93a3c0ef8d02</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786317629</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="GIRmax">
  <data key="d0">GIRmax</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">GIRmax is a pharmacodynamic metric reported for insulin detemir, NPH insulin, and insulin glargine.&lt;SEP&gt;GIRmax is the maximal glucose infusion rate observed in pharmacodynamic testing, reported in Table 4 for Levemir®, NPH insulin and insulin glargina.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e5f5165b3185feb3c6ec93a3c0ef8d02&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-01fb767ae3a103c9d6c4775570df90c9</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786317629</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Lower Variability">
  <data key="d0">Lower Variability</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Lower variability describes the reduced intra‑individual variability of insulin detemir’s action profile compared with NPH insulin.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e5f5165b3185feb3c6ec93a3c0ef8d02</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786317630</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Intraindividual Variability">
  <data key="d0">Intraindividual Variability</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Intraindividual variability refers to the variability of insulin action within the same individual across dosing events.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e5f5165b3185feb3c6ec93a3c0ef8d02</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786317630</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Proportional Dose‑Response Relationship">
  <data key="d0">Proportional Dose‑Response Relationship</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Proportional dose‑response relationship describes the linear relationship between insulin dose and glucose‑lowering effect observed for insulin detemir and NPH insulin.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e5f5165b3185feb3c6ec93a3c0ef8d02</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786317630</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Treat‑to‑Target Basal‑Bolus Regimen">
  <data key="d0">Treat‑to‑Target Basal‑Bolus Regimen</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Treat‑to‑target basal‑bolus regimen is an insulin therapy strategy using basal insulin (e.g., detemir) and bolus insulin (e.g., aspart) to achieve specific glucose targets.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e5f5165b3185feb3c6ec93a3c0ef8d02</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786317630</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Randomised Controlled Trial">
  <data key="d0">Randomised Controlled Trial</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Randomised controlled trial is a study design employed in multiple cited investigations of insulin detemir.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e5f5165b3185feb3c6ec93a3c0ef8d02</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786317630</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
