<node id="Women With Type 1 Diabetes">
  <data key="d0">Women With Type 1 Diabetes</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Women with type 1 diabetes are pregnant patients enrolled in a randomized controlled trial comparing Levemir® and insulin NPH.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-767d025776f0f59c05788e25616f412c</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786317634</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Women With Type 2 Diabetes">
  <data key="d0">Women With Type 2 Diabetes</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Women with type 2 diabetes are pregnant patients enrolled in a prospective post‑authorization safety study comparing Levemir® with other basal insulins.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-767d025776f0f59c05788e25616f412c</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786317634</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Perinatal Death">
  <data key="d0">Perinatal Death</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Perinatal death encompasses fetal deaths occurring around the time of birth, monitored as an adverse pregnancy outcome.&lt;SEP&gt;Perinatal Death refers to fetal or neonatal death linked to early abnormal glucose metabolism.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-767d025776f0f59c05788e25616f412c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-83d72fbc44fe0c28f27702c0d4f2c140</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377414</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Neonatal Death">
  <data key="d0">Neonatal Death</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Neonatal death refers to death of the newborn within the first 28 days, tracked as an adverse outcome.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-767d025776f0f59c05788e25616f412c</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786317635</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Fetal Macrosomia">
  <data key="d0">Fetal Macrosomia</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Fetal macrosomia denotes excessive fetal growth, evaluated among pregnancy adverse outcomes.&lt;SEP&gt;Fetal macrosomia is a condition of excessive fetal growth associated with MODY-HNF4A.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-767d025776f0f59c05788e25616f412c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e26b32d53b78f97e8d7fa8b815f2cc87</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786373056</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Premature Birth">
  <data key="d0">Premature Birth</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Premature birth is delivery before full term, recorded as an adverse pregnancy outcome.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-767d025776f0f59c05788e25616f412c</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786317635</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Prospective Safety Post‑Authorization Study">
  <data key="d0">Prospective Safety Post‑Authorization Study</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">A prospective safety post‑authorization non‑interventional study monitored pregnant women using Levemir® or other basal insulins for adverse outcomes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-767d025776f0f59c05788e25616f412c</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786317635</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Randomized Controlled Clinical Trial">
  <data key="d0">Randomized Controlled Clinical Trial</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A randomized controlled clinical trial compared Levemir® with insulin NPH in pregnant women with type 1 diabetes.&lt;SEP&gt;A study design employed to compare insulin pens versus syringes in elderly patients with type 2 diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-767d025776f0f59c05788e25616f412c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-651d85a13edd23f654d52f95c75d4e32</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/blood glucose monitoring.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786335971</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Risk Difference">
  <data key="d0">Risk Difference</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Risk difference is the statistical measure (e.g., 0.015 with 95% CI) comparing the incidence of adverse pregnancy outcomes between Levemir® and other basal insulins.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-767d025776f0f59c05788e25616f412c</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786317635</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Body Weight Change">
  <data key="d0">Body Weight Change</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Body weight change refers to the reduction in body weight during the study, recorded as –3.47 kg versus –0.43 kg.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-767d025776f0f59c05788e25616f412c</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786317636</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Spontaneous Abortion">
  <data key="d0">Spontaneous Abortion</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Spontaneous abortion is a pregnancy loss not induced intentionally, listed among adverse pregnancy outcomes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-767d025776f0f59c05788e25616f412c</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786317636</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Large for Gestational Age">
  <data key="d0">Large for Gestational Age</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Large for gestational age describes fetuses whose size exceeds normative limits for their pregnancy age, evaluated as an adverse outcome.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-767d025776f0f59c05788e25616f412c</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786317636</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Infant Diabetes at One Year">
  <data key="d0">Infant Diabetes at One Year</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Infant diabetes at one year denotes the presence of diabetes in the baby at twelve months of age, monitored as a post‑natal outcome.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-767d025776f0f59c05788e25616f412c</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786317636</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Fetuses">
  <data key="d0">Fetuses</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Fetuses are the unborn offspring counted in each treatment group (e.g., 741 in the Levemir® group, 740 in the other basal insulin group).</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-767d025776f0f59c05788e25616f412c</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786317636</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Maternal Adverse Events">
  <data key="d0">Maternal Adverse Events</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Maternal adverse events refer to any undesirable health occurrences in pregnant women during the trial.&lt;SEP&gt;Maternal adverse events are any negative health occurrences experienced by pregnant women during the studies.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-767d025776f0f59c05788e25616f412c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b4d7abd3e1e5418ee5a931e28a18e8ad</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786317636</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Serious Adverse Events">
  <data key="d0">Serious Adverse Events</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Serious adverse events are severe health problems occurring during pregnancy, reported with higher numerical frequency in the Levemir® group.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-767d025776f0f59c05788e25616f412c</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786317637</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Week 24 of Pregnancy">
  <data key="d0">Week 24 of Pregnancy</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">Week 24 of pregnancy is a study time point at which HbA1c targets and fasting glucose levels were evaluated.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-767d025776f0f59c05788e25616f412c</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786317637</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Week 36 of Pregnancy">
  <data key="d0">Week 36 of Pregnancy</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">Week 36 of pregnancy is a study time point used to assess HbA1c non‑inferiority between Levemir® and insulin NPH.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-767d025776f0f59c05788e25616f412c</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786317637</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Erythema">
  <data key="d0">Erythema</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Erythema is a skin redness reaction identified among Levemir®’s adverse effects.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-831f4bbfc884fc8e9679630a819083e9</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786317638</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cutaneous Eruptions">
  <data key="d0">Cutaneous Eruptions</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Cutaneous eruptions are skin manifestations reported as adverse reactions to Levemir®.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-831f4bbfc884fc8e9679630a819083e9</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786317638</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Amyloidosis Cutânea">
  <data key="d0">Amyloidosis Cutânea</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Amyloidosis Cutânea is a cutaneous amyloid deposition noted as a possible adverse effect of Levemir®.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-831f4bbfc884fc8e9679630a819083e9</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786317638</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="SAC 0800 0144488">
  <data key="d0">SAC 0800 0144488</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">SAC 0800 0144488 is the customer service telephone number provided for Levemir® inquiries.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-831f4bbfc884fc8e9679630a819083e9</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786317638</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Neuropathic Pain">
  <data key="d0">Neuropathic Pain</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Acute painful neuropathy may occur with rapid improvement of glycemic control during Levemir® therapy and is generally reversible.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0ace26fdb0244e3d0f714a007c9bbb51</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786317640</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="NPH insulin">
  <data key="d0">NPH insulin</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">NPH insulin is an intermediate‑acting human insulin used as a basal insulin comparator in clinical trials.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-01fb767ae3a103c9d6c4775570df90c9</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786317641</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Insulin glargina">
  <data key="d0">Insulin glargina</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Insulin glargina is a long‑acting basal insulin analogue used as a comparator for variability assessments.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-01fb767ae3a103c9d6c4775570df90c9</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786317641</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Insulin aspart">
  <data key="d0">Insulin aspart</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Insulin aspart (IAsp) is a rapid‑acting insulin used as bolus insulin in combination therapy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-01fb767ae3a103c9d6c4775570df90c9</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786317641</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="IDeg">
  <data key="d0">IDeg</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">IDeg is a basal insulin analogue (insulin degludec) evaluated in clinical trials as a comparator to IDet.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-01fb767ae3a103c9d6c4775570df90c9</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786317641</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="IDet">
  <data key="d0">IDet</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">IDet refers to insulin detemir, the active ingredient of Levemir®, evaluated as a basal insulin in trials.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-01fb767ae3a103c9d6c4775570df90c9</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786317641</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Study NN 2211-1842">
  <data key="d0">Study NN 2211-1842</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">Study NN 2211-1842 evaluated insulin detemir combined with liraglutide and metformin versus liraglutide and metformin alone in type 2 diabetes.&lt;SEP&gt;Study NN 2211-1842 is a 26‑week, randomised, open‑label, parallel‑group, multicentre, multinational trial assessing insulin detemir combined with liraglutide and metformin versus liraglutide and metformin in type 2 diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-01fb767ae3a103c9d6c4775570df90c9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b4d7abd3e1e5418ee5a931e28a18e8ad</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786317641</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Study NN 304-1687">
  <data key="d0">Study NN 304-1687</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">Study NN 304-1687 is a randomized trial referenced without further detail in the text.&lt;SEP&gt;Study NN 304-1687 is a randomised, parallel‑group, open‑label, multinational trial comparing Levemir® with NPH insulin, both combined with insulin aspart, for treating pregnant women with type 1 diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-01fb767ae3a103c9d6c4775570df90c9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b4d7abd3e1e5418ee5a931e28a18e8ad</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786317641</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Study NN 1250-3561">
  <data key="d0">Study NN 1250-3561</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">Study NN 1250-3561 is a randomised, multinational, multicentre, two‑arm parallel group, treat‑to‑target safety and efficacy trial comparing IDeg and IDet as basal insulin together with IAsp in subjects with type 1 diabetes aged 1 to &lt;18 years.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-01fb767ae3a103c9d6c4775570df90c9</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786317641</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Study NN2211-3917">
  <data key="d0">Study NN2211-3917</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">Study NN2211-3917 is a 26‑week double‑blind, placebo‑controlled, randomised, multicentre, multinational parallel‑group trial evaluating liraglutide versus placebo added to basal insulin analogues with or without metformin in type 2 diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-01fb767ae3a103c9d6c4775570df90c9</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786317641</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="AUCGIR (0-24h)">
  <data key="d0">AUCGIR (0-24h)</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">AUCGIR (0‑24h) is a pharmacodynamic data metric representing glucose infusion rate over 24 hours, reported in Table 4 for Levemir®, NPH insulin and insulin glargina.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-01fb767ae3a103c9d6c4775570df90c9</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786317641</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Randomised Parallel-Group Multinational Trial">
  <data key="d0">Randomised Parallel-Group Multinational Trial</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Randomised Parallel-Group Multinational Trial denotes a study design involving random allocation, parallel groups, and multinational sites, used in several listed studies.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-01fb767ae3a103c9d6c4775570df90c9</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786317642</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Double-blind Placebo-Controlled Randomised Multicentre Multinational Parallel-Group Trial">
  <data key="d0">Double-blind Placebo-Controlled Randomised Multicentre Multinational Parallel-Group Trial</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Double-blind Placebo-Controlled Randomised Multicentre Multinational Parallel-Group Trial denotes a rigorous study design featuring blinding, placebo control, randomisation, and multiple centres, applied in Study NN2211-3917.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-01fb767ae3a103c9d6c4775570df90c9</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786317642</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Basal Insulin Analogues">
  <data key="d0">Basal Insulin Analogues</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Basal insulin analogues are long‑acting insulin formulations, such as Levemir®, used as background therapy in diabetes trials.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-01fb767ae3a103c9d6c4775570df90c9</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786317642</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Open‑Label">
  <data key="d0">Open‑Label</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Open‑Label denotes a study design in which both investigators and participants are aware of the treatment allocation, mentioned in several trials.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-01fb767ae3a103c9d6c4775570df90c9</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786317642</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Double‑Blind">
  <data key="d0">Double‑Blind</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Double‑Blind describes a study design where neither participants nor investigators know the treatment assignment, used in Study NN2211-3917.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-01fb767ae3a103c9d6c4775570df90c9</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786317642</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Randomised">
  <data key="d0">Randomised</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Randomised indicates that participants are assigned to study arms by chance, a feature of all listed clinical trials.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-01fb767ae3a103c9d6c4775570df90c9</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786317642</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Multicentre">
  <data key="d0">Multicentre</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Multicentre refers to a trial conducted across multiple clinical sites, as noted in the study descriptions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-01fb767ae3a103c9d6c4775570df90c9</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786317643</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Multinational">
  <data key="d0">Multinational</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Multinational describes studies performed in more than one country, referenced in the trial designs.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-01fb767ae3a103c9d6c4775570df90c9</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
