</node>
<node id="2 °C to 8 °C Temperature Range">
  <data key="d0">2 °C to 8 °C Temperature Range</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">The advised storage temperature for Levemir® FlexPen® before opening is between 2 °C and 8 °C.&lt;SEP&gt;The temperature range of 2 °C to 8 °C required for storing closed insulin.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a49c8461f43dc12d7df9c921efeb0465&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e94cedc7134adbb256c931b851235c53</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/Documento sem título.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1786330482</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Ambient Temperature Below 30 °C">
  <data key="d0">Ambient Temperature Below 30 °C</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">After opening, Levemir® FlexPen® may be kept at room temperature provided it does not exceed 30 °C.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a49c8461f43dc12d7df9c921efeb0465</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786317647</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="42 Days Storage Limit">
  <data key="d0">42 Days Storage Limit</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Once opened, Levemir® FlexPen® can be used for a maximum of 42 days (6 weeks).</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a49c8461f43dc12d7df9c921efeb0465</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786317647</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Solução Injetável Aquosa">
  <data key="d0">Solução Injetável Aquosa</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Levemir® FlexPen® is described as a clear, color‑less aqueous injectable solution.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a49c8461f43dc12d7df9c921efeb0465</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786317647</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Agulhas Descartáveis NovoFine®">
  <data key="d0">Agulhas Descartáveis NovoFine®</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Disposable NovoFine® needles up to 8 mm long are the recommended needles for administering Levemir® FlexPen®.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a49c8461f43dc12d7df9c921efeb0465</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786317647</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Bula do Profissional">
  <data key="d0">Bula do Profissional</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">The professional leaflet provides detailed instructions, warnings, and storage information for Levemir® FlexPen®.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a49c8461f43dc12d7df9c921efeb0465</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786317647</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="30 Meses Validity">
  <data key="d0">30 Meses Validity</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Levemir® FlexPen® has a shelf life of 30 months from the date of manufacture.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a49c8461f43dc12d7df9c921efeb0465</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786317647</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Terapia Basal‑Bolus">
  <data key="d0">Terapia Basal‑Bolus</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A treatment regimen that combines basal insulin (such as Levemir®) with rapid‑acting bolus insulin.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a49c8461f43dc12d7df9c921efeb0465</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786317648</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Luz Direta">
  <data key="d0">Luz Direta</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Direct light that can degrade Levemir® FlexPen® and must be avoided during storage.&lt;SEP&gt;Luz direta is direct light exposure that should be avoided during transport of the medication.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a49c8461f43dc12d7df9c921efeb0465&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0689fd73d2061ee466b9b90e03bda141</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786318539</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Calor Excessivo">
  <data key="d0">Calor Excessivo</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Excessive heat that can affect the stability of Levemir® FlexPen® and must be avoided.&lt;SEP&gt;Calor Excessivo refers to excessive heat, which should be avoided for Novolin® R FlexPen® storage.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a49c8461f43dc12d7df9c921efeb0465&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ba6b31518be6fff1db8b68a28e82f200</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786318548</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Freezer Compartment">
  <data key="d0">Freezer Compartment</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The freezer section of a refrigerator where Levemir® FlexPen® must not be stored.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a49c8461f43dc12d7df9c921efeb0465</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786317648</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Congelado">
  <data key="d0">Congelado</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The frozen state of Levemir® FlexPen®, which renders the medication unusable.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a49c8461f43dc12d7df9c921efeb0465</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786317648</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Outras Preparações de Insulina">
  <data key="d0">Outras Preparações de Insulina</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Any other insulin preparations that must not be mixed or diluted with Levemir®.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a49c8461f43dc12d7df9c921efeb0465</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786317648</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Pregnant Women with Diabetes Type 1">
  <data key="d0">Pregnant Women with Diabetes Type 1</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The study population consists of pregnant women diagnosed with Type 1 diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-42ddf181cf4422a3b24643a2252d99b0</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786317648</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Gestational Week 24">
  <data key="d0">Gestational Week 24</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Week 24 of gestation is a time point at which fasting glucose and HbA1c targets were evaluated.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-42ddf181cf4422a3b24643a2252d99b0</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786317649</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Gestational Week 36">
  <data key="d0">Gestational Week 36</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Week 36 of gestation is a later time point used to compare HbA1c levels and fasting glucose between treatment groups.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-42ddf181cf4422a3b24643a2252d99b0</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786317649</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Congenital Malformation Severe">
  <data key="d0">Congenital Malformation Severe</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Severe congenital malformations are major birth defects observed in infants of the study cohorts.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-42ddf181cf4422a3b24643a2252d99b0</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786317649</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Congenital Malformation Mild">
  <data key="d0">Congenital Malformation Mild</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Mild congenital malformations are less serious birth defects reported in the trial.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-42ddf181cf4422a3b24643a2252d99b0</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786317649</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Maternal Serious Adverse Events">
  <data key="d0">Maternal Serious Adverse Events</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Serious adverse events in mothers occurred in 61 (40%) of Levemir® participants versus 49 (31%) of Insulin NPH participants.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-42ddf181cf4422a3b24643a2252d99b0</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786317649</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Infant Serious Adverse Events">
  <data key="d0">Infant Serious Adverse Events</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Serious adverse events in infants occurred in 36 (24%) of Levemir® participants versus 32 (20%) of Insulin NPH participants.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-42ddf181cf4422a3b24643a2252d99b0</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786317649</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="HbA1c Goal Achievement">
  <data key="d0">HbA1c Goal Achievement</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">41 % of participants on Levemir® and 32 % on Insulin NPH achieved HbA1c ≤ 6.0 % at weeks 24 and 36.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-42ddf181cf4422a3b24643a2252d99b0</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786317649</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hypoglycemia Episodes">
  <data key="d0">Hypoglycemia Episodes</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Episodes of hypoglycemia during pregnancy were monitored for safety comparison between the two insulin groups.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-42ddf181cf4422a3b24643a2252d99b0</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786317649</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Pre‑eclampsia Incidence">
  <data key="d0">Pre‑eclampsia Incidence</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Pre‑eclampsia occurred in 10.5 % (16 cases) of the Levemir® group and 7.0 % (11 cases) of the Insulin NPH group.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-42ddf181cf4422a3b24643a2252d99b0</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786317649</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Congenital Malformations Frequency">
  <data key="d0">Congenital Malformations Frequency</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Four infants (5 %) in the Levemir® group and eleven infants (7 %) in the Insulin NPH group had any congenital malformation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-42ddf181cf4422a3b24643a2252d99b0</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786317649</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Severe Congenital Malformations Frequency">
  <data key="d0">Severe Congenital Malformations Frequency</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Three infants (4 %) in the Levemir® group and three infants (2 %) in the Insulin NPH group had severe congenital malformations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-42ddf181cf4422a3b24643a2252d99b0</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786317649</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Levemir® Cord Blood Detection">
  <data key="d0">Levemir® Cord Blood Detection</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Levemir® was detected in cord blood of about one quarter of infants at concentrations above the lower limit of quantification (&lt;25 pmol/L).</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-42ddf181cf4422a3b24643a2252d99b0</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786317649</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Live Births after Randomization">
  <data key="d0">Live Births after Randomization</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Fifty live births (83 %) occurred in the Levemir® group versus fifty‑five (89 %) in the Insulin NPH group.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-42ddf181cf4422a3b24643a2252d99b0</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786317650</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Robertson KJ">
  <data key="d0">Robertson KJ</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Robertson KJ is an author of a study comparing insulin detemir with NPH insulin in children and adolescents.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-42ddf181cf4422a3b24643a2252d99b0</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786317650</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Novo Nordisk Farm. Do Brasil Ltda.">
  <data key="d0">Novo Nordisk Farm. Do Brasil Ltda.</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Novo Nordisk Farm. Do Brasil Ltda. is the Brazilian subsidiary of Novo Nordisk that markets Levemir® FlexPen®.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b65a4249ac93aec086cb333ed1507ea7</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786317650</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="HSI">
  <data key="d0">HSI</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">HSI (Human Soluble Insulin) is a rapid‑acting insulin used as a comparator in combination therapy studies with Levemir® FlexPen®.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b65a4249ac93aec086cb333ed1507ea7</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786317650</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Terapia Basal-Bolus">
  <data key="d0">Terapia Basal-Bolus</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Terapia basal‑bolus is an insulin regimen that can include Levemir® FlexPen®.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b65a4249ac93aec086cb333ed1507ea7</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786317650</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Terapia ADO">
  <data key="d0">Terapia ADO</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Terapia ADO is a combination insulin therapy protocol evaluated with Levemir® FlexPen®.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b65a4249ac93aec086cb333ed1507ea7</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786317651</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="International Unit (UI)">
  <data key="d0">International Unit (UI)</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">International Unit (UI) is the standard measurement equivalent to one unit (U) of insulin detemir.&lt;SEP&gt;International Unit (UI) is a measurement unit used to quantify insulin dosage.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b65a4249ac93aec086cb333ed1507ea7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c0a2dce3852e38344f91c86f45dda403</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786330179</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Tiazolidinedionas">
  <data key="d0">Tiazolidinedionas</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Tiazolidinedionas are a class of drugs that, when combined with insulin, have been associated with congestive heart failure.&lt;SEP&gt;Tiazolidinedionas are a class of oral antidiabetic drugs that can interact with insulin therapy.&lt;SEP&gt;Tiazolidinedionas are a class of antidiabetic drugs mentioned in combination with insulin.&lt;SEP&gt;Tiazolidinedionas are a class of drugs that should be discontinued if cardiac symptoms worsen.&lt;SEP&gt;Tiazolidinedionas are a class of drugs mentioned as being combined with insulins, associated with risk of congestive heart failure.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9bcc4202330d45ebfca8f79c3d4998b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4615ca664e7ff898d8c5929cbc79e7d8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d6101c469482b48e341b4095a54907fd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0851222a21a012cffce7a16710847208&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ba6b31518be6fff1db8b68a28e82f200</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786318512</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Pré-eclâmpsia">
  <data key="d0">Pré-eclâmpsia</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Pré-eclâmpsia is a pregnancy complication with reported incidence rates in the Levemir® and insulin NPH study groups.&lt;SEP&gt;A pregnancy complication characterized by high blood pressure, mentioned as a risk reduced by post‑prandial testing.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9bcc4202330d45ebfca8f79c3d4998b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-91a09040fc4581d7aad2216dba9fba79</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/cgm.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786335249</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Malformações Congênitas">
  <data key="d0">Malformações Congênitas</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Malformações Congênitas are congenital malformations with reported incidence in the Levemir® and insulin NPH study.&lt;SEP&gt;Malformações Congênitas are fetal birth defects, described as risks increased by hypoglycemia and hyperglycemia in poorly controlled diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9bcc4202330d45ebfca8f79c3d4998b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ba6b31518be6fff1db8b68a28e82f200</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786318549</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Dados Pós-comercialização">
  <data key="d0">Dados Pós-comercialização</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Dados Pós-comercialização are post‑marketing safety data involving thousands of pregnancy outcomes with Levemir®.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9bcc4202330d45ebfca8f79c3d4998b3</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786317652</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Ganho de Peso">
  <data key="d0">Ganho de Peso</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Ganho de Peso is a symptom associated with congestive heart failure risk when tiazolidinedionas are combined with insulin.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9bcc4202330d45ebfca8f79c3d4998b3</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786317652</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Capacidade de Dirigir ou Operar Máquinas">
  <data key="d0">Capacidade de Dirigir ou Operar Máquinas</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Capacidade de Dirigir ou Operar Máquinas refers to the ability to drive or operate machinery, noted as potentially affected by insulin therapy.&lt;SEP&gt;Capacidade de Dirigir ou Operar Máquinas refers to the ability to safely drive or operate machinery, which may be impaired by hypoglycemia.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9bcc4202330d45ebfca8f79c3d4998b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d6101c469482b48e341b4095a54907fd</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786318524</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Antidiabetic Drugs">
  <data key="d0">Antidiabetic Drugs</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Antidiabetic Drugs are medications used to control blood glucose that may be administered together with Levemir® and can require dose or timing adjustments.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8a68ba1e8cc1defda76cde0eff9592e6</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786317653</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Reação Anafilática">
  <data key="d0">Reação Anafilática</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Reação Anafilática is a very rare hypersensitivity reaction to Levemir® that can be life‑threatening.&lt;SEP&gt;Reação Anafilática is a very rare anaphylactic reaction that can be life‑threatening when associated with Novolin® R Penfill®.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8a68ba1e8cc1defda76cde0eff9592e6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0b4034f7cf7e37425b7c76f5e0f9fd11</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786318536</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Neuropatia Dolorosa Aguda">
  <data key="d0">Neuropatia Dolorosa Aguda</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Neuropatia Dolorosa Aguda is an acute painful neuropathy that may occur transiently after rapid improvement of glycemic control with Levemir®.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8a68ba1e8cc1defda76cde0eff9592e6</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786317653</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Reação no Local de Injeção">
  <data key="d0">Reação no Local de Injeção</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Reação no Local de Injeção encompasses pain, redness, urticaria, inflammation, ecchymosis, edema, and pruritus that occur more frequently with Levemir® than with human insulin.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8a68ba1e8cc1defda76cde0eff9592e6</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786317653</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Controle Glicêmico Rápido">
  <data key="d0">Controle Glicêmico Rápido</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Controle Glicêmico Rápido denotes a swift improvement in blood‑glucose levels that can be associated with transient adverse events.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8a68ba1e8cc1defda76cde0eff9592e6</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786317653</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Controle Glicêmico a Longo Prazo">
  <data key="d0">Controle Glicêmico a Longo Prazo</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Controle Glicêmico a Longo Prazo describes sustained glycemic management that reduces the risk of diabetic retinopathy progression.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8a68ba1e8cc1defda76cde0eff9592e6</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786317653</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Rubor">
  <data key="d0">Rubor</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Rubor is redness of the skin at the injection site observed more frequently with Levemir® than with human insulin.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8a68ba1e8cc1defda76cde0eff9592e6</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786317654</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Eritema">
  <data key="d0">Eritema</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Eritema is a generalized skin redness that may appear as an adverse reaction to Levemir®.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8a68ba1e8cc1defda76cde0eff9592e6</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786317654</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Erupções Cutâneas">
  <data key="d0">Erupções Cutâneas</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Erupções Cutâneas are skin eruptions reported as injection‑site adverse events associated with Levemir®.&lt;SEP&gt;Erupções Cutâneas are skin rashes, listed as an uncommon immune‑system disorder.&lt;SEP&gt;Erupções Cutâneas are skin rash reactions classified as an uncommon immune-system disorder linked to Novolin® R Penfill®.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8a68ba1e8cc1defda76cde0eff9592e6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3396320470ee682ec5cc4f70ab001ef4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0b4034f7cf7e37425b7c76f5e0f9fd11</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786318505</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Inflamação">
  <data key="d0">Inflamação</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Inflamação is localized swelling and inflammation at the Levemir® injection site.&lt;SEP&gt;Inflamação refers to pancreatic inflammation often caused by alcoholism or biliary lithiasis.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8a68ba1e8cc1defda76cde0eff9592e6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fee32f1fb0c848b0799071a86119b142</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786373084</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Equimose">
  <data key="d0">Equimose</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Equimose is ecchymosis or bruising that may develop after Levemir® injection.&lt;SEP&gt;Equimose is a bruising reaction that can appear at insulin injection sites.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8a68ba1e8cc1defda76cde0eff9592e6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d6101c469482b48e341b4095a54907fd</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786318523</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Anomalia de Refração">
  <data key="d0">Anomalia de Refração</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Anomalia de Refração refers to refraction disturbances that can occur early in insulin therapy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8a68ba1e8cc1defda76cde0eff9592e6</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786317654</data>
