  <data key="d0">Adolescent Patients with Type 2 Diabetes</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Adolescent Patients with Type 2 Diabetes are a population subgroup for which Levemir® use was supported.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3059be019782459a72891cea5e0434ea</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786317655</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Serious Maternal Adverse Events">
  <data key="d0">Serious Maternal Adverse Events</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Serious maternal adverse events are severe health complications experienced by pregnant participants in the study.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b4d7abd3e1e5418ee5a931e28a18e8ad</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786317655</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Live Births">
  <data key="d0">Live Births</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Live births denote the number of children born alive to women who became pregnant after randomization in the trial.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b4d7abd3e1e5418ee5a931e28a18e8ad</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786317655</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Umbilical Cord Blood">
  <data key="d0">Umbilical Cord Blood</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Umbilical cord blood is the fetal blood sample where Levemir® was detected at levels above the lower limit of quantification.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b4d7abd3e1e5418ee5a931e28a18e8ad</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786317655</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Double‑blind Dose‑Response Study">
  <data key="d0">Double‑blind Dose‑Response Study</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A double‑blind dose‑response study design described in citation 1 comparing pharmacodynamic properties of insulin detemir.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b4d7abd3e1e5418ee5a931e28a18e8ad</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786317655</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="GLP-1 Receptor Agonist">
  <data key="d0">GLP-1 Receptor Agonist</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">GLP-1 receptor agonist refers to a class of drugs that can be combined with Levemir® and require a 20 % reduction in Levemir® dose.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-56fc1d5df1b34d9120c3cf8a760c40f9</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786317656</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Basal-Bolus Therapy">
  <data key="d0">Basal-Bolus Therapy</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Basal‑bolus therapy is an insulin regimen that combines basal insulin with bolus insulin, in which Levemir® may be administered once or twice daily.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-56fc1d5df1b34d9120c3cf8a760c40f9</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786317656</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Dose Adjustment Guidelines">
  <data key="d0">Dose Adjustment Guidelines</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Dose adjustment guidelines are tables that specify the number of insulin units to add or subtract from Levemir® dose based on fasting plasma glucose levels.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-56fc1d5df1b34d9120c3cf8a760c40f9</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786317656</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Renal or Hepatic Dysfunction Patients">
  <data key="d0">Renal or Hepatic Dysfunction Patients</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Patients with renal or hepatic dysfunction are a special population needing intensified glucose monitoring and individualized Levemir® dose adjustments.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-56fc1d5df1b34d9120c3cf8a760c40f9</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786317656</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Bolus Insulin">
  <data key="d0">Bolus Insulin</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Bolus insulin is the rapid‑acting insulin component used in a basal‑bolus regimen, where it complements basal insulin such as Levemir® to achieve overall glycemic control. It is administered as a single, relatively large dose that is timed around meals or given to correct an elevated blood glucose reading.

The primary purpose of bolus insulin is to manage the post‑prandial glucose surge that occurs after carbohydrate consumption. By delivering a rapid dose immediately before, during, or shortly after eating, it helps blunt the rise in blood glucose and brings levels back toward target ranges. Bolus doses are also employed when a pre‑meal glucose value is already high, providing an acute correction.

In many insulin‑pumping and pump‑supported therapy systems, the exact amount of bolus insulin is calculated by algorithms such as the Bolus Wizard or SmartGuard, which take into account current glucose readings, carbohydrate intake, insulin‑to‑carbohydrate ratios, and individual correction factors. This calculated dose is then delivered as the rapid‑acting insulin needed to cover the expected glucose increase or to lower the existing high glucose level.&lt;SEP&gt;Rapid‑acting insulin administered before meals to control post‑prandial glucose.&lt;SEP&gt;The portion of the daily insulin dose administered before meals, representing the remainder after basal insulin allocation.&lt;SEP&gt;Bolus insulin delivers a rapid dose of insulin to cover meals.&lt;SEP&gt;Bolus insulin is a rapid‑acting insulin taken before meals to control post‑prandial glucose spikes.&lt;SEP&gt;Bolus Insulin is a rapid dose administered to cover meals or correct high glucose, delivered in increments by pumps.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-56fc1d5df1b34d9120c3cf8a760c40f9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b7715667f5fca178f0988984e932ecfb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-65c6beab51324e055f4a39b388e2eefe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6b867cec4c5eed3b10e431cbd4078dee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-83bb94d08bdb958eff25f76c9a6ac18a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b03b7fdf0dd9c96dc459929ccccdccff&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a0267d2986a48c4c31790b6f183277dc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-92417ae942a11c591feb2ee9b5fadd7e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1c5a5c97986d9b31b155b0c8f0cac1c5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c7e6ef38db0b62d161b13473af47d738&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ca8620e735c40bfe850134ccea9a7154&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0932e9c21a330869629b3fa70d2e1f5e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-06425d1f80d868bd58871b6a6e740102&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9cd925790899146eeb8a373879b5feac</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/Documento sem título.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/Insulinoterapia – Diretriz da Sociedade Brasileira de Diabetes – Ed. 2024.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/Understanding insulin - International Diabetes Federation.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/blood glucose monitoring.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786335886</data>
