<node id="Disposal">
  <data key="d0">Disposal</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ddb8954aaa1e1230598596ce6f5df249&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0eedfa9db50d515c53181256a5959a40&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7fef140d95c1acc260149fd1d20f7853&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-02bf2da7f1cdbbbcbe760df43f00b2e0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c4d5551bd34470fa603c62d5b51b1ea6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f013a672ce03f1b20f7a515bae12be15&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f3d819d6498d4482286628946e37a6b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a111edb31d6739acf013ce812b952366</data>
  <data key="d2">Disposal is the process of discarding used medical devices, their components, and related consumables in a manner that safeguards people and the environment. It includes the careful removal of items such as needles, pumps, and other equipment to prevent injury, contamination, or accidental reuse.  

Guidelines for disposal require that used products—such as Accu‑Chk Solo glucose meters, batteries, and any ancillary parts—be placed in appropriate waste streams in accordance with local regulations, environmental standards, and any specific instructions issued by local authorities. These regulations often dictate whether items should be treated as clinical waste, hazardous waste, or recyclable material, and they may prescribe particular containers, labeling, or collection procedures.  

The recommended approach emphasizes environmentally friendly practices, urging users to follow legislation that promotes safe handling, segregation, and final treatment of waste. When disposing of a pump or similar device, the method must ensure that the device and its parts are rendered non‑functional and are processed in a way that minimizes ecological impact while complying with the applicable legal framework.</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/IFU Accu-Chek Guide Solo Diabetes Manager.PDF&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329637</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
