<node id="Sistema de aplicação preenchido (FlexPen®)">
  <data key="d0">Sistema de aplicação preenchido (FlexPen®)</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Sistema de aplicação preenchido (FlexPen®) describes the filled application system used by the FlexPen® device.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-813e7e990dba10e8d4147252f6547423</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786318473</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Novolin® R Penfill">
  <data key="d0">Novolin® R Penfill</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Novolin® R Penfill is a rapid‑acting insulin formulation supplied in a penfill device, noted as unsuitable for use in pump catheters for continuous subcutaneous insulin infusion because of precipitation risk.&lt;SEP&gt;Novolin® R Penfill is a rapid‑acting insulin product supplied in a pen device for subcutaneous or intravenous administration.&lt;SEP&gt;Novolin® R Penfill is an aqueous, clear insulin solution provided in a pen cartridge, requiring specific storage and handling precautions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9a6f9e10c0d4af5fff0338eb861f9c86&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0955cb70a6ce135722726162a9811e78&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4615ca664e7ff898d8c5929cbc79e7d8</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786318473</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Pump Catheter">
  <data key="d0">Pump Catheter</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Pump Catheter is a component of an insulin pump where precipitation of Novolin® R may occur.&lt;SEP&gt;A catheter component of an insulin pump used for continuous subcutaneous infusion, into which Novolin® R Penfill should not be placed.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9a6f9e10c0d4af5fff0338eb861f9c86&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea9b3836b3275f451c3acfb189f42a6f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786318473</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Medication Label Checking">
  <data key="d0">Medication Label Checking</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The practice of verifying insulin labels before each injection to avoid accidental mixing of different insulin products.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9a6f9e10c0d4af5fff0338eb861f9c86</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786318478</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Accidental Insulin Mixes">
  <data key="d0">Accidental Insulin Mixes</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Unintended combination of different insulin types, which should be prevented by label checking.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9a6f9e10c0d4af5fff0338eb861f9c86</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786318479</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Dose Titration">
  <data key="d0">Dose Titration</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Dose titration refers to the process of adjusting insulin dose individually based on patient response.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9a6f9e10c0d4af5fff0338eb861f9c86</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786318479</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Contraindications">
  <data key="d0">Contraindications</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Contraindications are conditions such as hypersensitivity to the active substance or excipients that preclude the use of Novolin® R Penfill.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9a6f9e10c0d4af5fff0338eb861f9c86</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786318479</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Warnings and Precautions">
  <data key="d0">Warnings and Precautions</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Warnings and precautions advise patients traveling across time zones to consult a physician regarding insulin dosing and meal timing.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9a6f9e10c0d4af5fff0338eb861f9c86</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786318480</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Pharmacokinetic Profile in Children and Adolescents">
  <data key="d0">Pharmacokinetic Profile in Children and Adolescents</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The pharmacokinetic profile in children and adolescents describes drug absorption and disposition, suggested to be similar to adults.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9a6f9e10c0d4af5fff0338eb861f9c86</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786318481</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Individual Dose">
  <data key="d0">Individual Dose</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Individual dose refers to the specific amount of insulin tailored to a patient’s needs, subject to titration.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9a6f9e10c0d4af5fff0338eb861f9c86</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786318482</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Meal Omission">
  <data key="d0">Meal Omission</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Meal Omission refers to skipping a scheduled food intake, which can precipitate hypoglycemia.&lt;SEP&gt;Skipping a meal, identified as a factor that can lead to hypoglycemia.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-dd396c45bc09fb646d156b4e69d328e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dd2bfbe7cac15c6f6dc444a35691ae83</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/Orientacoes_Hipoglicemia_SBD_transcricao.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1786338256</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Strenuous Exercise">
  <data key="d0">Strenuous Exercise</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Strenuous Exercise denotes unplanned vigorous physical activity that can increase insulin demand and cause hypoglycemia.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-dd396c45bc09fb646d156b4e69d328e3</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786318488</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Animal Origin Insulin">
  <data key="d0">Animal Origin Insulin</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Animal Origin Insulin is an insulin product derived from animal sources.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-dd396c45bc09fb646d156b4e69d328e3</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786318489</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Half‑Life">
  <data key="d0">Half‑Life</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Half‑Life denotes the time required for the plasma insulin concentration to reduce by half, reported as 2–5 hours in the study.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-dd396c45bc09fb646d156b4e69d328e3</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786318490</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Time Zones">
  <data key="d0">Time Zones</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Time Zones refer to different regional times that may require patients to adjust their insulin schedule.&lt;SEP&gt;Time Zones refer to regions with differing local times, relevant for travel advice for insulin users.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-dd396c45bc09fb646d156b4e69d328e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea9b3836b3275f451c3acfb189f42a6f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786318491</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="NovoFine® Disposable Needles">
  <data key="d0">NovoFine® Disposable Needles</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">NovoFine® Disposable Needles are 8 mm length syringes intended for use with Novolin® R Penfill.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0955cb70a6ce135722726162a9811e78</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786318493</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Collection Posts">
  <data key="d0">Collection Posts</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Collection Posts are designated locations for disposing of used needles and related waste.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0955cb70a6ce135722726162a9811e78</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786318495</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Pharmacies">
  <data key="d0">Pharmacies</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Pharmacies are drugstores that host Collection Posts for safe needle disposal.&lt;SEP&gt;Pharmacies are retail outlets where individuals can purchase sharps collectors.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0955cb70a6ce135722726162a9811e78&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-de69fd058597c808e8be5bd334395b84</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Descarte/Documento sem título.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1786321781</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Drugstores">
  <data key="d0">Drugstores</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Drugstores (Drogarias) are retail outlets that host Collection Posts for safe needle disposal.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0955cb70a6ce135722726162a9811e78</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786318495</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Health Posts">
  <data key="d0">Health Posts</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Health Posts (Postos de Saúde) are public health facilities that host Collection Posts for safe needle disposal.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0955cb70a6ce135722726162a9811e78</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786318495</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hospitals">
  <data key="d0">Hospitals</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Hospitals are medical institutions that host Collection Posts for safe needle disposal.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0955cb70a6ce135722726162a9811e78</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786318496</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Leaflet">
  <data key="d0">Leaflet</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">The leaflet provides detailed instructions for using Novolin® R Penfill.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0955cb70a6ce135722726162a9811e78</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786318496</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Sodium Chloride 0.9% Infusion Fluid">
  <data key="d0">Sodium Chloride 0.9% Infusion Fluid</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Sodium Chloride 0.9% Infusion Fluid is a saline solution used as a diluent for intravenous Novolin® R.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0955cb70a6ce135722726162a9811e78</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786318497</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Dextrose 5% Infusion Fluid">
  <data key="d0">Dextrose 5% Infusion Fluid</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Dextrose 5% Infusion Fluid is a glucose solution used as a diluent for intravenous Novolin® R.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0955cb70a6ce135722726162a9811e78</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786318497</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Dextrose 10% Infusion Fluid">
  <data key="d0">Dextrose 10% Infusion Fluid</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Dextrose 10% Infusion Fluid is a higher‑concentration glucose solution used as a diluent for intravenous Novolin® R.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0955cb70a6ce135722726162a9811e78</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786318497</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Potassium Chloride 40 mmol/L Infusion Fluid">
  <data key="d0">Potassium Chloride 40 mmol/L Infusion Fluid</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Potassium Chloride 40 mmol/L Infusion Fluid is an electrolyte solution used as a diluent for intravenous Novolin® R.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0955cb70a6ce135722726162a9811e78</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786318498</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Concomitant Diseases">
  <data key="d0">Concomitant Diseases</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Concomitant Diseases are additional illnesses that can affect insulin requirements and may require dose adjustments.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0955cb70a6ce135722726162a9811e78</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786318498</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Low Temperature Storage">
  <data key="d0">Low Temperature Storage</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Low Temperature Storage refers to conditions where temperatures are very low, potentially freezing medication.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0955cb70a6ce135722726162a9811e78</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786318499</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Infusion System">
  <data key="d0">Infusion System</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Infusion System is equipment that delivers insulin solutions intravenously, often using infusion bags.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0955cb70a6ce135722726162a9811e78</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786318500</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Insulin Dosage Range">
  <data key="d0">Insulin Dosage Range</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Insulin Dosage Range provides recommended daily insulin units per kilogram for patients based on weight and diabetes type.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0955cb70a6ce135722726162a9811e78</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786318501</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Novolin® N">
  <data key="d0">Novolin® N</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Novolin® N is an insulin product supplied in a vial that must be administered using a syringe.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3396320470ee682ec5cc4f70ab001ef4</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786318501</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Bolsa De Infusão">
  <data key="d0">Bolsa De Infusão</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Bolsa De Infusão is the infusion‑bag material onto which insulin is initially adsorbed during preparation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3396320470ee682ec5cc4f70ab001ef4</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786318502</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Bula Do Profissional">
  <data key="d0">Bula Do Profissional</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Bula Do Profissional is a professional booklet that provides detailed instructions for the use of Novolin® R.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3396320470ee682ec5cc4f70ab001ef4</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786318502</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Monitorização Da Glicemia">
  <data key="d0">Monitorização Da Glicemia</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Monitorização Da Glicemia is the practice of monitoring blood‑glucose levels that is necessary during insulin infusion.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3396320470ee682ec5cc4f70ab001ef4</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786318503</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Bombas Para Infusão De Insulina Subcutânea Contínua">
  <data key="d0">Bombas Para Infusão De Insulina Subcutânea Contínua</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Bombas Para Infusão De Insulina Subcutânea Contínua are continuous subcutaneous insulin infusion pumps that should not be used with Novolin® R.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3396320470ee682ec5cc4f70ab001ef4</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786318503</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Reações No Local De Aplicação">
  <data key="d0">Reações No Local De Aplicação</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Reações No Local De Aplicação are local site reactions such as pain, erythema, pruritus, inflammation, ecchymosis, edema, and urticaria.&lt;SEP&gt;Reações No Local De Aplicação are injection‑site reactions such as pain, redness, and pruritus listed as uncommon adverse events for Novolin® R Penfill®.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3396320470ee682ec5cc4f70ab001ef4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0b4034f7cf7e37425b7c76f5e0f9fd11</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786318503</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Neuropatia Dolorosa">
  <data key="d0">Neuropatia Dolorosa</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Neuropatia Dolorosa is an acute painful nerve disorder that may appear with rapid improvement of glucose control.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3396320470ee682ec5cc4f70ab001ef4</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786318504</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Distúrbios De Refração">
  <data key="d0">Distúrbios De Refração</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Distúrbios De Refração are refractive vision disturbances, listed as an uncommon visual adverse reaction associated with insulin.&lt;SEP&gt;Distúrbios De Refração are refraction disorders listed as uncommon vision disturbances associated with Novolin® R Penfill®.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3396320470ee682ec5cc4f70ab001ef4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0b4034f7cf7e37425b7c76f5e0f9fd11</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786318506</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Reações Anafiláticas">
  <data key="d0">Reações Anafiláticas</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Reações Anafiláticas are generalized hypersensitivity reactions that can be life‑threatening.&lt;SEP&gt;Reações Anafiláticas are very rare severe anaphylactic reactions that may occur as an adverse effect of insulin.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3396320470ee682ec5cc4f70ab001ef4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-786395f3716fb61a79fd183c63e1a9d6</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786318506</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Perfil De Segurança">
  <data key="d0">Perfil De Segurança</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Perfil De Segurança is a safety‑profile summary describing the frequency and nature of insulin’s adverse reactions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3396320470ee682ec5cc4f70ab001ef4</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786318507</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Solução De Insulina">
  <data key="d0">Solução De Insulina</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Solução De Insulina is the liquid insulin preparation used for infusion; it must be clear, colorless, and compatible with added medications.&lt;SEP&gt;Solução De Insulina is the insulin solution that must be clear, colorless, and free of contaminants for safe use with Novolin® R Penfill®.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3396320470ee682ec5cc4f70ab001ef4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0b4034f7cf7e37425b7c76f5e0f9fd11</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786318507</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Dose of Insulin">
  <data key="d0">Dose of Insulin</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Dose of Insulin refers to the amount of insulin given, identified as a factor that influences Novolin® R’s pharmacokinetics.&lt;SEP&gt;Dose of insulin is the amount prescribed by a physician, adjusted based on diet, activity, work schedule, disease, exercise, travel, and individual metabolic needs.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ea9b3836b3275f451c3acfb189f42a6f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8ac99e7359716e2cecc2ec93159218b6</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786319740</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Subcutaneous Fat Thickness">
  <data key="d0">Subcutaneous Fat Thickness</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Subcutaneous Fat Thickness denotes the thickness of subcutaneous tissue, which affects the absorption rate of Novolin® R.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ea9b3836b3275f451c3acfb189f42a6f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786318508</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Type of Diabetes">
  <data key="d0">Type of Diabetes</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Type of Diabetes describes classifications of diabetes (e.g., type 1) that modify the pharmacokinetic behavior of insulin therapies.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ea9b3836b3275f451c3acfb189f42a6f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786318509</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Plasma Protein Binding">
  <data key="d0">Plasma Protein Binding</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Plasma Protein Binding indicates the degree to which insulin binds to plasma proteins, reported as low except when antibodies are present.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ea9b3836b3275f451c3acfb189f42a6f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786318509</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Circulating Insulin Antibodies">
  <data key="d0">Circulating Insulin Antibodies</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Circulating Insulin Antibodies are plasma antibodies that can bind insulin, representing the primary exception to low plasma protein binding.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ea9b3836b3275f451c3acfb189f42a6f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786318509</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Insulin Protease">
  <data key="d0">Insulin Protease</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Insulin Protease is an enzyme that degrades insulin during its metabolic breakdown.&lt;SEP&gt;Insulin protease is an enzyme that degrades insulin during metabolism.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ea9b3836b3275f451c3acfb189f42a6f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2378c57a337d1ce7103c7086ebba76ac</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786318509</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Insulin Degradation Enzymes">
  <data key="d0">Insulin Degradation Enzymes</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Insulin Degradation Enzymes are enzymes involved in the breakdown of insulin molecules.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ea9b3836b3275f451c3acfb189f42a6f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786318509</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Protein Disulfide Isomerase">
  <data key="d0">Protein Disulfide Isomerase</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Protein Disulfide Isomerase is a protein posited to participate in insulin metabolism.&lt;SEP&gt;Protein disulfide isomerase is an enzyme possibly involved in insulin degradation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ea9b3836b3275f451c3acfb189f42a6f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2378c57a337d1ce7103c7086ebba76ac</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786318510</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Metabolites of Insulin">
  <data key="d0">Metabolites of Insulin</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Metabolites of Insulin are cleavage products of insulin reported to be pharmacologically inactive.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ea9b3836b3275f451c3acfb189f42a6f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786318510</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Terminal Half-Life">
  <data key="d0">Terminal Half-Life</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Terminal Half-Life is a measure reflecting the rate of absorption of insulin from subcutaneous tissue, typically ranging from 2‑5 hours.&lt;SEP&gt;Terminal half-life (t½) is the measure of the rate of insulin absorption from subcutaneous tissue, typically 2‑5 hours, and does not represent true elimination.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ea9b3836b3275f451c3acfb189f42a6f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-acaa1440ae268669e1894588bb9e37c2</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786318510</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Animal-Origin Insulin">
  <data key="d0">Animal-Origin Insulin</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Animal-Origin Insulin is insulin derived from animal sources, referenced when patients switch to Novolin® R.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ea9b3836b3275f451c3acfb189f42a6f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786318511</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Intense Physical Exercise">
  <data key="d0">Intense Physical Exercise</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Intense Physical Exercise is unplanned strenuous activity that can precipitate hypoglycemia.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ea9b3836b3275f451c3acfb189f42a6f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786318511</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Active Substance">
  <data key="d0">Active Substance</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Active Substance refers to the insulin component of Novolin® R that exerts therapeutic effect and may cause hypersensitivity.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ea9b3836b3275f451c3acfb189f42a6f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786318512</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Embalagem">
  <data key="d0">Embalagem</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Embalagem is the external packaging that protects Novolin® R Penfill from heat, light, and physical damage.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4615ca664e7ff898d8c5929cbc79e7d8</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786318515</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Postos De Coleta">
  <data key="d0">Postos De Coleta</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">Postos De Coleta are collection sites where used needles are disposed of safely.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4615ca664e7ff898d8c5929cbc79e7d8</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786318516</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Inibidores da Monoaminoxidase (IMAO)">
  <data key="d0">Inibidores da Monoaminoxidase (IMAO)</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Inibidores da Monoaminoxidase (IMAO) are MAO‑inhibitor drugs that can diminish insulin needs.&lt;SEP&gt;Inibidores da Monoaminoxidase (IMAO) are drugs that can lower the insulin needs of a patient.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4615ca664e7ff898d8c5929cbc79e7d8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d6101c469482b48e341b4095a54907fd</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786318517</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Inibidores da Enzima Conversora de Angiotensina (ECA)">
  <data key="d0">Inibidores da Enzima Conversora de Angiotensina (ECA)</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Inibidores da Enzima Conversora de Angiotensina (ECA) are ACE‑inhibitor drugs that can lower insulin requirements.&lt;SEP&gt;Inibidores da Enzima Conversora de Angiotensina (ECA) are ACE inhibitors that can reduce insulin requirements.&lt;SEP&gt;Inibidores da Enzima Conversora de Angiotensina (ECA) are ACE inhibitors that may reduce insulin needs.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4615ca664e7ff898d8c5929cbc79e7d8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d6101c469482b48e341b4095a54907fd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ba6b31518be6fff1db8b68a28e82f200</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786318517</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Esteroides Anabolizantes">
  <data key="d0">Esteroides Anabolizantes</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Esteroides Anabolizantes are anabolic steroids that can lower a patient’s insulin requirements.&lt;SEP&gt;Esteroides Anabolizantes are anabolic steroids that may lower insulin needs.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4615ca664e7ff898d8c5929cbc79e7d8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ba6b31518be6fff1db8b68a28e82f200</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786318518</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Sulfonamidas">
  <data key="d0">Sulfonamidas</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Sulfonamidas are sulfonamide antibiotics that can lower the dose of insulin needed.&lt;SEP&gt;Sulfonamidas are sulfonamide drugs that may reduce the amount of insulin a patient needs.&lt;SEP&gt;Sulfonamidas are sulfonamide drugs that may decrease insulin requirements.&lt;SEP&gt;Sulfonamide antibiotics that, when used with insulin, increase insulin’s hypoglycemic action.&lt;SEP&gt;Sulfonamides listed as interacting with insulin to raise hypoglycemia risk.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4615ca664e7ff898d8c5929cbc79e7d8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d6101c469482b48e341b4095a54907fd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ba6b31518be6fff1db8b68a28e82f200&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cbede05ec60d9c79d637d9a0eb0efe48&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dd2bfbe7cac15c6f6dc444a35691ae83</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/Orientacoes_Hipoglicemia_SBD_transcricao.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1786338243</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Contraceptivos Orais">
  <data key="d0">Contraceptivos Orais</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Contraceptivos Orais are oral contraceptive pills that can increase a patient's insulin requirements.&lt;SEP&gt;Contraceptivos Orais are oral contraceptives that can increase insulin needs.&lt;SEP&gt;Contraceptivos Orais are oral contraceptive drugs that can increase a patient’s insulin requirements.&lt;SEP&gt;Contraceptivos Orais are oral contraceptives that can increase insulin requirements.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4615ca664e7ff898d8c5929cbc79e7d8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d6101c469482b48e341b4095a54907fd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0851222a21a012cffce7a16710847208&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ba6b31518be6fff1db8b68a28e82f200</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786318518</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Tiazidas">
  <data key="d0">Tiazidas</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Tiazidas are thiazide diuretics that can raise the amount of insulin a patient needs.&lt;SEP&gt;Tiazidas are thiazide diuretics that may raise the insulin dosage needed by a patient.&lt;SEP&gt;Tiazidas are thiazide diuretics that can increase insulin needs.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4615ca664e7ff898d8c5929cbc79e7d8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d6101c469482b48e341b4095a54907fd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ba6b31518be6fff1db8b68a28e82f200</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786318519</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Glicocorticoides">
  <data key="d0">Glicocorticoides</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Glicocorticoides are glucocorticoid steroids that can increase insulin demand.&lt;SEP&gt;Glicocorticoides are glucocorticoid medications that can increase insulin requirements.&lt;SEP&gt;Glicocorticoides are glucocorticoid steroids that can increase insulin requirements.&lt;SEP&gt;Glucocorticoids are steroid medications (e.g., prednisolona, hidrocortisona, dexametasona) that can induce hyperglycemia and increase diabetes risk.&lt;SEP&gt;Glicocorticoides are glucocorticoid medications with a potential hyperglycemic effect, prompting diabetes screening before and after use.&lt;SEP&gt;Glicocorticoides are corticosteroid medications that may trigger diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4615ca664e7ff898d8c5929cbc79e7d8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d6101c469482b48e341b4095a54907fd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ba6b31518be6fff1db8b68a28e82f200&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e7b4535dbb2554b84c7a2e024c4b82c4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea6df8d05eb3fdd356a1eaef16a26dd5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-72da6fb8b6a9ed059d146b43a3174f90</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Diagnóstico de diabetes mellitus.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786373027</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hormônios da Tireoide">
  <data key="d0">Hormônios da Tireoide</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Hormônios da Tireoide are thyroid hormone preparations that can elevate insulin requirements.&lt;SEP&gt;Hormônios da Tireoide are thyroid hormones that may elevate a patient’s insulin needs.&lt;SEP&gt;Hormônios da Tireoide are thyroid hormones that can raise the insulin requirements.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4615ca664e7ff898d8c5929cbc79e7d8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d6101c469482b48e341b4095a54907fd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ba6b31518be6fff1db8b68a28e82f200</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786318519</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Simpatomiméticos">
  <data key="d0">Simpatomiméticos</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Simpatomiméticos are sympathomimetic agents that can boost the need for insulin.&lt;SEP&gt;Simpatomiméticos are sympathomimetic agents that can increase insulin requirements.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4615ca664e7ff898d8c5929cbc79e7d8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d6101c469482b48e341b4095a54907fd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ba6b31518be6fff1db8b68a28e82f200</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786318519</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hormônio do Crescimento">
  <data key="d0">Hormônio do Crescimento</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Hormônio do Crescimento is growth hormone therapy that can increase insulin dosage needs.&lt;SEP&gt;Hormônio do Crescimento is a growth hormone that may raise the insulin dosage required.&lt;SEP&gt;Hormônio do Crescimento is growth hormone, listed as increasing insulin needs.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4615ca664e7ff898d8c5929cbc79e7d8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d6101c469482b48e341b4095a54907fd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ba6b31518be6fff1db8b68a28e82f200</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786318519</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Agulha Descartável Nova">
  <data key="d0">Agulha Descartável Nova</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Agulha Descartável Nova is a new disposable needle that must be attached to Novolin® R FlexPen® for each injection and never reused.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e9b085ae33d49450f3f8bc342b5eae55</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786318520</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Algodão Umedecido com Álcool">
  <data key="d0">Algodão Umedecido com Álcool</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Algodão Umedecido com Álcool is a cotton pad moistened with alcohol recommended for cleaning the external surface of Novolin® R FlexPen®.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e9b085ae33d49450f3f8bc342b5eae55</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786318520</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Sistema de Aplicação de Insulina Reserva">
  <data key="d0">Sistema de Aplicação de Insulina Reserva</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Sistema de Aplicação de Insulina Reserva is the preventive practice of carrying an extra insulin pen in case the primary device is lost or damaged.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e9b085ae33d49450f3f8bc342b5eae55</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786318522</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Prevenção">
  <data key="d0">Prevenção</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Prevenção is the measure of always having a reserve insulin application system to avoid missed doses.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e9b085ae33d49450f3f8bc342b5eae55</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786318522</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Bolha de Ar">
  <data key="d0">Bolha de Ar</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Bolha de Ar is the air trapped inside the carpule that must be moved to the top and removed to ensure correct insulin delivery.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e9b085ae33d49450f3f8bc342b5eae55</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786318522</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Indicador Injetor">
  <data key="d0">Indicador Injetor</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Indicador Injetor is a visual indicator on the Novolin® R FlexPen® that shows injection status.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e9b085ae33d49450f3f8bc342b5eae55</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786318522</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Gota de Insulina">
  <data key="d0">Gota de Insulina</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Gota de Insulina is the drop of insulin that should appear at the needle tip to confirm proper insulin flow.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e9b085ae33d49450f3f8bc342b5eae55</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786318523</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Esteróides Anabolizantes">
  <data key="d0">Esteróides Anabolizantes</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Esteróides Anabolizantes are anabolic steroids that may reduce insulin requirements.&lt;SEP&gt;Anabolic steroids mentioned as medications that, when used with insulin, increase insulin’s hypoglycemic action.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d6101c469482b48e341b4095a54907fd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dd2bfbe7cac15c6f6dc444a35691ae83</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/Orientacoes_Hipoglicemia_SBD_transcricao.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1786338254</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Categoria B (Gravidez)">
  <data key="d0">Categoria B (Gravidez)</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Categoria B (Gravidez) is the pregnancy risk classification indicating no known fetal risk from insulin.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d6101c469482b48e341b4095a54907fd</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786318524</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Dextrose 10% Solution">
  <data key="d0">Dextrose 10% Solution</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">A 10% dextrose solution is a carbohydrate‑containing fluid compatible with Novolin® R for intravenous infusion.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-73559dc5d86ea52a348d603482e056e9</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786318525</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Potassium Chloride 40 mmol/L Solution">
  <data key="d0">Potassium Chloride 40 mmol/L Solution</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">A potassium chloride solution at 40 mmol/L may be mixed with Novolin® R for intravenous infusion.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-73559dc5d86ea52a348d603482e056e9</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786318525</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Meal">
  <data key="d0">Meal</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A meal is a food intake that should contain carbohydrates and is recommended to follow a Novolin® R injection within 30 minutes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-73559dc5d86ea52a348d603482e056e9</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786318525</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="30 Minutes">
  <data key="d0">30 Minutes</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A period of 30 minutes is the recommended maximum interval between a Novolin® R injection and the subsequent meal.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-73559dc5d86ea52a348d603482e056e9</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786318526</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="6 Seconds">
  <data key="d0">6 Seconds</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A period of 6 seconds is indicated to ensure the entire dose of Novolin® R has been administered.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-73559dc5d86ea52a348d603482e056e9</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786318526</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Adsorption">
  <data key="d0">Adsorption</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Adsorption is the process by which a portion of insulin initially binds to the material of the infusion bag.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-73559dc5d86ea52a348d603482e056e9</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786318526</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Thiol-Containing Medication">
  <data key="d0">Thiol-Containing Medication</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Medications containing thiols or sulfides are chemical compounds that can cause degradation of insulin solutions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-73559dc5d86ea52a348d603482e056e9</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786318527</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Frozen Insulin">
  <data key="d0">Frozen Insulin</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Frozen insulin refers to insulin preparations that have been previously frozen and should not be used.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-73559dc5d86ea52a348d603482e056e9</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786318527</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Clear and Colorless Solution">
  <data key="d0">Clear and Colorless Solution</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A clear and colorless solution describes the visual appearance required for insulin solutions before use.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-73559dc5d86ea52a348d603482e056e9</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786318527</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Reações anafiláticas">
  <data key="d0">Reações anafiláticas</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Reações anafiláticas are severe generalized hypersensitivity reactions that can be potentially fatal.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7f2714936869e55e840f5294caefeaee</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786318527</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="CCDS V.17_V7.0">
  <data key="d0">CCDS V.17_V7.0</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">CCDS V.17_V7.0 is the version identifier of the professional health leaflet for Novolin® R FlexPen®.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7f2714936869e55e840f5294caefeaee</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786318528</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="MedDRA SOC">
  <data key="d0">MedDRA SOC</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">MedDRA SOC is the System Organ Class classification within the MedDRA dictionary used to categorize adverse reactions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7f2714936869e55e840f5294caefeaee</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786318528</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Agulhas descartáveis">
  <data key="d0">Agulhas descartáveis</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Agulhas descartáveis are disposable needles up to 8 mm in length used with the Novolin® R FlexPen® insulin delivery system.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7f2714936869e55e840f5294caefeaee</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786318528</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Approval date 17/04/2026">
  <data key="d0">Approval date 17/04/2026</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Approval date 17/04/2026 is the date on which Anvisa approved the Novolin® R FlexPen® professional health leaflet.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7f2714936869e55e840f5294caefeaee</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786318528</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Continuous Subcutaneous Insulin Infusion Pump">
  <data key="d0">Continuous Subcutaneous Insulin Infusion Pump</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">A continuous subcutaneous insulin infusion pump is a medical device delivering insulin continuously, but may cause precipitation with Novolin® R.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-acaa1440ae268669e1894588bb9e37c2</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786318528</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Clivagem (Hidrólise)">
  <data key="d0">Clivagem (Hidrólise)</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Clivagem (hidrólise) is the hydrolytic cleavage of the human insulin molecule, resulting in metabolites.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-acaa1440ae268669e1894588bb9e37c2</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786318528</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Inactive Metabolites">
  <data key="d0">Inactive Metabolites</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Inactive metabolites are the cleavage products of insulin that lack biological activity.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-acaa1440ae268669e1894588bb9e37c2</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786318528</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Excipient">
  <data key="d0">Excipient</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Excipient refers to any inactive ingredient in a pharmaceutical formulation that may cause hypersensitivity.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-acaa1440ae268669e1894588bb9e37c2</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786318529</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Collection Bin">
  <data key="d0">Collection Bin</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">A collection bin is a sturdy container (e.g., metal or plastic) used for safe disposal of used syringes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-df616353e032c899b02bfa4368bc2667</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786318529</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Outer Packaging">
  <data key="d0">Outer Packaging</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Outer Packaging is a protective outer layer that shields the frasco of Novolin® R from light.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-df616353e032c899b02bfa4368bc2667</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786318530</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Betabloqueadores Não Seletivos">
  <data key="d0">Betabloqueadores Não Seletivos</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Betabloqueadores Não Seletivos are non‑selective beta‑blockers that can mask hypoglycemia symptoms.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0851222a21a012cffce7a16710847208</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786318530</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Validity Period">
  <data key="d0">Validity Period</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Validity Period indicates that Novolin® R remains usable for 30 months from manufacture.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0851222a21a012cffce7a16710847208</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786318530</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Risk Category B">
  <data key="d0">Risk Category B</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Risk Category B is the pregnancy risk classification assigned to Novolin® R.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0851222a21a012cffce7a16710847208</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786318531</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Label Verification">
  <data key="d0">Label Verification</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Label Verification is the practice of checking the insulin label before each injection to avoid accidental mixing.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0851222a21a012cffce7a16710847208</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786318531</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Prolonged‑Acting Insulin">
  <data key="d0">Prolonged‑Acting Insulin</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Prolonged‑Acting Insulin is a type of insulin with extended duration, which may be combined with Novolin® R FlexPen®.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2cd48799a027437b9fe2e1a48b61cb3d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786318531</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Puberty">
  <data key="d0">Puberty</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Puberty is a physiological stage that can increase insulin needs, as noted for patients using Novolin® R FlexPen®.&lt;SEP&gt;Puberty is a developmental stage after which screening for type 2 diabetes may be considered.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2cd48799a027437b9fe2e1a48b61cb3d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1a111d4b40ec241cf54126f594a80308</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
