<node id="Normoglycemia">
  <data key="d0">Normoglycemia</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Normoglycemia refers to a blood glucose range of 4.4–6.1 mmol/L considered normal.&lt;SEP&gt;Normoglycemia is the target blood glucose range (4.4–6.1 mmol/L) achieved after insulin administration.&lt;SEP&gt;Normoglycemia denotes normal blood glucose levels, observed in Stage 1 of type 1 diabetes.&lt;SEP&gt;Normal blood glucose levels observed in Stage 1 diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2378c57a337d1ce7103c7086ebba76ac&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cd40a6d69921cf300ed8eda043698d1a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3cc61bc2e95346d553972b4371912e7f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ba38023866c2db7437e618a60033f21f</data>
