<node id="Food and Drug Administration (FDA)">
  <data key="d0">Food and Drug Administration (FDA)</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">U.S. regulatory agency that approved metreleptin for generalized lipodystrophy.&lt;SEP&gt;U.S. regulatory agency whose labeling and dose‑conversion updates for inhaled insulin are referenced.&lt;SEP&gt;The Food and Drug Administration (FDA) is the U.S. regulatory agency that approves CGM devices and sets standards for integrated CGM.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7eabee57ef0af575162ce8d36f3589a5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e76c949a607724dd052d9fc4c7127a18&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0fe1eff7b58582dec4c8ae7578e20e66</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/cengiz-beck-2026-use-of-inhaled-insulin-with-automated-insulin-delivery-systems.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/blood glucose monitoring.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786335978</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="HIV">
  <data key="d0">HIV</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">HIV, the human immunodeficiency virus, is a retroviral pathogen that infects immune cells such as macrophages and can also invade adipocytes, contributing to metabolic complications. By targeting these cell types, HIV is directly implicated in the development of HIV‑associated lipodystrophy, a specific form of acquired lipodystrophy characterized by abnormal fat distribution and metabolic disturbances.

In addition to its effects on body composition, HIV infection is recognized as a significant risk factor for glucose metabolism disorders. Individuals living with HIV have a higher incidence of type 2 diabetes mellitus and prediabetes, and the infection is listed as a comorbidity that warrants routine diabetes screening, particularly before the initiation of antiretroviral therapy. This heightened risk is attributed both to the virus itself and to the metabolic side effects of certain antiretroviral drugs.

Interpretation of glycated hemoglobin (A1C) measurements can be problematic in people with HIV. The infection may interfere with A1C assay results, especially when co‑existing hemoglobinopathies are present, leading to potential misclassification of glycemic status. Clinicians therefore need to consider alternative methods for assessing glucose control in this population.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7eabee57ef0af575162ce8d36f3589a5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f86b5a9c60ab13c2016dd454edf634c7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f54dda12a0c5f43832ff3c6f0dc78369&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c92d117f7109ea1ce6995f23bc680ce3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea6df8d05eb3fdd356a1eaef16a26dd5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fee32f1fb0c848b0799071a86119b142&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d01033177672e6c36e0a368db88e586d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-55e58732610596ce9a8f3145d34f75a7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3cc61bc2e95346d553972b4371912e7f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2a430bf53157529ccb22e67171fb28e5</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Diagnóstico de diabetes mellitus.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377354</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Autoimunidade">
  <data key="d0">Autoimunidade</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Presence of autoimmune activity evaluated in patients with lipodystrophy.&lt;SEP&gt;Autoimunidade denotes the presence of an immune response directed against the body's own tissues, relevant to autoimmune diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7eabee57ef0af575162ce8d36f3589a5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ed325288512881a80fa42dba504c4bff</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786373083</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Exames Complementares">
  <data key="d0">Exames Complementares</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Additional diagnostic tests performed to assess metabolic complications and autoimmunity.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7eabee57ef0af575162ce8d36f3589a5</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786321223</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Antiretroviral Therapy">
  <data key="d0">Antiretroviral Therapy</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Antiretroviral therapy is a treatment regimen using antiretroviral drugs to control HIV, which can be linked to lipodystrophy.&lt;SEP&gt;Treatment for HIV infection, investigated for its link to incident diabetes.&lt;SEP&gt;Antiretroviral Therapy is a treatment for HIV, during which diabetes screening is advised.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f86b5a9c60ab13c2016dd454edf634c7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ec7e786a85b1b6e6cc75bcfc9189fd27&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2a430bf53157529ccb22e67171fb28e5</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Diagnóstico de diabetes mellitus.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377410</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Nelfinavir">
  <data key="d0">Nelfinavir</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Nelfinavir is a first‑generation protease inhibitor that induces lipodystrophy by blocking adipocyte differentiation, promoting insulin resistance and pro‑inflammatory cytokine production.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f86b5a9c60ab13c2016dd454edf634c7</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786321223</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Indinavir">
  <data key="d0">Indinavir</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Indinavir is a first‑generation protease inhibitor with lipodystrophy‑inducing effects similar to nelfinavir.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f86b5a9c60ab13c2016dd454edf634c7</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786321223</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Ritonavir">
  <data key="d0">Ritonavir</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Ritonavir is a second‑generation protease inhibitor that exerts deleterious effects on adipose tissue through oxidative stress and altered adipokine secretion.&lt;SEP&gt;Ritonavir is a protease inhibitor used in HIV therapy and linked to acquired lipodystrophy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f86b5a9c60ab13c2016dd454edf634c7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fee32f1fb0c848b0799071a86119b142</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786373085</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Lopinavir">
  <data key="d0">Lopinavir</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Lopinavir is a second‑generation protease inhibitor that causes harmful changes in adipose tissue comparable to ritonavir.&lt;SEP&gt;Lopinavir is a protease inhibitor used in HIV treatment associated with lipodystrophy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f86b5a9c60ab13c2016dd454edf634c7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fee32f1fb0c848b0799071a86119b142</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786373086</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Atazanavir">
  <data key="d0">Atazanavir</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Atazanavir is a second‑generation protease inhibitor that, when used alone, does not produce deleterious effects on adipocytes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f86b5a9c60ab13c2016dd454edf634c7</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786321224</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Amprenavir">
  <data key="d0">Amprenavir</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Amprenavir is a second‑generation protease inhibitor that, when used alone, lacks harmful effects on adipocytes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f86b5a9c60ab13c2016dd454edf634c7</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786321224</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Nucleoside Reverse Transcriptase Inhibitors">
  <data key="d0">Nucleoside Reverse Transcriptase Inhibitors</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Nucleoside reverse transcriptase inhibitors (NRTIs) are thymidine‑analog antiretroviral drugs associated with lipodystrophy, especially subcutaneous lipoatrophy.&lt;SEP&gt;A class of HIV drugs that reduces the reliability of A1C measurements.&lt;SEP&gt;NRTIs are antiretroviral agents that affect fat distribution and are linked to insulin resistance.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f86b5a9c60ab13c2016dd454edf634c7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d01033177672e6c36e0a368db88e586d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-55e58732610596ce9a8f3145d34f75a7</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377316</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Stavudine">
  <data key="d0">Stavudine</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Stavudine is a first‑generation NRTI linked to subcutaneous lipoatrophy and mitochondrial dysfunction contributing to lipodystrophy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f86b5a9c60ab13c2016dd454edf634c7</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786321224</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Zidovudine">
  <data key="d0">Zidovudine</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Zidovudine is a first‑generation NRTI associated with lipodystrophy through mitochondrial toxicity and oxidative stress.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f86b5a9c60ab13c2016dd454edf634c7</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786321224</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Tenofovir">
  <data key="d0">Tenofovir</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Tenofovir is a second‑generation NRTI that does not cause the adverse metabolic effects linked to lipodystrophy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f86b5a9c60ab13c2016dd454edf634c7</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786321225</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Adipocytes">
  <data key="d0">Adipocytes</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Adipocytes are fat cells whose differentiation, hypertrophy, insulin sensitivity and survival can be altered by antiretroviral drugs and HIV infection.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f86b5a9c60ab13c2016dd454edf634c7</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786321225</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Macrophages">
  <data key="d0">Macrophages</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Macrophages are immune cells residing in adipose tissue that can shift from an anti‑inflammatory (M2) to a pro‑inflammatory (M1) phenotype during HIV infection.&lt;SEP&gt;Macrophages are pulmonary scavenger cells derived from circulating monocytes that help keep the lungs clean.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f86b5a9c60ab13c2016dd454edf634c7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-941c5035ce1f85963f1f564bf2bf73fb</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/Inhaling medicines_ delivering drugs to the body through the lungs _ Nature Reviews Drug Discovery.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786330886</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Pro‑inflammatory Cytokines">
  <data key="d0">Pro‑inflammatory Cytokines</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Pro‑inflammatory cytokines are signaling proteins whose production is increased by protease inhibitors and HIV‑infected M1 macrophages, driving inflammation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f86b5a9c60ab13c2016dd454edf634c7</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786321225</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Adiponectin">
  <data key="d0">Adiponectin</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Adiponectin is an insulin‑sensitizing hormone that is reduced in lipodystrophy and by certain antiretroviral drugs.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f86b5a9c60ab13c2016dd454edf634c7</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786321225</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="VLDL">
  <data key="d0">VLDL</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">VLDL (very‑low‑density lipoprotein) is a hepatic lipoprotein whose production is increased by protease inhibitors.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f86b5a9c60ab13c2016dd454edf634c7</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786321225</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Oxidative Stress">
  <data key="d0">Oxidative Stress</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Oxidative stress is a cellular condition induced by some antiretroviral drugs that damages adipocytes and contributes to lipodystrophy.&lt;SEP&gt;Oxidative stress is intracellular stress activated by RAGE receptor signaling in diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f86b5a9c60ab13c2016dd454edf634c7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2d8f17f3f250a37a1effaaa88cc8b382</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/glicemias capilares.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786338525</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="M1 Macrophage Phenotype">
  <data key="d0">M1 Macrophage Phenotype</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">M1 macrophage phenotype is a pro‑inflammatory state adopted by macrophages infected with HIV, leading to increased cytokine release.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f86b5a9c60ab13c2016dd454edf634c7</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786321225</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="M2 Macrophage Phenotype">
  <data key="d0">M2 Macrophage Phenotype</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">M2 macrophage phenotype is an anti‑inflammatory state of macrophages that predominates before HIV infection.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f86b5a9c60ab13c2016dd454edf634c7</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786321225</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Metabolic Syndrome">
  <data key="d0">Metabolic Syndrome</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Metabolic syndrome is a cluster of conditions (diabetes mellitus, severe hypertriglyceridemia, hepatomegaly, hepatic steatosis, acanthosis nigricans) used to suspect partial lipodystrophy.&lt;SEP&gt;Metabolic Syndrome is a cluster of risk factors including insulin resistance, hypertension, and dyslipidemia.&lt;SEP&gt;A cluster of metabolic abnormalities associated with increased risk of NAFLD and type 2 diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f86b5a9c60ab13c2016dd454edf634c7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-44aa59c0e5cc620a11b8fb017d1aefcf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ec7e786a85b1b6e6cc75bcfc9189fd27</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Diagnóstico de diabetes mellitus.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786372011</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hepatic Steatosis">
  <data key="d0">Hepatic Steatosis</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Hepatic steatosis is fatty liver disease included in metabolic syndrome criteria.&lt;SEP&gt;Hepatic steatosis is fatty liver disease associated with lipodystrophic conditions.&lt;SEP&gt;Fatty liver condition linked to Lpf Tipo 4.&lt;SEP&gt;A fatty liver condition characterized by accumulation of fat in liver tissue, associated with elevated ALT, AST, and GGT.&lt;SEP&gt;Fat accumulation in the liver that improves with metreleptin therapy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f86b5a9c60ab13c2016dd454edf634c7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-003b19adf9ab32e9587902e8d639d701&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-383b02cc66391d66174344ff49464766&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-005de970178a46619506bcc15fe94fa9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c96221c60c19f02ac6efa6a987b1e15b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786321226</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Partial Lipodystrophy">
  <data key="d0">Partial Lipodystrophy</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Partial lipodystrophy is a subtype of lipodystrophy suspected in young patients with metabolic‑syndrome signs and without obesity.&lt;SEP&gt;Partial lipodystrophy denotes lipodystrophic disorders where fat loss is limited to specific body regions.&lt;SEP&gt;Partial lipodystrophy refers to a localized form of the condition.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f86b5a9c60ab13c2016dd454edf634c7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-336c6084eb6cb7c8ada29ed26c0cd20d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-003b19adf9ab32e9587902e8d639d701</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786321226</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Ultrasonography">
  <data key="d0">Ultrasonography</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Ultrasonography is an imaging method used to assess organomegaly in patients with lipodystrophy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f86b5a9c60ab13c2016dd454edf634c7</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786321226</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Organomegaly">
  <data key="d0">Organomegaly</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Organomegaly denotes enlargement of internal organs and can be evaluated by ultrasonography.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f86b5a9c60ab13c2016dd454edf634c7</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786321226</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Adipose Tissue Inflammation">
  <data key="d0">Adipose Tissue Inflammation</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Adipose tissue inflammation is an inflammatory process within fat tissue driven by HIV infection and certain antiretroviral drugs.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f86b5a9c60ab13c2016dd454edf634c7</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786321226</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Lipodystrophy Phenotype">
  <data key="d0">Lipodystrophy Phenotype</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Lipodystrophy phenotype describes the observable pattern of abnormal fat distribution in HIV‑infected patients.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f86b5a9c60ab13c2016dd454edf634c7</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786321226</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="HIV Protease Inhibitors">
  <data key="d0">HIV Protease Inhibitors</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">HIV protease inhibitors are discussed in relation to obesity.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-336c6084eb6cb7c8ada29ed26c0cd20d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786321227</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Berardinelli-Seip Congenital Lipodystrophy">
  <data key="d0">Berardinelli-Seip Congenital Lipodystrophy</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Berardinelli-Seip Congenital Lipodystrophy is a rare genetic disorder characterized by severe lipodystrophy and metabolic abnormalities.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-336c6084eb6cb7c8ada29ed26c0cd20d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786321227</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Gigantism">
  <data key="d0">Gigantism</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Gigantism is mentioned as an endocrine manifestation associated with lipodystrophy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-336c6084eb6cb7c8ada29ed26c0cd20d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786321227</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Diencephalic Syndrome">
