  <data key="d5">1786329455</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Menu">
  <data key="d0">Menu</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Menu is the navigation interface of the insulin pump that provides access to functions like Bolus, Basal, and Settings.&lt;SEP&gt;The navigation menu within the device software.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8762fcba31adb064a87d5d846c9a8aff&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db8e2f5011e0e0fe7dc11273e2f345b9</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329575</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Infusion">
  <data key="d0">Infusion</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Infusion is the continuous delivery of insulin by the pump.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8762fcba31adb064a87d5d846c9a8aff</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786322840</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Basal">
  <data key="d0">Basal</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Basal is the term used in insulin pump systems to denote the continuous background insulin delivery mode that provides the steady supply of insulin required between meals and overnight. It represents the basal insulin delivery rate, expressed in units per hour, and may also be described as the portion of total daily insulin that is allocated to basal delivery, often reported as a percentage of the total dose.

The Basal setting is accessed through a dedicated menu category on the pump, which allows users to view and modify basal rates and pre‑programmed basal patterns. Within this menu, rates can be changed temporarily (for example, to cover exercise or illness) or permanently, and the interface typically permits selection of different temporal segments or patterns to match the user’s daily routine. Adjustments made in the menu are applied to the pump’s continuous insulin delivery function.

In addition to setting rates, the Basal feature includes safety mechanisms: if basal delivery is unexpectedly blocked or interrupted, the pump generates an alarm to alert the user. This ensures that any interruption to the background insulin supply can be addressed promptly, maintaining glycemic control.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8762fcba31adb064a87d5d846c9a8aff&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-84bb2bb0df91a594c6936b2fe97e4220&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1312783ffe5039c618a48f7f29ec51ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9b74c4d587eaa1f27358b25bcf758f1f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c1a77062463b62317e84265a3b2b6d4a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8fdb2f497ff0665f2860089645ba9450&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0cf7c487c5bd4a61120add295be9d518&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db8e2f5011e0e0fe7dc11273e2f345b9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a111edb31d6739acf013ce812b952366&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-71de01baf40871c616eaa39cb8189f43&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-da4119d4fc266b13dd11e47dd6f506ca</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329590</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Reservorio">
  <data key="d0">Reservorio</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Reservorio is the insulin‑reservoir component of an insulin pump system. It is a removable cartridge that fits into the pump’s reservoir compartment and serves as the storage chamber for a measurable quantity of insulin, typically expressed in units. Positioned inside the pump’s housing, the reservoir connects directly to the infusion set, allowing insulin to flow through tubing to the subcutaneous cannula for delivery.

The reservoir holds enough insulin for several days of therapy and must be attached securely to the pump and infusion set. Because it is a consumable part, it requires periodic replacement when the insulin supply is exhausted. Users are advised to inspect the reservoir regularly for emptiness or the presence of air bubbles, both of which can interfere with accurate insulin delivery. Proper attachment and routine checks are essential for reliable pump operation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8aa63853b30ac5d214c8cd80df90e517&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1f5ccf80661c0e52c3a3465ab87c6343&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-84bb2bb0df91a594c6936b2fe97e4220&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ca7afb2078bd96edf087859a2c89920c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-644dc086af7b196cc5bc332524608d5f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-beee0553403f566be565a996251cac46&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1255cfcf42afb2c6045de0d45b11e99d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4ed0e4c13d1643a77d1d74092a8cda5a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4eaa74c3ef8165f52ddf18e17a240a9d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cfb7c582936fb68746bd1911895df40c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a967066e623ddb0c9381f89dfe0f3d42&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8fdb2f497ff0665f2860089645ba9450&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0cf7c487c5bd4a61120add295be9d518&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1577ef83aca01016db533eba7c49d2a1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-220ba7466dbb8a2a07b8e4b09b215d39&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-01785f6f03692dc5e35c672e21b345f7</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786325483</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hidratos De Carbono">
  <data key="d0">Hidratos De Carbono</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Carbohydrates are nutrients that may require a bolus of insulin to be covered.&lt;SEP&gt;Hidratos De Carbono are the grams of carbohydrates entered to calculate a meal bolus.&lt;SEP&gt;Hidratos De Carbono are carbohydrates in food that are broken down into glucose.&lt;SEP&gt;Carbohydrates counted in meals that affect blood glucose levels when consumed alone or with other nutrients.&lt;SEP&gt;Hidratos De Carbono are carbohydrate foods recommended for ingestion to treat low glucose episodes.&lt;SEP&gt;Hidratos De Carbono are carbohydrates whose intake must be calculated for correct bolus dosing.&lt;SEP&gt;Carbohydrates whose amount was not calculated correctly and whose absorption rate was not considered.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8aa63853b30ac5d214c8cd80df90e517&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-63f6eb3be969569b166fc1e5f7e7567f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-505b4450257d1a728c397959b044ee97&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50d9a787da93a3bf7ea1e315273b560c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3dd65471e9cdf7a7389998e6124f5b10&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7cbaec668e54aa5cf462a7bd08d7813c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2fb90cfe4a3993c8a19c8fd291cc4d67</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786324184</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Bolus De Comida">
  <data key="d0">Bolus De Comida</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Bolus De Comida is a meal bolus administered without a GS value, based solely on the entered amount of Hidratos De Carbono.&lt;SEP&gt;Bolus De Comida is the method for calculating meal‑time insulin doses.&lt;SEP&gt;Meal bolus: insulin administered to cover the rise in blood glucose after consuming carbohydrate‑containing foods or drinks.&lt;SEP&gt;Bolus De Comida is the insulin dose calculated to cover carbohydrate intake for a meal.&lt;SEP&gt;Meal bolus calculated based on entered carbohydrate amount to cover upcoming food intake.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8aa63853b30ac5d214c8cd80df90e517&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1fa7ad1de214645f0e643708dc1efab8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f3d0dd38cbfd29061a0c9916efb7c5d8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bec9e867c8de5a0beabd70ea9209c1a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-01785f6f03692dc5e35c672e21b345f7</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786325535</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Bolus Corrector">
  <data key="d0">Bolus Corrector</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Bolus Corrector is a correction bolus administered without food, based on a current GS value.&lt;SEP&gt;A method for delivering corrective insulin doses when the pump is disconnected and reconnected.&lt;SEP&gt;Bolus Corrector is a corrective insulin dose calculated by the pump to lower high glucose levels.&lt;SEP&gt;Correction bolus administered when the current GS is high, without additional carbohydrate intake.&lt;SEP&gt;Bolus Corrector is a corrective insulin dose calculated by the Bolus Wizard that must be delivered immediately and cannot be given as a square bolus.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8aa63853b30ac5d214c8cd80df90e517&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cf3629e41b33d8907b96157ddd2be394&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-644dc086af7b196cc5bc332524608d5f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-35a3bbe287cd55b2fd0a1505c706e7a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-01785f6f03692dc5e35c672e21b345f7</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786325505</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Mensaje GS Alta">
  <data key="d0">Mensaje GS Alta</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Mensaje GS Alta is a warning message shown when the GS value is lower than 70 mg/dL or higher than 250 mg/dL, indicating how to proceed.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8aa63853b30ac5d214c8cd80df90e517</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786322842</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cetoacidosis Diabética">
  <data key="d0">Cetoacidosis Diabética</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Cetoacidosis Diabética is a diabetic complication that the user is instructed to prevent through appropriate actions.&lt;SEP&gt;Cetoacidosis Diabética is diabetic ketoacidosis, a risk that increases during illness and is monitored via glucose and ketone testing.&lt;SEP&gt;Cetoacidosis Diabética is a medical condition whose prevention is covered in the guide.&lt;SEP&gt;Cetoacidosis diabética is a severe complication of diabetes involving ketoacids.&lt;SEP&gt;Cetoacidosis Diabética is a severe metabolic complication characterized by high ketone bodies and low insulin.&lt;SEP&gt;Diabetic ketoacidosis, a condition to prevent by appropriate insulin dosing.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8aa63853b30ac5d214c8cd80df90e517&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-644dc086af7b196cc5bc332524608d5f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1fa7ad1de214645f0e643708dc1efab8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1255cfcf42afb2c6045de0d45b11e99d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-646b0d64191b72fd929f7fb514a8cb8c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-01785f6f03692dc5e35c672e21b345f7</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786325534</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hipoglucemia">
  <data key="d0">Hipoglucemia</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Hipoglucemia is a medical condition characterized by abnormally low blood‑glucose levels, defined as blood glucose falling below safe thresholds. The condition can arise from several iatrogenic and physiological factors, including the infusion or administration of an excessive amount of insulin (or “Insulina”), interruption of an insulin bolus, mismatched insulin action relative to carbohydrate absorption, and increased glucose utilization during physical activity. In the early weeks of diabetes therapy, patients are especially vulnerable as treatment regimens are being adjusted.

Because hypoglycemia can become dangerously low, it often requires prompt corrective action. Standard emergency measures include the rapid ingestion of carbohydrates and, when oral intake is not feasible or glucose is critically low, the administration of glucagon. The body’s natural counter‑regulatory response also involves glucagon signaling to raise blood glucose.

Modern insulin‑pump and continuous‑glucose‑monitoring systems are designed to detect and mitigate hipoglucemia. Features such as high‑glucose alerts, the Autoapagado function (which intervenes when the user fails to respond), and overall pump therapy have been shown to reduce the frequency of low‑glucose episodes. These technologies aim to prevent hypoglycemia by delivering timely alerts and, in some cases, automatically adjusting insulin delivery.

Clinical guidance emphasizes that hipoglucemia should be discussed with the medical team and is typically covered in device manuals and patient education materials. Recognizing the condition early, monitoring glucose trends, and employing both pharmacologic (glucagon) and nutritional (rapid‑acting carbohydrates) interventions are essential components of safe diabetes management.&lt;SEP&gt;Condition of low blood glucose that can result from excessive insulin infusion.&lt;SEP&gt;Low blood glucose condition that can result from administering excessive insulin.&lt;SEP&gt;Hipoglucemia is a medical condition characterized by abnormally low blood glucose levels, mentioned as a potential risk of pump malfunction.&lt;SEP&gt;Hipoglucemia is a medical condition defined as glucose sensor readings below 70 mg/dL, with various severity criteria described.&lt;SEP&gt;Hipoglucemia is a low blood glucose condition that the Autoapagado function aims to protect against.&lt;SEP&gt;Hipoglucemia refers to low blood glucose episodes, especially occurring at night for runners like Thomas.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8aa63853b30ac5d214c8cd80df90e517&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1f5ccf80661c0e52c3a3465ab87c6343&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5863810bebfd1be64b8af80afcd57e11&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f5a3c673db465ff57a023abf1cd26053&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9688a6d3c7f751ad34af5a1cde24fa2a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-644dc086af7b196cc5bc332524608d5f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-310d06ee583c6aa24af77816642d0ba7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a717b5a81dbba0bd3cf2aae23dc0e309&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b4cf85d0e1e129080fae6f9bea5bd77f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-beee0553403f566be565a996251cac46&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1fa7ad1de214645f0e643708dc1efab8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-34da912924aa29d035c8cd1c3f4f6ae3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6c123ae434326de3ccfe03d252e5d267&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-646b0d64191b72fd929f7fb514a8cb8c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d0a4d039b786601ed8a06d8adad50938&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7d6466bdd61e024e50acc3fed9a5f9f8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3ce8c9873da330aac077f7ccaf108ccd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6737e479a665e986547e5e1e29ef26da&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-da325dc5071cd02bfe55ffc2f9b79aa5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-505b4450257d1a728c397959b044ee97&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d9b29e7a7839d7ff2b29e72fb4912618&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4eaa74c3ef8165f52ddf18e17a240a9d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3dd65471e9cdf7a7389998e6124f5b10&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7cbaec668e54aa5cf462a7bd08d7813c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-381370d223aabc9b355b55a05c98e07b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8f3505927abeefb80af00bfabdaff7cd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dc1b97c88d050500f2b90b8837bd34bd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-de8328f990d0902170699f76dac78b01&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2e303ffa37ca96974ad7399e052659bb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-01785f6f03692dc5e35c672e21b345f7</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786325496</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Inyección Manual De Insulina">
  <data key="d0">Inyección Manual De Insulina</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Inyección Manual De Insulina is a manual insulin injection using a syringe or pen that is not accounted for by the Bolus Wizard calculation.&lt;SEP&gt;Delivery of insulin using a syringe or pen, which is not considered in the Bolus Wizard calculation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8aa63853b30ac5d214c8cd80df90e517&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-01785f6f03692dc5e35c672e21b345f7</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786325535</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Jeringa">
  <data key="d0">Jeringa</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Jeringa is a syringe used to deliver a manual injection of Insulina.&lt;SEP&gt;Jeringa is a syringe used to deliver glucagón or corrective insulin doses.&lt;SEP&gt;Jeringa is a syringe used to administer insulin when pump delivery is not effective.&lt;SEP&gt;Jeringa is a syringe used to administer insulin corrections when the pump is not used.&lt;SEP&gt;A syringe used to administer a corrective insulin dose as directed by the health professional.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8aa63853b30ac5d214c8cd80df90e517&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-644dc086af7b196cc5bc332524608d5f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1255cfcf42afb2c6045de0d45b11e99d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4ed0e4c13d1643a77d1d74092a8cda5a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-220ba7466dbb8a2a07b8e4b09b215d39</data>
