<node id="Bolus Wizard">
  <data key="d0">Bolus Wizard</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Bolus Wizard is a trademarked, software‑driven calculation feature integrated into Medtronic MiniMed insulin pumps, notably the MiniMed 770G and MiniMed 670G models. Appearing as a guided option within the pump’s menu, it assists users in determining the appropriate bolus insulin dose for meals and glucose corrections when the pump is operating in Manual mode. By prompting the entry of the current glucose sensor reading and the amount of carbohydrates to be consumed, the algorithm computes the insulin needed to cover the carbohydrate load and, if the glucose level exceeds the programmed target range, adds a correction bolus to bring glucose toward that target.

The Bolus Wizard calculation incorporates several individualized parameters stored in the pump, including the user’s insulin‑to‑carbohydrate ratio, insulin sensitivity factor (ISF), glucose target range, and the amount of active insulin remaining from previously delivered doses. These settings enable the feature to provide a personalized bolus recommendation that reflects both immediate glucose values and residual insulin activity. The tool supports multiple bolus delivery patterns—standard, extended (Square Wave), and combination (dual‑wave) boluses—allowing users to select the pattern that best matches their meal composition and insulin needs. It can be configured during the pump’s startup sequence and functions solely for insulin delivered by the pump, not accounting for manually injected doses.

Overall, Bolus Wizard serves as an assisted bolus calculation and delivery tool that streamlines the dosing process, reduces the need for manual arithmetic, and helps users achieve more accurate glycemic control by leveraging real‑time sensor data and personalized therapy settings.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8aa63853b30ac5d214c8cd80df90e517&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9526502ad449d7dc77120264e206f332&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5863810bebfd1be64b8af80afcd57e11&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-84bb2bb0df91a594c6936b2fe97e4220&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-27a9a11fec63f11922c3e40119833245&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2dada456819c45230012103650ccc14a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9855ca7ae42a0c01685280c4cc5bb56a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9b74c4d587eaa1f27358b25bcf758f1f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dd31a315488bb0669257b83dd88b9809&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1c8229e79576a8ad79f8dc8a3290e5ac&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7ce776458e256df9d6070a419cab7449&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1f3c75e751c36c2f270820a403b40ac0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-995e322b08a5c6d446f5fd68e5c3fe5a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-35a3bbe287cd55b2fd0a1505c706e7a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-da0dcb28a160ed0e11da58b075919575&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fcff234f91816c50c56d0113b934824c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8f3505927abeefb80af00bfabdaff7cd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b9eee903de4b7e25fc53f52e2e739637&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-785aac5c827baebbe0c372f8c4550f23&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8fdb2f497ff0665f2860089645ba9450&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-653ce0324c2ed605bfadb08f01e649c7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-83bb94d08bdb958eff25f76c9a6ac18a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db8e2f5011e0e0fe7dc11273e2f345b9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a0267d2986a48c4c31790b6f183277dc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-28515a0aca492eeee478cd9947226498&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bcdc240f555b6c71532ea6d04e0c5798&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ae3b43add031516d14e51c6d2a985bd7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eb80f00ba2dab32852874cb384b38de3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a111edb31d6739acf013ce812b952366&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-20af4762343b8357c2c72473211f2918&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b23dfd3ae95fca711f8f10fc98ab467c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f94cd06ab0d1bcc7a9349bc40ea3eb22&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-da4119d4fc266b13dd11e47dd6f506ca&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-27b3ea1063acf8e0a407a89daea0dc32</data>
