<node id="Insulina Activa">
  <data key="d0">Insulina Activa</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Insulina Activa is the term used by insulin pump systems to denote the quantity of insulin that remains biologically active in the user’s body after previous bolus deliveries. The pump calculates this residual amount based on the timing and size of each bolus, continuously updating the value as insulin’s action wanes.  

The active insulin value is displayed on the pump’s home screen or main interface, allowing the user to see at a glance how much insulin is still influencing blood glucose levels. This information is taken into account when the pump determines the size of subsequent correction or meal boluses, helping to avoid insulin stacking and to maintain tighter glucose control.  

In essence, Insulina Activa represents the remaining, effective insulin from earlier bolus doses that continues to lower blood glucose until its activity diminishes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8aa63853b30ac5d214c8cd80df90e517&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cf725cb54eea97f946e1f27eae125a0b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-63f6eb3be969569b166fc1e5f7e7567f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7d6466bdd61e024e50acc3fed9a5f9f8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f369332c7e5ee7ed284fec07f68d394d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-817893fc39ccf7551d476cefaf7f32ca&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4eaa74c3ef8165f52ddf18e17a240a9d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-da0dcb28a160ed0e11da58b075919575</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786325509</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Índice Basal">
  <data key="d0">Índice Basal</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Índice Basal is the term used in the MiniMed 770G insulin‑pump system to denote a basal insulin rate setting. It appears throughout the pump’s documentation and user interface as the numeric value (expressed in units per hour, e.g., 0.900 U/h) that defines how much rapid‑acting insulin is delivered continuously during a specific segment of a basal pattern.

Within the pump’s basal patterns configuration, each Índice Basal entry corresponds to a defined time interval—such as the period before meals, overnight, or upon waking—and the value is displayed in the pump’s status information. The setting represents the standard basal insulin rate that the device will deliver unless a temporary adjustment is applied using the temporal basal index method.

The primary clinical purpose of the Índice Basal is to maintain blood glucose within target ranges throughout the day. When correctly programmed, it helps prevent both hyperglycemia and hypoglycemia by providing a steady background insulin supply that matches the body’s basal needs. The same value is referenced when the pump resumes basal infusion after a pause or interruption, ensuring continuity of insulin delivery.

In summary, Índice Basal (also referred to as Basal Index) is a core parameter of the MiniMed 770G pump: a numeric basal rate (units per hour) assigned to specific time segments, shown in the device’s status screen, and essential for achieving stable glucose control while being adjustable on a temporary basis when required.&lt;SEP&gt;Numerical rate (units per hour) that specifies how much basal insulin the pump delivers at a given time.&lt;SEP&gt;Índice Basal is a concept referring to a specific basal insulin rate value within a basal pattern.&lt;SEP&gt;The basal insulin rate setting on the pump that can be reviewed and modified via the screen.&lt;SEP&gt;A basal insulin rate setting that can be reviewed, edited, and saved within the pump.</data>
