<node id="Bomba">
  <data key="d0">Bomba</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Bomba is the insulin‑pump component of Medtronic’s MiniMed™ hybrid closed‑loop systems, most notably the MiniMed 770G and the earlier MiniMed 670G. As a medical device, Bomba houses a reservoir compartment, a piston‑driven delivery mechanism, and an embedded mini‑computer that together administer insulin to the user through an infusion set. The pump can accommodate changes in infusion site, equipment, reservoir, and insulin type, allowing flexible therapy management.

Bomba delivers both basal insulin—programmed according to user‑defined indices and patterns—and bolus insulin, which can be entered manually or generated automatically. When paired with a continuous glucose sensor (CGM), the pump receives real‑time glucose readings and can calculate corrective boluses without user intervention, supporting the system’s SmartGuard (or “Auto‑Mode”) safety algorithm.

The device features a built‑in screen that presents icons, status screens, and notifications. Through a configurable menu, users can set basal‑max and bolus‑max limits, adjust safety functions, select audio options, and modify sensor settings. An inactivity mode conserves power when the pump is not in active use. Bomba continuously monitors operational parameters such as battery level, reservoir volume, and delivery integrity, issuing visual alerts (e.g., a red light) and audible alarms to warn of low battery, empty reservoir, occlusions, or other delivery issues.

Overall, Bomba functions as the central insulin‑delivery unit within the MiniMed hybrid closed‑loop platforms, integrating insulin storage, precise dosing, CGM data processing, and user‑friendly interface elements to provide automated and customizable diabetes management.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8aa63853b30ac5d214c8cd80df90e517&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1f5ccf80661c0e52c3a3465ab87c6343&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5863810bebfd1be64b8af80afcd57e11&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-84bb2bb0df91a594c6936b2fe97e4220&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f5a3c673db465ff57a023abf1cd26053&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ca7afb2078bd96edf087859a2c89920c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1312783ffe5039c618a48f7f29ec51ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9b74c4d587eaa1f27358b25bcf758f1f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9688a6d3c7f751ad34af5a1cde24fa2a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-644dc086af7b196cc5bc332524608d5f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d9b29e7a7839d7ff2b29e72fb4912618&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cfb7c582936fb68746bd1911895df40c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a967066e623ddb0c9381f89dfe0f3d42&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8fdb2f497ff0665f2860089645ba9450&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0cf7c487c5bd4a61120add295be9d518&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-adb365cf52e00c7b4647e65dc0411d56&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2e303ffa37ca96974ad7399e052659bb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-220ba7466dbb8a2a07b8e4b09b215d39&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-01785f6f03692dc5e35c672e21b345f7</data>
