<node id="Medtronic">
  <data key="d0">Medtronic</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Medtronic is a global medical‑technology company that designs, manufactures, and markets a wide range of diabetes‑management devices under the MiniMed brand. Its product portfolio includes insulin‑pump systems such as the MiniMed™ 770G, 640G, 670G, 780G, the MiniMed Paradigm® Veo 754, and the MiniMed 722, as well as continuous glucose monitors (CGMs). Medtronic holds the trademarks for the MiniMed line, the Bolus Wizard™ feature, its corporate logo, and the slogan “Further, Together.” The company distributes these devices worldwide, including specific supply of the MiniMed 640G, Paradigm Veo 754, and MiniMed 722 pumps in Brazil.

Beyond hardware, Medtronic provides a suite of supporting services and digital tools. The CareLink Personal program links users to their pump and CGM data, while the MiniMed Mobile app and related software updates enable remote monitoring on supported mobile devices and operating systems. The firm offers formal user training, technical assistance, a network of company representatives, and extensive documentation—user guides and manuals that carry its branding and include educational disclosures advising users to consult qualified healthcare professionals and noting that Medtronic assumes no liability for the content.

Medtronic’s insulin‑pump technology also incorporates advanced features such as block‑programming capabilities, allowing clinicians to temporarily suspend insulin delivery when needed. Clinical research has utilized Medtronic’s pumps, including the 780G system, in various studies, and the company has supplied study materials to researchers such as R.W.B. It has further supported academic investigation by providing research funding to authors like T.C.B. Performance data indicate that Medtronic’s pumps achieve optimal results when the insulin‑action time is set to the maximum allowable duration for rapid‑acting inhaled insulin (Afrezza).

Overall, Medtronic functions as a comprehensive provider of insulin‑pump and CGM technologies, combining hardware, software, training, and research support to enable safe and effective diabetes management for patients and clinicians worldwide.&lt;SEP&gt;Medtronic is the manufacturer of the Guardian Real-Time continuous glucose monitoring system.&lt;SEP&gt;Medtronic is a medical technology company that produced the SMCG Medtronic MiniMed device.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1f5ccf80661c0e52c3a3465ab87c6343&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9526502ad449d7dc77120264e206f332&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-30dc18e012cfdf2d8f9b961fdd1ba644&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-212366dd9a740ddcb430c2f3d36ca4dd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-644dc086af7b196cc5bc332524608d5f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-beee0553403f566be565a996251cac46&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1fa7ad1de214645f0e643708dc1efab8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2dc33cf2a90bf53c26226e44bc285c22&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-646b0d64191b72fd929f7fb514a8cb8c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-75ab69ff55dee7eb424c572ea28a45ad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6737e479a665e986547e5e1e29ef26da&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f3d0dd38cbfd29061a0c9916efb7c5d8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8e89a2540c525a104b0a1a5513347a8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-995e322b08a5c6d446f5fd68e5c3fe5a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fcff234f91816c50c56d0113b934824c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-95ba6f1fa7d1791230f690255a8ba2df&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cdb000b83632c89167783ad4e6f1fb64&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4a4a75301f61fc3c86ad768de09d0c3f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eb80f00ba2dab32852874cb384b38de3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9ec9cae555a06ac660e6c16d90116c8b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a764dcbdd73fd1c50fa72a7cd60b6e19&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e796e8f4bb4721a269775c3d2ef0c06a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c0a2dce3852e38344f91c86f45dda403&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dfa23fc15cc4d520a32488843dbd710b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-127dc0e8b8b960bfd1fce3df4f590120&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2767372b4b5395439f542016058306a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5419de5a030f812ab408ef47f361bebd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8644d98286c4a296063176435b45d589&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-97acd5016384ec4abfe4d43c6a9cad08&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-40fdfdc209a5e3bb46f199c55baac15b</data>
