  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cánula">
  <data key="d0">Cánula</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Cannula is the subcutaneous needle component of the infusion set used to deliver insulin.&lt;SEP&gt;Cánula is the small tube inserted under the skin that delivers insulin from the infusion set.&lt;SEP&gt;The tiny flexible tube inserted into the body after the needle is removed, forming part of the infusion set.&lt;SEP&gt;The small tube component of the infusion set that enters the body to allow insulin flow.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1f5ccf80661c0e52c3a3465ab87c6343&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ca7afb2078bd96edf087859a2c89920c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cfb7c582936fb68746bd1911895df40c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-220ba7466dbb8a2a07b8e4b09b215d39</data>
