<node id="Autoapagado">
  <data key="d0">Autoapagado</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Autoapagado is an automatic shut‑off safety function incorporated in the MiniMed 770G insulin pump. The feature is designed to conserve battery life and enhance user safety by powering down the device after a user‑defined period of inactivity, meaning no button is pressed for a specified number of hours.  

When the inactivity threshold is reached, Autoapagado first emits an audible alarm to alert the user. If the alarm is not acknowledged, the system proceeds to disable insulin delivery, effectively stopping all infusion. This behavior is intended to protect users who may be unresponsive to hypoglycemia or otherwise unable to interact with the pump.  

The shutdown interval is configurable within the pump’s settings, allowing users or clinicians to tailor the duration to individual needs and risk profiles. By automatically turning off the pump after prolonged inactivity, Autoapagado helps preserve the pump’s battery charge while providing a built‑in safeguard against unintended insulin administration.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9526502ad449d7dc77120264e206f332&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-84bb2bb0df91a594c6936b2fe97e4220&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f5a3c673db465ff57a023abf1cd26053&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1c8229e79576a8ad79f8dc8a3290e5ac&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-310d06ee583c6aa24af77816642d0ba7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1f3c75e751c36c2f270820a403b40ac0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-995e322b08a5c6d446f5fd68e5c3fe5a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8fdb2f497ff0665f2860089645ba9450&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dc1b97c88d050500f2b90b8837bd34bd</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
