<node id="MiniMed™">
  <data key="d0">MiniMed™</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">MiniMed™ is a trademarked product line of Medtronic that comprises an insulin‑pump system used in sensor‑augmented therapy for diabetes. The device is referenced throughout training manuals, guides, and diabetes‑therapy documentation as a core component of continuous insulin delivery and glucose management.

The MiniMed™ pump can be programmed to deliver basal insulin at varying rates, allowing individualized background dosing throughout the day. In addition to basal delivery, it provides precise bolus dosing—including fractional‑unit increments—and incorporates the Bolus Wizard™ feature to calculate recommended bolus amounts based on current glucose readings and carbohydrate intake. Users can review and download bolus history to a computer for analysis and record‑keeping.

Because the system relies on frequent glucose monitoring, it is typically employed alongside continuous glucose sensors, enabling real‑time adjustments and tighter glycemic control. Overall, MiniMed™ functions as an integrated insulin‑pump platform that supports both basal and bolus insulin administration, data management, and advanced dosing algorithms within diabetes therapy programs.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9526502ad449d7dc77120264e206f332&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b7715667f5fca178f0988984e932ecfb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d2f8a0d67f7320d6157b61dbbf428a40&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-07b23fc13c50867e0aa61204fb79bc2b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-646b0d64191b72fd929f7fb514a8cb8c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-75ab69ff55dee7eb424c572ea28a45ad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6737e479a665e986547e5e1e29ef26da&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fb3bd140c8e2ac53cf1b45386cb861ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f3d0dd38cbfd29061a0c9916efb7c5d8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f369332c7e5ee7ed284fec07f68d394d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786324104</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Bolus Dual">
  <data key="d0">Bolus Dual</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Bolus Dual is a dual‑wave bolus delivery option available on the MiniMed 770G insulin pump. It is described in the MiniMed 770G user guide as a specific bolus mode that allows the pump to administer insulin in two distinct phases.

The first phase is a normal (or immediate) bolus that is delivered right away to cover the rapid rise in blood glucose that follows carbohydrate ingestion. The second phase is a square (or extended) bolus that is released gradually over a programmed period, providing insulin to address delayed glucose excursions that can occur with meals high in fat, protein, or complex carbohydrates. By combining these two components, Bolus Dual aims to better match the timing of insulin action with the absorption profile of the food, thereby improving post‑meal glucose control.

When a Bolus Dual is initiated, the pump’s home screen displays the progress of both the immediate and the extended portions, allowing users to monitor delivery in real time. This advanced bolus method is intended for situations where a single, standard bolus would be insufficient to manage both the immediate and later phases of glucose rise, offering a more flexible and precise insulin therapy option for pump users.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9526502ad449d7dc77120264e206f332&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2dada456819c45230012103650ccc14a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dd31a315488bb0669257b83dd88b9809&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1c8229e79576a8ad79f8dc8a3290e5ac&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d9b29e7a7839d7ff2b29e72fb4912618&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1f3c75e751c36c2f270820a403b40ac0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-35a3bbe287cd55b2fd0a1505c706e7a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c1a77062463b62317e84265a3b2b6d4a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-de8328f990d0902170699f76dac78b01</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786325489</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Bolus Cuadrado">
  <data key="d0">Bolus Cuadrado</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Bolus Cuadrado is a square‑wave bolus delivery option supported by the MiniMed 770G insulin pump.&lt;SEP&gt;Bolus Cuadrado is a square‑bolus delivery method mentioned in the MiniMed 770G guide.&lt;SEP&gt;Bolus Cuadrado is an extended square-wave insulin bolus used for certain meals.&lt;SEP&gt;Bolus Cuadrado is a square-wave bolus mode available in the pump.&lt;SEP&gt;Bolus Cuadrado is an insulin delivery method that administers the dose over a selectable duration (30 minutes to 8 hours) in increments of 15 minutes to align insulin action with carbohydrate digestion.&lt;SEP&gt;Bolus cuadrado is a square‑wave insulin delivery method where a fixed amount is infused over a set duration.&lt;SEP&gt;Bolus Cuadrado is a square‑wave bolus method that delivers insulin over an extended period to address delayed digestion, high‑fat meals, or spaced carbohydrate intake.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9526502ad449d7dc77120264e206f332&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1c8229e79576a8ad79f8dc8a3290e5ac&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d9b29e7a7839d7ff2b29e72fb4912618&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1f3c75e751c36c2f270820a403b40ac0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-35a3bbe287cd55b2fd0a1505c706e7a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c1a77062463b62317e84265a3b2b6d4a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-de8328f990d0902170699f76dac78b01</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786325487</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Índice Basal Temporal">
  <data key="d0">Índice Basal Temporal</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Índice Basal Temporal is a temporary basal insulin rate setting used in insulin pump therapy. It allows the user to modify the standard basal insulin delivery for a limited, defined period, either by specifying a percentage change relative to the existing basal index or by entering an absolute insulin amount. The adjustment can be increased or decreased immediately and is typically programmed for short‑term situations such as physical activity, illness, nocturnal glucose management, or other circumstances that may alter insulin needs.

The setting is configurable on devices such as the MiniMed 670G pump, where it appears as a distinct “temporary basal” option in the pump’s menu. Users can select the desired percentage or absolute value, set the duration of the temporary basal, and the pump will automatically revert to the regular basal profile once the period expires. This flexibility helps reduce the risk of hypoglycemia during exercise, manage hyperglycemia during illness, and fine‑tune insulin delivery during nighttime periods, as exemplified by individuals like Thomas who employ the feature for nocturnal glucose control.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9526502ad449d7dc77120264e206f332&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1312783ffe5039c618a48f7f29ec51ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-310d06ee583c6aa24af77816642d0ba7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-34da912924aa29d035c8cd1c3f4f6ae3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4eaa74c3ef8165f52ddf18e17a240a9d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7cbaec668e54aa5cf462a7bd08d7813c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-995e322b08a5c6d446f5fd68e5c3fe5a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8f3505927abeefb80af00bfabdaff7cd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c1a77062463b62317e84265a3b2b6d4a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0cf7c487c5bd4a61120add295be9d518&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-adb365cf52e00c7b4647e65dc0411d56</data>
