<node id="Duración Insulina Activa">
  <data key="d0">Duración Insulina Activa</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Duración Insulina Activa is the time period during which insulin remains active after delivery.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5863810bebfd1be64b8af80afcd57e11</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786322860</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Menú Principal">
  <data key="d0">Menú Principal</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">The main menu contains seven elements that provide access to bolus, basal, audio, and other settings.&lt;SEP&gt;Menú Principal is the main menu interface on the pump where options like Parar Bolus are accessed.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5863810bebfd1be64b8af80afcd57e11&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9b74c4d587eaa1f27358b25bcf758f1f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786322860</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Parar Bolus">
  <data key="d0">Parar Bolus</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Parar Bolus is the command used to interrupt an ongoing insulin bolus.&lt;SEP&gt;The stop bolus function allows interruption of an ongoing bolus.&lt;SEP&gt;Parar Bolus is the menu option that interrupts an ongoing insulin infusion.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5863810bebfd1be64b8af80afcd57e11&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-63f6eb3be969569b166fc1e5f7e7567f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c1a77062463b62317e84265a3b2b6d4a</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786325514</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Bolus Wizard™">
  <data key="d0">Bolus Wizard™</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Bolus Wizard™ is a software feature incorporated in Medtronic MiniMed insulin pumps—including the MiniMed™ 770G, MiniMed™ 640G, and other MiniMed™ models—that assists users in determining the appropriate insulin bolus for both meals and corrections. The function calculates recommended bolus doses by integrating several inputs: the amount of carbohydrate intake, the user‑specific insulin‑to‑carbohydrate ratio, the insulin‑sensitivity factor (or correction factor), the current glucose reading, and the programmed glucose target. It also accounts for the amount of active (remaining) insulin on board, displaying this information on the home screen and using it to refine dose recommendations and help prevent hyperglycemia.

In addition to generating a total bolus recommendation, Bolus Wizard™ separates the calculation into a meal bolus and a correction bolus, then sums them to present the final suggested dose. The tool tracks and records administered insulin and carbohydrate portions, allowing users to review and modify bolus settings within the pump interface. Some versions automatically adjust the bolus based on real‑time glucose values, providing a “smart” bolus calculation that reflects active insulin levels and current glucose trends.

Overall, Bolus Wizard™ functions as a comprehensive dosing aid that streamlines insulin‑pump therapy by combining carbohydrate counting, glucose monitoring, and insulin‑on‑board data into a single, user‑friendly calculation engine, branded by Medtronic MiniMed Inc. as a smart bolus calculation feature.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9c435da9a83d88897df07d2d5ee02574&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-30dc18e012cfdf2d8f9b961fdd1ba644&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1312783ffe5039c618a48f7f29ec51ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-644dc086af7b196cc5bc332524608d5f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-310d06ee583c6aa24af77816642d0ba7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e91ce385a4956221ce891caa7456655a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-65c6beab51324e055f4a39b388e2eefe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2dc33cf2a90bf53c26226e44bc285c22&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4bbf34cee3d731d22b25c31db33dd183&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-07b23fc13c50867e0aa61204fb79bc2b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6ab7cedc48ea8fdd199a2c12c99416a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1255cfcf42afb2c6045de0d45b11e99d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d0a4d039b786601ed8a06d8adad50938&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f3d0dd38cbfd29061a0c9916efb7c5d8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f369332c7e5ee7ed284fec07f68d394d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4ed0e4c13d1643a77d1d74092a8cda5a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d9b29e7a7839d7ff2b29e72fb4912618&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-817893fc39ccf7551d476cefaf7f32ca&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bec9e867c8de5a0beabd70ea9209c1a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c8ef457272b70b6404625941c8d26a3d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4eaa74c3ef8165f52ddf18e17a240a9d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786324119</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Carbohydrate Ratio">
  <data key="d0">Carbohydrate Ratio</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Carbohydrate Ratio defines the amount of insulin needed per gram of carbohydrate and can have multiple time‑segmented values.&lt;SEP&gt;Carbohydrate Ratio is the grams of carbohydrate per unit of insulin used in bolus calculations.&lt;SEP&gt;The carbohydrate ratio defines the grams of carbohydrate covered by one unit of insulin, used in bolus calculations.&lt;SEP&gt;Carbohydrate Ratio indicates the amount of carbohydrate that can be consumed per unit of insulin without raising glucose, obtained by dividing 400 by the Daily Insulin Total.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9c435da9a83d88897df07d2d5ee02574&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b9eee903de4b7e25fc53f52e2e739637&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-785aac5c827baebbe0c372f8c4550f23&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0f272d1c9c38e2a6b6d02b5aa66809e1</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/Insulinoterapia – Diretriz da Sociedade Brasileira de Diabetes – Ed. 2024.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786331412</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Insulin Sensitivity Factor">
  <data key="d0">Insulin Sensitivity Factor</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Insulin Sensitivity Factor (ISF) is a numerical parameter that quantifies how much blood glucose is reduced by a single unit of insulin, typically expressed in milligrams per deciliter (mg/dL) per unit. The factor translates a deviation in glucose concentration into the corresponding insulin dose needed to correct that deviation, and it serves as a core component of bolus‑calculation algorithms such as the Bolus Wizard. Because the physiological response to insulin can vary throughout the day, many insulin‑pump and continuous glucose monitoring systems allow users to define one or several time‑segmented ISF values, enabling more precise dosing during different periods (e.g., dawn, daytime, nighttime).

In practice, the ISF is used to compute correction bolus amounts: the current glucose reading is compared to a target value, the difference is multiplied by the ISF, and the resulting figure is converted into insulin units that the patient should deliver. This calculation is performed automatically in model‑based bolus calculators and can also be applied manually when users operate in Manual mode. As a coefficient linking glucose levels to insulin dosing, the ISF effectively captures the individual’s insulin effect on glucose and is essential for tailoring therapy to each person’s sensitivity.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9c435da9a83d88897df07d2d5ee02574&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-27a9a11fec63f11922c3e40119833245&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f2b8be67edef23560656776b89947c10&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b9eee903de4b7e25fc53f52e2e739637&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-785aac5c827baebbe0c372f8c4550f23&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-83bb94d08bdb958eff25f76c9a6ac18a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d68acc5f59d78c14cf4d2e4d34edf5e4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db8e2f5011e0e0fe7dc11273e2f345b9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b6025fa711665988fad0f789b9eb901a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a111edb31d6739acf013ce812b952366&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-97eb00dc26d33c23bf8bf473c0a98472&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-20af4762343b8357c2c72473211f2918</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329555</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="GS Target">
  <data key="d0">GS Target</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">GS Target is the glucose value entered into Bolus Wizard™ to guide insulin dosing, including low (Ba) and high (Al) targets.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9c435da9a83d88897df07d2d5ee02574</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786322860</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Active Insulin Duration">
  <data key="d0">Active Insulin Duration</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Active Insulin Duration is the period during which previously administered insulin remains active, exemplified by a 4:00‑hour duration in the guide.&lt;SEP&gt;Active Insulin Duration is the time period during which previously administered insulin remains active and can be adjusted in the Bolus Wizard™.&lt;SEP&gt;Active Insulin Duration is the time period during which administered insulin remains effective, incorporated into bolus calculations.&lt;SEP&gt;Active insulin duration represents the time insulin remains active after a dose, influencing bolus calculations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9c435da9a83d88897df07d2d5ee02574&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-27a9a11fec63f11922c3e40119833245&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b9eee903de4b7e25fc53f52e2e739637&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-785aac5c827baebbe0c372f8c4550f23</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786325512</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Linked Meter">
  <data key="d0">Linked Meter</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Linked Meter is a device that can automatically transmit glucose sensor (GS) values to the insulin pump.&lt;SEP&gt;Linked Meter is an external glucose measurement device that can be connected to the insulin pump to provide glucose sensor (GS) values.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9c435da9a83d88897df07d2d5ee02574&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b9eee903de4b7e25fc53f52e2e739637</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786325513</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Active Insulin">
  <data key="d0">Active Insulin</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Active Insulin is the quantity of insulin from prior bolus doses that remains biologically active in the body and continues to lower blood glucose until it degrades or is cleared. The pump’s algorithm tracks this amount in real time, displaying it on the Home screen and using it in bolus‑calculation formulas such as SmartGuard and correction‑bolus adjustments. Because active insulin still exerts a glucose‑lowering effect, the pump subtracts it from any planned correction dose and may increase a bolus when the active‑insulin pool is low.

The concept encompasses insulin that has already been delivered by the pump and is still bioavailable in the bloodstream, as well as the insulin that the pump records as “currently active” for dosing purposes. When the pump enters storage mode, the stored active‑insulin value is cleared, reflecting that no further physiological effect is expected. Some sources also note that a small residual amount of insulin may remain in the pump after previous use and must be cleared before the device’s first use, but the primary definition used in clinical and pump‑management contexts refers to the insulin actively influencing glucose metabolism in the user’s circulation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9c435da9a83d88897df07d2d5ee02574&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-65c6beab51324e055f4a39b388e2eefe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6ab7cedc48ea8fdd199a2c12c99416a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3ce8c9873da330aac077f7ccaf108ccd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3d24fce6aa8866fb4a11514ae0e4d675&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-527777f044e20410ca47d2c5b35306ca&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-05241912c4f8f5e79ae75071a1c7c604&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d68acc5f59d78c14cf4d2e4d34edf5e4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bf54a88e051fe74fd94b773f8b5d98da&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4faffc449b4b8ea09acbae135d21baa6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b48243f8e773d3c94abc58e2314db2c0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eb80f00ba2dab32852874cb384b38de3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-691a5ee6c6fdbea7a2ef1c835f0e66ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-27b3ea1063acf8e0a407a89daea0dc32&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a111edb31d6739acf013ce812b952366&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a01dc8dc15b92e2b0b570753b0f57632&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fd8af150d14c8fd9fd3b20e486220f65&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ede0f32eb8f8ea1eaab76cc0bc7648fd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f677e56841fc57bffd8bf5b6cc4a7797&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-20af4762343b8357c2c72473211f2918&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1c5a5c97986d9b31b155b0c8f0cac1c5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f94cd06ab0d1bcc7a9349bc40ea3eb22</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329511</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Meal Bolus">
  <data key="d0">Meal Bolus</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Meal Bolus is an insulin dose calculated to cover carbohydrate intake entered via the Bolus Wizard™.&lt;SEP&gt;Meal bolus is the insulin dose calculated to cover the carbohydrate amount of a meal.&lt;SEP&gt;Meal Bolus is an insulin dose administered to cover carbohydrate intake from a meal.&lt;SEP&gt;A meal bolus is an insulin dose calculated to cover carbohydrate intake from a meal.&lt;SEP&gt;An insulin dose calculated to cover carbohydrate intake of a meal.&lt;SEP&gt;A bolus dose intended to cover carbohydrate intake from meals.&lt;SEP&gt;Meal Bolus is the insulin dose calculated to cover the carbohydrate content of a meal, using the Insulin-to-Carbohydrate Ratio.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9c435da9a83d88897df07d2d5ee02574&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f2b8be67edef23560656776b89947c10&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c8ef457272b70b6404625941c8d26a3d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b9eee903de4b7e25fc53f52e2e739637&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db8e2f5011e0e0fe7dc11273e2f345b9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f677e56841fc57bffd8bf5b6cc4a7797&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7e3c3741659a85988124e5ddaf69c849</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786330154</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Correction Bolus">
  <data key="d0">Correction Bolus</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Correction Bolus is an insulin dose specifically calculated to lower an elevated blood‑glucose (BG) or sensor‑glucose (SG) reading toward a predetermined target range. It is a supplemental bolus that is used when a high glucose value is detected and no carbohydrate intake is accompanying the reading.  

The amount of insulin in a Correction Bolus is determined from the current glucose measurement—obtained either from a finger‑stick blood glucose meter or from continuous glucose sensor data—and the individual’s insulin sensitivity factor (ISF). By applying the ISF to the difference between the measured value and the target glucose level, the pump or calculator derives the precise amount of insulin needed to bring the glucose level down to the desired range.  

Correction Bolus may be delivered manually by the user or automatically by an insulin pump operating in features such as SmartGuard or other closed‑loop modes. In automatic mode the pump uses real‑time SG readings to compute and administer the corrective insulin without user intervention.  

Overall, the purpose of a Correction Bolus is to correct high glucose readings—whether from BG meters or CGM sensors—by delivering the calculated insulin dose that reduces the value to within the target glucose range, without the need to account for carbohydrate intake.&lt;SEP&gt;Correction Bolus is the insulin dose calculated to lower elevated blood glucose toward a target level, using the Insulin Sensitivity Factor.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9c435da9a83d88897df07d2d5ee02574&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dd31a315488bb0669257b83dd88b9809&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d03a310916c005d1dfa70800a753d1c5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c8ef457272b70b6404625941c8d26a3d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b9eee903de4b7e25fc53f52e2e739637&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-05241912c4f8f5e79ae75071a1c7c604&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4a4a75301f61fc3c86ad768de09d0c3f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d68acc5f59d78c14cf4d2e4d34edf5e4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b48243f8e773d3c94abc58e2314db2c0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ae3b43add031516d14e51c6d2a985bd7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9ec9cae555a06ac660e6c16d90116c8b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-542e3b31a3f3a9496f26d05d1255498a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-97eb00dc26d33c23bf8bf473c0a98472&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f677e56841fc57bffd8bf5b6cc4a7797&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-20af4762343b8357c2c72473211f2918&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1c5a5c97986d9b31b155b0c8f0cac1c5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7e3c3741659a85988124e5ddaf69c849</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786330153</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Daily History">
  <data key="d0">Daily History</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Daily History is a screen in the pump interface that displays the history of administered bolus doses.&lt;SEP&gt;Daily History displays a record of past bolus doses and glucose readings for a selected day.&lt;SEP&gt;Daily History is the log of insulin delivery events stored by the pump.&lt;SEP&gt;Daily history provides details of events entered or actions performed using the insulin pump.&lt;SEP&gt;A daily log of device activity.&lt;SEP&gt;Daily History is content recording daily device activity.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9c435da9a83d88897df07d2d5ee02574&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9855ca7ae42a0c01685280c4cc5bb56a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db8e2f5011e0e0fe7dc11273e2f345b9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a111edb31d6739acf013ce812b952366&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9bfe428f5a1381000cf6932b37aa2239&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1c5a5c97986d9b31b155b0c8f0cac1c5</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329573</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Options Menu">
  <data key="d0">Options Menu</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Options Menu provides navigation choices such as History, Adjustments, and Settings within the insulin pump interface.&lt;SEP&gt;Options Menu is a selectable screen on the insulin pump that provides access to various configuration options.&lt;SEP&gt;Options Menu is the interface within Preset Bolus Setup that provides edit, rename, and delete functions for a preset bolus.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9c435da9a83d88897df07d2d5ee02574&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b9eee903de4b7e25fc53f52e2e739637&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a074860e7f25b8dfbcccbabb53c645d7</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329653</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="HC">
  <data key="d0">HC</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">HC is the carbohydrate count input.&lt;SEP&gt;HC represents the carbohydrate amount entered into the Bolus Wizard (e.g., 41 grams or 63 grams).&lt;SEP&gt;HC represents the amount of carbohydrates (in grams) entered for a meal to calculate a Meal Bolus.&lt;SEP&gt;HC represents the carbohydrate‑to‑insulin ratio setting.&lt;SEP&gt;HC is the carbohydrate count entered into the Bolus Wizard for insulin dose calculation.&lt;SEP&gt;HC denotes the amount of carbohydrates (gramos de carbohidratos) entered to determine the appropriate bolus.</data>
