<node id="Alarma">
  <data key="d0">Alarma</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Alarma is an audible alert that sounds when the Autoapagado timer expires without user input, indicating a potential danger.&lt;SEP&gt;Audible alert generated by the Autoapagado function when the inactivity period exceeds the configured threshold.&lt;SEP&gt;Alarm is a critical notification indicating a problem that prevents insulin administration, such as blocked infusion or battery replacement, accompanied by a red light flashing twice, an audio tone or vibration, and a red screen icon.&lt;SEP&gt;An alarm condition indicated by the flashing notification light.&lt;SEP&gt;A critical notification from the pump indicating that insulin delivery is blocked and must be addressed immediately.&lt;SEP&gt;Alarma is the alert generated by the Autoapagado function when insulin delivery is stopped.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f5a3c673db465ff57a023abf1cd26053&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ca7afb2078bd96edf087859a2c89920c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-310d06ee583c6aa24af77816642d0ba7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cfb7c582936fb68746bd1911895df40c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dc1b97c88d050500f2b90b8837bd34bd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-220ba7466dbb8a2a07b8e4b09b215d39</data>
