<node id="Normal Bolus">
  <data key="d0">Normal Bolus</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Normal Bolus is the standard insulin bolus type provided in both Manual Mode and the Bolus Wizard of insulin pump systems. It delivers the entire prescribed insulin amount in a single, immediate injection at the moment the user initiates the bolus. This delivery mode is used to cover carbohydrate intake from meals, to correct elevated blood glucose readings, or for combined food‑and‑correction dosing. Because the dose is administered all at once, it represents the “full‑dose” or “single‑dose” bolus option.

The Normal Bolus can be stopped or interrupted using the system’s Stop Bolus command if the user decides to cancel or modify the dose before completion. Although it is a standalone delivery method, it may be employed alongside other bolus types (such as extended or dual wave boluses) when a more complex insulin regimen is required. As a concept, Normal Bolus defines the baseline, immediate insulin delivery option from which alternative bolus strategies deviate.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2dada456819c45230012103650ccc14a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d68acc5f59d78c14cf4d2e4d34edf5e4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db8e2f5011e0e0fe7dc11273e2f345b9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a0267d2986a48c4c31790b6f183277dc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b6025fa711665988fad0f789b9eb901a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ae3b43add031516d14e51c6d2a985bd7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a111edb31d6739acf013ce812b952366&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9639df6feeacb49b96ddc51763dec77d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a01dc8dc15b92e2b0b570753b0f57632&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-97eb00dc26d33c23bf8bf473c0a98472&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a074860e7f25b8dfbcccbabb53c645d7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b907eb92deb747df3fb3b37fb9974142&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-20af4762343b8357c2c72473211f2918</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329564</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="GS">
  <data key="d0">GS</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">GS is the abbreviation used for the glucose sensor reading (also referred to in Spanish as “Glucosa en sangre”) that appears on an insulin pump’s screen and is expressed in milligrams per deciliter (mg/dL). The term can denote either the continuous glucose value supplied by the pump’s built‑in sensor or a capillary blood glucose measurement obtained with a handheld glucose meter, both of which represent the patient’s current blood‑sugar level.

The GS value shown on the home screen reflects the sensor’s measurement averaged over the most recent 12 minutes. Users may also input a GS value manually—such as 103 mg/dL or 131 mg/dL—when they have a specific reading from a meter, and the pump can accept remote sensor data transmitted via the Accu‑Chek Guide Link. Thus, GS can be displayed automatically by the sensor, entered directly by the user, or received from an external device.

GS serves as the primary glucose datum for the pump’s Bolus Wizard™ feature, which uses the current reading to calculate corrective insulin boluses and to guide overall dosing decisions. The reading is consulted during routine dosing, when resolving alerts (for example, a blocked infusion alarm), and for regular glucose‑trend monitoring, including nightly checks typically performed around 10 PM. Health professionals often advise that a glucose measurement be taken at least every two hours, or according to individualized instructions, to ensure accurate insulin delivery.

In summary, the GS reading functions as a central data point on the insulin pump platform, providing real‑time glucose information that drives insulin dosing calculations, alerts, and broader glucose‑management strategies.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8aa63853b30ac5d214c8cd80df90e517&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5863810bebfd1be64b8af80afcd57e11&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9c435da9a83d88897df07d2d5ee02574&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-84bb2bb0df91a594c6936b2fe97e4220&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f5a3c673db465ff57a023abf1cd26053&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2dada456819c45230012103650ccc14a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ca7afb2078bd96edf087859a2c89920c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9855ca7ae42a0c01685280c4cc5bb56a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9b74c4d587eaa1f27358b25bcf758f1f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dd31a315488bb0669257b83dd88b9809&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cf725cb54eea97f946e1f27eae125a0b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-644dc086af7b196cc5bc332524608d5f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-63f6eb3be969569b166fc1e5f7e7567f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b0caf812af55afd2de9fea4fdd33fd06&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f5f31f609ed760b9e36f235d0109b470&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3d24fce6aa8866fb4a11514ae0e4d675&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-35a3bbe287cd55b2fd0a1505c706e7a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-da0dcb28a160ed0e11da58b075919575&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8fdb2f497ff0665f2860089645ba9450&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0cf7c487c5bd4a61120add295be9d518&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-de8328f990d0902170699f76dac78b01&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1577ef83aca01016db533eba7c49d2a1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d7305e2b34a4a57db2afea4935fe2fc2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-220ba7466dbb8a2a07b8e4b09b215d39&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-01785f6f03692dc5e35c672e21b345f7</data>
