<node id="Piston">
  <data key="d0">Piston</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The piston inside the pump acts as a syringe plunger, pressing the reservoir to move insulin.&lt;SEP&gt;The piston (Émbolo) is a movable part that pushes insulin from the reservoir into the tubing.&lt;SEP&gt;Mechanical part inside the pump that pushes on the reservoir to move insulin through the tubing.&lt;SEP&gt;A component located in the reservoir compartment of the pump that engages the reservoir and pushes insulin through the tubing.&lt;SEP&gt;Piston is the part of the insulin pump that engages the reservoir and moves insulin through the tubing.</data>
