<node id="Caregivers">
  <data key="d0">Caregivers</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Caregivers are individuals authorized to view a patient’s pump data through CareLink Personal.&lt;SEP&gt;Individuals who can activate Block Mode to protect the pump from unauthorized use.&lt;SEP&gt;Caregivers are individuals who may assist people with diabetes in using insulin pump technology.&lt;SEP&gt;Caregivers are individuals who support patients at risk of hypoglycemia.&lt;SEP&gt;Caregivers (roommates, school personnel, childcare professionals, correctional staff, coworkers) should be trained in glucagon administration.&lt;SEP&gt;Caregivers are individuals providing care to patients with gestational diabetes mellitus.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9855ca7ae42a0c01685280c4cc5bb56a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d4d222786e6ed163a90874659266c72a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9cd925790899146eeb8a373879b5feac&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cc39a0c02d5f1bd08d5cb71bacc69a24&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-36ddeaa53bc38bee375d7ac6d71485d4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8ba9c9c7fe9dd4e901eb52088f3d59f8</data>
