<node id="Bolus Normal">
  <data key="d0">Bolus Normal</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Bolus Normal is the standard single‑dose insulin delivery used for meals or high glucose correction.&lt;SEP&gt;Standard insulin bolus where the total programmed dose is delivered in a few minutes.&lt;SEP&gt;Bolus Normal is the standard insulin bolus administered for meals.&lt;SEP&gt;Bolus normal is a type of bolus indicated by an (N) after the dose amount.&lt;SEP&gt;Bolus Normal is the portion of insulin delivered instantly at the start of a dual bolus.&lt;SEP&gt;Bolus Normal is the standard single‑dose immediate insulin bolus used for typical meals or to correct high glucose values.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-dd31a315488bb0669257b83dd88b9809&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d9b29e7a7839d7ff2b29e72fb4912618&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7cbaec668e54aa5cf462a7bd08d7813c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-35a3bbe287cd55b2fd0a1505c706e7a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fcff234f91816c50c56d0113b934824c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-de8328f990d0902170699f76dac78b01</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786325505</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Alarm">
  <data key="d0">Alarm</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Alarm is an audible or visual notification generated by an insulin pump (and, when applicable, displayed on the MiniMed Mobile app) to warn the user of a problem that requires immediate attention.  The pump may emit a beeping sound, a vibration, or flash a notification light, and the same warning can appear as a message on the handheld device or app screen.

Alarms indicate a wide range of issues affecting the pump, its sensor, or the continuous glucose monitoring (CGM) system.  They can signal critical conditions such as stopped insulin delivery, low glucose (low SG) levels, low power, required battery or cartridge “rewind,” sensor failures, imminent sensor expiration, or extreme sensor temperatures.  Specific pump functions, such as Auto‑Suspend activation, also trigger an audible alert to inform the user that insulin delivery has been temporarily halted.

The term “alarm” is used generically for any high‑priority notification—whether sound, vibration, or visual cue—that denotes a condition demanding prompt user action.  Examples include alerts for power loss, sensor malfunctions, or any situation that could compromise therapy safety.  In all cases, the alarm serves as a critical safety feature, ensuring the user is aware of and can respond to potentially hazardous events.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-dd31a315488bb0669257b83dd88b9809&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6a9714e3b2aaad60242e3827215230bc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-83bb94d08bdb958eff25f76c9a6ac18a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4a75df3ab63706f501e8d3134e74a64b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-87a1bd89a18cb218431ff9359e299ee6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f3d819d6498d4482286628946e37a6b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-27b3ea1063acf8e0a407a89daea0dc32&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a111edb31d6739acf013ce812b952366&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9bfe428f5a1381000cf6932b37aa2239&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-14031c05fdb4152e391234af47d0cfe4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2e9f02579c179c758cc6393322299d9c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dd545bc80ceae270c16406af736789b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e8e9d04ca4b641b5d8d5ef85044f4566&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dcea1ff62aae96936f552880e96faa69&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1c5a5c97986d9b31b155b0c8f0cac1c5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-59d8fcf807f0beb090b2f3d68cc7c168&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-46d04af5292fae98e3aa651d9cec4512</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329534</data>
