<node id="Glucagón">
  <data key="d0">Glucagón</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Glucagón is an emergency medication administered by injection to raise blood glucose during severe hypoglycemia.&lt;SEP&gt;Glucagón is a medication used to treat hypoglycemia when the patient cannot eat or drink, to be administered by a familiar, coworker, or friend.&lt;SEP&gt;Glucagón is a hormone mentioned in the manual for treating hypoglycemia.&lt;SEP&gt;Glucagon is a hormone produced by the pancreas that raises blood glucose by signaling the liver to release stored glucose.&lt;SEP&gt;Glucagón is a hormone that can be injected to raise blood glucose levels during severe hypoglycemia.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-644dc086af7b196cc5bc332524608d5f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-310d06ee583c6aa24af77816642d0ba7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a717b5a81dbba0bd3cf2aae23dc0e309&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1fa7ad1de214645f0e643708dc1efab8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6c123ae434326de3ccfe03d252e5d267</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786324122</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Monitorización Continua de Glucosa">
  <data key="d0">Monitorización Continua de Glucosa</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Monitorización Continua de Glucosa is a continuous glucose monitoring method that advises not to rely on sensor glucose values for treatment decisions or on the low‑limit suspend function.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-644dc086af7b196cc5bc332524608d5f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786322883</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Glucosa">
  <data key="d0">Glucosa</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Glucosa is the term used for glucose, a simple carbohydrate that serves as the primary source of energy for the human body. The molecule circulates in the bloodstream, interstitial fluid, and within cells, providing the fuel needed for cellular metabolism and overall physiological function.  

In clinical practice, Glucosa refers specifically to the concentration of blood glucose, typically expressed in milligrams per deciliter (mg/dL) or as sensor glucose (SG) values when measured by continuous glucose monitoring systems. These values are obtained multiple times each day and are essential for assessing whether an individual is experiencing hyperglycemia (high blood sugar) or hypoglycemia (low blood sugar).  

The level of Glucosa in the blood is tightly regulated by the hormones insulin and glucagon. Insulin, released by the pancreas in response to rising glucose after carbohydrate, fat, or protein ingestion, promotes the uptake of glucose into tissues and lowers blood concentrations. Conversely, glucagon raises blood glucose by stimulating hepatic glucose production when levels fall.  

Monitoring Glucosa is a cornerstone of diabetes management. Blood glucose readings guide therapeutic decisions such as insulin dosing, adjustments to insulin pump settings, and other medication regimens. Trends and alerts derived from continuous monitoring help clinicians and patients modify diet, activity, and medication to maintain glucose within target ranges, thereby reducing the risk of complications associated with chronic dysregulation.&lt;SEP&gt;Glucosa is the blood glucose level that is measured frequently to guide insulin dosing.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-644dc086af7b196cc5bc332524608d5f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-63f6eb3be969569b166fc1e5f7e7567f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a717b5a81dbba0bd3cf2aae23dc0e309&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1fa7ad1de214645f0e643708dc1efab8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-34da912924aa29d035c8cd1c3f4f6ae3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1255cfcf42afb2c6045de0d45b11e99d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7d6466bdd61e024e50acc3fed9a5f9f8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6737e479a665e986547e5e1e29ef26da&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f3d0dd38cbfd29061a0c9916efb7c5d8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-505b4450257d1a728c397959b044ee97&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4ed0e4c13d1643a77d1d74092a8cda5a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-817893fc39ccf7551d476cefaf7f32ca&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50d9a787da93a3bf7ea1e315273b560c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4eaa74c3ef8165f52ddf18e17a240a9d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3dd65471e9cdf7a7389998e6124f5b10&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7cbaec668e54aa5cf462a7bd08d7813c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-35a3bbe287cd55b2fd0a1505c706e7a4</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786325505</data>
