  <data key="d5">1786329573</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Inactivation Mode">
  <data key="d0">Inactivation Mode</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Inactivation mode disables the pump after a period of inactivity until reactivated.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4fe81d733c2a429da0726794b55350b0</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786322885</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Certified Instructor">
  <data key="d0">Certified Instructor</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">The certified instructor provides formal training on the insulin pump product.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4fe81d733c2a429da0726794b55350b0</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786322885</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Insertion Needle">
  <data key="d0">Insertion Needle</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The insertion needle is a small needle used in the insertion site section that is removed after the cannula is placed.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4fe81d733c2a429da0726794b55350b0</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786322885</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Alert">
  <data key="d0">Alert</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Alert is a generic term for any notification generated by an insulin pump, its associated software, or a connected sensor that indicates a condition, error, or safety issue requiring the user’s attention or action. These notifications can appear on the pump’s screen, be delivered through the MiniMed Mobile app, or be signaled by an audible beep, vibration, or flashing notification light, often accompanied by a yellow icon to denote higher priority.

Alerts cover a wide range of situations, including but not limited to low reservoir volume, low or depleted battery, empty reservoir, sensor malfunctions, calibration failures, and missed scheduled bolus deliveries. While an alert informs the user of a problem, it does not necessarily halt pump operation immediately; instead, it prompts the user to address the issue to maintain safe and effective therapy. Higher‑priority alerts, such as calibration failures, are distinguished by more prominent visual or audible cues to ensure rapid response.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4fe81d733c2a429da0726794b55350b0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d9b29e7a7839d7ff2b29e72fb4912618&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6a9714e3b2aaad60242e3827215230bc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-87a1bd89a18cb218431ff9359e299ee6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bcdc240f555b6c71532ea6d04e0c5798&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f3d819d6498d4482286628946e37a6b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a111edb31d6739acf013ce812b952366&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-14031c05fdb4152e391234af47d0cfe4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fd8af150d14c8fd9fd3b20e486220f65&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2e9f02579c179c758cc6393322299d9c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dd545bc80ceae270c16406af736789b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b23dfd3ae95fca711f8f10fc98ab467c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dcea1ff62aae96936f552880e96faa69&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1c5a5c97986d9b31b155b0c8f0cac1c5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-59d8fcf807f0beb090b2f3d68cc7c168&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-46d04af5292fae98e3aa651d9cec4512</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329535</data>
