  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Thomas">
  <data key="d0">Thomas</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Thomas is a runner who experiences nocturnal hypoglycemia and configures the Autoapagado feature to improve sleep safety.&lt;SEP&gt;Thomas is a runner who experiences increased risk of nocturnal hypoglycemia and often sets a temporary basal rate; he uses the Función Autoapagado to sleep more peacefully because the pump will stop insulin delivery and sound an alarm if he does not wake.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-310d06ee583c6aa24af77816642d0ba7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8f3505927abeefb80af00bfabdaff7cd</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786325510</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Glucosa En Sangre">
  <data key="d0">Glucosa En Sangre</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Glucosa En Sangre (GS) is the blood glucose measurement taken at various times such as upon waking, before meals, and during sleep.&lt;SEP&gt;Glucosa En Sangre refers to blood glucose measurements expressed in mg/dL as recorded in the therapy log.&lt;SEP&gt;Blood glucose measurement (GS) representing the glucose concentration in the bloodstream.&lt;SEP&gt;Glucosa En Sangre refers to the measured concentration of glucose in the bloodstream, used to guide therapy decisions.&lt;SEP&gt;Glucosa en sangre refers to the blood glucose level that is monitored, displayed, and used to make therapy decisions.&lt;SEP&gt;Blood glucose concentration that should be within an acceptable range.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-310d06ee583c6aa24af77816642d0ba7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6c123ae434326de3ccfe03d252e5d267&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d0a4d039b786601ed8a06d8adad50938&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fb3bd140c8e2ac53cf1b45386cb861ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-da325dc5071cd02bfe55ffc2f9b79aa5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2fb90cfe4a3993c8a19c8fd291cc4d67</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786324152</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Regla 15‑15">
  <data key="d0">Regla 15‑15</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Regla 15‑15 is a treatment protocol for mild to moderate hypoglycemia that recommends 15 g of fast‑acting carbohydrate and rechecking glucose after 15 minutes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-310d06ee583c6aa24af77816642d0ba7</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786322886</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Equipo De Emergencia De Glucagón">
  <data key="d0">Equipo De Emergencia De Glucagón</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Equipo De Emergencia De Glucagón is a kit containing glucagón for use in life‑threatening hypoglycemia.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-310d06ee583c6aa24af77816642d0ba7</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786322886</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Sensor De Monitorización Continua De Glucosa">
  <data key="d0">Sensor De Monitorización Continua De Glucosa</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Sensor De Monitorización Continua De Glucosa (MCG) continuously measures interstitial glucose but should not be solely relied upon for treatment decisions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-310d06ee583c6aa24af77816642d0ba7</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786322886</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Función Suspender En Límite Bajo">
  <data key="d0">Función Suspender En Límite Bajo</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Función Suspender En Límite Bajo is a pump method that automatically suspends insulin delivery when glucose falls below a low‑limit threshold.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-310d06ee583c6aa24af77816642d0ba7</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786322887</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hipoglucemia Leve">
  <data key="d0">Hipoglucemia Leve</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Hipoglucemia Leve is a mild form of low blood glucose requiring treatment with fast‑acting carbohydrates.&lt;SEP&gt;Hipoglucemia Leve is a mild low blood glucose condition that can be recognized and self‑treated.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-310d06ee583c6aa24af77816642d0ba7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6c123ae434326de3ccfe03d252e5d267</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786324151</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hipoglucemia Moderada">
  <data key="d0">Hipoglucemia Moderada</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Hipoglucemia Moderada is a moderate low‑glucose condition treated similarly to mild hypoglycemia.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-310d06ee583c6aa24af77816642d0ba7</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786322887</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hipoglucemia Grave">
  <data key="d0">Hipoglucemia Grave</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Hipoglucemia Grave is a severe low‑glucose emergency that may require glucagón injection.&lt;SEP&gt;Hipoglucemia Grave is a severe low blood glucose condition requiring assistance from another person.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-310d06ee583c6aa24af77816642d0ba7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6c123ae434326de3ccfe03d252e5d267</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786324151</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hidratos De Carbono De Acción Rápida">
  <data key="d0">Hidratos De Carbono De Acción Rápida</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Hidratos De Carbono De Acción Rápida are fast‑acting carbohydrates recommended to raise blood glucose during hypoglycemia.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-310d06ee583c6aa24af77816642d0ba7</data>
