</node>
<node id="MiniMed™ Insulin Pump">
  <data key="d0">MiniMed™ Insulin Pump</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">MiniMed™ Insulin Pump is a device that delivers insulin basal and bolus doses and can be programmed with various basal rate settings.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-65c6beab51324e055f4a39b388e2eefe</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786324117</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Temporal Basal Rate">
  <data key="d0">Temporal Basal Rate</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Temporal Basal Rate is a programmable basal‑rate setting that adjusts insulin delivery for temporary changes in basal needs.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-65c6beab51324e055f4a39b388e2eefe</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786324118</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Basal Rate">
  <data key="d0">Basal Rate</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Basal Rate is the programmed background insulin delivery amount that an insulin pump provides continuously, typically expressed as units per hour, to meet the body’s basal insulin needs when no meals are being consumed. It is a scheduled setting that can be defined for each time segment of a basal pattern, allowing multiple basal rates to be programmed throughout a 24‑hour period.

The Basal Rate functions as a low‑level, continuous infusion that can be temporally adjusted in response to factors such as physical activity, illness, or changing insulin sensitivity. Temporary basal settings enable the rate to be increased—for example, during sickness to prevent hyperglycemia—or reduced for other circumstances. When the pump operates in Manual mode, the Basal Rate remains the continuous infusion rate that maintains basal insulin delivery.

Because the Basal Rate directly influences glucose levels, an inappropriately high setting can contribute to hypoglycemia, while an insufficient rate may allow hyperglycemia. Consequently, the programmed rate must be verified after any pump storage or battery change, and users are advised to monitor glucose trends and adjust the rate as needed under clinical guidance.

In summary, the Basal Rate is the continuous, programmable insulin delivery rate of an insulin pump, customizable by time segment and temporary adjustments, essential for maintaining basal glucose control, and requiring careful verification and monitoring to avoid adverse glycemic events.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-65c6beab51324e055f4a39b388e2eefe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b0caf812af55afd2de9fea4fdd33fd06&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d2f8a0d67f7320d6157b61dbbf428a40&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-59137a5f20ce729bcde5c65e1e45aa29&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-36de8c99d97d234e12244c240c45f156&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9ff2787d1cec4a771ee14b7d5d97324a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-05241912c4f8f5e79ae75071a1c7c604&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b03b7fdf0dd9c96dc459929ccccdccff&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b48243f8e773d3c94abc58e2314db2c0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f3d819d6498d4482286628946e37a6b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eb80f00ba2dab32852874cb384b38de3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a111edb31d6739acf013ce812b952366&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9639df6feeacb49b96ddc51763dec77d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fd8af150d14c8fd9fd3b20e486220f65&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7b2af59ac9cf813cb07dac53f30250d0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1c5a5c97986d9b31b155b0c8f0cac1c5</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329504</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cells">
  <data key="d0">Cells</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Cells employ glucose to obtain energy for their metabolic activities.&lt;SEP&gt;Cells are the basic units of the body that require glucose for energy.&lt;SEP&gt;Cells are the basic biological units that require glucose to generate energy.&lt;SEP&gt;Cells are the body’s basic units that take up glucose under insulin’s influence.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-65c6beab51324e055f4a39b388e2eefe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9f4d152d83c514f926b18413e065c2fa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-780f90d656277126a05ed136a084fd77&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6b867cec4c5eed3b10e431cbd4078dee</data>
