<node id="Capillary Glucose Measurement">
  <data key="d0">Capillary Glucose Measurement</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A finger‑stick method of measuring blood glucose, not replaced by a sensor‑augmented pump.&lt;SEP&gt;Capillary Glucose Measurement is a finger‑stick test used to confirm sensor glucose values or alerts.&lt;SEP&gt;Capillary Glucose Measurement is a finger‑stick glucose check used to confirm values before dosing or carbohydrate intake.&lt;SEP&gt;Capillary glucose measurement is the self‑testing of blood glucose, whose absence is listed as a contraindication for SICI use.&lt;SEP&gt;Point-of-care blood glucose testing performed by finger‑stick.&lt;SEP&gt;Measurement of glucose from capillary blood, including fasting and post‑prandial values.&lt;SEP&gt;Capillary glucose measurement is a finger‑stick testing method used to obtain glucose values for calculating variability metrics such as the Coefficient of Variation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5913d17c337be62cd526d46fbdcd9a6e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-36de8c99d97d234e12244c240c45f156&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d03a310916c005d1dfa70800a753d1c5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6fba8ea0c6bdb8427804ba05f9fe49f9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-91a09040fc4581d7aad2216dba9fba79&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6d83801272f7a0ae0d797d60572fe578&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c5c8fa42a8437c5708b04fb4ad1272cf</data>
