<node id="Glucose‑Insulin Balance">
  <data key="d0">Glucose‑Insulin Balance</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The physiological equilibrium between blood glucose levels and insulin action discussed in Chapter 1.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5913d17c337be62cd526d46fbdcd9a6e</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786324122</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Páncreas">
  <data key="d0">Páncreas</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Páncreas is an organ that secretes insulin to control glucose.&lt;SEP&gt;Páncreas is the organ that produces the hormone insulin.&lt;SEP&gt;The pancreas is an organ that generates the hormones insulin and glucagon to regulate blood glucose levels.&lt;SEP&gt;The organ that naturally secretes insulin, whose function the pump aims to emulate.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a717b5a81dbba0bd3cf2aae23dc0e309&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-34da912924aa29d035c8cd1c3f4f6ae3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6737e479a665e986547e5e1e29ef26da&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50d9a787da93a3bf7ea1e315273b560c</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786324122</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hígado">
  <data key="d0">Hígado</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Hígado is an organ that works with the pancreas to maintain glucose balance.&lt;SEP&gt;Hígado is the organ that stores excess glucose as glycogen and can convert it to fat.&lt;SEP&gt;The liver is an organ that stores and releases glucose based on hormonal signals from the pancreas.&lt;SEP&gt;Organ that stores glycogen and releases glucose during sustained exercise.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a717b5a81dbba0bd3cf2aae23dc0e309&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6737e479a665e986547e5e1e29ef26da&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50d9a787da93a3bf7ea1e315273b560c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7cbaec668e54aa5cf462a7bd08d7813c</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786324122</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Torrente Sanguíneo">
  <data key="d0">Torrente Sanguíneo</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Torrente Sanguíneo is the circulatory system that transports glucose throughout the body.&lt;SEP&gt;The bloodstream is the circulatory fluid that transports glucose throughout the body.&lt;SEP&gt;The bloodstream through which insulin enters the body after administration.&lt;SEP&gt;Bloodstream through which glucose travels after digestion and glycogen breakdown.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a717b5a81dbba0bd3cf2aae23dc0e309&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-34da912924aa29d035c8cd1c3f4f6ae3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50d9a787da93a3bf7ea1e315273b560c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7cbaec668e54aa5cf462a7bd08d7813c</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786324122</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Líquido Intersticial">
  <data key="d0">Líquido Intersticial</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Líquido Intersticial is the fluid surrounding cells where glucose resides before entering cells.&lt;SEP&gt;Interstitial fluid is the fluid surrounding cells that contains glucose and participates in its transport.&lt;SEP&gt;The fluid surrounding cells where glucose moves after leaving the bloodstream.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a717b5a81dbba0bd3cf2aae23dc0e309&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-da325dc5071cd02bfe55ffc2f9b79aa5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50d9a787da93a3bf7ea1e315273b560c</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786324123</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Células">
  <data key="d0">Células</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Células are the body's cells that require glucose to produce energy.&lt;SEP&gt;Cells are biological units that take up glucose from the bloodstream and interstitial fluid under the influence of insulin.&lt;SEP&gt;Body cells that receive insulin signals to absorb glucose from the bloodstream.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a717b5a81dbba0bd3cf2aae23dc0e309&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50d9a787da93a3bf7ea1e315273b560c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7cbaec668e54aa5cf462a7bd08d7813c</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786324123</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Inyecciones">
  <data key="d0">Inyecciones</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Injections are a method of delivering insulin to individuals with diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a717b5a81dbba0bd3cf2aae23dc0e309</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786324123</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Terapia SAP">
  <data key="d0">Terapia SAP</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">SAP therapy is a sensor‑augmented insulin pump method used to control glucose levels.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a717b5a81dbba0bd3cf2aae23dc0e309</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786324123</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Equilibrio Entre La Glucosa Y La Insulina">
  <data key="d0">Equilibrio Entre La Glucosa Y La Insulina</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Equilibrio Entre La Glucosa Y La Insulina describes the physiological balance of glucose and insulin.&lt;SEP&gt;Glucose‑insulin balance is the physiological state where blood glucose remains within the normal range through coordinated hormone action.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a717b5a81dbba0bd3cf2aae23dc0e309&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6737e479a665e986547e5e1e29ef26da</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786324124</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Suspensión Dinámica">
  <data key="d0">Suspensión Dinámica</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Suspensión Dinámica is a function that suspends insulin delivery when sensor glucose is ≤70 mg/dL and predicts a rise of 20 mg/dL within 30 minutes, provided the pump is not in the refractory period.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b4cf85d0e1e129080fae6f9bea5bd77f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786324124</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Reanudación Dinámica">
  <data key="d0">Reanudación Dinámica</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Reanudación Dinámica is a function that resumes insulin delivery when sensor glucose is 20 mg/dL above the low limit and is expected to be 40 mg/dL above it within 30 minutes, with insulin suspended for at least 30 minutes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b4cf85d0e1e129080fae6f9bea5bd77f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786324125</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Alerta Antes De Límite Bajo">
  <data key="d0">Alerta Antes De Límite Bajo</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Alerta Antes De Límite Bajo is an alert activated by MiniMed™ 640G thirty minutes before the low‑glucose limit is reached.&lt;SEP&gt;Alerta Antes De Límite Bajo is a pre‑alert warning that signals an approaching low‑glucose threshold.&lt;SEP&gt;Alerta antes de límite bajo is an alert that activates a set time before the sensor glucose is expected to reach the low limit.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b4cf85d0e1e129080fae6f9bea5bd77f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-817893fc39ccf7551d476cefaf7f32ca&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3dd65471e9cdf7a7389998e6124f5b10</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786324126</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Suspensión Antes De Límite Bajo">
  <data key="d0">Suspensión Antes De Límite Bajo</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Suspensión Antes De Límite Bajo is a suspension mode that can be combined with Alerta Antes De Límite Bajo to stop insulin infusion.&lt;SEP&gt;Suspensión Antes De Límite Bajo is an option that, when selected, causes a low‑glucose alert to activate automatically.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b4cf85d0e1e129080fae6f9bea5bd77f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3dd65471e9cdf7a7389998e6124f5b10</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786324126</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Suspensión En Límite Bajo">
  <data key="d0">Suspensión En Límite Bajo</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Suspensión En Límite Bajo is a mode in which the MiniMed™ 640G suspends insulin delivery for a set period when a low‑glucose alert occurs.&lt;SEP&gt;Suspensión En Límite Bajo is a suspension mode triggered when glucose reaches the low limit.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b4cf85d0e1e129080fae6f9bea5bd77f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3dd65471e9cdf7a7389998e6124f5b10</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786324126</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Alerta En Límite Bajo">
  <data key="d0">Alerta En Límite Bajo</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Alerta En Límite Bajo is a low‑glucose warning that the MiniMed™ 640G activates when sensor glucose values reach the predefined low limit.&lt;SEP&gt;Alerta En Límite Bajo is an alert indicating that glucose has reached the low limit.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b4cf85d0e1e129080fae6f9bea5bd77f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3dd65471e9cdf7a7389998e6124f5b10</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786324126</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Alerta En Límite Alto">
  <data key="d0">Alerta En Límite Alto</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Alerta En Límite Alto is an alert indicating that glucose has reached the high limit.&lt;SEP&gt;Alerta En Límite Alto is a high‑glucose warning that the MiniMed™ 640G can generate when sensor glucose exceeds the upper limit.&lt;SEP&gt;Alerta en límite alto is an alert intended to prevent excessively high glucose values and possible ketoacidosis.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b4cf85d0e1e129080fae6f9bea5bd77f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-817893fc39ccf7551d476cefaf7f32ca&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3dd65471e9cdf7a7389998e6124f5b10</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786324127</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Alerta Antes De Límite Alto">
  <data key="d0">Alerta Antes De Límite Alto</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Alerta Antes De Límite Alto is an alert issued before glucose reaches the high limit.&lt;SEP&gt;Alerta Antes De Límite Alto is an early warning of an approaching high‑glucose threshold.&lt;SEP&gt;Alerta antes de límite alto is an alert that activates a set number of minutes before the sensor glucose is expected to reach the high limit.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b4cf85d0e1e129080fae6f9bea5bd77f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-817893fc39ccf7551d476cefaf7f32ca&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3dd65471e9cdf7a7389998e6124f5b10</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786324127</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Alerta Ascenso">
  <data key="d0">Alerta Ascenso</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Alerta Ascenso is an alert that signals a rising glucose trend.&lt;SEP&gt;Alerta Ascenso is a notification indicating a rising glucose trend.&lt;SEP&gt;Alerta ascenso notifies the user of an upward trend in sensor glucose values, working together with trend arrows on the screen.&lt;SEP&gt;An “ascending alert” indicating a rising glucose trend that requires specific checks.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b4cf85d0e1e129080fae6f9bea5bd77f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-817893fc39ccf7551d476cefaf7f32ca&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3dd65471e9cdf7a7389998e6124f5b10&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2fb90cfe4a3993c8a19c8fd291cc4d67</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786324127</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Reanudación Basal Manual">
  <data key="d0">Reanudación Basal Manual</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Reanudación Basal Manual allows the user to restart basal insulin infusion at any time by selecting a suspension option on the screen.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b4cf85d0e1e129080fae6f9bea5bd77f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786324127</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Alerta Reanudar Basal">
  <data key="d0">Alerta Reanudar Basal</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Alerta Reanudar Basal is a notification that the MiniMed™ 640G issues when basal insulin infusion resumes after a suspension.&lt;SEP&gt;Alerta Reanudar Basal notifies the user when basal insulin infusion has been resumed.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b4cf85d0e1e129080fae6f9bea5bd77f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3dd65471e9cdf7a7389998e6124f5b10</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786324127</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Glucosa Del Sensor">
  <data key="d0">Glucosa Del Sensor</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Sensor glucose measurement (SG) representing the glucose concentration in the interstitial fluid as read by the CGM sensor.&lt;SEP&gt;Glucosa Del Sensor is the glucose measurement obtained from the pump’s sensor.&lt;SEP&gt;Glucosa del sensor is the glucose reading provided by the continuous glucose sensor.&lt;SEP&gt;Glucose value measured by the sensor, used to assess trend acceptability.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b4cf85d0e1e129080fae6f9bea5bd77f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-da325dc5071cd02bfe55ffc2f9b79aa5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-817893fc39ccf7551d476cefaf7f32ca&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2fb90cfe4a3993c8a19c8fd291cc4d67</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786324128</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Límite Bajo">
  <data key="d0">Límite Bajo</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Límite Bajo is the low‑glucose threshold that can be set between 50 mg/dL and 90 mg/dL.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b4cf85d0e1e129080fae6f9bea5bd77f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786324128</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Límite Alto">
  <data key="d0">Límite Alto</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Límite Alto is the high‑glucose threshold used for alerts.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b4cf85d0e1e129080fae6f9bea5bd77f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786324128</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="SmartGuard™">
  <data key="d0">SmartGuard™</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">SmartGuard™ is an automated safety algorithm integrated into the MiniMed™ 640G insulin pump system. It continuously analyzes glucose sensor data to forecast an approaching low‑glucose limit and, when a hypoglycemia risk is detected, automatically suspends basal insulin infusion to prevent the low glucose event. The feature not only predicts impending low glucose levels but also manages the temporary interruption of insulin delivery, and it can subsequently resume basal insulin once glucose levels rise above the predefined threshold. By relying on real‑time glucose trends and preset low‑glucose thresholds, SmartGuard™ provides a predictive, hands‑free safeguard against hypoglycemia for pump users.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b4cf85d0e1e129080fae6f9bea5bd77f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b0caf812af55afd2de9fea4fdd33fd06&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6ab7cedc48ea8fdd199a2c12c99416a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-36de8c99d97d234e12244c240c45f156&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c2474d83c9e01bbd20c6e68744a2dad5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3ce8c9873da330aac077f7ccaf108ccd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-da325dc5071cd02bfe55ffc2f9b79aa5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3dd65471e9cdf7a7389998e6124f5b10</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786324128</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hidratos De Carbono De Absorción Rápida">
  <data key="d0">Hidratos De Carbono De Absorción Rápida</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Hidratos De Carbono De Absorción Rápida are fast‑acting carbohydrates (e.g., glucose tablets) used to treat low glucose.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b4cf85d0e1e129080fae6f9bea5bd77f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786324128</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Tabletas De Glucosa">
  <data key="d0">Tabletas De Glucosa</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Tabletas De Glucosa are glucose tablets recommended for rapid carbohydrate intake.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b4cf85d0e1e129080fae6f9bea5bd77f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786324129</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Equipo De Formación">
  <data key="d0">Equipo De Formación</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Equipo De Formación is the training team that provides personalized instruction on pump use.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b4cf85d0e1e129080fae6f9bea5bd77f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786324129</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Plan De Tratamiento">
  <data key="d0">Plan De Tratamiento</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Plan De Tratamiento is the user’s individualized therapy plan for managing glucose.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b4cf85d0e1e129080fae6f9bea5bd77f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786324129</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Guía De Usuario Del Sistema MiniMed™ 640G">
  <data key="d0">Guía De Usuario Del Sistema MiniMed™ 640G</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Guía De Usuario Del Sistema MiniMed™ 640G is the user manual that describes how to manage alerts, suspensions, and carbohydrate treatment.&lt;SEP&gt;Guía De Usuario Del Sistema MiniMed™ 640G is the user manual that explains system functions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b4cf85d0e1e129080fae6f9bea5bd77f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3dd65471e9cdf7a7389998e6124f5b10</data>
