</node>
<node id="Trend Arrows">
  <data key="d0">Trend Arrows</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Trend Arrows are visual, graphical indicators displayed on the screen of Medtronic MiniMed insulin pumps—including the MiniMed™ and MiniMed 640G models—that convey the speed and direction of recent sensor glucose (SG) changes. They appear as arrow symbols on the pump’s display and inform the user whether glucose levels are rising, falling, or remaining stable.  

Each arrow reflects the rate of change of sensor glucose over the most recent minutes, typically summarizing the trend observed during the previous 20 minutes. A upward‑pointing arrow denotes a rapid increase in glucose, a downward‑pointing arrow signals a rapid decrease, and a flat or neutral arrow indicates minimal change. By presenting both direction and magnitude of glucose movement, Trend Arrows help users and clinicians quickly assess glucose dynamics without examining raw glucose values.&lt;SEP&gt;Trend arrows are visual indicators on a CGM that show the direction and speed of glucose changes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b0caf812af55afd2de9fea4fdd33fd06&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-36de8c99d97d234e12244c240c45f156&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c2474d83c9e01bbd20c6e68744a2dad5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b3d901ee668c4fdbd518454aa3ebea3a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f2b8be67edef23560656776b89947c10&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f5f31f609ed760b9e36f235d0109b470&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bec9e867c8de5a0beabd70ea9209c1a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8cceea4f7036977c7ddcbe81f76f8aa1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ede0f32eb8f8ea1eaab76cc0bc7648fd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b23dfd3ae95fca711f8f10fc98ab467c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-59d8fcf807f0beb090b2f3d68cc7c168&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4e6371d8083fb20b137912cdaeec1b8b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/edelman-et-al-2026-dosing-afrezza-it-s-not-that-complicated.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786333244</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
