</node>
<node id="FSI">
  <data key="d0">FSI</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">FSI (Factor Sensitivity Index) is the value indicating how many mg/dL of glucose are reduced by one unit of insulin.&lt;SEP&gt;Factor de Sensibilidad a la Insulina, the amount of glucose (mg/dL) reduced by one unit of insulin.&lt;SEP&gt;FSI (Factor Sensitivity Index) is a numerical factor representing how many mg/dL of glucose correspond to one unit of insulin.&lt;SEP&gt;FSI is the insulin sensitivity factor used to determine correction bolus when glucose drops excessively.&lt;SEP&gt;FSI (Insulin Sensitivity Factor) quantifies how much one unit of insulin lowers glucose.&lt;SEP&gt;FSI (Factor de Sensibilidad a la Insulina) indicates how much glucose is lowered by a unit of insulin.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b0caf812af55afd2de9fea4fdd33fd06&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7d6466bdd61e024e50acc3fed9a5f9f8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f369332c7e5ee7ed284fec07f68d394d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-505b4450257d1a728c397959b044ee97&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bec9e867c8de5a0beabd70ea9209c1a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c8ef457272b70b6404625941c8d26a3d</data>
