<node id="CAD">
  <data key="d0">CAD</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">CAD (Diabetic Ketoacidosis) is a severe, potentially life‑threatening metabolic complication that occurs when high blood glucose and elevated ketone bodies accumulate because of insufficient insulin. The condition is characterized by rapid metabolic decompensation, especially in individuals with type 1 diabetes, and can develop quickly if insulin therapy is inadequate. It is commonly described as a serious medical emergency that requires an explicit emergency plan for prompt recognition and treatment. The underlying pathophysiology involves high ketone levels resulting from the body’s inability to use glucose for energy, leading to acidosis and a cascade of systemic effects. All descriptions emphasize the seriousness of the condition and the need for immediate medical intervention.  

CAD (Coronary Artery Disease) is a distinct cardiovascular disorder in which atherosclerotic plaque narrows the coronary arteries, reducing blood flow to the heart muscle. One description notes that the risk of CAD can increase during periods of illness because the body’s insulin requirements rise, potentially exacerbating underlying vascular disease. This relationship highlights how metabolic stressors may aggravate coronary artery pathology.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2dc33cf2a90bf53c26226e44bc285c22&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1255cfcf42afb2c6045de0d45b11e99d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4ed0e4c13d1643a77d1d74092a8cda5a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6b867cec4c5eed3b10e431cbd4078dee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-817893fc39ccf7551d476cefaf7f32ca&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4eaa74c3ef8165f52ddf18e17a240a9d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9ff2787d1cec4a771ee14b7d5d97324a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-494fef0b8efc2c44b3b49ebf9d74b7f2</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/Insulinoterapia – Diretriz da Sociedade Brasileira de Diabetes – Ed. 2024.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786331426</data>
