<node id="Active Insulin Time">
  <data key="d0">Active Insulin Time</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Active Insulin Time is the defined duration that a bolus of insulin continues to exert its glucose‑lowering effect after it has been delivered. It represents the period during which previously administered insulin is considered “active” and therefore contributes to lowering blood glucose levels. This concept applies both to standard bolus insulin and to correction boluses, indicating how long the insulin remains physiologically effective in the body.

In diabetes management systems, Active Insulin Time is implemented as a user‑adjustable setting. It directly influences insulin‑activity calculations used by features such as SmartGuard therapy as well as by manual insulin‑delivery modes. By specifying the length of time that insulin is tracked as active, the setting helps the pump or software estimate remaining insulin effect, avoid insulin stacking, and determine appropriate dosing for subsequent boluses or corrections.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d2f8a0d67f7320d6157b61dbbf428a40&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f2b8be67edef23560656776b89947c10&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-83bb94d08bdb958eff25f76c9a6ac18a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ae3b43add031516d14e51c6d2a985bd7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a111edb31d6739acf013ce812b952366&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fd8af150d14c8fd9fd3b20e486220f65&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-97eb00dc26d33c23bf8bf473c0a98472&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-20af4762343b8357c2c72473211f2918&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1c5a5c97986d9b31b155b0c8f0cac1c5</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329554</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
