</node>
<node id="Correction Dose">
  <data key="d0">Correction Dose</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Correction dose is the insulin amount given to correct blood glucose deviations from the target range.&lt;SEP&gt;Correction Dose is an insulin amount calculated to lower glucose toward the target range.&lt;SEP&gt;Correction Dose is the insulin amount calculated when BG Reading exceeds the high target value.&lt;SEP&gt;Correction Dose is an additional insulin amount given to lower elevated glucose levels before or after meals.&lt;SEP&gt;Correction Dose is a prandial insulin dose of Afrezza administered to lower elevated glucose levels.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d2f8a0d67f7320d6157b61dbbf428a40&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f2b8be67edef23560656776b89947c10&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-97eb00dc26d33c23bf8bf473c0a98472&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4e6371d8083fb20b137912cdaeec1b8b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4655f823785fa91e72cba96e00dba34c</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/edelman-et-al-2026-dosing-afrezza-it-s-not-that-complicated.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786333251</data>
