<node id="Sensor Glucose (SG)">
  <data key="d0">Sensor Glucose (SG)</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Sensor Glucose (SG) is the continuous glucose value measured by a continuous glucose monitoring (CGM) sensor that is placed in the interstitial fluid. The sensor records glucose concentrations in real time and reports them in milligrams per deciliter (mg/dL) on the device’s home screen, sensor graph, and other display interfaces. Each SG reading reflects the current glucose level detected by the sensor and is typically accompanied by trend arrows that indicate the direction and rate of change.

The SG values are used for a variety of therapeutic purposes. They inform the user and healthcare professionals when making insulin‑dosing decisions, trigger alerts for hypo‑ or hyperglycemic events, and can be integrated with insulin pumps to automatically adjust insulin delivery. Because SG is derived from interstitial fluid rather than a direct blood sample, it provides a near‑continuous picture of glucose dynamics rather than isolated finger‑stick measurements.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-59137a5f20ce729bcde5c65e1e45aa29&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-36de8c99d97d234e12244c240c45f156&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-edbbe2e207a7e0a28611a2a16fa2845f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4a75df3ab63706f501e8d3134e74a64b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b6025fa711665988fad0f789b9eb901a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3d0824c9d8a9ff5f2da52b7b5ea69c86&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ede0f32eb8f8ea1eaab76cc0bc7648fd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f677e56841fc57bffd8bf5b6cc4a7797&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-59d8fcf807f0beb090b2f3d68cc7c168</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329569</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
