<node id="SG">
  <data key="d0">SG</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Sensor Glucose (SG) is the term used by the MiniMed™ 640G system and its associated SAP (Sensor‑augmented Pump) device to denote the glucose concentration measured by the continuous glucose monitoring (CGM) sensor. The sensor samples interstitial fluid, converts the glucose level into a numeric value expressed in milligrams per deciliter (mg/dL), and continuously updates this reading on the pump’s display and trend graphs. Because SG is derived directly from the sensor, it is often referred to as “sensor‑derived glucose” or simply “sensor glucose.”

The SG value serves several critical functions within the pump’s therapy algorithms. It provides the real‑time data that drive trend analysis, alerts for hypo‑ or hyperglycemia, and automatic insulin delivery decisions, including low‑glucose suspend features. The reading can fall below the programmed low‑glucose limit, prompting the system to suspend insulin delivery or issue alarms. SG is also the numeric glucose figure used to trigger therapy adjustments and to inform users of current glucose status without the need for separate finger‑stick measurements.

One description in the source material characterizes SG as “the recorded glucose value obtained from capillary testing used to confirm high or low alerts.” This statement conflicts with the predominant definition that SG originates from the CGM sensor rather than a finger‑stick (capillary) measurement. The consensus across the majority of descriptions is that SG refers exclusively to sensor‑derived glucose; the capillary‑testing reference likely reflects a misunderstanding or a secondary use case where a finger‑stick value is compared to SG for verification, but it does not redefine the meaning of SG itself.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d0a4d039b786601ed8a06d8adad50938&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7d6466bdd61e024e50acc3fed9a5f9f8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-505b4450257d1a728c397959b044ee97&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f5f31f609ed760b9e36f235d0109b470&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4eaa74c3ef8165f52ddf18e17a240a9d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3dd65471e9cdf7a7389998e6124f5b10&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2fb90cfe4a3993c8a19c8fd291cc4d67&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-653c72495ca2211399f4a6660e1905e2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b6025fa711665988fad0f789b9eb901a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7ceebe6fbf743053d7b55523365689e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dd545bc80ceae270c16406af736789b2</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329472</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
