<node id="Autocontrol De Glucemia Capilar">
  <data key="d0">Autocontrol De Glucemia Capilar</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Autocontrol de glucemia capilar is a finger‑stick glucose test used to confirm a high SG or high alert before adjusting therapy.&lt;SEP&gt;Autocontrol De Glucemia Capilar is a self‑performed capillary blood glucose test used as a decision basis when alerts occur.&lt;SEP&gt;A finger‑stick capillary glucose test used to confirm sensor glucose readings.&lt;SEP&gt;Autocontrol de glucemia capilar is a finger‑stick blood glucose test used to confirm sensor readings before adjusting therapy.&lt;SEP&gt;Self‑monitoring of capillary blood glucose used to confirm sensor values and guide therapy.</data>
