<node id="Comida">
  <data key="d0">Comida</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Comida denotes food intake that can raise glucose if insufficient insulin is administered.&lt;SEP&gt;Comida denotes a meal around which insulin bolus doses are timed.&lt;SEP&gt;Any meal, whose composition of carbohydrates, fats, and proteins determines its impact on glucose and insulin needs.&lt;SEP&gt;Comida is the meal whose timing relative to bolus administration affects glucose control.&lt;SEP&gt;Comida is a generic term for a meal whose composition affects glucose levels.&lt;SEP&gt;Comida is an event type for logging meals and carbohydrate intake.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d0a4d039b786601ed8a06d8adad50938&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7d6466bdd61e024e50acc3fed9a5f9f8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-505b4450257d1a728c397959b044ee97&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d9b29e7a7839d7ff2b29e72fb4912618&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7cbaec668e54aa5cf462a7bd08d7813c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8fdb2f497ff0665f2860089645ba9450</data>
