<node id="Basal Insulin Delivery">
  <data key="d0">Basal Insulin Delivery</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Basal Insulin Delivery is the continuous low‑rate or background insulin infusion provided by an insulin pump to mimic the natural pancreas and maintain baseline glucose control between meals and overnight. It represents the steady, ongoing dose of insulin that is distinct from bolus (mealtime) delivery and is programmed into the pump as a basal rate schedule.

When features such as SmartGuard are active, the pump calculates the basal insulin dose and can automatically suspend delivery if low‑glucose conditions are detected, then automatically resume once glucose levels rise to a safe range. Users may also manually resume or adjust basal delivery through the pump’s Home screen or other interface controls.

Overall, basal insulin delivery ensures a constant supply of low‑dose insulin, supporting the body’s background metabolic needs while allowing both automated safety suspensions and manual interventions as required.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c2474d83c9e01bbd20c6e68744a2dad5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-653c72495ca2211399f4a6660e1905e2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4a4a75301f61fc3c86ad768de09d0c3f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4a75df3ab63706f501e8d3134e74a64b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-14031c05fdb4152e391234af47d0cfe4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fd751b869edcd6c88d9e467cfb2cb0fd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d3b794ead59ea83de139af0358a0e7b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a074860e7f25b8dfbcccbabb53c645d7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b907eb92deb747df3fb3b37fb9974142&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dd545bc80ceae270c16406af736789b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f94cd06ab0d1bcc7a9349bc40ea3eb22</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
