<node id="Sensor Glucose">
  <data key="d0">Sensor Glucose</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Sensor Glucose (often abbreviated SG) is the glucose concentration measured by a continuous glucose monitoring (CGM) sensor that is placed under the skin in the interstitial fluid. The sensor detects glucose levels continuously and provides a numerical reading that is reported by the CGM device and displayed on the insulin pump or receiver as an SG value.

These SG readings are updated at regular five‑minute intervals, allowing the user to see a near‑real‑time trend of glucose concentrations. The values are displayed on the pump’s screen (or the associated device) and are also used internally by the pump’s algorithms, such as the SmartGuard feature, to inform automated insulin dosing decisions.

Sensor Glucose values are typically calibrated against a reference blood glucose meter measurement, ensuring that the interstitial fluid reading aligns with capillary blood glucose. By integrating the calibrated SG data, the CGM system supplies the information needed for both user‑guided and algorithm‑driven therapy adjustments.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3ce8c9873da330aac077f7ccaf108ccd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8cceea4f7036977c7ddcbe81f76f8aa1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-83bb94d08bdb958eff25f76c9a6ac18a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a0267d2986a48c4c31790b6f183277dc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6b53b69acbef0e172ea7719cc15bf3ad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8a0307c83d7b514ca00334e4c8ca2357&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1dd74224daea51112742135154e46244&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1c5a5c97986d9b31b155b0c8f0cac1c5</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329518</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
