  <data key="d0">NICE Recommendations</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">NICE recommendations set glucose ranges 70‑126 mg/dL before meals, 90‑162 mg/dL after meals, and 70‑126 mg/dL before bedtime.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-780f90d656277126a05ed136a084fd77</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786324182</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Glucose Measurement">
  <data key="d0">Glucose Measurement</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Glucose measurement is performed in blood, expressed in mg/dL, to determine the amount of glucose present in the bloodstream.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-780f90d656277126a05ed136a084fd77</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786324182</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Organism">
  <data key="d0">Organism</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Organism is the living body that requires glucose as its primary fuel and maintains glucose levels throughout the day and during sleep.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-780f90d656277126a05ed136a084fd77</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786324182</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Food">
  <data key="d0">Food</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Food refers to ingested items that are digested and converted into nutrients, including glucose, to supply energy to the organism.&lt;SEP&gt;Food refers to ingested nutrients that may be absorbed at varying rates.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-780f90d656277126a05ed136a084fd77&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-542e3b31a3f3a9496f26d05d1255498a</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329640</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Nutrients">
  <data key="d0">Nutrients</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Nutrients are substances derived from food, such as glucose, that are absorbed into the bloodstream to support cellular metabolism.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-780f90d656277126a05ed136a084fd77</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786324182</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="mg/dL">
  <data key="d0">mg/dL</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">mg/dL (milligrams per deciliter) is the measurement unit used to express glucose concentration in the blood.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-780f90d656277126a05ed136a084fd77</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786324182</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Stored Glucose">
  <data key="d0">Stored Glucose</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Stored glucose is excess glucose that is kept in the liver as a reserve fuel for later release into the bloodstream.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-780f90d656277126a05ed136a084fd77</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786324183</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Fuel Reserve">
  <data key="d0">Fuel Reserve</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Fuel reserve refers to the stored glucose in the liver that can be mobilized to provide energy during exercise or prolonged fasting.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-780f90d656277126a05ed136a084fd77</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786324183</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Night">
  <data key="d0">Night</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Night represents the period of sleep during which the organism relies on stored glucose to maintain energy levels.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-780f90d656277126a05ed136a084fd77</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786324183</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Tendencia Ascendente">
  <data key="d0">Tendencia Ascendente</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Tendencia Ascendente describes a rising glucose trend observed after meals or during the night.&lt;SEP&gt;Tendencia Ascendente denotes a rising trend in blood glucose readings.&lt;SEP&gt;A rising glucose trend displayed on the MiniMed™ 640G screen.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-505b4450257d1a728c397959b044ee97&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d9b29e7a7839d7ff2b29e72fb4912618&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2fb90cfe4a3993c8a19c8fd291cc4d67</data>
