</node>
<node id="Hemoglobin A1C">
  <data key="d0">Hemoglobin A1C</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Hemoglobin A1C is a laboratory test that provides a percentage reflecting average blood glucose over the previous 2‑3 months.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f8e89a2540c525a104b0a1a5513347a8</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786324191</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Blood Glucose Meter">
  <data key="d0">Blood Glucose Meter</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Blood Glucose Meter is a medical device designed to measure the concentration of glucose in a blood sample, typically obtained from a fingertip prick. The meter generates an immediate blood glucose (BG) reading that reflects the user’s current glucose level at the time of testing.

These BG readings serve several critical functions in diabetes management systems. They are entered into insulin pumps for accurate insulin dosing, used to calibrate or verify continuous glucose sensors, and act as reference values during pump troubleshooting or after changing an infusion set or reservoir. The device also provides target glucose values for situations when food is not being consumed, helping users maintain appropriate glycaemic control.

Commercially available Blood Glucose Meters intended for use with the MiniMed 780G system must comply with ISO 15197:2013 standards, ensuring accuracy and reliability for sensor calibration and verification within that closed‑loop therapy platform. In all contexts, the meter functions as the primary artifact for obtaining trustworthy blood glucose measurements that inform insulin delivery decisions and overall diabetes self‑management.&lt;SEP&gt;Blood Glucose Meter is a medical device that measures blood glucose concentrations and must meet regulatory accuracy criteria.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f8e89a2540c525a104b0a1a5513347a8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-05241912c4f8f5e79ae75071a1c7c604&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8cceea4f7036977c7ddcbe81f76f8aa1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-379a204614747df98c1296e2f76c264f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b03b7fdf0dd9c96dc459929ccccdccff&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a0267d2986a48c4c31790b6f183277dc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-177e9aca0bf1c1724474ea529826bece&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9ec9cae555a06ac660e6c16d90116c8b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a01dc8dc15b92e2b0b570753b0f57632&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-97eb00dc26d33c23bf8bf473c0a98472&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3895d65c9a22c257a4717f300d4086b0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f677e56841fc57bffd8bf5b6cc4a7797&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b907eb92deb747df3fb3b37fb9974142&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f94cd06ab0d1bcc7a9349bc40ea3eb22&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db5749bec4af1c3ea068b257c4376aaf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-40c2c862887db201b07c741a1862dcc1</data>
