<node id="Pump">
  <data key="d0">Pump</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Pump is the medical insulin‑delivery device that serves as the core component of the MiniMed 780G system and similar MiniMed platforms. It is an infusion pump that stores a replaceable insulin reservoir, locks the reservoir in place, and delivers insulin through an attached infusion set. The device is capable of administering both basal (continuous) and bolus (mealtime) insulin doses according to programmed settings, and it can automatically suspend delivery when sensor glucose readings fall below predefined thresholds or when specific SmartGuard feature settings are active.

The pump integrates several user‑interface elements: a multi‑line screen, speaker, and vibration motor that convey alarms, alerts, and status messages. It generates audible and visual alerts for events such as low‑glucose warnings, delivery errors, hardware issues, or loss of sensor communication, and it allows users to snooze or acknowledge these alerts. Alerts may also be triggered if the pump cannot locate a paired continuous glucose monitoring (CGM) sensor or transmitter. The device can be paired with a CGM sensor and its transmitter, enabling real‑time glucose data exchange and closed‑loop insulin adjustments. It also connects to a glucose meter for data sharing and displays serial numbers for identification.

Power for the pump is supplied either by an internal rechargeable source or by a standard AA battery, and the unit can be detached from the body for inspection, cleaning, or replacement of components. Users are instructed to check the pump for cracks or damage before each use. The pump’s firmware can be updated via software tools, ensuring that features such as SmartGuard, sensor communication protocols, and alert logic remain current. Overall, the Pump functions as a self‑contained, programmable medical device that delivers insulin, manages delivery settings, monitors CGM data, and provides comprehensive safety alerts to support safe and effective diabetes management.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fdabdf4730f349f4b46e7242c65d440d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-527777f044e20410ca47d2c5b35306ca&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d8e2c8beb0e0581ef5724dc5c631252e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-653c72495ca2211399f4a6660e1905e2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6a9714e3b2aaad60242e3827215230bc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bf54a88e051fe74fd94b773f8b5d98da&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-df77f2ea988e5724effb4c71cc79a65a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db8e2f5011e0e0fe7dc11273e2f345b9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fe844728a502927fee80d42268408b1a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-87a1bd89a18cb218431ff9359e299ee6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-28515a0aca492eeee478cd9947226498&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bcdc240f555b6c71532ea6d04e0c5798&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b48243f8e773d3c94abc58e2314db2c0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f3d819d6498d4482286628946e37a6b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7ceebe6fbf743053d7b55523365689e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a111edb31d6739acf013ce812b952366&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9bfe428f5a1381000cf6932b37aa2239&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fd751b869edcd6c88d9e467cfb2cb0fd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fd8af150d14c8fd9fd3b20e486220f65&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d3b794ead59ea83de139af0358a0e7b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3895d65c9a22c257a4717f300d4086b0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8a0307c83d7b514ca00334e4c8ca2357&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b907eb92deb747df3fb3b37fb9974142&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b23dfd3ae95fca711f8f10fc98ab467c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1c5a5c97986d9b31b155b0c8f0cac1c5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f94cd06ab0d1bcc7a9349bc40ea3eb22&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c030749e7f9a2ae77cb8993d7250cffe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-46d04af5292fae98e3aa651d9cec4512</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329451</data>
