<node id="AA Battery">
  <data key="d0">AA Battery</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">AA Battery is a standard AA‑size, 1.5 V power source—available in lithium, alkaline, or rechargeable NiMH chemistries—that is supplied as part of the accessories for the MiniMed insulin pump. It is a replaceable external battery that must be physically inserted into the pump to provide its primary power and to resolve the “insert battery” alarm when the internal power source is insufficient or cannot charge.

The AA Battery powers the pump continuously during normal use and, during storage, should be installed for an 8‑ to 12‑hour period every six months to maintain battery health. Because it is removable, users can inspect the battery and replace it as needed, ensuring reliable operation of the insulin delivery system.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-527777f044e20410ca47d2c5b35306ca&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d8e2c8beb0e0581ef5724dc5c631252e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-df77f2ea988e5724effb4c71cc79a65a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eb80f00ba2dab32852874cb384b38de3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9bfe428f5a1381000cf6932b37aa2239&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a01dc8dc15b92e2b0b570753b0f57632&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-71de01baf40871c616eaa39cb8189f43&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f94cd06ab0d1bcc7a9349bc40ea3eb22</data>
