<node id="Change Sensor Alert">
  <data key="d0">Change Sensor Alert</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Change sensor alert advises the user to replace the sensor.&lt;SEP&gt;Alert that prompts the user to replace a sensor that is not securely connected.&lt;SEP&gt;Change Sensor Alert advises the user to discard the current sensor and insert a new one.&lt;SEP&gt;Change sensor alert prompts the user to replace the sensor after certain failure conditions.&lt;SEP&gt;Change Sensor Alert is an alarm prompting sensor replacement.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-95ba6f1fa7d1791230f690255a8ba2df&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-87a1bd89a18cb218431ff9359e299ee6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-28515a0aca492eeee478cd9947226498&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a111edb31d6739acf013ce812b952366&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8a0307c83d7b514ca00334e4c8ca2357</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329415</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Calibration Not Accepted Alert">
  <data key="d0">Calibration Not Accepted Alert</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Alert that appears when a calibration attempt fails due to invalid BG reading or signal issues.&lt;SEP&gt;Calibration Not Accepted Alert is an alarm indicating calibration data was rejected.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-95ba6f1fa7d1791230f690255a8ba2df&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a111edb31d6739acf013ce812b952366</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329416</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Simplera Sync">
  <data key="d0">Simplera Sync</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Simplera Sync is a component of the Guardian 4 continuous glucose monitoring (CGM) system that encompasses both hardware and software elements. In the device documentation it is listed under the Sensor Section as a CGM sensor model or accessory that works directly with the Guardian 4 sensor, and the MiniMed Mobile App can be used optionally with this accessory.  

As a software application, Simplera Sync functions as the interface that synchronizes glucose data from the sensor to the Guardian 4 insulin pump. It presents alerts and messages for the pump‑sensor system, and it supports sensor calibration by incorporating blood‑glucose meter readings. The system is referenced alongside Guardian 4 in sensor alert messages and is described in the CGM device documentation as a hardware or software component integral to the overall CGM solution.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-95ba6f1fa7d1791230f690255a8ba2df&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-87a1bd89a18cb218431ff9359e299ee6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-177e9aca0bf1c1724474ea529826bece&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1dd74224daea51112742135154e46244&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dd545bc80ceae270c16406af736789b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-59d8fcf807f0beb090b2f3d68cc7c168&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c030749e7f9a2ae77cb8993d7250cffe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-46d04af5292fae98e3aa651d9cec4512</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329416</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Mobile Device">
  <data key="d0">Mobile Device</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Mobile Device refers to a compatible smartphone or tablet required for the MiniMed Mobile App to function.&lt;SEP&gt;Device such as a smartphone used to run the MiniMed Mobile app and communicate via NFC.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-95ba6f1fa7d1791230f690255a8ba2df&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1dd74224daea51112742135154e46244</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329417</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Suspend By Sensor Icon">
  <data key="d0">Suspend By Sensor Icon</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Suspend By Sensor Icon appears on the Home Screen when the pump is awaiting sensor status or a suspend event occurs.&lt;SEP&gt;Red X icon indicating that suspend features are unavailable due to sensor issues.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-95ba6f1fa7d1791230f690255a8ba2df&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-92417ae942a11c591feb2ee9b5fadd7e</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329417</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Suspend Before Low Feature">
  <data key="d0">Suspend Before Low Feature</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Suspend Before Low Feature is a pump setting that can suspend insulin delivery when low glucose is detected, and triggers specific status icons.&lt;SEP&gt;Suspend Before Low Feature is a feature that temporarily suspends insulin delivery for up to two hours, is off by default, activates alerts, and cannot be used simultaneously with Suspend On Low Feature.&lt;SEP&gt;Suspend Before Low Feature is a pump function that suspends insulin delivery when glucose is predicted to drop low; unavailable when SmartGuard is active.&lt;SEP&gt;Feature that automatically suspends insulin delivery when glucose is predicted to fall low.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-95ba6f1fa7d1791230f690255a8ba2df&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b48243f8e773d3c94abc58e2314db2c0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-92417ae942a11c591feb2ee9b5fadd7e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d3b794ead59ea83de139af0358a0e7b3</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329418</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Guardian 4">
  <data key="d0">Guardian 4</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Guardian 4 is a specific model of continuous glucose monitoring (CGM) sensor that is integrated with Medtronic’s MiniMed insulin‑pump ecosystem. In the product literature it is listed under the Sensor Section as the “Guardian 4” sensor, and it is the sensor that pairs the pump with the transmitter, enabling wireless communication of glucose data to the pump’s display.  

Within the MiniMed 780G insulin pump, Guardian 4 appears as a dedicated feature or mode of operation. The pump’s software recognizes the sensor and provides a set of sensor‑related alerts, messages, and alarms that inform the user about sensor status, calibration needs, and other critical events. These alerts are presented on the pump’s screen and are also reflected in the alerts list of the device manual.  

Guardian 4 employs blood‑glucose meter readings for sensor calibration, meaning that users must enter finger‑stick values to fine‑tune the CGM’s accuracy. The calibration process and related prompts are displayed by the pump, ensuring that the sensor’s glucose readings remain reliable throughout its wear period.  

Overall, Guardian 4 functions both as a CGM sensor model compatible with MiniMed pumps and as an integrated software component that manages sensor‑pump communication, calibration, and alerting. It is referenced throughout the MiniMed manual as the sensor that provides real‑time glucose data, triggers calibration messages, and generates the sensor‑related alarms that guide users in maintaining optimal diabetes management.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-95ba6f1fa7d1791230f690255a8ba2df&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4a75df3ab63706f501e8d3134e74a64b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-87a1bd89a18cb218431ff9359e299ee6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f3d819d6498d4482286628946e37a6b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-177e9aca0bf1c1724474ea529826bece&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3d0824c9d8a9ff5f2da52b7b5ea69c86&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3895d65c9a22c257a4717f300d4086b0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8a0307c83d7b514ca00334e4c8ca2357&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dd545bc80ceae270c16406af736789b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-59d8fcf807f0beb090b2f3d68cc7c168&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-46d04af5292fae98e3aa651d9cec4512</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329418</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Suspend On Low Feature">
  <data key="d0">Suspend On Low Feature</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Suspend On Low Feature is a pump setting that can suspend insulin delivery when low glucose persists, and triggers specific status icons.&lt;SEP&gt;Suspend On Low Feature is a feature that temporarily suspends insulin delivery when SG reaches the low limit, is off by default, and cannot be used simultaneously with Suspend Before Low Feature.&lt;SEP&gt;Suspend On Low Feature is a pump function that suspends insulin delivery when glucose is low; unavailable when SmartGuard is active.&lt;SEP&gt;Feature that automatically suspends insulin delivery when glucose is low.</data>
