<node id="Instinct Sensor">
  <data key="d0">Instinct Sensor</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Instinct Sensor is a continuous glucose monitoring (CGM) sensor designed for use with Medtronic’s MiniMed 780G insulin‑pump system. The sensor is inserted subcutaneously to measure interstitial glucose levels and communicates with the pump through the MiniMed Mobile app rather than a direct pump‑to‑sensor link. Activation of a new sensor session, as well as pairing and unpairing with the pump, must be performed via the MiniMed Mobile app, which also enforces security precautions during the pairing process.  

The Instinct Sensor is fully compatible with the MiniMed 780G’s advanced glucose‑control features, including SmartGuard and Predictive Low Glucose technologies, which enable automated insulin delivery adjustments and low‑glucose alerts. In addition, the system uses periodic blood‑glucose meter (BG) readings to verify sensor performance; the sensor can trigger BG checks to confirm accuracy and system reliability.  

Performance characteristics note that the sensor’s accuracy may be reduced after high intake of vitamin C, and users may occasionally encounter startup errors when initiating the sensor through the mobile app. Despite these considerations, the sensor provides reliable continuous glucose data that support the MiniMed 780G’s hybrid closed‑loop operation.  

Overall, the Instinct Sensor is a dedicated CGM component that requires the MiniMed Mobile app for activation, can be paired or unpaired with the MiniMed 780G pump, integrates with SmartGuard and Predictive Low Glucose algorithms, and incorporates BG‑check verification while being susceptible to interference from excessive vitamin C consumption.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-95ba6f1fa7d1791230f690255a8ba2df&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ab510c8377992bab31045a97eb95893a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cdb000b83632c89167783ad4e6f1fb64&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8cceea4f7036977c7ddcbe81f76f8aa1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-caf5071e54a797f595d8cac8e4653918&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-28515a0aca492eeee478cd9947226498&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f3d819d6498d4482286628946e37a6b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-177e9aca0bf1c1724474ea529826bece&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9ec9cae555a06ac660e6c16d90116c8b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5e1196548781bdac364853fdfd2074ec&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a764dcbdd73fd1c50fa72a7cd60b6e19&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-71de01baf40871c616eaa39cb8189f43&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3895d65c9a22c257a4717f300d4086b0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2e9f02579c179c758cc6393322299d9c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1dd74224daea51112742135154e46244&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-36ace822cd4873b8fd2adcfef0a7f9fd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b23dfd3ae95fca711f8f10fc98ab467c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c030749e7f9a2ae77cb8993d7250cffe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db5749bec4af1c3ea068b257c4376aaf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-da4119d4fc266b13dd11e47dd6f506ca</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329423</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="MiniMed Mobile App">
  <data key="d0">MiniMed Mobile App</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">MiniMed Mobile App is a smartphone‑based software application that works with Medtronic’s MiniMed insulin‑pump systems, most notably the MiniMed 780G, to extend the functionality of the pump onto a user’s mobile device. The app serves as a secondary display, showing real‑time pump data, CGM sensor graphs, and the pump’s alarms, alerts, and messages, thereby allowing users to monitor therapy without needing the pump’s built‑in screen.

In addition to displaying information, MiniMed Mobile App is required to start, restart, pair, and manage the Instinct continuous glucose monitoring (CGM) sensor. It guides users through secure pairing, sensor activation, sensor replacement, and sensor‑related error handling, and it can clear alerts and follow on‑screen instructions for sensor management. The app also enables users to receive notifications about pump status and CGM readings.

Data captured by the pump and sensor are uploaded to Medtronic’s CareLink service through the app, providing cloud‑based storage and remote access for clinicians and caregivers. The application also supports wireless firmware updates, allowing the pump’s software to be upgraded directly from the mobile device.

The app is distributed as two platform‑specific versions—MMT‑6101 for Android devices and MMT‑6102 for iOS devices—ensuring compatibility across the major mobile operating systems while maintaining the same core capabilities for pump display, sensor control, data synchronization, and software updating.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-95ba6f1fa7d1791230f690255a8ba2df&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ab510c8377992bab31045a97eb95893a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cdb000b83632c89167783ad4e6f1fb64&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4a75df3ab63706f501e8d3134e74a64b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-caf5071e54a797f595d8cac8e4653918&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-87a1bd89a18cb218431ff9359e299ee6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-177e9aca0bf1c1724474ea529826bece&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eb80f00ba2dab32852874cb384b38de3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a764dcbdd73fd1c50fa72a7cd60b6e19&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-71de01baf40871c616eaa39cb8189f43&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7827239a998e7ac7379613d9e5f81ae0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3895d65c9a22c257a4717f300d4086b0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2e9f02579c179c758cc6393322299d9c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1dd74224daea51112742135154e46244&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-36ace822cd4873b8fd2adcfef0a7f9fd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dd545bc80ceae270c16406af736789b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c030749e7f9a2ae77cb8993d7250cffe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-46d04af5292fae98e3aa651d9cec4512</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329429</data>
