</node>
<node id="MiniMed 780G Insulin Pump">
  <data key="d0">MiniMed 780G Insulin Pump</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">MiniMed 780G Insulin Pump is a medical device that provides continuous subcutaneous insulin delivery for people with diabetes. It administers both basal insulin, according to a programmed basal pattern, and bolus insulin for meals or corrections, using an infusion set that inserts into the body. Insulin dosing parameters are established by a healthcare professional, and the pump can operate in a manual “pancreas‑simulation” mode that mimics normal pancreatic function.

The pump serves as the central delivery component of the MiniMed 780G system and interfaces with compatible continuous glucose monitoring (CGM) sensors, including the Guardian 4, Instinct, and Simplera Sync sensors. Through these connections it supports advanced automation features such as SmartGuard, which autonomously adjusts insulin delivery to keep glucose within a target range, and Block Mode for safety. SmartGuard operation typically requires a daily insulin usage of 8 to 250 units. The device also offers a Suspend All Delivery command, alerts, reminders, and a user‑friendly screen layout with Home and Bolus screens, buttons, and navigation controls.

Communication with the broader system is achieved via wired or Bluetooth links to transmitters and the MiniMed Mobile App, which supplies software updates and enables data synchronization. The pump does not connect wirelessly to a separate blood‑glucose meter. Routine maintenance includes regular cleaning of the pump hardware. Throughout the user manual and procedural instructions, the MiniMed 780G Insulin Pump is repeatedly referenced as the primary insulin‑delivery platform that supports sensor integration, software upgrades, and a suite of safety and convenience features designed to facilitate automated insulin therapy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-95ba6f1fa7d1791230f690255a8ba2df&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-83bb94d08bdb958eff25f76c9a6ac18a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4a75df3ab63706f501e8d3134e74a64b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-caf5071e54a797f595d8cac8e4653918&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b03b7fdf0dd9c96dc459929ccccdccff&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a0267d2986a48c4c31790b6f183277dc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-177e9aca0bf1c1724474ea529826bece&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-691a5ee6c6fdbea7a2ef1c835f0e66ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-27b3ea1063acf8e0a407a89daea0dc32&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9ec9cae555a06ac660e6c16d90116c8b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-92417ae942a11c591feb2ee9b5fadd7e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9639df6feeacb49b96ddc51763dec77d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a01dc8dc15b92e2b0b570753b0f57632&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a764dcbdd73fd1c50fa72a7cd60b6e19&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d4d222786e6ed163a90874659266c72a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2e9f02579c179c758cc6393322299d9c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ede0f32eb8f8ea1eaab76cc0bc7648fd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1dd74224daea51112742135154e46244&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dcea1ff62aae96936f552880e96faa69&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8741750a7bf86eb5d1fadf82a9c7720e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-da4119d4fc266b13dd11e47dd6f506ca</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329434</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="MiniMed 780G System">
  <data key="d0">MiniMed 780G System</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The MiniMed 780G System is a body‑worn diabetes management platform that combines an insulin pump with continuous glucose monitoring (CGM) and associated software. The system delivers rapid‑acting U‑100 insulin in both basal rates and correction boluses, and it incorporates the Active Insulin Time setting to calculate insulin on board.  

The pump integrates Medtronic’s SmartGuard technology and Predictive Low Glucose features, which automatically suspend insulin delivery when glucose is projected to fall below a preset threshold. Users can also employ the Bolus Wizard and Manual Bolus functions to calculate and deliver mealtime or correction doses.  

The MiniMed 780G System is designed to work with a range of Medtronic sensors, including the Guardian 4, Instinct, and Simplera Sync CGM devices, communicating via radio‑frequency links. All components—pump, sensors, and accessories—are compatible with the MiniMed Mobile app, allowing remote monitoring, data review, and pump control from a smartphone.  

The platform requires compatible Medtronic Diabetes components and includes comprehensive care instructions for safe operation. Overall, the MiniMed 780G System provides an integrated insulin delivery and glucose monitoring solution that automates many aspects of diabetes therapy while supporting user‑initiated dosing and mobile connectivity.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-95ba6f1fa7d1791230f690255a8ba2df&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4a4a75301f61fc3c86ad768de09d0c3f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8cceea4f7036977c7ddcbe81f76f8aa1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-474703bb16e6e26e009e9d433c3d3647&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d68acc5f59d78c14cf4d2e4d34edf5e4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-caf5071e54a797f595d8cac8e4653918&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ae3b43add031516d14e51c6d2a985bd7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eb80f00ba2dab32852874cb384b38de3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9ec9cae555a06ac660e6c16d90116c8b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5e1196548781bdac364853fdfd2074ec&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a764dcbdd73fd1c50fa72a7cd60b6e19&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-71de01baf40871c616eaa39cb8189f43&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7827239a998e7ac7379613d9e5f81ae0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1dd74224daea51112742135154e46244&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-20af4762343b8357c2c72473211f2918&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1c5a5c97986d9b31b155b0c8f0cac1c5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c030749e7f9a2ae77cb8993d7250cffe</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329435</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Tubing Connector">
  <data key="d0">Tubing Connector</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Tubing Connector is the small junction component that links the infusion set tubing to other parts of an insulin delivery system, such as the medication reservoir, the infusion set itself, or the pump. It provides the point where insulin or other therapeutic liquids can enter the tubing, and it is typically designed to be attached by pushing the connector onto the tubing and then turning it clockwise until it locks securely in place. This push‑and‑turn mechanism ensures a tight seal and prevents accidental detachment during use.

The connector functions as the interface between the reservoir and the tubing, allowing the fluid to flow from the reservoir into the delivery line. It also serves to join the tubing to the pump or directly to the infusion set, depending on the specific configuration of the device. Because the connector forms the entry point for the medication, it is a potential site for blockage if particles or air become trapped, so proper attachment and periodic inspection are important to maintain reliable flow.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d8e2c8beb0e0581ef5724dc5c631252e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4a4a75301f61fc3c86ad768de09d0c3f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-474703bb16e6e26e009e9d433c3d3647&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fe844728a502927fee80d42268408b1a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-28515a0aca492eeee478cd9947226498&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-691a5ee6c6fdbea7a2ef1c835f0e66ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a01dc8dc15b92e2b0b570753b0f57632&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b23dfd3ae95fca711f8f10fc98ab467c</data>
