<node id="Sensor Feature">
  <data key="d0">Sensor Feature</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Sensor Feature is a system capability of insulin pumps that governs the device’s interaction with a continuous glucose monitoring (CGM) sensor. When enabled, the pump receives real‑time glucose data from a paired sensor, allowing continuous glucose monitoring (CGM) to be displayed on the Home screen and to power sensor‑specific settings such as high SG alerts, sensor‑glucose (SG) configuration, and optional sensor alerts.  

The feature can be turned on or off in the Device Settings menu. Activating it automatically connects the pump to any sensor that is paired, while deactivating it disables the flow of sensor data and halts CGM‑related functions. Because the pump must be set to receive sensor data in order to configure SG alerts, high‑alert thresholds, and other sensor‑related parameters, the Sensor Feature must be enabled for any CGM‑based monitoring or alerts to operate.  

Conversely, the Sensor Feature may be deliberately disabled when a user does not wish to use continuous glucose monitoring, effectively turning off CGM integration while still allowing the pump to function for insulin delivery alone. This optional setting provides flexibility for users who prefer intermittent glucose checks or who are not using a compatible CGM sensor.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d8e2c8beb0e0581ef5724dc5c631252e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-653c72495ca2211399f4a6660e1905e2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8cceea4f7036977c7ddcbe81f76f8aa1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bf54a88e051fe74fd94b773f8b5d98da&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4faffc449b4b8ea09acbae135d21baa6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5e1196548781bdac364853fdfd2074ec&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fd751b869edcd6c88d9e467cfb2cb0fd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ede0f32eb8f8ea1eaab76cc0bc7648fd</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329455</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Alert On Low">
  <data key="d0">Alert On Low</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Alert On Low is an alert automatically enabled when either suspend feature is active and signals when SG reaches the low limit.&lt;SEP&gt;An alert that notifies the user when sensor glucose reaches the low limit.&lt;SEP&gt;Alert On Low is an alert displayed by the pump when sensor glucose reaches or falls below the low limit, automatically activated by low‑glucose suspend features.&lt;SEP&gt;An alert indicating that sensor glucose is at or below the specified low limit.&lt;SEP&gt;Alert on low is an alert that occurs when the sensor glucose reading reaches or falls below the low limit.&lt;SEP&gt;Alert on low is a notification that triggers when the glucose level meets or falls below the low threshold.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-653c72495ca2211399f4a6660e1905e2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6b53b69acbef0e172ea7719cc15bf3ad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7ceebe6fbf743053d7b55523365689e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fd8af150d14c8fd9fd3b20e486220f65&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d3b794ead59ea83de139af0358a0e7b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1c5a5c97986d9b31b155b0c8f0cac1c5</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329456</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Alert Before Low">
  <data key="d0">Alert Before Low</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Alert Before Low is an optional alert that warns approximately 30 minutes before SG is predicted to reach the low limit.&lt;SEP&gt;An alert that notifies the user before sensor glucose falls below the low limit.&lt;SEP&gt;Alert Before Low is an alert that notifies the user before the low glucose limit is reached.&lt;SEP&gt;Alert before low is an alert that occurs when the low sensor glucose reading is being approached.&lt;SEP&gt;Alert before low is a notification issued shortly before the glucose level drops to the low threshold.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-653c72495ca2211399f4a6660e1905e2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7ceebe6fbf743053d7b55523365689e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fd8af150d14c8fd9fd3b20e486220f65&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d3b794ead59ea83de139af0358a0e7b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1c5a5c97986d9b31b155b0c8f0cac1c5</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329456</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Resume Basal Alert">
  <data key="d0">Resume Basal Alert</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Resume Basal Alert indicates when basal insulin delivery has resumed automatically and can be turned off while a resume message still appears.&lt;SEP&gt;Resume Basal Alert is an alert that can be activated when either suspend feature is on, indicating that basal insulin delivery may be resumed.&lt;SEP&gt;Resume Basal Alert is an alert that occurs when the insulin pump automatically resumes basal insulin delivery after a Suspend before low or Suspend on low event.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-653c72495ca2211399f4a6660e1905e2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b6025fa711665988fad0f789b9eb901a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d3b794ead59ea83de139af0358a0e7b3</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329457</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="User Guide">
  <data key="d0">User Guide</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">User Guide is the official instructional documentation provided with the MiniMed 780G insulin‑pump system, its associated sensors, and meter, serving as the primary reference for safe and effective device use.  

The guide contains the most up‑to‑date warnings, risk information, and safety instructions required for operating the pump and its components. It also lists relevant support phone numbers, ensuring users can obtain immediate assistance when needed.  

Detailed operating procedures are presented throughout the manual, including step‑by‑step directions for setting up the device, selecting and changing infusion sets, and utilizing the pump’s full range of features. The guide explains how to configure basal and bolus delivery, calibrate sensors, and interpret meter readings, thereby covering the complete workflow for diabetes management with the MiniMed 780G system.  

In addition to routine operations, the User Guide provides comprehensive troubleshooting content. It outlines how to recognize and respond to pump errors, alarms, and alerts, offering recommended corrective actions and procedural checks to resolve common issues. The reference material also includes detailed troubleshooting steps for more complex problems, helping users restore normal device function and maintain therapy continuity.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d8e2c8beb0e0581ef5724dc5c631252e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6a9714e3b2aaad60242e3827215230bc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-df77f2ea988e5724effb4c71cc79a65a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bcdc240f555b6c71532ea6d04e0c5798&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9ec9cae555a06ac660e6c16d90116c8b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9bfe428f5a1381000cf6932b37aa2239&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d3b794ead59ea83de139af0358a0e7b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-71de01baf40871c616eaa39cb8189f43&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f94cd06ab0d1bcc7a9349bc40ea3eb22&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db5749bec4af1c3ea068b257c4376aaf</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329457</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Manual Mode">
  <data key="d0">Manual Mode</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Manual Mode is an operating state of the MiniMed™ 780G insulin pump in which all automated, sensor‑glucose‑based insulin delivery functions are disabled. In this mode the Predictive Low Glucose technology, SmartGuard automatic adjustments, Auto Basal, and any other automatic insulin‑delivery features are turned off, and the pump relies exclusively on user‑directed inputs rather than continuous glucose (CGM) values for treatment decisions. The sensor feature may be off, yet CGM data can still be viewed on the Home Screen if a sensor is present.  

In Manual Mode the user must manually enter all relevant diabetes‑management data. Bolus doses are calculated with the Bolus Wizard, which requires the user to input carbohydrate intake and a blood‑glucose meter reading before delivery. Users can also manually select bolus types and settings, and the Bolus Wizard screen as well as other summary screens are available for review. This mode can be used with a CGM attached or without one, giving flexibility in how glucose information is obtained.  

Basal insulin delivery in Manual Mode follows the pre‑programmed basal patterns and respects the Max Basal Rate setting. Users set basal rates and limits directly, and the automatic basal algorithm is inactive. The Max Basal setting remains applicable, and users have full control over basal parameters without interference from automated adjustments.  

Overall, Manual Mode provides a fully user‑controlled environment for insulin therapy on the MiniMed 780G pump, allowing direct entry of bolus, carbohydrate, and glucose data, manual selection of delivery settings, and visibility of CGM information while disabling all smart, sensor‑driven automation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d8e2c8beb0e0581ef5724dc5c631252e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4a4a75301f61fc3c86ad768de09d0c3f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8cceea4f7036977c7ddcbe81f76f8aa1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-83bb94d08bdb958eff25f76c9a6ac18a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db8e2f5011e0e0fe7dc11273e2f345b9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b03b7fdf0dd9c96dc459929ccccdccff&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a0267d2986a48c4c31790b6f183277dc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4faffc449b4b8ea09acbae135d21baa6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b48243f8e773d3c94abc58e2314db2c0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b6025fa711665988fad0f789b9eb901a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ae3b43add031516d14e51c6d2a985bd7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-27b3ea1063acf8e0a407a89daea0dc32&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9ec9cae555a06ac660e6c16d90116c8b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9639df6feeacb49b96ddc51763dec77d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-542e3b31a3f3a9496f26d05d1255498a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a764dcbdd73fd1c50fa72a7cd60b6e19&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-97eb00dc26d33c23bf8bf473c0a98472&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7b2af59ac9cf813cb07dac53f30250d0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ede0f32eb8f8ea1eaab76cc0bc7648fd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4b8de1434b9d9f57cd225b5d3e0d7f3b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-36ace822cd4873b8fd2adcfef0a7f9fd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b907eb92deb747df3fb3b37fb9974142&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-20af4762343b8357c2c72473211f2918&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8741750a7bf86eb5d1fadf82a9c7720e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-59d8fcf807f0beb090b2f3d68cc7c168&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db5749bec4af1c3ea068b257c4376aaf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-da4119d4fc266b13dd11e47dd6f506ca</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329458</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Low SG Settings">
  <data key="d0">Low SG Settings</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Low SG settings are programmable parameters that adjust insulin delivery when sensor glucose readings are low.&lt;SEP&gt;Settings that alert or suspend insulin delivery when sensor glucose approaches or reaches a low limit, including various alert types.&lt;SEP&gt;Low SG Settings are configurable parameters that define low glucose limits and time segments for the pump’s low‑glucose features.&lt;SEP&gt;Low SG Settings are the parameters on the pump that define the low glucose threshold and related alert options.&lt;SEP&gt;Low SG Settings is the configuration page that controls low glucose limit behavior.&lt;SEP&gt;Configuration options for low glucose alerts.&lt;SEP&gt;Low SG Settings is a concept configuring alerts for low sensor glucose.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-653c72495ca2211399f4a6660e1905e2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db8e2f5011e0e0fe7dc11273e2f345b9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b48243f8e773d3c94abc58e2314db2c0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7ceebe6fbf743053d7b55523365689e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a111edb31d6739acf013ce812b952366&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fd751b869edcd6c88d9e467cfb2cb0fd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7b2af59ac9cf813cb07dac53f30250d0</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329458</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Low Setup Screen">
  <data key="d0">Low Setup Screen</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Low Setup Screen is the pump interface where the user selects time segments, end times and low glucose limits.&lt;SEP&gt;Low Setup Screen is the interface that appears after selecting Low Alert in the Alert Settings menu.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-653c72495ca2211399f4a6660e1905e2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fd751b869edcd6c88d9e467cfb2cb0fd</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329458</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Emergency Message">
  <data key="d0">Emergency Message</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Emergency Message is a text displayed by the pump when an alert is not cleared after a low‑glucose suspension.&lt;SEP&gt;Emergency Message is the message displayed if a suspend alarm is not cleared within two hours.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-653c72495ca2211399f4a6660e1905e2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d3b794ead59ea83de139af0358a0e7b3</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329458</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Sleep Mode">
  <data key="d0">Sleep Mode</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Sleep Mode is a low‑power, low‑activity state of an insulin pump that is designed to conserve battery life while keeping the device fully functional. The pump enters Sleep Mode automatically after a period of inactivity—typically around two minutes—or it can be manually activated when the user presses and holds a button. In this state the screen darkens or goes completely blank, and the pump becomes locked, but insulin delivery continues unchanged and features such as the Easy Bolus remain operational.

The device can be awakened from Sleep Mode simply by pressing a button, at which point the Home screen is displayed and normal interaction resumes. Although the screen is dark, the pump remains responsive to bolus entry and other essential functions, ensuring that therapeutic performance is not compromised while power consumption is reduced.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d8e2c8beb0e0581ef5724dc5c631252e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-83bb94d08bdb958eff25f76c9a6ac18a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db8e2f5011e0e0fe7dc11273e2f345b9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4faffc449b4b8ea09acbae135d21baa6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b6025fa711665988fad0f789b9eb901a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-542e3b31a3f3a9496f26d05d1255498a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a074860e7f25b8dfbcccbabb53c645d7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b23dfd3ae95fca711f8f10fc98ab467c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e8e9d04ca4b641b5d8d5ef85044f4566</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329459</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Time Segment">
  <data key="d0">Time Segment</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A defined portion of the 24‑hour day for which specific high or low SG alert settings can be programmed.&lt;SEP&gt;Time Segment is a defined portion of the 24‑hour day (up to eight) for which a specific low limit can be set.&lt;SEP&gt;Time segment is a portion of the 24‑hour period used to assign individual high limits for high SG alerts.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-653c72495ca2211399f4a6660e1905e2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7ceebe6fbf743053d7b55523365689e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5e1196548781bdac364853fdfd2074ec</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329460</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Alert Settings">
  <data key="d0">Alert Settings</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">The menu area where users configure high, low, rise, and snooze alerts on the pump.&lt;SEP&gt;Alert Settings is the menu interface where users select High Alert configurations for high SG settings.&lt;SEP&gt;Alert Settings is the menu section where users configure alerts such as Low Alert, Alert Before Low, and Alert On Low.&lt;SEP&gt;Alert Settings is the menu where users configure low alerts, snooze options, and other alarm preferences.&lt;SEP&gt;Alert Settings is the menu system used to configure all reminder types.&lt;SEP&gt;The menu where users configure alert thresholds, snooze options, and reminders.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-653c72495ca2211399f4a6660e1905e2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bcdc240f555b6c71532ea6d04e0c5798&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7ceebe6fbf743053d7b55523365689e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5e1196548781bdac364853fdfd2074ec&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fd751b869edcd6c88d9e467cfb2cb0fd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dcea1ff62aae96936f552880e96faa69</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329461</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Low Alert">
  <data key="d0">Low Alert</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Low Alert is the specific alert option within Alert Settings that notifies when glucose reaches the low limit.&lt;SEP&gt;Low Alert is a configurable alarm that notifies the user when sensor glucose falls below the preset low SG value.&lt;SEP&gt;A type of alert indicating a glucose value below the configured low limit.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-653c72495ca2211399f4a6660e1905e2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bcdc240f555b6c71532ea6d04e0c5798&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fd751b869edcd6c88d9e467cfb2cb0fd</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329461</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Suspend by Sensor Icon">
  <data key="d0">Suspend by Sensor Icon</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Suspend by Sensor Icon is the pump icon displayed on the Home Screen (with a red X) indicating that a low‑glucose suspend feature is unavailable.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-653c72495ca2211399f4a6660e1905e2</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329462</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Suspend Before Low">
  <data key="d0">Suspend Before Low</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Suspend Before Low is an insulin‑pump feature that automatically suspends or pauses insulin delivery when the continuous glucose monitor predicts that sensor‑measured glucose is approaching or about to fall below a user‑set low‑glucose threshold. The function not only stops insulin infusion but also generates an alert to inform the user that delivery has been halted because the glucose level is nearing the low limit. Suspend Before Low operates on predicted values rather than waiting for the glucose reading to actually drop below the threshold, providing a proactive safety margin. The feature may become unavailable for a short period after a low‑glucose event, and it cannot be active at the same time as the separate “Suspend on Low” setting, which triggers suspension only after the low limit has been reached. Overall, Suspend Before Low serves to reduce the risk of hypoglycemia by temporarily halting insulin when the sensor indicates an imminent low glucose condition.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-653c72495ca2211399f4a6660e1905e2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-83bb94d08bdb958eff25f76c9a6ac18a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-caf5071e54a797f595d8cac8e4653918&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6b53b69acbef0e172ea7719cc15bf3ad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b6025fa711665988fad0f789b9eb901a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7ceebe6fbf743053d7b55523365689e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fd751b869edcd6c88d9e467cfb2cb0fd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b23dfd3ae95fca711f8f10fc98ab467c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-46d04af5292fae98e3aa651d9cec4512&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-da4119d4fc266b13dd11e47dd6f506ca</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329462</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Suspend On Low">
  <data key="d0">Suspend On Low</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Suspend On Low is a pump feature that automatically halts insulin delivery when the sensor‑measured glucose level reaches or falls below a predefined low threshold. The function stops insulin flow as soon as the glucose reading meets the low limit, and it may also generate an alert to notify the user that delivery has been suspended due to low glucose.  

Once a low event occurs, Suspend On Low can become unavailable for a short period, preventing immediate re‑activation, and it cannot be active at the same time as the “Suspend before low” feature. The feature’s primary purpose is to protect users from hypoglycemia by pausing insulin when sensor glucose is at or below the low limit.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-653c72495ca2211399f4a6660e1905e2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-83bb94d08bdb958eff25f76c9a6ac18a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-caf5071e54a797f595d8cac8e4653918&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6b53b69acbef0e172ea7719cc15bf3ad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b6025fa711665988fad0f789b9eb901a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7ceebe6fbf743053d7b55523365689e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fd751b869edcd6c88d9e467cfb2cb0fd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b23dfd3ae95fca711f8f10fc98ab467c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-46d04af5292fae98e3aa651d9cec4512&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-da4119d4fc266b13dd11e47dd6f506ca</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329465</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Sensor Pairing">
  <data key="d0">Sensor Pairing</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Sensor Pairing is the procedure of linking a CGM sensor to the insulin pump, establishing a wireless connection via the MiniMed Mobile App.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ab510c8377992bab31045a97eb95893a</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329468</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Sensor Unpairing">
  <data key="d0">Sensor Unpairing</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Sensor Unpairing is the procedure of disconnecting a CGM sensor from the insulin pump, automatically performed when a new sensor is started.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ab510c8377992bab31045a97eb95893a</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329469</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Paired Devices Screen">
  <data key="d0">Paired Devices Screen</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Paired Devices Screen is a pump interface that lists currently paired CGM devices.&lt;SEP&gt;Paired Devices Screen shows information about devices linked to the pump, including sensor serial numbers.&lt;SEP&gt;Screen showing devices that are linked to the pump.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ab510c8377992bab31045a97eb95893a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db8e2f5011e0e0fe7dc11273e2f345b9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b48243f8e773d3c94abc58e2314db2c0</data>
