  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Pairing Successful! Message appears on the pump when a CGM sensor has been successfully paired.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ab510c8377992bab31045a97eb95893a</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329471</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Sensor Warm Up Message">
  <data key="d0">Sensor Warm Up Message</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Sensor Warm Up Message displays the remaining warm‑up time (e.g., “Sensor warm up 1:30 hr”) on the Home screen after sensor insertion.&lt;SEP&gt;Sensor Warm Up Message displays the remaining warm‑up time (e.g., X:XX hr) after starting a new sensor.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ab510c8377992bab31045a97eb95893a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c030749e7f9a2ae77cb8993d7250cffe</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329472</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="No Paired CGM Banner">
  <data key="d0">No Paired CGM Banner</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">The No Paired CGM banner appears on the Home screen when the sensor is not paired with the pump.&lt;SEP&gt;No Paired CGM Banner is a banner on the Home screen indicating that no CGM sensor is currently paired with the pump.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ab510c8377992bab31045a97eb95893a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c030749e7f9a2ae77cb8993d7250cffe</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329472</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Health Care Professional">
  <data key="d0">Health Care Professional</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Health Care Professional is a medical practitioner who advises users on discarding used sensors.&lt;SEP&gt;Health care professionals are medical practitioners who interpret blood glucose data with patients.&lt;SEP&gt;Medical practitioners who can provide input and education for insulin dosing and device selection.&lt;SEP&gt;Health Care Professional denotes clinicians who interpret glucose data and guide diabetes treatment.&lt;SEP&gt;Health Care Professional is the clinician who works with individuals to adjust glycemic targets and treatment plans.&lt;SEP&gt;A clinician responsible for recognizing the complexity of diabetes classification and avoiding misdiagnosis.&lt;SEP&gt;Health care professional is the practitioner who should discuss signs and symptoms with patients and repeat tests.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ab510c8377992bab31045a97eb95893a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c9bc5d11c9f848439320623cad3d3a38&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c93787ffd2c022283fc0663decb1a184&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b275f50028ef32e322bf8643e0342810&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a19f43c10a7a756e1597ff1a7f53296e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6601fea85bfbb9f20040c70b7e21695d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ba38023866c2db7437e618a60033f21f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/blood glucose monitoring.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Metas glicêmicas/metas cuidado do diabetes.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377323</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Electronic Equipment">
  <data key="d0">Electronic Equipment</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Electronic Equipment refers to electronic devices, including CGM sensors, that must be disposed of according to local regulations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ab510c8377992bab31045a97eb95893a</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329473</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Sharps">
  <data key="d0">Sharps</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Sharps are needle‑like components that may be present in sensor kits and are subject to regulated disposal.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ab510c8377992bab31045a97eb95893a</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329473</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Body Fluids">
  <data key="d0">Body Fluids</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Body Fluids are bodily substances that can contaminate sensor components and are considered in disposal regulations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ab510c8377992bab31045a97eb95893a</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
