<node id="Blood Glucose Meter Reading">
  <data key="d0">Blood Glucose Meter Reading</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Blood glucose (BG) meter readings are manual glucose measurements that can be used for calibration or verification.&lt;SEP&gt;Blood Glucose Meter Reading is a numeric glucose value entered from a blood glucose meter, used for sensor calibration or system checks.&lt;SEP&gt;Blood glucose (BG) meter reading is a measurement of glucose concentration in the blood used for calibration and verification.&lt;SEP&gt;Blood Glucose Meter Reading is a data value entered from the meter to calculate a correction bolus or to fulfill missing glucose information.&lt;SEP&gt;Blood Glucose (BG) meter reading provides the glucose value required when setting up a bolus in Manual mode.&lt;SEP&gt;Blood Glucose Meter Reading is the numeric glucose value entered from the BG meter to calculate a correction bolus.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-05241912c4f8f5e79ae75071a1c7c604&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5e1196548781bdac364853fdfd2074ec&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9639df6feeacb49b96ddc51763dec77d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-542e3b31a3f3a9496f26d05d1255498a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-36ace822cd4873b8fd2adcfef0a7f9fd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b907eb92deb747df3fb3b37fb9974142</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329480</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Sensor Glucose Value">
  <data key="d0">Sensor Glucose Value</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">A sensor glucose (SG) value is a continuous glucose reading provided by CGM sensors, used by the pump for automated dosing when SmartGuard is active.&lt;SEP&gt;Sensor Glucose Value is a glucose measurement obtained directly from the sensor, not to be entered as a blood glucose meter reading.&lt;SEP&gt;Sensor Glucose Value is a glucose measurement from a continuous sensor that should not replace a BG meter reading.&lt;SEP&gt;Sensor Glucose Value is a data value provided by the continuous glucose sensor, displayed on the Home and Bolus screens.&lt;SEP&gt;Sensor Glucose (SG) value is not used for bolus delivery in Manual mode.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-05241912c4f8f5e79ae75071a1c7c604&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9639df6feeacb49b96ddc51763dec77d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-97eb00dc26d33c23bf8bf473c0a98472&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b907eb92deb747df3fb3b37fb9974142&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db5749bec4af1c3ea068b257c4376aaf</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329480</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="CGM Device">
  <data key="d0">CGM Device</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">CGM Device is a continuous glucose monitoring (CGM) system that pairs with an insulin pump—most commonly the MiniMed 780G—to exchange sensor glucose data. The device consists of a glucose‑sensing sensor, a low‑power transmitter, and associated software; each unit is identified by a unique serial number and may include specific models such as the Guardian 4 sensor. By linking to the pump, the CGM Device supplies real‑time sensor glucose values that the pump can use for automated insulin delivery and therapeutic decisions.  

In addition to providing continuous glucose readings, the CGM Device generates alerts, alarms, and messages when glucose levels cross pre‑programmed thresholds, helping the user and caregivers respond promptly to hypo‑ or hyperglycemic events. The system records sensor glucose values, transmits them wirelessly to the pump, and supports the pump’s alerting functions and sensor‑related operations.  

For safety, the CGM Device must be removed before the patient undergoes any magnetic‑resonance imaging (MRI), X‑ray, computed tomography (CT), or diathermy procedures, as these environments can interfere with the device’s electronics and sensor functionality.  

Overall, the term “CGM Device” encompasses any continuous glucose monitoring hardware capable of pairing with the insulin pump, providing accurate glucose sensing, data transmission, and safety‑related notifications to support integrated diabetes management.&lt;SEP&gt;Continuous glucose monitoring device used for patient monitoring in hospitals.&lt;SEP&gt;The CGM device is the wearable sensor system that records interstitial glucose continuously.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ab510c8377992bab31045a97eb95893a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cdb000b83632c89167783ad4e6f1fb64&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-379a204614747df98c1296e2f76c264f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bf54a88e051fe74fd94b773f8b5d98da&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-87a1bd89a18cb218431ff9359e299ee6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b48243f8e773d3c94abc58e2314db2c0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6b53b69acbef0e172ea7719cc15bf3ad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-177e9aca0bf1c1724474ea529826bece&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eb80f00ba2dab32852874cb384b38de3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3d0824c9d8a9ff5f2da52b7b5ea69c86&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8a0307c83d7b514ca00334e4c8ca2357&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dd545bc80ceae270c16406af736789b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e8e9d04ca4b641b5d8d5ef85044f4566&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-59d8fcf807f0beb090b2f3d68cc7c168&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c030749e7f9a2ae77cb8993d7250cffe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-46d04af5292fae98e3aa651d9cec4512&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6fe769b03fc66d4a691f3b7f741b92cb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a19f43c10a7a756e1597ff1a7f53296e</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/blood glucose monitoring.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Metas glicêmicas/metas cuidado do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786372165</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Carb Amount">
  <data key="d0">Carb Amount</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Carb Amount is a data input representing the grams of carbohydrates for which a food bolus is calculated.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-05241912c4f8f5e79ae75071a1c7c604</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329482</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Temporary Target">
  <data key="d0">Temporary Target</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A temporary target is a programmable glucose set‑point used for up to eight hours when certain interfering substances are present.&lt;SEP&gt;Temporary Target is a configurable glucose setpoint (e.g., 150 mg/dL) used for a limited period such as exercise, reducing insulin needs.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-05241912c4f8f5e79ae75071a1c7c604&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db5749bec4af1c3ea068b257c4376aaf</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329483</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Bolus Screen">
  <data key="d0">Bolus Screen</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The Bolus screen allows users to deliver bolus insulin; its layout varies with the active bolus feature.&lt;SEP&gt;Bolus Screen is the interface where the user initiates normal or wave bolus deliveries.&lt;SEP&gt;Bolus Screen is the interface that shows glucose reading information and allows entry of carb or BG data for bolus calculation.&lt;SEP&gt;A screen displayed during bolus delivery that shows amount delivered and allows stopping the bolus.&lt;SEP&gt;The Bolus Screen is the pump interface used to deliver bolus insulin and displays related alerts.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-05241912c4f8f5e79ae75071a1c7c604&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4faffc449b4b8ea09acbae135d21baa6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a01dc8dc15b92e2b0b570753b0f57632&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-97eb00dc26d33c23bf8bf473c0a98472&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f94cd06ab0d1bcc7a9349bc40ea3eb22</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329484</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Auto Correction Feature">
  <data key="d0">Auto Correction Feature</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Auto Correction Feature is a sub‑feature of SmartGuard that automatically delivers correction boluses when glucose is high.&lt;SEP&gt;Auto Correction Feature is a component that automatically adjusts insulin but is disabled while a temporary target is active.&lt;SEP&gt;An automated function that adjusts insulin delivery based on glucose readings.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-05241912c4f8f5e79ae75071a1c7c604&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b48243f8e773d3c94abc58e2314db2c0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f677e56841fc57bffd8bf5b6cc4a7797</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329484</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="SmartGuard Min Delivery Alert">
  <data key="d0">SmartGuard Min Delivery Alert</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">SmartGuard Min Delivery Alert is a notification shown when the minimum delivery time limit is reached, prompting a BG entry.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-05241912c4f8f5e79ae75071a1c7c604</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329487</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="SmartGuard Max Delivery Alert">
  <data key="d0">SmartGuard Max Delivery Alert</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">SmartGuard Max Delivery Alert is a notification shown after basal insulin has been delivered at maximum limit for 7 hours, advising a BG entry and checklist review.&lt;SEP&gt;An on‑screen alert that appears when the SmartGuard Feature reaches its maximum insulin delivery limit.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-05241912c4f8f5e79ae75071a1c7c604&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d4d222786e6ed163a90874659266c72a</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329488</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Enter BG Now Alert">
  <data key="d0">Enter BG Now Alert</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Enter BG Now Alert is a system prompt that appears when the pump requires the user to input a blood glucose meter reading.&lt;SEP&gt;Enter BG Now Alert is a notification displayed when sensor glucose values may be inaccurate, requesting an immediate BG reading.&lt;SEP&gt;An alert that prompts the user to enter a blood glucose reading immediately.&lt;SEP&gt;Enter BG now alert notifies the user to input a BG reading within a time window.&lt;SEP&gt;Alert prompting the user to enter a blood glucose reading because SmartGuard has been at maximum or minimum delivery rate for several hours.&lt;SEP&gt;Enter BG Now Alert is an alarm urging immediate glucose entry.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-05241912c4f8f5e79ae75071a1c7c604&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3d0824c9d8a9ff5f2da52b7b5ea69c86&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a111edb31d6739acf013ce812b952366&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d4d222786e6ed163a90874659266c72a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8a0307c83d7b514ca00334e4c8ca2357&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8741750a7bf86eb5d1fadf82a9c7720e</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329489</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Exit In Message">
  <data key="d0">Exit In Message</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Exit In Message is a brief screen message indicating the remaining time before the pump exits SmartGuard and switches to Manual mode.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-05241912c4f8f5e79ae75071a1c7c604</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329489</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Temp Target Started Message">
  <data key="d0">Temp Target Started Message</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Temp Target Started Message is a banner shown on the Home screen confirming that a temporary target has begun and displaying its remaining duration.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-05241912c4f8f5e79ae75071a1c7c604</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329490</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hyperglycemic Event">
  <data key="d0">Hyperglycemic Event</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Hyperglycemic Event is a severe condition characterized by excessively high blood glucose levels, mentioned as requiring a BG meter reading.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-05241912c4f8f5e79ae75071a1c7c604</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329490</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="SG Readings">
  <data key="d0">SG Readings</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">SG readings are sensor‑derived glucose values used by the pump for insulin calculations.&lt;SEP&gt;Sensor glucose (SG) readings generated by CGMs and used by SmartGuard for insulin dosing calculations.&lt;SEP&gt;SG readings are glucose sensor readings received by the pump after the sensor warm‑up period.&lt;SEP&gt;Sensor glucose (SG) readings are continuous glucose values supplied by the sensor to the pump.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4a4a75301f61fc3c86ad768de09d0c3f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-177e9aca0bf1c1724474ea529826bece&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9ec9cae555a06ac660e6c16d90116c8b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d4d222786e6ed163a90874659266c72a</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329496</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="BG Meter">
  <data key="d0">BG Meter</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">A blood‑glucose meter provides reference glucose measurements that must be used to verify SG readings in certain situations.&lt;SEP&gt;BG Meter is a blood glucose meter used to obtain BG readings for correction boluses.&lt;SEP&gt;BG meter is a blood glucose meter whose readings are used to calibrate the CGM sensor and verify system performance.&lt;SEP&gt;The device used to obtain blood glucose readings entered into the insulin pump.&lt;SEP&gt;BG meter is a device that measures blood glucose levels in the blood.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4a4a75301f61fc3c86ad768de09d0c3f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-542e3b31a3f3a9496f26d05d1255498a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4b8de1434b9d9f57cd225b5d3e0d7f3b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8a0307c83d7b514ca00334e4c8ca2357&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1c5a5c97986d9b31b155b0c8f0cac1c5</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329497</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Low SG Alarm">
  <data key="d0">Low SG Alarm</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Low SG alarm is an alert that activates when SG values fall at or below a programmed threshold.&lt;SEP&gt;An alarm displayed on the pump indicating that sensor glucose has fallen below the preset low value.&lt;SEP&gt;Low SG alarm notifies when sensor glucose falls below the preset low SG value.&lt;SEP&gt;Low SG Alarm is an alarm that occurs when SG falls below a defined threshold (e.g., 64 mg/dL).&lt;SEP&gt;Low SG Alarm is a factory‑set alarm that activates when sensor glucose falls below the low threshold (e.g., 64 mg/dL) and cannot be silenced.&lt;SEP&gt;Alarm that triggers when sensor glucose falls below 55 mg/dL, updated after a new sensor type is paired.&lt;SEP&gt;An alert triggered by low sensor glucose.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4a4a75301f61fc3c86ad768de09d0c3f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db8e2f5011e0e0fe7dc11273e2f345b9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3d0824c9d8a9ff5f2da52b7b5ea69c86&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7ceebe6fbf743053d7b55523365689e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fd751b869edcd6c88d9e467cfb2cb0fd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dd545bc80ceae270c16406af736789b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-59d8fcf807f0beb090b2f3d68cc7c168</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329498</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Alert on Low">
  <data key="d0">Alert on Low</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Alert on Low is a configurable pump warning that notifies the user of low SG values.&lt;SEP&gt;Alert on low is a specific sensor alert that notifies when glucose reaches the low threshold.&lt;SEP&gt;Alert on Low is an alert type that notifies the user of a low sensor glucose reading.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4a4a75301f61fc3c86ad768de09d0c3f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fd751b869edcd6c88d9e467cfb2cb0fd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-59d8fcf807f0beb090b2f3d68cc7c168</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329498</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Alert before Low">
  <data key="d0">Alert before Low</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Alert before Low notifies the user shortly before SG values cross the low‑threshold level.&lt;SEP&gt;Alert before low is a sensor alert that warns before glucose falls below the low threshold.&lt;SEP&gt;Alert before Low is an alert type that warns the user before sensor glucose reaches the low threshold.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4a4a75301f61fc3c86ad768de09d0c3f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fd751b869edcd6c88d9e467cfb2cb0fd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-59d8fcf807f0beb090b2f3d68cc7c168</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329499</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Rapid-Acting U-100 Insulin">
  <data key="d0">Rapid-Acting U-100 Insulin</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Rapid‑acting U‑100 insulin is the medication prescribed for use with the infusion pump.&lt;SEP&gt;A vial of rapid-acting U-100 insulin intended for use with the insulin pump.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4a4a75301f61fc3c86ad768de09d0c3f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-691a5ee6c6fdbea7a2ef1c835f0e66ae</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329500</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Luer Sets">
  <data key="d0">Luer Sets</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Luer sets are incompatible connectors that must not be used with the MiniMed 780G system.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4a4a75301f61fc3c86ad768de09d0c3f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329501</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Medtronic Reservoir">
  <data key="d0">Medtronic Reservoir</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Medtronic reservoirs are consumable cartridges designed specifically for the MiniMed™ 780G system.&lt;SEP&gt;Medtronic reservoirs are approved insulin containers for the MiniMed 780G system.&lt;SEP&gt;A reservoir compatible with Medtronic pumps, mentioned as an alternative component.&lt;SEP&gt;Medtronic Reservoir is a compatible insulin reservoir alternative for the MiniMed 780G insulin pump.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4a4a75301f61fc3c86ad768de09d0c3f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a0267d2986a48c4c31790b6f183277dc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-691a5ee6c6fdbea7a2ef1c835f0e66ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-36ace822cd4873b8fd2adcfef0a7f9fd</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329501</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Guardian 4 Transmitter">
  <data key="d0">Guardian 4 Transmitter</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The Guardian 4 transmitter is an interoperable device that works with the Simplera Sync sensor and other CGMs for data transmission.&lt;SEP&gt;The Guardian 4 transmitter pairs with the Guardian™ 4 sensor for data communication with the pump.&lt;SEP&gt;The Guardian 4 transmitter (model MMT-7841) works with Guardian 4 sensors and is compatible with SmartGuard and Predictive Low Glucose technologies.&lt;SEP&gt;The Guardian 4 transmitter communicates sensor data to the pump via Bluetooth.&lt;SEP&gt;The Guardian 4 transmitter communicates glucose data from the Guardian 4 sensor to the insulin pump via a wireless connection.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4a4a75301f61fc3c86ad768de09d0c3f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-caf5071e54a797f595d8cac8e4653918&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9ec9cae555a06ac660e6c16d90116c8b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a764dcbdd73fd1c50fa72a7cd60b6e19&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-36ace822cd4873b8fd2adcfef0a7f9fd</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329502</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Bluetooth Wireless Technology">
  <data key="d0">Bluetooth Wireless Technology</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Bluetooth wireless technology is the communication method employed by the MiniMed 780G system.&lt;SEP&gt;Bluetooth is the wireless protocol used by the Guardian 4 transmitter to link with the pump.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4a4a75301f61fc3c86ad768de09d0c3f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3895d65c9a22c257a4717f300d4086b0</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329502</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cell Phone">
  <data key="d0">Cell Phone</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">A cell phone is a mobile communication device that can emit RF signals near the pump.&lt;SEP&gt;A mobile device used to view sensor data.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4a4a75301f61fc3c86ad768de09d0c3f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5c804699375feba4c866cc3a1bc00211</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/Documento sem título.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1786336919</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="GPS Navigation System">
  <data key="d0">GPS Navigation System</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">GPS navigation systems are electronic devices that may generate RF interference.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4a4a75301f61fc3c86ad768de09d0c3f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329503</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Anti-Theft System">
  <data key="d0">Anti-Theft System</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
