  <data key="d5">1786329505</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="SmartGuard Checklist">
  <data key="d0">SmartGuard Checklist</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">SmartGuard Checklist is a screen‑based list that presents the items and requirements associated with the SmartGuard feature on the pump interface. It serves as a reference document displayed to users when SmartGuard cannot be activated, when a maximum‑delivery alert occurs, or whenever the system needs verification of the feature’s configuration and operation.  

The checklist guides users through the specific steps required to start, continue, pause, or resume SmartGuard, ensuring that all safety and operational conditions are met. It is also consulted when exiting the SmartGuard feature, providing a final verification of required actions before the system is left.  

In practice, the SmartGuard Checklist functions as a safety verification tool, presenting a documented sequence of checks that must be completed to maintain compliance with the feature’s protocols and to support safe, reliable pump performance.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-05241912c4f8f5e79ae75071a1c7c604&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4a75df3ab63706f501e8d3134e74a64b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bf54a88e051fe74fd94b773f8b5d98da&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bcdc240f555b6c71532ea6d04e0c5798&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b48243f8e773d3c94abc58e2314db2c0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d4d222786e6ed163a90874659266c72a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4b8de1434b9d9f57cd225b5d3e0d7f3b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b23dfd3ae95fca711f8f10fc98ab467c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1c5a5c97986d9b31b155b0c8f0cac1c5</data>
