<node id="Acetaminophen">
  <data key="d0">Acetaminophen</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Acetaminophen is a medication that can falsely raise sensor glucose readings, leading to potential insulin over‑delivery.&lt;SEP&gt;A medication that can falsely raise sensor glucose readings, potentially leading to insulin over‑delivery during CGM.&lt;SEP&gt;Acetaminophen is a medication ingredient that can falsely raise sensor glucose readings.&lt;SEP&gt;Acetaminophen is a medication that interferes with glucose oxidase monitor readings.&lt;SEP&gt;Acetaminophen, when taken above 4 g/day, can cause higher sensor readings on certain CGM devices.&lt;SEP&gt;A common analgesic whose repeated doses were shown to affect the performance of a permselective membrane glucose monitoring system.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8cceea4f7036977c7ddcbe81f76f8aa1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f677e56841fc57bffd8bf5b6cc4a7797&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db5749bec4af1c3ea068b257c4376aaf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-00f6c2252dc945e977b3a2b2f495ffe0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-05cc642337c2a615c9b40de9336aec18&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-651d85a13edd23f654d52f95c75d4e32</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/blood glucose monitoring.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786335922</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Paracetamol">
  <data key="d0">Paracetamol</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Paracetamol is a medication that can falsely raise sensor glucose readings, similar to acetaminophen.&lt;SEP&gt;A medication similar to acetaminophen that may falsely elevate sensor glucose readings during CGM.&lt;SEP&gt;Paracetamol is a medication ingredient that can falsely raise sensor glucose readings.&lt;SEP&gt;A medication mentioned in the index.&lt;SEP&gt;A medication referenced in the pump’s alert list.&lt;SEP&gt;Paracetamol is a medication listed as an example of a drug that may be used by patients.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8cceea4f7036977c7ddcbe81f76f8aa1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db8e2f5011e0e0fe7dc11273e2f345b9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f3d819d6498d4482286628946e37a6b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f677e56841fc57bffd8bf5b6cc4a7797&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db5749bec4af1c3ea068b257c4376aaf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b2ef71fb1a347df36dbb8ea8f4856bcb</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/Orientacoes_Glicemia_SBD.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786337565</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Food Bolus">
  <data key="d0">Food Bolus</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Food Bolus is an insulin bolus specifically calculated to cover the carbohydrate intake of a meal. The dose is determined by applying the individual’s carbohydrate‑to‑insulin ratio to the amount of carbohydrates entered for the upcoming food, thereby estimating the amount of insulin needed to offset the expected rise in blood glucose. 

Because the purpose of a Food Bolus is solely to address the glucose increase that will result from the consumed carbohydrates, it is administered without an additional correction factor for any existing hyperglycaemia. In other words, the calculation does not include a supplemental dose to lower elevated pre‑meal blood glucose; it focuses exclusively on matching insulin delivery to the carbohydrate content of the meal.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-05241912c4f8f5e79ae75071a1c7c604&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d68acc5f59d78c14cf4d2e4d34edf5e4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a0267d2986a48c4c31790b6f183277dc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b6025fa711665988fad0f789b9eb901a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ae3b43add031516d14e51c6d2a985bd7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-542e3b31a3f3a9496f26d05d1255498a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-97eb00dc26d33c23bf8bf473c0a98472&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1c5a5c97986d9b31b155b0c8f0cac1c5</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329508</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
