<node id="Glucose Levels">
  <data key="d0">Glucose Levels</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Measurements of glucose concentration that can be high or low, used for alerts in the CGM system.&lt;SEP&gt;Glucose levels denote the concentration of blood glucose, which can drop rapidly after exercise following Afrezza dosing.&lt;SEP&gt;Glucose levels refer to blood sugar measurements that guide insulin dosing and correction decisions.&lt;SEP&gt;Glucose levels are quantitative measurements of blood sugar concentration.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8cceea4f7036977c7ddcbe81f76f8aa1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4e6371d8083fb20b137912cdaeec1b8b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8644d98286c4a296063176435b45d589&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-511f6be03d2ea98970bd4c1b29b3e5c8</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/edelman-et-al-2026-dosing-afrezza-it-s-not-that-complicated.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/blood glucose monitoring.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786335963</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Glucose Trends">
  <data key="d0">Glucose Trends</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Patterns of glucose changes over time displayed by graphs and trend arrows.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8cceea4f7036977c7ddcbe81f76f8aa1</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329513</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="SmartGuard Feature">
  <data key="d0">SmartGuard Feature</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">SmartGuard Feature is an automated insulin‑delivery safety algorithm integrated into the MiniMed 780G insulin pump system. The feature continuously monitors sensor glucose (SG) values from the attached continuous glucose monitor and automatically modulates insulin delivery without requiring a confirmatory fingertip blood‑glucose meter reading, although it can request a meter check when needed. By using SG data together with entered carbohydrate information and user‑defined target glucose values, SmartGuard automatically adjusts basal rates and can issue auto‑correction boluses as frequently as every five minutes to keep glucose within the prescribed target range.

When activated, SmartGuard operates as a dedicated pump function that provides a separate Home screen view and can be visualized on the Graph screen, displaying real‑time insulin delivery decisions and alerts. The algorithm determines individualized limits for each auto‑correction bolus, delivers those boluses, and generates alerts or messages if glucose trends approach unsafe levels. It also includes an automatic insulin‑suspension component that halts basal delivery under low‑glucose conditions; this suspension mode disables the “suspend‑before‑low” feature and is not intended for use after a manual insulin injection. Certain alarms—particularly those related to low glucose—cannot be silenced while SmartGuard is active.

SmartGuard requires a five‑hour warm‑up period after a pump software update before it can deliver automated corrections, and it may become unavailable after a pump reset until recalibrated. Calibration of the CGM still relies on periodic fingertip blood‑glucose values. The feature is designed as a safety‑focused, hands‑free insulin management system that continuously adapts insulin delivery based on sensor data, providing both basal modulation and corrective dosing while issuing alerts to support safe glucose control.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4a4a75301f61fc3c86ad768de09d0c3f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8cceea4f7036977c7ddcbe81f76f8aa1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d68acc5f59d78c14cf4d2e4d34edf5e4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4a75df3ab63706f501e8d3134e74a64b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-caf5071e54a797f595d8cac8e4653918&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-379a204614747df98c1296e2f76c264f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bf54a88e051fe74fd94b773f8b5d98da&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-df77f2ea988e5724effb4c71cc79a65a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4faffc449b4b8ea09acbae135d21baa6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b48243f8e773d3c94abc58e2314db2c0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b6025fa711665988fad0f789b9eb901a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eb80f00ba2dab32852874cb384b38de3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3d0824c9d8a9ff5f2da52b7b5ea69c86&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5e1196548781bdac364853fdfd2074ec&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-92417ae942a11c591feb2ee9b5fadd7e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-71de01baf40871c616eaa39cb8189f43&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d4d222786e6ed163a90874659266c72a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2e9f02579c179c758cc6393322299d9c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ede0f32eb8f8ea1eaab76cc0bc7648fd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4b8de1434b9d9f57cd225b5d3e0d7f3b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8a0307c83d7b514ca00334e4c8ca2357&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1dd74224daea51112742135154e46244&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-36ace822cd4873b8fd2adcfef0a7f9fd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f677e56841fc57bffd8bf5b6cc4a7797&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8741750a7bf86eb5d1fadf82a9c7720e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-46d04af5292fae98e3aa651d9cec4512&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db5749bec4af1c3ea068b257c4376aaf</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329514</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Blood Glucose (BG)">
  <data key="d0">Blood Glucose (BG)</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Blood Glucose (BG) is the quantitative measurement of the concentration of glucose present in a blood sample. It is expressed as a numeric value that reflects an individual’s metabolic status and serves as the primary reference for clinical and self‑management decisions related to insulin therapy.  

In practice, BG is most commonly obtained through a finger‑stick whole‑blood test using a portable meter; the resulting reading constitutes the data that users monitor and record. These finger‑stick measurements are also employed to confirm or calibrate glucose values reported by continuous glucose‑monitoring sensors, ensuring that sensor‑derived glucose concentrations align with true blood values.  

Healthcare providers and closed‑loop insulin pump systems use BG readings to adjust insulin delivery rates, calculate insulin sensitivity factors, and clear automated alerts. Consequently, BG functions as the foundational metric for guiding insulin pump therapy, making dosing decisions, and maintaining optimal glycemic control.  

Overall, Blood Glucose (BG) denotes the measured glucose concentration in the blood, whether obtained directly via finger‑stick meters or used as a reference point for sensor data, and it underpins both personal diabetes management and automated insulin delivery algorithms.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4a4a75301f61fc3c86ad768de09d0c3f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-474703bb16e6e26e009e9d433c3d3647&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4a75df3ab63706f501e8d3134e74a64b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-df77f2ea988e5724effb4c71cc79a65a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bcdc240f555b6c71532ea6d04e0c5798&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b6025fa711665988fad0f789b9eb901a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3d0824c9d8a9ff5f2da52b7b5ea69c86&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a111edb31d6739acf013ce812b952366&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f677e56841fc57bffd8bf5b6cc4a7797&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dcea1ff62aae96936f552880e96faa69&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-59d8fcf807f0beb090b2f3d68cc7c168</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329515</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Now Portion">
  <data key="d0">Now Portion</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The immediate phase of a Dual Wave bolus that is delivered first.&lt;SEP&gt;The now portion is the immediate part of a dual wave bolus delivered at the start of the dose.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6a9714e3b2aaad60242e3827215230bc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a01dc8dc15b92e2b0b570753b0f57632</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329526</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Square Portion">
  <data key="d0">Square Portion</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The later phase of a Dual Wave bolus or the entire phase of a Square Wave bolus.&lt;SEP&gt;The square portion is the extended part of a dual wave bolus delivered over a set duration after the now portion.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6a9714e3b2aaad60242e3827215230bc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a01dc8dc15b92e2b0b570753b0f57632</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329527</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Insulin Delivery">
  <data key="d0">Insulin Delivery</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Insulin Delivery is the overall process by which a insulin‑pump administers insulin from the device into a user’s body. The pump delivers both basal insulin, which provides a continuous low‑level supply, and bolus insulin, which is given in larger, timed doses to cover meals or correct high glucose levels.  

The delivery system can be controlled by the user through the pump’s interface, allowing insulin to be suspended, paused, or resumed as needed. In addition, many pumps include an Auto‑Suspend feature that automatically pauses insulin infusion when preset conditions—such as low glucose detections—are met, enhancing safety. Together, these functions constitute the complete insulin delivery mechanism of modern pump therapy.&lt;SEP&gt;Insulin delivery refers to the methods by which insulin is administered to people with diabetes, including syringes, pens, pumps, and inhalation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6a9714e3b2aaad60242e3827215230bc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db8e2f5011e0e0fe7dc11273e2f345b9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fe844728a502927fee80d42268408b1a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b48243f8e773d3c94abc58e2314db2c0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-27b3ea1063acf8e0a407a89daea0dc32&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-92417ae942a11c591feb2ee9b5fadd7e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ede0f32eb8f8ea1eaab76cc0bc7648fd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b23dfd3ae95fca711f8f10fc98ab467c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e8e9d04ca4b641b5d8d5ef85044f4566&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f94cd06ab0d1bcc7a9349bc40ea3eb22&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-05cc642337c2a615c9b40de9336aec18</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/blood glucose monitoring.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786335933</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Rewind">
  <data key="d0">Rewind</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Rewind is the procedure the pump performs to reset its internal mechanisms after an error.&lt;SEP&gt;Rewind is a feature that returns the piston to its start position to place a new reservoir into the insulin pump.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6a9714e3b2aaad60242e3827215230bc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b6025fa711665988fad0f789b9eb901a</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329529</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Stuck Button Alarm">
  <data key="d0">Stuck Button Alarm</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">The stuck button alarm notifies the user that a pump button has been pressed for an unusually long time.&lt;SEP&gt;Stuck Button Alarm indicates that a physical button on the pump is not responding.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6a9714e3b2aaad60242e3827215230bc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b23dfd3ae95fca711f8f10fc98ab467c</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329529</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="BG">
  <data key="d0">BG</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">BG denotes blood glucose meter readings recorded by the pump.&lt;SEP&gt;BG refers to blood glucose data that may be checked during pump troubleshooting.&lt;SEP&gt;BG (blood glucose) is the measurement of glucose concentration that may be checked when insulin delivery issues occur.&lt;SEP&gt;BG represents blood glucose measurements used for sensor calibration.&lt;SEP&gt;BG represents a blood glucose measurement value.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6a9714e3b2aaad60242e3827215230bc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-28515a0aca492eeee478cd9947226498&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dd545bc80ceae270c16406af736789b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b23dfd3ae95fca711f8f10fc98ab467c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-da4119d4fc266b13dd11e47dd6f506ca</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329529</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Replace Battery">
  <data key="d0">Replace Battery</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Replace battery is the action of installing a new AA battery to restore pump power.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6a9714e3b2aaad60242e3827215230bc</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329529</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Change Reservoir">
  <data key="d0">Change Reservoir</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Change reservoir is the procedure of removing an empty reservoir and inserting a new one with insulin.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6a9714e3b2aaad60242e3827215230bc</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329530</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Resume Bolus">
  <data key="d0">Resume Bolus</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Resume bolus is the option to continue an interrupted bolus delivery within ten minutes of interruption.&lt;SEP&gt;Action to continue a previously paused bolus delivery.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6a9714e3b2aaad60242e3827215230bc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db8e2f5011e0e0fe7dc11273e2f345b9</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329530</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cancel Bolus">
  <data key="d0">Cancel Bolus</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Cancel bolus is the option to stop a partially delivered bolus and discard the remaining dose.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6a9714e3b2aaad60242e3827215230bc</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329530</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Select OK">
  <data key="d0">Select OK</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Select OK is the user action to acknowledge and clear alarms or alerts on the pump.&lt;SEP&gt;Select OK is a user action used to clear alerts or alarms displayed by the pump.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6a9714e3b2aaad60242e3827215230bc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-87a1bd89a18cb218431ff9359e299ee6</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329530</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Contact Technical Support">
  <data key="d0">Contact Technical Support</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Contact technical support is the recommended step when an alarm or alert recurs frequently.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6a9714e3b2aaad60242e3827215230bc</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329530</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Low Battery Alert">
  <data key="d0">Low Battery Alert</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">An alert indicating that the pump’s battery charge has fallen below 10 hours of operation.&lt;SEP&gt;Low Battery Alert notifies that the pump battery power is low and will be exhausted within 30 minutes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6a9714e3b2aaad60242e3827215230bc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-df77f2ea988e5724effb4c71cc79a65a</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329531</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Rewind Required Alarm">
  <data key="d0">Rewind Required Alarm</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Rewind Required Alarm indicates that the pump has encountered an error and must perform a rewind to resume delivery.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6a9714e3b2aaad60242e3827215230bc</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329531</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="High Basal Setting">
  <data key="d0">High Basal Setting</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">High Basal Setting refers to a basal insulin rate that is set to a very high level, potentially triggering alerts.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6a9714e3b2aaad60242e3827215230bc</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329531</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Auto Correction Bolus">
  <data key="d0">Auto Correction Bolus</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Auto Correction bolus is an automatic correction dose that SmartGuard may deliver to maximize time in glucose range.&lt;SEP&gt;An automatically delivered correction bolus generated by SmartGuard based on active insulin time and BG readings.&lt;SEP&gt;Automatic correction bolus delivered by the SmartGuard feature.&lt;SEP&gt;Automatic correction boluses that can be administered when the SmartGuard Feature is turned on.&lt;SEP&gt;A small correction bolus automatically delivered by SmartGuard at frequent intervals.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-83bb94d08bdb958eff25f76c9a6ac18a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d68acc5f59d78c14cf4d2e4d34edf5e4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bf54a88e051fe74fd94b773f8b5d98da&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d4d222786e6ed163a90874659266c72a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-20af4762343b8357c2c72473211f2918</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329535</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Dual Wave Bolus">
  <data key="d0">Dual Wave Bolus</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Dual Wave Bolus is an insulin‑pump bolus option that can be selected through the device’s Bolus Wizard. It delivers insulin in two distinct phases: an immediate “Now” portion that provides a rapid, normal bolus, followed by a Square Wave portion that releases a delayed, extended dose over a programmed time interval. Both phases are defined by the pump’s programming and can be stopped independently if needed.

The combination of an immediate dose with a square‑wave component makes the Dual Wave Bolus especially useful for high‑carbohydrate or high‑fat meals, as well as for situations that require a combined meal‑correction dosing strategy. By splitting the total insulin amount between the rapid and extended deliveries, the Dual Wave Bolus aims to meet both the quick‑acting insulin needs for rising blood glucose and the later‑onset glucose excursion that follows slower‑digesting nutrients.&lt;SEP&gt;Dual Wave Bolus combines an initial rapid insulin dose with a subsequent extended portion to cover meals high in fat or protein.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6a9714e3b2aaad60242e3827215230bc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d68acc5f59d78c14cf4d2e4d34edf5e4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ae3b43add031516d14e51c6d2a985bd7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9639df6feeacb49b96ddc51763dec77d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a01dc8dc15b92e2b0b570753b0f57632&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-542e3b31a3f3a9496f26d05d1255498a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-97eb00dc26d33c23bf8bf473c0a98472&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a074860e7f25b8dfbcccbabb53c645d7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-20af4762343b8357c2c72473211f2918&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1c5a5c97986d9b31b155b0c8f0cac1c5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7e3c3741659a85988124e5ddaf69c849</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786330152</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Carb Entry">
  <data key="d0">Carb Entry</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Carb entry is user‑entered information about carbohydrate consumption that informs bolus calculations in both Manual mode and SmartGuard.&lt;SEP&gt;Carb Entry records carbohydrate intake used in insulin dosing calculations.&lt;SEP&gt;User‑entered carbohydrate amount associated with a bolus.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-83bb94d08bdb958eff25f76c9a6ac18a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bf54a88e051fe74fd94b773f8b5d98da&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ede0f32eb8f8ea1eaab76cc0bc7648fd</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329536</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Basal Pattern and Basal Rates">
  <data key="d0">Basal Pattern and Basal Rates</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Basal pattern and basal rates define scheduled basal insulin delivery and apply to Manual mode but not to SmartGuard.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-83bb94d08bdb958eff25f76c9a6ac18a</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329537</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="BG Target in Bolus Wizard">
  <data key="d0">BG Target in Bolus Wizard</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">BG target in Bolus Wizard specifies the desired blood glucose level for bolus calculations and is used only in Manual mode.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-83bb94d08bdb958eff25f76c9a6ac18a</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329538</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Bolus Increment">
  <data key="d0">Bolus Increment</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Bolus increment defines the smallest step size for manual bolus dosing and is applicable only in Manual mode.&lt;SEP&gt;The predefined amount of insulin units added or subtracted with each button press when setting a bolus.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-83bb94d08bdb958eff25f76c9a6ac18a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-20af4762343b8357c2c72473211f2918</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329538</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Bolus Speed">
  <data key="d0">Bolus Speed</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Bolus speed determines how quickly a bolus is delivered and applies to both SmartGuard and Manual mode.&lt;SEP&gt;The rate at which the pump infuses bolus insulin, selectable as standard (1.5 units/min) or quick (15 units/min).</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-83bb94d08bdb958eff25f76c9a6ac18a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-20af4762343b8357c2c72473211f2918</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329539</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Carb Ratio">
  <data key="d0">Carb Ratio</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Carb ratio translates carbohydrate intake into insulin units and is used in both SmartGuard and Manual mode.&lt;SEP&gt;The number of carbohydrate grams covered by one unit of insulin for food bolus calculations.&lt;SEP&gt;Carb Ratio is the setting that defines how many grams of carbohydrate are covered by one unit of insulin.&lt;SEP&gt;Carb Ratio is the insulin-to-carbohydrate conversion factor required for accurate insulin dosing.&lt;SEP&gt;A parameter defining how many grams of carbohydrate correspond to one unit of insulin.&lt;SEP&gt;Carb ratio is the number of grams of carbohydrates covered by one unit of insulin, used to calculate bolus amounts.&lt;SEP&gt;Carb Ratio is a concept defining insulin needed per gram of carbohydrate.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-83bb94d08bdb958eff25f76c9a6ac18a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d68acc5f59d78c14cf4d2e4d34edf5e4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b48243f8e773d3c94abc58e2314db2c0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a111edb31d6739acf013ce812b952366&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-97eb00dc26d33c23bf8bf473c0a98472&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-20af4762343b8357c2c72473211f2918&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1c5a5c97986d9b31b155b0c8f0cac1c5</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329540</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Square Wave Bolus">
  <data key="d0">Square Wave Bolus</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Square Wave Bolus is a bolus delivery option that can be selected through the insulin pump’s Bolus Wizard and delivers insulin at a constant, “square‑shaped” rate for a user‑defined duration. Unlike a standard or dual‑wave bolus, the Square Wave Bolus releases a steady dose of insulin continuously over the chosen time interval, and the delivery can be interrupted or stopped by the user if needed.  

The period over which the insulin is administered can be set anywhere from approximately 30 minutes up to 8 hours. By spreading the total insulin amount evenly across this interval, the Square Wave Bolus provides a more gradual rise in insulin action, which is useful for meals that digest slowly, extended snacking, or situations where a rapid drop in blood glucose (BG) is undesirable.  

Because the rate of delivery remains constant throughout the selected window, the Square Wave Bolus offers a predictable and controlled insulin exposure, helping users match insulin delivery to prolonged carbohydrate absorption or to fine‑tune glucose control when immediate, peak‑type insulin spikes are not appropriate.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6a9714e3b2aaad60242e3827215230bc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d68acc5f59d78c14cf4d2e4d34edf5e4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b6025fa711665988fad0f789b9eb901a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ae3b43add031516d14e51c6d2a985bd7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9639df6feeacb49b96ddc51763dec77d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a01dc8dc15b92e2b0b570753b0f57632&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-542e3b31a3f3a9496f26d05d1255498a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-97eb00dc26d33c23bf8bf473c0a98472&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a074860e7f25b8dfbcccbabb53c645d7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-20af4762343b8357c2c72473211f2918&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b23dfd3ae95fca711f8f10fc98ab467c</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329540</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Dual/Square Wave Bolus">
  <data key="d0">Dual/Square Wave Bolus</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Dual/Square Wave bolus is a bolus delivery option available only in Manual mode.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-83bb94d08bdb958eff25f76c9a6ac18a</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329541</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Max Basal">
  <data key="d0">Max Basal</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Max basal sets the upper limit for basal insulin delivery and is applicable only in Manual mode.&lt;SEP&gt;Max Basal is the maximum basal insulin delivery rate setting that can be configured on the pump.&lt;SEP&gt;The maximum allowable basal insulin rate.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-83bb94d08bdb958eff25f76c9a6ac18a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db8e2f5011e0e0fe7dc11273e2f345b9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-59d8fcf807f0beb090b2f3d68cc7c168</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329541</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="CGM">
  <data key="d0">CGM</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">CGM, short for Continuous Glucose Monitoring, is a glucose‑sensing technology that continuously measures interstitial glucose levels using a subcutaneously placed sensor. The system typically consists of a sensor, a transmitter, and often an integrated insulin pump, and it delivers real‑time glucose data that can be displayed on the pump’s Home screen or a separate receiver. Readings are generated at regular intervals—commonly every five minutes—and are presented as current glucose values, trend arrows, and historical graphs.

The continuous data stream from a CGM is used to guide insulin‑dosing decisions. In insulin pumps equipped with features such as SmartGuard or Manual mode, the pump can automatically access sensor glucose readings to adjust insulin delivery, or the user can view the information to make manual adjustments. This integration enables more precise diabetes management and supports tighter glucose control.

CGM technology can be incorporated into certain insulin pump platforms and is recommended for individuals who require close glucose tracking, including those using inhaled insulin products such as Afrezza. As a core component of modern diabetes therapy, CGM is frequently referenced in device documentation and indexes as the primary method for real‑time glucose measurement.&lt;SEP&gt;Continuous glucose monitoring (CGM) is a method that provides real‑time interstitial glucose data and new metrics such as Time in Range.&lt;SEP&gt;CGM (continuous glucose monitoring) is a device used to achieve time‑in‑range and hypoglycemia targets.&lt;SEP&gt;Continuous Glucose Monitoring, a method of measuring glucose trends, used with A1C for glycemic control.&lt;SEP&gt;Continuous glucose monitoring (CGM) devices may be used to assess glycemic targets.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-83bb94d08bdb958eff25f76c9a6ac18a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db8e2f5011e0e0fe7dc11273e2f345b9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4faffc449b4b8ea09acbae135d21baa6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bcdc240f555b6c71532ea6d04e0c5798&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f3d819d6498d4482286628946e37a6b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a111edb31d6739acf013ce812b952366&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b23dfd3ae95fca711f8f10fc98ab467c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1c5a5c97986d9b31b155b0c8f0cac1c5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db5749bec4af1c3ea068b257c4376aaf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c0a2dce3852e38344f91c86f45dda403&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ca8620e735c40bfe850134ccea9a7154&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8644d98286c4a296063176435b45d589&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-70c5a1107fcc9b632361d9c52064f45d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-276b766b8d515b1e7f388b5b7381bfbc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c9bc5d11c9f848439320623cad3d3a38&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-511f6be03d2ea98970bd4c1b29b3e5c8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9dee0a79e4583f41e757f9a20f56f397&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d35e6caf612b4c4984ade9315ebc7431&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fc59aba81df88fe020f6e1d93d9e403b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-066ba9218f6293a2f3dc5459d69239cb</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/Insulinoterapia – Diretriz da Sociedade Brasileira de Diabetes – Ed. 2024.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/edelman-et-al-2026-dosing-afrezza-it-s-not-that-complicated.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/cgm.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/blood glucose monitoring.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Metas glicêmicas/Metas no tratamento.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Metas glicêmicas/metas cuidado do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786372086</data>
