<node id="Auto Basal">
  <data key="d0">Auto Basal</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Auto Basal is a function that automatically adjusts basal insulin rates.&lt;SEP&gt;Auto Basal is a method that continuously calculates and delivers basal insulin automatically using SG readings.&lt;SEP&gt;Automatic basal insulin delivery mode managed by the pump.&lt;SEP&gt;Auto basal is the automatically adjusted basal insulin delivered by the SmartGuard feature based on current sensor glucose readings.&lt;SEP&gt;Automatic basal insulin delivery mode that resumes after entering a blood glucose reading following an alert.&lt;SEP&gt;Auto Basal is an automated feature that adjusts the basal insulin rate based on glucose trends.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4a75df3ab63706f501e8d3134e74a64b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3d0824c9d8a9ff5f2da52b7b5ea69c86&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fd8af150d14c8fd9fd3b20e486220f65&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4b8de1434b9d9f57cd225b5d3e0d7f3b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1c5a5c97986d9b31b155b0c8f0cac1c5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8741750a7bf86eb5d1fadf82a9c7720e</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329555</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Auto Correction">
  <data key="d0">Auto Correction</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Auto Correction is a function that delivers correction boluses automatically.&lt;SEP&gt;Auto Correction is an automatic insulin adjustment mode used with SmartGuard.&lt;SEP&gt;Auto Correction automatically delivers a correction bolus based on SG values without user acknowledgment.&lt;SEP&gt;Auto Correction is a method that delivers correction boluses automatically when SG values indicate glucose is outside the target range.&lt;SEP&gt;Auto Correction delivers insulin units automatically based on the SmartGuard algorithm.&lt;SEP&gt;Auto correction is a correction bolus automatically delivered by the MiniMed 780G system to maximize time in range, occurring only when using the SmartGuard feature.&lt;SEP&gt;Auto Correction is an automated feature that delivers correction boluses in response to elevated glucose readings.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4a75df3ab63706f501e8d3134e74a64b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fd8af150d14c8fd9fd3b20e486220f65&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ede0f32eb8f8ea1eaab76cc0bc7648fd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-36ace822cd4873b8fd2adcfef0a7f9fd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1c5a5c97986d9b31b155b0c8f0cac1c5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8741750a7bf86eb5d1fadf82a9c7720e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-da4119d4fc266b13dd11e47dd6f506ca</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329555</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Block Mode">
  <data key="d0">Block Mode</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Block mode is a setting that temporarily stops insulin delivery.&lt;SEP&gt;A mode that allows caregivers to lock the pump, restricting access to critical features.&lt;SEP&gt;Block Mode is a feature that can be turned on or off to restrict certain functions when the pump is locked.&lt;SEP&gt;Block mode is a feature that restricts the ability to change all settings while still allowing suspend insulin delivery or clear alarms and alerts.&lt;SEP&gt;A mode that blocks insulin delivery under certain conditions.&lt;SEP&gt;Block Mode is a concept representing a mode that blocks insulin delivery.&lt;SEP&gt;Block Mode is a safety setting that prevents insulin delivery under defined conditions, referenced alongside SmartGuard.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4a75df3ab63706f501e8d3134e74a64b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db8e2f5011e0e0fe7dc11273e2f345b9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a111edb31d6739acf013ce812b952366&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d4d222786e6ed163a90874659266c72a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b23dfd3ae95fca711f8f10fc98ab467c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e8e9d04ca4b641b5d8d5ef85044f4566&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1c5a5c97986d9b31b155b0c8f0cac1c5</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329555</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Notifications">
  <data key="d0">Notifications</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Notifications are alerts and reminders generated by the MiniMed Mobile app.&lt;SEP&gt;Notifications are designed to get attention and convey information such as alarms, alerts, reminders, and messages.&lt;SEP&gt;Visual or auditory alerts provided by the device to inform the user.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4a75df3ab63706f501e8d3134e74a64b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db8e2f5011e0e0fe7dc11273e2f345b9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b6025fa711665988fad0f789b9eb901a</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329555</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Pump Software Update">
  <data key="d0">Pump Software Update</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Pump software update is a package that updates the insulin pump’s firmware.&lt;SEP&gt;Pump Software Update is a procedure performed via the MiniMed Mobile App to install new firmware on the insulin pump.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4a75df3ab63706f501e8d3134e74a64b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1dd74224daea51112742135154e46244</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329556</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Device Data">
  <data key="d0">Device Data</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Device data includes therapy and sensor information uploaded from the insulin pump.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4a75df3ab63706f501e8d3134e74a64b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329556</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
