<node id="Time in Range">
  <data key="d0">Time in Range</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Time in Range is a glycemic metric that quantifies the proportion of monitoring time during which a person’s glucose values remain within a predefined target interval. It is typically expressed as a percentage of the total time recorded by continuous glucose monitoring (CGM) devices, indicating how often glucose readings fall inside the desired range. In most clinical contexts the target range is defined as 70 to 180 mg/dL, though the specific limits can be adjusted to suit individual treatment goals.

The metric is derived directly from CGM data, calculating the duration or percentage of time that glucose measurements stay within the set boundaries. It is displayed on the “Time in Range” screen of CGM software, providing users and clinicians with a clear, at‑a‑glance view of glycemic control. By summarizing the proportion of time spent in range, the metric helps assess overall glucose management, guide therapeutic adjustments, and track progress toward personalized diabetes care objectives.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-db8e2f5011e0e0fe7dc11273e2f345b9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-27b3ea1063acf8e0a407a89daea0dc32&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b23dfd3ae95fca711f8f10fc98ab467c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a7387e81b8141435df1372f5d8b27662&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b4b76ae88b212b3a0a4d05c250e05e0c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e0d0e5c511e72e62db88a57fa6ea198e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2d8f17f3f250a37a1effaaa88cc8b382&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b2cd796639bdb0e10eeda7ef3d9ebbce&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b9fe6f17fdb504b9177e8ebc48505716</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/blood glucose monitoring.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/glicemias capilares.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Metas glicêmicas/metas cuidado do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786372122</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
