<node id="Appendix A">
  <data key="d0">Appendix A</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Appendix A is a dedicated section of the MiniMed 780G user guide and related manuals that enumerates every alarm, alert, and message associated with the insulin pump system. It provides a comprehensive list of the notifications that can be generated by the pump itself, the continuous glucose monitoring (CGM) sensor, and the integrated pump‑sensor (pump‑sensor) configuration. The appendix also includes references to messages that may appear when the device communicates with CareLink software, ensuring users have a single reference for all possible system alerts.

The section serves as a reference tool for clinicians, patients, and support personnel, allowing them to identify and interpret each alarm, alert, or message described in the manual. By consolidating this information in one location, Appendix A facilitates troubleshooting, training, and safe operation of the MiniMed 780G insulin delivery system.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-df77f2ea988e5724effb4c71cc79a65a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-87a1bd89a18cb218431ff9359e299ee6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bcdc240f555b6c71532ea6d04e0c5798&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6b53b69acbef0e172ea7719cc15bf3ad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eb80f00ba2dab32852874cb384b38de3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-71de01baf40871c616eaa39cb8189f43&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4b8de1434b9d9f57cd225b5d3e0d7f3b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dd545bc80ceae270c16406af736789b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-59d8fcf807f0beb090b2f3d68cc7c168</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329584</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Status Screen">
  <data key="d0">Status Screen</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The Status screen provides detailed status information of the pump system.&lt;SEP&gt;Status Screen provides detailed information about pump status, sensor status, and insulin units remaining.&lt;SEP&gt;A screen that can still be accessed to manually suspend the pump even when locked.&lt;SEP&gt;Status Screen is a user interface screen that provides shortcuts to suspend or resume insulin delivery and other actions.&lt;SEP&gt;Status screen is the pump’s display area showing current information and alerts.&lt;SEP&gt;Screen summarizing current device status.&lt;SEP&gt;Status Screen presents real‑time system information and alerts.</data>
