  <data key="d2">Basal Pattern Setup is a menu accessed from Delivery Settings that allows users to create or edit basal patterns in Manual mode.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b03b7fdf0dd9c96dc459929ccccdccff</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329589</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Body">
  <data key="d0">Body</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">The body is the site where the infusion set is inserted and an insertion site is selected for delivery.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fe844728a502927fee80d42268408b1a</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329590</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Steel Cannula">
  <data key="d0">Steel Cannula</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The steel cannula is a type of cannula on certain infusion sets that does not require filling.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fe844728a502927fee80d42268408b1a</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329590</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Infusion Set User Guide">
  <data key="d0">Infusion Set User Guide</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">The infusion set user guide provides instructions and duration of use for the infusion set.&lt;SEP&gt;A user guide that provides instructions for removing and connecting the infusion set.&lt;SEP&gt;The infusion set user guide provides step‑by‑step instructions for handling and inserting the infusion set.&lt;SEP&gt;Infusion set user guide provides instructions for disconnecting, reconnecting, and using the infusion set.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fe844728a502927fee80d42268408b1a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a0267d2986a48c4c31790b6f183277dc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-177e9aca0bf1c1724474ea529826bece&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-691a5ee6c6fdbea7a2ef1c835f0e66ae</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329590</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Fill Cannula Screen">
  <data key="d0">Fill Cannula Screen</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">The Fill Cannula screen appears on the pump when filling the cannula, during which insulin delivery is suspended.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fe844728a502927fee80d42268408b1a</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329590</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="High Limit">
  <data key="d0">High Limit</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">High Limit is a configurable numeric threshold that defines the upper bound for sensor‑generated glucose (SG) values.  The setting can be entered on the SG Review screen and typically ranges between 100 mg/dL and 400 mg/dL, depending on the user’s clinical goals and device configuration.  

When the sensor glucose reading reaches or exceeds the High Limit, the device—such as an insulin pump or continuous glucose monitoring system—activates high‑glucose alerts and initiates any associated actions programmed for a high‑SG condition.  These alerts serve both as a safety mechanism and as a visual cue for the user to review glucose data that surpasses the defined upper threshold.  

The High Limit is referenced in device documentation and indexed as the primary parameter for identifying high glucose events, providing a clear, standardized point at which high‑glucose management protocols are triggered.  

Overall, High Limit functions as the key upper‑threshold setting that enables users and automated insulin delivery systems to detect, display, and respond to sensor glucose values that are considered excessively high.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-db8e2f5011e0e0fe7dc11273e2f345b9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6b53b69acbef0e172ea7719cc15bf3ad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b6025fa711665988fad0f789b9eb901a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7ceebe6fbf743053d7b55523365689e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a111edb31d6739acf013ce812b952366&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5e1196548781bdac364853fdfd2074ec&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2e9f02579c179c758cc6393322299d9c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1c5a5c97986d9b31b155b0c8f0cac1c5</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329590</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Fill Amount">
  <data key="d0">Fill Amount</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">The fill amount indicates how much insulin is delivered to fill the cannula and can be verified or adjusted on the pump.&lt;SEP&gt;Fill amount is the numerical value entered to specify how much insulin to deliver.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fe844728a502927fee80d42268408b1a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-177e9aca0bf1c1724474ea529826bece</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329591</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Infusion Set Needle">
  <data key="d0">Infusion Set Needle</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The infusion set needle is the component of the infusion set that penetrates the skin to deliver insulin into the body.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fe844728a502927fee80d42268408b1a</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329591</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Infusion Set Occlusion">
  <data key="d0">Infusion Set Occlusion</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Infusion set occlusion is a blockage of the infusion set that can interrupt insulin delivery.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fe844728a502927fee80d42268408b1a</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329591</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Site Infection">
  <data key="d0">Site Infection</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Site infection is a possible complication at the insertion site resulting from prolonged or improper use of the infusion set.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fe844728a502927fee80d42268408b1a</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329591</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Transfer Guard">
  <data key="d0">Transfer Guard</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">A device placed on the insulin vial to secure it during the filling process.&lt;SEP&gt;The transfer guard is a component referenced at the beginning of the instructions, likely used to protect the pump during reservoir changes.&lt;SEP&gt;Transfer guard is a plastic piece attached to the reservoir, used to connect the reservoir to the insulin vial while the reservoir fills with insulin.&lt;SEP&gt;Transfer Guard is the plastic piece that attaches to the reservoir and connects the reservoir to the insulin vial.&lt;SEP&gt;Transfer Guard is a safety feature that monitors data transmission between sensor and pump.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fe844728a502927fee80d42268408b1a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b6025fa711665988fad0f789b9eb901a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-691a5ee6c6fdbea7a2ef1c835f0e66ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fd8af150d14c8fd9fd3b20e486220f65&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b23dfd3ae95fca711f8f10fc98ab467c</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329591</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Infusion Set Tubing">
  <data key="d0">Infusion Set Tubing</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The tubing that connects the reservoir to the infusion set and carries insulin to the body.&lt;SEP&gt;Infusion set tubing is the specific tubing that connects the reservoir to the infusion set for insulin delivery.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fe844728a502927fee80d42268408b1a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-691a5ee6c6fdbea7a2ef1c835f0e66ae</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329591</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Serter User Guide">
  <data key="d0">Serter User Guide</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">The serter user guide is mentioned as an additional reference for instructions on inserting the infusion set.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fe844728a502927fee80d42268408b1a</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329591</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Instinct">
  <data key="d0">Instinct</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Instinct is a specific CGM device model referenced with its own set of alerts and alarms.&lt;SEP&gt;Instinct is a pump model that generates alerts when the sensor has expired.&lt;SEP&gt;Instinct is a category label applied to several alerts indicating their type.&lt;SEP&gt;Instinct is a display mode or setting referenced in the pump’s low sensor glucose instructions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-87a1bd89a18cb218431ff9359e299ee6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8a0307c83d7b514ca00334e4c8ca2357&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-59d8fcf807f0beb090b2f3d68cc7c168&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-46d04af5292fae98e3aa651d9cec4512</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329591</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Safety Alert">
  <data key="d0">Safety Alert</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Safety Alert is a specific type of alert warning about sensor calibration issues and incorrect BG entries.&lt;SEP&gt;An alert related to safety warnings.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-87a1bd89a18cb218431ff9359e299ee6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f3d819d6498d4482286628946e37a6b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329591</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Rise Alert">
  <data key="d0">Rise Alert</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">An alert that activates when sensor glucose is rising quickly, prompting configuration of a Rise Limit.&lt;SEP&gt;Rise alert is an alert that triggers when glucose is rising rapidly, defined by specific rise‑rate thresholds.&lt;SEP&gt;Rise alert is a sensor alert that signals a rapid increase in glucose levels.&lt;SEP&gt;Rise Alert notifies that sensor glucose readings are rising rapidly beyond a preset limit.&lt;SEP&gt;Rise Alert is an alert that occurs if the sensor glucose reading is rising rapidly.&lt;SEP&gt;An alert indicating a rapid rise in glucose levels.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-87a1bd89a18cb218431ff9359e299ee6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b6025fa711665988fad0f789b9eb901a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f3d819d6498d4482286628946e37a6b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7ceebe6fbf743053d7b55523365689e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5e1196548781bdac364853fdfd2074ec&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fd751b869edcd6c88d9e467cfb2cb0fd</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329591</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Signal Interference">
  <data key="d0">Signal Interference</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Signal Interference denotes external electronic disturbances that affect communication between the pump and CGM Device.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-87a1bd89a18cb218431ff9359e299ee6</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329591</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Warm‑up Message">
  <data key="d0">Warm‑up Message</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Warm‑up Message informs the user that the sensor is in a warm‑up period before delivering readings.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-87a1bd89a18cb218431ff9359e299ee6</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329592</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="BG Reading">
  <data key="d0">BG Reading</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">BG reading shows the current blood glucose meter reading on the Home screen.&lt;SEP&gt;BG Reading refers to a blood glucose value requested by the system.&lt;SEP&gt;BG Reading is the blood glucose measurement displayed by the pump for dose calculations.&lt;SEP&gt;BG Reading is a blood glucose measurement obtained from the sensor or meter.&lt;SEP&gt;BG reading is a measurement of blood glucose that influences bolus calculations.&lt;SEP&gt;BG Reading is a blood‑glucose value entered by the user for sensor calibration and monitoring.&lt;SEP&gt;BG reading is the blood glucose value measured by a BG meter used for calibration and verification.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-87a1bd89a18cb218431ff9359e299ee6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4faffc449b4b8ea09acbae135d21baa6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b48243f8e773d3c94abc58e2314db2c0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ae3b43add031516d14e51c6d2a985bd7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-92417ae942a11c591feb2ee9b5fadd7e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-97eb00dc26d33c23bf8bf473c0a98472&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8a0307c83d7b514ca00334e4c8ca2357</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329592</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Select Continue">
  <data key="d0">Select Continue</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Select Continue is a user action used to confirm pairing a new sensor with the pump.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-87a1bd89a18cb218431ff9359e299ee6</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329592</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Select Cancel">
  <data key="d0">Select Cancel</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Select Cancel is a user action used to retain the existing sensor paired with the pump.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-87a1bd89a18cb218431ff9359e299ee6</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329592</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Select Yes">
  <data key="d0">Select Yes</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Select Yes is a confirmation button displayed on the Fill Stopped screen.&lt;SEP&gt;Select Yes is a user action confirming that the entered BG reading is correct for sensor calibration.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-87a1bd89a18cb218431ff9359e299ee6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-177e9aca0bf1c1724474ea529826bece</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329592</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Select No">
  <data key="d0">Select No</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Select No is a user action indicating that the entered BG reading is incorrect, prompting sensor replacement.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-87a1bd89a18cb218431ff9359e299ee6</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329592</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Start New Sensor">
  <data key="d0">Start New Sensor</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Start New Sensor is a pump screen option that initiates insertion and activation of a new CGM sensor.&lt;SEP&gt;Start New Sensor is a command that initiates a new sensor’s warm‑up period after connection.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-87a1bd89a18cb218431ff9359e299ee6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c030749e7f9a2ae77cb8993d7250cffe</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329592</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Reconnect Sensor">
  <data key="d0">Reconnect Sensor</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Reconnect Sensor is an option on the pump to re‑establish communication with a sensor already inserted in the body.&lt;SEP&gt;Reconnect Sensor is a command that reconnects an already‑used sensor to the pump.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-87a1bd89a18cb218431ff9359e299ee6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c030749e7f9a2ae77cb8993d7250cffe</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329593</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Bolus Wizard Screen">
  <data key="d0">Bolus Wizard Screen</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Bolus Wizard Screen is an interface used for configuring bolus deliveries, including BG entry in Manual mode.&lt;SEP&gt;Bolus Wizard Screen shows the current BG reading and calculates correction bolus amounts.&lt;SEP&gt;The Bolus Wizard screen is a user interface display that appears when the pump operates in Manual mode.&lt;SEP&gt;Bolus Wizard Screen is the display shown after selecting the Bolus Wizard option, where bolus parameters can be reviewed and adjusted.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a0267d2986a48c4c31790b6f183277dc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-542e3b31a3f3a9496f26d05d1255498a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-97eb00dc26d33c23bf8bf473c0a98472&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b907eb92deb747df3fb3b37fb9974142</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329593</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Carbs">
  <data key="d0">Carbs</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Carbs represent the carbohydrate count entered for a food bolus calculation.&lt;SEP&gt;Carbs represents the carbohydrate count of a meal entered when using a food bolus.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a0267d2986a48c4c31790b6f183277dc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-542e3b31a3f3a9496f26d05d1255498a</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329593</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Bolus Field">
  <data key="d0">Bolus Field</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The Bolus field displays the calculated insulin bolus amount on the pump screen.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a0267d2986a48c4c31790b6f183277dc</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329593</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Deliver Bolus">
  <data key="d0">Deliver Bolus</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Deliver Bolus is a command that starts the insulin bolus delivery process.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a0267d2986a48c4c31790b6f183277dc</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329593</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Manual Bolus Screen">
  <data key="d0">Manual Bolus Screen</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The Manual Bolus screen is displayed when the user selects manual bolus entry.&lt;SEP&gt;A user interface screen for manually delivering a bolus, referenced alongside the Bolus Wizard and Preset Bolus screens.&lt;SEP&gt;Manual Bolus Screen is the interface where users can set up and deliver boluses, including Square Wave Bolus, in Manual Mode.&lt;SEP&gt;Manual Bolus Screen is the interface displayed when selecting the manual bolus option, allowing selection of bolus type and amount.&lt;SEP&gt;Manual Bolus Screen is the pump interface used for manually entering bolus doses.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a0267d2986a48c4c31790b6f183277dc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ae3b43add031516d14e51c6d2a985bd7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-542e3b31a3f3a9496f26d05d1255498a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-20af4762343b8357c2c72473211f2918&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f94cd06ab0d1bcc7a9349bc40ea3eb22</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329593</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Insulin Menu">
  <data key="d0">Insulin Menu</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The Insulin menu provides options related to insulin delivery, such as stopping a bolus.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a0267d2986a48c4c31790b6f183277dc</data>
