  <data key="d5">1786329595</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Alkaline Battery">
  <data key="d0">Alkaline Battery</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Alkaline batteries are power sources that may be kept in the emergency kit.&lt;SEP&gt;Alkaline battery is a type of spare battery recommended for the pump emergency kit.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-28515a0aca492eeee478cd9947226498&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-36ace822cd4873b8fd2adcfef0a7f9fd</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329595</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="NiMH Battery">
  <data key="d0">NiMH Battery</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">NiMH rechargeable batteries are power sources that may be kept in the emergency kit.&lt;SEP&gt;NiMH battery is a fully charged rechargeable battery type suggested for the pump emergency kit.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-28515a0aca492eeee478cd9947226498&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-36ace822cd4873b8fd2adcfef0a7f9fd</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329595</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Display Options">
  <data key="d0">Display Options</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Display Options is the setting that controls the timeout duration for the pump screen and related reminders.&lt;SEP&gt;Settings that allow adjustment of screen brightness and backlight timeout.&lt;SEP&gt;Display Options are settings that control how long the pump display stays on before timing out.&lt;SEP&gt;Display Options is a concept for customizing screen appearance.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-28515a0aca492eeee478cd9947226498&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a111edb31d6739acf013ce812b952366&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d4d222786e6ed163a90874659266c72a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7b2af59ac9cf813cb07dac53f30250d0</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329595</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Check Settings Alarm">
  <data key="d0">Check Settings Alarm</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Check Settings alarm prompts the user to review pump configuration after a reset.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-28515a0aca492eeee478cd9947226498</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329595</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Possible Signal Interference Alert">
  <data key="d0">Possible Signal Interference Alert</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Possible signal interference alert indicates that external devices may be disrupting sensor communication.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-28515a0aca492eeee478cd9947226498</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329595</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Check Connection Alert">
  <data key="d0">Check Connection Alert</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Check connection alert warns that the link between transmitter and sensor is not secure.&lt;SEP&gt;Check Connection Alert is an alarm advising verification of sensor connection.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-28515a0aca492eeee478cd9947226498&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a111edb31d6739acf013ce812b952366</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329596</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Check Sensor Insertion Message">
  <data key="d0">Check Sensor Insertion Message</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Check sensor insertion message indicates the sensor may not be properly inserted.&lt;SEP&gt;Check Sensor Insertion Message is a prompt asking the user to confirm whether the sensor is fully inserted.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-28515a0aca492eeee478cd9947226498&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dd545bc80ceae270c16406af736789b2</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329596</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Emergency Kit">
  <data key="d0">Emergency Kit</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">An emergency kit is a collection of supplies kept on hand for diabetes emergencies.&lt;SEP&gt;Emergency Kit contains supplies for backup insulin delivery during pump downtime.&lt;SEP&gt;Emergency kit is a storage container mentioned for keeping spare AA lithium, alkaline, or fully charged NiMH batteries for the pump.&lt;SEP&gt;Emergency Kit is an artifact containing supplies for urgent situations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-28515a0aca492eeee478cd9947226498&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a111edb31d6739acf013ce812b952366&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1dd74224daea51112742135154e46244&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-36ace822cd4873b8fd2adcfef0a7f9fd</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329596</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Physical Impact">
  <data key="d0">Physical Impact</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Physical impact describes a drop or bump against a hard surface that can cause pump malfunction.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-28515a0aca492eeee478cd9947226498</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329596</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Battery Life">
  <data key="d0">Battery Life</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Battery life denotes the duration of pump operation from its batteries, noted as potentially shorter than usual after impact.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-28515a0aca492eeee478cd9947226498</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329596</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Startup Screen">
  <data key="d0">Startup Screen</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Startup Screen is the pump’s display that shows messages and prompts during the startup wizard process.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-28515a0aca492eeee478cd9947226498</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329596</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Current Time">
  <data key="d0">Current Time</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Current time displays the present clock setting on the Home screen, configurable via the Time and Date settings.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4faffc449b4b8ea09acbae135d21baa6</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329597</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Shortcuts">
  <data key="d0">Shortcuts</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Shortcuts are UI elements on the Home screen that allow rapid access to specific pump functions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4faffc449b4b8ea09acbae135d21baa6</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329597</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Time in Range Screen">
  <data key="d0">Time in Range Screen</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The Time in Range screen displays glucose time‑in‑range data when the Sensor feature is enabled.&lt;SEP&gt;A screen that shows the percentage of time glucose levels stay within target ranges.&lt;SEP&gt;The Time in Range screen displays the percentage of time SG stays between 70 mg/dL and 180 mg/dL, with fixed values.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4faffc449b4b8ea09acbae135d21baa6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-27b3ea1063acf8e0a407a89daea0dc32&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2e9f02579c179c758cc6393322299d9c</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329597</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Active Insulin Reset Icon">
  <data key="d0">Active Insulin Reset Icon</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The Active Insulin reset icon appears after the active‑insulin‑reset alarm and remains visible until the alarm time expires.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4faffc449b4b8ea09acbae135d21baa6</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329597</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Alert Silence Icon">
  <data key="d0">Alert Silence Icon</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The Alert Silence icon indicates that the Alert Silence feature is active, muting selected alerts.&lt;SEP&gt;Alert Silence Icon shows on the Home Screen when sensor alerts are temporarily silenced.&lt;SEP&gt;Alert Silence Icon is the visual indicator displayed on the Home screen when alert silence is active.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4faffc449b4b8ea09acbae135d21baa6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-92417ae942a11c591feb2ee9b5fadd7e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fd751b869edcd6c88d9e467cfb2cb0fd</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329597</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Block Mode Icon">
  <data key="d0">Block Mode Icon</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The Block mode icon signals that the pump is locked.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4faffc449b4b8ea09acbae135d21baa6</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329597</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Connection Icon">
  <data key="d0">Connection Icon</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The Connection icon shows whether the Sensor feature is communicating with the pump.&lt;SEP&gt;Connection Icon shows whether the pump is linked to a sensor or transmitter.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4faffc449b4b8ea09acbae135d21baa6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b23dfd3ae95fca711f8f10fc98ab467c</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329597</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Sensor Life Icon">
  <data key="d0">Sensor Life Icon</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The Sensor life icon indicates how many days remain before the sensor expires.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4faffc449b4b8ea09acbae135d21baa6</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329598</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Sensor Status Icon">
  <data key="d0">Sensor Status Icon</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The Sensor status icon conveys the sensor’s operational state, such as warming up or unavailable.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4faffc449b4b8ea09acbae135d21baa6</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329598</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Pump System">
  <data key="d0">Pump System</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The pump system encompasses the hardware and software that control insulin delivery and sensor communication.&lt;SEP&gt;Pump System is the software component of the pump that may request a blood glucose meter reading to continue sensor use.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4faffc449b4b8ea09acbae135d21baa6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b907eb92deb747df3fb3b37fb9974142</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329598</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="MiniMed/Medtronic Reservoir">
  <data key="d0">MiniMed/Medtronic Reservoir</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The MiniMed or Medtronic 3.0 mL reservoir stores insulin for delivery by the pump.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4faffc449b4b8ea09acbae135d21baa6</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329598</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Alert Silence Feature">
  <data key="d0">Alert Silence Feature</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The Alert Silence feature allows temporary silencing of alerts and vibrations.&lt;SEP&gt;Alert Silence feature allows the user to mute selected sensor alerts for a chosen duration, displaying an icon on the Home screen.&lt;SEP&gt;A feature that silences certain sensor alerts for a set period of time.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4faffc449b4b8ea09acbae135d21baa6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fd751b869edcd6c88d9e467cfb2cb0fd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d4d222786e6ed163a90874659266c72a</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329598</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Active Insulin Reset Alarm">
  <data key="d0">Active Insulin Reset Alarm</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">Active Insulin Reset Alarm is an alarm that triggers the Active Insulin Reset Icon when the active‑insulin counter is reset to zero.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4faffc449b4b8ea09acbae135d21baa6</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329598</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="SmartGuard Settings">
  <data key="d0">SmartGuard Settings</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">SmartGuard Settings is the menu where users configure SmartGuard options such as target and auto correction.&lt;SEP&gt;The submenu where SmartGuard parameters such as target and auto correction are adjusted.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bcdc240f555b6c71532ea6d04e0c5798&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b48243f8e773d3c94abc58e2314db2c0</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329598</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Basal X">
  <data key="d0">Basal X</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Basal X is an active basal setting on the insulin pump that delivers a specific amount of insulin per day.&lt;SEP&gt;A basal insulin delivery mode that can be started manually or automatically.&lt;SEP&gt;A specific basal setting that may deliver significantly more insulin than typically needed.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bcdc240f555b6c71532ea6d04e0c5798&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6b53b69acbef0e172ea7719cc15bf3ad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4b8de1434b9d9f57cd225b5d3e0d7f3b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329598</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Manual mode">
  <data key="d0">Manual mode</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">An operational mode in which basal delivery is controlled manually rather than automatically.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bcdc240f555b6c71532ea6d04e0c5798</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329598</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Snooze">
  <data key="d0">Snooze</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">An option to postpone an alert for a set period of time.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bcdc240f555b6c71532ea6d04e0c5798</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329599</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Snooze High &amp; Low">
  <data key="d0">Snooze High &amp; Low</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">An alert‑snoozing function specifically for high and low glucose alerts.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bcdc240f555b6c71532ea6d04e0c5798</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329599</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Reminders">
  <data key="d0">Reminders</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Reminders are scheduled prompts that can be set for various actions such as blood glucose measurements or medication.&lt;SEP&gt;Scheduled notifications to remind the user about diabetes‑related tasks.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bcdc240f555b6c71532ea6d04e0c5798&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2e9f02579c179c758cc6393322299d9c</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329599</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Appendix B">
  <data key="d0">Appendix B</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Section providing the menu map that diagrams available screens and features.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bcdc240f555b6c71532ea6d04e0c5798</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329599</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Mobile">
  <data key="d0">Mobile</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">A mobile device that can be paired with the insulin pump for data exchange.&lt;SEP&gt;Mobile denotes a mobile device (e.g., smartphone) that can be paired with the insulin pump for data display and management.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bcdc240f555b6c71532ea6d04e0c5798&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1c5a5c97986d9b31b155b0c8f0cac1c5</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329599</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Reservoir &amp; Set">
  <data key="d0">Reservoir &amp; Set</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Components used to store insulin and attach the infusion set to the pump.&lt;SEP&gt;Reservoir &amp; Set is a menu option that allows the user to manage both the insulin reservoir and the insulin delivery set together.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bcdc240f555b6c71532ea6d04e0c5798&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1c5a5c97986d9b31b155b0c8f0cac1c5</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329600</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Paired Devices">
  <data key="d0">Paired Devices</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Paired Devices is a menu option that allows the pump to pair with external devices or CareLink software.&lt;SEP&gt;A screen listing devices that are currently linked to the insulin pump.&lt;SEP&gt;Paired Devices refers to external devices that can be linked to the insulin pump, such as mobile phones or CareLink.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bcdc240f555b6c71532ea6d04e0c5798&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-92417ae942a11c591feb2ee9b5fadd7e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1c5a5c97986d9b31b155b0c8f0cac1c5</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329600</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Pair New Device">
  <data key="d0">Pair New Device</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Pair New Device is a screen option on the pump used to initiate pairing of a new CGM device.&lt;SEP&gt;The menu option to initiate pairing with a new device.&lt;SEP&gt;Pair New Device is the procedure for adding a new external device to the insulin pump's list of paired devices.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bcdc240f555b6c71532ea6d04e0c5798&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1c5a5c97986d9b31b155b0c8f0cac1c5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c030749e7f9a2ae77cb8993d7250cffe</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329600</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Pair CareLink">
  <data key="d0">Pair CareLink</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">The menu option to establish a connection between the pump and CareLink software.&lt;SEP&gt;Pair CareLink is the procedure for establishing a connection between the insulin pump and the CareLink service.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bcdc240f555b6c71532ea6d04e0c5798&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1c5a5c97986d9b31b155b0c8f0cac1c5</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329600</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="SmartGuard Target">
  <data key="d0">SmartGuard Target</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">SmartGuard Target is the user‑selected glucose goal (e.g., 100 mg/dL, 110 mg/dL, or 120 mg/dL) that SmartGuard aims to maintain.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b48243f8e773d3c94abc58e2314db2c0</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329600</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Warm‑Up Period">
  <data key="d0">Warm‑Up Period</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Warm‑Up Period is the time (48 hours or 5 hours) required after powering the pump before SmartGuard becomes active.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b48243f8e773d3c94abc58e2314db2c0</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329601</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="SmartGuard Active Insulin Amount">
  <data key="d0">SmartGuard Active Insulin Amount</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">SmartGuard Active Insulin Amount is the calculated insulin on board used by SmartGuard to adjust dosing.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b48243f8e773d3c94abc58e2314db2c0</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329601</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Clear Active Insulin Feature">
  <data key="d0">Clear Active Insulin Feature</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Clear Active Insulin Feature allows users to erase active insulin and total daily dose data used by SmartGuard.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b48243f8e773d3c94abc58e2314db2c0</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329601</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Manage Settings Menu">
  <data key="d0">Manage Settings Menu</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Manage Settings Menu is the pump interface that contains options like Clear Active Insulin.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b48243f8e773d3c94abc58e2314db2c0</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329601</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Wait Icon">
  <data key="d0">Wait Icon</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Wait Icon is a visual indicator on the SmartGuard Checklist screen showing the system is processing.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b48243f8e773d3c94abc58e2314db2c0</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329601</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Question Icon">
  <data key="d0">Question Icon</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Question Icon is a visual indicator on the SmartGuard Checklist screen signaling user action is required.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b48243f8e773d3c94abc58e2314db2c0</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329601</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Sensor Serial Number">
  <data key="d0">Sensor Serial Number</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Sensor Serial Number is the unique identifier displayed on the Paired Devices screen for the CGM sensor.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b48243f8e773d3c94abc58e2314db2c0</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329601</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="High and Low Limit Settings">
  <data key="d0">High and Low Limit Settings</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">High and Low Limit Settings define glucose thresholds used in Manual mode and SmartGuard operation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b48243f8e773d3c94abc58e2314db2c0</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329601</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Sensor Alert Settings">
  <data key="d0">Sensor Alert Settings</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Sensor Alert Settings is a configuration page referenced for details on high and low limit settings.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b48243f8e773d3c94abc58e2314db2c0</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329602</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Pump Reset">
  <data key="d0">Pump Reset</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Pump Reset is a complete reset of the insulin pump caused by loss of power or a software error.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b48243f8e773d3c94abc58e2314db2c0</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329602</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Software Update">
  <data key="d0">Software Update</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Software Update is the process of installing new firmware on the insulin pump.&lt;SEP&gt;The process of updating the pump’s firmware.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b48243f8e773d3c94abc58e2314db2c0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f3d819d6498d4482286628946e37a6b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329602</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Total Daily Dose">
  <data key="d0">Total Daily Dose</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Total Daily Dose is the cumulative insulin amount delivered by the pump over a 24‑hour period.&lt;SEP&gt;Total Daily Dose (TDD) is the calculated amount of insulin delivered in a 24‑hour period.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b48243f8e773d3c94abc58e2314db2c0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fd8af150d14c8fd9fd3b20e486220f65</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329602</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Very High Basal Setting">
  <data key="d0">Very High Basal Setting</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A basal configuration that delivers significantly more insulin than typically needed and may be unsafe.&lt;SEP&gt;A basal insulin delivery configuration that may deliver significantly more insulin than typically needed.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6b53b69acbef0e172ea7719cc15bf3ad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4b8de1434b9d9f57cd225b5d3e0d7f3b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329602</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Alert Before High Limit">
  <data key="d0">Alert Before High Limit</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">An alert generated when sensor glucose is approaching the high limit, prompting the user to check blood glucose.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6b53b69acbef0e172ea7719cc15bf3ad</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329602</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Alert Before Low Limit">
  <data key="d0">Alert Before Low Limit</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">An alert generated when sensor glucose is approaching the low limit, prompting the user to check blood glucose.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6b53b69acbef0e172ea7719cc15bf3ad</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329602</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Alert On High">
  <data key="d0">Alert On High</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Alert on high is an alert that triggers when SG reaches or exceeds the high limit.&lt;SEP&gt;An alert option that notifies the user when sensor glucose reaches the configured high limit.&lt;SEP&gt;An alert indicating that sensor glucose is at or above the specified high limit.&lt;SEP&gt;Alert on high is a notification that triggers when the glucose level meets or exceeds the high threshold.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6b53b69acbef0e172ea7719cc15bf3ad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7ceebe6fbf743053d7b55523365689e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5e1196548781bdac364853fdfd2074ec&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fd8af150d14c8fd9fd3b20e486220f65</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329602</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Alarm Low Sensor Glucose With Suspend">
  <data key="d0">Alarm Low Sensor Glucose With Suspend</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">An alarm indicating that sensor glucose is low and the pump has suspended insulin delivery due to a low‑glucose suspend feature.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6b53b69acbef0e172ea7719cc15bf3ad</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329603</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Message Basal Delivery Resumed">
  <data key="d0">Message Basal Delivery Resumed</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A message informing the user that basal insulin delivery has resumed after a suspend event.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6b53b69acbef0e172ea7719cc15bf3ad</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329603</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Manual Mode Basal Pattern">
  <data key="d0">Manual Mode Basal Pattern</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A basal pattern detected by the insulin pump in manual mode that delivers significantly more insulin than typically needed.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6b53b69acbef0e172ea7719cc15bf3ad</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329603</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Alert Manual Mode Basal Pattern">
  <data key="d0">Alert Manual Mode Basal Pattern</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">An alert indicating that the insulin pump has detected a manual‑mode basal pattern delivering excessive insulin.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6b53b69acbef0e172ea7719cc15bf3ad</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329603</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Snooze Option">
  <data key="d0">Snooze Option</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A selectable option allowing the user to postpone receiving an alert or message for a set period of time.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6b53b69acbef0e172ea7719cc15bf3ad</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329603</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="OK Acknowledgment">
  <data key="d0">OK Acknowledgment</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A selectable option to acknowledge and clear an alert or alarm.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6b53b69acbef0e172ea7719cc15bf3ad</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329603</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Maximum 2 Hour Suspend Time">
  <data key="d0">Maximum 2 Hour Suspend Time</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A time limit after which the pump automatically resumes basal insulin delivery following a suspend event.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6b53b69acbef0e172ea7719cc15bf3ad</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329603</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Low Settings Change">
  <data key="d0">Low Settings Change</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A change in basal settings caused by low‑glucose conditions that leads to resumption of basal insulin delivery.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6b53b69acbef0e172ea7719cc15bf3ad</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329603</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="EMC">
  <data key="d0">EMC</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">EMC is the acronym for electromagnetic compatibility.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b6025fa711665988fad0f789b9eb901a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1c5a5c97986d9b31b155b0c8f0cac1c5</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329603</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="ESD">
  <data key="d0">ESD</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">ESD is the acronym for electrostatic discharge.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b6025fa711665988fad0f789b9eb901a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1c5a5c97986d9b31b155b0c8f0cac1c5</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329604</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="GPS">
  <data key="d0">GPS</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">GPS is the acronym for global positioning system.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b6025fa711665988fad0f789b9eb901a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1c5a5c97986d9b31b155b0c8f0cac1c5</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329604</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Insulin Stacking">
  <data key="d0">Insulin Stacking</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Insulin Stacking occurs when a bolus is delivered while active insulin from a previous bolus is still lowering glucose levels, potentially causing hypoglycemia.&lt;SEP&gt;Insulin stacking is the risk of overlapping insulin doses that can lead to hypoglycemia, which Afrezza re‑dosing aims to avoid.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b6025fa711665988fad0f789b9eb901a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8644d98286c4a296063176435b45d589</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/edelman-et-al-2026-dosing-afrezza-it-s-not-that-complicated.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786333265</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="IV">
  <data key="d0">IV</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">IV is the acronym for intravenous.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b6025fa711665988fad0f789b9eb901a</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329604</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Lock">
  <data key="d0">Lock</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Lock is a feature that prevents accidental button presses on an insulin pump.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b6025fa711665988fad0f789b9eb901a</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329604</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="NiMH">
  <data key="d0">NiMH</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">NiMH is the acronym for nickel-metal hydride.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b6025fa711665988fad0f789b9eb901a</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329604</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Occlusion">
  <data key="d0">Occlusion</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Occlusion is a blockage or crimp of the cannula or tubing that prevents proper insulin flow.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b6025fa711665988fad0f789b9eb901a</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329604</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Power Save Mode">
  <data key="d0">Power Save Mode</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Power Save Mode is a state in which the insulin pump is fully functional but the screen goes dark to save power.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b6025fa711665988fad0f789b9eb901a</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329605</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Preset Temp Basal">
  <data key="d0">Preset Temp Basal</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Preset Temp Basal is a predefined temporary basal insulin delivery mode that can be started, paused, or canceled, resuming the programmed basal rate afterward.&lt;SEP&gt;Preset Temp Basal is a feature to set up and save temporary basal rates for repeated use.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b6025fa711665988fad0f789b9eb901a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9639df6feeacb49b96ddc51763dec77d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329605</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="RF">
  <data key="d0">RF</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">RF is the acronym for radio frequency.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b6025fa711665988fad0f789b9eb901a</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329605</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="SmartGuard Bolus Feature">
  <data key="d0">SmartGuard Bolus Feature</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The automated feature that delivers auto correction boluses based on active insulin time.&lt;SEP&gt;SmartGuard Bolus Feature assists in calculating a recommended bolus amount based on optional carbohydrate intake and optional BG or SG measurement.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b6025fa711665988fad0f789b9eb901a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-20af4762343b8357c2c72473211f2918</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329605</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="SN">
  <data key="d0">SN</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">SN is the acronym for serial number.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b6025fa711665988fad0f789b9eb901a</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329605</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Suspend Delivery">
  <data key="d0">Suspend Delivery</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Suspend Delivery stops all insulin delivery until it is resumed, after which only basal insulin restarts.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b6025fa711665988fad0f789b9eb901a</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329606</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="TDD">
  <data key="d0">TDD</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">TDD is the acronym for total daily dose.&lt;SEP&gt;TDD (Total Daily Dose) records the total amount of insulin delivered in a day.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b6025fa711665988fad0f789b9eb901a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b23dfd3ae95fca711f8f10fc98ab467c</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329606</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="CGM System">
  <data key="d0">CGM System</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">CGM System is the continuous glucose monitoring system of which the glucose sensor is a component.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b6025fa711665988fad0f789b9eb901a</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329606</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Sensor Data">
  <data key="d0">Sensor Data</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Sensor Data is the information collected by the glucose sensor and transmitted wirelessly to the insulin pump or compatible device.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b6025fa711665988fad0f789b9eb901a</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329606</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Glycemic Control Data">
  <data key="d0">Glycemic Control Data</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Glycemic control data are historic blood‑sugar measurements used to personalize Active Insulin Time.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ae3b43add031516d14e51c6d2a985bd7</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329606</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Square Wave Bolus Feature">
  <data key="d0">Square Wave Bolus Feature</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Square Wave Bolus Feature is a toggle that must be on to set up and deliver a Square Wave bolus.&lt;SEP&gt;Square Wave Bolus Feature is the enabling setting that allows selection of Square Wave Bolus type.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ae3b43add031516d14e51c6d2a985bd7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a074860e7f25b8dfbcccbabb53c645d7</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329606</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Dual Wave Bolus Feature">
  <data key="d0">Dual Wave Bolus Feature</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Dual Wave Bolus Feature is a toggle that must be on to deliver a Dual Wave bolus.&lt;SEP&gt;Dual Wave Bolus Feature is the enabling setting that allows selection of Dual Wave Bolus type.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ae3b43add031516d14e51c6d2a985bd7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a074860e7f25b8dfbcccbabb53c645d7</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329606</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Active Insulin Amount">
  <data key="d0">Active Insulin Amount</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Active Insulin Amount is the amount of insulin displayed on the Home Screen that includes only bolus insulin received.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ae3b43add031516d14e51c6d2a985bd7</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329606</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Bolus Wizard Setup">
  <data key="d0">Bolus Wizard Setup</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Bolus Wizard Setup is the configuration screen where the four Bolus Wizard settings are entered.&lt;SEP&gt;The configuration area within Delivery Settings where parameters like Carb Ratio, Insulin Sensitivity Factor, BG Target, and Active Insulin Time are set.&lt;SEP&gt;Bolus Wizard Setup is a menu option under Delivery Settings used to configure the Active Insulin Time.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ae3b43add031516d14e51c6d2a985bd7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-97eb00dc26d33c23bf8bf473c0a98472&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-20af4762343b8357c2c72473211f2918</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329607</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Duration">
  <data key="d0">Duration</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Duration is the length of time entered for the active insulin time setting.&lt;SEP&gt;Duration is the time length over which a Square Wave or the square portion of a Dual Wave bolus is delivered.&lt;SEP&gt;Duration is a selectable option used to set the length of a Square Wave or Dual Wave bolus delivery period in 15‑minute increments.&lt;SEP&gt;Duration specifies the time period over which the Square Wave portion of a bolus is delivered.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ae3b43add031516d14e51c6d2a985bd7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-542e3b31a3f3a9496f26d05d1255498a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-97eb00dc26d33c23bf8bf473c0a98472&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a074860e7f25b8dfbcccbabb53c645d7</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329607</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Pairing">
  <data key="d0">Pairing</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The procedure to connect a sensor or transmitter with the pump.&lt;SEP&gt;Pairing is the process of establishing a communication link between a sensor or transmitter and the pump.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6f3d819d6498d4482286628946e37a6b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b23dfd3ae95fca711f8f10fc98ab467c</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329607</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Unpairing">
  <data key="d0">Unpairing</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The procedure to disconnect a sensor or transmitter from the pump.&lt;SEP&gt;Unpairing is the process of disconnecting a previously paired sensor or transmitter from the pump.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6f3d819d6498d4482286628946e37a6b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b23dfd3ae95fca711f8f10fc98ab467c</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329607</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Safety Information">
  <data key="d0">Safety Information</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Guidelines, risks, and warnings related to pump usage and insulin therapy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6f3d819d6498d4482286628946e37a6b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329607</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Summary Screen">
  <data key="d0">Summary Screen</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">A screen that shows aggregated information about past insulin deliveries, sensor glucose readings, and meter readings.&lt;SEP&gt;The Summary screen is a UI view that separates information into categories such as time in range, insulin delivery overview, Bolus Wizard, SmartGuard, BG, sensor, and low management mode.&lt;SEP&gt;A screen that summarizes pump data such as history and settings.&lt;SEP&gt;Summary Screen provides an overview of recent glucose and insulin data.&lt;SEP&gt;Summary Screen is an artifact displaying summarized information on the device.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6f3d819d6498d4482286628946e37a6b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-27b3ea1063acf8e0a407a89daea0dc32&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a111edb31d6739acf013ce812b952366&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b23dfd3ae95fca711f8f10fc98ab467c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-da4119d4fc266b13dd11e47dd6f506ca</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329607</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Language Setting">
  <data key="d0">Language Setting</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The selectable language used by the pump to display information.&lt;SEP&gt;An option on the pump to select the display language.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6f3d819d6498d4482286628946e37a6b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-27b3ea1063acf8e0a407a89daea0dc32</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329607</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Time Format Setting">
  <data key="d0">Time Format Setting</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">An option on the pump to choose the time format.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6f3d819d6498d4482286628946e37a6b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329607</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Status screen">
  <data key="d0">Status screen</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">A display screen showing current pump status.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6f3d819d6498d4482286628946e37a6b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329607</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Outside typical range alert">
  <data key="d0">Outside typical range alert</data>
  <data key="d1">alert</data>
  <data key="d2">An alert indicating glucose readings are outside the typical range.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6f3d819d6498d4482286628946e37a6b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329608</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Pair device">
  <data key="d0">Pair device</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A method to initiate pairing between the pump and a sensor.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6f3d819d6498d4482286628946e37a6b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329608</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Pairing transmitter">
