  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Notifications generated by the pump, CGM device, SmartGuard feature, and CareLink software, categorized in the user guide.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-eb80f00ba2dab32852874cb384b38de3</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329619</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="70% Alcohol Wipe">
  <data key="d0">70% Alcohol Wipe</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The 70% alcohol wipe is a cleaning material used to disinfect the insulin pump surface.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-eb80f00ba2dab32852874cb384b38de3</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329619</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Clean Cloth">
  <data key="d0">Clean Cloth</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">A clean cloth is a cleaning tool used to wipe the insulin pump and remove detergent residue.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-eb80f00ba2dab32852874cb384b38de3</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329620</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cotton Swab">
  <data key="d0">Cotton Swab</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">A cotton swab is a cleaning implement used to remove battery residue from the battery cap and battery compartment housing.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-eb80f00ba2dab32852874cb384b38de3</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329620</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Detergent Residue">
  <data key="d0">Detergent Residue</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Detergent residue is the leftover cleaning agent that may remain on the insulin pump after washing.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-eb80f00ba2dab32852874cb384b38de3</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329620</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Battery Residue">
  <data key="d0">Battery Residue</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Battery residue is the leftover material that can accumulate on the battery cap and battery compartment housing.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-eb80f00ba2dab32852874cb384b38de3</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329620</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Temperature Limits">
  <data key="d0">Temperature Limits</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Temperature limits specify that the insulin pump must not be exposed below -4 °F (-20 °C) or above 122 °F (50 °C) to avoid damage.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-eb80f00ba2dab32852874cb384b38de3</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329620</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Internal Battery">
  <data key="d0">Internal Battery</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The internal battery is a built‑in power source in the insulin pump in addition to the removable AA battery.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-eb80f00ba2dab32852874cb384b38de3</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329621</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Suspend on Low Alarm">
  <data key="d0">Suspend on Low Alarm</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Alarm that activates when sensor glucose falls at or below a defined low limit and delivery is suspended.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3d0824c9d8a9ff5f2da52b7b5ea69c86</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329621</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Transmitter Battery Depleted Alert">
  <data key="d0">Transmitter Battery Depleted Alert</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Alert indicating that the transmitter battery is exhausted and must be recharged before glucose data can be recorded.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3d0824c9d8a9ff5f2da52b7b5ea69c86&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b23dfd3ae95fca711f8f10fc98ab467c</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329621</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Warm Up Not Started Alert">
  <data key="d0">Warm Up Not Started Alert</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Alert that occurs when a newly paired sensor fails to begin warm‑up, indicating insertion issues.&lt;SEP&gt;Warm Up Not Started Alert notifies that the pump has not entered its warm‑up sequence.&lt;SEP&gt;Warm Up Not Started Alert notifies the user that the pump’s warm‑up sequence has not begun.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3d0824c9d8a9ff5f2da52b7b5ea69c86&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b23dfd3ae95fca711f8f10fc98ab467c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f2dcbcd5e78200b20900f8955c826b2e</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329621</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Very High Basal Setting Message">
  <data key="d0">Very High Basal Setting Message</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Message warning that a manually set basal insulin pattern would deliver significantly more insulin than typical and advises consulting a healthcare professional.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3d0824c9d8a9ff5f2da52b7b5ea69c86</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329621</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="CGM Sensor">
  <data key="d0">CGM Sensor</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The sensor component of the CGM device that detects interstitial fluid glucose levels and requires a warm‑up period.&lt;SEP&gt;CGM sensor is the component of continuous glucose monitoring devices that measures interstitial glucose, whose adherence can affect efficacy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3d0824c9d8a9ff5f2da52b7b5ea69c86&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-276b766b8d515b1e7f388b5b7381bfbc</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/cgm.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786335254</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Maximum Delivery Alert">
  <data key="d0">Maximum Delivery Alert</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Alert notifying that SmartGuard has been delivering at the maximum basal delivery rate for several hours and requires a blood glucose entry.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3d0824c9d8a9ff5f2da52b7b5ea69c86</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329621</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Minimum Delivery Time Limit Alert">
  <data key="d0">Minimum Delivery Time Limit Alert</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Alert indicating that SmartGuard has reached the minimum delivery time limit (three to six hours) and prompts the user to enter a blood glucose reading.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3d0824c9d8a9ff5f2da52b7b5ea69c86</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329621</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="MiniMed Mobile app">
  <data key="d0">MiniMed Mobile app</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">A mobile application that can display the sensor glucose graph on a mobile device.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7ceebe6fbf743053d7b55523365689e3</data>
