  <data key="d5">1786329622</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Guardian 4 sensor">
  <data key="d0">Guardian 4 sensor</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">A CGM sensor model with a preset low sensor glucose value of 64 mg/dL.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7ceebe6fbf743053d7b55523365689e3</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329622</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="BG meter">
  <data key="d0">BG meter</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">A blood glucose meter used to confirm glucose levels when sensor readings and symptoms disagree.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7ceebe6fbf743053d7b55523365689e3</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329622</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Alert Before High">
  <data key="d0">Alert Before High</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Alert before high is an alert that triggers when SG is predicted to reach the high limit.&lt;SEP&gt;An alert option that notifies the user before sensor glucose reaches the configured high limit.&lt;SEP&gt;Alert before high is a notification issued shortly before the glucose level reaches the high threshold.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7ceebe6fbf743053d7b55523365689e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5e1196548781bdac364853fdfd2074ec&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fd8af150d14c8fd9fd3b20e486220f65</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329622</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Time Before High">
  <data key="d0">Time Before High</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Time before high is a configurable duration (5–30 minutes) that determines how early the alert before high occurs.&lt;SEP&gt;A configurable interval (5 to 30 minutes) that determines how early the Alert Before High triggers.&lt;SEP&gt;Time Before High measures the duration until glucose is projected to exceed the high threshold.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7ceebe6fbf743053d7b55523365689e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5e1196548781bdac364853fdfd2074ec&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b23dfd3ae95fca711f8f10fc98ab467c</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329622</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="High Setup Screen">
  <data key="d0">High Setup Screen</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">High Setup screen displays options for configuring high SG alerts for each time segment.&lt;SEP&gt;The screen shown when accessing High Alert settings, allowing editing of high SG parameters.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7ceebe6fbf743053d7b55523365689e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5e1196548781bdac364853fdfd2074ec</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329622</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Snooze Screen">
  <data key="d0">Snooze Screen</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The screen displayed when configuring snooze options for high and low alerts.&lt;SEP&gt;Snooze screen is the interface where users select Low Snooze duration and save the setting.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7ceebe6fbf743053d7b55523365689e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fd751b869edcd6c88d9e467cfb2cb0fd</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329622</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Custom Limit Screen">
  <data key="d0">Custom Limit Screen</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The screen where a user can enter a custom rise rate when setting a Rise Limit.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7ceebe6fbf743053d7b55523365689e3</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329623</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Pump Rewind Procedure">
  <data key="d0">Pump Rewind Procedure</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A method for rewinding the pump, required when inserting a new reservoir, involving confirmation of infusion set disconnection.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-691a5ee6c6fdbea7a2ef1c835f0e66ae</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329623</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Plunger Rod">
  <data key="d0">Plunger Rod</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">A rod used to pull and push the plunger while filling the reservoir with insulin.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-691a5ee6c6fdbea7a2ef1c835f0e66ae</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329623</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Activity Guard">
  <data key="d0">Activity Guard</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The activity guard helps prevent the reservoir from being rotated or removed from the pump during physical activities.&lt;SEP&gt;An optional safety device that can be attached to the reservoir compartment of the pump.&lt;SEP&gt;Activity guard is an attachment that secures the reservoir during activity or when the insulin pump is worn by a child.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-691a5ee6c6fdbea7a2ef1c835f0e66ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a764dcbdd73fd1c50fa72a7cd60b6e19&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1c5a5c97986d9b31b155b0c8f0cac1c5</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329623</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Disposal Information">
  <data key="d0">Disposal Information</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Guidance detailing how to properly dispose of used reservoirs and infusion sets.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-691a5ee6c6fdbea7a2ef1c835f0e66ae</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329623</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hand Washing Procedure">
  <data key="d0">Hand Washing Procedure</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The recommended step of washing hands with soap and water before operating the insulin pump.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-691a5ee6c6fdbea7a2ef1c835f0e66ae</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329623</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Clearing Active Insulin Procedure">
  <data key="d0">Clearing Active Insulin Procedure</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The process of ensuring that any insulin remaining active in the pump is cleared before first use.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-691a5ee6c6fdbea7a2ef1c835f0e66ae</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329623</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Inaccurate Insulin Delivery">
  <data key="d0">Inaccurate Insulin Delivery</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A condition where the amount of insulin delivered does not match the intended dosage, often due to air bubbles or liquid contamination.</data>
