  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329634</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Replacing">
  <data key="d0">Replacing</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Replacing describes the action of installing a new component in place of an old one.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a111edb31d6739acf013ce812b952366</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329634</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Icon">
  <data key="d0">Icon</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Icon is the visual indicator on the Bolus Wizard Screen that shows a recent BG meter reading is being used.&lt;SEP&gt;Icon is a visual symbol used in the device interface.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a111edb31d6739acf013ce812b952366&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-97eb00dc26d33c23bf8bf473c0a98472</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329634</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Rate">
  <data key="d0">Rate</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Rate is a temp basal rate type that delivers a fixed basal insulin rate in units per hour for the duration of the temporary basal period.&lt;SEP&gt;Rate is a data value representing units of insulin per hour, used when configuring a preset temp basal rate.&lt;SEP&gt;Rate refers to the speed or amount of insulin delivery.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a111edb31d6739acf013ce812b952366&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-14031c05fdb4152e391234af47d0cfe4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b907eb92deb747df3fb3b37fb9974142</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329634</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Date">
  <data key="d0">Date</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Date records a specific calendar day for logged events.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a111edb31d6739acf013ce812b952366</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329634</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Power Error">
  <data key="d0">Power Error</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Power Error is an alarm indicating that the internal power source cannot charge and the pump is operating on AA battery only.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9bfe428f5a1381000cf6932b37aa2239</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329635</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Pump Error">
  <data key="d0">Pump Error</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Pump Error is a malfunction that can cause active insulin values to be inaccurate.&lt;SEP&gt;Pump Error is a generic alarm indicating a malfunction that may require a pump restart.&lt;SEP&gt;Pump error is an alert indicating a generic malfunction within the insulin pump.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9bfe428f5a1381000cf6932b37aa2239&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fd8af150d14c8fd9fd3b20e486220f65&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f94cd06ab0d1bcc7a9349bc40ea3eb22</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329635</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Backup Settings">
  <data key="d0">Backup Settings</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Backup Settings are previously saved pump configuration values that can be restored after a restart.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9bfe428f5a1381000cf6932b37aa2239</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329635</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Internal Power Source">
  <data key="d0">Internal Power Source</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Internal Power Source is the built‑in power component of the pump that charges the device.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9bfe428f5a1381000cf6932b37aa2239</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329635</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Power Loss">
  <data key="d0">Power Loss</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Power Loss is the condition when the pump loses power after the AA battery is removed for more than ten minutes.&lt;SEP&gt;Power loss is an alert generated when the pump loses electrical power unexpectedly.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9bfe428f5a1381000cf6932b37aa2239&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fd8af150d14c8fd9fd3b20e486220f65</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329635</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Error Code">
  <data key="d0">Error Code</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Error Code is the numeric or alphanumeric identifier displayed on the alarm screen when an alarm occurs.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9bfe428f5a1381000cf6932b37aa2239</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329635</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="BG Check">
  <data key="d0">BG Check</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">BG check is the process of using an entered glucose value as a blood glucose meter reading to verify system performance.&lt;SEP&gt;A verification of blood glucose performed by the system, which may trigger a second check if it fails.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5e1196548781bdac364853fdfd2074ec&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f677e56841fc57bffd8bf5b6cc4a7797</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329635</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="SmartGuard Checklist Screen">
  <data key="d0">SmartGuard Checklist Screen</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">SmartGuard Checklist Screen lists required conditions before the pump can enable the SmartGuard Feature.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-92417ae942a11c591feb2ee9b5fadd7e</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329635</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Temporary Network Connection Icon">
  <data key="d0">Temporary Network Connection Icon</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Temporary Network Connection Icon indicates that the pump is temporarily linked to a remote upload device.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-92417ae942a11c591feb2ee9b5fadd7e</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329635</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Pump Status Screen">
  <data key="d0">Pump Status Screen</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Pump Status Screen displays detailed pump information such as reservoir, infusion set, battery, serial number, and model.&lt;SEP&gt;Pump Status Screen displays the remaining insulin units in the reservoir.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-92417ae942a11c591feb2ee9b5fadd7e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dcea1ff62aae96936f552880e96faa69</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329636</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Sensor Status Screen">
  <data key="d0">Sensor Status Screen</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Sensor Status Screen presents CGM device details, serial number, software version, and transmitter battery status for Guardian 4 sensor.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-92417ae942a11c591feb2ee9b5fadd7e</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329636</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Red Icon">
  <data key="d0">Red Icon</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Red Icon signals that a BG reading has been requested by the system.&lt;SEP&gt;Red icon is a visual symbol displayed on the pump screen to denote critical alerts or errors.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-92417ae942a11c591feb2ee9b5fadd7e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fd8af150d14c8fd9fd3b20e486220f65</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329636</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Question Mark Icon">
  <data key="d0">Question Mark Icon</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Question Mark Icon with a blue circle denotes that sensor information is unavailable.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-92417ae942a11c591feb2ee9b5fadd7e</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329636</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Three White Dots Icon">
  <data key="d0">Three White Dots Icon</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Three White Dots Icon shows that the pump is waiting for the sensor status to update.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-92417ae942a11c591feb2ee9b5fadd7e</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329636</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Red X Icon">
  <data key="d0">Red X Icon</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Red X Icon appears when a suspend feature is turned on but unavailable, indicating a recent suspend by sensor event or missing SG values.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-92417ae942a11c591feb2ee9b5fadd7e</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329636</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Remote Upload Device">
  <data key="d0">Remote Upload Device</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Remote Upload Device is a device that can receive temporary data uploads from the MiniMed 780G Insulin Pump.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-92417ae942a11c591feb2ee9b5fadd7e</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329636</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Battery Status">
  <data key="d0">Battery Status</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Battery Status indicates the current charge level of the pump’s internal battery.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-92417ae942a11c591feb2ee9b5fadd7e</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329636</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Pump Model Number">
  <data key="d0">Pump Model Number</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Pump Model Number specifies the model designation of the insulin pump.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-92417ae942a11c591feb2ee9b5fadd7e</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329636</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Pump Name">
  <data key="d0">Pump Name</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Pump Name is the user‑defined label assigned to the insulin pump.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-92417ae942a11c591feb2ee9b5fadd7e</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329636</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Volume">
  <data key="d0">Volume</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Volume is the adjustable sound level setting available on the Sound &amp; Vibration screen.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-92417ae942a11c591feb2ee9b5fadd7e</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329637</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Sound">
  <data key="d0">Sound</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Sound is the auditory notification setting that can be turned on or off via the Sound &amp; Vibration screen.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-92417ae942a11c591feb2ee9b5fadd7e</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329637</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Vibration">
  <data key="d0">Vibration</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Vibration is the haptic feedback setting that can be turned on or off via the Sound &amp; Vibration screen.&lt;SEP&gt;Vibration provides tactile feedback during self‑test.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-92417ae942a11c591feb2ee9b5fadd7e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e8e9d04ca4b641b5d8d5ef85044f4566</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329637</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Low Alert Time Segment">
  <data key="d0">Low Alert Time Segment</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Low Alert Time Segment is the time window during which low‑glucose alerts can trigger suspend‑by‑sensor actions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-92417ae942a11c591feb2ee9b5fadd7e</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329637</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="SG Values">
  <data key="d0">SG Values</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">SG Values are sensor‑derived glucose measurements used by the pump for monitoring blood glucose.&lt;SEP&gt;SG values are sensor‑generated glucose measurements used by SmartGuard to determine insulin dosing.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-92417ae942a11c591feb2ee9b5fadd7e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8741750a7bf86eb5d1fadf82a9c7720e</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329637</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Sensor Alerts">
  <data key="d0">Sensor Alerts</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Sensor Alerts are notifications generated by the pump when sensor information requires user attention.&lt;SEP&gt;Sensor alerts are notifications generated by the pump for conditions such as high SG, low SG, calibration reminders, and sensor status.&lt;SEP&gt;Sensor Alerts are notifications generated when sensor conditions such as errors or out‑of‑range values occur.&lt;SEP&gt;General alerts generated by the sensor when glucose data issues occur.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-92417ae942a11c591feb2ee9b5fadd7e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fd751b869edcd6c88d9e467cfb2cb0fd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d4d222786e6ed163a90874659266c72a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ede0f32eb8f8ea1eaab76cc0bc7648fd</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329637</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Silencing Sensor Alerts">
  <data key="d0">Silencing Sensor Alerts</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Silencing Sensor Alerts is the option to temporarily mute sensor notifications via the Sound &amp; Vibration screen.&lt;SEP&gt;The method used by the Alert Silence Feature to suppress specific sensor alerts.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-92417ae942a11c591feb2ee9b5fadd7e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d4d222786e6ed163a90874659266c72a</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329637</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Resume Basal">
  <data key="d0">Resume Basal</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Resume Basal is a status‑screen option that restarts basal insulin delivery after a suspension.&lt;SEP&gt;Resume Basal is a selectable option on the Home Screen that restarts basal insulin delivery after suspension.&lt;SEP&gt;Resume Basal is the action used to clear an alarm and restart basal insulin delivery.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-92417ae942a11c591feb2ee9b5fadd7e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b907eb92deb747df3fb3b37fb9974142&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f94cd06ab0d1bcc7a9349bc40ea3eb22</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329638</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Basal 2">
  <data key="d0">Basal 2</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Basal 2 is a predefined basal pattern option.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9639df6feeacb49b96ddc51763dec77d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329638</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Workday">
  <data key="d0">Workday</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Workday is a predefined basal pattern option for regular work days.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9639df6feeacb49b96ddc51763dec77d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329638</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Day Off">
  <data key="d0">Day Off</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Day Off is a predefined basal pattern option for non‑working days.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9639df6feeacb49b96ddc51763dec77d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329638</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Sick Day">
  <data key="d0">Sick Day</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Sick Day is a predefined basal pattern option for illness days.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9639df6feeacb49b96ddc51763dec77d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329638</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Basal Pattern Setup Screen">
  <data key="d0">Basal Pattern Setup Screen</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The Basal Pattern Setup screen allows users to add, edit, copy, or delete basal patterns and set their rates.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9639df6feeacb49b96ddc51763dec77d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329638</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Select Name Screen">
  <data key="d0">Select Name Screen</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The Select Name screen appears when creating or copying a basal pattern and is used to assign a name to the pattern.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9639df6feeacb49b96ddc51763dec77d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329638</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Max Basal Limit">
  <data key="d0">Max Basal Limit</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Max Basal Limit is the upper bound for basal rates; preset temp basal rates exceeding it appear grayed out and cannot be selected.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9639df6feeacb49b96ddc51763dec77d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329638</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Preset Temp Screen">
  <data key="d0">Preset Temp Screen</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The Preset Temp screen appears when selecting Preset Temp Basal and shows preset temp basal rates and their percentages or amount values.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9639df6feeacb49b96ddc51763dec77d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329638</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Temp Basal Screen">
  <data key="d0">Temp Basal Screen</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The Temp Basal screen appears when managing or canceling a Temp Basal delivery.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9639df6feeacb49b96ddc51763dec77d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329639</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Delivery Settings Screen">
  <data key="d0">Delivery Settings Screen</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The Delivery Settings screen provides access to Basal Pattern Setup and other basal configuration options.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9639df6feeacb49b96ddc51763dec77d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329639</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Active Insulin Reset to Zero Alarm">
  <data key="d0">Active Insulin Reset to Zero Alarm</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">An alarm that appears on the Home or Bolus screens when active insulin is reset to zero, requiring acknowledgment.&lt;SEP&gt;The Active Insulin Reset to zero alarm notifies the user that the active insulin value has been reset to zero.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a01dc8dc15b92e2b0b570753b0f57632&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f94cd06ab0d1bcc7a9349bc40ea3eb22</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329639</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="List of Alarms, Alerts, and Messages">
  <data key="d0">List of Alarms, Alerts, and Messages</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">A reference section that enumerates pump alarms, alerts, and messages.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a01dc8dc15b92e2b0b570753b0f57632</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329639</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Critical Pump Error">
  <data key="d0">Critical Pump Error</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">Critical pump error is a condition that triggers a specific screen and activates the pump siren.&lt;SEP&gt;Critical Pump Error triggers a warning screen, siren, and instruction to disconnect the pump and contact support.&lt;SEP&gt;A severe pump malfunction event that triggers an audible siren and a dedicated error screen.&lt;SEP&gt;Critical Pump Error is a severe malfunction that stops the pump from working properly.&lt;SEP&gt;Critical Pump Error is an alarm indicating an unresolved mechanical problem that prevents insulin delivery.&lt;SEP&gt;Critical pump error is a high‑severity alert indicating a malfunction that may require immediate attention.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a01dc8dc15b92e2b0b570753b0f57632&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-14031c05fdb4152e391234af47d0cfe4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fd8af150d14c8fd9fd3b20e486220f65&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-71de01baf40871c616eaa39cb8189f43&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dcea1ff62aae96936f552880e96faa69&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f94cd06ab0d1bcc7a9349bc40ea3eb22</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329639</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Critical Pump Error Screen">
  <data key="d0">Critical Pump Error Screen</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">The display shown on the pump when a critical pump error occurs.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a01dc8dc15b92e2b0b570753b0f57632</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329639</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Pump Siren">
  <data key="d0">Pump Siren</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Pump siren is an audible alarm that sounds when a critical pump error occurs.&lt;SEP&gt;The audible alarm on the pump that sounds during a critical pump error.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a01dc8dc15b92e2b0b570753b0f57632&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-14031c05fdb4152e391234af47d0cfe4</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329639</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Pump Buttons">
  <data key="d0">Pump Buttons</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The tactile controls on the pump used for navigation, which may become stuck during pressure changes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a01dc8dc15b92e2b0b570753b0f57632</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329639</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Airplane Travel">
  <data key="d0">Airplane Travel</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A scenario involving atmospheric pressure changes that can affect pump operation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a01dc8dc15b92e2b0b570753b0f57632</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329639</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Dual Wave Feature">
  <data key="d0">Dual Wave Feature</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Dual Wave Feature is a pump setting that enables delivery of Dual Wave Bolus when turned on.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-542e3b31a3f3a9496f26d05d1255498a</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329639</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Step Size">
  <data key="d0">Step Size</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Step Size is the incremental bolus amount (0.1 to 2.0 units) added for each press of the Easy Bolus button.&lt;SEP&gt;Step Size is a setting that determines the increment amount used to calculate total bolus amount.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-542e3b31a3f3a9496f26d05d1255498a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a074860e7f25b8dfbcccbabb53c645d7</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329640</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Max Bolus Amount">
  <data key="d0">Max Bolus Amount</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Max Bolus Amount is the upper limit for a single bolus delivery, constraining the step size and total steps.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-542e3b31a3f3a9496f26d05d1255498a</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329640</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Device Settings">
  <data key="d0">Device Settings</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Device Settings is a menu option in the pump that allows selection of the Sensor feature.&lt;SEP&gt;Menu area where users adjust pump parameters such as time, date, and display options.&lt;SEP&gt;Device Settings is the menu area where Block Mode, Self Test, and Manage Settings are configured.&lt;SEP&gt;Device Settings is the menu section where pump features such as Easy Bolus can be enabled.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-542e3b31a3f3a9496f26d05d1255498a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d4d222786e6ed163a90874659266c72a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ede0f32eb8f8ea1eaab76cc0bc7648fd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e8e9d04ca4b641b5d8d5ef85044f4566</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329640</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Delayed Bolus">
  <data key="d0">Delayed Bolus</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Delayed Bolus is a type of insulin bolus used for food that is absorbed slowly.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-542e3b31a3f3a9496f26d05d1255498a</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329640</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Dual/Square Wave Option">
  <data key="d0">Dual/Square Wave Option</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Dual/Square Wave Option is the selectable setting that enables or disables Dual Wave and Square Wave bolus modes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-542e3b31a3f3a9496f26d05d1255498a</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329640</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Red Notification Light">
  <data key="d0">Red Notification Light</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Red notification light is a pump indicator that blinks according to alarm or alert patterns.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-14031c05fdb4152e391234af47d0cfe4</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329640</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Blue Icon">
  <data key="d0">Blue Icon</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Blue icon is a visual symbol shown on the pump screen for messages.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-14031c05fdb4152e391234af47d0cfe4</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329640</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Yellow Icon">
  <data key="d0">Yellow Icon</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Yellow icon is a visual symbol shown on the pump screen for alerts and some messages.&lt;SEP&gt;Yellow icon is a visual symbol displayed on the pump screen to denote cautionary alerts.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-14031c05fdb4152e391234af47d0cfe4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fd8af150d14c8fd9fd3b20e486220f65</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329640</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Emergency Siren">
  <data key="d0">Emergency Siren</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Emergency siren is a loud alarm that escalates after ten minutes if an alarm or alert is not resolved.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-14031c05fdb4152e391234af47d0cfe4</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329640</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Preset Temp Setup">
  <data key="d0">Preset Temp Setup</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Preset temp setup is a screen accessed from Delivery Settings where users can add, edit, rename, or delete preset temp basal rates.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-14031c05fdb4152e391234af47d0cfe4</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329641</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Percent">
  <data key="d0">Percent</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Percent is a temp basal rate type that delivers a percentage of the scheduled basal pattern during the temporary basal period.&lt;SEP&gt;Percent is a data value representing a portion of the total basal rate, used when configuring a preset temp basal rate.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-14031c05fdb4152e391234af47d0cfe4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b907eb92deb747df3fb3b37fb9974142</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329641</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Ten Minutes">
  <data key="d0">Ten Minutes</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Ten minutes is a time duration after which an alarm or alert tone escalates to the emergency siren if the underlying problem remains unresolved.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-14031c05fdb4152e391234af47d0cfe4</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329641</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Notification">
  <data key="d0">Notification</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Notification is a message displayed on the pump to inform the user of alarms, alerts, or other information.&lt;SEP&gt;Notification is a generic message displayed on the insulin pump indicating status, alerts, alarms, or required actions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-14031c05fdb4152e391234af47d0cfe4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dcea1ff62aae96936f552880e96faa69</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329641</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Pump Screen">
  <data key="d0">Pump Screen</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Pump screen is the visual display interface of the insulin pump where notifications, alerts, alarms, and messages appear.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-14031c05fdb4152e391234af47d0cfe4</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329641</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Low Glucose Levels">
  <data key="d0">Low Glucose Levels</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Low glucose levels is a condition that can trigger an alarm on the insulin pump.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-14031c05fdb4152e391234af47d0cfe4</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329641</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Stopped Insulin Delivery">
  <data key="d0">Stopped Insulin Delivery</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Stopped insulin delivery is a condition that can trigger an alarm on the insulin pump.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-14031c05fdb4152e391234af47d0cfe4</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329641</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Sound and Vibration Settings">
  <data key="d0">Sound and Vibration Settings</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Sound and vibration settings are configurable options that determine the pump's audio output for alarms, alerts, and messages.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-14031c05fdb4152e391234af47d0cfe4</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329641</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Additional Basal Features">
  <data key="d0">Additional Basal Features</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Additional basal features is a chapter describing extra settings for basal insulin delivery, including preset temp basal rates.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-14031c05fdb4152e391234af47d0cfe4</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329641</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="SmartGuard Exit Alert">
  <data key="d0">SmartGuard Exit Alert</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">SmartGuard exit alert signals that the pump has left the SmartGuard safety feature.&lt;SEP&gt;An alert indicating that the SmartGuard feature has exited, often due to sensor being turned off or a suspend event not cleared.&lt;SEP&gt;SmartGuard Exit Alert signals that the SmartGuard algorithm is terminating its monitoring session.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fd751b869edcd6c88d9e467cfb2cb0fd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4b8de1434b9d9f57cd225b5d3e0d7f3b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b23dfd3ae95fca711f8f10fc98ab467c</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329642</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Alarm History Screen">
  <data key="d0">Alarm History Screen</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Alarm History screen displays a record of past alerts and their timestamps.&lt;SEP&gt;Alarm History screen lists alarms and alerts that occurred on a selected day, showing the most recent first.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fd751b869edcd6c88d9e467cfb2cb0fd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-da4119d4fc266b13dd11e47dd6f506ca</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329642</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Device Settings &gt; Sensor">
  <data key="d0">Device Settings &gt; Sensor</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Device Settings &gt; Sensor is the submenu where the sensor feature can be turned on or off.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fd751b869edcd6c88d9e467cfb2cb0fd</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329642</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Low SG Value">
  <data key="d0">Low SG Value</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Low SG value is the preset glucose threshold below which a low alert or alarm is triggered.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fd751b869edcd6c88d9e467cfb2cb0fd</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329642</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="High SG Value">
  <data key="d0">High SG Value</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">High SG value is the glucose level above 250 mg/dL that triggers a high alert if sustained for three hours.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fd751b869edcd6c88d9e467cfb2cb0fd</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329642</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Alert before High">
  <data key="d0">Alert before High</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Alert before high is a sensor alert that warns before glucose exceeds the high threshold.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fd751b869edcd6c88d9e467cfb2cb0fd</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329642</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="High Alerts Only">
  <data key="d0">High Alerts Only</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">High Alerts Only is an option to silence only high‑level sensor alerts.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fd751b869edcd6c88d9e467cfb2cb0fd</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329642</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="High &amp; Low Alerts">
  <data key="d0">High &amp; Low Alerts</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">High &amp; Low Alerts is an option to silence both high and low sensor alerts.</data>
