<node id="Review">
  <data key="d0">Review</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Review is the action/button used to display the configured basal pattern before finalizing changes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7b2af59ac9cf813cb07dac53f30250d0</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329659</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Resume Basal Feature">
  <data key="d0">Resume Basal Feature</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Resume Basal is a feature that restarts the programmed basal pattern after a suspension without restarting any pending bolus deliveries.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7b2af59ac9cf813cb07dac53f30250d0</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329659</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Carb Ratios">
  <data key="d0">Carb Ratios</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Carb ratios define how many grams of carbohydrate are covered by one unit of insulin in bolus calculations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7b2af59ac9cf813cb07dac53f30250d0</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329659</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Insulin Sensitivities">
  <data key="d0">Insulin Sensitivities</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Insulin sensitivities specify the blood glucose reduction achieved by one unit of insulin for bolus calculations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7b2af59ac9cf813cb07dac53f30250d0</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329659</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="BG Targets">
  <data key="d0">BG Targets</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">BG targets are the desired blood glucose range used by the Bolus Wizard to calculate appropriate insulin doses.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7b2af59ac9cf813cb07dac53f30250d0</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329659</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="24‑Hour Insulin Total">
  <data key="d0">24‑Hour Insulin Total</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">The 24‑hour insulin total is the cumulative amount of insulin scheduled for a basal pattern across a full day.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7b2af59ac9cf813cb07dac53f30250d0</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329659</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Sound or Vibrate Options">
  <data key="d0">Sound or Vibrate Options</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Sound or vibrate options configure auditory or tactile alerts for pump notifications.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7b2af59ac9cf813cb07dac53f30250d0</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329660</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Active Basal Pattern">
  <data key="d0">Active Basal Pattern</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The active basal pattern is the basal pattern currently engaged by the insulin pump to deliver basal insulin.&lt;SEP&gt;Active Basal Pattern is the currently applied basal rate schedule when no temporary basal is active.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7b2af59ac9cf813cb07dac53f30250d0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b907eb92deb747df3fb3b37fb9974142</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329660</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Reminder Alert">
  <data key="d0">Reminder Alert</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A reminder alert is a beep, vibration, or both generated by the pump every 15 minutes to indicate that insulin delivery is suspended.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7b2af59ac9cf813cb07dac53f30250d0</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329660</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Speaker">
  <data key="d0">Speaker</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The speaker is a hardware component of the insulin pump that produces audible alerts.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7b2af59ac9cf813cb07dac53f30250d0</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329660</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Vibrator">
  <data key="d0">Vibrator</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The vibrator is a hardware component of the insulin pump that provides tactile alerts.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7b2af59ac9cf813cb07dac53f30250d0</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329660</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Timeout Setting">
  <data key="d0">Timeout Setting</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The timeout setting controls how long the pump screen remains active before dimming and triggering reminder alerts.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7b2af59ac9cf813cb07dac53f30250d0</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329660</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Paired Sensors Screen">
  <data key="d0">Paired Sensors Screen</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">The Paired Sensors screen is a UI screen that provides a history of sensors that were paired with and unpaired from the pump.&lt;SEP&gt;Paired Sensors screen displays serial number, code, date, and time of the current sensor paired to the pump and a history of sensor pairings.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2e9f02579c179c758cc6393322299d9c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-da4119d4fc266b13dd11e47dd6f506ca</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329660</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="SG Review Screen">
  <data key="d0">SG Review Screen</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">The SG Review screen is a UI screen that displays a graph of sensor glucose (SG) history based on high and low limits and allows viewing of SG data for multiple days.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2e9f02579c179c758cc6393322299d9c</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329660</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="SG Data">
  <data key="d0">SG Data</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Sensor glucose (SG) data represents glucose readings captured by paired CGM sensors and can be reviewed over one or multiple days.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2e9f02579c179c758cc6393322299d9c</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329660</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="SG Alerts">
  <data key="d0">SG Alerts</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">SG alerts are notifications based on high and low glucose limits separate from the limits used for SG data viewing.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2e9f02579c179c758cc6393322299d9c</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329661</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Backfilled SG Values">
  <data key="d0">Backfilled SG Values</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Backfilled SG Values are recorded glucose values added to the graph when the sensor was out of wireless range.&lt;SEP&gt;Backfilled SG values are sensor glucose values recorded when the sensor is out of wireless range from the pump.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2e9f02579c179c758cc6393322299d9c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ede0f32eb8f8ea1eaab76cc0bc7648fd</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329661</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Personal Reminder">
  <data key="d0">Personal Reminder</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Personal reminders are user‑defined prompts that can be set up to occur at specific times each day.&lt;SEP&gt;Personal Reminder is a reminder that occurs at a specified time each day, can be edited, renamed, or deleted via the pump’s interface.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2e9f02579c179c758cc6393322299d9c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dcea1ff62aae96936f552880e96faa69</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329661</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Blood Glucose Entry">
  <data key="d0">Blood Glucose Entry</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Blood glucose entries are user‑recorded glucose measurements displayed on the Graph screen.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2e9f02579c179c758cc6393322299d9c</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329661</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Auto Correction Bolus Delivery">
  <data key="d0">Auto Correction Bolus Delivery</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Auto correction bolus deliveries are automatically calculated insulin doses shown on the Graph screen.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2e9f02579c179c758cc6393322299d9c</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329661</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Bolus Entry">
  <data key="d0">Bolus Entry</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Bolus entries are manually entered insulin doses displayed on the Graph screen.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2e9f02579c179c758cc6393322299d9c</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329661</data>
