  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Sensor Failed to Pair with Pump">
  <data key="d0">Sensor Failed to Pair with Pump</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Sensor Failed to Pair with Pump is an alert that occurs when the pump cannot locate or pair with the sensor.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-46d04af5292fae98e3aa651d9cec4512</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329684</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Sensor Grace Period Starting Soon">
  <data key="d0">Sensor Grace Period Starting Soon</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Sensor Grace Period Starting Soon is an alert warning that the sensor’s grace period is about to begin, prompting replacement soon.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-46d04af5292fae98e3aa651d9cec4512</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329684</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Insert New Sensor">
  <data key="d0">Insert New Sensor</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Insert New Sensor is the procedure of replacing an expired or expiring sensor with a fresh unit.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-46d04af5292fae98e3aa651d9cec4512</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329684</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Restart Sensor">
  <data key="d0">Restart Sensor</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Restart Sensor is the procedure of re‑initiating sensor operation, typically via the MiniMed Mobile App.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-46d04af5292fae98e3aa651d9cec4512</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329684</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Keep Pump Near Sensor">
  <data key="d0">Keep Pump Near Sensor</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Keep Pump Near Sensor is the instruction to position the insulin pump close to the sensor to facilitate successful pairing.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-46d04af5292fae98e3aa651d9cec4512</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329684</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Monitor BG">
  <data key="d0">Monitor BG</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Monitor BG is the action of continuously observing blood glucose values while sensor issues are present.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-46d04af5292fae98e3aa651d9cec4512</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329684</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Check BG">
  <data key="d0">Check BG</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Check BG is the action of measuring blood glucose to confirm levels during alerts such as suspend‑before‑low.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-46d04af5292fae98e3aa651d9cec4512</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786329684</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Vitamin C">
  <data key="d0">Vitamin C</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Vitamin C is a nutrient that, at doses above 1000 mg, can falsely raise sensor glucose readings and increase the risk of hypoglycemia.&lt;SEP&gt;High‑dose vitamin C is a natural substance that can interfere with the accuracy of blood glucose meters.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-db5749bec4af1c3ea068b257c4376aaf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4b355007bba178588f3928b6c8620a78</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/blood glucose monitoring.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786335874</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hydroxyurea">
  <data key="d0">Hydroxyurea</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Hydroxyurea (hydroxycarbamide) is a medication that can cause higher sensor glucose readings and interfere with CGM performance.&lt;SEP&gt;Hydroxyurea is a medication used for myeloproliferative disorders that can interfere with CGM sensors.&lt;SEP&gt;Hydroxyurea is a medication that can cause higher sensor readings on Dexcom G6 and Medtronic Guardian.&lt;SEP&gt;A medication whose administration was reported to cause inaccurate glucose sensor values in CGM systems.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-db5749bec4af1c3ea068b257c4376aaf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-05cc642337c2a615c9b40de9336aec18&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b4b76ae88b212b3a0a4d05c250e05e0c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-651d85a13edd23f654d52f95c75d4e32</data>
