  <data key="d0">Diabetes Obes Metab</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Scientific journal that published the overnight CSII article in 2008.&lt;SEP&gt;Diabetes Obes Metab is a scholarly journal covering diabetes, obesity, and metabolism, referenced for a 2014 treat‑to‑target review.&lt;SEP&gt;Diabetes, Obesity and Metabolism, a journal that published the nationwide study on first stroke risk in type 2 diabetes.&lt;SEP&gt;Diabetes Obesity and Metabolism is a journal focusing on metabolic disorders.&lt;SEP&gt;Diabetes, Obesity and Metabolism, a journal publishing a network meta‑analysis of metabolic surgery for type 2 diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a23aee717dff7fe908d8a006fd48a5c7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-76eaa3af026fbb91a96f70d3502e809d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e668c40e3bc21d982ed03a052f0f9339&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-703ccc96df3edd610232f0cca4bf7afa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-acba683ee0809d1c3f6e35c228f485ac&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d5ec01ed3c32ac663f3dc6cfa6fa09a3</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/blood glucose monitoring.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Metas glicêmicas/metas cuidado do diabetes.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377387</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hypoglycemia and Ketoacidosis with Insulin Pump Therapy in Children and Adolescents">
  <data key="d0">Hypoglycemia and Ketoacidosis with Insulin Pump Therapy in Children and Adolescents</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Article examining occurrences of hypoglycemia and ketoacidosis linked to insulin pump therapy in pediatric patients, published in 2006.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a23aee717dff7fe908d8a006fd48a5c7</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786330145</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Continuous Subcutaneous Insulin Infusion for the Treatment of Diabetic Patients">
  <data key="d0">Continuous Subcutaneous Insulin Infusion for the Treatment of Diabetic Patients</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Article describing the use of CSII as a treatment approach for patients with diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a23aee717dff7fe908d8a006fd48a5c7</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786330147</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Fenômeno Do Amanhecer">
  <data key="d0">Fenômeno Do Amanhecer</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The early‑morning rise in blood glucose that occurs in many individuals.&lt;SEP&gt;Fenômeno do amanhecer is a phenomenon that occurs after approximately five hours before waking, observed in individuals without diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7823719c01e7c914b4a58a1bb0d707bd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-60530d1861f7c2d1efecc069c0913d37</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786330147</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hormônio De Crescimento">
  <data key="d0">Hormônio De Crescimento</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Hormônio de crescimento is a hormone whose nocturnal secretion increases and contributes to the dawn phenomenon.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7823719c01e7c914b4a58a1bb0d707bd</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786330147</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Resistência À Insulina">
  <data key="d0">Resistência À Insulina</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Resistência à insulina refers to increased insulin resistance that participates in the dawn phenomenon.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7823719c01e7c914b4a58a1bb0d707bd</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786330148</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Produção Hepática De Glicose">
  <data key="d0">Produção Hepática De Glicose</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Produção hepática de glicose is the hepatic glucose output that rises and adds to the dawn phenomenon.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7823719c01e7c914b4a58a1bb0d707bd</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786330148</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Puberdade">
  <data key="d0">Puberdade</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Puberdade is a developmental stage during which the mechanisms of the dawn phenomenon become more potent.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7823719c01e7c914b4a58a1bb0d707bd</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786330148</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Dose Basal C">
  <data key="d0">Dose Basal C</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Dose basal C is the basal insulin dose that maintains euglycemic periods between meals, the time of greatest caloric intake, and may be reduced with exercise.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7823719c01e7c914b4a58a1bb0d707bd</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786330148</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Dose Basal D">
  <data key="d0">Dose Basal D</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Dose basal D is the basal insulin dose that covers the early night when most individuals are awake with reduced activity.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7823719c01e7c914b4a58a1bb0d707bd</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786330148</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Bomba De Infusão Contínua">
  <data key="d0">Bomba De Infusão Contínua</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Bomba de infusão contínua is an insulin pump that requires registration of two configurable factors for insulin calculations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7823719c01e7c914b4a58a1bb0d707bd</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786330148</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Fator De Sensibilidade (FS)">
  <data key="d0">Fator De Sensibilidade (FS)</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Fator de sensibilidade (FS) quantifies how many mg/dL of glucose are reduced by one unit of insulin; it varies among individuals, times of day, and growth phases.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7823719c01e7c914b4a58a1bb0d707bd</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786330149</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Relação Insulina/Carboidrato (RIC)">
  <data key="d0">Relação Insulina/Carboidrato (RIC)</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Relação insulina/carboidrato (RIC) links the grams of carbohydrate that can be covered by one unit of insulin and is used to calculate meal boluses.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7823719c01e7c914b4a58a1bb0d707bd</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786330149</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Pré‑prandial">
  <data key="d0">Pré‑prandial</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Pré‑prandial is the pre‑meal glucose target range included in the metas glicêmicas.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7823719c01e7c914b4a58a1bb0d707bd</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786330150</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Pós‑prandial">
  <data key="d0">Pós‑prandial</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Pós‑prandial is the post‑meal glucose target range included in the metas glicêmicas.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7823719c01e7c914b4a58a1bb0d707bd</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786330150</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="DTD (Dose Total Diária)">
  <data key="d0">DTD (Dose Total Diária)</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">DTD (dose total diária) is the total daily insulin dose calculated by weight, with formulas provided for adults and children.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7823719c01e7c914b4a58a1bb0d707bd</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786330150</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Daily Total Dose (DTD)">
  <data key="d0">Daily Total Dose (DTD)</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Daily Total Dose (DTD) is the total amount of insulin prescribed per day, calculated based on weight and other patient factors.&lt;SEP&gt;Daily Total Dose is the total amount of insulin prescribed per day, used to calculate sensitivity factor and carbohydrate ratio.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7e3c3741659a85988124e5ddaf69c849&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0f272d1c9c38e2a6b6d02b5aa66809e1</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/Insulinoterapia – Diretriz da Sociedade Brasileira de Diabetes – Ed. 2024.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786331411</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Insulin Sensitivity Factor (FS)">
  <data key="d0">Insulin Sensitivity Factor (FS)</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Insulin Sensitivity Factor (FS) is the factor used to calculate correction bolus based on the difference between current and target glucose.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7e3c3741659a85988124e5ddaf69c849</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786330151</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Insulin-to-Carbohydrate Ratio (RIC)">
  <data key="d0">Insulin-to-Carbohydrate Ratio (RIC)</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Insulin-to-Carbohydrate Ratio (RIC) indicates how many grams of carbohydrate are covered by one unit of insulin and is used to compute meal bolus.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7e3c3741659a85988124e5ddaf69c849</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786330152</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Fat-Insulin Ratio (RGI)">
  <data key="d0">Fat-Insulin Ratio (RGI)</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Fat-Insulin Ratio (RGI) determines the insulin needed to metabolize fats and proteins in a meal.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7e3c3741659a85988124e5ddaf69c849</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786330152</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Standard Bolus">
  <data key="d0">Standard Bolus</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Standard Bolus is the traditional insulin dose delivered at the start of a meal, usually consumed within 15‑30 minutes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7e3c3741659a85988124e5ddaf69c849</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786330152</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Extended Bolus">
  <data key="d0">Extended Bolus</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Extended Bolus is an insulin dose released slowly over several hours to match prolonged food absorption.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7e3c3741659a85988124e5ddaf69c849</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786330152</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Low Carb Diet">
  <data key="d0">Low Carb Diet</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Low Carb Diet is a dietary approach low in carbohydrates that influences insulin-to-carbohydrate ratio calculations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7e3c3741659a85988124e5ddaf69c849</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786330152</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Continuous Insulin Infusion System">
  <data key="d0">Continuous Insulin Infusion System</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Continuous Insulin Infusion System (SICI) denotes the class of devices that deliver basal and bolus insulin automatically.&lt;SEP&gt;Continuous Insulin Infusion System provides uninterrupted insulin delivery and is indicated for mixed meals with high fat or protein.&lt;SEP&gt;A device that delivers insulin continuously via infusion.&lt;SEP&gt;Continuous Insulin Infusion System is a device that delivers insulin continuously to patients with intensive diabetes therapy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7e3c3741659a85988124e5ddaf69c849&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c0a2dce3852e38344f91c86f45dda403&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-91a09040fc4581d7aad2216dba9fba79&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a5f7cad1fb0e1a0a02f63b5928b8acd2</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/cgm.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/glicemias capilares.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786338532</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Danne T">
  <data key="d0">Danne T</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Danne T is an author cited in 2018 for recommendations on insulin pump use.&lt;SEP&gt;Danne T is a co-author of studies and guidelines concerning insulin treatment in pediatric diabetes.&lt;SEP&gt;Danne T contributed as a co‑author to the international consensus on time in range.&lt;SEP&gt;Danne T is an author of an international consensus on the use of continuous glucose monitoring.&lt;SEP&gt;Danne T authored the International Consensus on Use of Continuous Glucose Monitoring.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7e3c3741659a85988124e5ddaf69c849&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-08f12a2de420625ccc88f737d06b7e84&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b50a9fb21c77773aec36a9b8e9f5e1d5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1dec009976a44828d0e619e7fa5b1c5d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-29ea6999715cd3886bd7d4abc2a653b0</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/Insulinoterapia – Diretriz da Sociedade Brasileira de Diabetes – Ed. 2024.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/ref.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Metas glicêmicas/Metas no tratamento.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786370054</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Moore LE">
  <data key="d0">Moore LE</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Moore LE is an author cited in 2017 for guidance on insulin dosing.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7e3c3741659a85988124e5ddaf69c849&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-08f12a2de420625ccc88f737d06b7e84</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786330153</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Insulin Dosing Guidelines">
  <data key="d0">Insulin Dosing Guidelines</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Insulin Dosing Guidelines are the set of recommendations on basal/bolus ratios and bolus types referenced from ADA and the cited authors.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7e3c3741659a85988124e5ddaf69c849</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786330153</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Postprandial Hypoglycemia">
  <data key="d0">Postprandial Hypoglycemia</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Postprandial Hypoglycemia is low blood glucose occurring after meals, which dual wave bolus strategies help prevent.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7e3c3741659a85988124e5ddaf69c849</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786330153</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Arnold Kadish">
  <data key="d0">Arnold Kadish</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Arnold Kadish was the doctor who, in the early 1960s, developed the first continuous insulin infusion system (SICI).</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e796e8f4bb4721a269775c3d2ef0c06a</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786330154</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Sistema De Infusão Contínua De Insulina">
  <data key="d0">Sistema De Infusão Contínua De Insulina</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The Sistema De Infusão Contínua De Insulina (SICI) is the first continuous insulin infusion device, originally large and heavy, later mini‑scaled for portable use.&lt;SEP&gt;A continuous insulin pump that delivers basal and bolus insulin doses and requires configuration of dosing coefficients.&lt;SEP&gt;A continuous insulin infusion system used for intensive insulin therapy, referenced throughout the document.&lt;SEP&gt;Continuous insulin infusion system (insulin pump) used for intensive diabetes therapy.&lt;SEP&gt;Sistema De Infusão Contínua De Insulina is a continuous insulin infusion system suggested for recurrent asymptomatic level‑3 hypoglycemia.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e796e8f4bb4721a269775c3d2ef0c06a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-60530d1861f7c2d1efecc069c0913d37&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-336a2f2c9b510e23c35be95e2ff7a72a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-51c7617f1e335789b870332231de4058&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f645bd7019e94151caaff47d6cbfcaf</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/Orientacoes_Hipoglicemia_SBD_transcricao.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1786338267</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Diabetes Control And Complications Trial">
  <data key="d0">Diabetes Control And Complications Trial</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">The Diabetes Control And Complications Trial (DCCT) was a landmark study in which early insulin pumps were employed for research on diabetes management.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e796e8f4bb4721a269775c3d2ef0c06a</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786330154</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Reservatório De Insulina">
  <data key="d0">Reservatório De Insulina</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The reservatório de insulina is the insulin cartridge of a pump that stores rapid‑acting or ultra‑rapid insulin for continuous delivery.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e796e8f4bb4721a269775c3d2ef0c06a</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786330155</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cateter">
  <data key="d0">Cateter</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The cateter is a flexible plastic tube that connects the pump reservoir to the subcutaneous tissue for insulin delivery.&lt;SEP&gt;The catheter used in SICI, whose occlusion can lead to hyperglycemia.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e796e8f4bb4721a269775c3d2ef0c06a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-336a2f2c9b510e23c35be95e2ff7a72a</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786330155</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cânula">
  <data key="d0">Cânula</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The cânula is a flexible plastic (often Teflon®) needle that remains implanted in subcutaneous tissue to allow insulin flow from the catheter.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e796e8f4bb4721a269775c3d2ef0c06a</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786330155</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Conjunto De Infusão">
  <data key="d0">Conjunto De Infusão</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The conjunto de infusão is the combined catheter and cannula set that is replaced regularly to prevent infection and blockage.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e796e8f4bb4721a269775c3d2ef0c06a</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786330155</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Baterias">
  <data key="d0">Baterias</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Baterias are the power source of insulin pumps, typically small button cells that drive the motor and electronics.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e796e8f4bb4721a269775c3d2ef0c06a</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786330155</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Agulha-Guia">
  <data key="d0">Agulha-Guia</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The agulha‑guia is a guiding needle that is withdrawn after catheter placement, leaving only the Teflon® cannula in the tissue.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e796e8f4bb4721a269775c3d2ef0c06a</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786330156</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cânula De Teflon®">
  <data key="d0">Cânula De Teflon®</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Cânula De Teflon® is a Teflon®‑coated cannula left in the subcutaneous tissue after the guiding needle is removed.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e796e8f4bb4721a269775c3d2ef0c06a</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786330156</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="MiniMed® 640G">
  <data key="d0">MiniMed® 640G</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">MiniMed® 640G is a Medtronic insulin pump model that can be paired with a glucose sensor, emits hypoglycemia alerts, and is not water‑proof.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e796e8f4bb4721a269775c3d2ef0c06a</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786330156</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="MiniMed Paradigm® Veo 754">
  <data key="d0">MiniMed Paradigm® Veo 754</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">MiniMed Paradigm® Veo 754 is a Medtronic insulin pump model compatible with continuous glucose sensors and hypoglycemia alerts.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e796e8f4bb4721a269775c3d2ef0c06a</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786330156</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="MiniMed 722">
  <data key="d0">MiniMed 722</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">MiniMed 722 is an older Medtronic insulin pump model that can be used with a glucose sensor from the same manufacturer.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e796e8f4bb4721a269775c3d2ef0c06a</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786330156</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Accu-Chek® Spirit">
  <data key="d0">Accu-Chek® Spirit</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Accu-Chek® Spirit is a Roche Diagnostics insulin pump model formerly commercialized in Brazil.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e796e8f4bb4721a269775c3d2ef0c06a</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786330156</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Accu-Chek® Spirit Combo">
  <data key="d0">Accu-Chek® Spirit Combo</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Accu-Chek® Spirit Combo is a Roche Diagnostics system that combines an insulin pump with a smart control glucometer and bolus calculator.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e796e8f4bb4721a269775c3d2ef0c06a</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786330156</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Roche Diagnostics">
  <data key="d0">Roche Diagnostics</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Roche Diagnostics is a manufacturer that supplies the Accu‑Chek® Spirit and Accu‑Chek® Spirit Combo insulin pumps in Brazil.&lt;SEP&gt;Roche Diagnostics is a company that provides consulting fees to author C.G.P. and advisory board membership to author I.H.B.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e796e8f4bb4721a269775c3d2ef0c06a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5419de5a030f812ab408ef47f361bebd</data>
