  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="DM2">
  <data key="d0">DM2</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">DM2 denotes type 2 diabetes mellitus, a chronic metabolic disorder characterized by insulin resistance and hyperglycemia. It is commonly abbreviated as DM2 in clinical and research literature to refer specifically to this form of diabetes, distinguishing it from type 1 diabetes and other glucose‑regulation conditions.

In clinical practice and guideline development, DM2 is referenced in several contexts. The National Institute for Health and Care Excellence (NICE) guidelines discuss DM2 when comparing the use of short‑acting insulin analogues (SICI) with multiple daily injections (MDI), noting that the appropriateness of SICI for patients with DM2 remains a debated topic. Similarly, discussions about hypoglycemia time‑target goals include DM2 as a patient subgroup for which specific targets may be considered.

DM2 also appears in the obstetric literature as part of pre‑gestational diabetes, indicating that women with type 2 diabetes who become pregnant are classified under this term. In the realm of clinical research, participants diagnosed with DM2 have been enrolled in major cardiovascular outcome trials such as ADVANCE, ACCORD, and the Veterans Affairs Diabetes Trial (VADT), underscoring the relevance of this population in evaluating therapeutic strategies and disease progression.&lt;SEP&gt;DM2, or type 2 diabetes, is the specific form of diabetes targeted for detection by various screening methods.&lt;SEP&gt;DM2 (type 2 diabetes mellitus) is referenced as the condition for which screening intervals are recommended and whose risk is increased by HIV infection and certain antiretroviral drugs.&lt;SEP&gt;DM2 refers to type 2 diabetes, a metabolic disorder associated with insulin resistance.&lt;SEP&gt;DM2 denotes type 2 diabetes mellitus, a metabolic form of diabetes associated with insulin resistance.&lt;SEP&gt;DM2 refers to Diabetes Mellitus type 2, classified when antibodies are negative and residual beta‑cell function is present.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6fba8ea0c6bdb8427804ba05f9fe49f9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-336a2f2c9b510e23c35be95e2ff7a72a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-276b766b8d515b1e7f388b5b7381bfbc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0e484a5a1df875be2e1525c8c64e2007&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9dee0a79e4583f41e757f9a20f56f397&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4f9624abde6cf128707fcc0466a4c9a7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d35e6caf612b4c4984ade9315ebc7431&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ad23b9b7ef0802d02c046415e54e3fcf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-23ad6eb7138be249f01b479174a34076&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-078f5907e86c2158587c79b26b0cd683&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c92d117f7109ea1ce6995f23bc680ce3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-858cd6ea7fba353827f5ab95be1157ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fee32f1fb0c848b0799071a86119b142</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/cgm.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/Orientacoes_Hipoglicemia_SBD_transcricao.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Metas glicêmicas/Metas no tratamento.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Diagnóstico de diabetes mellitus.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786373001</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="C-Peptide Positive">
  <data key="d0">C-Peptide Positive</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Positive C-peptide is a clinical marker mentioned as part of criteria for DM2 patients using insulin.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6fba8ea0c6bdb8427804ba05f9fe49f9</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf</data>
