<node id="Bergenstal RM">
  <data key="d0">Bergenstal RM</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Bergenstal RM is a prolific researcher and author in the field of diabetes technology and clinical management. He has contributed to a wide range of peer‑reviewed studies and consensus documents that address both type 1 and type 2 diabetes, with a particular focus on continuous glucose monitoring (CGM), insulin‑pump therapy, and automated insulin dosing systems.

In the type 1 diabetes arena, Bergenstal RM is listed as an author on a study evaluating the effectiveness of sensor‑augmented insulin‑pump therapy, as well as on a randomized controlled trial investigating threshold‑based insulin‑pump interruption (the ASPIRE In‑Home Study) published in the New England Journal of Medicine in 2013, which demonstrated reduced hypoglycaemia. He also co‑authored the analysis of the T1D Exchange Clinic Registry that examined how self‑monitoring frequency relates to HbA1c outcomes, and he contributed to a safety study of a hybrid closed‑loop system.

Bergenstal RM’s work extends to type 2 diabetes, where he is credited as a co‑author of a randomized controlled trial assessing automated insulin dosing guidance. His expertise in digital health is reflected in his co‑authorship of the consensus report “Diabetes Digital App Technology: Benefits, Challenges, and Recommendations,” and in the consensus recommendations for CGM data interpretation.

In addition to original research, Bergenstal RM has helped shape clinical practice guidelines. He co‑authored the 2012 Diabetes Care position statement on hyperglycemia management and the 2015 patient‑centered hyperglycemia management statement, both of which provide evidence‑based recommendations for clinicians managing elevated blood glucose in diabetes patients.&lt;SEP&gt;First author of the 2017 Ann Intern Med T1D Exchange Racial Differences Study on glucose‑A1c relationships.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-08f12a2de420625ccc88f737d06b7e84&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b50a9fb21c77773aec36a9b8e9f5e1d5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9e0c6a8245e883948688f77c2440ca4b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5ed3ce00d7a52cdffe7b550ffe0dd568&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e2be91fb7e754fe1c4357d221d0c50f9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f35eed8b49aa0b698012777f6ec96ce5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6db2125b1b94840ea29100039a6fef20&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-998bee92df7a33cd9c3ddc60144e14f1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-034c9e1f42f0eec15fed18c25580b0eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-acba683ee0809d1c3f6e35c228f485ac&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-84032013252fd71963ed381e09a3116d</data>
