<node id="Diabetes Mellitus Type 1 (DM1)">
  <data key="d0">Diabetes Mellitus Type 1 (DM1)</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">DM1 is an autoimmune form of diabetes requiring insulin therapy.&lt;SEP&gt;DM1 is an autoimmune form of diabetes characterized by insulin deficiency.&lt;SEP&gt;Diabetes Mellitus Type 1 (DM1) is a form of diabetes for which TIR, hypoglycemia, and hyperglycemia targets can be set.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-dfa23fc15cc4d520a32488843dbd710b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-277e136948d5572acf031988fd092dce&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-94150b57cc35a773b7c36f33f237f8a1</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/cgm.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786335242</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Multiple Daily Injections (MDI)">
  <data key="d0">Multiple Daily Injections (MDI)</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">MDI is a therapy regimen that administers insulin via several daily injections.&lt;SEP&gt;Multiple Daily Injections (MDI) is a delivery method for insulin that involves several injections per day.&lt;SEP&gt;Multiple Daily Injections (MDI) is a method of delivering insulin via several daily injections, often used alongside CGM.&lt;SEP&gt;Multiple daily injections (MDI) are an alternative diabetes treatment method compared with insulin pump therapy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-dfa23fc15cc4d520a32488843dbd710b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fd6fa98b7767319460b4a421a719c5c2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b3b81193a603a098b1ff9f6f0f665fec&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0fe1eff7b58582dec4c8ae7578e20e66</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/Insulinoterapia – Diretriz da Sociedade Brasileira de Diabetes – Ed. 2024.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/blood glucose monitoring.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786335858</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Diabetes Control and Complications Trial (DCCT)">
  <data key="d0">Diabetes Control and Complications Trial (DCCT)</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">DCCT is a clinical study that evaluated intensive insulin therapy, including MDI, in type 1 diabetes.&lt;SEP&gt;The DCCT was a clinical trial in which severe hypoglycemia was a major adverse effect of intensified insulin therapy.&lt;SEP&gt;A prospective randomized controlled trial comparing intensive (mean A1C ≈7%) versus standard (mean A1C ≈9%) glycemic control in people with type 1 diabetes, demonstrating benefits on microvascular outcomes.&lt;SEP&gt;A landmark clinical trial investigating intensive diabetes therapy and its impact on long‑term complications in insulin‑dependent diabetes mellitus.&lt;SEP&gt;The DCCT provides the reference assay to which A1C methods are standardized.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-dfa23fc15cc4d520a32488843dbd710b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b3b81193a603a098b1ff9f6f0f665fec&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-74ef8c063d84e34c44021aa138b9b903&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-54ce8d1437c0ec0329819123568df11e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3cc61bc2e95346d553972b4371912e7f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/blood glucose monitoring.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Metas glicêmicas/metas cuidado do diabetes.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377381</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
