<node id="Sociedade Brasileira De Diabetes">
  <data key="d0">Sociedade Brasileira De Diabetes</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Sociedade Brasileira de Diabetes (SBD), also referred to in English as the Brazilian Diabetes Society, is the principal professional organization in Brazil dedicated to the study, prevention, and management of diabetes mellitus.  

The society is responsible for developing and publishing a range of clinical recommendations and official guidelines that address various aspects of diabetes care. These include comprehensive guidelines on diabetes treatment, specific treatment‑goal recommendations, and protocols for the diagnosis and screening of diabetes mellitus. The SBD’s publications are frequently cited in national and international references, such as the hypoglycemia guidelines, underscoring its influence on diabetes practice standards.  

Among its clinical recommendations, the Sociedade Brasileira de Diabetes specifically endorses continuous insulin infusion (insulin pump therapy) as the primary treatment modality for small children diagnosed with type 1 diabetes, reflecting its commitment to evidence‑based, age‑appropriate therapeutic strategies.  

Through these activities, the Sociedade Brasileira de Diabetes serves as a key authority shaping diabetes management policies and clinical practice throughout Brazil.&lt;SEP&gt;Sociedade Brasileira De Diabetes is the Brazilian Diabetes Society that issues clinical guidelines.&lt;SEP&gt;Sociedade Brasileira De Diabetes is the professional organization that issues guidelines for diabetes classification in Brazil.&lt;SEP&gt;The Sociedade Brasileira de Diabetes is the Brazilian Diabetes Society that issues guidelines on diabetes classification.&lt;SEP&gt;Sociedade Brasileira De Diabetes is the Brazilian Diabetes Society that issues official guidelines on diabetes classification.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-51c7617f1e335789b870332231de4058&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ca8620e735c40bfe850134ccea9a7154&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ee7ecd9171c82c15f635a8a9b605621c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d0cc9dbb0b2eb4685ac17cfe445b7ce7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d35e6caf612b4c4984ade9315ebc7431&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c5c8fa42a8437c5708b04fb4ad1272cf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-343246c2eef6e8430b581340d6cd4762&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5e551f4b7f03919afc1d663b3b2a2efa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2e6267110f4ae5f4df4c49c0653a09b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e4adabacd09697393ca15fc999724c51&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-27380916f7cd2065a9c21259b0aa7868&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ed325288512881a80fa42dba504c4bff</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/Insulinoterapia – Diretriz da Sociedade Brasileira de Diabetes – Ed. 2024.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/Orientacoes_Hipoglicemia_SBD_transcricao.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Metas glicêmicas/Metas no tratamento.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Diagnóstico de diabetes mellitus.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf</data>
