<node id="Neonatal Diabetes">
  <data key="d0">Neonatal Diabetes</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Neonatal Diabetes is diabetes diagnosed in newborns or very early onset type 1 diabetes.&lt;SEP&gt;Neonatal Diabetes is a monogenic form of diabetes that presents in the newborn period.&lt;SEP&gt;Neonatal Diabetes is diabetes diagnosed within the first six months of life, requiring immediate genetic testing.&lt;SEP&gt;Neonatal diabetes is diabetes occurring under 6 months of age, also called congenital diabetes, often monogenic.&lt;SEP&gt;Neonatal diabetes is diabetes presenting in the first six months of life, caused by mutations such as KCNJ11, INS, ABCC8, and 6q24.&lt;SEP&gt;Neonatal Diabetes is a diabetes form discussed in relation to expanding gene lists for diagnosis.&lt;SEP&gt;Diabetes presenting in the first six months of life.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-277e136948d5572acf031988fd092dce&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-355eedbe74750d3739f7257279494c9a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9e1f69c1d604e82e14a23a29231bd587&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c83accc14a3b482690949ff04716a0aa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e4e7eef761aec994cc4558b2db5e1e08&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0bdb8ef335f3531317a3a5bd7de3a561&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f7b840a0b5327c5e583eb70dd354d1d0</data>
