<node id="Inhaled Insulin">
  <data key="d0">Inhaled Insulin</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Inhaled Insulin is a rapid‑acting, protein‑based form of insulin that is delivered to the systemic circulation through the pulmonary route using a specialized inhaler. It was the first inhaled protein‑based drug to receive regulatory approval in both the United States and Europe for the systemic treatment of diabetes, and it is commonly exemplified by the technosphere insulin formulation.

The pharmacokinetic profile of inhaled insulin is characterized by very fast absorption (“rapid on, rapid off”), which closely mimics the physiological burst of endogenous insulin that follows a meal. Because of this rapid onset and short duration, it is primarily used as a prandial (post‑meal) insulin to improve postprandial glucose control in individuals with type 1 or type 2 diabetes.

Clinical development of inhaled insulin has included numerous trials evaluating its efficacy, safety, and convenience for both type 1 and type 2 diabetes populations. These studies have examined its ability to lower postprandial glucose excursions, its dosing flexibility, and its impact on patient quality of life compared with traditional subcutaneous rapid‑acting insulins.

The therapeutic approach has also been the subject of scholarly review. Notably, J. S. Patton authored a comprehensive review article that discusses the historical development, clinical evidence, and practical considerations surrounding insulin administered by inhalation, summarizing the current state of knowledge and future directions for this delivery method.&lt;SEP&gt;Inhaled insulin is a form of insulin administered via inhalation for people who prefer to avoid injections.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-495ecc36cb3ac19034eacfd82aa72475&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-61a59544bbd02c2c82b13c7808f72c73&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e76c949a607724dd052d9fc4c7127a18&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3c9d162accf67a3761df6b1c9113e193&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2767372b4b5395439f542016058306a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d30bfc1840eec64224c3568470e6c539&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-516458dac1dbd08de0719a17162e4979&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-05cc642337c2a615c9b40de9336aec18</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/Inhaling medicines_ delivering drugs to the body through the lungs _ Nature Reviews Drug Discovery.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/cengiz-beck-2026-use-of-inhaled-insulin-with-automated-insulin-delivery-systems.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/insulina inalavel.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/blood glucose monitoring.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786335934</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="United States">
  <data key="d0">United States</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">United States

The United States is a major regulatory region that approved the use of inhaled insulin, and it is also the market where the inhaled product Afrezza is commercially available. In addition, the United States received approval for the Dexcom G6 continuous glucose monitoring system to be used for direct insulin decision‑making, reflecting its role in advancing diabetes technology.

Historically, the United States has been identified as one of the richest countries with a high prevalence of diabetes as early as 1920. It was the nation in which James Havens received the first insulin dose, and it is where Eli Lilly filed a U.S. patent related to insulin products. The country is also noted as the correspondence address in relevant scientific and regulatory communications.

The United States was the birthplace of the insulin infusion pump, which was originally developed and began diffusing throughout the country in the 1970s. Since then, geographical variations in pump therapy adoption have been observed across different regions of the United States, highlighting regional differences in the uptake of diabetes management technologies.&lt;SEP&gt;The United States is the geographic setting of the TID Exchange study on type 1 diabetes.&lt;SEP&gt;Country where part of the pediatric cohort study on autoantibodies was conducted.&lt;SEP&gt;United States is the country referenced in several diabetes screening studies.&lt;SEP&gt;United States is a country from which a pediatric cohort was studied for autoantibody positivity and type 1 diabetes risk.&lt;SEP&gt;The United States, referenced regarding the proportion of undiagnosed diabetes cases.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-495ecc36cb3ac19034eacfd82aa72475&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0ba3c49b467b6d37cd2aab29bf4a3119&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9043f44e67d9ed02b4864043d3cbb59a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-161a201d846100f42e643139469a1e6c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cbb54288f56e407604ea361f58e58233&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-08c7f7bb0209cabd75e27f9c8556c214&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b3b81193a603a098b1ff9f6f0f665fec&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-93594146e1ebe099cfc47906e940939f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7f716359c14483f9be36a73861d75008&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a05276c5db43e3a1e9f987056012750f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-343246c2eef6e8430b581340d6cd4762&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2a430bf53157529ccb22e67171fb28e5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9eb02ab1ab7d834858bf60a8b402e6ea</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/Inhaling medicines_ delivering drugs to the body through the lungs _ Nature Reviews Drug Discovery.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/The Discovery and Development.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/cengiz-beck-2026-use-of-inhaled-insulin-with-automated-insulin-delivery-systems.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/edelman-et-al-2026-dosing-afrezza-it-s-not-that-complicated.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/Documento sem título.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/blood glucose monitoring.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/monitoramento contínuo de glicose.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/glicemias capilares.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Diagnóstico de diabetes mellitus.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377409</data>
