</node>
<node id="Lungs">
  <data key="d0">Lungs</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">The lungs provide a highly permeable surface that enables rapid systemic delivery of both small‑molecule drugs and macromolecules.&lt;SEP&gt;The lungs are the organ where inhaled particles are deposited.&lt;SEP&gt;The lungs are the primary organ providing a large absorptive surface area and thin mucosal membrane for pulmonary drug delivery.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-495ecc36cb3ac19034eacfd82aa72475&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e337602a6f677dde49f4899bab5a07c9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-292ec5ef0e73074be4398f1729c06661</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/Inhaling medicines_ delivering drugs to the body through the lungs _ Nature Reviews Drug Discovery.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/insulina inalavel.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786333593</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Systemic Delivery">
  <data key="d0">Systemic Delivery</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Systemic delivery refers to delivering medicines into the bloodstream to achieve whole‑body therapeutic effect.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-495ecc36cb3ac19034eacfd82aa72475</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/Inhaling medicines_ delivering drugs to the body through the lungs _ Nature Reviews Drug Discovery.pdf</data>
