<node id="Subcutaneous Insulin">
  <data key="d0">Subcutaneous Insulin</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Subcutaneous insulin therapy is the conventional route of insulin administration used as a comparator in inhaled insulin clinical trials.&lt;SEP&gt;Subcutaneous Insulin refers to insulin administered under the skin, forming the basis of current Automated Insulin Delivery formulations.&lt;SEP&gt;Subcutaneous Insulin is insulin administered via injection, contrasted with inhaled Afrezza.&lt;SEP&gt;Subcutaneous insulin refers to insulin administered under the skin, used as a comparison unit for Afrezza dosing.&lt;SEP&gt;Subcutaneous insulin is the traditional injection route for insulin therapy, contrasted with Afrezza’s inhaled delivery.&lt;SEP&gt;Subcutaneous insulin is the traditional injectable insulin delivery method used for diabetes management.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-61a59544bbd02c2c82b13c7808f72c73&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3c9d162accf67a3761df6b1c9113e193&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4e6371d8083fb20b137912cdaeec1b8b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5419de5a030f812ab408ef47f361bebd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8644d98286c4a296063176435b45d589&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-70c5a1107fcc9b632361d9c52064f45d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/Inhaling medicines_ delivering drugs to the body through the lungs _ Nature Reviews Drug Discovery.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/cengiz-beck-2026-use-of-inhaled-insulin-with-automated-insulin-delivery-systems.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/edelman-et-al-2026-dosing-afrezza-it-s-not-that-complicated.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786333248</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Macromolecule Absorption by the Lungs">
  <data key="d0">Macromolecule Absorption by the Lungs</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Macromolecule absorption by the lungs describes mechanisms by which large molecules traverse the pulmonary epithelium into systemic circulation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-61a59544bbd02c2c82b13c7808f72c73</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/Inhaling medicines_ delivering drugs to the body through the lungs _ Nature Reviews Drug Discovery.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786330912</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Reproducibility in Normal and Diabetic Subjects">
  <data key="d0">Reproducibility in Normal and Diabetic Subjects</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Reproducibility in Normal and Diabetic Subjects is a study published in Diabetes (1983) examining measurement consistency in both populations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-61a59544bbd02c2c82b13c7808f72c73</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/Inhaling medicines_ delivering drugs to the body through the lungs _ Nature Reviews Drug Discovery.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786330912</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
