<node id="Particle Transport System">
  <data key="d0">Particle Transport System</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The system moves inhaled particles deposited in the lungs up and out into the oesophagus where material is coughed up or swallowed.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e337602a6f677dde49f4899bab5a07c9</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/Inhaling medicines_ delivering drugs to the body through the lungs _ Nature Reviews Drug Discovery.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786330914</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Oesophagus">
  <data key="d0">Oesophagus</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">The oesophagus is the organ through which particles are expelled from the lungs by coughing or swallowing.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e337602a6f677dde49f4899bab5a07c9</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/Inhaling medicines_ delivering drugs to the body through the lungs _ Nature Reviews Drug Discovery.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786330914</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Pulmonary Macrophages">
  <data key="d0">Pulmonary Macrophages</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Pulmonary macrophages are scavenger cells in the lung derived from monocytes that help keep the lungs clean and can produce inflammatory mediators.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e337602a6f677dde49f4899bab5a07c9</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/Inhaling medicines_ delivering drugs to the body through the lungs _ Nature Reviews Drug Discovery.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786330914</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Monocytes">
  <data key="d0">Monocytes</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Monocytes are circulating cells that give rise to pulmonary macrophages in the lung.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e337602a6f677dde49f4899bab5a07c9</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/Inhaling medicines_ delivering drugs to the body through the lungs _ Nature Reviews Drug Discovery.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786330914</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Transporters">
  <data key="d0">Transporters</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Transporters are proteins embedded in plasma membranes that facilitate the absorption of small or large molecules.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e337602a6f677dde49f4899bab5a07c9</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/Inhaling medicines_ delivering drugs to the body through the lungs _ Nature Reviews Drug Discovery.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786330915</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Tight Junctions">
  <data key="d0">Tight Junctions</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Tight junctions are a complex molecular apparatus that enables cell adhesion in epithelial and endothelial sheets and restricts solute diffusion between cells.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e337602a6f677dde49f4899bab5a07c9</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/Inhaling medicines_ delivering drugs to the body through the lungs _ Nature Reviews Drug Discovery.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786330915</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Transcytosis">
  <data key="d0">Transcytosis</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Transcytosis is the transport of material through cell layers via the cytoplasm, often using caveoli.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e337602a6f677dde49f4899bab5a07c9</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/Inhaling medicines_ delivering drugs to the body through the lungs _ Nature Reviews Drug Discovery.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786330915</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Caveoli">
  <data key="d0">Caveoli</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Caveoli are plasma‑membrane vesicles that enable transcytosis by carrying bound material across the cell and can fuse with the plasma membrane to release cargo.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e337602a6f677dde49f4899bab5a07c9</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/Inhaling medicines_ delivering drugs to the body through the lungs _ Nature Reviews Drug Discovery.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786330915</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Monodisperse Particles">
  <data key="d0">Monodisperse Particles</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Monodisperse particles are aerosol particles that are all the same size.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e337602a6f677dde49f4899bab5a07c9</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/Inhaling medicines_ delivering drugs to the body through the lungs _ Nature Reviews Drug Discovery.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786330915</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Octanol–Water Partition Coefficients">
  <data key="d0">Octanol–Water Partition Coefficients</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Octanol–water partition coefficients are the equilibrium ratio of drug concentrations between water and octanol, reflecting lipophilicity.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e337602a6f677dde49f4899bab5a07c9</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/Inhaling medicines_ delivering drugs to the body through the lungs _ Nature Reviews Drug Discovery.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786330915</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="First‑Pass Metabolism">
  <data key="d0">First‑Pass Metabolism</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">First‑pass metabolism is the reduction of intact drug passage into systemic circulation by enzymes in the gastrointestinal wall and liver, and is low for inhaled small‑molecule drugs.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e337602a6f677dde49f4899bab5a07c9</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/Inhaling medicines_ delivering drugs to the body through the lungs _ Nature Reviews Drug Discovery.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786330915</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
