  <data key="d0">Aerosol Delivery</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Aerosol delivery refers to the method of delivering drugs to the body through the lungs.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d4c5bc67580e092cf1b0f395c39326f1</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/Inhaling medicines_ delivering drugs to the body through the lungs _ Nature Reviews Drug Discovery.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786330921</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Differential Permeability">
  <data key="d0">Differential Permeability</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Differential permeability describes the varying passage of substances across endothelial and epithelial barriers.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d4c5bc67580e092cf1b0f395c39326f1</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/Inhaling medicines_ delivering drugs to the body through the lungs _ Nature Reviews Drug Discovery.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786330921</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Endothelial Barrier">
  <data key="d0">Endothelial Barrier</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The endothelial barrier is one of the tissue layers examined for permeability to albumin flux.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d4c5bc67580e092cf1b0f395c39326f1</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/Inhaling medicines_ delivering drugs to the body through the lungs _ Nature Reviews Drug Discovery.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786330921</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Epithelial Barrier">
  <data key="d0">Epithelial Barrier</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The epithelial barrier is examined alongside the endothelial barrier for permeability to albumin flux.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d4c5bc67580e092cf1b0f395c39326f1</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/Inhaling medicines_ delivering drugs to the body through the lungs _ Nature Reviews Drug Discovery.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786330921</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Albumin Flux">
  <data key="d0">Albumin Flux</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Albumin flux is the transport of albumin across biological barriers studied in the differential permeability paper.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d4c5bc67580e092cf1b0f395c39326f1</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/Inhaling medicines_ delivering drugs to the body through the lungs _ Nature Reviews Drug Discovery.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786330921</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Tracheal Epithelial Permeability">
  <data key="d0">Tracheal Epithelial Permeability</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Tracheal epithelial permeability to nonelectrolytes and species differences is the focus of a cited study.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d4c5bc67580e092cf1b0f395c39326f1</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/Inhaling medicines_ delivering drugs to the body through the lungs _ Nature Reviews Drug Discovery.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786330921</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Nonelectrolytes">
  <data key="d0">Nonelectrolytes</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Nonelectrolytes are the solutes whose permeability across tracheal epithelium was investigated.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d4c5bc67580e092cf1b0f395c39326f1</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/Inhaling medicines_ delivering drugs to the body through the lungs _ Nature Reviews Drug Discovery.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786330921</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Solute Flux">
  <data key="d0">Solute Flux</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Solute flux in the airways was investigated mechanistically to distinguish diffusive and carrier‑mediated transport.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d4c5bc67580e092cf1b0f395c39326f1</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/Inhaling medicines_ delivering drugs to the body through the lungs _ Nature Reviews Drug Discovery.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786330921</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Pulmonary Delivery">
  <data key="d0">Pulmonary Delivery</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Pulmonary delivery is discussed as a route for administering macromolecules and fusion proteins to the lung.&lt;SEP&gt;Pulmonary delivery is a route of administration that targets the lungs for drug absorption.&lt;SEP&gt;Pulmonary delivery denotes the administration of therapeutics via the respiratory tract, a recurring theme across the referenced works.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d4c5bc67580e092cf1b0f395c39326f1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-72d17b623cb9a58c2a50eac2ea814699&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-516458dac1dbd08de0719a17162e4979</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/Inhaling medicines_ delivering drugs to the body through the lungs _ Nature Reviews Drug Discovery.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/insulina inalavel.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786333588</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
