<node id="Basal‑Bolus Strategy">
  <data key="d0">Basal‑Bolus Strategy</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Basal‑bolus strategy is an insulin therapy approach that combines basal and prandial insulin to mimic normal insulin secretion.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fd6fa98b7767319460b4a421a719c5c2</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/Insulinoterapia – Diretriz da Sociedade Brasileira de Diabetes – Ed. 2024.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786331389</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Continuous Subcutaneous Insulin Infusion (SICI)">
  <data key="d0">Continuous Subcutaneous Insulin Infusion (SICI)</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Continuous Subcutaneous Insulin Infusion (SICI) is an insulin pump method that provides continuous basal insulin delivery.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fd6fa98b7767319460b4a421a719c5c2</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/Insulinoterapia – Diretriz da Sociedade Brasileira de Diabetes – Ed. 2024.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786331390</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Ketoacidosis Diabética">
  <data key="d0">Ketoacidosis Diabética</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Ketoacidosis Diabética (CAD) is a severe complication of DM1 marked by ketone body accumulation, metabolic acidosis, and hyperglycemia.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fd6fa98b7767319460b4a421a719c5c2</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/Insulinoterapia – Diretriz da Sociedade Brasileira de Diabetes – Ed. 2024.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786331390</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Catecholamines">
  <data key="d0">Catecholamines</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Catecholamines are counter‑regulatory hormones that increase during insulin deficiency.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fd6fa98b7767319460b4a421a719c5c2</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/Insulinoterapia – Diretriz da Sociedade Brasileira de Diabetes – Ed. 2024.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786331390</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cortisol">
  <data key="d0">Cortisol</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Cortisol is a stress hormone that rises as a counter‑regulatory substance in DM1.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fd6fa98b7767319460b4a421a719c5c2</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/Insulinoterapia – Diretriz da Sociedade Brasileira de Diabetes – Ed. 2024.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786331390</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Glargina U100">
  <data key="d0">Glargina U100</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Glargina U100 is a long‑acting insulin analogue produced by recombinant DNA technology, used for basal insulinization.&lt;SEP&gt;Glargina U100 is a long‑acting basal insulin analog listed in the Brazilian insulin formulation table.&lt;SEP&gt;Glargina U100 is a long‑acting insulin analog presented with a duration range of 20‑24h.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fd6fa98b7767319460b4a421a719c5c2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-65cd86aee374fd1ea91bb4fd5ebee2a7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9d86d36b30e6f5b8ff44caade2d2400d</data>
