<node id="Mortality">
  <data key="d0">Mortality</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Mortality refers to death from any cause and is commonly expressed as a death rate or risk of death within a defined population. In diabetes research, mortality is used as a primary outcome measure to assess the impact of disease characteristics, treatment strategies, and complications.

In type 1 diabetes, mortality has been examined by comparing death rates in the DCCT/EDIC cohort with those of the general population, highlighting differences in survival between trial participants and broader community samples. Large cardiovascular outcome trials such as ACCORD and ADVANCE have also reported all‑cause mortality, noting that intensive glycemic‑control arms experienced higher death rates. These trials identified a specific association between level 3 (severe) hypoglycemia and increased mortality, and further analyses have linked mortality risk to patterns of severe hypoglycaemia and longitudinal HbA1c trends.

Mortality is similarly a key endpoint in studies of cystic fibrosis‑related diabetes (CFRD). Individuals with CFRD exhibit a higher risk of death compared with non‑diabetic counterparts, although longitudinal data indicate that mortality rates for people with CFRD have declined substantially over recent decades.

Across epidemiological investigations, mortality serves as a standardized outcome to quantify overall survival, compare sub‑populations, and evaluate the safety and effectiveness of therapeutic interventions in diabetes and related conditions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e7e6ca9bf63e843b814736c0409c70fb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a5f7cad1fb0e1a0a02f63b5928b8acd2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d0cc9dbb0b2eb4685ac17cfe445b7ce7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fc59aba81df88fe020f6e1d93d9e403b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e668c40e3bc21d982ed03a052f0f9339&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-acba683ee0809d1c3f6e35c228f485ac&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-38ab5af7e42588297df4330ffb2c046b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9cdf6af658e42c2f4f7dca5e4dbdd3db&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-55e58732610596ce9a8f3145d34f75a7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9eb02ab1ab7d834858bf60a8b402e6ea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0631ff2b95dd459677eaaebe9283a776</data>
