  <data key="d2">Nocturnal hypoglycaemia is low blood glucose occurring during sleep, a concern in pediatric diabetes management.&lt;SEP&gt;Nocturnal hypoglycaemia is a nighttime low‑blood‑glucose event discussed as an outcome reduced by certain insulin therapies.</data>
