<node id="Comparative Trial">
  <data key="d0">Comparative Trial</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Comparative trial is a study design that directly compares two treatments, such as insulin glargine versus NPH insulin in children.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e7e6ca9bf63e843b814736c0409c70fb</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/Insulinoterapia – Diretriz da Sociedade Brasileira de Diabetes – Ed. 2024.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786331411</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Insulin Basal Dose">
  <data key="d0">Insulin Basal Dose</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Insulin basal dose is the portion of daily insulin provided continuously to maintain basal glycaemia in patients.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0f272d1c9c38e2a6b6d02b5aa66809e1</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/Insulinoterapia – Diretriz da Sociedade Brasileira de Diabetes – Ed. 2024.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786331411</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Insulin Bolus Dose">
  <data key="d0">Insulin Bolus Dose</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Insulin bolus dose is the portion of insulin administered around meals, adjusted according to pre‑meal glucose and carbohydrate intake.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0f272d1c9c38e2a6b6d02b5aa66809e1</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/Insulinoterapia – Diretriz da Sociedade Brasileira de Diabetes – Ed. 2024.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786331411</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Daily Insulin Total (DTI)">
  <data key="d0">Daily Insulin Total (DTI)</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Daily Insulin Total is the total insulin amount used in the formula that derives the carbohydrate ratio.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0f272d1c9c38e2a6b6d02b5aa66809e1</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/Insulinoterapia – Diretriz da Sociedade Brasileira de Diabetes – Ed. 2024.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786331411</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Sensitivity Factor (FS)">
  <data key="d0">Sensitivity Factor (FS)</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Sensitivity Factor represents how much 1 unit of prandial insulin lowers glucose, calculated by dividing a constant (e.g., 2000) by the Daily Total Dose.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0f272d1c9c38e2a6b6d02b5aa66809e1</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/Insulinoterapia – Diretriz da Sociedade Brasileira de Diabetes – Ed. 2024.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786331411</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Long‑Acting Insulin Analogs">
  <data key="d0">Long‑Acting Insulin Analogs</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Long‑acting insulin analogs are insulin formulations with prolonged action recommended for basal insulin therapy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0f272d1c9c38e2a6b6d02b5aa66809e1</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/Insulinoterapia – Diretriz da Sociedade Brasileira de Diabetes – Ed. 2024.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786331412</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Ultra‑Long‑Acting Insulin Analogs">
  <data key="d0">Ultra‑Long‑Acting Insulin Analogs</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Ultra‑long‑acting insulin analogs are insulin formulations with very prolonged action considered for basal insulin in patients at high risk of hypoglycaemia.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0f272d1c9c38e2a6b6d02b5aa66809e1</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/Insulinoterapia – Diretriz da Sociedade Brasileira de Diabetes – Ed. 2024.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786331412</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Ultra‑Rapid Insulin Analogs">
  <data key="d0">Ultra‑Rapid Insulin Analogs</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Ultra‑rapid insulin analogs are ultra‑fast insulin formulations that can be administered after meals when intake is uncertain.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0f272d1c9c38e2a6b6d02b5aa66809e1</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/Insulinoterapia – Diretriz da Sociedade Brasileira de Diabetes – Ed. 2024.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786331412</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Post‑Meal Administration">
  <data key="d0">Post‑Meal Administration</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Post‑Meal Administration describes the practice of giving insulin after the start of a meal.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0f272d1c9c38e2a6b6d02b5aa66809e1</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/Insulinoterapia – Diretriz da Sociedade Brasileira de Diabetes – Ed. 2024.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786331413</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Effective Glycemic Control">
  <data key="d0">Effective Glycemic Control</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Effective Glycemic Control denotes the achievement of stable blood glucose levels suitable for patient health.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0f272d1c9c38e2a6b6d02b5aa66809e1</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/Insulinoterapia – Diretriz da Sociedade Brasileira de Diabetes – Ed. 2024.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786331413</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Recommendation R1">
  <data key="d0">Recommendation R1</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">R1 recommends initiating insulin therapy immediately after a clinical diagnosis of Type 1 Diabetes to prevent metabolic decompensation and ketoacidosis.&lt;SEP&gt;Recommendation R1 advises a HbA1c target below 7.0% for all individuals with diabetes to prevent microvascular complications without severe hypoglycemia.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0f272d1c9c38e2a6b6d02b5aa66809e1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6d83801272f7a0ae0d797d60572fe578</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/Insulinoterapia – Diretriz da Sociedade Brasileira de Diabetes – Ed. 2024.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Metas glicêmicas/Metas no tratamento.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786370024</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Recommendation R4">
  <data key="d0">Recommendation R4</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">R4 advises that long‑acting insulin analogs be considered for basal insulin because they show lower glycaemic variability and fewer nocturnal hypoglycaemic episodes than NPH insulin.&lt;SEP&gt;Guideline recommendation to consider HbA1c &lt; 8 % for elderly patients with diabetes under specific conditions.&lt;SEP&gt;Recommendation R4 advises elderly individuals with functional compromise or frailty to aim for HbA1c below 8.0%.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0f272d1c9c38e2a6b6d02b5aa66809e1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6d83801272f7a0ae0d797d60572fe578&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c5c8fa42a8437c5708b04fb4ad1272cf</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/Insulinoterapia – Diretriz da Sociedade Brasileira de Diabetes – Ed. 2024.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Metas glicêmicas/Metas no tratamento.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786370024</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Recommendation R5">
  <data key="d0">Recommendation R5</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">R5 states that ultra‑long‑acting insulin analogs may be considered for basal insulin in individuals with increased risk of hypoglycaemia due to their lower incidence of such events.&lt;SEP&gt;Guideline recommendation to consider HbA1c &lt; 7.5 % for children and adolescents with type 1 diabetes under specific conditions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0f272d1c9c38e2a6b6d02b5aa66809e1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c5c8fa42a8437c5708b04fb4ad1272cf</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/Insulinoterapia – Diretriz da Sociedade Brasileira de Diabetes – Ed. 2024.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Metas glicêmicas/Metas no tratamento.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786370041</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Recommendation R6">
  <data key="d0">Recommendation R6</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">R6 recommends using rapid‑acting or ultra‑rapid insulin analogs in basal‑bolus schemes to reduce the risk of hypoglycaemia.&lt;SEP&gt;Guideline recommendation defining fasting (80‑130 mg/dL) and 2‑hour post‑prandial (&lt;180 mg/dL) capillary glucose targets.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0f272d1c9c38e2a6b6d02b5aa66809e1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c5c8fa42a8437c5708b04fb4ad1272cf</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/Insulinoterapia – Diretriz da Sociedade Brasileira de Diabetes – Ed. 2024.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Metas glicêmicas/Metas no tratamento.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786370041</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Recommendation R7">
  <data key="d0">Recommendation R7</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">R7 recommends administering prandial insulin before each meal because it achieves better post‑prandial glucose control than injection after meal onset.&lt;SEP&gt;Guideline recommendation that Time In Range should be above 70 % for non‑pregnant patients with type 1 diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0f272d1c9c38e2a6b6d02b5aa66809e1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c5c8fa42a8437c5708b04fb4ad1272cf</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/Insulinoterapia – Diretriz da Sociedade Brasileira de Diabetes – Ed. 2024.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Metas glicêmicas/Metas no tratamento.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786370041</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Recommendation R8">
  <data key="d0">Recommendation R8</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">R8 allows the use of ultra‑rapid insulin after meals when there is uncertainty about food intake, offering advantages over rapid‑acting analogs.&lt;SEP&gt;Guideline recommendation limiting hypoglycemia level 1 (&lt;70 mg/dL) to &lt;4 % and level 2 (&lt;54 mg/dL) to &lt;1 % for non‑pregnant type 1 diabetes patients, measured via CGM.&lt;SEP&gt;Recommendation R8 advises that for non‑pregnant DM1 patients, time in hypoglycemia Level 1 should be &lt;4% and Level 2 &lt;1%, measured by CGM devices.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0f272d1c9c38e2a6b6d02b5aa66809e1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6d83801272f7a0ae0d797d60572fe578&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c5c8fa42a8437c5708b04fb4ad1272cf</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/Insulinoterapia – Diretriz da Sociedade Brasileira de Diabetes – Ed. 2024.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Metas glicêmicas/Metas no tratamento.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786370024</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Recommendation R9">
  <data key="d0">Recommendation R9</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">R9 recommends continuous subcutaneous insulin infusion as an effective therapeutic option when glycaemic targets cannot be reached with multiple daily injections.&lt;SEP&gt;Guideline recommendation that glycemic variability coefficient should be &lt;36 % for non‑pregnant type 1 diabetes patients, measured via CGM or capillary glucose.&lt;SEP&gt;Recommendation R9 advises that for non‑pregnant DM1 patients, glucose coefficient of variation should be &lt;36%, measured by CGM or capillary glucose.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0f272d1c9c38e2a6b6d02b5aa66809e1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6d83801272f7a0ae0d797d60572fe578&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c5c8fa42a8437c5708b04fb4ad1272cf</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/Insulinoterapia – Diretriz da Sociedade Brasileira de Diabetes – Ed. 2024.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Metas glicêmicas/Metas no tratamento.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786370025</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Recommendation R10">
  <data key="d0">Recommendation R10</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">R10 recommends periodic re‑evaluation of insulin doses to avoid clinical inertia in treatment.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0f272d1c9c38e2a6b6d02b5aa66809e1</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/Insulinoterapia – Diretriz da Sociedade Brasileira de Diabetes – Ed. 2024.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786331414</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Insulin Dose Reevaluation">
  <data key="d0">Insulin Dose Reevaluation</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Insulin Dose Reevaluation is the periodic review of insulin dosage to adjust therapy according to evolving patient needs.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0f272d1c9c38e2a6b6d02b5aa66809e1</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/Insulinoterapia – Diretriz da Sociedade Brasileira de Diabetes – Ed. 2024.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786331414</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Recommendation R2">
  <data key="d0">Recommendation R2</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">R2 recommends using insulin therapy regimens that mimic natural insulin secretion to achieve age‑appropriate glycemic control goals.&lt;SEP&gt;Recommendation R2 advises a HbA1c target below 7.0% for all individuals with diabetes to prevent macrovascular complications without severe hypoglycemia.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0f272d1c9c38e2a6b6d02b5aa66809e1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6d83801272f7a0ae0d797d60572fe578</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/Insulinoterapia – Diretriz da Sociedade Brasileira de Diabetes – Ed. 2024.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Metas glicêmicas/Metas no tratamento.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786370024</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Recommendation R3">
  <data key="d0">Recommendation R3</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">R3 advises intensive therapy with basal and prandial insulin, using multiple daily injections or continuous subcutaneous insulin infusion for individuals with Type 1 Diabetes.&lt;SEP&gt;Recommendation R3 advises elderly individuals with preserved cognition to aim for HbA1c between 7.0% and 7.5%.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0f272d1c9c38e2a6b6d02b5aa66809e1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6d83801272f7a0ae0d797d60572fe578</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/Insulinoterapia – Diretriz da Sociedade Brasileira de Diabetes – Ed. 2024.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Metas glicêmicas/Metas no tratamento.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786370024</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Insulin Therapy Regimens">
  <data key="d0">Insulin Therapy Regimens</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Insulin therapy regimens describe planned schedules and types of insulin used to replicate physiological insulin patterns.&lt;SEP&gt;Insulin therapy regimens describe the structured use of basal and bolus insulin to manage diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0f272d1c9c38e2a6b6d02b5aa66809e1</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/Insulinoterapia – Diretriz da Sociedade Brasileira de Diabetes – Ed. 2024.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786331415</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Pre‑Meal Glycemia">
  <data key="d0">Pre‑Meal Glycemia</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Pre‑Meal Glycemia is the blood glucose measurement taken before eating, used to adjust insulin bolus dose.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0f272d1c9c38e2a6b6d02b5aa66809e1</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/Insulinoterapia – Diretriz da Sociedade Brasileira de Diabetes – Ed. 2024.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786331415</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Fasting Glycemia">
  <data key="d0">Fasting Glycemia</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Fasting Glycemia is the blood glucose level measured after an overnight fast, used to adjust insulin basal dose.&lt;SEP&gt;Fasting glycemia is a metric measuring blood glucose after a period without food, used to assess diabetes control.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0f272d1c9c38e2a6b6d02b5aa66809e1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2d8f17f3f250a37a1effaaa88cc8b382</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/Insulinoterapia – Diretriz da Sociedade Brasileira de Diabetes – Ed. 2024.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/glicemias capilares.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786338525</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Fast‑acting Insulin Aspart">
  <data key="d0">Fast‑acting Insulin Aspart</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Fast‑acting insulin aspart is a formulation of insulin aspart designed to improve glycemic control in basal‑bolus therapy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f9416e8076c17175db0dbb12c3393566</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/Insulinoterapia – Diretriz da Sociedade Brasileira de Diabetes – Ed. 2024.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786331415</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Inhaled Technosphere Insulin">
  <data key="d0">Inhaled Technosphere Insulin</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Inhaled technosphere insulin is an inhaled prandial insulin compared with injected prandial insulin in type 1 diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f9416e8076c17175db0dbb12c3393566</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/Insulinoterapia – Diretriz da Sociedade Brasileira de Diabetes – Ed. 2024.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786331415</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="EDITION 4 Trial">
  <data key="d0">EDITION 4 Trial</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">EDITION 4 is a randomized, phase 3a, open‑label clinical trial comparing insulin glargine 300 U/mL with insulin glargine 100 U/mL in people with type 1 diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f9416e8076c17175db0dbb12c3393566</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/Insulinoterapia – Diretriz da Sociedade Brasileira de Diabetes – Ed. 2024.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786331416</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="BEGIN Basal‑Bolus Type 1 Trial">
  <data key="d0">BEGIN Basal‑Bolus Type 1 Trial</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">BEGIN basal‑bolus type 1 is a phase 3, randomised, open‑label, treat‑to‑target non‑inferiority trial comparing insulin degludec with insulin glargine in basal‑bolus treatment.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f9416e8076c17175db0dbb12c3393566</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/Insulinoterapia – Diretriz da Sociedade Brasileira de Diabetes – Ed. 2024.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786331416</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="SWITCH 1 Trial">
  <data key="d0">SWITCH 1 Trial</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">SWITCH 1 is a randomized clinical trial evaluating the effect of insulin degludec versus insulin glargine U100 on hypoglycaemia in patients with type 1 diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f9416e8076c17175db0dbb12c3393566</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/Insulinoterapia – Diretriz da Sociedade Brasileira de Diabetes – Ed. 2024.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786331416</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="BEGIN: Flex T1 Trial">
  <data key="d0">BEGIN: Flex T1 Trial</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">BEGIN: Flex T1 is a 26‑week randomized, treat‑to‑target trial with a 26‑week extension comparing flexible‑dose insulin degludec with insulin glargine in type 1 diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f9416e8076c17175db0dbb12c3393566</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/Insulinoterapia – Diretriz da Sociedade Brasileira de Diabetes – Ed. 2024.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786331416</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="STAT Study">
  <data key="d0">STAT Study</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">STAT is a study investigating improved postprandial glucose with inhaled technosphere insulin compared with insulin aspart in patients with type 1 diabetes on multiple daily injections.&lt;SEP&gt;STAT Study is a clinical trial that compared inhaled technosphere insulin with insulin aspart in type 1 diabetes patients.&lt;SEP&gt;Trial showing improved postprandial glucose with inhaled Technosphere insulin compared with insulin aspart in type 1 diabetes patients on multiple daily injections.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f9416e8076c17175db0dbb12c3393566&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d30bfc1840eec64224c3568470e6c539&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a0e51dec97ab970bbc2f21878a8735ed</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/Insulinoterapia – Diretriz da Sociedade Brasileira de Diabetes – Ed. 2024.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/cengiz-beck-2026-use-of-inhaled-insulin-with-automated-insulin-delivery-systems.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/edelman-et-al-2026-dosing-afrezza-it-s-not-that-complicated.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786333236</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hypoglycaemia">
  <data key="d0">Hypoglycaemia</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Hypoglycaemia denotes low blood glucose episodes, a key safety outcome in insulin trials.&lt;SEP&gt;Hypoglycaemia is a low blood sugar side effect of insulin therapy, causing symptoms such as shakiness and confusion.&lt;SEP&gt;Low blood‑glucose episodes that are reduced with Technosphere insulin use compared with insulin aspart.&lt;SEP&gt;Hypoglycaemia is a condition of low blood glucose, central to many cited studies examining its risks, treatment, and outcomes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f9416e8076c17175db0dbb12c3393566&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-06425d1f80d868bd58871b6a6e740102&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a0e51dec97ab970bbc2f21878a8735ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-acba683ee0809d1c3f6e35c228f485ac</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/Insulinoterapia – Diretriz da Sociedade Brasileira de Diabetes – Ed. 2024.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/Understanding insulin - International Diabetes Federation.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/edelman-et-al-2026-dosing-afrezza-it-s-not-that-complicated.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Metas glicêmicas/metas cuidado do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786372153</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Basal‑bolus Treatment">
  <data key="d0">Basal‑bolus Treatment</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Basal‑bolus treatment is an insulin regimen combining long‑acting basal insulin with rapid‑acting bolus insulin for glucose control in type 1 diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f9416e8076c17175db0dbb12c3393566</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/Insulinoterapia – Diretriz da Sociedade Brasileira de Diabetes – Ed. 2024.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786331417</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Postprandial Insulin">
  <data key="d0">Postprandial Insulin</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Postprandial insulin is a dose of insulin given after a meal to mitigate the rise in blood glucose.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f9416e8076c17175db0dbb12c3393566</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/Insulinoterapia – Diretriz da Sociedade Brasileira de Diabetes – Ed. 2024.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786331417</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Preprandial Insulin">
  <data key="d0">Preprandial Insulin</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Preprandial insulin is a dose of insulin administered before a meal to prevent post‑meal hyperglycaemia.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f9416e8076c17175db0dbb12c3393566</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/Insulinoterapia – Diretriz da Sociedade Brasileira de Diabetes – Ed. 2024.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786331417</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Pre-Mixed Insulins">
  <data key="d0">Pre-Mixed Insulins</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Pre-Mixed Insulins are formulations that combine basal and prandial insulin components in fixed ratios.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-494fef0b8efc2c44b3b49ebf9d74b7f2</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/Insulinoterapia – Diretriz da Sociedade Brasileira de Diabetes – Ed. 2024.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786331418</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
