<node id="Glycosuria">
  <data key="d0">Glycosuria</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Glycosuria is the condition of glucose in urine that Banting hoped to relieve by isolating the pancreatic internal secretion.&lt;SEP&gt;Glycosuria is the presence of glucose in urine, mentioned as a condition related to diabetes.&lt;SEP&gt;Glycosuria is the presence of sugar in the urine, noted to almost disappear following pancreatic extract therapy.&lt;SEP&gt;Glycosuria is the presence of glucose in urine, detected by tests such as Benedict's Test.&lt;SEP&gt;Presence of glucose in urine, a reason for referral of about 50% of type 2 diabetes cases to specialized services.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-172719b5694ed1fb8003b6874395d641&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-01bb90c243340c22c0d25864008eb9d5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c53f6d8d7aad59b28e557f5971d0d828&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2d8f17f3f250a37a1effaaa88cc8b382&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-343246c2eef6e8430b581340d6cd4762</data>
