<node id="Charles Best">
  <data key="d0">Charles Best</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Charles Best is a 4th‑year student assigned by Macleod to assist Banting in testing blood sugar and conducting surgeries on dogs.&lt;SEP&gt;Charles Best is a researcher who worked closely with Frederick Banting on pancreatic extract experiments and dog trials.&lt;SEP&gt;Charles Best is a Canadian medical researcher who worked with Sir Frederick Banting on the discovery of insulin.&lt;SEP&gt;Charles Best was a researcher who worked with Banting on insulin and was a signatory of the 1922 Connaught agreement.&lt;SEP&gt;Charles Best was a researcher who worked with Frederick Banting on pancreatic extract and performed self‑injections to test safety.&lt;SEP&gt;Charles Best was placed in charge of insulin development, purification, and production at Connaught and participated in patent correspondence.&lt;SEP&gt;Charles Best was a researcher who collaborated with Frederick Banting on the pioneering insulin experiments.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0ba3c49b467b6d37cd2aab29bf4a3119&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9043f44e67d9ed02b4864043d3cbb59a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9c2889fe850f241cf3ebb528da2adbb1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-047566df22e783e662966eb52799cb39&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ad5d126f417014eb5c7a07a85db48d1d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c53f6d8d7aad59b28e557f5971d0d828&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0932e9c21a330869629b3fa70d2e1f5e</data>
