<node id="University of Toronto">
  <data key="d0">University of Toronto</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">The University of Toronto is the academic institution where the landmark insulin research of Frederick Banting and Charles Best was carried out. The work began in the spring of 1921 within the university’s Medical Building, under the supervision of John J. R. Macleod, who served as head of the Department of Physiology. The physiology department, led by Macleod, directed the pancreatic‑extract investigations that ultimately led to the discovery of insulin.

The university’s research infrastructure played a central role in the project. It housed the Connaught Antitoxin Laboratories—later known as Connaught Medical Research Laboratories—and the Pharmacology Department, where Banting held a lecturer position. These facilities provided the laboratory space, technical expertise, and collaborative environment that supported the insulin experiments and subsequent development work.

Beyond the laboratory, the University of Toronto managed the intellectual‑property and commercial aspects of the discovery. It retained worldwide patent rights to insulin and, on 28 June 1922, signed an exclusive production agreement with Eli Lilly and Company, granting the firm the right to manufacture insulin for distribution while the university oversaw licensing and royalty arrangements.

The institution also established an Insulin Committee to coordinate ongoing research, production, and clinical application, and it is frequently cited in historical accounts of the insulin breakthrough. Through its combined roles in scientific research, education, laboratory collaboration, and patent management, the University of Toronto was instrumental in transforming insulin from a laboratory finding into a widely available therapeutic product.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-eff48c1408719e81f1f423f76dfd19e5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-172719b5694ed1fb8003b6874395d641&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0ba3c49b467b6d37cd2aab29bf4a3119&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-247d0735bf59962683d382203243d395&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9043f44e67d9ed02b4864043d3cbb59a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8c80fa00c2f059f9425a4ef62c162b1c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9c2889fe850f241cf3ebb528da2adbb1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-047566df22e783e662966eb52799cb39&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-01bb90c243340c22c0d25864008eb9d5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ad5d126f417014eb5c7a07a85db48d1d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-47acdaf58d4f121a3948976c07c3d03c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c53f6d8d7aad59b28e557f5971d0d828&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-17a38cd3b50722f2d9ae2a618121bb61</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/The Discovery and Development.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786332079</data>
