  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The Discovery Goes Public denotes the period when insulin was announced to the public and made widely available.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0ba3c49b467b6d37cd2aab29bf4a3119</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/The Discovery and Development.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786332080</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Frederick G. Banting">
  <data key="d0">Frederick G. Banting</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Dr. Frederick G. Banting was a 28‑year‑old researcher who conceptualized a novel experiment to isolate the pancreas’s internal secretion as a treatment for diabetes, recorded the idea in a notebook, and later met with John J. R. Macleod.&lt;SEP&gt;Frederick G. Banting was a researcher who, together with Charles H. Best, performed pancreatic extract experiments in December 1921.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-247d0735bf59962683d382203243d395&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-01bb90c243340c22c0d25864008eb9d5</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/The Discovery and Development.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786332080</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Charles H. Best">
  <data key="d0">Charles H. Best</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Charles H. Best was a researcher who collaborated with Frederick G. Banting on pancreatic extract studies in 1921.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-247d0735bf59962683d382203243d395</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/The Discovery and Development.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786332080</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="J. J. R. Macleod">
  <data key="d0">J. J. R. Macleod</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">J. J. R. Macleod was the senior physiologist who supervised the pancreatic extract project and invited James Bertram Collip to join the team.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-247d0735bf59962683d382203243d395</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/The Discovery and Development.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786332080</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="James Bertram Collip">
  <data key="d0">James Bertram Collip</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">James Bertram Collip was a biochemist who joined the pancreatic extract research team and refined the extract using evaporation and filtration.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-247d0735bf59962683d382203243d395</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/The Discovery and Development.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786332080</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Joseph Gilchrist">
  <data key="d0">Joseph Gilchrist</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Joseph Gilchrist was a physician with diabetes who was given pancreatic extract via a stomach tube in an experimental treatment.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-247d0735bf59962683d382203243d395</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/The Discovery and Development.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786332080</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="George H. A. Clowes">
  <data key="d0">George H. A. Clowes</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">George H. A. Clowes was the research director of Eli Lilly and Company who traveled to New Haven to attend the American Physiological Society meeting.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-247d0735bf59962683d382203243d395</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/The Discovery and Development.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786332081</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Dog #35">
  <data key="d0">Dog #35</data>
  <data key="d1">creature</data>
  <data key="d2">Dog #35 is a diabetic dog that received an injection of extract prepared from its own pancreas, leading to a blood sugar reduction.&lt;SEP&gt;Dog #35 was a laboratory dog whose pancreas was removed and later injected with its own pancreatic extract, resulting in a drop in blood sugar.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-247d0735bf59962683d382203243d395&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-047566df22e783e662966eb52799cb39</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/The Discovery and Development.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786332081</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Toronto General Hospital">
  <data key="d0">Toronto General Hospital</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Toronto General Hospital was the facility where James Bertram Collip conducted purification of the pancreatic extract.&lt;SEP&gt;Toronto General Hospital was the medical facility where diabetic patients received pancreatic extract treatment.&lt;SEP&gt;Toronto General Hospital is the medical facility in Toronto where Leonard Thompson was treated with insulin extracts.&lt;SEP&gt;Toronto General Hospital is the Toronto medical facility where Charlotte Clarke was admitted in July 1922.&lt;SEP&gt;Toronto General Hospital (TGH) is a hospital where, by December 1922, fifty diabetic patients were successfully treated with insulin.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-247d0735bf59962683d382203243d395&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8c80fa00c2f059f9425a4ef62c162b1c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ad5d126f417014eb5c7a07a85db48d1d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c53f6d8d7aad59b28e557f5971d0d828&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-17a38cd3b50722f2d9ae2a618121bb61</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/The Discovery and Development.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786332081</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="American Physiological Society">
  <data key="d0">American Physiological Society</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">American Physiological Society organized the thirty‑fourth annual meeting in New Haven where the insulin discoveries were presented.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-247d0735bf59962683d382203243d395</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/The Discovery and Development.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786332081</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="New Haven, Connecticut">
  <data key="d0">New Haven, Connecticut</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">New Haven, Connecticut was the city that hosted the American Physiological Society’s thirty‑fourth annual meeting in late December 1921.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-247d0735bf59962683d382203243d395</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/The Discovery and Development.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786332082</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Pancreatic Extract">
  <data key="d0">Pancreatic Extract</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Pancreatic Extract is the substance prepared from removed dog pancreas tissue and injected into diabetic dogs.&lt;SEP&gt;Pancreatic extract is the biological preparation derived from animal pancreas intended to reduce blood sugar in diabetic subjects.&lt;SEP&gt;Pancreatic Extract was a solution prepared from animal pancreas used experimentally to lower blood sugar in diabetic subjects.&lt;SEP&gt;Pancreatic extract is a medical preparation derived from the pancreas that was used to treat diabetic patients and demonstrated therapeutic effectiveness.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-247d0735bf59962683d382203243d395&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9c2889fe850f241cf3ebb528da2adbb1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-047566df22e783e662966eb52799cb39&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c53f6d8d7aad59b28e557f5971d0d828</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/The Discovery and Development.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786332082</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Alcohol Extraction Method">
  <data key="d0">Alcohol Extraction Method</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Alcohol extraction method is a technique used by Banting and Best to remove impurities from pancreatic extract solutions.&lt;SEP&gt;Alcohol Extraction Method was the technique Banting and Best used to obtain pancreatic extract from pancreas tissue.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-247d0735bf59962683d382203243d395&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-047566df22e783e662966eb52799cb39</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/The Discovery and Development.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786332082</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Vacuum Still Evaporation">
  <data key="d0">Vacuum Still Evaporation</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Vacuum Still Evaporation was the process Collip employed to partially remove alcohol from the extract solution.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-247d0735bf59962683d382203243d395</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/The Discovery and Development.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786332082</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Filtration">
  <data key="d0">Filtration</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Filtration was applied after evaporation to further purify the pancreatic extract.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-247d0735bf59962683d382203243d395</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/The Discovery and Development.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786332082</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Stomach Tube Administration">
  <data key="d0">Stomach Tube Administration</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Stomach Tube Administration was the route used to give pancreatic extract to Dr. Joseph Gilchrist.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-247d0735bf59962683d382203243d395</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/The Discovery and Development.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786332083</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Blood Sugar Level Data">
  <data key="d0">Blood Sugar Level Data</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Blood Sugar Level Data recorded the drop from .38 to .18 in Dog #35 four hours after extract injection.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-247d0735bf59962683d382203243d395</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/The Discovery and Development.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786332083</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Urine Sugar-Free Finding">
  <data key="d0">Urine Sugar-Free Finding</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Urine Sugar-Free Finding reported that dogs treated with the extract produced urine free of sugar and ketones.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-247d0735bf59962683d382203243d395</data>
