<node id="National Cancer Institute">
  <data key="d0">National Cancer Institute</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">National Cancer Institute is the organization referenced in the caption of Dr. George H. A. Clowes’s 1917 photograph.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-247d0735bf59962683d382203243d395</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/The Discovery and Development.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786332084</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Internal Pancreatic Secretion">
  <data key="d0">Internal Pancreatic Secretion</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Internal Pancreatic Secretion refers to the hormone secreted by the pancreas that regulates carbohydrate metabolism, identified through the pancreatic extract research.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-247d0735bf59962683d382203243d395</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/The Discovery and Development.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786332084</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Robert Falconer">
  <data key="d0">Robert Falconer</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Robert Falconer served as president of the University of Toronto and received a letter from the insulin research team concerning patent protection.&lt;SEP&gt;Robert Falconer served as the President of the University of Toronto and advised on securing a patent for the insulin extraction method.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9043f44e67d9ed02b4864043d3cbb59a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c53f6d8d7aad59b28e557f5971d0d828</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/The Discovery and Development.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786332084</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Frederick Banting">
  <data key="d0">Frederick Banting</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Frederick Banting was a physician‑researcher and medical scientist who played a central role in the discovery and early clinical use of insulin. In the early 1920s he secured a lecturer position in the Pharmacology Department at the University of Toronto, where he led experiments on pancreatic extracts and coordinated a research team that included Charles Best and several other collaborators.

Working together with Best, Banting conducted the pivotal experiments that led to the isolation of a pancreatic extract capable of lowering blood glucose. In 1921 he demonstrated the extract’s therapeutic potential by sustaining a diabetic dog through injections of canine pancreas extract. The success of these animal studies quickly progressed to human trials; Banting administered the first insulin preparations to patients such as Charlotte Clarke, Elizabeth Hughes, and Elsie Needham, and he consulted with contemporaries including Dr. Gladys Boyd to refine treatment protocols.

Banting’s contributions extended beyond the laboratory. He co‑discovered insulin, presented the findings publicly, and was instrumental in delivering the new therapy to early patients in the United States. In 1922 he participated in the agreement with the Connaught Laboratories that facilitated large‑scale production and distribution of insulin, and he allowed his name to be included on the patent application describing the Toronto pancreatic extract, thereby securing intellectual recognition for the work.

Through his combined roles as researcher, educator, clinician, and advocate, Frederick Banting helped transform diabetes from a fatal disease into a manageable condition, laying the foundation for modern endocrinology and the widespread use of insulin therapy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9043f44e67d9ed02b4864043d3cbb59a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8c80fa00c2f059f9425a4ef62c162b1c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-047566df22e783e662966eb52799cb39&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ad5d126f417014eb5c7a07a85db48d1d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c53f6d8d7aad59b28e557f5971d0d828&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-17a38cd3b50722f2d9ae2a618121bb61&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0932e9c21a330869629b3fa70d2e1f5e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2d8f17f3f250a37a1effaaa88cc8b382</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/The Discovery and Development.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/Understanding insulin - International Diabetes Federation.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/glicemias capilares.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786338533</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
