<node id="Elizabeth Hughes">
  <data key="d0">Elizabeth Hughes</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Elizabeth Hughes is an 11‑year‑old diabetic, daughter of a U.S. secretary of state, who arrived in Toronto in August 1922 and received insulin treatment from Frederick Banting, leading to rapid health improvement.&lt;SEP&gt;A patient highlighted in histories of insulin discovery and featured prominently in the book “Breakthrough…”.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9043f44e67d9ed02b4864043d3cbb59a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-17a38cd3b50722f2d9ae2a618121bb61</data>
