  <data key="d0">August Krogh</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">August Krogh is a Nobel Prize–winning biomedical scientist who visited Toronto in fall 1922 to learn about insulin.&lt;SEP&gt;August Krogh is a professor who co‑established the Nordisk Insulin Laboratory, served as the first chair of the Nordisk Insulin Foundation, and received the 1920 Nobel Prize in Medicine.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8c80fa00c2f059f9425a4ef62c162b1c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-47acdaf58d4f121a3948976c07c3d03c</data>
