</node>
<node id="J.J.R. Macleod">
  <data key="d0">J.J.R. Macleod</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">J.J.R. Macleod is a senior researcher who supervised the laboratory work and provided instructions for preparing pancreatic extract.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9c2889fe850f241cf3ebb528da2adbb1</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/The Discovery and Development.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786332090</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Medical Building at the University of Toronto">
  <data key="d0">Medical Building at the University of Toronto</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">Medical Building at the University of Toronto is the facility that housed the physiology department’s animal operating room used for the experiments.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9c2889fe850f241cf3ebb528da2adbb1</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/The Discovery and Development.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786332090</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Pancreatic Diabetes">
  <data key="d0">Pancreatic Diabetes</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Pancreatic Diabetes is the disease that the researchers aimed to treat through pancreatic extract.&lt;SEP&gt;Pancreatic diabetes refers to a form of diabetes that the pancreatic extract aimed to treat by reducing blood sugar.&lt;SEP&gt;Pancreatic diabetes is a form of diabetes resulting from exocrine pancreatic dysfunction, also called type 3c diabetes or pancreoprivic diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9c2889fe850f241cf3ebb528da2adbb1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-047566df22e783e662966eb52799cb39&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-090b8f9281aa75054311d8f275a2c8f8</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/The Discovery and Development.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377267</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Pancreatectomy">
  <data key="d0">Pancreatectomy</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Pancreatectomy is the surgical removal of the pancreas performed on experimental dogs.&lt;SEP&gt;Pancreatectomy is a surgical removal of the pancreas mentioned as a scenario where insulin pumps may be indicated.&lt;SEP&gt;Pancreatectomy is a surgical removal of pancreatic tissue mentioned as an etiology of pancreatic diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9c2889fe850f241cf3ebb528da2adbb1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9cd925790899146eeb8a373879b5feac&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-090b8f9281aa75054311d8f275a2c8f8</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/The Discovery and Development.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/blood glucose monitoring.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377268</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Duct Ligation">
  <data key="d0">Duct Ligation</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Duct Ligation is a surgical procedure on the pancreatic ducts of dogs that was attempted during the experiments.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9c2889fe850f241cf3ebb528da2adbb1</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/The Discovery and Development.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786332090</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Dog #387">
  <data key="d0">Dog #387</data>
  <data key="d1">creature</data>
  <data key="d2">Dog #387 is an experimental canine that underwent a successful pancreatic operation but later died on 1 June 1921.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9c2889fe850f241cf3ebb528da2adbb1</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/The Discovery and Development.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786332090</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Dog #391">
  <data key="d0">Dog #391</data>
  <data key="d1">creature</data>
  <data key="d2">Dog #391 is an experimental canine from which a degenerated pancreas was removed to prepare the first pancreatic extract.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9c2889fe850f241cf3ebb528da2adbb1</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/The Discovery and Development.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786332090</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Dog #410">
  <data key="d0">Dog #410</data>
  <data key="d1">creature</data>
  <data key="d2">Dog #410 is the first canine to receive an injection of pancreatic extract, later dying after entering a diabetic coma.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9c2889fe850f241cf3ebb528da2adbb1</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/The Discovery and Development.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786332090</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="17 May 1921">
  <data key="d0">17 May 1921</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">17 May 1921 is the date of the first pancreatectomy performed on a dog, lasting about 80 minutes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9c2889fe850f241cf3ebb528da2adbb1</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/The Discovery and Development.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786332090</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="28 May 1921">
  <data key="d0">28 May 1921</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">28 May 1921 is the date when an operation on Dog #387 proved successful.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9c2889fe850f241cf3ebb528da2adbb1</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/The Discovery and Development.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786332091</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="July 1921">
  <data key="d0">July 1921</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">July 1921 is the period when the researchers discovered many duct ligations had failed.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9c2889fe850f241cf3ebb528da2adbb1</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/The Discovery and Development.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786332091</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="30 July 1921">
  <data key="d0">30 July 1921</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">30 July 1921 is the date when the first pancreatic extract was prepared and injected into Dog #410.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9c2889fe850f241cf3ebb528da2adbb1</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/The Discovery and Development.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786332091</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="1 August 1921">
  <data key="d0">1 August 1921</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">1 August 1921 is the date when Banting administered pancreatic extract to Dog #406 while it was in a coma.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9c2889fe850f241cf3ebb528da2adbb1</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/The Discovery and Development.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786332091</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="London">
  <data key="d0">London</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">London is the city from which Dr. Banting departed before traveling to Toronto for his research.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9c2889fe850f241cf3ebb528da2adbb1</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/The Discovery and Development.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786332091</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="John J.R. Macleod">
  <data key="d0">John J.R. Macleod</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">John J.R. Macleod is a senior researcher who provided laboratory space, retroactive pay, and cautioned Banting and Best about overconfidence.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-047566df22e783e662966eb52799cb39</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/The Discovery and Development.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786332091</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Dr. John G. Fitzgerald">
  <data key="d0">Dr. John G. Fitzgerald</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Dr. John G. Fitzgerald is the director of the Connaught Antitoxin Laboratories at the University of Toronto, with whom Banting connected to test pancreatic duct ligation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-047566df22e783e662966eb52799cb39</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/The Discovery and Development.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786332091</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Dr. N.B. Taylor">
  <data key="d0">Dr. N.B. Taylor</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Dr. N.B. Taylor is a researcher who suggested a longevity experiment using the pancreatic extract on a diabetic dog.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-047566df22e783e662966eb52799cb39</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/The Discovery and Development.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786332091</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Pharmacology Department">
  <data key="d0">Pharmacology Department</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Pharmacology Department is the department at the University of Toronto where Banting secured a special lecturer position.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-047566df22e783e662966eb52799cb39</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/The Discovery and Development.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786332091</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Pancreatic Duct Ligation Procedure">
  <data key="d0">Pancreatic Duct Ligation Procedure</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Pancreatic duct ligation procedure is an experimental technique attempted on a calf to isolate internal secretion, which failed when the calf died.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-047566df22e783e662966eb52799cb39</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/The Discovery and Development.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786332092</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Dog #27">
  <data key="d0">Dog #27</data>
  <data key="d1">creature</data>
  <data key="d2">Dog #27 is a diabetic dog that received pancreatic extract, causing its blood sugar to fall and urine to become sugar‑free.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-047566df22e783e662966eb52799cb39</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/The Discovery and Development.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786332092</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Dog #33 Marjorie">
  <data key="d0">Dog #33 Marjorie</data>
  <data key="d1">creature</data>
  <data key="d2">Dog #33, named Marjorie, is a diabetic dog that received pancreatic extract and participated in longevity experiments.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-047566df22e783e662966eb52799cb39</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/The Discovery and Development.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786332092</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Dog #23">
  <data key="d0">Dog #23</data>
  <data key="d1">creature</data>
  <data key="d2">Dog #23 is a diabetic dog that received pancreatic extract prepared with the alcohol extraction method.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-047566df22e783e662966eb52799cb39</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/The Discovery and Development.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786332092</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Alliston, Ontario">
  <data key="d0">Alliston, Ontario</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">Alliston, Ontario is the hometown where Banting recalled helping slaughter cattle on his father's farm, inspiring his idea for extract preparation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-047566df22e783e662966eb52799cb39</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/The Discovery and Development.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786332092</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="30th Birthday of Banting">
  <data key="d0">30th Birthday of Banting</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">Banting’s 30th birthday on 14 November 1921 was marked by a talk given by Banting and Best to the Journal Club of the Department of Physiology.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-047566df22e783e662966eb52799cb39</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/The Discovery and Development.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786332092</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Journal Club of the Department of Physiology">
  <data key="d0">Journal Club of the Department of Physiology</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">Journal Club of the Department of Physiology is a meeting where Banting and Best presented their work and received a suggestion from Dr. N.B. Taylor.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-047566df22e783e662966eb52799cb39</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/The Discovery and Development.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786332092</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Self‑Injection of Extract">
  <data key="d0">Self‑Injection of Extract</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">On 23 November 1921 Banting and Best each injected themselves with a small dose of pancreatic extract, observing no adverse reaction.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-047566df22e783e662966eb52799cb39</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/The Discovery and Development.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786332093</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Longevity Experiment Suggestion">
  <data key="d0">Longevity Experiment Suggestion</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">A suggestion made by Dr. N.B. Taylor to conduct a longevity experiment by regularly administering extract to a diabetic dog.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-047566df22e783e662966eb52799cb39</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/The Discovery and Development.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786332093</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="1 October 1921 Lecturer Appointment">
  <data key="d0">1 October 1921 Lecturer Appointment</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">On 1 October 1921 Banting secured a special lecturer position in the Pharmacology Department with a salary of $250 per month.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-047566df22e783e662966eb52799cb39</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/The Discovery and Development.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786332093</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="4 October 1921 Connection with Fitzgerald">
  <data key="d0">4 October 1921 Connection with Fitzgerald</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">On 4 October 1921 Banting met Dr. John G. Fitzgerald to discuss testing pancreatic duct ligation on a calf.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-047566df22e783e662966eb52799cb39</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/The Discovery and Development.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786332093</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="16 November 1921 Extract Preparation">
  <data key="d0">16 November 1921 Extract Preparation</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">On 16 November 1921 Banting and Best procured foetal calf pancreases, prepared extract, and administered it to Dog #27.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-047566df22e783e662966eb52799cb39</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/The Discovery and Development.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786332093</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="7 December 1921 Alcohol Extract Administration">
  <data key="d0">7 December 1921 Alcohol Extract Administration</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">On 7 December 1921 Dogs Marjorie and #23 received extract prepared with the alcohol extraction method.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-047566df22e783e662966eb52799cb39</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/The Discovery and Development.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786332093</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="8 December 1921 Additional Alcohol Extraction">
  <data key="d0">8 December 1921 Additional Alcohol Extraction</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">On 8 December 1921 Banting and Best removed the pancreas from Dog #35 and prepared extract using the alcohol extraction method.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-047566df22e783e662966eb52799cb39</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/The Discovery and Development.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786332093</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="11 December 1921 Dog #35 Injection">
  <data key="d0">11 December 1921 Dog #35 Injection</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">On 11 December 1921 Dog #35 was injected with extract made from its own pancreas, reducing its blood sugar level.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-047566df22e783e662966eb52799cb39</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/The Discovery and Development.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786332093</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
