</node>
<node id="YouTube">
  <data key="d0">YouTube</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">YouTube hosts a digitized home recording of the full “Glory Enough For All” min‑series.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-01bb90c243340c22c0d25864008eb9d5</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/The Discovery and Development.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786332095</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Internal Secretion of the Pancreas">
  <data key="d0">Internal Secretion of the Pancreas</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The internal secretion of the pancreas refers to the hormone later identified as insulin, which Banting sought to isolate.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-01bb90c243340c22c0d25864008eb9d5</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/The Discovery and Development.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786332095</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Dog">
  <data key="d0">Dog</data>
  <data key="d1">creature</data>
  <data key="d2">Dogs were the experimental animals mentioned in Banting’s note for ligating pancreatic ducts.&lt;SEP&gt;Dog was the animal on which the whole beef pancreas extract potency was tested.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-01bb90c243340c22c0d25864008eb9d5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ad5d126f417014eb5c7a07a85db48d1d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/The Discovery and Development.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786332095</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Acini">
  <data key="d0">Acini</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Acini are the pancreatic tissue units whose degeneration leaves islets, as described in Banting’s experimental plan.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-01bb90c243340c22c0d25864008eb9d5</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/The Discovery and Development.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786332095</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Islets">
  <data key="d0">Islets</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Islets refer to clusters of pancreatic cells that remain after acini degeneration, targeted in Banting’s experiment.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-01bb90c243340c22c0d25864008eb9d5</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/The Discovery and Development.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786332095</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Notebook">
  <data key="d0">Notebook</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Banting recorded his compelling idea in a notebook during the night of 31 October 1920.&lt;SEP&gt;Notebook is a physical book used to manually log glucose values, measurement time, and symptoms.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-01bb90c243340c22c0d25864008eb9d5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-545c19428427ece2c838e352e759e388</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/The Discovery and Development.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/Documento sem título.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1786336917</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="31 October 1920">
  <data key="d0">31 October 1920</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">On 31 October 1920 in London, Ontario, Frederick G. Banting experienced his original insight into isolating the pancreatic internal secretion.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-01bb90c243340c22c0d25864008eb9d5</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/The Discovery and Development.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786332096</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="7 November 1920">
  <data key="d0">7 November 1920</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">On 7 November 1920 in Toronto, Banting met with John J. R. Macleod to discuss his pancreatic extract idea.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-01bb90c243340c22c0d25864008eb9d5</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/The Discovery and Development.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786332096</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Spring 1921">
  <data key="d0">Spring 1921</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">In spring 1921 Banting traveled to the University of Toronto to commence his insulin research with Macleod’s support.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-01bb90c243340c22c0d25864008eb9d5</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/The Discovery and Development.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786332096</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="11 March 1921">
  <data key="d0">11 March 1921</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">On 11 March 1921 a discussion addressed “the problem of Pancreatic Diabetes,” reflecting ongoing research.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-01bb90c243340c22c0d25864008eb9d5</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/The Discovery and Development.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786332096</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Connaught Research">
  <data key="d0">Connaught Research</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Connaught Research is a research unit of the University of Toronto that hosts a historical article about Frederick G. Banting.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-01bb90c243340c22c0d25864008eb9d5</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/The Discovery and Development.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786332096</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="The Discovery and Early Development of Insulin">
  <data key="d0">The Discovery and Early Development of Insulin</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">“The Discovery and Early Development of Insulin” is a University of Toronto archival collection referenced in Banting’s notes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-01bb90c243340c22c0d25864008eb9d5</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/The Discovery and Development.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786332096</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Dr. George Clowes">
  <data key="d0">Dr. George Clowes</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Dr. George Clowes was the director of research at Eli Lilly &amp; Co in Indianapolis who offered collaboration on the pancreatic extract.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ad5d126f417014eb5c7a07a85db48d1d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/The Discovery and Development.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786332096</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Eli Lilly &amp; Co">
  <data key="d0">Eli Lilly &amp; Co</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Eli Lilly &amp; Co is a pharmaceutical company based in Indianapolis that proposed to help develop the pancreatic extract.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ad5d126f417014eb5c7a07a85db48d1d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/The Discovery and Development.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786332096</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Toronto Star">
  <data key="d0">Toronto Star</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Toronto Star is a newspaper that published Greenaway’s article on the progress toward a diabetes cure.&lt;SEP&gt;Toronto Star is a newspaper that reported on the insulin discovery and published press coverage beginning 14 January 1922.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ad5d126f417014eb5c7a07a85db48d1d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c53f6d8d7aad59b28e557f5971d0d828</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/The Discovery and Development.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786332097</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Pancreatic Ducts">
  <data key="d0">Pancreatic Ducts</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Pancreatic ducts are anatomical structures whose ligation leads to degeneration of the pancreas used in early extract experiments.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ad5d126f417014eb5c7a07a85db48d1d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/The Discovery and Development.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786332097</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Neutral Extract">
  <data key="d0">Neutral Extract</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Neutral extract is a low‑temperature, faintly acidic preparation from the degenerated pancreas that reduced blood sugar when injected.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ad5d126f417014eb5c7a07a85db48d1d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/The Discovery and Development.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786332097</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Whole Beef Pancreas Extract">
  <data key="d0">Whole Beef Pancreas Extract</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Whole beef pancreas extract is a preparation developed by Charles Best using a vacuum still method to test potency on a dog.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ad5d126f417014eb5c7a07a85db48d1d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/The Discovery and Development.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786332097</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Macleods Serum">
  <data key="d0">Macleods Serum</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Macleod’s serum is the name given to the pancreatic extract administered to Leonard Thompson on 11 January 1922.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ad5d126f417014eb5c7a07a85db48d1d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/The Discovery and Development.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786332097</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Collips Extract">
  <data key="d0">Collips Extract</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Collip’s extract is the purified insulin preparation created by James Collip and used successfully on Leonard Thompson on 23 January 1922.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ad5d126f417014eb5c7a07a85db48d1d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/The Discovery and Development.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786332097</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Rectal Injection">
  <data key="d0">Rectal Injection</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Rectal injection is a method mentioned as ineffective for delivering the pancreatic extract.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ad5d126f417014eb5c7a07a85db48d1d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/The Discovery and Development.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786332098</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Alkaline Incubation">
  <data key="d0">Alkaline Incubation</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Alkaline incubation is a laboratory procedure that neutralizes the extract’s effect when performed for two hours with pancreatic juice.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ad5d126f417014eb5c7a07a85db48d1d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/The Discovery and Development.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786332098</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Vacuum Still Method">
  <data key="d0">Vacuum Still Method</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Vacuum still method is a technique developed by James Collip to concentrate pancreatic extract.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ad5d126f417014eb5c7a07a85db48d1d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/The Discovery and Development.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786332098</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Ringers Solution">
  <data key="d0">Ringers Solution</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Ringer’s solution is an ice‑cold physiological solution used to extract the degenerated gland.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ad5d126f417014eb5c7a07a85db48d1d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/The Discovery and Development.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786332098</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hemoglobin">
  <data key="d0">Hemoglobin</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Hemoglobin is the blood protein whose estimations were unchanged before and after extract administration.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ad5d126f417014eb5c7a07a85db48d1d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/The Discovery and Development.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786332098</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Degenerated Gland">
  <data key="d0">Degenerated Gland</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Degenerated gland is the pancreatic tissue that became atrophic after duct ligation and was used for extract preparation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ad5d126f417014eb5c7a07a85db48d1d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/The Discovery and Development.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786332098</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cold Storage">
  <data key="d0">Cold Storage</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Cold storage refers to keeping the neutral extract at low temperature to preserve its potency.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ad5d126f417014eb5c7a07a85db48d1d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/The Discovery and Development.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786332098</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Alcohol Concentration">
  <data key="d0">Alcohol Concentration</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Alcohol concentration denotes the percentage of alcohol used by Collip to isolate the pure internal secretion.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ad5d126f417014eb5c7a07a85db48d1d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/The Discovery and Development.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786332099</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Abscess">
  <data key="d0">Abscess</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Abscess is the local infection that formed at an injection site following administration of Macleod’s serum.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ad5d126f417014eb5c7a07a85db48d1d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/The Discovery and Development.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786332099</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Press Coverage">
  <data key="d0">Press Coverage</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">Press coverage is the media reporting that began on 14 January 1922 about the insulin discovery.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ad5d126f417014eb5c7a07a85db48d1d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/The Discovery and Development.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786332099</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Formal Photograph">
  <data key="d0">Formal Photograph</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Formal photograph is the 1930 image documenting Leonard Thompson.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ad5d126f417014eb5c7a07a85db48d1d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/The Discovery and Development.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786332099</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Therapeutic Effect">
  <data key="d0">Therapeutic Effect</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Therapeutic effect describes the reduction of blood sugar and glycosuria achieved by insulin extracts.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ad5d126f417014eb5c7a07a85db48d1d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/The Discovery and Development.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786332099</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Elsie">
  <data key="d0">Elsie</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Elsie is a patient who experienced fever, delirium, and regained consciousness after several days of hospital treatment.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-47acdaf58d4f121a3948976c07c3d03c</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/The Discovery and Development.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786332100</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Isoelectric Point Precipitation and Purification Process">
  <data key="d0">Isoelectric Point Precipitation and Purification Process</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The isoelectric point precipitation and purification process is a technique used to purify insulin during large-scale production.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-47acdaf58d4f121a3948976c07c3d03c</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/The Discovery and Development.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786332100</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Clowes">
  <data key="d0">Clowes</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Clowes was the research director at Eli Lilly who wrote to Macleod expressing interest in large‑scale insulin extract production.&lt;SEP&gt;Clowes is an individual who discussed insulin distribution with the University of Toronto Insulin Committee.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-47acdaf58d4f121a3948976c07c3d03c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c53f6d8d7aad59b28e557f5971d0d828</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/The Discovery and Development.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786332100</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="University of Toronto Insulin Committee">
  <data key="d0">University of Toronto Insulin Committee</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">The University of Toronto Insulin Committee oversaw insulin distribution, media relations, and patent applications in 1922.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-47acdaf58d4f121a3948976c07c3d03c</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/The Discovery and Development.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786332100</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Marie Krogh">
  <data key="d0">Marie Krogh</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Marie Krogh is a scientist, diabetic, and wife of August Krogh who participated in the insulin collaboration.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-47acdaf58d4f121a3948976c07c3d03c</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/The Discovery and Development.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786332100</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="October 14 1922 Toronto Star Article">
  <data key="d0">October 14 1922 Toronto Star Article</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">The October 14 1922 article in the Toronto Star focused on media attention and described insulin as a “certain cure.”</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-47acdaf58d4f121a3948976c07c3d03c</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/The Discovery and Development.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786332100</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="October 1 1922 Plant Operation">
  <data key="d0">October 1 1922 Plant Operation</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">On October 1 1922 Eli Lilly’s new large‑scale insulin production plant began operation using a novel purification method.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-47acdaf58d4f121a3948976c07c3d03c</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/The Discovery and Development.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786332100</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Fall 1922 Krogh Visit">
  <data key="d0">Fall 1922 Krogh Visit</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">In fall 1922 August and Marie Krogh visited Toronto to learn about insulin discovery, development, and purification.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-47acdaf58d4f121a3948976c07c3d03c</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/The Discovery and Development.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786332100</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="October 20 1922 Committee Statement">
  <data key="d0">October 20 1922 Committee Statement</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">On October 20 1922 the University of Toronto Insulin Committee issued an official statement detailing its patent application for insulin.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-47acdaf58d4f121a3948976c07c3d03c</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/The Discovery and Development.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786332100</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="December 7 1922 Insulin Revival Press">
  <data key="d0">December 7 1922 Insulin Revival Press</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">On December 7 1922 press coverage highlighted cases where insulin injections revived a child in Edmonton and a teenager in New York City.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-47acdaf58d4f121a3948976c07c3d03c</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/The Discovery and Development.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786332100</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Edmonton">
  <data key="d0">Edmonton</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">Edmonton is a Canadian city where insulin revived an eight‑year‑old girl in 1922.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-47acdaf58d4f121a3948976c07c3d03c</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/The Discovery and Development.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786332100</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="New York City">
  <data key="d0">New York City</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
