<node id="Afrezza">
  <data key="d0">Afrezza</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Afrezza is the commercial brand name for an inhaled insulin product that delivers recombinant human regular insulin in a dry‑powder form using Technosphere® insulin particles (TI microparticles) for pulmonary absorption. The formulation consists of insulin bound to these microparticles, allowing rapid uptake through the lungs and a short‑acting pharmacologic profile.

Designed for prandial (mealtime) glucose control in people with diabetes, Afrezza provides a rapid onset of action and a brief duration of effect, which helps to blunt post‑prandial glucose spikes while reducing the overall risk of hypoglycemia compared with some subcutaneous rapid‑acting insulins. Because the drug is administered via inhalation rather than injection, it is marketed as an alternative route for delivering rapid‑acting insulin.

Clinical labeling for Afrezza has been noted to cause dosing confusion among some clinicians, reflecting the need for careful education on its unique dosing units and administration technique. Despite this, the product remains distinguished by its inhalable dry‑powder delivery system, rapid lung absorption, and short‑acting insulin action.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-161a201d846100f42e643139469a1e6c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3c9d162accf67a3761df6b1c9113e193&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a0e51dec97ab970bbc2f21878a8735ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4e6371d8083fb20b137912cdaeec1b8b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4655f823785fa91e72cba96e00dba34c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5419de5a030f812ab408ef47f361bebd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cbb54288f56e407604ea361f58e58233&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8644d98286c4a296063176435b45d589&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-70c5a1107fcc9b632361d9c52064f45d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/cengiz-beck-2026-use-of-inhaled-insulin-with-automated-insulin-delivery-systems.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/edelman-et-al-2026-dosing-afrezza-it-s-not-that-complicated.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786333251</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
