</node>
<node id="Automated Insulin Delivery">
  <data key="d0">Automated Insulin Delivery</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Automated insulin delivery is a technology that provides insulin dosing without manual input, evaluated in multiple trials for type 2 diabetes.&lt;SEP&gt;Automated Insulin Delivery denotes technology that automatically administers insulin based on glucose sensor data.&lt;SEP&gt;Technology for delivering insulin automatically, included in the INHALE‑3 Study.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-161a201d846100f42e643139469a1e6c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d30bfc1840eec64224c3568470e6c539&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a0e51dec97ab970bbc2f21878a8735ed</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/cengiz-beck-2026-use-of-inhaled-insulin-with-automated-insulin-delivery-systems.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/edelman-et-al-2026-dosing-afrezza-it-s-not-that-complicated.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786333242</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="AID/TI Therapy">
  <data key="d0">AID/TI Therapy</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A combined approach using automated insulin delivery and inhaled insulin intended for individuals with type 1 diabetes and insulin‑requiring type 2 diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e76c949a607724dd052d9fc4c7127a18</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/cengiz-beck-2026-use-of-inhaled-insulin-with-automated-insulin-delivery-systems.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786332839</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Insulin‑requiring Type 2 Diabetes">
  <data key="d0">Insulin‑requiring Type 2 Diabetes</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Type 2 diabetes patients who need insulin therapy, mentioned as a target population for the therapy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e76c949a607724dd052d9fc4c7127a18</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/cengiz-beck-2026-use-of-inhaled-insulin-with-automated-insulin-delivery-systems.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786332839</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Fully Automated Closed‑Loop Artificial Pancreas System">
  <data key="d0">Fully Automated Closed‑Loop Artificial Pancreas System</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">A closed‑loop insulin delivery device that automatically regulates glucose, evaluated in the Zisser Study.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e76c949a607724dd052d9fc4c7127a18</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/cengiz-beck-2026-use-of-inhaled-insulin-with-automated-insulin-delivery-systems.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786332839</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Zone‑MPC">
  <data key="d0">Zone‑MPC</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Zone model predictive control algorithm that adjusts insulin delivery based on continuous glucose monitor readings.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e76c949a607724dd052d9fc4c7127a18</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/cengiz-beck-2026-use-of-inhaled-insulin-with-automated-insulin-delivery-systems.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786332839</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Time In Range (TIR)">
  <data key="d0">Time In Range (TIR)</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A metric representing the percentage of time glucose stays within a target range, used as primary and secondary endpoints.&lt;SEP&gt;Time In Range (TIR) is a metric representing the percentage of glucose readings within the target range, correlated with microvascular complications.&lt;SEP&gt;Time In Range (TIR) is a metric representing the percentage of glucose readings within the target range of 70–180 mg/dL.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e76c949a607724dd052d9fc4c7127a18&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-94150b57cc35a773b7c36f33f237f8a1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6d83801272f7a0ae0d797d60572fe578</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/cengiz-beck-2026-use-of-inhaled-insulin-with-automated-insulin-delivery-systems.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/cgm.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Metas glicêmicas/Metas no tratamento.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786370023</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Postprandial Glucose Control">
  <data key="d0">Postprandial Glucose Control</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Management of blood glucose levels after meals, the main outcome measured in the studies.&lt;SEP&gt;Postprandial glucose control refers to managing blood glucose levels after meals.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e76c949a607724dd052d9fc4c7127a18&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2767372b4b5395439f542016058306a4</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/cengiz-beck-2026-use-of-inhaled-insulin-with-automated-insulin-delivery-systems.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786332839</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Zisser Study">
  <data key="d0">Zisser Study</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">An early study that evaluated adding a fixed pre‑prandial inhaled insulin dose to a fully automated closed‑loop artificial pancreas system in adults with type 1 diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e76c949a607724dd052d9fc4c7127a18</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/cengiz-beck-2026-use-of-inhaled-insulin-with-automated-insulin-delivery-systems.pdf</data>
