<node id="Rapid On, Rapid Off Pharmacokinetic Profile">
  <data key="d0">Rapid On, Rapid Off Pharmacokinetic Profile</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Rapid On, Rapid Off Pharmacokinetic Profile describes the swift onset and offset of insulin action provided by inhaled insulin, closely resembling natural beta‑cell secretion.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3c9d162accf67a3761df6b1c9113e193</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/cengiz-beck-2026-use-of-inhaled-insulin-with-automated-insulin-delivery-systems.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786332844</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Rapid-Acting Insulin Analogs (RAA)">
  <data key="d0">Rapid-Acting Insulin Analogs (RAA)</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Rapid-Acting Insulin Analogs (RAA) are subcutaneously delivered insulin analogs used in Automated Insulin Delivery systems, noted for delayed pharmacokinetics relative to glucose absorption.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3c9d162accf67a3761df6b1c9113e193</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/cengiz-beck-2026-use-of-inhaled-insulin-with-automated-insulin-delivery-systems.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786332844</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Beta Cell">
  <data key="d0">Beta Cell</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Beta Cell is the pancreatic cell that normally provides the first‑phase insulin release essential for controlling post‑meal glucose rise.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3c9d162accf67a3761df6b1c9113e193</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/cengiz-beck-2026-use-of-inhaled-insulin-with-automated-insulin-delivery-systems.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786332844</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Time-in-Range (TIR)">
  <data key="d0">Time-in-Range (TIR)</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Time-in-Range (TIR) denotes the proportion of time a person’s glucose level stays within the target 70–180 mg/dL range, improved by Automated Insulin Delivery.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3c9d162accf67a3761df6b1c9113e193</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/cengiz-beck-2026-use-of-inhaled-insulin-with-automated-insulin-delivery-systems.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786332844</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Time-below-Range (TBR)">
  <data key="d0">Time-below-Range (TBR)</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Time-below-Range (TBR) denotes the proportion of time glucose falls below the target range, reduced by Automated Insulin Delivery.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3c9d162accf67a3761df6b1c9113e193</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/cengiz-beck-2026-use-of-inhaled-insulin-with-automated-insulin-delivery-systems.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786332845</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="FDA">
  <data key="d0">FDA</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">FDA is the United States Food and Drug Administration, whose labeling for Afrezza was updated as of January 2026.&lt;SEP&gt;The FDA is the regulatory agency whose requirements must be met for studies involving inhaled insulin and AID systems.&lt;SEP&gt;FDA (Food and Drug Administration) is the regulatory agency that authorized the use of Dexcom G6 interstitial glucose for therapy.&lt;SEP&gt;FDA is the U.S. Food and Drug Administration that has approved sensor‑augmented pumps with low‑glucose‑suspend functionality.&lt;SEP&gt;United States regulatory agency that approved teplizumab for use in type 1 diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3c9d162accf67a3761df6b1c9113e193&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2767372b4b5395439f542016058306a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-276b766b8d515b1e7f388b5b7381bfbc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9cd925790899146eeb8a373879b5feac&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2cf24d486949a568d61c1de206cd3e14</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/cengiz-beck-2026-use-of-inhaled-insulin-with-automated-insulin-delivery-systems.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/cgm.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/blood glucose monitoring.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Diagnóstico de diabetes mellitus.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786371994</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Afrezza Inhaled Insulin Delivery System">
  <data key="d0">Afrezza Inhaled Insulin Delivery System</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Afrezza Inhaled Insulin Delivery System is the commercial device delivering Technosphere Insulin via inhalation.&lt;SEP&gt;Afrezza is an inhaled insulin delivery device that employs Technosphere Insulin (TI) to mimic endogenous insulin effects.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3c9d162accf67a3761df6b1c9113e193&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c4daf1d7e9da44e316a5b4dd21bc2dee</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/cengiz-beck-2026-use-of-inhaled-insulin-with-automated-insulin-delivery-systems.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786332845</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="AID Algorithms">
  <data key="d0">AID Algorithms</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">AID Algorithms are the computational rules governing Automated Insulin Delivery systems, many of which are not currently designed to account for exogenous inhaled insulin.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3c9d162accf67a3761df6b1c9113e193</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/cengiz-beck-2026-use-of-inhaled-insulin-with-automated-insulin-delivery-systems.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786332845</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Inhaled Insulin (TI)">
  <data key="d0">Inhaled Insulin (TI)</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Inhaled insulin administered via the TI device, used as a bolus at meal start in clinical studies.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-127dc0e8b8b960bfd1fce3df4f590120</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/cengiz-beck-2026-use-of-inhaled-insulin-with-automated-insulin-delivery-systems.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786332845</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Subcutaneous RAA Insulin">
  <data key="d0">Subcutaneous RAA Insulin</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Rapid‑acting analog insulin delivered subcutaneously, used as the comparator insulin in the studies.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-127dc0e8b8b960bfd1fce3df4f590120</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/cengiz-beck-2026-use-of-inhaled-insulin-with-automated-insulin-delivery-systems.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786332845</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Control‑IQ Algorithm">
  <data key="d0">Control‑IQ Algorithm</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A proprietary AID algorithm that delivers auto‑boluses, but cannot account for exogenous inhaled insulin doses.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-127dc0e8b8b960bfd1fce3df4f590120</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/cengiz-beck-2026-use-of-inhaled-insulin-with-automated-insulin-delivery-systems.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786332845</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Omnipod 5 System">
  <data key="d0">Omnipod 5 System</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">An AID pump system whose algorithm adjusts basal insulin based on total daily insulin but does not consider inhaled insulin.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-127dc0e8b8b960bfd1fce3df4f590120</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/cengiz-beck-2026-use-of-inhaled-insulin-with-automated-insulin-delivery-systems.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786332845</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Tandem">
  <data key="d0">Tandem</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">A medical device manufacturer whose pumps were used by participants in the cited studies.&lt;SEP&gt;Tandem is a company that received a scientific consulting relationship with E.C.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-127dc0e8b8b960bfd1fce3df4f590120&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2767372b4b5395439f542016058306a4</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/cengiz-beck-2026-use-of-inhaled-insulin-with-automated-insulin-delivery-systems.pdf</data>
