</node>
<node id="Postmeal Hyperglycemia">
  <data key="d0">Postmeal Hyperglycemia</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Elevated blood glucose levels occurring after a meal, which was a primary outcome measured in the studies.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-127dc0e8b8b960bfd1fce3df4f590120</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/cengiz-beck-2026-use-of-inhaled-insulin-with-automated-insulin-delivery-systems.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786332846</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Glucose Excursion">
  <data key="d0">Glucose Excursion</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The rise in glucose concentration after a meal, quantified as area under the curve and peak values.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-127dc0e8b8b960bfd1fce3df4f590120</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/cengiz-beck-2026-use-of-inhaled-insulin-with-automated-insulin-delivery-systems.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786332846</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Time in Range (TIR)">
  <data key="d0">Time in Range (TIR)</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The percentage of time glucose values remain within a target range, reported as an outcome of the studies.&lt;SEP&gt;Time in Range (TIR) quantifies the percentage of time a person's glucose stays within a target range, reported in CGM outcomes.&lt;SEP&gt;Metric indicating the percentage of time glucose stays within target range (70‑180 mg/dL).&lt;SEP&gt;Time in Range is a metric indicating the percentage of glucose readings within a target range and is linked to microvascular complication risk and A1C correlation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-127dc0e8b8b960bfd1fce3df4f590120&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0fe1eff7b58582dec4c8ae7578e20e66&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ad23b9b7ef0802d02c046415e54e3fcf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ba0417a72f50cf7ca66c87a351bd1ff8</data>
