  <data key="d2">Insulin formulation administered twice daily, used as a comparator in the Rosenstock Study.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a0e51dec97ab970bbc2f21878a8735ed</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/edelman-et-al-2026-dosing-afrezza-it-s-not-that-complicated.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786333243</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Technosphere Insulin Inhalation Powder (TI)">
  <data key="d0">Technosphere Insulin Inhalation Powder (TI)</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Formulation of Technosphere insulin used in dose‑proportionality studies.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a0e51dec97ab970bbc2f21878a8735ed</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/edelman-et-al-2026-dosing-afrezza-it-s-not-that-complicated.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786333244</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Serum Insulin">
  <data key="d0">Serum Insulin</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Serum insulin refers to the insulin circulating in the bloodstream, which can rise sharply after inhalation of Afrezza.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4e6371d8083fb20b137912cdaeec1b8b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/edelman-et-al-2026-dosing-afrezza-it-s-not-that-complicated.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786333244</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Continuous Glucose Monitor">
  <data key="d0">Continuous Glucose Monitor</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">A Continuous Glucose Monitor (CGM) is a device that tracks blood glucose trends and displays trend arrows.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4e6371d8083fb20b137912cdaeec1b8b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/edelman-et-al-2026-dosing-afrezza-it-s-not-that-complicated.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786333244</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Ultra‑RAAs">
  <data key="d0">Ultra‑RAAs</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Ultra‑RAAs are ultra‑rapid‑acting insulin analogues used for mealtime glucose management.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4e6371d8083fb20b137912cdaeec1b8b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/edelman-et-al-2026-dosing-afrezza-it-s-not-that-complicated.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786333245</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Pulmonary Function">
  <data key="d0">Pulmonary Function</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Pulmonary function refers to the performance of the respiratory system, assessed before and during inhaled insulin therapy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4e6371d8083fb20b137912cdaeec1b8b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/edelman-et-al-2026-dosing-afrezza-it-s-not-that-complicated.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786333245</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Spirometry">
  <data key="d0">Spirometry</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Spirometry is a pulmonary function test measuring airflow, commonly used to evaluate suitability for Afrezza.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4e6371d8083fb20b137912cdaeec1b8b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/edelman-et-al-2026-dosing-afrezza-it-s-not-that-complicated.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786333245</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="FEV1">
  <data key="d0">FEV1</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">FEV1 is a spirometric measurement of the volume of air expelled in the first second of forced exhalation.&lt;SEP&gt;FEV1 is a lung‑function measurement taken before prescribing Afrezza and at follow‑up intervals to monitor safety.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4e6371d8083fb20b137912cdaeec1b8b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8644d98286c4a296063176435b45d589</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/edelman-et-al-2026-dosing-afrezza-it-s-not-that-complicated.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786333245</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Supplementary Table S1">
  <data key="d0">Supplementary Table S1</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Supplementary Table S1 provides a quick reference guide for clinicians regarding Afrezza use.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4e6371d8083fb20b137912cdaeec1b8b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/edelman-et-al-2026-dosing-afrezza-it-s-not-that-complicated.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786333245</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Supplementary Table S2">
  <data key="d0">Supplementary Table S2</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Supplementary Table S2 lists helpful hints that can be printed for patients using Afrezza.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4e6371d8083fb20b137912cdaeec1b8b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/edelman-et-al-2026-dosing-afrezza-it-s-not-that-complicated.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786333245</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Prior Authorization">
  <data key="d0">Prior Authorization</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Prior Authorization is an insurance requirement that must be obtained before Afrezza can be covered.&lt;SEP&gt;Prior authorization (PA) is an insurance approval process required for Afrezza prescription.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4e6371d8083fb20b137912cdaeec1b8b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8644d98286c4a296063176435b45d589</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/edelman-et-al-2026-dosing-afrezza-it-s-not-that-complicated.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786333246</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Insurance Companies">
  <data key="d0">Insurance Companies</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Insurance companies are payers that often require prior authorization for specialty medications like Afrezza.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4e6371d8083fb20b137912cdaeec1b8b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/edelman-et-al-2026-dosing-afrezza-it-s-not-that-complicated.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786333246</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Patients with Type 2 Diabetes">
  <data key="d0">Patients with Type 2 Diabetes</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Patients with Type 2 Diabetes are individuals inadequately controlled on oral agents who may be prescribed Afrezza.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4e6371d8083fb20b137912cdaeec1b8b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/edelman-et-al-2026-dosing-afrezza-it-s-not-that-complicated.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786333246</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Clinicians">
  <data key="d0">Clinicians</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Clinicians are health‑care providers responsible for prescribing Afrezza and monitoring patient outcomes.&lt;SEP&gt;Clinicians are healthcare professionals who prescribe and manage insulin therapies, including Afrezza.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4e6371d8083fb20b137912cdaeec1b8b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cbb54288f56e407604ea361f58e58233</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/edelman-et-al-2026-dosing-afrezza-it-s-not-that-complicated.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786333246</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Spirometer">
  <data key="d0">Spirometer</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">A spirometer is a device used to perform spirometry tests, provided free of charge by MannKind Corporation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4e6371d8083fb20b137912cdaeec1b8b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/edelman-et-al-2026-dosing-afrezza-it-s-not-that-complicated.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786333247</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Chronic Obstructive Pulmonary Disease">
  <data key="d0">Chronic Obstructive Pulmonary Disease</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Chronic Obstructive Pulmonary Disease is a respiratory condition that contraindicates Afrezza therapy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4e6371d8083fb20b137912cdaeec1b8b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/edelman-et-al-2026-dosing-afrezza-it-s-not-that-complicated.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786333247</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Upper Respiratory Tract Infection">
  <data key="d0">Upper Respiratory Tract Infection</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Upper Respiratory Tract Infection is an acute infection that has no significant impact on Afrezza’s pharmacokinetic profile.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4e6371d8083fb20b137912cdaeec1b8b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/edelman-et-al-2026-dosing-afrezza-it-s-not-that-complicated.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786333247</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Current Smokers">
  <data key="d0">Current Smokers</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Current Smokers are individuals who smoke and for whom Afrezza is not recommended.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4e6371d8083fb20b137912cdaeec1b8b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/edelman-et-al-2026-dosing-afrezza-it-s-not-that-complicated.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786333247</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Former Smokers">
  <data key="d0">Former Smokers</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Former Smokers are individuals who quit smoking within the past six months and for whom Afrezza is not recommended.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4e6371d8083fb20b137912cdaeec1b8b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/edelman-et-al-2026-dosing-afrezza-it-s-not-that-complicated.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786333247</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Pulmonologist">
  <data key="d0">Pulmonologist</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">A pulmonologist is a medical specialist to whom clinicians may refer patients for lung evaluation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4e6371d8083fb20b137912cdaeec1b8b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/edelman-et-al-2026-dosing-afrezza-it-s-not-that-complicated.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786333248</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Noninjectable Option">
  <data key="d0">Noninjectable Option</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Noninjectable Option refers to inhaled insulin like Afrezza, preferred by patients with unpredictable meal schedules.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4e6371d8083fb20b137912cdaeec1b8b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/edelman-et-al-2026-dosing-afrezza-it-s-not-that-complicated.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786333248</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Sticky Highs">
  <data key="d0">Sticky Highs</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Sticky Highs describe persistent high glucose levels resistant to correction with subcutaneous insulin.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4e6371d8083fb20b137912cdaeec1b8b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/edelman-et-al-2026-dosing-afrezza-it-s-not-that-complicated.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786333248</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Pump Users">
  <data key="d0">Pump Users</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Pump Users are patients using insulin pumps who may benefit from Afrezza’s rapid onset.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4e6371d8083fb20b137912cdaeec1b8b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/edelman-et-al-2026-dosing-afrezza-it-s-not-that-complicated.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786333248</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Prior Treatment Failures">
  <data key="d0">Prior Treatment Failures</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Prior Treatment Failures refer to unsuccessful use of other insulins, required documentation for prior authorization.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4e6371d8083fb20b137912cdaeec1b8b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/edelman-et-al-2026-dosing-afrezza-it-s-not-that-complicated.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786333249</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="4 U Cartridge">
  <data key="d0">4 U Cartridge</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">A 4 U Cartridge is a dosage form of Afrezza used for initial correction dosing when glucose exceeds 220 mg/dL.&lt;SEP&gt;The 4‑unit cartridge is a smaller Afrezza inhaler cartridge that is generally better tolerated initially.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4e6371d8083fb20b137912cdaeec1b8b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8644d98286c4a296063176435b45d589</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/edelman-et-al-2026-dosing-afrezza-it-s-not-that-complicated.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786333249</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="8 U Cartridge">
  <data key="d0">8 U Cartridge</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">An 8 U Cartridge is a higher‑dose form of Afrezza used if a 4 U cartridge does not correct hyperglycemia.&lt;SEP&gt;The 8‑unit cartridge is a larger Afrezza inhaler cartridge option for higher dose requirements.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4e6371d8083fb20b137912cdaeec1b8b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8644d98286c4a296063176435b45d589</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/edelman-et-al-2026-dosing-afrezza-it-s-not-that-complicated.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786333249</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Dosage Conversion and Titration">
  <data key="d0">Dosage Conversion and Titration</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Dosage Conversion and Titration is a method for adjusting Afrezza doses based on glucose readings.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4e6371d8083fb20b137912cdaeec1b8b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/edelman-et-al-2026-dosing-afrezza-it-s-not-that-complicated.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786333249</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Trial and Error Approach">
  <data key="d0">Trial and Error Approach</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Trial and Error Approach is a strategy for initiating Afrezza correction doses by observing glucose response.&lt;SEP&gt;The trial and error approach is a dosing strategy recommended when initiating Afrezza therapy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4e6371d8083fb20b137912cdaeec1b8b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5419de5a030f812ab408ef47f361bebd</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/edelman-et-al-2026-dosing-afrezza-it-s-not-that-complicated.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786333250</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Insurance Coverage">
  <data key="d0">Insurance Coverage</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Insurance Coverage denotes the process of obtaining payer approval for Afrezza as a specialty medication.&lt;SEP&gt;Insurance coverage describes the extent to which payers reimburse Afrezza.&lt;SEP&gt;The provision of financial reimbursement for diabetes technology by insurers.&lt;SEP&gt;Insurance coverage refers to health insurance provisions that may lag behind the availability of diabetes devices.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4e6371d8083fb20b137912cdaeec1b8b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5419de5a030f812ab408ef47f361bebd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4b355007bba178588f3928b6c8620a78&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e4c5ae163a494feafedb71ed2205c02f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/edelman-et-al-2026-dosing-afrezza-it-s-not-that-complicated.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/blood glucose monitoring.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786335876</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Specialty Medication">
  <data key="d0">Specialty Medication</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Specialty Medication classifies Afrezza as a high‑cost, narrowly prescribed drug requiring special authorization.&lt;SEP&gt;Specialty medication is a classification that makes Afrezza’s insurance approval more complex.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4e6371d8083fb20b137912cdaeec1b8b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5419de5a030f812ab408ef47f361bebd</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/edelman-et-al-2026-dosing-afrezza-it-s-not-that-complicated.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786333250</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Acute Bronchospasm">
  <data key="d0">Acute Bronchospasm</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Acute Bronchospasm is a sudden narrowing of the airways that increases risk when using inhaled insulin.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4e6371d8083fb20b137912cdaeec1b8b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/edelman-et-al-2026-dosing-afrezza-it-s-not-that-complicated.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786333250</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hyper-sensitivity">
  <data key="d0">Hyper-sensitivity</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Hyper-sensitivity describes allergic reactions to regular human insulin or excipients, contraindicating Afrezza.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4e6371d8083fb20b137912cdaeec1b8b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/edelman-et-al-2026-dosing-afrezza-it-s-not-that-complicated.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786333251</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Pulmonary Function Test">
  <data key="d0">Pulmonary Function Test</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Pulmonary Function Test (PFT) measures lung capacity and is used to evaluate suitability for Afrezza therapy.&lt;SEP&gt;Pulmonary function tests are clinical measurements required before and during Afrezza therapy to assess lung suitability.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4e6371d8083fb20b137912cdaeec1b8b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5419de5a030f812ab408ef47f361bebd</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/edelman-et-al-2026-dosing-afrezza-it-s-not-that-complicated.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786333251</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Patients with Unpredictable Meal Schedules">
  <data key="d0">Patients with Unpredictable Meal Schedules</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Patients with Unpredictable Meal Schedules are individuals who prefer a noninjectable insulin option like Afrezza.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4e6371d8083fb20b137912cdaeec1b8b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/edelman-et-al-2026-dosing-afrezza-it-s-not-that-complicated.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786333251</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Patients with Postprandial Hyperglycemia">
  <data key="d0">Patients with Postprandial Hyperglycemia</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Patients with Postprandial Hyperglycemia experience high glucose after meals and may benefit from Afrezza.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4e6371d8083fb20b137912cdaeec1b8b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/edelman-et-al-2026-dosing-afrezza-it-s-not-that-complicated.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786333251</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Patients with Sticky Highs">
  <data key="d0">Patients with Sticky Highs</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Patients with Sticky Highs have persistent hyperglycemia resistant to subcutaneous insulin, potentially improved by Afrezza.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4e6371d8083fb20b137912cdaeec1b8b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/edelman-et-al-2026-dosing-afrezza-it-s-not-that-complicated.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786333251</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Patients with Insulin Resistance">
  <data key="d0">Patients with Insulin Resistance</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Patients with Insulin Resistance require higher insulin doses and may need increased Afrezza dosing.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4e6371d8083fb20b137912cdaeec1b8b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/edelman-et-al-2026-dosing-afrezza-it-s-not-that-complicated.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786333251</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="GLP‑1 Receptor Agonist">
  <data key="d0">GLP‑1 Receptor Agonist</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">GLP‑1 Receptor Agonist is a class of medications that enhance glucose control; it includes weekly and daily formulations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4655f823785fa91e72cba96e00dba34c</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/edelman-et-al-2026-dosing-afrezza-it-s-not-that-complicated.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786333251</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Ozempic">
  <data key="d0">Ozempic</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Ozempic is a weekly GLP‑1 receptor agonist mentioned as compatible with Afrezza after the titration phase.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4655f823785fa91e72cba96e00dba34c</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/edelman-et-al-2026-dosing-afrezza-it-s-not-that-complicated.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786333252</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Mounjaro">
  <data key="d0">Mounjaro</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Mounjaro is a weekly GLP‑1 receptor agonist mentioned as compatible with Afrezza after the titration phase.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4655f823785fa91e72cba96e00dba34c</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/edelman-et-al-2026-dosing-afrezza-it-s-not-that-complicated.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786333252</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Victoza">
  <data key="d0">Victoza</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Victoza is a daily GLP‑1 receptor agonist that may cause issues when used concurrently with Afrezza.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4655f823785fa91e72cba96e00dba34c</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/edelman-et-al-2026-dosing-afrezza-it-s-not-that-complicated.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786333252</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Byetta">
  <data key="d0">Byetta</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Byetta is a daily GLP‑1 receptor agonist that may cause issues when used concurrently with Afrezza.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4655f823785fa91e72cba96e00dba34c</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/edelman-et-al-2026-dosing-afrezza-it-s-not-that-complicated.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786333252</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Control IQ">
  <data key="d0">Control IQ</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Control IQ is a pump‑algorithm feature that can provide automatic correction boluses and a sleep mode.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4655f823785fa91e72cba96e00dba34c</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/edelman-et-al-2026-dosing-afrezza-it-s-not-that-complicated.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786333252</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Afrezza Cartridge 4 U">
  <data key="d0">Afrezza Cartridge 4 U</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Afrezza Cartridge 4 U is a 4‑unit inhalable insulin cartridge used for initial dosing.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4655f823785fa91e72cba96e00dba34c</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/edelman-et-al-2026-dosing-afrezza-it-s-not-that-complicated.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786333252</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Afrezza Cartridge 8 U">
  <data key="d0">Afrezza Cartridge 8 U</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Afrezza Cartridge 8 U is an 8‑unit inhalable insulin cartridge commonly used to correct hyperglycemia.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4655f823785fa91e72cba96e00dba34c</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/edelman-et-al-2026-dosing-afrezza-it-s-not-that-complicated.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786333253</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Afrezza Cartridge 12 U">
  <data key="d0">Afrezza Cartridge 12 U</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Afrezza Cartridge 12 U is a 12‑unit inhalable insulin cartridge available for larger dosing needs.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4655f823785fa91e72cba96e00dba34c</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/edelman-et-al-2026-dosing-afrezza-it-s-not-that-complicated.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786333253</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Basal Insulin Dose">
  <data key="d0">Basal Insulin Dose</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Basal Insulin Dose is the background insulin amount that should be correctly set before adding Afrezza.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4655f823785fa91e72cba96e00dba34c</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/edelman-et-al-2026-dosing-afrezza-it-s-not-that-complicated.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786333253</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Titration">
  <data key="d0">Titration</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Titration is the process of adjusting Afrezza dose based on meal size and pre‑meal glucose levels.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4655f823785fa91e72cba96e00dba34c</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/edelman-et-al-2026-dosing-afrezza-it-s-not-that-complicated.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786333253</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Rapid‑On Rapid‑Off Pharmacokinetics">
  <data key="d0">Rapid‑On Rapid‑Off Pharmacokinetics</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Rapid‑On Rapid‑Off Pharmacokinetics describes Afrezza’s fast onset and quick offset, minimizing insulin depot time.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4655f823785fa91e72cba96e00dba34c</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/edelman-et-al-2026-dosing-afrezza-it-s-not-that-complicated.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786333253</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Meal Size">
  <data key="d0">Meal Size</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Meal Size refers to the quantity of food consumed, influencing the required Afrezza dose.&lt;SEP&gt;Meal size influences the amount of Afrezza administered to match carbohydrate intake.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4655f823785fa91e72cba96e00dba34c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5419de5a030f812ab408ef47f361bebd</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/edelman-et-al-2026-dosing-afrezza-it-s-not-that-complicated.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786333253</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Insulin‑Naïve Patient">
  <data key="d0">Insulin‑Naïve Patient</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Insulin‑Naïve Patients are individuals who have not previously used insulin and start therapy with a 4 U Afrezza cartridge at the largest meal.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4655f823785fa91e72cba96e00dba34c</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/edelman-et-al-2026-dosing-afrezza-it-s-not-that-complicated.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786333254</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Injected Insulin">
  <data key="d0">Injected Insulin</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Injected Insulin refers to traditional subcutaneous insulin administered via injection, contrasted with inhaled Afrezza.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4655f823785fa91e72cba96e00dba34c</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/edelman-et-al-2026-dosing-afrezza-it-s-not-that-complicated.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786333254</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Postprandial Glucose Level">
  <data key="d0">Postprandial Glucose Level</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Postprandial Glucose Level is the blood glucose measurement after a meal, used to titrate Afrezza dosing.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4655f823785fa91e72cba96e00dba34c</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/edelman-et-al-2026-dosing-afrezza-it-s-not-that-complicated.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786333254</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Education/Training Areas">
  <data key="d0">Education/Training Areas</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Education/Training Areas are topics outlined in Table 2 to teach patients about Afrezza use and dosing.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4655f823785fa91e72cba96e00dba34c</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/edelman-et-al-2026-dosing-afrezza-it-s-not-that-complicated.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786333254</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="ASPN Portal">
  <data key="d0">ASPN Portal</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The ASPN portal is a digital platform provided by MannKind Corporation to streamline prior‑authorization submissions for Afrezza.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5419de5a030f812ab408ef47f361bebd</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/edelman-et-al-2026-dosing-afrezza-it-s-not-that-complicated.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786333255</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Chronic Respiratory Conditions">
  <data key="d0">Chronic Respiratory Conditions</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Chronic respiratory conditions are lung diseases that contraindicate the use of Afrezza.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5419de5a030f812ab408ef47f361bebd</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/edelman-et-al-2026-dosing-afrezza-it-s-not-that-complicated.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786333255</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Reduced Lung Function">
  <data key="d0">Reduced Lung Function</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Reduced lung function is a condition that contraindicates Afrezza therapy.</data>
