</node>
<node id="Postprandial Glucose Spikes">
  <data key="d0">Postprandial Glucose Spikes</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Postprandial glucose spikes refer to rapid rises in blood glucose after meals.&lt;SEP&gt;Postprandial glucose spikes are elevated blood‑sugar levels after meals that Afrezza aims to reduce.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cbb54288f56e407604ea361f58e58233&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8644d98286c4a296063176435b45d589</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/edelman-et-al-2026-dosing-afrezza-it-s-not-that-complicated.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786333264</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Delayed Hypoglycemia">
  <data key="d0">Delayed Hypoglycemia</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Delayed hypoglycemia describes low blood glucose occurring several hours after insulin administration.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cbb54288f56e407604ea361f58e58233</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/edelman-et-al-2026-dosing-afrezza-it-s-not-that-complicated.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786333264</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Inhaled Insulin Delivery System">
  <data key="d0">Inhaled Insulin Delivery System</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The inhaled insulin delivery system is the method by which Afrezza administers insulin via the lungs.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cbb54288f56e407604ea361f58e58233</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/edelman-et-al-2026-dosing-afrezza-it-s-not-that-complicated.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786333264</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Subcutaneous Rapid‑Acting Insulin">
  <data key="d0">Subcutaneous Rapid‑Acting Insulin</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Subcutaneous rapid‑acting insulin refers to injectable insulin analogs delivered under the skin.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cbb54288f56e407604ea361f58e58233</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/edelman-et-al-2026-dosing-afrezza-it-s-not-that-complicated.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786333264</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="1:1 Units Conversion">
  <data key="d0">1:1 Units Conversion</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">1:1 units conversion denotes a non‑equivalent dosing equivalence between Afrezza and subcutaneous insulin.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cbb54288f56e407604ea361f58e58233</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/edelman-et-al-2026-dosing-afrezza-it-s-not-that-complicated.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786333264</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Dosing Afrezza: Its Not That Complicated">
  <data key="d0">Dosing Afrezza: Its Not That Complicated</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">“Dosing Afrezza: It’s Not That Complicated” is the original article discussing Afrezza dosing and titration.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cbb54288f56e407604ea361f58e58233</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/edelman-et-al-2026-dosing-afrezza-it-s-not-that-complicated.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786333264</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Correction Doses">
  <data key="d0">Correction Doses</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Correction doses are insulin adjustments administered before or after meals to manage elevated glucose, including safe re‑dosing 1–2 hours after meals.&lt;SEP&gt;Additional insulin amounts calculated to correct high glucose levels in DIY closed‑loop systems.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8644d98286c4a296063176435b45d589&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5227749196a4c9226dba64a500d84b3a</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/edelman-et-al-2026-dosing-afrezza-it-s-not-that-complicated.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/blood glucose monitoring.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786335986</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Bedtime Corrections">
  <data key="d0">Bedtime Corrections</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Bedtime corrections are insulin adjustments given at night, benefiting from Afrezza’s rapid clearance to reduce overnight hypoglycemia.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8644d98286c4a296063176435b45d589</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/edelman-et-al-2026-dosing-afrezza-it-s-not-that-complicated.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786333265</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Tandem Control-IQ System">
  <data key="d0">Tandem Control-IQ System</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The Tandem Control‑IQ system is an insulin pump with a fixed insulin action time of 5 hours, compatible with Afrezza and able to disable auto corrections in sleep mode.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8644d98286c4a296063176435b45d589</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/edelman-et-al-2026-dosing-afrezza-it-s-not-that-complicated.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786333265</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="iLet Bionic Pancreas">
  <data key="d0">iLet Bionic Pancreas</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The iLet Bionic Pancreas is an automated insulin‑delivery system that does not allow insulin action duration adjustment and is not advised for use with Afrezza.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8644d98286c4a296063176435b45d589</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/edelman-et-al-2026-dosing-afrezza-it-s-not-that-complicated.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786333265</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Exenatide">
  <data key="d0">Exenatide</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Exenatide is a daily GLP‑1 receptor agonist cited alongside liraglutide.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8644d98286c4a296063176435b45d589</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/edelman-et-al-2026-dosing-afrezza-it-s-not-that-complicated.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786333265</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Semaglutide">
  <data key="d0">Semaglutide</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Semaglutide is a weekly GLP‑1 receptor agonist generally compatible with Afrezza after a stable maintenance dose is reached.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8644d98286c4a296063176435b45d589</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/edelman-et-al-2026-dosing-afrezza-it-s-not-that-complicated.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786333265</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Tirzepatide">
  <data key="d0">Tirzepatide</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Tirzepatide is a weekly GLP‑1 receptor agonist compatible with Afrezza once the patient has reached a stable maintenance dose.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8644d98286c4a296063176435b45d589</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/edelman-et-al-2026-dosing-afrezza-it-s-not-that-complicated.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786333266</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Basal Bolus Therapy">
  <data key="d0">Basal Bolus Therapy</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Basal‑bolus therapy is an insulin regimen that requires patients to continue basal insulin injections alongside other insulin doses.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8644d98286c4a296063176435b45d589</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/edelman-et-al-2026-dosing-afrezza-it-s-not-that-complicated.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786333266</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="EMR">
  <data key="d0">EMR</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Electronic Medical Record (EMR) systems are used by clinicians to order Afrezza cartridges.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8644d98286c4a296063176435b45d589</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/edelman-et-al-2026-dosing-afrezza-it-s-not-that-complicated.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786333266</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Walgreens">
  <data key="d0">Walgreens</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Walgreens is a major pharmacy chain where Afrezza is available.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8644d98286c4a296063176435b45d589</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/edelman-et-al-2026-dosing-afrezza-it-s-not-that-complicated.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786333266</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="CVS">
  <data key="d0">CVS</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">CVS is a major pharmacy chain where Afrezza is available.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8644d98286c4a296063176435b45d589</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/edelman-et-al-2026-dosing-afrezza-it-s-not-that-complicated.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786333266</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Lung Health">
  <data key="d0">Lung Health</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Lung health refers to the assessment of respiratory function, monitored via FEV1 for patients using Afrezza.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8644d98286c4a296063176435b45d589</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/edelman-et-al-2026-dosing-afrezza-it-s-not-that-complicated.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786333266</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Sore Throat">
  <data key="d0">Sore Throat</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Sore Throat is a throat irritation that may be experienced after Afrezza inhalation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8644d98286c4a296063176435b45d589</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/edelman-et-al-2026-dosing-afrezza-it-s-not-that-complicated.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786333267</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Larynx">
  <data key="d0">Larynx</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">The larynx is a part of the airway that can receive insulin powder if the inhaler is not angled correctly.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8644d98286c4a296063176435b45d589</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/edelman-et-al-2026-dosing-afrezza-it-s-not-that-complicated.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786333267</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="TI Microparticles">
  <data key="d0">TI Microparticles</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">TI microparticles are particles to which the recombinant insulin in Afrezza is bound, enabling rapid lung absorption.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8644d98286c4a296063176435b45d589</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/edelman-et-al-2026-dosing-afrezza-it-s-not-that-complicated.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786333267</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Dry Powder Formulation">
  <data key="d0">Dry Powder Formulation</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Dry powder formulation describes Afrezza’s presentation as a powdered insulin for inhalation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8644d98286c4a296063176435b45d589</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/edelman-et-al-2026-dosing-afrezza-it-s-not-that-complicated.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786333267</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Time-in-Range">
  <data key="d0">Time-in-Range</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Time-in-range is a metric indicating the proportion of time glucose stays within target limits.&lt;SEP&gt;Time-in-Range is a metric of glucose control linked to hemoglobin A1c in a cited analysis.&lt;SEP&gt;The percentage of time a person's blood glucose stays within a predefined target range.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8644d98286c4a296063176435b45d589&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-29ea6999715cd3886bd7d4abc2a653b0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-664916c2444f157f5d7d9bc41b032d26</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/edelman-et-al-2026-dosing-afrezza-it-s-not-that-complicated.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Metas glicêmicas/Metas no tratamento.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Metas glicêmicas/metas cuidado do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786372138</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Clinical Notes">
  <data key="d0">Clinical Notes</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Clinical notes are detailed documentation of a patient’s history used to support Afrezza prescription approval.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8644d98286c4a296063176435b45d589</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/edelman-et-al-2026-dosing-afrezza-it-s-not-that-complicated.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786333268</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Conversion Ratio">
  <data key="d0">Conversion Ratio</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Conversion ratio expresses the relationship between Afrezza units and subcutaneous insulin units.&lt;SEP&gt;The 2:1 conversion ratio defines the dose of Afrezza needed to match the effect of subcutaneous insulin.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8644d98286c4a296063176435b45d589&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-70c5a1107fcc9b632361d9c52064f45d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/edelman-et-al-2026-dosing-afrezza-it-s-not-that-complicated.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786333268</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Clinician">
  <data key="d0">Clinician</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Clinicians are healthcare providers who prescribe Afrezza and prepare supporting documentation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8644d98286c4a296063176435b45d589</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/edelman-et-al-2026-dosing-afrezza-it-s-not-that-complicated.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786333268</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="USPI">
  <data key="d0">USPI</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">The USPI is prescribing information that reports a 1.3:1 conversion ratio for Afrezza.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-70c5a1107fcc9b632361d9c52064f45d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/edelman-et-al-2026-dosing-afrezza-it-s-not-that-complicated.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786333268</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="INHALE-3 Study">
  <data key="d0">INHALE-3 Study</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">INHALE-3 is a clinical trial that reported an initial conversion ratio of 1.8:1 and a titrated dose near 2.5:1 for Afrezza.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-70c5a1107fcc9b632361d9c52064f45d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/edelman-et-al-2026-dosing-afrezza-it-s-not-that-complicated.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786333268</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="INHALE-1 Study">
  <data key="d0">INHALE-1 Study</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">INHALE-1 is a pediatric trial that reported a titrated conversion ratio just under 3:1 for Afrezza.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-70c5a1107fcc9b632361d9c52064f45d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/edelman-et-al-2026-dosing-afrezza-it-s-not-that-complicated.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786333268</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="U300 Lantus">
  <data key="d0">U300 Lantus</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">U300 Lantus (glargine) is a long‑acting insulin formulation with lower hypoglycemia risk than U100 Lantus.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-70c5a1107fcc9b632361d9c52064f45d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/edelman-et-al-2026-dosing-afrezza-it-s-not-that-complicated.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786333268</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="U100 Lantus">
  <data key="d0">U100 Lantus</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">U100 Lantus (glargine) is a standard‑dose insulin formulation sometimes used despite higher hypoglycemia risk.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-70c5a1107fcc9b632361d9c52064f45d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/edelman-et-al-2026-dosing-afrezza-it-s-not-that-complicated.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786333268</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="BeAM Score">
  <data key="d0">BeAM Score</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">BeAM score is the difference between bedtime average glucose and AM average glucose, with a target below 30 mg/dL.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-70c5a1107fcc9b632361d9c52064f45d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/edelman-et-al-2026-dosing-afrezza-it-s-not-that-complicated.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786333268</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="15/15 Rule">
  <data key="d0">15/15 Rule</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The 15/15 rule recommends 15 g of carbohydrate and a repeat dose after 15 minutes to treat hypoglycemia.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-70c5a1107fcc9b632361d9c52064f45d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/edelman-et-al-2026-dosing-afrezza-it-s-not-that-complicated.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786333269</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="CGM Trend Arrow">
  <data key="d0">CGM Trend Arrow</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">CGM trend arrows indicate the direction of glucose change and are used to adjust Afrezza timing and dose.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-70c5a1107fcc9b632361d9c52064f45d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/edelman-et-al-2026-dosing-afrezza-it-s-not-that-complicated.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786333269</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="BeAM Target">
  <data key="d0">BeAM Target</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">BeAM target is a goal of a BeAM score less than 30 mg/dL for optimal Tresiba dosing.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-70c5a1107fcc9b632361d9c52064f45d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/edelman-et-al-2026-dosing-afrezza-it-s-not-that-complicated.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786333269</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Afrezza/Tresiba (Degludec) Therapy">
  <data key="d0">Afrezza/Tresiba (Degludec) Therapy</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Afrezza/Tresiba (Degludec) Therapy is a titration approach combining inhaled Afrezza with basal Tresiba insulin.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-70c5a1107fcc9b632361d9c52064f45d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/edelman-et-al-2026-dosing-afrezza-it-s-not-that-complicated.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786333269</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Bedtime">
  <data key="d0">Bedtime</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Bedtime is the period when correction dosing of Afrezza may be administered to achieve safe morning glucose levels.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-70c5a1107fcc9b632361d9c52064f45d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Tipos de insulinas/edelman-et-al-2026-dosing-afrezza-it-s-not-that-complicated.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786333269</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
