<node id="Gestational Diabetes Mellitus">
  <data key="d0">Gestational Diabetes Mellitus</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Gestational Diabetes Mellitus (GDM) is a form of glucose intolerance or hyper‑glycemia that is first recognized during pregnancy, most commonly in the second or third trimester. It constitutes a pregnancy‑related type of diabetes in which the mother’s ability to regulate blood glucose becomes impaired, often due to β‑cell dysfunction, and the condition is identified through specific screening protocols that may employ either a one‑step (75 g oral glucose tolerance test) or a two‑step (50 g glucose challenge followed by a 100 g oral glucose tolerance test) approach.

The diagnosis of GDM carries important short‑term and long‑term implications for both the mother and her offspring. In the short term, elevated maternal glucose levels increase the risk of obstetric complications, fetal overgrowth (macrosomia), neonatal hypoglycemia, and delivery interventions. In the long term, women who experience GDM have a markedly higher likelihood of developing type 2 diabetes and other metabolic disorders after delivery, prompting recommendations for lifelong screening for diabetes or prediabetes. Children born to mothers with GDM are also at an elevated risk of obesity, impaired glucose tolerance, and type 2 diabetes later in life.

Because of these health consequences, GDM is a major focus of clinical research aimed at refining diagnostic criteria, optimizing treatment strategies, and improving maternal‑offspring outcomes. Ongoing studies continue to evaluate how early detection and intervention can mitigate both immediate pregnancy complications and the enduring metabolic risks for the mother and her child.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-91a09040fc4581d7aad2216dba9fba79&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b4b76ae88b212b3a0a4d05c250e05e0c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-090b8f9281aa75054311d8f275a2c8f8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-525031caa389d084bc170433212cdca8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-59dd4faf2a2706d073fdb93e1a29da81&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8ba9c9c7fe9dd4e901eb52088f3d59f8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f7b840a0b5327c5e583eb70dd354d1d0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-83d72fbc44fe0c28f27702c0d4f2c140&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ae844f5b99d595c38f74e375112238e6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-49c21dd27a63d44c5d80b53aa7e1f48d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c14456299df06b01b603504def87f381&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1a111d4b40ec241cf54126f594a80308&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-037075addb77da4a5a1721a95ee298c0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fedb8cdc485be3c8e38133ddb9ea67cf</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/cgm.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/blood glucose monitoring.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
