<node id="U.S. Food and Drug Administration">
  <data key="d0">U.S. Food and Drug Administration</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">The U.S. Food and Drug Administration issues guidance on glucose meter accuracy and recommends access to blood glucose monitoring for CGM users.&lt;SEP&gt;The U.S. Food and Drug Administration (FDA) is the regulatory agency that defines blood glucose meter accuracy standards for home and hospital use.&lt;SEP&gt;The U.S. regulatory agency that approves and monitors medical devices and digital therapeutics.&lt;SEP&gt;U.S. Food and Drug Administration is the regulatory agency that issued news releases expanding indications for continuous glucose monitoring systems.&lt;SEP&gt;The U.S. Food and Drug Administration is the federal agency that issued an enforcement policy for non‑invasive remote monitoring devices during the COVID‑19 public health emergency.&lt;SEP&gt;U.S. Food and Drug Administration is the U.S. regulatory agency that issued policies and guidance documents related to glucose monitoring devices.&lt;SEP&gt;The U.S. Food and Drug Administration approves point-of-care A1C testing for clinical use.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-dbd74c7f87bf62557b2b4c750ec596b7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9e0c6a8245e883948688f77c2440ca4b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-40c2c862887db201b07c741a1862dcc1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c9bc5d11c9f848439320623cad3d3a38&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5958ff9ae6e3f3fb00f413f28bcde97c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5227749196a4c9226dba64a500d84b3a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-44888abd4ca8a1953f751ed6c41922e6</data>
