<node id="Multiple Daily Insulin Injections">
  <data key="d0">Multiple Daily Insulin Injections</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Multiple daily insulin injections are a regimen for delivering insulin in type 1 diabetes examined in the GOLD trial.&lt;SEP&gt;A regimen in which individuals administer rapid‑acting insulin several times per day to manage blood glucose.&lt;SEP&gt;Multiple daily insulin injections (MDI) involve several injections of insulin each day as a diabetes treatment regimen.&lt;SEP&gt;Multiple daily insulin injections is a conventional insulin delivery method used as a comparator in diabetes studies.</data>
