<node id="Health Care Professionals">
  <data key="d0">Health Care Professionals</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Health care professionals are individuals who support people with diabetes, including troubleshooting device difficulties.&lt;SEP&gt;Health care professionals are the clinicians working in intensive care unit settings who must monitor glucose meter accuracy during critical illness.&lt;SEP&gt;Health care professionals are individuals who provide diabetes care and use resources such as DiabetesWise and the PANTHER Program to choose devices.&lt;SEP&gt;Health Care Professionals are medical providers who participate in shared decision‑making with people with diabetes about pump therapy.&lt;SEP&gt;Medical staff who provide diabetes management support but cannot prescribe DIY closed‑loop systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Individuals providing medical care, guided by the ADA risk test.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b3b81193a603a098b1ff9f6f0f665fec&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4b355007bba178588f3928b6c8620a78&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9cd925790899146eeb8a373879b5feac&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-00f6c2252dc945e977b3a2b2f495ffe0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5227749196a4c9226dba64a500d84b3a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9eb02ab1ab7d834858bf60a8b402e6ea</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/blood glucose monitoring.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377427</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="People With Diabetes">
  <data key="d0">People With Diabetes</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">People with diabetes are individuals managing diabetes who need devices, education, and support.&lt;SEP&gt;People with diabetes are individuals who benefit from diabetes devices and guidance from health care professionals and online resources.&lt;SEP&gt;People with diabetes are the patient population whose therapy effectiveness and data usage are the focus of the discussion.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b3b81193a603a098b1ff9f6f0f665fec&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4b355007bba178588f3928b6c8620a78&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-679002669c87907578534904694e17dc</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/blood glucose monitoring.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/Orientacoes_Glicemia_SBD.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786337568</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Higher Socioeconomic Status">
  <data key="d0">Higher Socioeconomic Status</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Higher socioeconomic status, reflected by race/ethnicity, private health insurance, family income, and education, is associated with more common pump therapy use.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b3b81193a603a098b1ff9f6f0f665fec</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/blood glucose monitoring.pdf</data>
