<node id="Intensive Care Unit Settings">
  <data key="d0">Intensive Care Unit Settings</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">Intensive care unit settings are hospital locations where critically ill patients receive care and where glucose meter readings must be closely monitored.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-00f6c2252dc945e977b3a2b2f495ffe0</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/blood glucose monitoring.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786335921</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Glucose Monitors">
  <data key="d0">Glucose Monitors</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Glucose monitors are devices that measure blood glucose levels, employing enzymatic and electrochemical reactions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-00f6c2252dc945e977b3a2b2f495ffe0</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/blood glucose monitoring.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786335921</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Glucose Oxidase Monitors">
  <data key="d0">Glucose Oxidase Monitors</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Glucose oxidase monitors are a type of glucose monitor that rely on glucose oxidase and are sensitive to ambient oxygen levels.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-00f6c2252dc945e977b3a2b2f495ffe0</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/blood glucose monitoring.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786335921</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Glucose Dehydrogenase Monitors">
  <data key="d0">Glucose Dehydrogenase Monitors</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Glucose dehydrogenase monitors are a type of glucose monitor that use glucose dehydrogenase and are not sensitive to oxygen.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-00f6c2252dc945e977b3a2b2f495ffe0</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/blood glucose monitoring.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786335921</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Arterial Blood">
  <data key="d0">Arterial Blood</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Arterial blood is oxygen‑rich blood that, when used with glucose oxidase monitors, may cause falsely low glucose readings.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-00f6c2252dc945e977b3a2b2f495ffe0</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/blood glucose monitoring.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786335921</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Venous Blood">
  <data key="d0">Venous Blood</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Venous blood is oxygen‑poor blood that may cause falsely high glucose readings with glucose oxidase monitors.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-00f6c2252dc945e977b3a2b2f495ffe0</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/blood glucose monitoring.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786335921</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Oxygen">
  <data key="d0">Oxygen</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Oxygen is the gas whose tension affects the accuracy of glucose oxidase monitors and is irrelevant to glucose dehydrogenase monitors.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-00f6c2252dc945e977b3a2b2f495ffe0</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/blood glucose monitoring.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786335921</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="High Oxygen Tension">
  <data key="d0">High Oxygen Tension</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">High oxygen tension refers to elevated arterial or therapy‑related oxygen levels that can produce false low glucose readings with glucose oxidase monitors.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-00f6c2252dc945e977b3a2b2f495ffe0</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/blood glucose monitoring.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786335921</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Low Oxygen Tension">
  <data key="d0">Low Oxygen Tension</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Low oxygen tension includes high‑altitude, hypoxic, or venous blood conditions that can produce false high glucose readings with glucose oxidase monitors.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-00f6c2252dc945e977b3a2b2f495ffe0</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/blood glucose monitoring.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786335921</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Humidity">
  <data key="d0">Humidity</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Humidity is an environmental factor that may alter glucose monitor readings.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-00f6c2252dc945e977b3a2b2f495ffe0</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/blood glucose monitoring.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786335921</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Altitude">
  <data key="d0">Altitude</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Altitude is an environmental condition that may alter glucose monitor readings, especially at high elevations.&lt;SEP&gt;High altitude environments (above 2000 m) that can produce falsely elevated glucose readings.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-00f6c2252dc945e977b3a2b2f495ffe0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8fe1b07f3c84733fcbfca023fbfd70e6</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/blood glucose monitoring.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/Orientacoes_Glicemia_SBD.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786337573</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Uric Acid">
  <data key="d0">Uric Acid</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Uric acid is a physiologic substance that interferes with glucose oxidase monitor readings.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-00f6c2252dc945e977b3a2b2f495ffe0</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/blood glucose monitoring.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786335921</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Galactose">
  <data key="d0">Galactose</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Galactose is a sugar that interferes with glucose oxidase monitor readings.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-00f6c2252dc945e977b3a2b2f495ffe0</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/blood glucose monitoring.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786335921</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Xylose">
  <data key="d0">Xylose</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Xylose is a sugar that interferes with glucose oxidase monitor readings.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-00f6c2252dc945e977b3a2b2f495ffe0</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/blood glucose monitoring.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786335922</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="L-DOPA">
  <data key="d0">L-DOPA</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">L‑DOPA is a compound that interferes with glucose oxidase monitor readings.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-00f6c2252dc945e977b3a2b2f495ffe0</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/blood glucose monitoring.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786335922</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Ascorbic Acid">
  <data key="d0">Ascorbic Acid</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Ascorbic acid is a vitamin that interferes with glucose oxidase monitor readings.&lt;SEP&gt;Ascorbic acid (vitamin C) taken above 500 mg/day can cause higher sensor readings on FreeStyle Libre.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-00f6c2252dc945e977b3a2b2f495ffe0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-05cc642337c2a615c9b40de9336aec18</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/blood glucose monitoring.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786335922</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Icodextrin">
  <data key="d0">Icodextrin</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Icodextrin, used in peritoneal dialysis, interferes with glucose dehydrogenase monitor readings.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-00f6c2252dc945e977b3a2b2f495ffe0</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/blood glucose monitoring.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786335922</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Real-Time Continuous Glucose Monitoring A">
  <data key="d0">Real-Time Continuous Glucose Monitoring A</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Real‑time continuous glucose monitoring A is a CGM device recommended for adults with diabetes on multiple daily injections or continuous subcutaneous insulin infusion.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-00f6c2252dc945e977b3a2b2f495ffe0</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/blood glucose monitoring.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786335922</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
