<node id="BGM">
  <data key="d0">BGM</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">BGM stands for Blood Glucose Monitoring, the practice of intermittent finger‑stick glucose testing.&lt;SEP&gt;BGM (blood glucose monitoring) devices are used for measuring glucose levels via finger‑stick tests.&lt;SEP&gt;Point‑of‑care blood glucose monitoring, the approved method for glucose measurement in hospitals.&lt;SEP&gt;Blood Glucose Monitoring, a method of measuring glucose levels, used in combination with A1C for glycemic control.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c9bc5d11c9f848439320623cad3d3a38&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6fe769b03fc66d4a691f3b7f741b92cb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-511f6be03d2ea98970bd4c1b29b3e5c8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-066ba9218f6293a2f3dc5459d69239cb</data>
