<node id="Ambulatory Glucose Profile">
  <data key="d0">Ambulatory Glucose Profile</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Ambulatory Glucose Profile (AGP) is software that standardizes continuous glucose monitoring data, generating reports with metrics such as time‑in‑range, average glucose, and estimated hemoglobin A1c.&lt;SEP&gt;Ambulatory glucose profile is a data summary of glucose readings collected throughout daily life.&lt;SEP&gt;Ambulatory Glucose Profile is a data set generated by continuous glucose monitoring, showing glucose trends over time.&lt;SEP&gt;Ambulatory Glucose Profile is a visual cue report format suggested for summarizing data from all CGM devices on a single page.&lt;SEP&gt;A standardized report summarizing glucose data over time for clinical use.</data>
