<node id="N Engl J Med">
  <data key="d0">N Engl J Med</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">N Engl J Med, the abbreviation for the New England Journal of Medicine, is a leading, peer‑reviewed medical journal that publishes high‑impact clinical research across a broad range of therapeutic areas. The journal has published randomized trials and landmark studies on diabetes management, including investigations of intermittently scanned continuous glucose monitoring for type 1 diabetes, continuous glucose monitoring generally, and comparative research on diet versus gastric‑bypass surgery in diabetic patients. It also reported pivotal trials of the anti‑CD3 antibody teplizumab, including studies involving at‑risk relatives of individuals with type 1 diabetes. Additional notable publications in N Engl J Med cover severe hypoglycaemia, vascular events, and the effects of insulin‑pump interruption. The journal is frequently cited in reference lists and recognized as a primary source for cutting‑edge medical evidence.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-76eaa3af026fbb91a96f70d3502e809d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d3a9b76fabae2f788f96d06b7d98c924&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cc0d4df5f59432ca990767b120f983a7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ddc3658b93eb925d28d625c4e2ce652f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-acba683ee0809d1c3f6e35c228f485ac&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-703ccc96df3edd610232f0cca4bf7afa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-525031caa389d084bc170433212cdca8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c122c1c6d7dd36110b6ddba2c074d122&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d5ec01ed3c32ac663f3dc6cfa6fa09a3</data>
