<node id="Blood Glucose Monitoring (BGM)">
  <data key="d0">Blood Glucose Monitoring (BGM)</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Blood Glucose Monitoring (BGM) is a traditional finger‑stick method used to obtain plasma glucose readings for treatment decisions.&lt;SEP&gt;Blood Glucose Monitoring (BGM) is a method of measuring blood glucose levels, mentioned as a tool for insulin dose adjustments.&lt;SEP&gt;Blood Glucose Monitoring (BGM) is a method for measuring glucose levels before and after meals in diabetes management.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0fe1eff7b58582dec4c8ae7578e20e66&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-36ddeaa53bc38bee375d7ac6d71485d4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ba0417a72f50cf7ca66c87a351bd1ff8</data>
