<node id="HiperGlicemia">
  <data key="d0">HiperGlicemia</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">HiperGlicemia is a condition of high blood glucose, defined as a Glicemia level above 100 mg/dL or HI, which is above the detection limit of the device.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d6a0699569d4d9d7344609e3680eec66</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/HIPO_HIPER.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786337248</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="HI">
  <data key="d0">HI</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">HI is an abbreviation representing HiperGlicemia, indicating a glycemia level above the device’s detection limit.&lt;SEP&gt;An indicator shown by the glucose meter meaning the blood glucose level is too high, suggesting hyperglycemia.&lt;SEP&gt;Indicator on glucose meters meaning the measured glucose is above the device’s detectable range, signifying hyperglycemia.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d6a0699569d4d9d7344609e3680eec66&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5dce7a759a9de18a4d1bcc77a071fbe2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1136d6aac4c2e881387a4db1a0f4a3a3</data>
