  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Type 1 Diabetes (DMI)">
  <data key="d0">Type 1 Diabetes (DMI)</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Type 1 Diabetes, referred to as DMI, is a form of diabetes caused by immune-mediated destruction of insulin-producing cells in the Islets of Langerhans.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2d8f17f3f250a37a1effaaa88cc8b382</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/glicemias capilares.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786338524</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Type 2 Diabetes (DM2)">
  <data key="d0">Type 2 Diabetes (DM2)</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Type 2 Diabetes, referred to as DM2, is a form of diabetes characterized by insulin resistance and relative insulin deficiency.&lt;SEP&gt;Type 2 Diabetes (DM2) is another form of diabetes referenced in the guideline.&lt;SEP&gt;A chronic metabolic disease characterized by high blood glucose levels and insulin resistance.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2d8f17f3f250a37a1effaaa88cc8b382&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6d83801272f7a0ae0d797d60572fe578&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e428438c632682ef93541430ec497ed5</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/glicemias capilares.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Metas glicêmicas/Metas no tratamento.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Diagnóstico de diabetes mellitus.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786372024</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Macrovascular Disease">
  <data key="d0">Macrovascular Disease</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Macrovascular disease refers to large vessel complications associated with diabetes, contributing to increased mortality.&lt;SEP&gt;Macrovascular Disease refers to large‑vessel complications associated with diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2d8f17f3f250a37a1effaaa88cc8b382&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9ab98b1c07f7bbaa3ad28fb83167f489</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/glicemias capilares.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377388</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Microvascular Disease">
  <data key="d0">Microvascular Disease</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Microvascular disease refers to small vessel complications associated with diabetes, contributing to increased mortality.&lt;SEP&gt;Microvascular Disease denotes small‑vessel complications linked to diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2d8f17f3f250a37a1effaaa88cc8b382&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9ab98b1c07f7bbaa3ad28fb83167f489</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/glicemias capilares.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377388</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Metabolic Memory Theory">
  <data key="d0">Metabolic Memory Theory</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Metabolic Memory Theory proposes that prior hyperglycemic conditions cause lasting cellular changes through advanced glycation end-products acting on RAGE receptors.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2d8f17f3f250a37a1effaaa88cc8b382</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/glicemias capilares.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786338524</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="RAGE Receptor">
  <data key="d0">RAGE Receptor</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">RAGE receptors are cellular receptors that bind advanced glycation end-products, triggering oxidative stress in target organ cells.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2d8f17f3f250a37a1effaaa88cc8b382</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/glicemias capilares.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786338524</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Epigenetic Modulation">
  <data key="d0">Epigenetic Modulation</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Epigenetic modulation involves changes in gene expression, such as activation of pro-inflammatory genes, driven by oxidative stress.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2d8f17f3f250a37a1effaaa88cc8b382</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/glicemias capilares.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786338525</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Pro-inflammatory Genes">
  <data key="d0">Pro-inflammatory Genes</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Pro-inflammatory genes are activated through epigenetic modulation during diabetic metabolic disturbances.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2d8f17f3f250a37a1effaaa88cc8b382</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/glicemias capilares.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786338525</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Postprandial Glycemia">
  <data key="d0">Postprandial Glycemia</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Postprandial glycemia measures blood glucose fluctuations after meals, used to assess diabetes control.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2d8f17f3f250a37a1effaaa88cc8b382</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/glicemias capilares.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786338525</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Canine Pancreas Extract">
  <data key="d0">Canine Pancreas Extract</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Canine pancreas extract is a biological preparation used by Banting to treat diabetes in a dog.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2d8f17f3f250a37a1effaaa88cc8b382</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/glicemias capilares.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786338526</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Benedict's Test">
  <data key="d0">Benedict's Test</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Benedict's Test is a chemical assay that changes color in the presence of glucose, historically used to detect glycosuria.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2d8f17f3f250a37a1effaaa88cc8b382</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/glicemias capilares.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786338526</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Clinitest">
  <data key="d0">Clinitest</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Clinitest is an improved version of Benedict's Test used for detecting glycosuria.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2d8f17f3f250a37a1effaaa88cc8b382</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/glicemias capilares.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786338526</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Gelatest">
  <data key="d0">Gelatest</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Gelatest is another modified form of Benedict's Test for glycosuria detection.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2d8f17f3f250a37a1effaaa88cc8b382</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/glicemias capilares.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786338527</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Clinistix">
  <data key="d0">Clinistix</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Clinistix is a reagent strip test designed to detect glycosuria.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2d8f17f3f250a37a1effaaa88cc8b382</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/glicemias capilares.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786338527</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Combur-Test">
  <data key="d0">Combur-Test</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Combur-Test is a reagent strip test used for detecting glycosuria.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2d8f17f3f250a37a1effaaa88cc8b382</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/glicemias capilares.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786338527</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Glycosuria Test">
  <data key="d0">Glycosuria Test</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Glycosuria Test refers to methods, including reagent strips, used to detect glucose in urine.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2d8f17f3f250a37a1effaaa88cc8b382</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/glicemias capilares.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786338528</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Islets of Langerhans">
  <data key="d0">Islets of Langerhans</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Islets of Langerhans are clusters of insulin-producing cells in the pancreas, targeted in Type 1 Diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2d8f17f3f250a37a1effaaa88cc8b382</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/glicemias capilares.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786338528</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Clinical Reports">
  <data key="d0">Clinical Reports</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Clinical Reports are documented summaries of patient glucose data generated from continuous monitoring systems.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2d8f17f3f250a37a1effaaa88cc8b382</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/glicemias capilares.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786338528</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="1921 Milestone in Diabetes Treatment">
  <data key="d0">1921 Milestone in Diabetes Treatment</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">In 1921 Frederick Banting demonstrated the survival of a diabetic dog by injecting canine pancreas extract, marking a pivotal moment in diabetes research.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2d8f17f3f250a37a1effaaa88cc8b382</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/glicemias capilares.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786338528</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="1923 Insulin Commercialization">
  <data key="d0">1923 Insulin Commercialization</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">In 1923 Eli Lilly launched the first commercially available insulin product for human use.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2d8f17f3f250a37a1effaaa88cc8b382</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/glicemias capilares.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786338528</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="1925 Home Glycosuria Test Development">
  <data key="d0">1925 Home Glycosuria Test Development</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">In 1925 home tests for detecting glycosuria were created, requiring urine mixed with Benedict's solution in a test tube and producing color changes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2d8f17f3f250a37a1effaaa88cc8b382</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/glicemias capilares.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786338528</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="1964 Dextrostix Introduction">
  <data key="d0">1964 Dextrostix Introduction</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">In 1964 the Dextrostix capillary glucose test was introduced, employing oxidase/peroxidase reagents on a semipermeable membrane.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2d8f17f3f250a37a1effaaa88cc8b382</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/glicemias capilares.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786338528</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Diabetic Dog">
  <data key="d0">Diabetic Dog</data>
  <data key="d1">creature</data>
  <data key="d2">Diabetic Dog is the animal subject used by Frederick Banting in 1921 to demonstrate the effect of canine pancreas extract on diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2d8f17f3f250a37a1effaaa88cc8b382</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/glicemias capilares.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786338528</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Oxidase/Peroxidase Reagents">
  <data key="d0">Oxidase/Peroxidase Reagents</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Oxidase/Peroxidase Reagents are chemical substances used in capillary glucose tests to react with glucose and produce a measurable signal.&lt;SEP&gt;Oxidase/peroxidase reagents are chemicals employed in the Dextrostix reaction to interact with blood.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2d8f17f3f250a37a1effaaa88cc8b382&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7f716359c14483f9be36a73861d75008</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/glicemias capilares.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786338528</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Semipermeable Membrane">
  <data key="d0">Semipermeable Membrane</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Semipermeable Membrane is a thin barrier in the Dextrostix test that allows glucose to pass while blocking blood cells during measurement.&lt;SEP&gt;The semipermeable external membrane in Dextrostix blocks red blood cells while allowing glucose to pass.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2d8f17f3f250a37a1effaaa88cc8b382&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7f716359c14483f9be36a73861d75008</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/glicemias capilares.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786338528</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Test Tube">
  <data key="d0">Test Tube</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Test Tube is a small glass container used in the 1925 glycosuria assay to mix urine with Benedict's solution for colorimetric analysis.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2d8f17f3f250a37a1effaaa88cc8b382</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/glicemias capilares.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786338529</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Benedict's Solution">
  <data key="d0">Benedict's Solution</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Benedict's Solution is a chemical reagent that changes color in the presence of reducing sugars, forming the basis of the Benedict's Test for glycosuria.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2d8f17f3f250a37a1effaaa88cc8b382</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/glicemias capilares.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786338529</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Clinical Guidelines">
  <data key="d0">Clinical Guidelines</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Clinical Guidelines are recommendations that address the risk of hypoglycemia when targeting HbA1c levels.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a5f7cad1fb0e1a0a02f63b5928b8acd2</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/glicemias capilares.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786338529</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cobelli C">
  <data key="d0">Cobelli C</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Cobelli C is an author cited for the adaptation of Figure 2.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a5f7cad1fb0e1a0a02f63b5928b8acd2</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/glicemias capilares.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786338530</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="SMCG Devices">
  <data key="d0">SMCG Devices</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">SMCG Devices are modern continuous glucose monitoring devices that generate glucose data.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a5f7cad1fb0e1a0a02f63b5928b8acd2</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/glicemias capilares.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786338530</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Estimated HbA1c (eA1C)">
  <data key="d0">Estimated HbA1c (eA1C)</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Estimated HbA1c (eA1C) is a calculated HbA1c value derived from average glucose measured by SMCG devices.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a5f7cad1fb0e1a0a02f63b5928b8acd2</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/glicemias capilares.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786338530</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Glucose Management Indicator (GMI)">
  <data key="d0">Glucose Management Indicator (GMI)</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Glucose Management Indicator (GMI) is an indicator of glucose control based on average glucose values.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a5f7cad1fb0e1a0a02f63b5928b8acd2</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/glicemias capilares.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786338530</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Diabetes Mellitus (DM)">
  <data key="d0">Diabetes Mellitus (DM)</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Diabetes Mellitus is a chronic disease characterized by impaired glucose regulation.&lt;SEP&gt;Diabetes Mellitus is the chronic condition defined by persistent hyperglycemia.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a5f7cad1fb0e1a0a02f63b5928b8acd2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5e551f4b7f03919afc1d663b3b2a2efa</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/glicemias capilares.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Diagnóstico de diabetes mellitus.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786372033</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Wang et al.">
  <data key="d0">Wang et al.</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Wang et al. are researchers who conducted a study on the relationship between HbA1c levels and health outcomes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a5f7cad1fb0e1a0a02f63b5928b8acd2</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/glicemias capilares.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786338531</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Capillary Glucose (GC)">
  <data key="d0">Capillary Glucose (GC)</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Capillary Glucose (GC) is the glucose concentration measured from a drop of capillary blood.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a5f7cad1fb0e1a0a02f63b5928b8acd2</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/glicemias capilares.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786338532</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Plasma Glucose Measurement">
  <data key="d0">Plasma Glucose Measurement</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Plasma Glucose Measurement is the quantification of glucose concentration in blood plasma, typically ranging from 10 to 600 mg/dL.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a5f7cad1fb0e1a0a02f63b5928b8acd2</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/glicemias capilares.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786338532</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Computerized Data Transfer">
  <data key="d0">Computerized Data Transfer</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Computerized Data Transfer is a method that moves glucose monitoring results from a device to a computer using specific software.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a5f7cad1fb0e1a0a02f63b5928b8acd2</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/glicemias capilares.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786338532</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Specific Software">
  <data key="d0">Specific Software</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Specific Software refers to programs designed to receive and process glucose monitoring data.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a5f7cad1fb0e1a0a02f63b5928b8acd2</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/glicemias capilares.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786338532</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="14-Day Analysis Period">
  <data key="d0">14-Day Analysis Period</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">The 14‑Day Analysis Period is a recommended duration for analyzing glucose data and predicting the next 30 days.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a5f7cad1fb0e1a0a02f63b5928b8acd2</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/glicemias capilares.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786338532</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Red Blood Cells">
  <data key="d0">Red Blood Cells</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Red blood cells are blocked by the semipermeable membrane during the Dextrostix test.&lt;SEP&gt;Red blood cells are the cellular component of blood whose lifespan influences HbA1c measurements.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a5f7cad1fb0e1a0a02f63b5928b8acd2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7f716359c14483f9be36a73861d75008</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/glicemias capilares.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786338533</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Fragility Marker">
  <data key="d0">Fragility Marker</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Fragility Marker is a clinical indicator associated with very low HbA1c levels indicating patient vulnerability.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a5f7cad1fb0e1a0a02f63b5928b8acd2</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/glicemias capilares.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786338533</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="J-shaped Relationship">
  <data key="d0">J-shaped Relationship</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">J-shaped Relationship describes the pattern where both low (&lt;6%) and high (&gt;8%) HbA1c levels are linked to increased mortality.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a5f7cad1fb0e1a0a02f63b5928b8acd2</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/glicemias capilares.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786338533</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="All Types of Diabetes">
  <data key="d0">All Types of Diabetes</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">All Types of Diabetes refers to the various forms of diabetes mellitus for which AMGC is recommended.</data>
