  <data key="d0">DCCT</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">The Diabetes Control and Complications Trial (DCCT) established a direct relationship between HbA1c levels and microvascular complications in diabetes.&lt;SEP&gt;DCCT (Diabetes Control and Complications Trial) was a clinical trial that showed benefits of maintaining HbA1c below 7%.&lt;SEP&gt;The Diabetes Control and Complications Trial (DCCT) was a landmark study of intensive glycemic control in type 1 diabetes that showed a trend toward lower risk of cardiovascular events.&lt;SEP&gt;The Diabetes Control and Complications Trial (DCCT) is a landmark study of intensive diabetes treatment and its long‑term effects on complications.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7f716359c14483f9be36a73861d75008&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9dee0a79e4583f41e757f9a20f56f397&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f99d05e1089d59496d56d86ff40197cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-acba683ee0809d1c3f6e35c228f485ac</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/glicemias capilares.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Metas glicêmicas/Metas no tratamento.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Metas glicêmicas/metas cuidado do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786372142</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="TID Exchange">
  <data key="d0">TID Exchange</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">The TID Exchange study analyzed American databases and found that only a minority of adults and youth with type 1 diabetes meet ADA HbA1c targets.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7f716359c14483f9be36a73861d75008</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/glicemias capilares.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786338541</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="EASD">
  <data key="d0">EASD</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">The European Association for the Study of Diabetes (EASD) recommends HbA1c monitoring in its diabetes care guidelines.&lt;SEP&gt;EASD is the abbreviation for the European Association for the Study of Diabetes, co‑author of a consensus report on type 1 diabetes management.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7f716359c14483f9be36a73861d75008&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8ba9c9c7fe9dd4e901eb52088f3d59f8</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/glicemias capilares.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377365</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Point of Care">
  <data key="d0">Point of Care</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Point‑of‑Care (POC) testing measures HbA1c from a small drop of blood at the site of patient care without fasting.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7f716359c14483f9be36a73861d75008</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/glicemias capilares.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786338541</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Variability (VG)">
  <data key="d0">Variability (VG)</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Variability (VG) denotes fluctuations in glucose levels throughout the day.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7f716359c14483f9be36a73861d75008</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/glicemias capilares.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786338542</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hemoglobinopathies">
  <data key="d0">Hemoglobinopathies</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Hemoglobinopathies are blood disorders that can alter HbA1c measurements.&lt;SEP&gt;Hemoglobinopathies are inherited hemoglobin disorders that interfere with HbA1c accuracy.&lt;SEP&gt;Hemoglobinopathies are genetic blood disorders that can interfere with A1C accuracy.&lt;SEP&gt;Hemoglobinopathies are genetic blood disorders that may interfere with A1C assay accuracy.&lt;SEP&gt;Genetic disorders of hemoglobin, such as sickle cell disease, that can affect A1C interpretation.&lt;SEP&gt;Hemoglobinopathies are blood disorders for which only interference‑free A1C assays are appropriate in children.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7f716359c14483f9be36a73861d75008&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-23ad6eb7138be249f01b479174a34076&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-44888abd4ca8a1953f751ed6c41922e6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d01033177672e6c36e0a368db88e586d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3cc61bc2e95346d553972b4371912e7f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0631ff2b95dd459677eaaebe9283a776</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/glicemias capilares.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Diagnóstico de diabetes mellitus.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377222</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Gestation">
  <data key="d0">Gestation</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Gestation (pregnancy) can influence HbA1c values due to altered red cell turnover.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7f716359c14483f9be36a73861d75008</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/glicemias capilares.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786338542</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Uremia">
  <data key="d0">Uremia</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Uremia, a condition of kidney failure, can interfere with HbA1c accuracy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7f716359c14483f9be36a73861d75008</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/glicemias capilares.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786338543</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Basal Glucose">
  <data key="d0">Basal Glucose</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Basal glucose is the reference glucose level used to compare Dextrostix measurements, which the test overestimated.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7f716359c14483f9be36a73861d75008</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/glicemias capilares.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786338543</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Glucosuria">
  <data key="d0">Glucosuria</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Glucosuria is the presence of glucose in urine, referenced as a newer method of analysis in glucose monitoring.&lt;SEP&gt;Glucosuria is the presence of glucose in urine, noted as a feature of MODY-HNF1A.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7f716359c14483f9be36a73861d75008&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e26b32d53b78f97e8d7fa8b815f2cc87</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/glicemias capilares.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786373057</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Ear Lobe">
  <data key="d0">Ear Lobe</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">The ear lobe is the body site where GlucoTrack devices are placed to estimate blood glucose non‑invasively.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7f716359c14483f9be36a73861d75008</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/glicemias capilares.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786338543</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hospital Hyperglycemia">
  <data key="d0">Hospital Hyperglycemia</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Hospital hyperglycemia is a condition mentioned as a scenario where point‑of‑care HbA1c testing can aid decision‑making.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7f716359c14483f9be36a73861d75008</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/glicemias capilares.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786338543</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Emergency Department">
  <data key="d0">Emergency Department</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">Emergency department (pronto‑socorro) is listed as a setting where rapid HbA1c testing may be useful.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7f716359c14483f9be36a73861d75008</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/glicemias capilares.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786338544</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Emergency Surgery">
  <data key="d0">Emergency Surgery</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">Emergency surgery in a patient with diabetes is cited as a situation benefiting from point‑of‑care HbA1c testing.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7f716359c14483f9be36a73861d75008</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/glicemias capilares.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786338544</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Clinical Study Screening">
  <data key="d0">Clinical Study Screening</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Screening of clinical studies is mentioned as an application for point‑of‑care HbA1c testing.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7f716359c14483f9be36a73861d75008</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/glicemias capilares.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786338544</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Systematic Review 2017">
  <data key="d0">Systematic Review 2017</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">A systematic review and meta‑analysis published in 2017 demonstrated the efficacy and safety of point‑of‑care HbA1c testing.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7f716359c14483f9be36a73861d75008</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/glicemias capilares.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786338544</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Red Blood Cell Turnover Variability">
  <data key="d0">Red Blood Cell Turnover Variability</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Variation in the lifespan of red blood cells causes inter‑individual differences affecting HbA1c measurements.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7f716359c14483f9be36a73861d75008</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/glicemias capilares.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786338544</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="ADA HbA1c Targets">
  <data key="d0">ADA HbA1c Targets</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The ADA defines target HbA1c levels for diabetes management, referenced as goals in the TID Exchange study.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7f716359c14483f9be36a73861d75008</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/glicemias capilares.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786338544</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="patient">
  <data key="d0">patient</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7ac99b8588a8c480f44a5519509f7713</data>
  <data key="d2">tR‑SMCG delivers continuous glucose data directly to the patient via a receiver or insulin pump.</data>
  <data key="d1">UNKNOWN</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/glicemias capilares.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786338592</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="health professionals">
  <data key="d0">health professionals</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7ac99b8588a8c480f44a5519509f7713</data>
  <data key="d2">retro‑SMCG enables health professionals to analyze stored glucose patterns for treatment adjustments.</data>
  <data key="d1">UNKNOWN</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/glicemias capilares.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786338592</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="calibration">
  <data key="d0">calibration</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7ac99b8588a8c480f44a5519509f7713</data>
  <data key="d2">SFMG is calibrated at the factory and therefore does not require additional user calibration.</data>
  <data key="d1">UNKNOWN</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/glicemias capilares.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786338592</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="sensor lifespan">
  <data key="d0">sensor lifespan</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7ac99b8588a8c480f44a5519509f7713</data>
  <data key="d2">The subcutaneous stability of GOx is linked to the lifespan of each SMCG sensor.</data>
  <data key="d1">UNKNOWN</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/glicemias capilares.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786338594</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="hypoglycemia incidence">
  <data key="d0">hypoglycemia incidence</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7ac99b8588a8c480f44a5519509f7713</data>
  <data key="d2">retro‑SMCG can reduce the incidence of hypoglycemic episodes in patients with Diabetes Type 1 and Diabetes Type 2.</data>
  <data key="d1">UNKNOWN</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/glicemias capilares.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786338595</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="night period">
  <data key="d0">night period</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7ac99b8588a8c480f44a5519509f7713</data>
  <data key="d2">AMGD provides limited glucose monitoring coverage during the night period.</data>
  <data key="d1">UNKNOWN</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/glicemias capilares.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786338596</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="post‑prandial period">
  <data key="d0">post‑prandial period</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7ac99b8588a8c480f44a5519509f7713</data>
  <data key="d2">AMGD provides limited glucose monitoring coverage during the post‑prandial period.</data>
  <data key="d1">UNKNOWN</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/glicemias capilares.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786338597</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="tR‑SMCG">
  <data key="d0">tR‑SMCG</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7ac99b8588a8c480f44a5519509f7713</data>
  <data key="d2">tR‑SMCG delivers continuous glucose data directly to the patient.</data>
  <data key="d1">UNKNOWN</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/glicemias capilares.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786338597</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="retro‑SMCG">
  <data key="d0">retro‑SMCG</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7ac99b8588a8c480f44a5519509f7713</data>
  <data key="d2">retro‑SMCG data are analyzed by health professionals to adjust diabetes treatment.</data>
  <data key="d1">UNKNOWN</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/glicemias capilares.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786338599</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="metabolic control">
  <data key="d0">metabolic control</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7ac99b8588a8c480f44a5519509f7713</data>
  <data key="d2">Continuous use of SMCG sensors aims to improve metabolic control in individuals with diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d1">UNKNOWN</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/GLICEMIAS CAPILARES/glicemias capilares.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786338600</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Sensores De Glicose">
  <data key="d0">Sensores De Glicose</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Sensores de glicose are devices that continuously monitor blood glucose levels.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-82e0d8e22a06c73855abed11561ce467</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Documento sem título.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1786368415</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Grupo De Pacientes">
  <data key="d0">Grupo De Pacientes</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Grupo de pacientes categorizes individuals (adults, children, elderly) for glycemic target recommendations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-82e0d8e22a06c73855abed11561ce467</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Documento sem título.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1786368415</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Adultos Em Geral (DM1 Ou DM2)">
  <data key="d0">Adultos Em Geral (DM1 Ou DM2)</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Adultos em geral (DM1 ou DM2) are adult patients with type 1 or type 2 diabetes and have specific HbA1c and glucose targets.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-82e0d8e22a06c73855abed11561ce467</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Documento sem título.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1786368415</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Crianças E Adolescentes (DM1)">
  <data key="d0">Crianças E Adolescentes (DM1)</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Crianças e adolescentes (DM1) are young patients with type 1 diabetes and have distinct glycemic goals.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-82e0d8e22a06c73855abed11561ce467</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Documento sem título.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1786368415</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Idosos Saudáveis">
  <data key="d0">Idosos Saudáveis</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Idosos saudáveis are healthy older adults with individualized glycemic targets.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-82e0d8e22a06c73855abed11561ce467</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Documento sem título.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1786368415</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Idosos Com Doenças Ou Limitações">
  <data key="d0">Idosos Com Doenças Ou Limitações</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Idosos com doenças ou limitações are elderly individuals with health issues and adjusted glucose goals.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-82e0d8e22a06c73855abed11561ce467</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Documento sem título.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1786368415</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Idosos Frágeis / Com Doenças Graves">
  <data key="d0">Idosos Frágeis / Com Doenças Graves</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Idosos frágeis / com doenças graves are frail elderly patients requiring flexible and comfort‑focused glycemic management.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-82e0d8e22a06c73855abed11561ce467</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Documento sem título.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1786368415</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Suor Frio">
  <data key="d0">Suor Frio</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Suor frio is a common symptom of hypoglycemia.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-82e0d8e22a06c73855abed11561ce467</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Documento sem título.docx</data>
  <data key="d5">1786368415</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Fome Repentina">
  <data key="d0">Fome Repentina</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Fome repentina is a common symptom of hypoglycemia.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-82e0d8e22a06c73855abed11561ce467</data>
