  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="0.86 Hazard Ratio">
  <data key="d0">0.86 Hazard Ratio</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">A hazard ratio of 0.86 (95 % CI 0.77‑0.97) is reported for microvascular events under intensive glucose control.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4f9624abde6cf128707fcc0466a4c9a7</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Metas glicêmicas/Metas no tratamento.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786370028</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="HbA1c Target &lt; 7.0 %">
  <data key="d0">HbA1c Target &lt; 7.0 %</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">HbA1c target of less than 7.0 % is recommended for all diabetes patients to prevent macrovascular complications when severe hypoglycemia is unlikely.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4f9624abde6cf128707fcc0466a4c9a7</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Metas glicêmicas/Metas no tratamento.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786370028</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="HbA1c Target &lt; 6.5 %">
  <data key="d0">HbA1c Target &lt; 6.5 %</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">HbA1c target of less than 6.5 % is a more stringent goal proposed for some type 1 diabetes patients when hypoglycemia risk is acceptable.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4f9624abde6cf128707fcc0466a4c9a7</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Metas glicêmicas/Metas no tratamento.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786370028</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
