<node id="International Expert Committee">
  <data key="d0">International Expert Committee</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">The International Expert Committee is an organization that, in 2009, suggested HbA1c ≥6.5% as a diagnostic criterion for diabetes mellitus.&lt;SEP&gt;The International Expert Committee is a panel that produced a report on using the A1c assay for diagnosing diabetes.&lt;SEP&gt;The International Expert Committee added A1C to diabetes diagnostic criteria to increase screening.&lt;SEP&gt;International Expert Committee produced a report on the role of the A1C assay in diabetes diagnosis, published in Diabetes Care.\</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6a92f811a7d2d835dc4b730c9bbf08cf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8393954b021d0ad02018d1a449e0cc93&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-44888abd4ca8a1953f751ed6c41922e6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3a15ed0aa8749d4f76e8d725e8752873</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Diagnóstico de diabetes mellitus.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377218</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="TTGO-2h">
  <data key="d0">TTGO-2h</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">TTGO-2h is a two‑hour oral glucose tolerance test used for diagnosing diabetes mellitus.&lt;SEP&gt;TTGO-2h is the two‑hour oral glucose tolerance test used as a reference standard for diagnosing diabetes mellitus.&lt;SEP&gt;TTGO-2h is the traditional two‑hour oral glucose tolerance test historically used for diabetes diagnosis.&lt;SEP&gt;TTGO-2h is the two‑hour oral glucose tolerance test used as a comparative marker in diabetes prediction studies.&lt;SEP&gt;The two‑hour oral glucose tolerance test measurement used to assess glucose metabolism.&lt;SEP&gt;TTGO-2h is an alternative two‑hour oral glucose tolerance test method that can be used for diabetes diagnosis.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6a92f811a7d2d835dc4b730c9bbf08cf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-80893468bbc3744e2e535806ea31e346&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-23ad6eb7138be249f01b479174a34076&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2faebf8275a86cd8d9995c769b0926a3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-078f5907e86c2158587c79b26b0cd683&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e428438c632682ef93541430ec497ed5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c92d117f7109ea1ce6995f23bc680ce3</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Diagnóstico de diabetes mellitus.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786371919</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="2-Hour Glucose">
  <data key="d0">2-Hour Glucose</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">2‑Hour Glucose is the blood glucose level measured two hours after an oral glucose load.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6a92f811a7d2d835dc4b730c9bbf08cf</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Diagnóstico de diabetes mellitus.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786371920</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Coronary Disease">
  <data key="d0">Coronary Disease</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Coronary Disease denotes disease of the coronary arteries, a cardiovascular complication linked to high glucose levels.&lt;SEP&gt;Coronary disease is a cardiovascular condition whose risk was found to be significantly higher in individuals with fasting glucose (GJ) ≥126 mg/dL.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6a92f811a7d2d835dc4b730c9bbf08cf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5e551f4b7f03919afc1d663b3b2a2efa</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Diagnóstico de diabetes mellitus.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786371920</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Vascular Death">
  <data key="d0">Vascular Death</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Vascular death denotes mortality caused by vascular diseases and its risk doubled in persons with GJ ≥126 mg/dL.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6a92f811a7d2d835dc4b730c9bbf08cf</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Diagnóstico de diabetes mellitus.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786371921</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="HbA1c ≥6.5% Diagnostic Cutoff">
  <data key="d0">HbA1c ≥6.5% Diagnostic Cutoff</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">HbA1c ≥6.5% is the diagnostic threshold recommended for identifying diabetes mellitus.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6a92f811a7d2d835dc4b730c9bbf08cf</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Diagnóstico de diabetes mellitus.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786371921</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="GJ ≥126 mg/dL">
  <data key="d0">GJ ≥126 mg/dL</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">GJ ≥126 mg/dL is a fasting glucose level threshold associated with increased risk of coronary disease, stroke, and vascular death.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6a92f811a7d2d835dc4b730c9bbf08cf</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Diagnóstico de diabetes mellitus.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786371921</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="GJ ≤100 mg/dL">
  <data key="d0">GJ ≤100 mg/dL</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">GJ ≤100 mg/dL is a lower fasting glucose level used as a reference comparison in risk assessments.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6a92f811a7d2d835dc4b730c9bbf08cf</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Diagnóstico de diabetes mellitus.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786371921</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="TTGO-1h Cut-off 209 mg/dL">
  <data key="d0">TTGO-1h Cut-off 209 mg/dL</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">TTGO-1h Cut-off 209 mg/dL is the threshold value for the one‑hour oral glucose tolerance test considered in recent evaluations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6a92f811a7d2d835dc4b730c9bbf08cf</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Diagnóstico de diabetes mellitus.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786371922</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Odds Ratio (OR)">
  <data key="d0">Odds Ratio (OR)</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Odds Ratio (OR) is a statistical measure reported in the studies to quantify the association between HbA1c levels and diabetic retinopathy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6a92f811a7d2d835dc4b730c9bbf08cf</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Diagnóstico de diabetes mellitus.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786371922</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Undiagnosed Diabetes Prevalence (Single GJ)">
  <data key="d0">Undiagnosed Diabetes Prevalence (Single GJ)</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Undiagnosed Diabetes Prevalence (Single GJ) is the estimated 3.7% prevalence of diabetes when diagnosis relies on a single fasting‑glucose measurement.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6a92f811a7d2d835dc4b730c9bbf08cf</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Diagnóstico de diabetes mellitus.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786371922</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
