<node id="Prediabetes">
  <data key="d0">Prediabetes</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Prediabetes is a metabolic condition characterized by elevated blood glucose levels that do not yet meet the diagnostic thresholds for diabetes. The state is defined by specific laboratory criteria: an impaired fasting glucose (IFG) level, an impaired glucose tolerance (IGT) measured by a 2‑hour plasma glucose test, or an elevated glycated hemoglobin (A1C) value typically ranging from 5.7 % to 6.4 %. These glycemic markers signal early dysregulation of glucose metabolism and denote a higher risk of progressing to type 2 diabetes.

Because prediabetes represents a preclinical or early stage of dysglycemia, it is a target for screening and preventive interventions. Individuals with a history of gestational diabetes mellitus (GDM) are especially prone to develop prediabetes, and lifelong monitoring is recommended for this population. Screening programs aim to identify the condition promptly so that lifestyle modifications, pharmacologic therapy, or other risk‑reduction strategies can be instituted before overt diabetes develops.

Overall, prediabetes reflects a state of heightened diabetes risk that can be detected through routine testing of fasting plasma glucose, 2‑hour oral glucose tolerance, or A1C. Early identification provides an opportunity for intervention to delay or prevent the onset of type 2 diabetes, particularly among those with prior GDM or other risk factors.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8393954b021d0ad02018d1a449e0cc93&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-44aa59c0e5cc620a11b8fb017d1aefcf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-090b8f9281aa75054311d8f275a2c8f8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-59dd4faf2a2706d073fdb93e1a29da81&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ca8741dfdb9ff0f12f049953db6cb9c0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3cc61bc2e95346d553972b4371912e7f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2a430bf53157529ccb22e67171fb28e5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ae844f5b99d595c38f74e375112238e6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1a111d4b40ec241cf54126f594a80308&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9eb02ab1ab7d834858bf60a8b402e6ea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0631ff2b95dd459677eaaebe9283a776&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a22fadf52eaea018160e4dd41d1d39b8</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Diagnóstico de diabetes mellitus.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
