<node id="TTGO-1h">
  <data key="d0">TTGO-1h</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">TTGO‑1h is a one‑hour oral glucose tolerance test (OGTT) designed to measure plasma glucose levels after a single hour of glucose ingestion. It is employed as a diagnostic tool for diabetes mellitus, with particular emphasis on identifying type 2 diabetes (DM2) and detecting pre‑diabetes.  

The test is recommended for screening individuals who may have undiagnosed DM2, as well as for assessing future risk of developing the disease. Clinical evaluations have highlighted its practicality and suitability for routine diabetes screening, positioning TTGO‑1h as a preferred method for early detection of abnormal glucose metabolism.  

By providing a concise, one‑hour measurement, TTGO‑1h facilitates the identification of persons at higher risk for type 2 diabetes, supporting timely intervention and management strategies for both overt diabetes and its pre‑diabetic stages.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6a92f811a7d2d835dc4b730c9bbf08cf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-80893468bbc3744e2e535806ea31e346&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-23ad6eb7138be249f01b479174a34076&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2faebf8275a86cd8d9995c769b0926a3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-078f5907e86c2158587c79b26b0cd683&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e428438c632682ef93541430ec497ed5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c92d117f7109ea1ce6995f23bc680ce3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3c6dca13b685243e63fb6f24f7cb301d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Diagnóstico de diabetes mellitus.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786371970</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
