<node id="Estudo ERICA">
  <data key="d0">Estudo ERICA</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">The ERICA study (Estudo dos Riscos Cardiovasculares em Adolescentes) evaluated Brazilian adolescents and reported a 3.3 % prevalence of type 2 diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e7b4535dbb2554b84c7a2e024c4b82c4</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Diagnóstico de diabetes mellitus.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786371975</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Prevalência de DM2 nos EUA 2001‑2009">
  <data key="d0">Prevalência de DM2 nos EUA 2001‑2009</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">U.S. youth prevalence of type 2 diabetes rose from 0.34 to 0.46 per 1,000 between 2001 and 2009, a 30.5 % increase.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e7b4535dbb2554b84c7a2e024c4b82c4</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Diagnóstico de diabetes mellitus.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786371975</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Prevalência de DM2 no Brasil">
  <data key="d0">Prevalência de DM2 no Brasil</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">In Brazil, the ERICA study found a 3.3 % prevalence of type 2 diabetes among adolescents aged 12‑17.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e7b4535dbb2554b84c7a2e024c4b82c4</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Diagnóstico de diabetes mellitus.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786371975</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Obesidade">
  <data key="d0">Obesidade</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Obesity, especially severe obesity, is a major risk factor for type 2 diabetes in children and adolescents.&lt;SEP&gt;Obesidade is excess body weight that is strongly linked to Diabetes Tipo 2.&lt;SEP&gt;Obesidade is the condition of obesity, referenced alongside overweight in diabetes prevalence statistics.&lt;SEP&gt;Obesidade is obesity, identified as a risk factor for DM2 in adolescents.&lt;SEP&gt;Obesidade denotes excess body weight and is a typical characteristic of Diabetes Tipo 2 but does not exclude Diabetes Tipo 1.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e7b4535dbb2554b84c7a2e024c4b82c4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2e6267110f4ae5f4df4c49c0653a09b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-858cd6ea7fba353827f5ab95be1157ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-72da6fb8b6a9ed059d146b43a3174f90&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ed325288512881a80fa42dba504c4bff</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Diagnóstico de diabetes mellitus.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786372999</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Histórico Familiar de DM">
  <data key="d0">Histórico Familiar de DM</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A family history of diabetes adds an additive risk for developing type 2 diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e7b4535dbb2554b84c7a2e024c4b82c4</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Diagnóstico de diabetes mellitus.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786371976</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Afro‑Americanos">
  <data key="d0">Afro‑Americanos</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Afro‑American ethnicity is associated with lower insulin sensitivity and higher prevalence of type 2 diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e7b4535dbb2554b84c7a2e024c4b82c4</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Diagnóstico de diabetes mellitus.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786371976</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Caucasianos">
  <data key="d0">Caucasianos</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Caucasian ethnicity serves as a reference group with higher insulin sensitivity compared to Afro‑Americans.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e7b4535dbb2554b84c7a2e024c4b82c4</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Diagnóstico de diabetes mellitus.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786371976</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Antiretroviral Medications">
  <data key="d0">Antiretroviral Medications</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Antiretroviral medications are newer drugs used to treat HIV, whose potential association with increased risk of type 2 diabetes is currently uncertain.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e7b4535dbb2554b84c7a2e024c4b82c4</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Diagnóstico de diabetes mellitus.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786371977</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Overweight">
  <data key="d0">Overweight</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Overweight describes individuals with excess body weight, noted as a risk factor for type 2 diabetes, especially when combined with familial history.&lt;SEP&gt;A condition of excess body weight, identified as a risk factor for type 2 diabetes in children and adolescents.&lt;SEP&gt;Overweight describes individuals whose body weight exceeds standard percentiles, identified as a risk factor for insulin resistance and type 2 diabetes.&lt;SEP&gt;Overweight is a condition that, together with obesity, qualifies adults for diabetes screening.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e7b4535dbb2554b84c7a2e024c4b82c4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-343246c2eef6e8430b581340d6cd4762&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-55e58732610596ce9a8f3145d34f75a7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1a111d4b40ec241cf54126f594a80308</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Diagnóstico de diabetes mellitus.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377371</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Severe Obesity">
  <data key="d0">Severe Obesity</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Severe obesity denotes a high degree of excess body fat, present in 38% of patients with type 2 diabetes and linked to higher disease risk.&lt;SEP&gt;Extreme obesity noted as a clinical condition linked to insulin resistance.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e7b4535dbb2554b84c7a2e024c4b82c4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ca8741dfdb9ff0f12f049953db6cb9c0</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Diagnóstico de diabetes mellitus.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377327</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Caucasian">
  <data key="d0">Caucasian</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Caucasian refers to individuals of European ancestry, used as a reference group for insulin sensitivity and diabetes prevalence.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e7b4535dbb2554b84c7a2e024c4b82c4</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Diagnóstico de diabetes mellitus.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786371977</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hispanic">
  <data key="d0">Hispanic</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Hispanic denotes individuals of Latin American origin, reported with higher prevalence of type 2 diabetes among youth.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e7b4535dbb2554b84c7a2e024c4b82c4</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Diagnóstico de diabetes mellitus.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786371977</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Black">
  <data key="d0">Black</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Black refers to individuals of African descent, shown to have higher prevalence of type 2 diabetes among youth.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e7b4535dbb2554b84c7a2e024c4b82c4</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Diagnóstico de diabetes mellitus.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786371977</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Amerindian">
  <data key="d0">Amerindian</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Amerindian denotes indigenous peoples of the Americas, reported with the highest prevalence of type 2 diabetes among youth.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e7b4535dbb2554b84c7a2e024c4b82c4</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Diagnóstico de diabetes mellitus.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786371978</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Gestational Diabetes History">
  <data key="d0">Gestational Diabetes History</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Gestational diabetes history is a prior occurrence of diabetes during pregnancy, identified as a risk factor for later type 2 diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e7b4535dbb2554b84c7a2e024c4b82c4</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Diagnóstico de diabetes mellitus.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786371978</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Prior Glucose Intolerance">
  <data key="d0">Prior Glucose Intolerance</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Prior glucose intolerance indicates previous impaired glucose tolerance, listed as a risk factor for type 2 diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e7b4535dbb2554b84c7a2e024c4b82c4</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Diagnóstico de diabetes mellitus.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786371978</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="U.S. Youth Diabetes Study 2001‑2009">
  <data key="d0">U.S. Youth Diabetes Study 2001‑2009</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">The U.S. Youth Diabetes Study 2001‑2009 evaluated diabetes prevalence among youths, finding a 30.5% increase over the period.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e7b4535dbb2554b84c7a2e024c4b82c4</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Diagnóstico de diabetes mellitus.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786371978</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Pre-diabetes">
  <data key="d0">Pre-diabetes</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Pre‑diabetes is a metabolic condition with blood glucose levels higher than normal but below the diabetes threshold.&lt;SEP&gt;Pre-diabetes is a metabolic condition identified as a precursor to Type 2 Diabetes, discussed in relation to diagnostic thresholds.&lt;SEP&gt;Pre-diabetes refers to an intermediate glycemic state defined by fasting glucose and HbA1c thresholds, considered for additional testing.&lt;SEP&gt;Pre-diabetes is described as a heterogeneous group with varying risk of progression to DM2, influencing recommended screening frequency.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-80893468bbc3744e2e535806ea31e346&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-23ad6eb7138be249f01b479174a34076&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2faebf8275a86cd8d9995c769b0926a3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c92d117f7109ea1ce6995f23bc680ce3</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Diagnóstico de diabetes mellitus.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786371979</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="National Diabetes Data Group">
  <data key="d0">National Diabetes Data Group</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">The National Diabetes Data Group (NDDG) issued earlier recommendations on intermediate glucose values during TTGO‑2h for diabetes diagnosis.&lt;SEP&gt;Group that provides an alternative set of diagnostic thresholds for the 3‑hour 100‑g OGTT.&lt;SEP&gt;The National Diabetes Data Group is an organization that established classification and diagnosis criteria for diabetes mellitus and glucose intolerance, referenced in gestational diabetes research.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-80893468bbc3744e2e535806ea31e346&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-49c21dd27a63d44c5d80b53aa7e1f48d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-037075addb77da4a5a1721a95ee298c0</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Diagnóstico de diabetes mellitus.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377419</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="San Antonio Heart Study">
  <data key="d0">San Antonio Heart Study</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">The San Antonio Heart Study is a longitudinal cohort that evaluated glycemic profiles of Mexican‑American participants using TTGO.&lt;SEP&gt;A prospective cohort study that evaluated TTGO‑1h glucose levels and the subsequent incidence of Type 2 Diabetes Mellitus.&lt;SEP&gt;San Antonio Heart Study is a longitudinal cohort study assessing the sensitivity of TTGO-1h, GJ, and TTGO-2h for predicting DM2.&lt;SEP&gt;A longitudinal study that observed normoglycemic individuals with TTGO‑2h and TTGO‑1h ≥ 155 mg/dl developing type 2 diabetes within 7–8 years, showing higher annual risk than those with TTGO‑1h &lt; 155 mg/dl.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-80893468bbc3744e2e535806ea31e346&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-23ad6eb7138be249f01b479174a34076&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e428438c632682ef93541430ec497ed5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3c6dca13b685243e63fb6f24f7cb301d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Diagnóstico de diabetes mellitus.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786371979</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Abdul‑Ghani et al.">
  <data key="d0">Abdul‑Ghani et al.</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Abdul‑Ghani and colleagues are researchers who evaluated TTGO results in 1,611 Mexican‑American participants without diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-80893468bbc3744e2e535806ea31e346</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Diagnóstico de diabetes mellitus.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786371979</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Botnia Study">
  <data key="d0">Botnia Study</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">The Botnia Study is a population‑based study included in a multicenter analysis of TTGO indices.&lt;SEP&gt;Botnia Study is a research investigation that evaluated the predictive performance of TTGO-1h versus other markers.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-80893468bbc3744e2e535806ea31e346&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-23ad6eb7138be249f01b479174a34076</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Diagnóstico de diabetes mellitus.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786371979</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Malmo Preventive Project">
  <data key="d0">Malmo Preventive Project</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">The Malmo Preventive Project (MPP) is a Swedish cohort combined with the Botnia Study to assess TTGO predictors.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-80893468bbc3744e2e535806ea31e346</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Diagnóstico de diabetes mellitus.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786371979</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Metanalysis of 35,551 Individuals">
  <data key="d0">Metanalysis of 35,551 Individuals</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">A meta‑analysis comprising 35,551 participants of multiple ethnicities evaluated TTGO‑1h thresholds for diabetes diagnosis.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-80893468bbc3744e2e535806ea31e346</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Diagnóstico de diabetes mellitus.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786371979</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="TTGO">
  <data key="d0">TTGO</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">TTGO (oral glucose tolerance test) is a diagnostic procedure for assessing glucose metabolism.&lt;SEP&gt;TTGO refers to the oral glucose tolerance test, a method used to assess glucose metabolism for diabetes diagnosis.&lt;SEP&gt;TTGO is the oral glucose tolerance test mentioned as less practical than fasting glucose or HbA1c for DM2 screening.&lt;SEP&gt;TTGO (oral glucose tolerance test) is a diagnostic test recommended, with TTGO‑1h preferred and TTGO‑2h as an alternative.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-80893468bbc3744e2e535806ea31e346&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2faebf8275a86cd8d9995c769b0926a3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-67792416bc5f0609842dd2a9940d8749&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c92d117f7109ea1ce6995f23bc680ce3</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Diagnóstico de diabetes mellitus.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786371979</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="209 mg/dL">
  <data key="d0">209 mg/dL</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">209 mg/dL is the glucose concentration threshold in TTGO‑1h used for diagnosing Type 2 Diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-80893468bbc3744e2e535806ea31e346</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Diagnóstico de diabetes mellitus.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786371979</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="155 mg/dL">
  <data key="d0">155 mg/dL</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">155 mg/dL is the glucose concentration threshold in TTGO‑1h used for detecting pre‑diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-80893468bbc3744e2e535806ea31e346</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Diagnóstico de diabetes mellitus.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786371980</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="200 mg/dL">
  <data key="d0">200 mg/dL</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">200 mg/dL is the glucose concentration threshold in TTGO‑2h used for diagnosing Type 2 Diabetes.&lt;SEP&gt;200 mg/dL is the numeric value defining the diagnostic glucose threshold for diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-80893468bbc3744e2e535806ea31e346&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6601fea85bfbb9f20040c70b7e21695d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Diagnóstico de diabetes mellitus.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377324</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="140 mg/dL">
  <data key="d0">140 mg/dL</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">140 mg/dL is the glucose concentration threshold in TTGO‑2h used for detecting pre‑diabetes.</data>
