<node id="Autoantibodies">
  <data key="d0">Autoantibodies</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Autoantibodies are immune proteins that target self‑antigens such as insulin, glutamic acid decarboxylase (GAD), the protein tyrosine phosphatase IA‑2 (also referred to as anti‑tirosina fosfatase), and zinc transporter 8 (ZnT8). In the context of diabetes, these autoantibodies serve as biomarkers for type 1 diabetes (T1D). Laboratory tests that detect anti‑GAD, anti‑IA‑2, anti‑ZnT8, and anti‑insulin are routinely used for screening, risk assessment, and confirmation of a T1D diagnosis. A positive autoantibody result can confirm the disease, and the persistent presence of two or more autoantibodies strongly predicts progression to clinical diabetes, especially in children.

Beyond confirming T1D, autoantibody testing helps differentiate T1D from other forms of diabetes. They are typically absent in classic maturity‑onset diabetes of the young (MODY) cases, making a negative result one of the criteria used to suspect latent autoimmune diabetes in adults (LADA). Conversely, the detection of autoantibodies can preclude further genetic testing for monogenic diabetes, although occasional reports describe autoantibody positivity in some monogenic diabetes patients.

Overall, autoantibodies function as key immunological markers for identifying pre‑clinical disease, estimating future risk, and guiding diagnostic pathways in the management of type 1 diabetes and related autoimmune diabetes phenotypes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2cf24d486949a568d61c1de206cd3e14&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-343246c2eef6e8430b581340d6cd4762&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-429fba9c3900b6d0b0c3ccfb38323e54&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-299bcef3259f8ab6bc70544e12616624&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e4adabacd09697393ca15fc999724c51&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9e1f69c1d604e82e14a23a29231bd587&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6601fea85bfbb9f20040c70b7e21695d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2752a78fbaafd94ca566ff099a4ba551&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ba38023866c2db7437e618a60033f21f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2a430bf53157529ccb22e67171fb28e5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3cc61bc2e95346d553972b4371912e7f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Diagnóstico de diabetes mellitus.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classificação do diabetes.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377250</data>
