<node id="Screening">
  <data key="d0">Screening</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Screening is the systematic medical process of testing individuals—often asymptomatic—to identify the presence or risk of diabetes or abnormal glucose metabolism at an early stage. The overarching goal is to detect disease before symptoms develop, enabling timely intervention and potentially improving health outcomes.

In the context of type 1 diabetes, screening commonly involves measuring autoantibodies that signal a heightened risk of developing the condition. For type 2 diabetes and prediabetes, a variety of biomarkers and tools are employed, including hemoglobin A1C, fasting plasma glucose, oral glucose tolerance tests, and risk‑calculation algorithms. These methods are used to assess adults who show no overt symptoms, and research suggests that such population‑level screening can be cost‑effective when appropriately targeted.

Screening also extends to specific groups with unique risk profiles. Pregnant individuals are routinely screened for gestational diabetes mellitus, typically using either a one‑step 75‑gram oral glucose tolerance test or a two‑step approach that begins with a glucose challenge test followed by a diagnostic test if warranted. People with cystic fibrosis are screened for cystic fibrosis‑related diabetes (CFRD); clinicians may initiate evaluation when clinical cues such as unexplained weight loss arise. 

Overall, diabetes screening encompasses a range of protocols designed to identify both established disease and elevated risk across diverse populations, employing standardized tests and clinical judgment to guide further diagnostic evaluation and preventive care.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2cf24d486949a568d61c1de206cd3e14&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-44888abd4ca8a1953f751ed6c41922e6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-090b8f9281aa75054311d8f275a2c8f8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-59dd4faf2a2706d073fdb93e1a29da81&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9cdf6af658e42c2f4f7dca5e4dbdd3db&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-55e58732610596ce9a8f3145d34f75a7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2a430bf53157529ccb22e67171fb28e5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1a111d4b40ec241cf54126f594a80308&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9eb02ab1ab7d834858bf60a8b402e6ea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a22fadf52eaea018160e4dd41d1d39b8</data>
