<node id="Oral Glucose Tolerance Test (OGTT)">
  <data key="d0">Oral Glucose Tolerance Test (OGTT)</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">OGTT is a diagnostic procedure measuring blood glucose response to an oral glucose load over time.&lt;SEP&gt;Oral Glucose Tolerance Test is a clinical test measuring glucose response after oral glucose ingestion.&lt;SEP&gt;A 75‑gram glucose challenge used to assess plasma glucose response.&lt;SEP&gt;Oral glucose tolerance test (OGTT) is a diagnostic procedure recommended for children and for cystic fibrosis‑related diabetes screening.&lt;SEP&gt;The Oral Glucose Tolerance Test (OGTT) is the gold‑standard diagnostic test for PTDM one year after transplant.&lt;SEP&gt;Oral Glucose Tolerance Test (OGTT) is the recommended screening test for detecting CFRD.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a05276c5db43e3a1e9f987056012750f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-44aa59c0e5cc620a11b8fb017d1aefcf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e4e7eef761aec994cc4558b2db5e1e08&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9cdf6af658e42c2f4f7dca5e4dbdd3db&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ba38023866c2db7437e618a60033f21f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0631ff2b95dd459677eaaebe9283a776</data>
