<node id="Dysglycemia">
  <data key="d0">Dysglycemia</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Dysglycemia describes abnormal blood glucose levels, including prediabetes and diabetes.&lt;SEP&gt;Abnormal glucose metabolism, predicted by one‑hour post‑load plasma glucose levels.&lt;SEP&gt;Dysglycemia denotes abnormal glucose levels (IFG and/or IGT) present in Stage 2 of type 1 diabetes.&lt;SEP&gt;Abnormal glucose regulation seen in Stage 2 diabetes.&lt;SEP&gt;Dysglycemia denotes abnormal blood glucose levels observed in dental patients.&lt;SEP&gt;Dysglycemia refers to abnormal blood glucose levels, including hyperglycemia and hypoglycemia.</data>
