<node id="Level 2 Hypoglycemia">
  <data key="d0">Level 2 Hypoglycemia</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Level 2 Hypoglycemia refers to glucose readings below 54 mg/dL (&lt;3.0 mmol/L).&lt;SEP&gt;Level 2 hypoglycemia is defined as a blood glucose concentration below 54 mg/dL (3.0 mmol/L) with neuroglycopenic symptoms.&lt;SEP&gt;Level 2 hypoglycemia is a moderate low blood glucose state without adrenergic or neuroglycopenic symptoms, often indicating hypoglycemia unawareness.&lt;SEP&gt;Level 2 Hypoglycemia is a moderate severity classification of low blood glucose.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fc59aba81df88fe020f6e1d93d9e403b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-345ad64f464691cc28341ccd246032db&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-36ddeaa53bc38bee375d7ac6d71485d4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a19f43c10a7a756e1597ff1a7f53296e</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Metas glicêmicas/metas cuidado do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786372085</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hypoglycemia Unawareness">
  <data key="d0">Hypoglycemia Unawareness</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Hypoglycemia unawareness refers to the lack of typical warning symptoms in patients experiencing low blood glucose.&lt;SEP&gt;Hypoglycemia unawareness is a condition where individuals fail to recognize low‑blood‑glucose symptoms.&lt;SEP&gt;Hypoglycemia unawareness describes a condition where individuals fail to recognize low‑blood‑glucose symptoms, increasing severe hypoglycemia risk.&lt;SEP&gt;Hypoglycemia Unawareness is a condition where individuals do not perceive low blood glucose symptoms.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fc59aba81df88fe020f6e1d93d9e403b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cc39a0c02d5f1bd08d5cb71bacc69a24&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-36ddeaa53bc38bee375d7ac6d71485d4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-208cda7ee40e8d266fadd1eadff49e03</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Metas glicêmicas/metas cuidado do diabetes.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/hipoglicemia.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786372327</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Clarke Score">
  <data key="d0">Clarke Score</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Clarke score is a method used to assess impaired hypoglycemia awareness.&lt;SEP&gt;Clarke score is a scoring system used to assess impaired hypoglycemia awareness.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fc59aba81df88fe020f6e1d93d9e403b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-36ddeaa53bc38bee375d7ac6d71485d4</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Metas glicêmicas/metas cuidado do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786372085</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
