<node id="Intensive Glycemic Control">
  <data key="d0">Intensive Glycemic Control</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A treatment strategy aiming for lower A1C targets (e.g., ≈7% or less) through tighter glucose management.&lt;SEP&gt;Intensive glycemic control is a therapeutic strategy aiming for lower A1C targets (e.g., 6.5%) that was evaluated in major diabetes trials.&lt;SEP&gt;Intensive glycemic control refers to targeting near‑normal A1C levels (often &lt;6–6.5%) in diabetes management.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-74ef8c063d84e34c44021aa138b9b903&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f99d05e1089d59496d56d86ff40197cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-38ab5af7e42588297df4330ffb2c046b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Metas glicêmicas/metas cuidado do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786372128</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Standard Glycemic Control">
  <data key="d0">Standard Glycemic Control</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A conventional treatment approach targeting higher A1C levels (e.g., ≈9%) with less stringent glucose lowering.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-74ef8c063d84e34c44021aa138b9b903</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Metas glicêmicas/metas cuidado do diabetes.pdf</data>
