  <data key="d0">Life Expectancy</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Life expectancy denotes the anticipated remaining years of life for a patient.&lt;SEP&gt;Life expectancy is a patient characteristic considered in determining appropriate glycemic targets.&lt;SEP&gt;Life Expectancy is the anticipated remaining years of life, influencing the aggressiveness of glycemic targets.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f99d05e1089d59496d56d86ff40197cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-38ab5af7e42588297df4330ffb2c046b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aff91698679a52cd7b07563b7b2627a3</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Metas glicêmicas/metas cuidado do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786372144</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Disease Duration">
  <data key="d0">Disease Duration</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Disease duration is the length of time a person has lived with diabetes.&lt;SEP&gt;Disease duration denotes how long a person has had diabetes and influences glycemic target stringency.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f99d05e1089d59496d56d86ff40197cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-38ab5af7e42588297df4330ffb2c046b</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Metas glicêmicas/metas cuidado do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786372144</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Established Vascular Complications">
  <data key="d0">Established Vascular Complications</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Established vascular complications are pre‑existing cardiovascular or renal disease in a patient.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f99d05e1089d59496d56d86ff40197cc</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Metas glicêmicas/metas cuidado do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786372144</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Long‑standing Diabetes">
  <data key="d0">Long‑standing Diabetes</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Long‑standing diabetes describes a prolonged duration of diabetes, often associated with higher cardiovascular risk.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f99d05e1089d59496d56d86ff40197cc</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Metas glicêmicas/metas cuidado do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786372144</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Therapeutic Inertia">
  <data key="d0">Therapeutic Inertia</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Therapeutic inertia refers to the failure to intensify treatment when indicated, a barrier to achieving intensive glycemic targets.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f99d05e1089d59496d56d86ff40197cc</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Metas glicêmicas/metas cuidado do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786372144</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Clinician Judgment">
  <data key="d0">Clinician Judgment</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Clinician judgment denotes the healthcare provider’s assessment and decision‑making regarding diabetes treatment intensity.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f99d05e1089d59496d56d86ff40197cc</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Metas glicêmicas/metas cuidado do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786372144</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Higher vs Lower A1C">
  <data key="d0">Higher vs Lower A1C</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Higher versus lower A1C compares more intensive versus standard glycemic targets in clinical trials.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f99d05e1089d59496d56d86ff40197cc</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Metas glicêmicas/metas cuidado do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786372144</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Near‑Normal A1C Goals">
  <data key="d0">Near‑Normal A1C Goals</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Near‑normal A1C goals refer to target A1C levels close to normal, typically below 6–6.5%, pursued in intensive glycemic control strategies.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f99d05e1089d59496d56d86ff40197cc</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Metas glicêmicas/metas cuidado do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786372144</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
