  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="AGP Report">
  <data key="d0">AGP Report</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">AGP Report is a summary of glucose values from the report period, showing median and percentile values as if they occurred in a single day.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b275f50028ef32e322bf8643e0342810</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Metas glicêmicas/metas cuidado do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786372154</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Test Patient">
  <data key="d0">Test Patient</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Test Patient is an individual with diabetes whose CGM data are presented in the report.&lt;SEP&gt;Test Patient is an individual with date of birth Jan 1, 1970, whose glucose data were collected over a 14‑day period.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b275f50028ef32e322bf8643e0342810&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a19f43c10a7a756e1597ff1a7f53296e</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Metas glicêmicas/metas cuidado do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786372154</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Average Glucose">
  <data key="d0">Average Glucose</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Average glucose is the mean glucose concentration recorded over a period, reported as 175 mg/dL for the test patient.&lt;SEP&gt;Average Glucose is the calculated glucose level derived from A1C measurements, often expressed as estimated average glucose (eAG) in mg/dL or mmol/L.&lt;SEP&gt;Average Glucose is a metric reported as 175 mg/dL for the test patient.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b275f50028ef32e322bf8643e0342810&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a19f43c10a7a756e1597ff1a7f53296e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ba0417a72f50cf7ca66c87a351bd1ff8</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Metas glicêmicas/metas cuidado do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786372155</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Holt Et Al">
  <data key="d0">Holt Et Al</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Holt Et Al are the authors credited for Figure 6.1.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b275f50028ef32e322bf8643e0342810</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Metas glicêmicas/metas cuidado do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786372155</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Consensus Document">
  <data key="d0">Consensus Document</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">A recent consensus document discusses the format of AGP reports and recommends their generation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b275f50028ef32e322bf8643e0342810</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Metas glicêmicas/metas cuidado do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786372155</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Older Adults">
  <data key="d0">Older Adults</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Older Adults is a population group for which specific glycemic goals are provided.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b275f50028ef32e322bf8643e0342810</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Metas glicêmicas/metas cuidado do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786372155</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Children And Adolescents">
  <data key="d0">Children And Adolescents</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Children And Adolescents is a population group for which specific glycemic goals are provided.&lt;SEP&gt;Children And Adolescents are age groups for which A1C, FPG, or 2-H PG can be used to screen for pre-diabetes or type 2 diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b275f50028ef32e322bf8643e0342810&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-44888abd4ca8a1953f751ed6c41922e6</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Metas glicêmicas/metas cuidado do diabetes.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377223</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Person‑Centered Strategy">
  <data key="d0">Person‑Centered Strategy</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Person‑Centered Strategy is an overall approach that integrates glycemic targets into individualized care.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b275f50028ef32e322bf8643e0342810</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Metas glicêmicas/metas cuidado do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786372155</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Glycemic Goals">
  <data key="d0">Glycemic Goals</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Glycemic Goals are target values for glucose metrics such as time in range, A1C, and hypoglycemia risk.&lt;SEP&gt;Glycemic goals are individualized blood‑glucose targets for patients with diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b275f50028ef32e322bf8643e0342810&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0631ff2b95dd459677eaaebe9283a776</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Metas glicêmicas/metas cuidado do diabetes.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377435</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Standard Ambulatory Glucose Profile">
  <data key="d0">Standard Ambulatory Glucose Profile</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Standard Ambulatory Glucose Profile (AGP) is the standardized method for summarizing continuous glucose data in a report.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b275f50028ef32e322bf8643e0342810</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Metas glicêmicas/metas cuidado do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786372156</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Retrospective Studies">
  <data key="d0">Retrospective Studies</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Retrospective Studies are published analyses that suggest a strong correlation between TIR and A1C.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b275f50028ef32e322bf8643e0342810</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Metas glicêmicas/metas cuidado do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786372156</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="S100 Glycemic Targets">
  <data key="d0">S100 Glycemic Targets</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">S100 Glycemic Targets is the title of the supplement article in Diabetes Care that includes the AGP figure.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b275f50028ef32e322bf8643e0342810</data>
