  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Metas glicêmicas/metas cuidado do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786372191</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Non‑Hispanic White Individuals">
  <data key="d0">Non‑Hispanic White Individuals</data>
  <data key="d1">other</data>
  <data key="d2">Non‑Hispanic White individuals are a population group used as a reference cohort for comparing A1C values against African American cohorts.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ba0417a72f50cf7ca66c87a351bd1ff8</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Metas glicêmicas/metas cuidado do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786372192</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="HbS Variant">
  <data key="d0">HbS Variant</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">HbS is a common hemoglobin variant; African American individuals heterozygous for HbS exhibit A1C values about 0.3 percentage points lower than those without the variant.&lt;SEP&gt;The sickle hemoglobin (HbS) variant that may lower A1C by about 0.3% in carriers.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ba0417a72f50cf7ca66c87a351bd1ff8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d01033177672e6c36e0a368db88e586d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Metas glicêmicas/metas cuidado do diabetes.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377311</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="G202A Variant">
  <data key="d0">G202A Variant</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The X‑linked glucose‑6‑phosphate dehydrogenase G202A variant is carried by a subset of African American individuals and is associated with A1C reductions of approximately 0.8% in men and 0.7% in women.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ba0417a72f50cf7ca66c87a351bd1ff8</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Metas glicêmicas/metas cuidado do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786372192</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Continuous Glucose Monitoring (CGM) Devices">
  <data key="d0">Continuous Glucose Monitoring (CGM) Devices</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">CGM devices are continuous glucose monitoring technologies that generate glucose data and are recommended for standardized single‑page reports.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ba0417a72f50cf7ca66c87a351bd1ff8</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Metas glicêmicas/metas cuidado do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786372192</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Professional Diabetes Organization eAG Calculator">
  <data key="d0">Professional Diabetes Organization eAG Calculator</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The eAG calculator is an online tool at professional.diabetes.org/eAG that converts A1C results into estimated average glucose values.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ba0417a72f50cf7ca66c87a351bd1ff8</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Metas glicêmicas/metas cuidado do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786372192</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Nathan et al. Study">
  <data key="d0">Nathan et al. Study</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">The Nathan et al. study provided a high correlation (0.92) between A1C and average glucose based on a large dataset of 507 adults.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ba0417a72f50cf7ca66c87a351bd1ff8</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Metas glicêmicas/metas cuidado do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786372192</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Table 6.1 – Estimated Average Glucose Table">
  <data key="d0">Table 6.1 – Estimated Average Glucose Table</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Table 6.1 lists A1C percentages alongside corresponding estimated average glucose values with 95 % confidence intervals.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ba0417a72f50cf7ca66c87a351bd1ff8</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Metas glicêmicas/metas cuidado do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786372192</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Table 6.2 – Time in Range Parameters Table">
  <data key="d0">Table 6.2 – Time in Range Parameters Table</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Table 6.2 presents recommended time‑in‑range, time‑below‑range, and time‑above‑range parameters for evaluating diabetes treatment plans.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ba0417a72f50cf7ca66c87a351bd1ff8</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Metas glicêmicas/metas cuidado do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786372192</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Standardized Single‑Page Glucose Report">
  <data key="d0">Standardized Single‑Page Glucose Report</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">A standardized single‑page glucose report is a recommended format for summarizing data from continuous glucose monitoring devices, incorporating visual cues such as the ambulatory glucose profile.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ba0417a72f50cf7ca66c87a351bd1ff8</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Metas glicêmicas/metas cuidado do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786372193</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Insulin Dose Adjustments">
  <data key="d0">Insulin Dose Adjustments</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Insulin Dose Adjustments refer to the modifications of insulin therapy based on glucose monitoring data to achieve optimal glycemic control.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ba0417a72f50cf7ca66c87a351bd1ff8</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Metas glicêmicas/metas cuidado do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786372193</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Section 7 – Diabetes Technology">
  <data key="d0">Section 7 – Diabetes Technology</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Section 7 – Diabetes Technology is a subsection of the document that reviews studies supporting the use of continuous glucose monitoring and related metrics.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ba0417a72f50cf7ca66c87a351bd1ff8</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Metas glicêmicas/metas cuidado do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786372193</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Children Type 1 Diabetes CGM Study">
  <data key="d0">Children Type 1 Diabetes CGM Study</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">The Children Type 1 Diabetes CGM Study is a small study that compared A1C to continuous glucose monitoring data in children with type 1 diabetes, reporting a correlation of r = 0.7.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ba0417a72f50cf7ca66c87a351bd1ff8</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Metas glicêmicas/metas cuidado do diabetes.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786372193</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
