<node id="MODY">
  <data key="d0">MODY</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">MODY is a group of monogenic forms of diabetes characterized by mutations in single genes.&lt;SEP&gt;MODY (Maturity‑Onset Diabetes of the Young) is a monogenic form of diabetes mellitus.&lt;SEP&gt;Maturity Onset Diabetes of the Young, a monogenic form of diabetes.&lt;SEP&gt;Maturity‑Onset Diabetes of the Young (MODY) is a monogenic form of diabetes characterized by early hyperglycemia and autosomal dominant inheritance involving at least 13 genes.&lt;SEP&gt;MODY is a monogenic form of diabetes characterized by atypical features distinct from type 1 and type 2 diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5c23c0554362bde8c591c91d4a0185a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e26b32d53b78f97e8d7fa8b815f2cc87&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cc432bf15c11ef31f7aff87b534b5eaf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-299bcef3259f8ab6bc70544e12616624&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9e1f69c1d604e82e14a23a29231bd587&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0bdb8ef335f3531317a3a5bd7de3a561</data>
