</node>
<node id="Diabetes Risk Test">
  <data key="d0">Diabetes Risk Test</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Diabetes Risk Test is a questionnaire developed by the American Diabetes Association that assigns points based on age, gender, family history, gestational diabetes, blood pressure, physical activity, and weight to assess risk of Type 2 Diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2c37e26e62468b725533260347fb4e31</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377190</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Bang et al., Ann Intern Med 151:775–783, 2009">
  <data key="d0">Bang et al., Ann Intern Med 151:775–783, 2009</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Bang et al., Ann Intern Med 151:775–783, 2009 is the research article that originally validated the Diabetes Risk Test algorithm.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2c37e26e62468b725533260347fb4e31</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377190</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Figure 2.1 - ADA Risk Test">
  <data key="d0">Figure 2.1 - ADA Risk Test</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Figure 2.1 - ADA Risk Test is an illustration that presents the scoring table used in the Diabetes Risk Test.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2c37e26e62468b725533260347fb4e31</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377190</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Diabetes Care Volume 46, Supplement 1, January 2023">
  <data key="d0">Diabetes Care Volume 46, Supplement 1, January 2023</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">This publication contains tables and guidelines for staging and diagnosing type 1 diabetes.&lt;SEP&gt;Diabetes Care Volume 46, Supplement 1, January 2023 is a journal supplement that includes classification and diagnosis guidelines for diabetes.&lt;SEP&gt;Diabetes Care Volume 46, Supplement 1, January 2023 is the source document from which the excerpt is taken.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2c37e26e62468b725533260347fb4e31&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3cc61bc2e95346d553972b4371912e7f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-83d72fbc44fe0c28f27702c0d4f2c140</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377190</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="High Blood Pressure">
  <data key="d0">High Blood Pressure</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">High Blood Pressure is a medical condition that adds a point in the Diabetes Risk Test scoring.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2c37e26e62468b725533260347fb4e31</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377190</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="African Americans">
  <data key="d0">African Americans</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">African Americans are an ethnic group identified as having higher prevalence of Type 2 Diabetes.&lt;SEP&gt;African Americans are individuals in the United States who have ancestry from Africa.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2c37e26e62468b725533260347fb4e31&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c14456299df06b01b603504def87f381</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377191</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hispanics/Latinos">
  <data key="d0">Hispanics/Latinos</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Hispanics/Latinos are an ethnic group identified as having higher prevalence of Type 2 Diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2c37e26e62468b725533260347fb4e31</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377191</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Native Americans">
  <data key="d0">Native Americans</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Native Americans are an ethnic group identified as having higher prevalence of Type 2 Diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2c37e26e62468b725533260347fb4e31</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377191</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Asian Americans">
  <data key="d0">Asian Americans</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Asian Americans are an ethnic group identified as having higher prevalence of Type 2 Diabetes, with increased risk at lower body weight.&lt;SEP&gt;Asian Americans are a population group for which specific BMI cut points are investigated.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2c37e26e62468b725533260347fb4e31&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9ab98b1c07f7bbaa3ad28fb83167f489</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377191</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Native Hawaiians and Pacific Islanders">
  <data key="d0">Native Hawaiians and Pacific Islanders</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Native Hawaiians and Pacific Islanders are an ethnic group identified as having higher prevalence of Type 2 Diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2c37e26e62468b725533260347fb4e31</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377191</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Intensive Diet and Exercise">
  <data key="d0">Intensive Diet and Exercise</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A combined approach of strict dietary control and exercise, reported to lead to diabetes remission.&lt;SEP&gt;Intensive Diet and Exercise is a therapeutic approach that can improve insulin resistance.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2c37e26e62468b725533260347fb4e31&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9eb02ab1ab7d834858bf60a8b402e6ea</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377192</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Surgical Weight Loss">
  <data key="d0">Surgical Weight Loss</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Operative procedures for weight reduction, reported to lead to diabetes remission.&lt;SEP&gt;Surgical Weight Loss is a therapeutic approach that can improve insulin resistance and lead to diabetes remission.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2c37e26e62468b725533260347fb4e31&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9eb02ab1ab7d834858bf60a8b402e6ea</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377192</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Diabetes Remission">
  <data key="d0">Diabetes Remission</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The reversal of diabetes, achieved through intensive diet/exercise or surgical weight loss.&lt;SEP&gt;Diabetes Remission is the condition where Type 2 Diabetes is no longer present after intensive interventions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2c37e26e62468b725533260347fb4e31&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9eb02ab1ab7d834858bf60a8b402e6ea</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377192</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Height-Weight Chart">
  <data key="d0">Height-Weight Chart</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Height-Weight Chart is the table of height and corresponding weight ranges used to assign points in the Diabetes Risk Test.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2c37e26e62468b725533260347fb4e31</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377192</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Risk Test Score">
  <data key="d0">Risk Test Score</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Risk Test Score is the total points calculated from the Diabetes Risk Test, indicating the individual's risk level for Type 2 Diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2c37e26e62468b725533260347fb4e31</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377192</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Gender">
  <data key="d0">Gender</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Gender (man or woman) is a demographic factor used in the Diabetes Risk Test to assign points for assessing Type 2 Diabetes risk.&lt;SEP&gt;Gender is a demographic characteristic classifying individuals as male, female, or other.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2c37e26e62468b725533260347fb4e31&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c14456299df06b01b603504def87f381</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377192</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Family History of Diabetes">
  <data key="d0">Family History of Diabetes</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Family History of Diabetes indicates having a mother, father, sister, or brother with diabetes and contributes a point in the Diabetes Risk Test.&lt;SEP&gt;A family history of diabetes across successive generations suggests an autosomal dominant inheritance pattern.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2c37e26e62468b725533260347fb4e31&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0bdb8ef335f3531317a3a5bd7de3a561</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377193</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Weight Category">
  <data key="d0">Weight Category</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Weight Category refers to the body weight range determined from the Height-Weight Chart that adds points in the Diabetes Risk Test risk assessment.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2c37e26e62468b725533260347fb4e31</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377193</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Height">
  <data key="d0">Height</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Height is a measurement used together with the Height-Weight Chart to determine the appropriate Weight Category for scoring the Diabetes Risk Test.&lt;SEP&gt;Height is a body measurement referenced alongside weight and BMI in the context of evaluating screening outcomes for CFRD.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2c37e26e62468b725533260347fb4e31&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9cdf6af658e42c2f4f7dca5e4dbdd3db</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377193</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Clinical Laboratory Improvement Amendments">
  <data key="d0">Clinical Laboratory Improvement Amendments</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Clinical Laboratory Improvement Amendments are regulatory standards governing laboratory testing quality and personnel requirements.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-44888abd4ca8a1953f751ed6c41922e6</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377195</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Point-of-Care A1C Assay">
  <data key="d0">Point-of-Care A1C Assay</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Point-of-care A1C assays are rapid tests used to monitor glycemic control in diabetes patients in various clinical settings.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-44888abd4ca8a1953f751ed6c41922e6</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377195</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hemodialysis">
  <data key="d0">Hemodialysis</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Hemodialysis is a medical procedure that can independently affect hemoglobin glycation measurements.&lt;SEP&gt;Hemodialysis is a renal replacement therapy that may alter A1C‑glucose concordance.&lt;SEP&gt;A renal treatment associated with increased red blood cell turnover.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-44888abd4ca8a1953f751ed6c41922e6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d01033177672e6c36e0a368db88e586d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3cc61bc2e95346d553972b4371912e7f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377219</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Diagnostic Criteria for Diabetes">
  <data key="d0">Diagnostic Criteria for Diabetes</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Diagnostic criteria for diabetes define thresholds for tests such as A1C, FPG, and OGTT to confirm the disease.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-44888abd4ca8a1953f751ed6c41922e6</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377221</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="2-H Plasma Glucose">
  <data key="d0">2-H Plasma Glucose</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">2-H Plasma Glucose is a blood test measuring glucose two hours after an oral glucose tolerance test, used in diabetes diagnosis.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-44888abd4ca8a1953f751ed6c41922e6</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377221</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Random Plasma Glucose">
  <data key="d0">Random Plasma Glucose</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Random Plasma Glucose is a blood glucose measurement taken at any time, used as a diagnostic criterion for diabetes.&lt;SEP&gt;A measurement of plasma glucose level used in diabetes diagnosis.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-44888abd4ca8a1953f751ed6c41922e6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d01033177672e6c36e0a368db88e586d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377221</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="HIV Treatment">
  <data key="d0">HIV Treatment</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">HIV Treatment refers to medical therapies for HIV infection, mentioned as a factor influencing A1C interpretation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-44888abd4ca8a1953f751ed6c41922e6</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377222</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="HbS">
  <data key="d0">HbS</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">HbS is a common hemoglobin variant in African American individuals that can affect A1C results.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-44888abd4ca8a1953f751ed6c41922e6</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377223</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Pre-Diabetes">
  <data key="d0">Pre-Diabetes</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Pre-Diabetes is a metabolic condition identified by elevated A1C, FPG, or 2-H PG values below diabetes thresholds.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-44888abd4ca8a1953f751ed6c41922e6</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377223</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Diagnostic Threshold">
  <data key="d0">Diagnostic Threshold</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Diagnostic Threshold refers to specific cutoff values (e.g., A1C ≥ 6.5%) used to diagnose diabetes.&lt;SEP&gt;Diagnostic threshold refers to the glucose level cut point used to determine abnormal test results.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-44888abd4ca8a1953f751ed6c41922e6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6601fea85bfbb9f20040c70b7e21695d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377227</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Proficiency Testing Program">
  <data key="d0">Proficiency Testing Program</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Proficiency Testing Program is a required component of CLIA compliance for point-of-care A1C assays.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-44888abd4ca8a1953f751ed6c41922e6</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377227</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Annual Competency Assessments">
  <data key="d0">Annual Competency Assessments</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Annual Competency Assessments are documented evaluations of personnel required by CLIA regulations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-44888abd4ca8a1953f751ed6c41922e6</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377228</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
