  <data key="d0">Search for Diabetes in Youth Study Group</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Search for Diabetes in Youth Study Group is an organization that conducts the SEARCH for Diabetes in Youth multicenter study on diabetes prevalence, incidence, and classification in youth.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-355eedbe74750d3739f7257279494c9a</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377236</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="HNF1A-MODY">
  <data key="d0">HNF1A-MODY</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">HNF1A‑MODY (MODY3) typically responds well to low‑dose sulfonylureas.&lt;SEP&gt;HNF1A-MODY is a subtype of MODY caused by HNF1A mutations and is sensitive to sulfonylureas.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9e1f69c1d604e82e14a23a29231bd587&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0bdb8ef335f3531317a3a5bd7de3a561</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377236</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="HNF4A-MODY">
  <data key="d0">HNF4A-MODY</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">HNF4A‑MODY (MODY1) typically responds well to low‑dose sulfonylureas.&lt;SEP&gt;HNF4A-MODY is a subtype of MODY caused by HNF4A mutations and is sensitive to sulfonylureas.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9e1f69c1d604e82e14a23a29231bd587&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0bdb8ef335f3531317a3a5bd7de3a561</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377237</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="GCK-MODY">
  <data key="d0">GCK-MODY</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">GCK‑MODY (MODY2) presents with mild, stable fasting hyperglycemia and generally requires no therapy except during pregnancy.&lt;SEP&gt;GCK-MODY is a subtype of MODY caused by GCK mutations, typically stable, non‑progressive and often does not require therapy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9e1f69c1d604e82e14a23a29231bd587&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0bdb8ef335f3531317a3a5bd7de3a561</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377237</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="HNF1B-MODY">
  <data key="d0">HNF1B-MODY</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">HNF1B-MODY is a subtype of MODY associated with developmental renal disease and genitourinary abnormalities.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9e1f69c1d604e82e14a23a29231bd587</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377237</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="6q24">
  <data key="d0">6q24</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The 6q24 region (including PLAGL1 and HYMA1) is linked to transient neonatal diabetes that may be treatable with medications other than insulin.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9e1f69c1d604e82e14a23a29231bd587</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377237</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="GATA6">
  <data key="d0">GATA6</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">GATA6 mutations are associated with pancreatic hypoplasia, cardiac malformations, and exocrine insufficiency.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9e1f69c1d604e82e14a23a29231bd587</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377237</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="EIF2B1">
  <data key="d0">EIF2B1</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">EIF2B1 mutations can be associated with fluctuating liver function in permanent diabetes.&lt;SEP&gt;EIF2B1 is a gene linked to permanent diabetes in the provided text.&lt;SEP&gt;A gene whose de novo mutations can cause neonatal diabetes and hepatic dysfunction.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9e1f69c1d604e82e14a23a29231bd587&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c83accc14a3b482690949ff04716a0aa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-090b8f9281aa75054311d8f275a2c8f8</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377238</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Genetic Screening">
  <data key="d0">Genetic Screening</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Genetic screening is used in research to identify high‑risk populations for type 1 diabetes.&lt;SEP&gt;Genetic screening is increasingly available and cost‑effective for detecting monogenic diabetes.&lt;SEP&gt;Genetic screening refers to increasingly available, cost‑effective testing to identify monogenic diabetes mutations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9e1f69c1d604e82e14a23a29231bd587&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6601fea85bfbb9f20040c70b7e21695d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0bdb8ef335f3531317a3a5bd7de3a561</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377238</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Commercial Genetic Testing">
  <data key="d0">Commercial Genetic Testing</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Commercial genetic testing provides affordable genetic diagnosis of MODY, often supported by health insurance.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9e1f69c1d604e82e14a23a29231bd587</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377238</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Biomarker Screening Pathway">
  <data key="d0">Biomarker Screening Pathway</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The biomarker screening pathway combines urinary C‑peptide/creatinine ratio and antibody screening to select candidates for MODY genetic testing.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9e1f69c1d604e82e14a23a29231bd587</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377238</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Urinary C‑Peptide/Creatinine Ratio">
  <data key="d0">Urinary C‑Peptide/Creatinine Ratio</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Urinary C‑peptide/creatinine ratio is a biomarker used within the screening pathway to assess endogenous insulin production.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9e1f69c1d604e82e14a23a29231bd587</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377239</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Antibody Screening">
  <data key="d0">Antibody Screening</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Antibody screening detects autoantibodies that help differentiate type 1 diabetes from monogenic diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9e1f69c1d604e82e14a23a29231bd587</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377239</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Genetic Counseling">
  <data key="d0">Genetic Counseling</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Genetic counseling helps patients understand the significance of genetic mutations and guides further evaluation.&lt;SEP&gt;Genetic counseling provides education on inheritance patterns and cardiovascular risk for individuals diagnosed with monogenic diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9e1f69c1d604e82e14a23a29231bd587&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0bdb8ef335f3531317a3a5bd7de3a561</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377239</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Alternative Medications">
  <data key="d0">Alternative Medications</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Alternative medications refer to treatments other than insulin for certain forms of neonatal diabetes, such as those linked to 6q24.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9e1f69c1d604e82e14a23a29231bd587</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377239</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Genetic Testing for MODY">
  <data key="d0">Genetic Testing for MODY</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Genetic testing for MODY is a diagnostic procedure that identifies specific gene mutations responsible for monogenic diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9e1f69c1d604e82e14a23a29231bd587</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377240</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Affected Individuals">
  <data key="d0">Affected Individuals</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Affected individuals are patients diagnosed with monogenic diabetes who benefit from genetic counseling.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9e1f69c1d604e82e14a23a29231bd587</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377240</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Pancreatic Hypoplasia and Cardiac Malformations">
  <data key="d0">Pancreatic Hypoplasia and Cardiac Malformations</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Pancreatic hypoplasia and cardiac malformations are clinical features associated with GATA6 mutations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9e1f69c1d604e82e14a23a29231bd587</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377240</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="IPEX Syndrome">
  <data key="d0">IPEX Syndrome</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">X‑linked early‑onset systemic autoimmune disorder caused by FOXP3 gene mutation.&lt;SEP&gt;IPEX syndrome is an X-linked disorder featuring autoimmune diabetes, autoimmune thyroid disease, exfoliative dermatitis, and insulin requiring.&lt;SEP&gt;IPEX syndrome is an X‑linked autoimmune disorder caused by FOXP3 mutations, featuring autoimmune diabetes and other autoimmune manifestations.&lt;SEP&gt;IPEX syndrome is a rare genetic disorder characterized by immune dysregulation, polyendocrinopathy, and enteropathy.&lt;SEP&gt;A syndrome whose genetics and treatment options are examined in the cited literature.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9e1f69c1d604e82e14a23a29231bd587&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-090b8f9281aa75054311d8f275a2c8f8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2752a78fbaafd94ca566ff099a4ba551&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c122c1c6d7dd36110b6ddba2c074d122&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c14456299df06b01b603504def87f381</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377241</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Transient Neonatal Diabetes">
  <data key="d0">Transient Neonatal Diabetes</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Transient neonatal diabetes is often due to over‑expression of genes on chromosome 6q24 and may be treatable with non‑insulin medications.&lt;SEP&gt;Transient neonatal diabetes is a form of neonatal diabetes that may resolve over time and can be linked to 6q24 abnormalities.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9e1f69c1d604e82e14a23a29231bd587&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0bdb8ef335f3531317a3a5bd7de3a561</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377241</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Permanent Neonatal Diabetes">
  <data key="d0">Permanent Neonatal Diabetes</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Permanent neonatal diabetes is commonly caused by autosomal dominant mutations in KCNJ11, ABCC8, EIF2B1, or INS.&lt;SEP&gt;Permanent neonatal diabetes is a lifelong form of neonatal diabetes often caused by KCNJ11, INS, or ABCC8 mutations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9e1f69c1d604e82e14a23a29231bd587&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0bdb8ef335f3531317a3a5bd7de3a561</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377241</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Specialist">
  <data key="d0">Specialist</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A specialist is a healthcare professional with expertise in monogenic diabetes evaluation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9e1f69c1d604e82e14a23a29231bd587</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377241</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Centers">
  <data key="d0">Centers</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Centers are medical facilities that provide specialized evaluation for suspected monogenic diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9e1f69c1d604e82e14a23a29231bd587</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377241</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Health Insurance">
  <data key="d0">Health Insurance</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Health insurance is a payer system that may cover commercial genetic testing for MODY.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9e1f69c1d604e82e14a23a29231bd587</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377242</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Early Adulthood Diabetes">
  <data key="d0">Early Adulthood Diabetes</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Early adulthood diabetes refers to diabetes diagnosed in adults during early adulthood, often considered for monogenic diabetes evaluation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9e1f69c1d604e82e14a23a29231bd587</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377242</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Infant-Onset Diabetes">
  <data key="d0">Infant-Onset Diabetes</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Infant‑onset diabetes describes diabetes diagnosed within the first six months of life, a key criterion for monogenic diabetes testing.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9e1f69c1d604e82e14a23a29231bd587</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377242</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cost-effective Therapy">
  <data key="d0">Cost-effective Therapy</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Cost‑effective therapy denotes treatment approaches that provide clinical benefit at lower economic cost, such as using sulfonylureas for certain MODY subtypes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9e1f69c1d604e82e14a23a29231bd587</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377242</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
