  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Insulin Independence">
  <data key="d0">Insulin Independence</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Insulin independence describes a state where patients no longer require exogenous insulin, achievable after islet autotransplantation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-090b8f9281aa75054311d8f275a2c8f8</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377271</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="75‑g Oral Glucose Tolerance Test">
  <data key="d0">75‑g Oral Glucose Tolerance Test</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The 75‑g oral glucose tolerance test is used to screen for gestational diabetes postpartum and in other contexts.&lt;SEP&gt;The 75‑g Oral Glucose Tolerance Test is a diagnostic test used to screen for gestational diabetes mellitus and other forms of diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-090b8f9281aa75054311d8f275a2c8f8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-83d72fbc44fe0c28f27702c0d4f2c140</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377272</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Type 1 Diabetes-Associated Autoimmunity">
  <data key="d0">Type 1 Diabetes-Associated Autoimmunity</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Type 1 diabetes-associated autoimmunity refers to the autoimmune response characteristic of type 1 diabetes, noted as absent in postpancreatitis diabetes mellitus.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-090b8f9281aa75054311d8f275a2c8f8</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377272</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Exocrine Pancreatic Dysfunction">
  <data key="d0">Exocrine Pancreatic Dysfunction</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Exocrine pancreatic dysfunction denotes impaired exocrine function of the pancreas, identified as a cause of pancreatic diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-090b8f9281aa75054311d8f275a2c8f8</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377273</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Insulin Secretion">
  <data key="d0">Insulin Secretion</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The overall release of insulin, described as defective and insufficient to compensate for insulin resistance.&lt;SEP&gt;Insulin secretion is the process of releasing insulin from pancreatic beta cells, which can be retained through islet autotransplantation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-090b8f9281aa75054311d8f275a2c8f8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9eb02ab1ab7d834858bf60a8b402e6ea</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377274</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Fluctuating Liver Function">
  <data key="d0">Fluctuating Liver Function</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Fluctuating liver function describes variable liver performance, reported as associated with EIF2B1-related permanent diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-090b8f9281aa75054311d8f275a2c8f8</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377274</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Early Pregnancy">
  <data key="d0">Early Pregnancy</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The initial trimester period of gestation examined for diabetes risk.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-525031caa389d084bc170433212cdca8</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377274</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Adverse Pregnancy Outcomes">
  <data key="d0">Adverse Pregnancy Outcomes</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Maternal, fetal, and neonatal complications that increase with higher maternal glycemia.&lt;SEP&gt;Adverse Pregnancy Outcomes are negative health results for mothers or infants linked to preconception diabetes.&lt;SEP&gt;Negative health results for mother or fetus associated with diabetes in pregnancy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-525031caa389d084bc170433212cdca8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9ab98b1c07f7bbaa3ad28fb83167f489&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ae844f5b99d595c38f74e375112238e6</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377274</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Lifestyle Intervention">
  <data key="d0">Lifestyle Intervention</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Program of behavioral changes aimed at preventing or delaying diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-525031caa389d084bc170433212cdca8</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377275</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Exercise During Pregnancy">
  <data key="d0">Exercise During Pregnancy</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Physical activity regimen tested to prevent gestational diabetes in overweight and obese pregnant women.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-525031caa389d084bc170433212cdca8</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377275</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="IADPSG Criteria">
  <data key="d0">IADPSG Criteria</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">IADPSG criteria are diagnostic thresholds based on pregnancy outcomes recommended for identifying Gestational Diabetes Mellitus.&lt;SEP&gt;Diagnostic cut points for GDM based on average fasting, 1‑hour, and 2‑hour plasma glucose values during a 75‑g OGTT.&lt;SEP&gt;The IADPSG criteria represent a “one-step strategy” for diagnosing gestational diabetes mellitus and have been adopted internationally as the preferred approach.&lt;SEP&gt;Consensus diagnostic criteria for gestational diabetes established by the International Association of Diabetes and Pregnancy Study Groups.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-525031caa389d084bc170433212cdca8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-59dd4faf2a2706d073fdb93e1a29da81&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8ba9c9c7fe9dd4e901eb52088f3d59f8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ae844f5b99d595c38f74e375112238e6</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377276</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="HAPO Study">
  <data key="d0">HAPO Study</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">A large‑scale multinational cohort study of more than 23,000 pregnant individuals that showed a continuous increase in adverse maternal, fetal, and neonatal outcomes as maternal glycemia rose.&lt;SEP&gt;Large collaborative research project investigating hyperglycemia and pregnancy outcomes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-525031caa389d084bc170433212cdca8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ae844f5b99d595c38f74e375112238e6</data>
