  <data key="d2">CFRD Guidelines Committee is the committee responsible for authoring clinical care guidelines for cystic fibrosis-related diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-72a2488e8176f7676c76504e76dd6c04</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377304</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="European-New-Onset Diabetes After Transplantation Working Group">
  <data key="d0">European-New-Onset Diabetes After Transplantation Working Group</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">European-New-Onset Diabetes After Transplantation Working Group is an organization that focuses on research and guidance for new-onset diabetes after transplantation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-72a2488e8176f7676c76504e76dd6c04</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377304</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="American College of Obstetricians and Gynecologists">
  <data key="d0">American College of Obstetricians and Gynecologists</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">The American College of Obstetricians and Gynecologists notes that a single elevated value can be used for GDM diagnosis.&lt;SEP&gt;Professional organization that notes a single elevated value can be used for GDM diagnosis.&lt;SEP&gt;The American College of Obstetricians and Gynecologists (ACOG) issues clinical practice bulletins on obstetric care, including gestational diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-59dd4faf2a2706d073fdb93e1a29da81&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ae844f5b99d595c38f74e375112238e6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fedb8cdc485be3c8e38133ddb9ea67cf</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377305</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Glucose Load Test">
  <data key="d0">Glucose Load Test</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The Glucose Load Test is a 1‑hour 50‑g glucose screening test employed in the two‑step method for GDM detection.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-59dd4faf2a2706d073fdb93e1a29da81</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377305</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Carpenter‑Coustan Criteria">
  <data key="d0">Carpenter‑Coustan Criteria</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Carpenter‑Coustan criteria are diagnostic thresholds applied to a 3‑hour OGTT in the two‑step GDM screening approach.&lt;SEP&gt;Diagnostic thresholds for the 3‑hour 100‑g OGTT based on Carpenter and Coustan methodology.&lt;SEP&gt;Interpretation criteria for the two‑step GDM screening approach, derived from older diagnostic standards.&lt;SEP&gt;Carpenter‑Coustan Criteria are a set of screening and diagnostic thresholds for gestational diabetes, frequently compared with other criteria in research.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-59dd4faf2a2706d073fdb93e1a29da81&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ae844f5b99d595c38f74e375112238e6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-49c21dd27a63d44c5d80b53aa7e1f48d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-037075addb77da4a5a1721a95ee298c0</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377305</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="One‑Step Method">
  <data key="d0">One‑Step Method</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The one‑step method uses a single 2‑hour 75‑g OGTT with IADPSG criteria to diagnose Gestational Diabetes Mellitus.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-59dd4faf2a2706d073fdb93e1a29da81</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377305</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Two‑Step Method">
  <data key="d0">Two‑Step Method</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The two‑step method screens with a Glucose Load Test followed by a 3‑hour OGTT interpreted by Carpenter‑Coustan criteria for Gestational Diabetes Mellitus.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-59dd4faf2a2706d073fdb93e1a29da81</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377305</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Lifestyle Therapy">
  <data key="d0">Lifestyle Therapy</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Lifestyle therapy refers to non‑pharmacologic interventions that can manage mild Gestational Diabetes Mellitus.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-59dd4faf2a2706d073fdb93e1a29da81</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377305</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="HAPO Cohort">
  <data key="d0">HAPO Cohort</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">The HAPO cohort is a study population whose follow‑up data link maternal GDM to offspring metabolic outcomes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-59dd4faf2a2706d073fdb93e1a29da81</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377306</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="HAPO Follow‑Up Study">
  <data key="d0">HAPO Follow‑Up Study</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">The HAPO Follow‑Up Study reports long‑term offspring outcomes associated with maternal Gestational Diabetes Mellitus.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-59dd4faf2a2706d073fdb93e1a29da81</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377306</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="NHANES Data">
  <data key="d0">NHANES Data</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">NHANES data demonstrate a 21.5% prevalence of prediabetes among people of childbearing age.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-59dd4faf2a2706d073fdb93e1a29da81</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377306</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Large‑For‑Gestational‑Age Births">
  <data key="d0">Large‑For‑Gestational‑Age Births</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Large‑for‑gestational‑age births are an adverse outcome occurring at higher rates among pregnancies affected by Gestational Diabetes Mellitus.&lt;SEP&gt;Births where the infant’s weight exceeds the gestational‑age norm, reduced by two‑step treatment.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-59dd4faf2a2706d073fdb93e1a29da81&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-49c21dd27a63d44c5d80b53aa7e1f48d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377307</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Preeclampsia">
  <data key="d0">Preeclampsia</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Preeclampsia is a pregnancy complication that occurs more frequently in women diagnosed with Gestational Diabetes Mellitus.&lt;SEP&gt;Preeclampsia is a hypertensive pregnancy complication associated with early abnormal glucose metabolism.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-59dd4faf2a2706d073fdb93e1a29da81&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-83d72fbc44fe0c28f27702c0d4f2c140</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377307</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Offspring Abnormal Glucose Metabolism">
  <data key="d0">Offspring Abnormal Glucose Metabolism</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Offspring abnormal glucose metabolism describes impaired glucose regulation observed in children of mothers with Gestational Diabetes Mellitus.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-59dd4faf2a2706d073fdb93e1a29da81</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377307</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Offspring Adiposity">
  <data key="d0">Offspring Adiposity</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Offspring adiposity refers to increased body fat observed in children of mothers who had Gestational Diabetes Mellitus.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-59dd4faf2a2706d073fdb93e1a29da81</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377307</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Impaired Glucose Tolerance">
  <data key="d0">Impaired Glucose Tolerance</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Impaired Glucose Tolerance is a metabolic condition indicating elevated glucose levels that was reported as higher in offspring of mothers with Gestational Diabetes Mellitus.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-59dd4faf2a2706d073fdb93e1a29da81</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377308</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Oral Disposition Index">
  <data key="d0">Oral Disposition Index</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Oral Disposition Index is a measure of beta‑cell function relative to insulin sensitivity, reported as reduced in offspring of mothers with Gestational Diabetes Mellitus.&lt;SEP&gt;A composite measure of insulin secretion and sensitivity derived from oral glucose challenge tests.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-59dd4faf2a2706d073fdb93e1a29da81&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-49c21dd27a63d44c5d80b53aa7e1f48d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377308</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Maternal Prediabetes">
  <data key="d0">Maternal Prediabetes</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Maternal Prediabetes denotes prediabetic glucose levels in mothers, identified as a long‑term risk associated with Gestational Diabetes Mellitus.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-59dd4faf2a2706d073fdb93e1a29da81</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377308</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Maternal Diabetes">
  <data key="d0">Maternal Diabetes</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Maternal Diabetes describes diabetes developing in mothers after a Gestational Diabetes Mellitus pregnancy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-59dd4faf2a2706d073fdb93e1a29da81</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377308</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Pregnancy Outcomes">
  <data key="d0">Pregnancy Outcomes</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Pregnancy Outcomes are health results of pregnancy, which form the basis for the IADPSG diagnostic criteria.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-59dd4faf2a2706d073fdb93e1a29da81</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377309</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hemoglobin Variant">
  <data key="d0">Hemoglobin Variant</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A genetic form of hemoglobin that can affect A1C measurements without altering red blood cell turnover.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d01033177672e6c36e0a368db88e586d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377309</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="NGSP Interference List">
  <data key="d0">NGSP Interference List</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">An online list of A1C assays with known interferences, available at ngsp.org/interf.asp.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d01033177672e6c36e0a368db88e586d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377310</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Glucose-6-Phosphate Dehydrogenase G202A">
  <data key="d0">Glucose-6-Phosphate Dehydrogenase G202A</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">An X-linked genetic variant present in about 11% of African American individuals, associated with decreased A1C values.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d01033177672e6c36e0a368db88e586d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377311</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Tanzania">
  <data key="d0">Tanzania</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">A country referenced as having a high likelihood of hemoglobinopathies among people with HIV.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d01033177672e6c36e0a368db88e586d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377311</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Glycated Albumin">
  <data key="d0">Glycated Albumin</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A glycated protein biomarker reported to be higher in African American individuals.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d01033177672e6c36e0a368db88e586d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377312</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Afro-Caribbean People">
  <data key="d0">Afro-Caribbean People</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Individuals of Afro-Caribbean descent reported to have lower A1C than predicted by glucose levels.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d01033177672e6c36e0a368db88e586d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377313</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Taiwanese Population">
  <data key="d0">Taiwanese Population</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">People from Taiwan in which age and sex have been linked to increased A1C in men.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d01033177672e6c36e0a368db88e586d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377313</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Sickle Cell Disease">
  <data key="d0">Sickle Cell Disease</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Sickle Cell Disease is a hemoglobinopathy that may cause discordance between A1C and glucose measurements.&lt;SEP&gt;A condition causing increased red blood cell turnover and affecting A1C reliability.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d01033177672e6c36e0a368db88e586d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3cc61bc2e95346d553972b4371912e7f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377313</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Pregnancy (Second and Third Trimesters)">
  <data key="d0">Pregnancy (Second and Third Trimesters)</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A stage of pregnancy associated with increased red blood cell turnover.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d01033177672e6c36e0a368db88e586d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377314</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Blood Loss">
  <data key="d0">Blood Loss</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Recent blood loss or transfusion can affect A1C measurements.&lt;SEP&gt;An event leading to increased red blood cell turnover.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d01033177672e6c36e0a368db88e586d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3cc61bc2e95346d553972b4371912e7f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377314</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Transfusion">
  <data key="d0">Transfusion</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Transfusion of blood products can cause A1C assay interference.&lt;SEP&gt;A medical procedure that influences red blood cell turnover.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d01033177672e6c36e0a368db88e586d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3cc61bc2e95346d553972b4371912e7f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377314</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Erythropoietin Therapy">
  <data key="d0">Erythropoietin Therapy</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Erythropoietin therapy can modify the relationship between A1C and actual glucose levels.&lt;SEP&gt;A therapy that affects red blood cell turnover.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d01033177672e6c36e0a368db88e586d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3cc61bc2e95346d553972b4371912e7f</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377314</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Postpartum State">
  <data key="d0">Postpartum State</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The period after childbirth during which A1C is less reliable.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d01033177672e6c36e0a368db88e586d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377315</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Iron-Deficient Anemia">
  <data key="d0">Iron-Deficient Anemia</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A condition that makes A1C less reliable.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d01033177672e6c36e0a368db88e586d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377317</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hyperglycemic Crisis">
  <data key="d0">Hyperglycemic Crisis</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">A severe acute elevation of blood glucose used as a clinical scenario for diabetes diagnosis.&lt;SEP&gt;Hyperglycemic crisis is a severe complication of diabetes mentioned alongside hyperglycemia.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d01033177672e6c36e0a368db88e586d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6601fea85bfbb9f20040c70b7e21695d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377317</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Diabetes Diagnosis">
  <data key="d0">Diabetes Diagnosis</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The process of confirming diabetes, requiring two abnormal screening tests or meeting specific criteria.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d01033177672e6c36e0a368db88e586d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377317</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Screening Test">
  <data key="d0">Screening Test</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Any test such as A1C assay, fasting plasma glucose, or 2‑hour plasma glucose used to screen for diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d01033177672e6c36e0a368db88e586d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377317</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="2-Hour Plasma Glucose">
  <data key="d0">2-Hour Plasma Glucose</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A glucose measurement taken two hours after a glucose load, used as a screening test for diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d01033177672e6c36e0a368db88e586d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377318</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Diagnostic Cut Point">
  <data key="d0">Diagnostic Cut Point</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The threshold value above which a test result confirms diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d01033177672e6c36e0a368db88e586d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377318</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Plasma Sample">
  <data key="d0">Plasma Sample</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The blood plasma specimen used to perform an A1C assay.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d01033177672e6c36e0a368db88e586d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377318</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Mean Glycemia">
  <data key="d0">Mean Glycemia</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The average level of blood glucose over time referenced in relation to A1C measurements.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d01033177672e6c36e0a368db88e586d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377318</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Mean Glucose Concentration">
  <data key="d0">Mean Glucose Concentration</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The average glucose concentration used to compare with A1C values, especially when measured by continuous glucose monitoring.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d01033177672e6c36e0a368db88e586d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377318</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Glycemic Burden">
  <data key="d0">Glycemic Burden</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The overall impact of glucose exposure on the body, suggested to be higher in African American individuals.&lt;SEP&gt;The cumulative exposure to high blood glucose, a strong predictor of adverse outcomes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d01033177672e6c36e0a368db88e586d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9eb02ab1ab7d834858bf60a8b402e6ea</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377318</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Risk for Complications">
  <data key="d0">Risk for Complications</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The likelihood of diabetes‑related health complications associated with A1C levels.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d01033177672e6c36e0a368db88e586d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377319</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Non-Hispanic White Individuals">
  <data key="d0">Non-Hispanic White Individuals</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">People identified as non‑Hispanic White referenced for comparative A1C levels.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d01033177672e6c36e0a368db88e586d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377319</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Preanalytic Variability">
  <data key="d0">Preanalytic Variability</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Preanalytic variability refers to variability in test results due to sample handling before analysis.&lt;SEP&gt;Variability occurring before analysis that can affect screening test results.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d01033177672e6c36e0a368db88e586d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6601fea85bfbb9f20040c70b7e21695d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377319</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Analytic Variability">
  <data key="d0">Analytic Variability</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Analytic variability refers to variability arising during the analytical measurement process.&lt;SEP&gt;Variability occurring during analysis that can affect screening test results.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d01033177672e6c36e0a368db88e586d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6601fea85bfbb9f20040c70b7e21695d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377319</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Plasma Blood Glucose Criteria">
  <data key="d0">Plasma Blood Glucose Criteria</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Diagnostic criteria based on plasma glucose levels used to diagnose diabetes when A1C is unreliable.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d01033177672e6c36e0a368db88e586d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377319</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="2-Hour Plasma Glucose (2-h PG)">
  <data key="d0">2-Hour Plasma Glucose (2-h PG)</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">2-h PG is the plasma glucose level measured two hours after an oral glucose challenge, also affected by preanalytic conditions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6601fea85bfbb9f20040c70b7e21695d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377320</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Mixed Diet">
  <data key="d0">Mixed Diet</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Mixed diet is a dietary regimen containing at least 150 g of carbohydrates for three days before OGTT.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6601fea85bfbb9f20040c70b7e21695d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377320</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Autoantibodies to Insulin">
  <data key="d0">Autoantibodies to Insulin</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Autoantibodies to insulin are immune markers used in screening for presymptomatic type 1 diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6601fea85bfbb9f20040c70b7e21695d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377320</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Autoantibodies to Glutamic Acid Decarboxylase">
  <data key="d0">Autoantibodies to Glutamic Acid Decarboxylase</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Autoantibodies to GAD are immune markers involved in type 1 diabetes risk assessment.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6601fea85bfbb9f20040c70b7e21695d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377320</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Autoantibodies to Islet Antigen 2">
  <data key="d0">Autoantibodies to Islet Antigen 2</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Autoantibodies to islet antigen 2 are part of the autoantibody panel for type 1 diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6601fea85bfbb9f20040c70b7e21695d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377320</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Autoantibodies to Zinc Transporter 8">
  <data key="d0">Autoantibodies to Zinc Transporter 8</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Autoantibodies to zinc transporter 8 are included in screening for type 1 diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6601fea85bfbb9f20040c70b7e21695d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377320</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Autoimmune Markers">
  <data key="d0">Autoimmune Markers</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Autoimmune markers encompass islet cell autoantibodies and specific autoantibodies such as insulin, GAD, IA-2, and ZnT8.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6601fea85bfbb9f20040c70b7e21695d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377321</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Glutamic Acid Decarboxylase">
  <data key="d0">Glutamic Acid Decarboxylase</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">GAD is an enzyme targeted by autoantibodies in type 1 diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6601fea85bfbb9f20040c70b7e21695d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377321</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Islet Antigen 2">
  <data key="d0">Islet Antigen 2</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Islet antigen 2 is a protein targeted by autoantibodies in type 1 diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6601fea85bfbb9f20040c70b7e21695d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377321</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Zinc Transporter 8">
  <data key="d0">Zinc Transporter 8</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Zinc transporter 8 is a protein targeted by autoantibodies in type 1 diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6601fea85bfbb9f20040c70b7e21695d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377321</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Immune-Mediated Diabetes">
  <data key="d0">Immune-Mediated Diabetes</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Immune-mediated diabetes, previously called insulin-dependent diabetes, accounts for 5–10 % of diabetes cases and is caused by autoimmune destruction of beta‑cells.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6601fea85bfbb9f20040c70b7e21695d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377321</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Pancreatic Beta-Cells">
  <data key="d0">Pancreatic Beta-Cells</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Pancreatic beta‑cells are the insulin‑producing cells destroyed in immune‑mediated diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6601fea85bfbb9f20040c70b7e21695d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377322</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="HLA">
  <data key="d0">HLA</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">HLA refers to human leukocyte antigen genes with strong associations to type 1 diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6601fea85bfbb9f20040c70b7e21695d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377322</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="DQB1">
  <data key="d0">DQB1</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">DQB1 is an HLA haplotype linked to type 1 diabetes risk.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6601fea85bfbb9f20040c70b7e21695d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377322</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="DRB1">
  <data key="d0">DRB1</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">DRB1 is an HLA haplotype linked to type 1 diabetes risk.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6601fea85bfbb9f20040c70b7e21695d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377322</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="High-Risk Populations">
  <data key="d0">High-Risk Populations</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">High‑risk populations are groups identified by genetic screening as having elevated risk for type 1 diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6601fea85bfbb9f20040c70b7e21695d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377322</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Stage 1">
  <data key="d0">Stage 1</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Stage 1 of type 1 diabetes is defined by the presence of two or more autoimmune markers.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6601fea85bfbb9f20040c70b7e21695d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377322</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="trialnet.org">
  <data key="d0">trialnet.org</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">trialnet.org is a website that hosts prevention studies for type 1 diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6601fea85bfbb9f20040c70b7e21695d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377322</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Prevention Studies">
  <data key="d0">Prevention Studies</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Prevention studies are research efforts aimed at avoiding onset of type 1 diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6601fea85bfbb9f20040c70b7e21695d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377322</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Plasma C-peptide">
  <data key="d0">Plasma C-peptide</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Plasma C-peptide is a laboratory measurement indicating insulin secretion levels.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6601fea85bfbb9f20040c70b7e21695d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377323</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Centrifugation">
  <data key="d0">Centrifugation</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Centrifugation is the process of spinning plasma samples to separate components promptly.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6601fea85bfbb9f20040c70b7e21695d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377323</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Oral Glucose Challenge">
  <data key="d0">Oral Glucose Challenge</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Oral glucose challenge is the ingestion of glucose used during testing, which can be affected by carbohydrate restriction.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6601fea85bfbb9f20040c70b7e21695d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377323</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Carbohydrate Restriction">
  <data key="d0">Carbohydrate Restriction</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Carbohydrate restriction is a dietary condition that can falsely elevate glucose levels during an oral glucose challenge.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6601fea85bfbb9f20040c70b7e21695d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377324</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Diagnostic Glucose Threshold">
  <data key="d0">Diagnostic Glucose Threshold</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Diagnostic glucose threshold is the plasma glucose level (≥200 mg/dL or 11.1 mmol/L) used to diagnose diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6601fea85bfbb9f20040c70b7e21695d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377324</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="11.1 mmol/L">
  <data key="d0">11.1 mmol/L</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">11.1 mmol/L is the equivalent concentration to 200 mg/dL for the diagnostic glucose threshold.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6601fea85bfbb9f20040c70b7e21695d</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377324</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Asian American Individuals">
  <data key="d0">Asian American Individuals</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A population subgroup for which a lower BMI threshold (≥23 kg/m2) is applied in diabetes screening.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ca8741dfdb9ff0f12f049953db6cb9c0</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377324</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="First-Degree Relative with Diabetes">
  <data key="d0">First-Degree Relative with Diabetes</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Having an immediate family member diagnosed with diabetes, listed as a risk factor.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ca8741dfdb9ff0f12f049953db6cb9c0</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377325</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="High-Risk Race/Ethnicity">
  <data key="d0">High-Risk Race/Ethnicity</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Demographic groups (African American, Latino, Native American, Asian American, Pacific Islander) associated with increased diabetes risk.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ca8741dfdb9ff0f12f049953db6cb9c0</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377325</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="African American">
