  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">NODAT (New-Onset Diabetes After Transplant) is a term used to exclude individuals with pretransplant diabetes or transient hyperglycemia that resolves before discharge.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e4e7eef761aec994cc4558b2db5e1e08</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377334</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Posttransplantation Diabetes Mellitus (PTDM)">
  <data key="d0">Posttransplantation Diabetes Mellitus (PTDM)</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">PTDM denotes diabetes occurring in the posttransplant setting regardless of when the condition first appears.&lt;SEP&gt;Posttransplantation Diabetes Mellitus (PTDM) is diabetes that develops after organ transplantation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e4e7eef761aec994cc4558b2db5e1e08&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9cdf6af658e42c2f4f7dca5e4dbdd3db</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377334</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Early Posttransplant Period">
  <data key="d0">Early Posttransplant Period</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The Early Posttransplant Period is the initial weeks after transplantation when metabolic disturbances are common.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e4e7eef761aec994cc4558b2db5e1e08</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377335</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Kidney Allograft Recipients">
  <data key="d0">Kidney Allograft Recipients</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Kidney Allograft Recipients are patients who have received a kidney transplant.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e4e7eef761aec994cc4558b2db5e1e08</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377335</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Immunosuppressive Therapies">
  <data key="d0">Immunosuppressive Therapies</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Immunosuppressive Therapies are medication regimens used to prevent transplant rejection and are major contributors to PTDM development.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e4e7eef761aec994cc4558b2db5e1e08</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377335</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Diabetes Care Health Care Professional">
  <data key="d0">Diabetes Care Health Care Professional</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Diabetes Care Health Care Professionals are clinicians responsible for managing hyperglycemia in transplant patients.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e4e7eef761aec994cc4558b2db5e1e08</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377335</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="General Diabetes Risk Factors">
  <data key="d0">General Diabetes Risk Factors</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">General Diabetes Risk Factors include age, family history, and other common determinants of diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e4e7eef761aec994cc4558b2db5e1e08</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377335</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Transplant-Specific Factors">
  <data key="d0">Transplant-Specific Factors</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Transplant-Specific Factors are elements such as immunosuppressant use that increase PTDM risk.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e4e7eef761aec994cc4558b2db5e1e08</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377336</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Immunosuppressant Agents">
  <data key="d0">Immunosuppressant Agents</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Immunosuppressant Agents are drugs administered to prevent organ rejection and act as risk factors for PTDM.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e4e7eef761aec994cc4558b2db5e1e08</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377336</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Posttransplantation Hyperglycemia">
  <data key="d0">Posttransplantation Hyperglycemia</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Posttransplantation Hyperglycemia is elevated glucose occurring after transplantation and serves as a risk factor for PTDM.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e4e7eef761aec994cc4558b2db5e1e08</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377336</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="hs-CRP">
  <data key="d0">hs-CRP</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">hs-CRP is a high‑sensitivity C‑reactive protein biomarker whose pretransplant elevation is linked to PTDM in renal transplant patients.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e4e7eef761aec994cc4558b2db5e1e08</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377337</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Antihyperglycemic Agents">
  <data key="d0">Antihyperglycemic Agents</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Antihyperglycemic agents are drugs that may still be necessary in certain cases alongside HIV care.&lt;SEP&gt;Antihyperglycemic Agents are medications used to control blood glucose in PTDM patients.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e4e7eef761aec994cc4558b2db5e1e08&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0631ff2b95dd459677eaaebe9283a776</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377337</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Noninsulin Agents">
  <data key="d0">Noninsulin Agents</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Noninsulin Agents are alternative glucose‑lowering drugs whose safety profile in PTDM remains uncertain.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e4e7eef761aec994cc4558b2db5e1e08</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377337</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Dipeptidyl Peptidase 4 Inhibitors">
  <data key="d0">Dipeptidyl Peptidase 4 Inhibitors</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Dipeptidyl Peptidase 4 Inhibitors are antihyperglycemic agents that do not interact with immunosuppressant drugs.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e4e7eef761aec994cc4558b2db5e1e08</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377337</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Monogenic Diabetes Syndromes">
  <data key="d0">Monogenic Diabetes Syndromes</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Monogenic Diabetes Syndromes are genetic forms of diabetes such as neonatal diabetes and maturity‑onset diabetes of the young.&lt;SEP&gt;Monogenic Diabetes Syndromes are rare forms of diabetes caused by single‑gene mutations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e4e7eef761aec994cc4558b2db5e1e08&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f7b840a0b5327c5e583eb70dd354d1d0</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377337</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Center Specializing in Diabetes">
  <data key="d0">Center Specializing in Diabetes</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">The Center Specializing in Diabetes is an organization that provides expert consultation for complex diabetes cases.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e4e7eef761aec994cc4558b2db5e1e08</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377337</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Heart Transplant Recipients">
  <data key="d0">Heart Transplant Recipients</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Heart Transplant Recipients are patients who have received a heart transplant.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e4e7eef761aec994cc4558b2db5e1e08</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377337</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Lung Transplant Recipients">
  <data key="d0">Lung Transplant Recipients</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Lung Transplant Recipients are patients who have received a lung transplant.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e4e7eef761aec994cc4558b2db5e1e08</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377337</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Liver Transplant Recipients">
  <data key="d0">Liver Transplant Recipients</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Liver Transplant Recipients are patients who have received a liver transplant.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e4e7eef761aec994cc4558b2db5e1e08</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377338</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hospital Discharge on Insulin">
  <data key="d0">Hospital Discharge on Insulin</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Hospital Discharge on Insulin refers to patients leaving the hospital while still requiring insulin therapy, a risk factor for PTDM.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e4e7eef761aec994cc4558b2db5e1e08</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377338</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Pre-Discharge Glucose Values">
  <data key="d0">Pre-Discharge Glucose Values</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Pre-Discharge Glucose Values are blood glucose measurements taken within 24 hours before hospital discharge, associated with PTDM risk.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e4e7eef761aec994cc4558b2db5e1e08</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377338</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Rehospitalization">
  <data key="d0">Rehospitalization</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">Rehospitalization is the event of a patient being readmitted to the hospital after discharge.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e4e7eef761aec994cc4558b2db5e1e08</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377338</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Transplant Rejection">
  <data key="d0">Transplant Rejection</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">Transplant Rejection is the immune‑mediated loss of a transplanted organ.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e4e7eef761aec994cc4558b2db5e1e08</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377338</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Acute Infection">
  <data key="d0">Acute Infection</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">Acute Infection is a sudden infection that may preclude PTDM diagnosis.&lt;SEP&gt;Acute infection is a sudden infectious condition, cited as a condition that should be absent when formally diagnosing posttransplantation diabetes mellitus.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e4e7eef761aec994cc4558b2db5e1e08&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9cdf6af658e42c2f4f7dca5e4dbdd3db</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377339</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Maintenance Immunosuppression">
  <data key="d0">Maintenance Immunosuppression</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Maintenance Immunosuppression is the ongoing regimen of immunosuppressive drugs required for transplant stability.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e4e7eef761aec994cc4558b2db5e1e08</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377339</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Side Effect Profile">
  <data key="d0">Side Effect Profile</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Side Effect Profile describes the adverse effects associated with a medication.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e4e7eef761aec994cc4558b2db5e1e08</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377339</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Fluid Retention">
  <data key="d0">Fluid Retention</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Fluid Retention is a side effect observed with thiazolidinediones.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e4e7eef761aec994cc4558b2db5e1e08</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377340</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Osteopenia">
  <data key="d0">Osteopenia</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Osteopenia is a reduction in bone density that can result from thiazolidinedione use.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e4e7eef761aec994cc4558b2db5e1e08</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377340</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Pretransplant Diabetes">
  <data key="d0">Pretransplant Diabetes</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Pretransplant Diabetes is diabetes present before transplantation, excluded from NODAT definition.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e4e7eef761aec994cc4558b2db5e1e08</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377340</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Posttransplant Setting">
  <data key="d0">Posttransplant Setting</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Posttransplant Setting refers to the clinical period after organ transplantation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e4e7eef761aec994cc4558b2db5e1e08</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377340</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Preexisting Diabetes">
  <data key="d0">Preexisting Diabetes</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Preexisting Diabetes refers to diabetes that was present before transplantation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e4e7eef761aec994cc4558b2db5e1e08</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377341</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Stress-Induced Hyperglycemia">
  <data key="d0">Stress-Induced Hyperglycemia</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Stress-Induced Hyperglycemia is a form of elevated blood glucose triggered by physiological stress after transplantation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e4e7eef761aec994cc4558b2db5e1e08</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377341</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Steroid-Induced Hyperglycemia">
  <data key="d0">Steroid-Induced Hyperglycemia</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Steroid-Induced Hyperglycemia is elevated blood glucose caused by steroid therapy in the posttransplant period.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e4e7eef761aec994cc4558b2db5e1e08</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377341</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Risk Factors for PTDM">
  <data key="d0">Risk Factors for PTDM</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Risk Factors for PTDM encompass general diabetes risk factors, transplant‑specific factors, and other contributors to posttransplantation diabetes mellitus.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e4e7eef761aec994cc4558b2db5e1e08</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377341</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Home Glucose Monitoring">
  <data key="d0">Home Glucose Monitoring</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Home Glucose Monitoring refers to patients regularly checking blood glucose at home to guide insulin dosing after discharge.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e4e7eef761aec994cc4558b2db5e1e08</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377341</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Drug Dose Adjustments">
  <data key="d0">Drug Dose Adjustments</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Drug Dose Adjustments are modifications to medication dosages required when glomerular filtration rate changes in transplant patients.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e4e7eef761aec994cc4558b2db5e1e08</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377341</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Immunosuppression Regimen">
  <data key="d0">Immunosuppression Regimen</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Immunosuppression Regimen is the schedule of immunosuppressive drugs used to maintain transplant stability.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e4e7eef761aec994cc4558b2db5e1e08</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377341</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Short-Term Pilot Study">
  <data key="d0">Short-Term Pilot Study</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">The Short-Term Pilot Study reported that metformin was safe for use in renal transplant recipients.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e4e7eef761aec994cc4558b2db5e1e08</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377342</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Randomized Controlled Studies">
  <data key="d0">Randomized Controlled Studies</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Randomized Controlled Studies have examined the short‑ and long‑term use of antihyperglycemic agents in PTDM.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e4e7eef761aec994cc4558b2db5e1e08</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377342</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Iranian Cohort">
  <data key="d0">Iranian Cohort</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The Iranian Cohort is a study group in which 19% of participants developed PTDM after heart and lung transplantation.</data>
