<node id="Cystic Fibrosis-Related Diabetes (CFRD)">
  <data key="d0">Cystic Fibrosis-Related Diabetes (CFRD)</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Cystic Fibrosis-Related Diabetes (CFRD) is a disease that commonly co-occurs with cystic fibrosis and is characterized by insulin insufficiency.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9cdf6af658e42c2f4f7dca5e4dbdd3db</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377348</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Insulin Insufficiency">
  <data key="d0">Insulin Insufficiency</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Insulin insufficiency describes inadequate insulin production contributing to diabetes in cystic fibrosis patients.&lt;SEP&gt;Insulin Insufficiency is the primary defect underlying CFRD.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9cdf6af658e42c2f4f7dca5e4dbdd3db&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0631ff2b95dd459677eaaebe9283a776</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377348</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="B-Cell Function">
  <data key="d0">B-Cell Function</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">B-Cell Function refers to the genetically determined capacity of pancreatic beta cells, influencing CFRD development.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9cdf6af658e42c2f4f7dca5e4dbdd3db</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
