  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Organ Transplantation">
  <data key="d0">Organ Transplantation</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">Organ Transplantation is a medical procedure that can lead to drug‑induced diabetes.&lt;SEP&gt;Organ Transplantation is a medical procedure after which screening for hyperglycemia and PTDM is recommended.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9cdf6af658e42c2f4f7dca5e4dbdd3db&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f7b840a0b5327c5e583eb70dd354d1d0</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377351</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="New-Onset Diabetes After Transplantation (NODAT)">
  <data key="d0">New-Onset Diabetes After Transplantation (NODAT)</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">New-Onset Diabetes After Transplantation (NODAT) describes diabetes that appears after transplantation, excluding pre‑transplant diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9cdf6af658e42c2f4f7dca5e4dbdd3db</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377351</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Immunosuppressive Regimen">
  <data key="d0">Immunosuppressive Regimen</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Immunosuppressive Regimen refers to medication protocols that improve patient and graft survival regardless of PTDM risk.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9cdf6af658e42c2f4f7dca5e4dbdd3db</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377352</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Early Diagnosis">
  <data key="d0">Early Diagnosis</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Early diagnosis refers to identifying CFRD promptly, which is linked to better outcomes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9cdf6af658e42c2f4f7dca5e4dbdd3db</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377352</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Patient Survival">
  <data key="d0">Patient Survival</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Patient survival refers to the continued life of transplant recipients, a benefit of immunosuppressive regimens.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9cdf6af658e42c2f4f7dca5e4dbdd3db</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377352</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Nutritional Status">
  <data key="d0">Nutritional Status</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Nutritional status refers to the health of diet‑related parameters, worsened in CFRD patients.&lt;SEP&gt;Nutritional status refers to the health condition related to nutrition, reported as worse in individuals with Cystic Fibrosis-Related Diabetes (CFRD) compared to those with type 1 or type 2 diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9cdf6af658e42c2f4f7dca5e4dbdd3db&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0631ff2b95dd459677eaaebe9283a776</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377353</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Inflammatory Lung Disease">
  <data key="d0">Inflammatory Lung Disease</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Inflammatory lung disease denotes severe respiratory involvement associated with CFRD.&lt;SEP&gt;Inflammatory lung disease denotes lung inflammation, described as more severe in people with CFRD than in those with type 1 or type 2 diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9cdf6af658e42c2f4f7dca5e4dbdd3db&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0631ff2b95dd459677eaaebe9283a776</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377353</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Lung Function">
  <data key="d0">Lung Function</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Lung function is a measure of respiratory performance, associated with greater mortality in CFRD and shown to be preserved with early diagnosis and treatment.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9cdf6af658e42c2f4f7dca5e4dbdd3db</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377353</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Genotype">
  <data key="d0">Genotype</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Genotype refers to the genetic makeup of individuals, identified as a factor associated with increased CFRD prevalence in registry data.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9cdf6af658e42c2f4f7dca5e4dbdd3db</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786377354</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Female Sex">
  <data key="d0">Female Sex</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Female sex denotes gender, reported as a risk factor for higher CFRD prevalence in the European Cystic Fibrosis Society Patient Registry.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9cdf6af658e42c2f4f7dca5e4dbdd3db</data>
  <data key="d4">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Classification and Diagnosis of.pdf</data>
