<edge source="Diabetes" target="Insulin">
  <data key="d7">7.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Insulin is used as a hypoglycemic hormone to treat diabetes.&lt;SEP&gt;Insulin is a primary medication used to treat diabetes by lowering blood glucose levels.&lt;SEP&gt;Patients with diabetes use insulin therapy.&lt;SEP&gt;Insulin is used to manage blood glucose levels in patients with diabetes.&lt;SEP&gt;Diabetes management includes the use of insulin therapy.&lt;SEP&gt;Insulin therapy is often required early and at high doses in lipodystrophy‑related diabetes.&lt;SEP&gt;Insulin is used as a treatment for diabetes.</data>
