<edge source="Hipoglicemia" target="Superdose">
  <data key="d7">8.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Hipoglicemia, Superdose refers to the clinical relationship in which an excessive or accidental overdose of insulin—whether any insulin preparation or the specific formulation Apidra Solostar—precipitates a drop in blood glucose to hypoglycemic levels. Such a superdose markedly raises the risk of developing severe hipoglicemia and can even produce successive or sequential hypoglycemic episodes if the excess insulin remains active in the circulation.

The hypoglycemia caused by an insulin superdose is typically severe, requiring prompt medical intervention. Clinical observations consistently report that patients may experience a range of neuro‑glycopenic and autonomic symptoms. Common manifestations include apathy (or apatia) and confusion, reflecting impaired cerebral function; palpitations and trembling due to sympathetic activation; nausea and vomiting; and headache (cefaleia). These signs may appear alone or in combination, underscoring the potentially rapid progression from mild to life‑threatening hypoglycemia after a superdose.</data>
  <data key="d9">adverse reaction,adverse_effect,causation,cause,consequence,overdose,risk,sequencing,severe hypoglycemia,symptom</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-8ef35bd45e4ba8d20f4e9181011ccfcd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aca0b919135813e1d5b772face36989d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-04b345bc26ec7f5d7c9db8c6004a50a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0e7689ca0fc736d9eae94256f73fed52&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-922791f49d1bf928fe4f02ddd336927b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7f2714936869e55e840f5294caefeaee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-786395f3716fb61a79fd183c63e1a9d6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a7ca732691e1cbcafd65e378b8d80144</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_1778357531609.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_apidra.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1786318705</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hipoglicemia" target="Coma">
  <data key="d7">2.0</data>
