<edge source="Insulin" target="Edema">
  <data key="d7">6.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Swollen areas should not be used for insulin injection.&lt;SEP&gt;Rarely, insulin can cause sodium retention and edema.&lt;SEP&gt;Edema, including peripheral edema, may result from insulin‑induced sodium retention.&lt;SEP&gt;Edema may occur at the site where insulin is administered.&lt;SEP&gt;Edema has been reported in patients receiving insulin therapy, particularly those with previously poor metabolic control.&lt;SEP&gt;Insulin therapy has been reported to cause edema in some patients.</data>
  <data key="d9">adverse effect,adverse reaction,associated effect,contraindication,fluid accumulation,fluid retention,local reaction,side effect,site avoidance</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-35a8ffab5eb63600b93fb2c67160b5ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4da80e99fd3e43cb7d3b260aca23fe56&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d194d06ef99b3f8aa6b6542b7e93e762&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c68e2c07786710dd5250c6610f52b14d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-779af610d7298ce98490962cd90b4e76&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8ac99e7359716e2cecc2ec93159218b6</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/LANTUS _ BulasMed.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Basaglar.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1786319802</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
