<edge source="Insulin" target="Hyperglycemia">
  <data key="d7">7.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Incorrect insulin use may result in high blood glucose (hyperglycemia).&lt;SEP&gt;Insulin therapy can lead to hyperglycemia, sometimes requiring dose adjustments.&lt;SEP&gt;Repeated insulin injections into amyloid‑affected skin areas have been associated with hyperglycemia.&lt;SEP&gt;Repeated insulin injections into lipodystrophic areas may result in hyperglycemia.&lt;SEP&gt;Insufficient insulin delivery can cause hyperglycemia.&lt;SEP&gt;Excess insulin can lead to hyperglycemia under certain conditions.&lt;SEP&gt;When insulin efficacy declines, it can result in hyperglycemia.</data>
  <data key="d9">adverse effect,adverse reaction,cause,condition,consequence,high_glucose,hyperglycemia,insufficient,metabolic risk,risk,side effect</data>
