<edge source="Sociedade Brasileira de Diabetes" target="Diretriz da Sociedade Brasileira de Diabetes">
  <data key="d7">11.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The Diretriz da Sociedade Brasileira de Diabetes is a clinical guideline issued, authored, and published by the Sociedade Brasileira de Diabetes (the Brazilian Diabetes Society). This guideline represents the Society’s official document that consolidates its recommendations for the management of diabetes in Brazil.

According to the various descriptions, the Diretriz provides detailed guidance on insulin therapy, including specific recommendations for insulin injection and application techniques. It also defines the classification of diabetes, offering criteria for distinguishing among different types of the disease, and includes recommendations related to the diagnosis of diabetes.

The guideline is consistently referenced as a formal publication of the Sociedade Brasileira de Diabetes, reflecting the organization’s role in producing authoritative resources for health professionals involved in diabetes care.</data>
  <data key="d9">authoring,authorship,classification,guideline,guideline author,guideline creation,guideline issuance,issuance,organization,policy,publication,recommendation</data>
