<edge source="HbA1c" target="Time In Range (TIR)">
  <data key="d7">3.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Each 10% change in Time In Range corresponds to a 0.8% change in HbA1c.&lt;SEP&gt;Time In Range percentages correlate negatively with HbA1c values (R = ‑0.84), indicating higher TIR associates with lower HbA1c.&lt;SEP&gt;Each absolute increase of 10% in Time In Range corresponds to a 0.8% decrease in HbA1c.</data>
  <data key="d9">biomarker,causal,correlation,inverse correlation,percentage effect,relationship</data>
