  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Lipodystrophy" target="Recommended Injection Sites">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Injection sites should not be selected if lipodystrophy is present.</data>
  <data key="d9">avoidance,condition</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-e150bb4043de862453b3e96cf6cb663e</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1786301862</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Lipodystrophy" target="Injection Site Rotation">
  <data key="d7">8.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Injection site rotation, the practice of systematically changing the locations where subcutaneous injections are administered, is recognized as an effective strategy for reducing and preventing lipodystrophy. Continuous or regular rotation of injection sites lowers the likelihood that fatty tissue will become altered, scarred, or atrophied as a result of repeated needle puncture in the same area. 

In addition to rotating sites, modifying the injection technique—such as varying needle angle, depth, or using proper hygiene—can further help alleviate existing lipodystrophic changes and support overall tissue health. Consistent adherence to these practices is therefore recommended for individuals who require frequent injections.</data>
  <data key="d9">management,mitigation,practice,prevention,preventive practice,risk reduction,skin health,technique,tissue health,tissue reaction</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-d59c9bf7f429a82cbfd7083e36ff8f9a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f9e5c50e8a808c537075377966ae2ccd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6d0f18c80f8de2dee960a03599d12052&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c95471c4c993fa3a499f99443ee7c922&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-14772c7de5db762c492a75a1c744dae6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9a6f9e10c0d4af5fff0338eb861f9c86&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-acaa1440ae268669e1894588bb9e37c2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-779af610d7298ce98490962cd90b4e76</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/LANTUS _ BulasMed.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/NOVORAPID _ BulasMed.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_apidra.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_fiasp.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1786319816</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Lipodystrophy" target="Lantus">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Lantus injections can lead to lipodystrophy, an alteration of subcutaneous fat at the injection site.</data>
  <data key="d9">adverse effect,injection site</data>
