<edge source="Alcohol 70%" target="Technique of Insulin Application">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The technique requires alcohol 70 % to clean the pen and injection area.</data>
  <data key="d9">disinfectant,preparation</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-a8768fa32f88d682aa4ddf677297047e</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Insulinas CANETAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1786300736</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Alcohol 70%" target="Preparation of Insulin">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Alcohol 70 % is applied to disinfect the vial cap and skin during insulin preparation.</data>
  <data key="d9">disinfection,preparation</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-cc6a26a5d2c41087b58a0f7f71ad21cc</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/insulinas em seringa.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1786301091</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Alcohol 70%" target="Rubber Stopper Of Insulin Vial">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Alcohol 70 % is applied to the rubber stopper of the insulin vial for aseptic preparation.</data>
  <data key="d9">asepsis,disinfection</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-d8310c065da1c624d58d9a0a8e9ff7d4</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1786301852</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Alcohol 70%" target="Subcutaneous Injection Technique">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Alcohol 70% is required to clean the skin before performing a subcutaneous insulin injection in institutional settings.</data>
  <data key="d9">cleaning,prerequisite</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-e150bb4043de862453b3e96cf6cb663e</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1786301862</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Alcohol 70%" target="Institutional Settings">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Health services, daycare centers, and elder care homes require cleaning the injection site with 70 % alcohol.</data>
  <data key="d9">cleaning,prerequisite</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-e150bb4043de862453b3e96cf6cb663e</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1786301863</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Alcohol 70%" target="Injection Technique">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Alcohol 70% is applied to the injection site during the injection technique.</data>
  <data key="d9">asepsis,disinfection</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-7ed0b3e64751c1a28d72e087f711cc20</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1786301867</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Vial" target="Insulin Supplies">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Insulin Supplies include Vials as backup containers for insulin.</data>
  <data key="d9">backup,contain</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-c1700b8f7c792afbd394001e28bf632f</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1786323017</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Vial" target="Reservorios">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Reservorios can be refilled with insulin taken from a Vial.</data>
  <data key="d9">insulin,refill source</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-6737e479a665e986547e5e1e29ef26da</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1786324413</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Vial" target="Equipo Médico">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Equipo Médico provides the vial of rapid‑acting insulin to the patient.</data>
  <data key="d9">provision,supply</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-6737e479a665e986547e5e1e29ef26da</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/41d0f4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1786324418</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Injection Site" target="Quadrant">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Each injection site is divided into quadrants to allow systematic rotation of injection points.</data>
  <data key="d9">rotation,subdivision</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-191286ebd759321d40620f77c84ef5a0</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d12">1786299857</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Injection Site" target="Arm">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The arm serves as a common injection site for insulin administration.</data>
  <data key="d9">body part,location</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-191286ebd759321d40620f77c84ef5a0</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d12">1786299859</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Injection Site" target="Leg">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The leg can be used as an injection site for insulin.</data>
  <data key="d9">body part,location</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-191286ebd759321d40620f77c84ef5a0</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d12">1786299859</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Injection Site" target="Healing Time">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">A 14‑day healing time is required before re‑using the same injection point to allow skin recovery.</data>
  <data key="d9">recovery,spacing</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-191286ebd759321d40620f77c84ef5a0</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d12">1786299861</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Injection Site" target="Skin">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The skin constitutes the tissue of the injection site where insulin is administered.</data>
  <data key="d9">location,tissue</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-191286ebd759321d40620f77c84ef5a0</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d12">1786299862</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Injection Site" target="Cotton">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Cotton is pressed on the injection site for 5 seconds after needle removal to aid hemostasis.</data>
  <data key="d9">compression,post‑injection</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-ebdb9452013f0e340884677832714553</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d12">1786299894</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Injection Site" target="Subcutaneous Fold">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">A subcutaneous fold is created at the injection site to facilitate proper needle placement.</data>
  <data key="d9">preparation,technique</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-7ed0b3e64751c1a28d72e087f711cc20</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1786301869</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Injection Site" target="Site Rotation">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Site rotation dictates alternating among injection sites over time.</data>
  <data key="d9">alternation,schedule</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-7ed0b3e64751c1a28d72e087f711cc20</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1786301870</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Injection Site" target="Humalog">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The injection site influences Humalog’s absorption rate and overall effect.</data>
  <data key="d9">absorption,effect</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-c3daabbd42055dc30154f5f97c85fb7d</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/Bula Humalog.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1786303854</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Injection Site" target="Insulin Dose">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Changing the injection area may necessitate insulin dose modification.</data>
  <data key="d9">adjustment,administration</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-ffb10c00517fa772be2ca9a42f497edf</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/LANTUS _ BulasMed.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1786304271</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Injection Site" target="Patient">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The patient chooses an injection site (e.g., abdomen, buttocks, thighs, upper arms) for each dose.</data>
  <data key="d9">selection,site</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-0b9c41c968bcc1d46185583661e8f989</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Basaglar.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1786310140</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Injection Site" target="Basaglar KwikPen">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The time of action of Basaglar KwikPen varies depending on the injection site.</data>
  <data key="d9">action variability</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-6ca13e396b094f0c2f482892f220f538</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Basaglar.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1786310311</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Injection Site" target="Insulin Lispro">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The speed of insulin lispro absorption and its activity can be affected by the injection site and other variables.</data>
  <data key="d9">absorption,variability</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-bf25fca295be60e28b7c7d3103f722fc</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_1778357531609.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1786310806</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Injection Site" target="Hypoglycemia">
  <data key="d7">2.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Changing the injection site to an unaffected area can cause delayed insulin absorption and result in hypoglycemia.&lt;SEP&gt;A sudden change to a non‑affected injection site can result in hypoglycemia.</data>
  <data key="d9">cause,injection site change,risk,site change</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-d10a1f849386df540104c79e33a7b242&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a1245bd9ff75c998b49dab861cc4cebf</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_fiasp.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1786319786</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Injection Site" target="Blood Glucose Monitoring">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Blood glucose monitoring is recommended after altering the injection site to detect potential hypoglycemia.</data>
  <data key="d9">monitoring,safety</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-d10a1f849386df540104c79e33a7b242</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_fiasp.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1786316307</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Injection Site" target="Hyperglycemia">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Repeated injections in lipodystrophic areas can cause hyperglycemia.</data>
  <data key="d9">cause,hyperglycemia</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-a1245bd9ff75c998b49dab861cc4cebf</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1786319785</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Injection Site" target="Insulin Administration">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Insulin administration is performed by subcutaneous injection at an injection site.</data>
  <data key="d9">delivery,method</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-a1245bd9ff75c998b49dab861cc4cebf</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1786319787</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Quadrant" target="Rotation of Injection Sites">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Using quadrants helps implement the rotation of injection sites.</data>
  <data key="d9">organization,rotation method</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-35a8ffab5eb63600b93fb2c67160b5ef</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d12">1786299909</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Quadrant" target="Injection Site Rotation">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Quadrants are employed as sub‑areas to organize systematic injection‑site rotation.</data>
  <data key="d9">used in</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-708e3c514f667dc9979cfa8df875e473</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Documento sem título.docx</data>
  <data key="d12">1786300328</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Arm" target="Rotation of Injection Sites">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Rotation includes using different points on the arm among other locations.</data>
  <data key="d9">application</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-b91b40e47c97be1b62c0f3d271cd4efd</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d12">1786299868</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Arm" target="Continuous Glucose Sensor">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The sensor is commonly attached to the arm for continuous glucose monitoring.</data>
  <data key="d9">attachment site,placement</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-c0ec5707b6df65f1a6822e01b9bb3fb9</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d12">1786299888</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Arm" target="Injection Site Rotation">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The arm can be used as one of the rotating injection locations.</data>
  <data key="d9">example site</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-708e3c514f667dc9979cfa8df875e473</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Documento sem título.docx</data>
  <data key="d12">1786300327</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Arm" target="Absorption Speed">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Injections in the Arm provide relatively fast insulin absorption.</data>
  <data key="d9">higher absorption</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-4902fb11e4844af5cf6fd61f18b6e4ce</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1786301892</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Leg" target="Rotation of Injection Sites">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Rotation includes using different points on the leg among other locations.</data>
  <data key="d9">application</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-b91b40e47c97be1b62c0f3d271cd4efd</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d12">1786299869</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Leg" target="Injection Site Rotation">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The leg can be used as one of the rotating injection locations.</data>
  <data key="d9">example site</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-708e3c514f667dc9979cfa8df875e473</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Documento sem título.docx</data>
  <data key="d12">1786300328</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Injection Angle" target="Needle Length">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Needle length dictates the appropriate injection angle (e.g., 4‑5 mm → 90°, 6‑8 mm → 45°‑90° for adults, &gt;8 mm → 45°).</data>
  <data key="d9">determination,guidance</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-191286ebd759321d40620f77c84ef5a0</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d12">1786299859</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Injection Angle" target="Injection Technique">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Injection technique specifies the appropriate angle based on needle length and patient age.</data>
  <data key="d9">guidance,procedure</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-191286ebd759321d40620f77c84ef5a0</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d12">1786299861</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Injection Angle" target="Insulin Injection Procedure">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The procedure specifies using a 45° or 90° injection angle depending on needle length.</data>
  <data key="d9">angle,procedure step</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-622f3feb1f15564393e91cefc71256ec</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Documento sem título.docx</data>
  <data key="d12">1786300307</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Injection Angle" target="Needle 6 Mm">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">A 45° angle is recommended when using a 6 mm needle for safer injection.</data>
  <data key="d9">angle recommendation,safety</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-622f3feb1f15564393e91cefc71256ec</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Documento sem título.docx</data>
  <data key="d12">1786300308</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Injection Angle" target="Needle 8 Mm">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">An 8 mm needle may be inserted at either 45° or 90° based on patient preference.</data>
  <data key="d9">angle recommendation</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-622f3feb1f15564393e91cefc71256ec</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Documento sem título.docx</data>
  <data key="d12">1786300309</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Injection Angle" target="Adult">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Adults are advised to use a 45°‑90° injection angle when using 6‑8 mm needles.</data>
  <data key="d9">dosage,patient guidance</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-8abf9336f83edf5c92071da1032dc483</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Documento sem título.docx</data>
  <data key="d12">1786300311</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Injection Angle" target="Child">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Children should use a 45° injection angle regardless of needle length.</data>
  <data key="d9">dosage,patient guidance</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-8abf9336f83edf5c92071da1032dc483</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/Documento sem título.docx</data>
  <data key="d12">1786300312</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Injection Angle" target="Administration of Insulin">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The needle is introduced at an angle oriented by the health professional.</data>
  <data key="d9">injection,orientation</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-cc6a26a5d2c41087b58a0f7f71ad21cc</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/insulinas em seringa.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1786301097</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Needle Length" target="Application Angle">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Needle length determines the recommended insertion angle to avoid intramuscular injection.</data>
  <data key="d9">angle recommendation,dosage guidance</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-64b999805e924800faef3b856e45d8bf</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Aplicação de insulina/uso da insulina - Diretrizes-Sociedade-Brasileira-de-Diabetes-2019-2020.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1786301903</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Pregnancy" target="Baby">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Proper diabetes control during pregnancy is essential for the health of the baby.</data>
  <data key="d9">affects,health</data>
