</edge>
<edge source="Hypoglycemia" target="Continuous Glucose Monitor (CGM)">
  <data key="d7">3.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Use of CGM during pregnancy reduces the occurrence of hypoglycemia in the mother.&lt;SEP&gt;CGM with automated low‑glucose suspend helps detect and reduce hypoglycemia episodes.&lt;SEP&gt;CGM can sound an alarm when hypoglycemia (low blood glucose) is detected.</data>
  <data key="d9">alert,detection,monitoring,outcome,reduction</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-cd6b0367ed2176146798e5cf697d0aeb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cc39a0c02d5f1bd08d5cb71bacc69a24&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-208cda7ee40e8d266fadd1eadff49e03</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Metas glicêmicas/metas cuidado do diabetes.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/hipoglicemia.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1786372348</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hypoglycemia" target="Continuous Glucose Monitoring (CGM)">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">CGM helps users detect and avoid episodes of hypoglycemia, especially in individuals with frequent lows.</data>
  <data key="d9">benefit,prevention</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-b6828aacfba0c2a6ae59c439a4e4b161</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d12">1786299896</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hypoglycemia" target="Glucose Alarm">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Glucose alarms warn users of impending hypoglycemia, helping prevent severe low‑glucose events.</data>
  <data key="d9">alert,prevention</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-b6828aacfba0c2a6ae59c439a4e4b161</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/DOC Completo.docx</data>
  <data key="d12">1786299898</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hypoglycemia" target="13 mm Needle">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The use of a 13 mm Needle can increase the risk of hypoglycemia by delivering insulin into muscle.</data>
  <data key="d9">causes,risk factor</data>
