</edge>
<edge source="Hypoglycemia" target="Glucagon">
  <data key="d7">8.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Glucagon is a peptide hormone that raises blood glucose levels and is used therapeutically to treat severe hypoglycemia. When a person experiences a hypoglycemic episode that is profound enough to prevent oral intake or to cause unconsciousness—often as a result of excessive insulin administration—glucagon can be administered by injection to rapidly increase circulating glucose.

For the treatment of severe hypoglycemia, glucagon is given either intramuscularly or subcutaneously. Both routes are accepted clinical practice, and the medication may be described simply as a glucagon injection. The injection is intended to restore adequate blood glucose when the patient cannot eat or is unable to respond due to the hypoglycemic state.</data>
  <data key="d9">emergency,glucose elevation,intramuscular,medication,subcutaneous,treatment</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-431b48980656b0322f263c358250b593&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4da80e99fd3e43cb7d3b260aca23fe56&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4f079198593c1702b56062aa87e7801a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d5bb996e52cb71f15bc8c30d1b1d321&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-831f4bbfc884fc8e9679630a819083e9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-779af610d7298ce98490962cd90b4e76&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7ce776458e256df9d6070a419cab7449</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/Bula Humalog.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/LANTUS _ BulasMed.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/NOVORAPID _ BulasMed.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_fiasp.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1786325551</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
