  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hypoglycemia" target="Humalog">
  <data key="d7">3.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Use of Humalog may lead to hypoglycemia, ranging from mild to severe.&lt;SEP&gt;A large dose of Humalog can cause hypoglycemia, a dangerous drop in blood sugar.&lt;SEP&gt;Improper dosing of Humalog can lead to hypoglycemia.</data>
  <data key="d9">adverse effect,metabolic effect,risk</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-431b48980656b0322f263c358250b593&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e89f1dbae629e925f06732cebf41df16&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4d26ce64e79b8c4a147140be2f9c63dd</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/Bula Humalog.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1786303834</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hypoglycemia" target="Lantus">
  <data key="d7">2.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Improper dosing of Lantus can increase the risk of hypoglycemia.&lt;SEP&gt;Lantus may induce hypoglycemia when the administered dose exceeds the patient’s insulin needs.</data>
  <data key="d9">adverse effect,monitoring,risk,safety</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-d59c9bf7f429a82cbfd7083e36ff8f9a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-67563459bb64c390a40207da52944afd</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/LANTUS _ BulasMed.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1786304230</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hypoglycemia" target="Neurological Disorders">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Severe or recurrent hypoglycemic episodes may lead to neurological disorders.</data>
  <data key="d9">complication,neurological</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-d59c9bf7f429a82cbfd7083e36ff8f9a</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/LANTUS _ BulasMed.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1786304231</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hypoglycemia" target="Vision">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Severe hypoglycemia can cause temporary visual disturbances or loss of vision, especially in patients with proliferative retinopathy.</data>
  <data key="d9">complication,visual</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-d59c9bf7f429a82cbfd7083e36ff8f9a</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/LANTUS _ BulasMed.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1786304231</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hypoglycemia" target="Diabetic Retinopathy">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Severe hypoglycemia may temporarily worsen diabetic retinopathy.</data>
  <data key="d9">complication,retinal</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-d59c9bf7f429a82cbfd7083e36ff8f9a</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/LANTUS _ BulasMed.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1786304232</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hypoglycemia" target="Neuroglycopenia">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Severe hypoglycemia can cause neoglycopenia, a deficiency of glucose in the brain.</data>
  <data key="d9">cerebral glucose deficiency,complication</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-d59c9bf7f429a82cbfd7083e36ff8f9a</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/LANTUS _ BulasMed.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1786304235</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hypoglycemia" target="Adrenérgica Counterregulation">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">As blood glucose declines, adrenérgica counterregulation intensifies during hypoglycemia.</data>
  <data key="d9">counterregulation,physiological response</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-d59c9bf7f429a82cbfd7083e36ff8f9a</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/LANTUS _ BulasMed.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1786304237</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hypoglycemia" target="Antibodies">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Presence of antibodies may require insulin dose adjustment to correct hypoglycemia.</data>
  <data key="d9">dose adjustment</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-4da80e99fd3e43cb7d3b260aca23fe56</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/LANTUS _ BulasMed.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1786304237</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hypoglycemia" target="Intravenous Glucose Solution">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Severe hypoglycemia can be treated with concentrated intravenous glucose solution.</data>
  <data key="d9">emergency,treatment</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-4da80e99fd3e43cb7d3b260aca23fe56</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/LANTUS _ BulasMed.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1786304239</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hypoglycemia" target="Insulin Glargina">
  <data key="d7">2.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The long‑acting nature of insulin glargine can postpone the correction of hypoglycemia.&lt;SEP&gt;Prolonged effect of insulin glargina may delay recovery from hypoglycemia.</data>
  <data key="d9">delayed recovery,effect,pharmacodynamics,pharmacology</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-ffb10c00517fa772be2ca9a42f497edf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-45d489de28e8fda3c3be3bb09ab29eb2</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/LANTUS _ BulasMed.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Basaglar.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1786310268</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hypoglycemia" target="Carbohydrate">
  <data key="d7">2.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Immediate ingestion of carbohydrate, such as orange juice or sugar, is used to raise low blood glucose.&lt;SEP&gt;Oral carbohydrate intake is recommended for mild episodes of hypoglycemia.</data>
  <data key="d9">nutrition,oral therapy,treatment</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-ffb10c00517fa772be2ca9a42f497edf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d7223c781e745e72311fccfcdd58583</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/LANTUS _ BulasMed.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Toujeo.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1786313853</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hypoglycemia" target="Retinopathy Proliferative">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Severe hypoglycemia can lead to proliferative retinopathy, risking transient blindness.</data>
  <data key="d9">complication,risk</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-ffb10c00517fa772be2ca9a42f497edf</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/LANTUS _ BulasMed.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1786304269</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hypoglycemia" target="Autonomic Neuropathy">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Patients with autonomic neuropathy may experience severe hypoglycemia without warning signs.</data>
  <data key="d9">comorbidity,risk factor</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-ffb10c00517fa772be2ca9a42f497edf</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/LANTUS _ BulasMed.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1786304270</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hypoglycemia" target="Psychiatric Diseases">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Psychiatric conditions may mask hypoglycemia symptoms, making detection harder.</data>
  <data key="d9">masking,risk</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-ffb10c00517fa772be2ca9a42f497edf</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/LANTUS _ BulasMed.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1786304271</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hypoglycemia" target="Endocrine Disorders">
  <data key="d7">2.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Certain endocrine disorders can increase the risk of hypoglycemia.&lt;SEP&gt;Uncompensated endocrine disorders increase hypoglycemia susceptibility.</data>
  <data key="d9">influence,risk,risk factor</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-ffb10c00517fa772be2ca9a42f497edf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-45d489de28e8fda3c3be3bb09ab29eb2</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/LANTUS _ BulasMed.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Basaglar.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1786310272</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hypoglycemia" target="Insulin Aspart (Novorapid®)">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Excessive insulin aspart dosing, missed meals, or unexpected strenuous exercise can cause hypoglycemia.</data>
  <data key="d9">adverse effect,overdose</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-f895f97a023b65cced82334a7f1d1e0b</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/NOVORAPID _ BulasMed.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1786305970</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hypoglycemia" target="Basal‑Bolus Insulin Regimen">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Improper coordination of basal‑bolus insulin with meals increases the risk of hypoglycemia.</data>
  <data key="d9">dosing schedule,risk factor</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-f895f97a023b65cced82334a7f1d1e0b</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/NOVORAPID _ BulasMed.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1786305971</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hypoglycemia" target="Insulin Transfer Between Types">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Switching patients to a different insulin formulation can reduce the prominence of early hypoglycemia alert symptoms.</data>
  <data key="d9">clinical transition,symptom modulation</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-f895f97a023b65cced82334a7f1d1e0b</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/NOVORAPID _ BulasMed.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1786305972</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hypoglycemia" target="Meal‑Related Insulin Administration">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Administering insulin too close to a meal or in excess can cause hypoglycemia.</data>
  <data key="d9">dosing mismatch,risk</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-f895f97a023b65cced82334a7f1d1e0b</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/NOVORAPID _ BulasMed.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1786305973</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hypoglycemia" target="NovoRapid®">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">NovoRapid® presents a lower risk of nocturnal hypoglycemia compared with regular insulin.</data>
  <data key="d9">nocturnal,risk reduction</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-9725072a361e9b1b97c5daa35e061e58</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/NOVORAPID _ BulasMed.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1786305983</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hypoglycemia" target="Adverse Reactions">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Hypoglycemia is a common type of adverse reaction reported with NovoRapid® therapy.</data>
  <data key="d9">adverse event,type of</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-9725072a361e9b1b97c5daa35e061e58</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/NOVORAPID _ BulasMed.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1786305984</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hypoglycemia" target="Patient">
  <data key="d7">4.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Patients may experience hypoglycemia as a common adverse reaction to NovoRapid® therapy.&lt;SEP&gt;Excessive insulin dosing, missed meals, or intense exercise can cause hypoglycemia in patients.&lt;SEP&gt;Patient may experience hypoglycemia as a frequent metabolic side effect of insulin therapy.&lt;SEP&gt;Patient may experience frequent hypoglycemia.</data>
  <data key="d9">adverse event,adverse reaction,condition,excess dosing,risk,risk of,symptom</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-9725072a361e9b1b97c5daa35e061e58&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-acaa1440ae268669e1894588bb9e37c2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8ac99e7359716e2cecc2ec93159218b6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-63f18f20af642d4a480c16e7a6780bb6</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/NOVORAPID _ BulasMed.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/CGM/Documento sem título.docx</data>
  <data key="d12">1786333911</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hypoglycemia" target="Insulin Therapy">
  <data key="d7">2.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Insulin therapy can cause hypoglycemia, the most frequently reported adverse reaction.&lt;SEP&gt;Improper insulin therapy can cause hypoglycemia.</data>
  <data key="d9">adverse effect,metabolic,risk</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-f9e5c50e8a808c537075377966ae2ccd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6ca13e396b094f0c2f482892f220f538</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/NOVORAPID _ BulasMed.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Basaglar.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1786310317</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hypoglycemia" target="MedDRA">
  <data key="d7">2.0</data>
  <data key="d8">MedDRA classifies hypoglycemia under metabolism and nutrition disorders as a very common adverse event.&lt;SEP&gt;MedDRA classifies hypoglycemia as a specific adverse event category in the tables.</data>
  <data key="d9">categorization,classification,frequency</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-f9e5c50e8a808c537075377966ae2ccd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5c580ebfc111aa29796af1a6f15941c7</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/NOVORAPID _ BulasMed.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Basaglar.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1786310121</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hypoglycemia" target="Metabolism and Nutrition Disorders">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Hypoglycemia is grouped under metabolism and nutrition disorders as a very common adverse reaction.</data>
  <data key="d9">category,metabolic</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-f9e5c50e8a808c537075377966ae2ccd</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/NOVORAPID _ BulasMed.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1786305999</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hypoglycemia" target="Driving">
  <data key="d7">6.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Hypoglycemia can impair concentration and reaction time, posing a risk while driving a car.&lt;SEP&gt;Severe low blood‑glucose can affect a person’s ability to drive safely.&lt;SEP&gt;Hypoglycemia can impair the concentration needed for safe driving.&lt;SEP&gt;Hypoglycemia can impair concentration and reaction, increasing the risk while driving.&lt;SEP&gt;Hypoglycemia can impair concentration and reaction, posing a safety risk while driving.&lt;SEP&gt;Hypoglycemia can impair concentration and reaction, posing a risk when patients drive.</data>
  <data key="d9">impairment,risk,safety,safety risk</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-6d0f18c80f8de2dee960a03599d12052&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4704ea4d5c15ebc8c043a077f05fd7a3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fd94288932ad6675a1de2b46b3fd9128&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3237e202569462c758ec3d878c9faeae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0fa819f7e1e42eb688d4894dc3ca7e64&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-577779892c0d463cd6bb1966b8a8ce2d</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/NOVORAPID _ BulasMed.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/TRESIBA _ BulasMed.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_1778357531609.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1786319825</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hypoglycemia" target="Operating Machines">
  <data key="d7">5.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Low blood glucose may reduce a patient’s ability to safely operate machines.&lt;SEP&gt;Hypoglycemia can impair the reaction required to safely operate machines.&lt;SEP&gt;Hypoglycemia can impair concentration and reaction, posing a risk when operating machines.&lt;SEP&gt;Hypoglycemia can reduce the ability to operate machines safely.&lt;SEP&gt;Hypoglycemia may compromise the ability to safely operate machines.</data>
  <data key="d9">impairment,risk,safety,safety risk</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-6d0f18c80f8de2dee960a03599d12052&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fd94288932ad6675a1de2b46b3fd9128&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f09811b149a29105854a0b1e84951e5d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3237e202569462c758ec3d878c9faeae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-577779892c0d463cd6bb1966b8a8ce2d</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/NOVORAPID _ BulasMed.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_1778357531609.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_apidra.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1786319848</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hypoglycemia" target="Injection Site Change">
  <data key="d7">7.0</data>
  <data key="d8">A sudden move to a non‑affected injection area may induce hypoglycemia.&lt;SEP&gt;A sudden change to an unaffected injection site has been reported to result in hypoglycemia.&lt;SEP&gt;Changing the injection area can affect susceptibility to hypoglycemia.&lt;SEP&gt;A sudden change to a non‑affected injection area has been reported to cause hypoglycemia.&lt;SEP&gt;A sudden switch to an unaffected injection area can precipitate hypoglycemia.&lt;SEP&gt;A sudden change to an unaffected injection area can result in hypoglycemia.&lt;SEP&gt;Changing the injection site to an unaffected area can precipitate hypoglycemia.</data>
  <data key="d9">adverse effect,cause,hypoglycemia,injection management,risk,risk factor,sudden shift</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-6d0f18c80f8de2dee960a03599d12052&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-45d489de28e8fda3c3be3bb09ab29eb2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6ca13e396b094f0c2f482892f220f538&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a2416b3e5e8ebc96cdb451a794fc78e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9a6f9e10c0d4af5fff0338eb861f9c86&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-acaa1440ae268669e1894588bb9e37c2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1e622f0079074cd1916470223d22aa66</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/NOVORAPID _ BulasMed.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Basaglar.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_1778357531609.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1786319805</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hypoglycemia" target="Novorapid">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Excessive doses of Novorapid can cause hypoglycemia in patients.</data>
  <data key="d9">adverse effect,overdose</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-4f079198593c1702b56062aa87e7801a</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/NOVORAPID _ BulasMed.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1786306028</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hypoglycemia" target="Oral Carbohydrate Administration">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Oral carbohydrate administration is recommended after hypoglycemia recovery to avoid recurrence.</data>
  <data key="d9">prevention</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-4f079198593c1702b56062aa87e7801a</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/NOVORAPID _ BulasMed.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1786306031</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hypoglycemia" target="Machines">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Very low or very high blood‑glucose can affect the ability to operate tools or machines safely.</data>
  <data key="d9">operation,safety</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-4704ea4d5c15ebc8c043a077f05fd7a3</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/TRESIBA _ BulasMed.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1786306384</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hypoglycemia" target="Beta‑Blockers">
  <data key="d7">2.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Beta‑blockers can make it harder to recognize signs of low blood‑glucose.&lt;SEP&gt;Beta‑blockers may reduce or mask the clinical signs of hypoglycemia.</data>
  <data key="d9">interaction,masking,symptom masking</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-4704ea4d5c15ebc8c043a077f05fd7a3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3db0edd23b6b502ccbbf62bfd601ce68</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/TRESIBA _ BulasMed.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Basaglar.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1786310198</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hypoglycemia" target="Sulfonamides">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Sulfonamides may cause a decrease in blood‑glucose levels.</data>
  <data key="d9">glucose‑lowering,interaction</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-4704ea4d5c15ebc8c043a077f05fd7a3</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/TRESIBA _ BulasMed.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1786306385</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hypoglycemia" target="Anabolic Steroids">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Anabolic steroids such as testosterone can lower blood‑glucose.</data>
  <data key="d9">glucose‑lowering,interaction</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-4704ea4d5c15ebc8c043a077f05fd7a3</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/TRESIBA _ BulasMed.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1786306386</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hypoglycemia" target="Acetylsalicylic Acid">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Acetylsalicylic acid and related salicylates may reduce blood‑glucose.</data>
  <data key="d9">glucose‑lowering,interaction</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-4704ea4d5c15ebc8c043a077f05fd7a3</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/TRESIBA _ BulasMed.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1786306387</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hypoglycemia" target="Monoamine Oxidase Inhibitors">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">MAO inhibitors can cause a decrease in blood‑glucose.</data>
  <data key="d9">glucose‑lowering,interaction</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-4704ea4d5c15ebc8c043a077f05fd7a3</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/TRESIBA _ BulasMed.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1786306387</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hypoglycemia" target="ACE Inhibitors">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">ACE inhibitors may make low‑glucose signs harder to detect.</data>
  <data key="d9">interaction,masking</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-4704ea4d5c15ebc8c043a077f05fd7a3</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/TRESIBA _ BulasMed.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1786306388</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hypoglycemia" target="High Blood Sugar">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">High blood sugar and hypoglycemia represent opposite extremes of blood‑glucose regulation.</data>
  <data key="d9">blood‑sugar range,contrast</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-2943becc796c8ce3f0aaedf0978c3213</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/TRESIBA _ BulasMed.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1786306405</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hypoglycemia" target="Tresiba® FlexTouch® 100 U/mL">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Use of Tresiba may lead to hypoglycemia if blood‑sugar levels become too low.</data>
  <data key="d9">adverse effect,risk</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-0a20360c489112f7848983049bae7125</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/TRESIBA _ BulasMed.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1786306436</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hypoglycemia" target="Lantus®">
  <data key="d7">2.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Hypoglycemia events were reported for Lantus®.&lt;SEP&gt;Lantus® treatment was associated with a modest increase in hypoglycemia events.</data>
  <data key="d9">adverse event occurrence,risk increase,safety outcome</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-c41538e94f00eba70740ff188bcb6a94&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5c580ebfc111aa29796af1a6f15941c7</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Basaglar.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1786310057</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hypoglycemia" target="Superdose">
  <data key="d7">5.0</data>
  <data key="d8">A superdose of insulin can cause severe, prolonged, potentially life‑threatening hypoglycemia.&lt;SEP&gt;An APIDRA superdose can result in severe hypoglycemia.&lt;SEP&gt;An insulin superdose may lead to hypoglycemia.&lt;SEP&gt;An insulin superdose can cause hypoglycemia accompanied by symptoms such as apathy, confusion, palpitations, sweating, vomiting, and headache.&lt;SEP&gt;A superdose of Humulin R can cause severe hypoglycemia accompanied by various symptoms.</data>
  <data key="d9">cause,overdose,severe adverse event,severe reaction,symptom</data>
