</edge>
<edge source="Hypoglycemia" target="Toujeo 300 U/mL">
  <data key="d7">3.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Toujeo 300 U/mL was associated with a 77.7 % incidence of hypoglycemia in adult Diabetes Type 1 patients and 80.3 % in pediatric Diabetes Type 1 patients over 26 weeks.&lt;SEP&gt;Toujeo 300 U/mL can cause hypoglycemia, especially after delivery, affecting driving safety.&lt;SEP&gt;High insulin dose from Toujeo can cause hypoglycemia.</data>
  <data key="d9">adverse effect,hypoglycemia,incidence,risk</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-3397508bdfddde019cb1dfdcfb352435&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-93623071acdcd0ba060c8826ab5a2a81&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e8934881ec5ab7cfeb836126b3f0e8b2</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Toujeo.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1786313728</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hypoglycemia" target="Uncompensated Endocrine Disorders">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Uncompensated endocrine disorders are associated with a higher likelihood of hypoglycemia.</data>
