<edge source="Hyperglycemia" target="Insulin Aspart (Novorapid®)">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Inadequate or discontinued dosing of insulin aspart, especially in type‑1 diabetes, may lead to hyperglycemia.</data>
  <data key="d9">adverse effect,dose‑related</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-f895f97a023b65cced82334a7f1d1e0b</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/NOVORAPID _ BulasMed.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1786305970</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hyperglycemia" target="Diabetic Ketoacidosis">
  <data key="d7">9.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The relation **Diabetic Ketoacidosis – Hyperglycemia** indicates that untreated, uncontrolled, or severe hyperglycemia—especially when it is persistent or persistent in patients with type 1 diabetes—can progress to diabetic ketoacidosis. This progression is recognized as a potentially lethal metabolic complication of diabetes, reflecting the critical need for prompt management of high blood‑glucose levels to prevent the development of ketoacidosis.&lt;SEP&gt;Prolonged hyperglycemia may progress to diabetic ketoacidosis.</data>
  <data key="d9">complication,progression,severe outcome,severity</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-f895f97a023b65cced82334a7f1d1e0b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-14772c7de5db762c492a75a1c744dae6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8ef15154a94043650617b3b24d8146a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f36263c657ad99a80e578ac49a333d5b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9a6f9e10c0d4af5fff0338eb861f9c86&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dd396c45bc09fb646d156b4e69d328e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea9b3836b3275f451c3acfb189f42a6f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-acaa1440ae268669e1894588bb9e37c2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b03b7fdf0dd9c96dc459929ccccdccff</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/NOVORAPID _ BulasMed.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_fiasp.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1786329880</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hyperglycemia" target="Meal‑Related Insulin Administration">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Improper timing of insulin relative to meals can lead to inadequate glucose control and hyperglycemia.</data>
