<edge source="Insulin NPH" target="Levemir®">
  <data key="d7">10.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Insulin NPH and Levemir® have been directly compared in multiple clinical investigations, including a randomized controlled trial involving pregnant women with type 1 diabetes in which the two products constituted the separate treatment arms. In the same pregnancy study, Levemir® was shown to achieve HbA1c levels that were non‑inferior to those obtained with Insulin NPH at week 36 of gestation, confirming comparable overall glycemic control during late pregnancy. Parallel pediatric studies also reported that Levemir® achieved HbA1c results similar to Insulin NPH, reinforcing its efficacy across age groups.

Across these trials, Levemir® demonstrated several advantages over Insulin NPH. Mean fasting glucose concentrations measured during weeks 24 and 36 of gestation were significantly lower in the Levemir® group, indicating superior fasting glycemic control. Levemir® also produced a lower rate of nighttime hypoglycemia, suggesting a more favorable safety profile during sleep periods. Weight-related outcomes favored Levemir® as well; participants on Levemir® experienced less weight gain than those receiving Insulin NPH, with a reported mean difference of approximately ‑0.15 kg. The formulation further allowed a more intensive dose titration, giving clinicians greater flexibility in adjusting therapy to meet individual patient targets.</data>
  <data key="d9">comparison,dose titration,efficacy,efficacy comparison,glucose,glycemic control,hypoglycemia reduction,non‑inferior,safety,weight gain,weight outcome</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-50a4f77ab697e068f8cf31533065722b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-767d025776f0f59c05788e25616f412c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-42ddf181cf4422a3b24643a2252d99b0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3059be019782459a72891cea5e0434ea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b4d7abd3e1e5418ee5a931e28a18e8ad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-56fc1d5df1b34d9120c3cf8a760c40f9</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1786317681</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
