  <data key="d12">1786317793</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Levemir" target="Injection Site Reactions">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Injection site reactions such as pain, redness, urticaria, inflammation, ecchymosis, edema, and pruritus are more common with Levemir® than with human insulin.</data>
  <data key="d9">adverse effect,comparison</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-0ace26fdb0244e3d0f714a007c9bbb51</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1786317793</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Levemir" target="Human Insulin">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Human insulin is used as a reference to show that injection site reactions occur more frequently with Levemir®.</data>
  <data key="d9">comparison,safety</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-0ace26fdb0244e3d0f714a007c9bbb51</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1786317794</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Levemir" target="Neuropathic Pain">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Rapid glycemic improvement during Levemir® therapy may be associated with acute painful neuropathy, which is generally reversible.</data>
  <data key="d9">association,reversible</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-0ace26fdb0244e3d0f714a007c9bbb51</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1786317794</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Levemir" target="Diabetic Retinopathy">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Rapid glycemic control with Levemir® can temporarily worsen diabetic retinopathy, while long‑term improved control reduces its progression risk.</data>
  <data key="d9">association,risk modulation</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-0ace26fdb0244e3d0f714a007c9bbb51</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_levemir.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1786317795</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
