</edge>
<edge source="Apidra" target="Insulin Humana Regular">
  <data key="d7">3.0</data>
  <data key="d8">When administered intravenously, Apidra and regular human insulin produce equipotent hypoglycemic activity.&lt;SEP&gt;Apidra begins to act more quickly after subcutaneous administration than regular human insulin.&lt;SEP&gt;The hypoglycemic effect of Apidra lasts a shorter time than that of regular human insulin.</data>
  <data key="d9">duration,equivalence,onset,pharmacodynamics,potency,speed</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-b65ee62ad12239ddc729c50a1aef854c</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_apidra.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1786315538</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Apidra" target="Estudo Em Pacientes Com Diabetes Tipo 1">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The study measured the glucose‑reduction profile of Apidra after a 0.15 UI/kg subcutaneous dose in patients with diabetes tipo 1.</data>
  <data key="d9">clinical trial,evaluation</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-b65ee62ad12239ddc729c50a1aef854c</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_apidra.pdf</data>
