<edge source="Insulina Glargina" target="Insulina Humana">
  <data key="d7">5.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Insulina glargina is designed as an analogue of human insulin, sharing receptor binding kinetics.&lt;SEP&gt;Clinical data showed that insulin glargina and insulin humana produced similar hormonal and hypoglycemia responses.&lt;SEP&gt;Insulina Glargina is an analogue of Insulina Humana, differing by specific amino‑acid modifications.&lt;SEP&gt;Insulin glargina is equipotent to human insulin.&lt;SEP&gt;Immunogenicity studies compared insulin glargina to insulin humana, indicating similar or lower immune response.</data>
  <data key="d9">analog,analogue,comparison,equipotent,immunogenicity comparison,similar response,similarity,structural difference</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-02780a8bc1d372cc47e0ccf2eaab1a99&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3a279eef99c9c70338c74ffc7b4e260e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-61cacf80ada6db26d2b975df763c137a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2db4ee43ed7cc39546184320e1328d06&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d99841fd6d1e1fbf23f184e202bc760e</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Basaglar.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Toujeo.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1786313794</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
