  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Insulina Glargina" target="Ratos">
  <data key="d7">5.0</data>
  <data key="d8">In combined pre‑ and post‑natal fertility studies in rats, insulin glargina caused dose‑dependent maternal hypoglycemia and reduced procreation rates at high dose.&lt;SEP&gt;Insulina Glargina was administered intravenously and subcutaneously to ratos to assess acute toxicity.&lt;SEP&gt;Repeated subcutaneous doses of insulin glargina were given to ratos to evaluate chronic toxicity.&lt;SEP&gt;Two‑year carcinogenicity studies of insulin glargina in ratos showed no increased cancer risk.&lt;SEP&gt;In rat embryotoxicity studies, insulin glargina was not embryotoxic nor teratogenic.</data>
  <data key="d9">acute toxicity,carcinogenicity,chronic toxicity,embryotoxicity,fertility,maternal toxicity,negative,testing</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-d99841fd6d1e1fbf23f184e202bc760e</data>
