<edge source="Reservoir" target="Infusion Set">
  <data key="d7">8.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Infusion Set, Reservoir

The infusion set functions as the connecting component that links the pump’s reservoir to the infusion site on the body. By attaching to the reservoir on one end, the set creates a conduit through which insulin (or other medication) is carried from the pump’s stored supply to the subcutaneous insertion point where delivery occurs. Proper connection of the infusion set to the reservoir is essential for reliable administration of the medication.

The reservoir itself is a component of the infusion set that stores the insulin; it holds the medication until it is drawn through the set’s tubing and into the infusion site. Because the reservoir is integral to the set’s operation, the infusion set must be disconnected from the body before any actions such as rewinding the pump or filling the reservoir tubing are performed, ensuring safety and preventing inadvertent dosing.</data>
  <data key="d9">component,connection,connects,contains,fluid storage,insulin flow,integration,safety,storage</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-7ce776458e256df9d6070a419cab7449&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4a4a75301f61fc3c86ad768de09d0c3f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-83bb94d08bdb958eff25f76c9a6ac18a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-474703bb16e6e26e009e9d433c3d3647&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-28515a0aca492eeee478cd9947226498&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b6025fa711665988fad0f789b9eb901a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-177e9aca0bf1c1724474ea529826bece&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a764dcbdd73fd1c50fa72a7cd60b6e19</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/MiniMed-780G-system-user-guide.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1786329784</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
