<edge source="Reservoir" target="Pump">
  <data key="d7">8.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The relation (Pump, Reservoir) describes how an insulin pump interacts with its attached insulin reservoir. The pump draws insulin from the reservoir that is mounted inside the device, using the stored insulin to provide scheduled or on‑demand delivery to the user.

To establish this connection, the reservoir is inserted into the pump and turned clockwise until it clicks or locks securely in place. This locking action ensures that the reservoir is properly seated, preventing leakage or disconnection during operation. Once locked, the pump’s internal mechanisms can access the insulin within the reservoir and dispense the medication as programmed.</data>
  <data key="d9">component,component usage,containment,contains,insertion,lock,locking,placement,security,storage,supply</data>
