  <data key="d12">1786330311</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Glulisine" target="Rapid‑Acting Insulin Analogs">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Glulisine is a type of rapid‑acting insulin analog.</data>
  <data key="d9">insulin,subcategory</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-c0a2dce3852e38344f91c86f45dda403</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1786330294</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Site Rotation" target="Localized Cutaneous Amyloidosis">
  <data key="d7">2.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Alternating injection locations lowers the chance of localized cutaneous amyloidosis.&lt;SEP&gt;Alternating injection areas lowers the chance of localized cutaneous amyloidosis.</data>
  <data key="d9">adverse effect,prevention,risk reduction</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-3db0edd23b6b502ccbbf62bfd601ce68&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1ee5400065df79b02b6c04efc0f4854d</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Basaglar.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Toujeo.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1786313856</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="SICI" target="MDI">
  <data key="d7">3.0</data>
  <data key="d8">SICI is reported to be more effective than MDI in lowering HbA1c.&lt;SEP&gt;SICI does not demonstrate a favorable cost‑benefit ratio relative to MDI.&lt;SEP&gt;Studies indicate that SICI is more costly than MDI.</data>
  <data key="d9">comparison,cost comparison,cost‑benefit,effectiveness,evaluation,expense</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-a7387e81b8141435df1372f5d8b27662&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6fba8ea0c6bdb8427804ba05f9fe49f9</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1786330205</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="SICI" target="United Kingdom">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">A study conducted in the United Kingdom estimated SICI’s annual cost to be £1,700 higher than MDI.</data>
  <data key="d9">cost analysis,research</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-a7387e81b8141435df1372f5d8b27662</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1786330205</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="SICI" target="CONITEC">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">CONITEC recommended that SICI not be incorporated into the SUS.</data>
  <data key="d9">non‑incorporation,policy</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-a7387e81b8141435df1372f5d8b27662</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1786330208</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="SICI" target="Pharmacoeconomics">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Pharmacoeconomics evaluates the higher cost of SICI compared with MDI.</data>
  <data key="d9">comparison,cost analysis</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-a7387e81b8141435df1372f5d8b27662</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1786330209</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="SICI" target="Gastroparesis">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Gastroparesis is listed as a medical indication for using SICI.</data>
  <data key="d9">medical indication,therapy</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-a7387e81b8141435df1372f5d8b27662</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1786330210</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="SICI" target="Autonomic Neuropathy">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Autonomic Neuropathy is a condition indicating SICI use.</data>
  <data key="d9">medical indication,therapy</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-a7387e81b8141435df1372f5d8b27662</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1786330211</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="SICI" target="Severe Hypoglycemia">
  <data key="d7">2.0</data>
  <data key="d8">SICI is indicated for patients experiencing frequent severe hypoglycemia.&lt;SEP&gt;Severe hypoglycemia is an indication for SICI use.</data>
  <data key="d9">indication,medical indication,therapy</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-a7387e81b8141435df1372f5d8b27662&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6fba8ea0c6bdb8427804ba05f9fe49f9</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1786330213</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="SICI" target="Sistema De Infusão Contínua De Insulina">
  <data key="d7">3.0</data>
  <data key="d8">SICI is the abbreviation referring to the continuous insulin infusion system.&lt;SEP&gt;SICI is the abbreviation representing Sistema De Infusão Contínua De Insulina.&lt;SEP&gt;SICI is the abbreviation for the insulin pump system (Sistema De Infusão Contínua De Insulina).</data>
  <data key="d9">abbreviation,alias,synonym</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-60530d1861f7c2d1efecc069c0913d37&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-336a2f2c9b510e23c35be95e2ff7a72a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-51c7617f1e335789b870332231de4058</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1786330248</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="SICI" target="AACE/ACE">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">AACE/ACE presents indications for using SICI that are similar to those of SBD.</data>
  <data key="d9">guidelines,indications</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-6fba8ea0c6bdb8427804ba05f9fe49f9</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1786330254</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="SICI" target="DM1">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">SICI is indicated for DM1 patients who are out of glycemic target, have recurrent ketoacidosis, severe hypoglycemia, expressive dawn phenomenon, extreme insulin sensitivity, or special groups such as pregnant women, children, adolescents, and athletes.</data>
  <data key="d9">indications,treatment</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-6fba8ea0c6bdb8427804ba05f9fe49f9</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1786330256</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="SICI" target="DM2">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">SICI is indicated for DM2 patients using excessive insulin doses, not reaching therapeutic goals, with positive C‑peptide, dawn phenomenon, severe insulin resistance, or irregular lifestyles (travel, shift work).</data>
  <data key="d9">indications,treatment</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-6fba8ea0c6bdb8427804ba05f9fe49f9</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1786330256</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="SICI" target="OpT2mise Study">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The OpT2mise study demonstrated that SICI is more effective than MDI in reducing HbA1c in poorly controlled DM2.</data>
  <data key="d9">efficacy,study</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-6fba8ea0c6bdb8427804ba05f9fe49f9</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1786330257</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="SICI" target="Rapid-Acting Insulin">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">When the insulin pump fails, rapid‑acting insulin administered by syringe or pen is recommended.</data>
  <data key="d9">alternative,emergency</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-6fba8ea0c6bdb8427804ba05f9fe49f9</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/sici.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1786330260</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="SICI" target="Long-Acting Insulin">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">During pump failure, long‑acting insulin is advised as a basal replacement at the same dose.</data>
  <data key="d9">alternative,basal</data>
