<edge source="Insulin Lispro" target="Insulin Regular Human">
  <data key="d7">5.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Rapid absorption of insulin lispro allows administration 15 minutes before a meal, versus 30‑45 minutes for regular insulin.&lt;SEP&gt;Insulin lispro is an analogue of human insulin created by inversion of amino acids at positions 28 and 29 of the B chain.&lt;SEP&gt;Insulin lispro reaches peak serum concentration faster than regular human insulin after subcutaneous injection.&lt;SEP&gt;Insulin lispro has the same volume of distribution as regular human insulin after injection.&lt;SEP&gt;Insulin lispro is equipotent to regular human insulin on a molar basis.</data>
  <data key="d9">absorption,analogue,distribution,dosing,molar equivalence,pharmacokinetics,potency,structural similarity,timing,volume</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-fb0fb965e5ddd796999856ca376d4b9d</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_1778357531609.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1786310813</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
