<edge source="Insulin Lispro" target="APIDRA">
  <data key="d7">5.0</data>
  <data key="d8">APIDRA was compared to insulin lispro in the clinical studies.&lt;SEP&gt;APIDRA’s onset of action is faster than that of insulin lispro in obese non‑diabetic subjects.&lt;SEP&gt;APIDRA was administered together with insulin lispro as a combined regimen in both adult and pediatric Type 1 diabetes arms.&lt;SEP&gt;In an obese non‑diabetic population, APIDRA maintained a faster onset of action than insulin lispro.&lt;SEP&gt;In obese non‑diabetic subjects, APIDRA and insulin lispro both exhibited a faster onset and shorter duration than regular insulin, with APIDRA’s onset comparable to lispro.</data>
  <data key="d9">combination therapy,comparator,comparison,efficacy,onset comparison,onset speed,pharmacodynamics,treatment</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-4d0e34bef478ed432c8de7ef68dc9025&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b18f8ab53481bf1b63fda1bb71fe80ec&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ee2684edaea64aa597fd29c3bbda611d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50719bcc88f4515ec825b9d5a7aba107&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-77dc1a2378f763ffabe8fa379881d1cc</data>
