<edge source="Insulina Humana Regular" target="APIDRA">
  <data key="d7">6.0</data>
  <data key="d8">APIDRA has a faster onset of action and a shorter duration than Insulina Humana Regular after subcutaneous injection.&lt;SEP&gt;When administered intravenously, APIDRA and Insulina Humana Regular produce equipotent hypoglycemic effects.&lt;SEP&gt;The effects of APIDRA did not differ from those observed with regular human insulin at the same subcutaneous doses.&lt;SEP&gt;In both the type 2 and type 1 studies, APIDRA was compared with insulin humana regular, showing greater A1C reduction and equivalent hypoglycemia rates.&lt;SEP&gt;APIDRA’s effects did not differ from those of regular human insulin at comparable subcutaneous doses.&lt;SEP&gt;APIDRA pre‑ and post‑meal regimens were compared with Insulina Humana Regular regarding glycaemic outcomes.</data>
  <data key="d9">comparative efficacy,comparison,efficacy,equivalence,onset,pharmacodynamics,safety,treatment comparison</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-2479751a6475c09415f0d79759db091d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3f0b85829c02f82470489f3f5e487996&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e212a20942ed5387efe96e92bdb4ba98&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7621ac447c9044986ade86ce5f9be201&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e3418c4ee80182ca29214dd54b0d9647</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_apidra.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1786315548</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
