<edge source="NovoRapid®" target="Regular Human Insulin">
  <data key="d7">5.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The substitution of proline with aspartic acid in NovoRapid® reduces hexamer formation, resulting in faster subcutaneous absorption than regular human insulin.&lt;SEP&gt;NovoRapid® demonstrated similar long‑term glucose control to regular human insulin when administered to children.&lt;SEP&gt;NovoRapid® reaches maximum plasma concentration in about half the time (tmax) required for regular human insulin.&lt;SEP&gt;NovoRapid® can replace regular human insulin in children aged one year or older when rapid onset is needed.&lt;SEP&gt;Intra‑individual variability in tmax is significantly lower for NovoRapid® than for regular human insulin.</data>
  <data key="d9">absorption speed,comparative efficacy,glucose control,molecular modification,pediatric,replaces,time to peak,tmax,variability</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-9725072a361e9b1b97c5daa35e061e58&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6b14c2f0985ae4a417c8fc99e339bd9e</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/NOVORAPID _ BulasMed.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1786305982</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
