<edge source="Body Mass Index (BMI)" target="Fiasp®">
  <data key="d7">3.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Higher BMI is associated with a trend toward a reduced initial hypoglycemic effect of Fiasp® in type 1 diabetes patients.&lt;SEP&gt;The greater initial insulin exposure of Fiasp® versus NovoRapid® is maintained across BMI categories and widens as BMI increases.&lt;SEP&gt;Analysis showed no association between total insulin exposure of Fiasp® and body mass index.</data>
  <data key="d9">BMI‑dependent exposure,no correlation,obesity,pharmacodynamics</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-2f4f01a72f35d6db3ff333e64f8400ce&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-88b97cde53943160602b20f634ba5c1f</data>
