<edge source="Insulin Glargine 100 U/mL" target="Toujeo 300 U/mL">
  <data key="d7">5.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Toujeo 300 U/mL is a higher‑concentration variant of insulin glargine compared with the 100 U/mL formulation.&lt;SEP&gt;For the same insulin units, Toujeo 300 U/mL needs about one‑third the injection volume of insulin glargine 100 U/mL.&lt;SEP&gt;Toujeo provides a more constant and prolonged glucose‑lowering effect than insulin glargine 100 U/mL.&lt;SEP&gt;Toujeo provides a more constant, slower and more prolonged insulin release than Insulin Glargine 100 U/mL.&lt;SEP&gt;Insulin Glargine 100 U/mL is not bioequivalent to, and therefore not interchangeable with, Toujeo 300 U/mL.</data>
  <data key="d9">absorption,administration,bioequivalence,comparative efficacy,concentration,dosage volume,glucose control,insulin variant,non‑interchangeability,pharmacokinetics,release profile</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-97208e231aa338c60205244ac12e0492&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3397508bdfddde019cb1dfdcfb352435&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-afc28422755c2c44f931bab7b6a2b477&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d6b9a8472aefa6e90793233284c15a3f</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_Toujeo.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1786313707</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
