  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Paciente Diabético" target="Controle Glicêmico">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Maintaining good glycemic control is crucial for all diabetic patients.</data>
  <data key="d9">clinical importance,management</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-e4ba52cc293c5c002b470566321026d6</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_apidra.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1786315505</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Mulher Grávida" target="Controle Glicêmico">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Strict glycemic control before conception and throughout pregnancy is essential for diabetic women.</data>
  <data key="d9">clinical importance,metabolic control</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-e4ba52cc293c5c002b470566321026d6</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_apidra.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1786315505</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Mulher Grávida" target="Categoria de risco C">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Pregnant women are advised that APIDRA SOLOSTAR falls under risk category C and should not be used without medical supervision.</data>
  <data key="d9">contraindication,risk classification</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-e4ba52cc293c5c002b470566321026d6</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_apidra.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1786315525</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Mulher Grávida" target="Novolin® R FlexPen®">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Insulin treatment with Novolin® R FlexPen® is allowed for pregnant women because insulin does not cross the placental barrier.</data>
  <data key="d9">pregnancy safety,usage</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-ba6b31518be6fff1db8b68a28e82f200</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_regular novonordiks.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1786318775</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Estrogênios" target="Síndrome dos Ovários Policísticos (SOP)">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Estrogens are not recommended for SOP patients with lipodystrophy due to hypertriglyceridemia risk.</data>
  <data key="d9">contraindication</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-7eabee57ef0af575162ce8d36f3589a5</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Complicações relacionadas ao uso da insulina/LIPODISTROFIAS.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1786321266</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="SoloStar" target="Apidra SoloStar">
  <data key="d7">2.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The SoloStar pen is the device that delivers the Apidra SoloStar insulin glulisine solution to the patient.&lt;SEP&gt;Apidra SoloStar is a specific blue model of the SoloStar insulin pen.</data>
  <data key="d9">delivery,device,model,variant</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-162882e6afffb0db8ae5e9153e5f1e82&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-79f891b1d7c0c6ca0eab9dbcc76c902d</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_apidra.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1786315526</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="SoloStar" target="Temperature Up To 30°C">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">SoloStar may be safely stored at ambient temperature not exceeding 30 °C during a 28‑day usage period.</data>
  <data key="d9">condition,storage</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-162882e6afffb0db8ae5e9153e5f1e82</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_apidra.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1786315529</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="SoloStar" target="Light and Heat">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">SoloStar must be protected from light and heat to maintain product integrity.</data>
  <data key="d9">handling,protection</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-162882e6afffb0db8ae5e9153e5f1e82</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_apidra.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1786315529</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="SoloStar" target="100 UI/ML SOL INJ">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">SoloStar is supplied as an injectable solution with a concentration of 100 UI/mL.</data>
  <data key="d9">dosage,formulation</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-2f2573669c38640b56efd6bd0668d1e2</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_apidra.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1786315578</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="SoloStar" target="Damage">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">SoloStar can be damaged if not lubricated or handled improperly, creating a risk of impairment.</data>
  <data key="d9">handling,risk</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-fdeef3e06ffaa7cc0442c3d94917f0c4</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_apidra.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1786315620</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="SoloStar" target="New Pen">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">If SoloStar is suspected of being damaged, it should be discarded and a new pen used as a safe replacement.</data>
  <data key="d9">replacement,safety</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-fdeef3e06ffaa7cc0442c3d94917f0c4</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_apidra.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1786315620</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="SoloStar" target="Dose Selector">
  <data key="d7">2.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Dose Selector is a rotating knob on the SoloStar used to set the amount of insulin to be injected.&lt;SEP&gt;SoloStar includes a dose selector that lets users set the insulin amount.</data>
  <data key="d9">adjustment,component,dosage adjustment,mechanism</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-ffe095bda1b787c5b5ae2d61a2f74c98&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-79f891b1d7c0c6ca0eab9dbcc76c902d</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_apidra.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1786315676</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="SoloStar" target="Temperature Range up to 30°C">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">SoloStar may be stored at room temperature up to 30°C for up to 28 days after removal from refrigeration.</data>
  <data key="d9">ambient storage,limit</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-ffe095bda1b787c5b5ae2d61a2f74c98</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_apidra.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1786315678</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="SoloStar" target="Insulin Reservoir">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Insulin Reservoir is the internal chamber that forms part of the SoloStar pen.</data>
  <data key="d9">component,part</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-ffe095bda1b787c5b5ae2d61a2f74c98</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_apidra.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1786315681</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="SoloStar" target="Light Exposure">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Exposure to light can degrade insulin and damage the SoloStar pen.</data>
  <data key="d9">degradation,risk</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-ffe095bda1b787c5b5ae2d61a2f74c98</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_apidra.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1786315682</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="SoloStar" target="Heat Exposure">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Exposure to heat can degrade insulin and damage the SoloStar pen.</data>
  <data key="d9">degradation,risk</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-ffe095bda1b787c5b5ae2d61a2f74c98</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_apidra.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1786315684</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="SoloStar" target="Plunger">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The SoloStar includes a plunger that moves with each injection and reaches the cartridge end when insulin is depleted.</data>
  <data key="d9">mechanism,part-of</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-e9835d6684db67541402527b3182b6c5</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_apidra.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1786315742</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="SoloStar" target="Dose Selection Step">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">During the dose selection step, the user adjusts the SoloStar’s dosage selector to set the required insulin units.</data>
  <data key="d9">dosage selection,procedure</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-e9835d6684db67541402527b3182b6c5</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/Bulas/bula_apidra.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1786315744</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="SoloStar" target="Injection Step">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">In the injection step, the user inserts the needle, presses the injection button, and holds it until the dose is fully delivered.</data>
  <data key="d9">injection,procedure</data>
