<edge source="Reservorio" target="Bomba">
  <data key="d7">10.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Bomba – Reservorio is the relationship that describes how the insulin pump (referred to as “Bomba”) incorporates the insulin‑holding component known as the “Reservorio.” In every description, the Bomba is identified as the device that contains, holds, or houses the Reservorio, positioning it within a dedicated reservoir compartment of the pump. The Reservorio itself is defined as the insulin reservoir component that stores insulin units ready for delivery, and it is physically placed inside the Bomba as part of the pump’s overall setup.

The reservoir (Reservorio) not only stores insulin but also reports the remaining amount of insulin available for use. When the pump encounters issues or reaches the end of its usable volume, the insulin reservoir may need to be replaced or changed. The design of the Bomba includes a specific compartment that accommodates the Reservorio, ensuring a secure fit and allowing the pump to draw insulin from the reservoir for accurate dosing.</data>
  <data key="d9">compartment,component,containment,contains,equipment,fits,hardware,information,placement,replacement,storage</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-8aa63853b30ac5d214c8cd80df90e517&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1f5ccf80661c0e52c3a3465ab87c6343&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-84bb2bb0df91a594c6936b2fe97e4220&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ca7afb2078bd96edf087859a2c89920c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-644dc086af7b196cc5bc332524608d5f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cfb7c582936fb68746bd1911895df40c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a967066e623ddb0c9381f89dfe0f3d42&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8fdb2f497ff0665f2860089645ba9450&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0cf7c487c5bd4a61120add295be9d518&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-01785f6f03692dc5e35c672e21b345f7</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/231037.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;data/raw/INSULINOTERAPIA/SICI (bomba de insulina)/887d88.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1786325544</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
