<edge source="TTGO-2h" target="TTGO-1h">
  <data key="d7">5.0</data>
  <data key="d8">TTGO‑1h is described as more practical than TTGO‑2h.&lt;SEP&gt;TTGO‑1h ≥ 209 mg/dL is considered equivalent to TTGO‑2h ≥ 200 mg/dL for diagnosing Diabetes Mellitus.&lt;SEP&gt;TTGO-1h is superior to TTGO-2h for detecting individuals at risk of developing Type 2 Diabetes.&lt;SEP&gt;TTGO-1h has reproducibility comparable to TTGO-2h.&lt;SEP&gt;TTGO-1h is considered more practical than TTGO-2h for diabetes screening.</data>
  <data key="d9">comparison,detection,diagnostic,equivalence,practicality,reproducibility,similarity,superiority</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-6a92f811a7d2d835dc4b730c9bbf08cf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-80893468bbc3744e2e535806ea31e346&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2faebf8275a86cd8d9995c769b0926a3</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Diagnóstico de diabetes mellitus.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1786372040</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
