<edge source="TTGO-1h" target="Pre-diabetes">
  <data key="d7">3.0</data>
  <data key="d8">A glucose level ≥ 155 mg/dL in TTGO‑1h is used as the cutoff for detecting pre‑diabetes.&lt;SEP&gt;TTGO-1h is recommended for the detection of pre‑diabetes.&lt;SEP&gt;TTGO-1h is recommended for individuals with low fasting glucose and HbA1c but multiple risk factors.</data>
  <data key="d9">criteria,cutoff,detection,recommendation</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-80893468bbc3744e2e535806ea31e346&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-23ad6eb7138be249f01b479174a34076</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Diagnóstico de diabetes mellitus.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1786372076</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="TTGO-1h" target="Abdul‑Ghani et al.">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Abdul‑Ghani and colleagues assessed glycemic profiles using TTGO‑1h in a cohort of Mexican‑American participants.</data>
  <data key="d9">assessment,research</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-80893468bbc3744e2e535806ea31e346</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Diagnóstico de diabetes mellitus.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1786372078</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="TTGO-1h" target="San Antonio Heart Study">
  <data key="d7">4.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The San Antonio Heart Study employed TTGO‑1h to evaluate future risk of Type 2 Diabetes.&lt;SEP&gt;San Antonio Heart Study evaluated TTGO‑1h glucose levels as predictors of Type 2 Diabetes Mellitus incidence.&lt;SEP&gt;In the San Antonio Heart Study, TTGO-1h had greater sensitivity than GJ and TTGO-2h for predicting DM2.&lt;SEP&gt;The study used TTGO‑1h values to stratify participants’ risk of developing type 2 diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d9">evaluation,glucose testing,prospective,risk assessment,sensitivity,study,superiority,usage</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-80893468bbc3744e2e535806ea31e346&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-23ad6eb7138be249f01b479174a34076&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e428438c632682ef93541430ec497ed5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3c6dca13b685243e63fb6f24f7cb301d</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Diagnóstico de diabetes mellitus.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1786372078</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="TTGO-1h" target="Botnia Study">
  <data key="d7">2.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The Botnia Study identified TTGO‑1h as the best predictor of Type 2 Diabetes among 14 TTGO‑derived indices.&lt;SEP&gt;In the Botnia Study, TTGO-1h showed higher predictive accuracy for DM2 than GJ and TTGO-2h.</data>
  <data key="d9">best‑predictor,evaluation,identification,predictive accuracy</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-80893468bbc3744e2e535806ea31e346&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-23ad6eb7138be249f01b479174a34076</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Diagnóstico de diabetes mellitus.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1786372080</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="TTGO-1h" target="Malmo Preventive Project">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The Malmo Preventive Project confirmed TTGO‑1h as the top predictor of Type 2 Diabetes in a combined multicenter analysis.</data>
  <data key="d9">best‑predictor,identification</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-80893468bbc3744e2e535806ea31e346</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Diagnóstico de diabetes mellitus.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1786372080</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="TTGO-1h" target="Metanalysis of 35,551 Individuals">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">A meta‑analysis of 35,551 participants validated TTGO‑1h ≥ 209 mg/dL as a diagnostic criterion for Diabetes Mellitus.</data>
  <data key="d9">threshold,validation</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-80893468bbc3744e2e535806ea31e346</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Diagnóstico de diabetes mellitus.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1786372081</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="TTGO-1h" target="209 mg/dL">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">TTGO‑1h uses a glucose level ≥ 209 mg/dL as the diagnostic cutoff for Type 2 Diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d9">cutoff,diagnostic</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-80893468bbc3744e2e535806ea31e346</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Diagnóstico de diabetes mellitus.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1786372082</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="TTGO-1h" target="155 mg/dL">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">TTGO‑1h uses a glucose level ≥ 155 mg/dL as the cutoff for detecting pre‑diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d9">cutoff,detection</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-80893468bbc3744e2e535806ea31e346</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Diagnóstico de diabetes mellitus.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1786372083</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="TTGO-1h" target="TTGO">
  <data key="d7">2.0</data>
  <data key="d8">TTGO‑1h is a one‑hour variant of the oral glucose tolerance test (TTGO).&lt;SEP&gt;TTGO-1h is the preferred timing for the oral glucose tolerance test in diabetes screening.</data>
  <data key="d9">method,preferred method,specialization,variant</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-80893468bbc3744e2e535806ea31e346&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c92d117f7109ea1ce6995f23bc680ce3</data>
  <data key="d11">data/raw/MONITORIZAÇÃO GLICÊMICA/METAS GLICÊMICAS/Diagnostico e Classificação/Diagnóstico de diabetes mellitus.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1786372084</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="TTGO-1h" target="Risco de Morte Prematura">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Individuals identified by TTGO-1h have increased risk of premature death.</data>
  <data key="d9">mortality,risk</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-23ad6eb7138be249f01b479174a34076</data>
